window.FWN_VILLAIN_CLAN_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_VILLAIN_CLAN_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":601,"title":"Chapter 601: The Bai Clan Gathers Its Forces","paragraphs":["Inside the secluded cultivation chamber, qi surged endlessly like a vast ocean.","Dense streams of qi revolved around Bai Zihan’s body before gradually being absorbed into his meridians.","Ever since returning to the Bai Clan, there had been very few matters capable of truly disturbing him.","As for the Imperial Family, Bai Zihan merely had Kong Zhanhong keep an eye on the situation from the shadows.","Even after hearing the news regarding the Second Prince’s conviction for murdering the Eleventh Prince and Thirteenth Princess before ultimately committing suicide within the Imperial Prison, Bai Zihan did not think much of it.","To him, the imperial throne struggle had little to do with the Bai Clan for now.","Knock! Knock!","The sound echoed from outside the chamber.","Bai Zihan slowly opened his eyes.","A faint ripple spread through the surrounding qi before the entire room gradually calmed down.","His brows furrowed slightly.","He had already given strict orders long ago.","Unless something truly important occurred, no one was allowed to disturb his cultivation.","Not even the clan elders were allowed to disturb him unless it was an extremely important matter.","Which meant something must have happened.","Bai Zihan slowly stood up before opening the chamber door.","Outside, a servant immediately bowed respectfully.","\"Clan Leader!\"","Bai Zihan nodded slightly.","\"What is it?\"","The servant quickly replied.","\"Miss Bai Xueqing wishes to see you.\"","Bai Zihan raised an eyebrow slightly.","(What does she want now?)","Considering it was Bai Xueqing, it was no wonder the servant dared disturb him without explaining the reason.","Within the Bai Clan, Bai Xueqing’s words carried almost as much weight as his own.","Not to mention, since she was his sister, if she said she wished to see her younger brother, who could truly stop her?","Even if it was for no reason, no one could.","Bai Zihan did not ask anything further.","He simply nodded before heading directly toward the Clan Leader’s study room where Bai Xueqing was waiting.","A short while later, he pushed open the doors.","Inside, Bai Xueqing was already seated calmly.","Beside her stood a familiar figure.","Fei Ling!","The moment Bai Zihan saw her, his eyes narrowed slightly.","Her complexion looked extremely poor.","Her expression was tense and uneasy, as though she had rushed here in great haste and emotional distress.","Clearly, something serious had happened.","Bai Zihan walked inside calmly.","Then he looked toward Bai Xueqing.","\"What happened?\"","Bai Xueqing’s expression immediately turned serious.","\"Yu Longxuan attacked the Fei Clan. He brought experts, including Grand Elders from the Crimson Thunder Palace, and forcefully pressured the Fei Clan into submission.\"","Fei Ling clenched her hands tightly as Bai Xueqing reiterated what had happened to her clan.","\"The Fei Clan already joined the Neutral Alliance...\"","Her voice sounded slightly shaky.","\"We never intended to participate in the struggle for the throne.\"","Her fingers tightened further.","\"But I didn’t expect Yu Longxuan to still make a move against us...\"","Fei Ling bit her lower lip lightly before finally looking directly toward Bai Zihan.","For the first time since meeting him, her usual pride and confidence were nowhere to be seen. Only anxiousness remained.","\"Junior Brother...\"","Her voice softened unconsciously.","\"Can you help us?\"","The pleading tone in her voice caused Bai Zihan to pause briefly.","Looking at Fei Ling’s current appearance, he almost wanted to tease her instinctively.","Unfortunately, this was neither the time nor place for such things.","The situation was already serious enough.","Bai Zihan’s expression gradually turned calm once more.","Then he spoke plainly.","\"Since the Fei Clan joined the Neutral Alliance, it is natural that the other members of the Neutral Alliance help.\"","\"Otherwise, the alliance would become nothing more than a joke.\"","His tone was calm, yet it carried unquestionable certainty.","The moment those words fell, Fei Ling’s tense expression visibly relaxed slightly.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan slowly stood up.","A faint pressure immediately spread throughout the room.","\"Pass down my orders. Gather all disciples, Elders, and Grand Elders who are not in seclusion.\"","Bai Zihan slowly clasped his hands behind his back. A terrifying aura faintly emanated from his body.","\"I shall show them...\"","His voice echoed calmly throughout the study room.","\"What it means to go against me.\"","The moment those words fell, even the surrounding qi seemed to tremble faintly.","Fei Ling looked at Bai Zihan blankly.","Previously, if someone had spoken such words before her, she would have found them arrogant and unbearably pretentious.","But now, knowing Bai Zihan was saying it for the sake of protecting her clan, she suddenly found herself unable to feel that way at all.","Instead, her eyes unconsciously brightened slightly as she looked toward him.","For some reason, the uneasiness within her heart seemed to lessen greatly the moment Bai Zihan decided to move personally.","Fei Ling immediately cupped her hands toward him seriously.","\"Thank you, Junior Brother.\"","However, Bai Zihan merely shook his head calmly.","\"There is no need to thank me.\"","His expression remained indifferent.","\"This is what I should do.\"","***","Meanwhile, Bai Xueqing had already begun passing down orders directly.","And very quickly, the entire Bai Clan began moving.","One after another, summons spread throughout the clan grounds.","All disciples, elders, and grand elders not in seclusion were ordered to gather immediately.","The moment the news spread, the atmosphere within the Bai Clan instantly became lively.","However, contrary to what one might expect, there was almost no nervousness.","Instead, excitement spread everywhere.","\"Hahaha! Finally!\"","\"I was wondering when the Clan Leader would make a move.\"","\"So who are we teaching a lesson this time?\"","...","Many clan members looked eager rather than worried.","The clan’s overall strength had undergone an enormous transformation recently.","Heaven-Grade Cultivation Technique!","High-grade pills!","High-grade artifacts!","The benefits Bai Zihan brought back had elevated the Bai Clan’s foundation to an entirely new level.","Many elders and grand elders who had long stagnated had recently broken through one after another.","Even the younger generation improved at astonishing speeds.","Compared to the past, the current Bai Clan was far stronger than before.","The only problem was...","They had never truly tested that strength yet.","After all, very few forces within the empire dared provoke the Bai Clan nowadays.","And the few that did were either too cautious or backed away quickly after seeing the Bai Clan’s momentum.","But now, the Clan Leader himself had personally ordered such a massive gathering.","Clearly, this was not some small matter, and their opponent should be quite formidable, which only made them more excited.","Very quickly, the Bai Clan entered a state of complete mobilization.","Streams of figures rushed across the clan grounds one after another as countless auras rose into the skies.","Within less than an hour, the Bai Clan’s central plaza was already filled with experts.","Nearly everyone available within the clan had gathered.","At the very front stood nine Immortal Ascension Realm experts.","Nine!","Even among peak factions, such a number was already enough to shock countless forces.","And that was not all.","Among them were also several Earth Immortal experts whose pressure alone caused the surrounding space to distort faintly.","Compared to before, the Bai Clan’s upper combat power had clearly risen enormously.","Although only two Immortal Ascension Realm grand elders had successfully broken through to the Earth Immortal Realm recently with the help of pills refined by the Mu Clan, it was still a lot considering that happened within a few months.","It is already very rare for such breakthroughs to happen even within 10 years.","The ones to break through to Earth Immortal were Bai Qingshan and Bai Yue.","Both had previously participated in the great war against the Demonic Forces.","With their addition, the Bai Clan now possessed a total of five Earth Immortal experts participating in this operation.","Bai Ren and Bai Chu were in seclusion. And there were two other Grand Elders who couldn’t make it.","But they needed to be in the Clan to protect it, not to mention, the force gathered was already overkill.","Five Earth Immortals!","Nine Immortal Ascension experts!","Such a terrifying force...","Even if they intended to invade a powerful empire directly, success would still be highly possible.","Not to mention, their target this time was merely the Seventh Prince and his faction.","At this moment, Bai Zihan slowly stepped forward.","The originally noisy plaza instantly became silent.","Countless gazes gathered upon him simultaneously.","Bai Zihan’s expression remained calm as usual.","Then he spoke briefly.","\"The Seventh Prince attacked the Fei Clan. The Fei Clan is part of the Neutral Alliance.\"","\"Yet he still dared pressure them into submission.\"","His eyes gradually turned cold.","\"This is no longer merely a matter concerning the Fei Clan.\"","\"It is a challenge against the entire Neutral Alliance and ultimately against us!\"","The surrounding Bai Clan members immediately understood.","And after understanding, many of them instantly sneered coldly.","\"The Crimson Thunder Palace? And the Seventh Prince?\"","\"Hah! Looks like they truly don’t wish to live anymore.\"","\"Daring to touch a clan under our protection...\"","\"Tsk! Tsk! I truly admire his courage.\"","Others looked even more eager.","Recently, everyone within the Bai Clan had improved tremendously.","But because no one dared provoke them, they had no opportunity to properly display their strength.","And now, someone had finally delivered themselves directly to their doorstep.","How could they not feel excited?","At the front, Bai Qingshan laughed loudly while releasing his newly stabilized Earth Immortal aura without restraint.","\"Hahaha! Perfect timing!\"","\"This old man was just wondering who I should test my breakthrough on!\"","Beside him, Bai Yue also revealed a cold smile.","\"Hopefully the Crimson Thunder Palace experts won’t disappoint us too badly.\"","Even the younger generation looked eager and battle-hungry.","The current atmosphere within the Bai Clan no longer resembled preparation for war.","Instead, it felt more like a grand hunting expedition.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan calmly swept his gaze across the gathered experts.","Then he spoke one final sentence.","\"Let’s not waste our time then. Advance on the Crimson Thunder Palace!\""]},{"number":602,"title":"Chapter 602: The Crimson Thunder Palace Trembles","paragraphs":["Inside the Crimson Thunder Palace, the atmosphere was completely different from the tense mood spreading throughout the empire.","The grand hall was filled with laughter and relaxed conversation.","At the very center, Yu Longxuan sat calmly with a faint sneer upon his face while several elders and grand elders of the Crimson Thunder Palace surrounded him.","Compared to before, his mood had improved greatly.","After all, the Fei Clan had already been successfully suppressed.","Although they had not completely submitted yet, the pressure placed upon them was enormous, and sooner or later they would have no choice but to submit.","One elder laughed coldly.","\"Hmph! This Neutral Alliance truly thinks too highly of itself.\"","Another elder nodded in agreement.","\"In the end, they are merely a group of clans trying to stay out of the throne struggle while still enjoying its benefits.\"","\"They want neutrality?\"","The elder sneered disdainfully.","\"In a battle for the throne, how could neutrality truly exist?\"","Several people in the hall laughed lightly.","Yu Longxuan also revealed a cold smile.","\"Exactly!\"","His fingers tapped lightly against the armrest of his chair.","\"When great powers struggle for supremacy, those without strength do not have the right to remain neutral.\"","\"If they refuse to choose a side, then they should prepare to be devoured.\"","His voice carried open disdain.","In his eyes, the Neutral Alliance’s existence itself was ridiculous.","There had been many throughout history that attempted the same thing, but against the Imperial Family and the top factions supporting various princes and princesses, they were nothing more than symbolic resistance.","This time, only because of the Bai Clan did many princes and princesses not dare make a move against them, with the Seventh Prince being the sole exception.","Now, after successfully pressuring the Fei Clan, they felt there was little left to fear.","Yu Longxuan slowly narrowed his eyes.","The success against the Fei Clan had indeed emboldened him greatly.","Originally, he still feared the Bai Clan’s possible reaction.","But now, several days had already passed without any movement from the Bai Clan.","They received neither warnings nor threats, which Yu Longxuan interpreted as exactly what he had expected.","The Bai Clan truly did not wish to openly clash with the Crimson Thunder Palace over a mere First-Rate Clan.","And to him, his choice has been correct.","Otherwise, if he remained passive while the others continued expanding their influence, he would eventually be devoured first.","Thinking about this, Yu Longxuan’s confidence grew even further.","\"If things continue smoothly...\"","He spoke slowly.","\"Then after the Fei Clan, we can continue pressuring the other clans we initially targeted.\"","A cold smile appeared on his face.","\"By then, hmph! My brothers and sisters who hesitated to act will regret it immensely.\"","Several elders immediately nodded.","Once enough clans submitted to them, Yu Longxuan’s power would inevitably expand greatly once more.","On the other hand, the other princes and princesses were still wary of provoking the Neutral Alliance directly.","If they continued remaining passive while Yu Longxuan expanded aggressively, then eventually his force would be much greater than theirs.","Thinking this way, many within the Crimson Thunder Palace actually believed the Bai Clan joining the Neutral Alliance had become advantageous for them.","After all, it caused the other imperial contenders to hesitate while Yu Longxuan alone continued moving proactively.","However, just as the joyous atmosphere continued—","BOOM!!!","A terrifying pressure suddenly descended from the heavens.","The entire Crimson Thunder Palace shook violently.","Countless disciples’ expressions changed drastically.","Several teacups inside the hall shattered instantly.","The smiles on the elders’ faces froze immediately.","Then their expressions abruptly changed.","\"Earth Immortal aura?!\"","\"And not just one!\"","The grand elders of the Crimson Thunder Palace instantly stood up.","Their expressions turned grave because they could clearly sense several terrifying auras pressing down upon the sect from above.","Without hesitation, the Crimson Thunder Palace experts immediately rushed outside.","Yu Longxuan’s expression also changed slightly before he quickly followed behind them.","The moment they stepped outside—","Everyone froze.","The skies above the Crimson Thunder Palace were already filled with figures.","An enormous army hovered in the air like dark clouds covering the heavens.","Countless Bai Clan experts stood proudly in formation.","Their auras surged endlessly.","At the very front stood five Earth Immortal experts.","Behind them were nine Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators.","And further back, thousands upon thousands of Bai Clan disciples and elders filled the skies completely.","The terrifying pressure alone caused the Crimson Thunder Palace’s protective formation to tremble faintly.","The expressions of the Crimson Thunder Palace elders instantly changed drastically.","Even Yu Longxuan’s pupils contracted violently.","Because this lineup was far more terrifying than anything they had anticipated.","At the very front of the army, Bai Zihan stood calmly with his hands behind his back.","His gaze overlooked the Crimson Thunder Palace indifferently.","As though he were merely looking at insignificant ants.","The moment Yu Longxuan saw the overwhelming lineup before him, his heart instantly sank.","Although he could not sense the Earth Immortals’ aura clearly himself, he still understood one terrifying fact.","There were simply too many Immortal Realm experts present.","Not to mention the Great Ascension and Void Refinement cultivators filling the skies so densely that he could barely count them.","And behind them stood an enormous force of Bai Clan elites radiating terrifying pressure.","Such a lineup...","This was no mere show of force.","The Bai Clan had truly come prepared for war.","For a brief moment, genuine fear flashed across Yu Longxuan’s eyes.","However, in front of so many elders and disciples of the Crimson Thunder Palace, how could he possibly reveal weakness?","His expression immediately darkened as lightning crackled violently around his body.","Then he stepped forward furiously.","\"Bai Zihan!\"","His roar echoed throughout the skies.","\"What are you trying to do?!\"","His eyes burned with anger and humiliation.","\"Do you truly wish to start a war against the Crimson Thunder Palace?!\"","The surrounding Crimson Thunder Palace disciples also became tense instantly.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan merely looked at him indifferently.","His expression did not change in the slightest.","Then he finally spoke calmly.","\"A war?\"","A faint cold smile appeared on his face.","\"You make it sound as though the Bai Clan was the one seeking trouble first.\"","His gaze gradually sharpened.","\"Was it not you who attacked the Fei Clan? Was it not you who pressured a member of the Neutral Alliance into submission?\"","Bai Zihan’s voice remained calm, yet every word carried immense pressure.","\"Now you ask what we are trying to do?\"","He slowly took a step forward.","BOOM!","A terrifying aura instantly swept across the heavens, causing countless Crimson Thunder Palace disciples to pale.","\"Do you truly not know what you have done? Or are you merely feigning ignorance?\"","Yu Longxuan’s expression stiffened slightly.","However, very quickly, the coldness within his eyes intensified once more.","Even now, he still could not fully suppress the pride ingrained within him since birth.","No matter how powerful the Bai Clan had become, he was still a prince of the empire and one of the contenders for the imperial throne.","Lightning crackled wildly around his body as he stepped forward again.","\"Bai Zihan!\"","His voice echoed across the skies.","\"Do not forget who you are speaking to!\"","\"I am the Seventh Prince of the Yu Imperial Family!\"","\"You dare surround the Crimson Thunder Palace like this and threaten me openly?\"","Yu Longxuan’s eyes turned increasingly fierce.","\"Do you truly wish to become enemies with the entire Imperial Family?!\"","The moment those words fell, many Crimson Thunder Palace disciples regained some confidence.","That was right.","No matter how powerful the Bai Clan was, the Yu Imperial Family still ruled the empire.","Provoking the Imperial Family openly was practically equivalent to rebellion.","However, the next moment, Bai Zihan suddenly laughed.","\"Hahaha...\"","Then Bai Zihan slowly raised his gaze toward Yu Longxuan.","\"A prince?\"","His lips curved faintly. The tone in his voice almost sounded dismissive.","Then his expression gradually turned cold.","\"Even if every force within the Yu Clan came here today, there is still nothing they could do to stop my Bai Clan.\"","The moment those words fell, the entire Crimson Thunder Palace became deathly silent.","Countless expressions changed drastically.","The fact that Bai Zihan referred to them as the \"Yu Clan\" rather than the \"Imperial Family\" instantly caused countless hearts to tremble.","Because everyone understood clearly what Bai Zihan was implying.","He no longer viewed the Yu Imperial Family as some untouchable supreme ruler.","In his eyes, the Yu Clan was merely another faction.","And perhaps...","Not even a stronger one anymore.","Such words could practically already be considered open rebellion against the empire.","Yet Bai Zihan showed no intention of retracting them.","Instead, he calmly continued.","\"Yu Longxuan.\"","His eyes looked directly into the Seventh Prince’s.","\"Do you truly believe your status as Seventh Prince amounts to anything before me?\"","Yu Longxuan looked at Bai Zihan, whose expression was completely devoid of emotion.","There truly seemed to be no difference in Bai Zihan’s eyes between him and any ordinary cultivator.","Before Yu Longxuan could speak again, Bai Zihan’s eyes turned completely cold.","\"Either way, today, you will pay the price.\"","The atmosphere instantly froze.","The expressions of the Crimson Thunder Palace experts changed drastically.","Because everyone could hear the undisguised killing intent within Bai Zihan’s voice.","At this moment, a middle-aged man in purple robes suddenly stepped forward.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader.","Unlike Yu Longxuan, his expression remained relatively calm, though deep shock still lingered within his eyes as he looked at the Bai Clan’s terrifying lineup.","Especially the five Earth Immortals.","Even now, he still found it difficult to believe the Bai Clan had developed to such a terrifying extent in such a short period of time.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader immediately cupped his hands politely.","\"Young Master Bai.\"","His tone was much gentler than before.","\"I believe there may be some misunderstanding here.\"","The moment those words fell, Yu Longxuan’s expression changed slightly.","However, the Sect Leader ignored him completely.","Because unlike the Seventh Prince, he could already clearly see the reality before him.","If the Bai Clan truly attacked today...","The Crimson Thunder Palace might genuinely suffer devastating losses.","Perhaps even destruction.","Just looking at the overwhelming force gathered above them was already enough to make one’s scalp numb.","The Sect Leader continued calmly.","\"The matter regarding the Fei Clan can still be discussed. There is no need for both sides to escalate things to this extent.\"","His attitude was extremely cautious.","Because he understood one thing very clearly now.","The current Bai Clan was no longer a force the Crimson Thunder Palace could casually offend anymore.","’Just when did they become so scary?’"]},{"number":603,"title":"Chapter 603: Amusement for the Strong, Despair for the Weak","paragraphs":["Fei Ling silently watched everything unfold beside Bai Xueqing.","Even now, her emotions still felt somewhat unreal.","Just a few days ago, the Crimson Thunder Palace had descended upon the Fei Clan with overwhelming pressure.","At that time, the Seventh Prince and the Crimson Thunder Palace had acted incomparably arrogantly.","Completely dismissive of the Fei Clan.","In their eyes, the Fei Clan seemed no different from prey waiting to be devoured.","Even her father, the Fei Clan Leader, had been forced into an extremely passive position beneath their pressure.","Yet now, those same people who once looked down upon the Fei Clan with disdain no longer possessed that arrogance.","The Crimson Thunder Palace elders’ expressions were stiff and uneasy.","Even the Sect Leader himself was lowering his posture and attempting to negotiate carefully.","As for Yu Longxuan, although he still tried maintaining a fierce appearance, anyone could see the fear hidden beneath his expression.","Seeing this scene, Fei Ling suddenly felt a deep sense of satisfaction rise within her heart.","Especially when she recalled how oppressive and arrogant the Crimson Thunder Palace had acted within the Fei Clan.","Now that same pressure was being returned to them several times over.","Beside her, Bai Xueqing merely smiled faintly.","At this moment, Bai Zihan looked indifferently toward the Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader.","Then he scoffed.","\"A misunderstanding?\"","The Sect Leader’s expression stiffened slightly.","Bai Zihan’s eyes gradually turned colder.","\"You should have already thought about that before attacking the Fei Clan.\"","His voice echoed calmly across the skies.","\"The moment you laid your hands upon a member of the Neutral Alliance, you had already made your choice.\"","Previously, Bai Zihan would not have cared much about conflicts between clans and sects.","However, he had intentionally joined the Neutral Alliance precisely to prevent those clans that wished to avoid the throne struggle from being forcefully dragged into it.","After all, if the entire empire descended into civil war, outside forces would inevitably benefit from the chaos.","That was something Bai Zihan wished to avoid.","Yet these people had clearly not taken him seriously and still dared to make such a move.","Not only were they disregarding him openly, they were also interfering with his plans.","If he failed to teach them a proper lesson today, then the other princes and princesses would likely begin doing the same thing soon enough.","BOOM!","The pressure surrounding the Bai Clan instantly intensified once more.","Many Crimson Thunder Palace disciples immediately turned pale.","Then Bai Zihan slowly continued.","\"It is time for you to face the consequences of that choice.\"","Bai Zihan stood calmly in the skies with his hands behind his back.","His indifferent gaze slowly swept across the faces of the Crimson Thunder Palace experts.","Fear!","Regret!","Their earlier confidence had already vanished completely.","Unfortunately for them, there was no medicine for regret in this world.","Then Bai Zihan finally raised his hand slightly.","That simple gesture immediately caused the Bai Clan experts’ eyes to brighten sharply.","Because they had already waited long enough.","\"Attack!\"","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Terrifying auras erupted throughout the heavens instantly.","The Bai Clan moved almost simultaneously.","Streams of light shot across the skies as countless attacks descended toward the Crimson Thunder Palace like a heavenly catastrophe.","The expressions of the Crimson Thunder Palace experts changed drastically.","\"Activate the formation immediately!\"","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader roared furiously.","RUMBLE!","A massive defensive formation instantly rose from the sect grounds.","Countless runes illuminated the skies as a gigantic barrier enveloped the entire Crimson Thunder Palace.","A Grade-6 Defensive Formation!","Even Immortal Realm experts would find it difficult to break through quickly.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader’s expression remained extremely grave.","Although he knew the formation could not withstand the Bai Clan forever, it should at least buy them several hours.","That would be enough time.","Enough time to think of a solution.","Enough time to contact reinforcements.","And perhaps, enough time for the Li-Zhao Alliance to make their move.","After all, the Bai Clan had mobilized nearly all their high-level experts here—or so he believed.","If the Li and Zhao Clans seized this opportunity to attack the Bai Clan estate directly, the Bai Clan might be forced to retreat.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader’s mind rapidly calculated various possibilities.","However—","CRACK!","A sharp cracking sound suddenly echoed throughout the heavens.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader’s expression froze instantly.","\"What?!\"","Before anyone could react—","SHATTER!!!","The entire defensive barrier trembled violently.","Massive cracks spread across it at terrifying speed.","Then, under the horrified gazes of countless Crimson Thunder Palace disciples, the Grade-6 Formation exploded apart completely.","It shattered after only a few attacks.","The terrifying shockwaves swept across the skies as fragments of spiritual light scattered everywhere.","At the very front, several Bai Clan Grand Elders slowly lowered their hands calmly.","Their expressions looked almost disappointed.","\"That’s it?\"","\"I thought a Grade-6 Formation would at least last a little longer.\"","\"Tsk! Tsk! It seems this is going to be another boring fight.\"","...","Meanwhile, the Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader stood completely stunned.","His mind nearly went blank.","This was a Grade-6 Formation!","A formation capable of resisting Immortal Realm experts!","Yet it had only endured a few attacks before collapsing completely?!","At this moment, countless Crimson Thunder Palace disciples finally began feeling true despair.","\"Don’t panic! Fight back!\"","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader gritted his teeth as he gave out the command.","The Crimson Thunder Palace disciples also knew they had no choice but to clash with the Bai Clan.","And clash they did.","The instant the formation shattered, the Bai Clan descended like a raging tide.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Explosions erupted throughout the Crimson Thunder Palace as streams of spiritual light collided violently across the skies.","Cries of battle echoed everywhere.","However, this was not a battle fought on equal footing.","It was complete one-sided suppression.","The gap between the two sides was simply too enormous.","The Bai Clan disciples were stronger.","Their cultivation realms were much higher.","Their cultivation techniques were vastly superior.","Even the artifacts in their hands far surpassed those of the Crimson Thunder Palace.","Many Crimson Thunder Palace disciples quickly discovered a horrifying reality.","Their attacks could barely penetrate the Bai Clan disciples’ defenses.","Meanwhile, every strike from the Bai Clan carried terrifying destructive force.","THUD!","A Crimson Thunder Palace elder was blasted backward by a single punch from a Bai Clan elder.","His protective artifact shattered instantly as blood sprayed from his mouth.","Before he could stabilize himself—","SWOOSH!","A Bai Clan disciple suddenly appeared before him while holding a High Profound Grade spear artifact.","The disciple grinned coldly.","\"Is this all the Crimson Thunder Palace amounts to?\"","BOOM!","The spear slammed down mercilessly, sending the elder crashing into the ground below.","Elsewhere, several Crimson Thunder Palace disciples joined forces to attack a Bai Clan young expert.","Lightning techniques exploded wildly.","Yet the Bai Clan disciple merely sneered before raising the sword in his hand.","A dazzling sword light swept across the skies instantly.","RIPPPP!","All of the incoming attacks were destroyed immediately.","The Crimson Thunder Palace disciples’ expressions changed drastically.","\"What?!\"","Before they could retreat—","BOOM!","The sword qi exploded through their defenses and sent all of them flying while coughing blood.","The Bai Clan disciple clicked his tongue disdainfully.","\"You people should take this more seriously.\"","His eyes turned cold.","\"Otherwise, you’ll all die here today.\"","Similar scenes unfolded everywhere throughout the battlefield.","The Crimson Thunder Palace experts were steadily pushed backward.","Many disciples had already begun feeling despair because the Bai Clan was simply too terrifying.","Meanwhile, the Bai Clan members became increasingly excited as the battle continued.","\"Hahaha! Is this the Crimson Thunder Palace? A top sect? Bah! More like a weak sect that only knows how to bully weaker clans.\"","\"Don’t say that, brother. Aren’t we also bullying a weak sect right now? Haha... \"","\"I thought you people were stronger than this!\"","...","While the disciples’ battlefield already looked one-sided, the situation among the elders and grand elders was not much different.","In fact, the gap there was even more obvious.","Most Crimson Thunder Palace elders were merely in the Void Refinement Realm.","Meanwhile, many Bai Clan elders had already stepped into the Great Ascension Realm.","The difference in strength was overwhelming.","BOOM!","A Crimson Thunder Palace elder was sent flying backward after exchanging only several moves with a Bai Clan elder.","His expression was filled with disbelief.","\"How is this possible?!\"","Previously, while the Bai Clan was obviously stronger, they didn’t think it was to this extent.","If in the same situation, the Bai Clan would win but this was their home ground where they have the advantage.","Still, the Bai Clan easily suppressed them.","Not only were their cultivation bases higher, but their techniques were also far more profound.","Even their qi felt denser and more refined.","Many Crimson Thunder Palace elders were rapidly pushed into desperate situations.","As for the Grand Elders, the disparity was even more hopeless.","The Crimson Thunder Palace only possessed four Immortal Realm experts in total.","And among them, only one had reached the Earth Immortal Realm.","Compared to the Bai Clan’s current lineup, the difference was simply too terrifying.","At this moment, Bai Qingshan suddenly stepped forward while laughing loudly.","\"Hahaha!\"","His newly stabilized Earth Immortal aura erupted without restraint.","Terrifying pressure swept across the battlefield instantly.","Then he directly pointed toward the strongest Grand Elder of the Crimson Thunder Palace.","\"You’re mine!\"","The Crimson Thunder Palace Earth Immortal expert’s expression changed drastically.","Meanwhile, Bai Qingshan cracked his neck slightly before grinning fiercely.","\"No one interfere!\"","His eyes burned with battle intent.","\"This old man just broke through recently. I want to see exactly how strong I’ve become!\"","Hearing this, several other Bai Clan Grand Elders merely laughed lightly and nodded.","\"Fine.\"","\"Then we’ll leave him to you.\"","\"Don’t embarrass yourself.\"","None of them objected.","It was not because they underestimated the Crimson Thunder Palace.","Rather, opponents at the Earth Immortal level were not easy to find.","Especially for newly ascended experts like Bai Qingshan, such battles were extremely valuable for understanding their own strength.","Besides, everyone understood clearly that if the Bai Clan truly fought seriously with full force...","The Crimson Thunder Palace would likely collapse within minutes.","Just by looking at the battlefield below, it was already obvious.","The Bai Clan disciples and elders were not fighting with killing intent from beginning to end.","Many were clearly holding back intentionally.","Some even treated the battle like entertainment.","\"Hahaha! Come on! Is that all?\"","One Bai Clan elder laughed loudly while casually suppressing two opponents at once.","Another Bai Clan disciple intentionally waited for his opponent to unleash their strongest technique before casually breaking it apart with a single strike.","\"So weak?\"","\"You people from the Crimson Thunder Palace should at least struggle properly.\"","Meanwhile, the Crimson Thunder Palace experts became increasingly desperate.","Because for them, this was a battle for survival.","Every second determined life and death.","Yet for the Bai Clan...","This entire war felt more like amusement."]},{"number":604,"title":"Chapter 604: When the Crimson Thunder Palace Collapsed","paragraphs":["Only now did Yu Longxuan finally understand exactly what kind of existence he had provoked.","The Crimson Thunder Palace was losing.","No, it was being completely overwhelmed.","And the most terrifying part was that the Bai Clan clearly was not even fighting seriously yet.","Some were even laughing casually while fighting.","Others treated the battlefield like some kind of training exercise.","Even the Earth Immortal experts of the Bai Clan had barely made any real moves.","Yet despite that, the Crimson Thunder Palace was already collapsing rapidly.","This was no war.","It was a slaughter disguised as battle.","Yu Longxuan’s face gradually turned pale.","Even if reinforcements arrive now...","Would it matter?","The Li Clan?","The Zhao Clan?","Other allied factions?","Yu Longxuan suddenly realized something horrifying.","Even if those forces truly came, they likely still would not be enough.","Because the Bai Clan had not even used twenty percent of their force. Others were merely watching.","And the Crimson Thunder Palace was already on the verge of destruction.","At this moment, Yu Longxuan’s thoughts rapidly raced.","What could he do now?","Challenge Bai Zihan to a one-on-one duel?","With the condition that if he won, perhaps he could negotiate for the Bai Clan to withdraw.","But the very thought caused bitterness to rise in his heart.","Win?","Against Bai Zihan?","Impossible!","It had been impossible for him to defeat Bai Zihan back in the Ancient Ruin, and it was even more impossible now that the gap between them had widened further.","He couldn’t even defeat Nie Fengzhuo, while on the other hand, Bai Zihan had reportedly defeated Nie Fengzhuo.","Then... capture Bai Zihan?","Yu Longxuan’s eyes flickered faintly.","If they could seize Bai Zihan hostage, perhaps the situation could still be salvaged.","The Bai Clan would definitely be forced to negotiate.","But the moment that thought appeared, it was quickly crushed by reality.","Capture Bai Zihan?","How?","Just reaching him was already nearly impossible.","Around Bai Zihan alone stood nearly fourteen Immortal Realm experts.","Five Earth Immortals!","Nine Immortal Ascension experts!","Not to mention countless Great Ascension Realm elders surrounding them.","That lineup alone was enough to make anyone despair.","Even if someone somehow managed to break through all those experts...","Was Bai Zihan himself truly someone easy to capture?","The more Yu Longxuan thought about it, the heavier his heart became.","An indescribable regret slowly spread through his chest.","Why?","Why did he have to provoke Bai Zihan of all people?","Originally, he merely wanted to expand his influence quickly before the First Prince completely stabilized his control over the Imperial Court.","He only wanted to force several clans into submission.","Yet now, before he could even truly begin fighting against the other princes and princesses for the throne...","His own foundation was already being destroyed.","BOOM!","Another massive explosion erupted in the distance.","Several palace buildings collapsed instantly beneath the clash of powerful techniques.","Yu Longxuan’s expression became uglier and uglier.","Not far away, the Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader was no different.","His face had already turned pale as he watched the sect he had protected for hundreds of years being dismantled piece by piece before his eyes.","The Crimson Thunder Palace had stood proudly at the peak of the empire for thousands of years.","Countless forces feared them.","Countless geniuses dreamed of joining them.","Yet now...","A single clan was crushing them so thoroughly that they could barely resist.","The Sect Leader’s heart trembled increasingly the longer he watched.","Everything the Crimson Thunder Palace previously knew about the Bai Clan had been completely wrong.","At this moment, the Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader no longer had any thoughts of resisting.","His only remaining thought was survival.","Without hesitation, he immediately cupped his hands toward Bai Zihan high in the skies.","\"Clan Leader Bai!\"","His voice echoed anxiously across the battlefield.","\"The Crimson Thunder Palace admits its mistakes! We are willing to compensate the Fei Clan!\"","\"We are willing to apologize and swear we will never make a move against them again. Please show mercy!\"","His voice carried genuine panic now.","However, Bai Zihan merely glanced at him briefly.","Then he ignored him completely.","Bai Zihan no longer cared about negotiation.","The Bai Clan had already given enough chances previously.","Yet the Crimson Thunder Palace still chose to test his bottom line.","Now they would naturally have to pay the price.","Bai Zihan’s gaze remained cold.","This battle would also serve as a warning to others.","Anyone who dared disregard his words would face consequences.","And until Bai Zihan was satisfied, he would not let the Crimson Thunder Palace off so easily.","BOOM!","A terrifying shockwave suddenly erupted high above the battlefield.","Everyone’s attention instinctively turned toward the clash between the Earth Immortal experts.","At this moment, the Crimson Thunder Palace Earth Immortal Grand Elder looked incomparably miserable.","His robes were already stained with blood.","Several defensive artifacts floating around him had already shattered completely.","His aura had become chaotic and unstable.","Meanwhile, opposite him, Bai Qingshan only looked increasingly excited as the battle continued.","\"Hahaha! This is all an old Earth Immortal amounts to?!\"","He had already used Fate Severing Slash once, and it had nearly killed the Crimson Thunder Palace’s Grand Elder.","If he had not held back, there might not even have been bones left of him.","\"UGH!\"","The Grand Elder coughed out blood while being blasted backward thousands of meters.","His heart was already filled with disbelief.","This was impossible!","He had already entered the Earth Immortal Realm many years ago.","Meanwhile, Bai Qingshan had only recently broken through.","Under normal circumstances, Bai Qingshan should not even have been his opponent.","Yet now, he was the one being completely suppressed.","And the more they fought, the more horrified he became.","Bai Qingshan’s qi was far denser and purer than his own.","Not to mention, the last technique Bai Qingshan used was terrifyingly profound.","The very same technique was rumored to have once slain the Half-Qilin during the war against the Demonic Forces.","He had not been entirely certain back then, but now, after personally experiencing the attack, he believed it completely.","Indeed, only such a terrifying technique could possibly kill a legendary beast carrying Qilin blood.","’Just where did the Bai Clan obtain such a terrifying technique?!’","His heart shook violently.","A technique of this level should not even exist within the empire.","At this moment, Bai Qingshan casually waved his hand.","BOOM!","A terrifying wave of qi instantly shattered another defensive artifact protecting the Crimson Thunder Palace Grand Elder.","The old man was blasted backward once more while coughing blood continuously.","Then Bai Qingshan frowned slightly.","His earlier excitement had already faded considerably.","\"This is it?\"","His disappointed voice echoed clearly across the battlefield.","\"Don’t you have any trump cards?\"","The Crimson Thunder Palace Grand Elder’s face turned red with fury and humiliation.","Trump cards?","He had already used nearly everything he possessed!","Defensive artifacts.","Secret techniques.","Even his life-saving methods had already been forced out one after another.","If not for them, could he have even remained alive until now?","Bai Qingshan slowly shook his head.","\"To think I was actually looking forward to this fight.\"","His tone sounded genuinely disappointed.","Earth Immortal opponents were not easy to find, especially for a life-and-death battle.","Yet the opponent before him could not even force him to use thirty percent of his qi.","Bai Qingshan sighed again.","\"What a waste!\"","Originally, he had been genuinely excited about this battle.","Yet this opponent before him could not even properly force him to become serious.","Bai Qingshan slowly clenched his fist.","Feeling the terrifying power flowing through his meridians, even he himself felt inwardly shocked.","Although he had already sensed the enormous changes after cultivating the new techniques and consuming the Mu Clan’s pills—","Only now, through actual combat, did he truly understand how monstrous his current strength had become.","Compared to the Bai Clan’s Earth Immortals, the Crimson Thunder Palace Earth Immortal experts were practically paper tigers.","Though both sides stood within the same realm, their actual combat power was completely different.","The Bai Clan completely surpassed them in every aspect.","The more Bai Qingshan fought, the more clearly he realized one terrifying truth.","The current Bai Clan had already begun walking down a completely different path from the other forces within the empire.","And the difference between both sides was only going to grow larger with time.","(I wonder which force in the Eastern Region can compete with our current strength?)","The situation across the other battlefields was not much different.","Everywhere one looked, the Crimson Thunder Palace was being completely suppressed.","Their disciples were retreating continuously.","Their elders were covered in injuries.","Even the Immortal Realm experts had already fallen into desperate situations.","The once lofty Crimson Thunder Palace now looked utterly miserable.","Bai Zihan calmly observed the battlefield from above, his expression remained indifferent.","However, after watching for a moment longer, his eyes flickered faintly.","If this continued, the Crimson Thunder Palace might genuinely be exterminated entirely today.","Under normal circumstances, Bai Zihan would not particularly care.","Since the moment the Crimson Thunder Palace dared challenge his authority and attack a member of the Neutral Alliance, they had already chosen their own fate.","But now was not the right time.","And right now, Bai Zihan still did not wish for the empire’s overall strength to weaken too much.","At least, not before the true storm arrived.","Thinking this, Bai Zihan slowly raised his hand.","The next moment—","\"Enough!\"","His calm voice instantly echoed across the entire battlefield.","Yet despite not being loud, it carried unquestionable authority.","In a heartbeat, every Bai Clan expert immediately stopped.","No hesitation.","No complaints.","No one questioned the order in the slightest.","The battlefield, which moments ago had been filled with violent explosions and chaotic clashes, abruptly became silent.","Only the sounds of collapsing rubble and heavy breathing remained.","Then, under countless gazes, Bai Zihan slowly stepped forward.","His indifferent eyes landed directly upon Yu Longxuan and the Crimson Thunder Palace experts below.","Then Bai Zihan finally spoke calmly.","\"Yu Longxuan! Crimson Thunder Palace!\"","His gaze became colder.","\"I wonder whether you have learned your lesson?\""]},{"number":605,"title":"Chapter 605: Mercy at Fei Ling’s Word","paragraphs":["The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader’s heart trembled violently.","Without even the slightest hesitation, he immediately cupped his hands deeply toward Bai Zihan.","\"Yes! Yes!\"","His voice carried obvious panic.","\"The Crimson Thunder Palace has learned its lesson! We were wrong!\"","\"We should never have touched the Fei Clan nor challenged the Neutral Alliance!\"","The Sect Leader lowered his posture completely.","He did not dare delay even a single moment.","Because he feared that even the slightest hesitation might anger Bai Zihan further.","And if that happened, The Crimson Thunder Palace might truly disappear from the empire today.","Meanwhile, beside him, Yu Longxuan’s expression looked extremely ugly.","His fists clenched tightly.","His heart was filled with humiliation and unwillingness.","He was a dignified imperial prince who would become the Emperor.","Yet now he was being forced into such a miserable state before countless people.","How could he possibly accept this?","However, the moment he noticed the gazes directed toward him by the Crimson Thunder Palace elders and Sect Leader, his heart sank heavily.","Those gazes clearly carried warning and pressure.","At this point, if he still dared provoke Bai Zihan further and caused the Bai Clan to continue attacking, then all responsibility would fall entirely upon him.","The Crimson Thunder Palace would hate him completely.","If he was abandoned by his biggest backer then, his dream of becoming the Emperor would be as good as gone.","Yu Longxuan’s expression twisted repeatedly before he finally lowered his head unwillingly.","\"...I was wrong.\"","His voice sounded extremely strained.","\"I should not have targeted the Fei Clan.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, it felt as though all the pride within his heart had shattered completely.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan merely watched calmly.","His expression did not change at all.","Would he end things so easily just because of a few apologies?","\"Hmmm...\"","Then, unexpectedly, Bai Zihan slowly turned his head.","His gaze landed upon Fei Ling beside Bai Xueqing.","\"Senior Sister Fei.\"","His tone sounded calm.","\"Are you satisfied?\"","Fei Ling froze slightly.","Clearly, she had not expected Bai Zihan to suddenly ask her directly.","For a moment, she genuinely did not know what to say.","Satisfied?","Originally, she would already have felt grateful enough if Bai Zihan had merely helped the Fei Clan escape the Crimson Thunder Palace’s suppression.","But now, The Crimson Thunder Palace has nearly been destroyed entirely.","Its disciples and elders were covered in injuries.","Even its Sect Leader and the Seventh Prince stood there trembling in fear.","The once lofty and arrogant Crimson Thunder Palace had been crushed completely beneath the Bai Clan’s feet.","What was there for her not to be satisfied with?","Seeing Fei Ling’s somewhat dumbfounded expression, Bai Zihan seemed to understand immediately.","Then he calmly looked back toward the Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader and Yu Longxuan.","His voice suddenly turned cold once more.","\"Kneel!\"","The Sect Leader’s pupils contracted violently.","Yu Longxuan’s expression changed drastically.","Before either of them could react, Bai Zihan continued indifferently.","\"Kneel before Senior Sister Fei and apologize properly.\"","His eyes gradually sharpened.","\"If she is not satisfied...\"","A terrifying pressure slowly spread from his body once more.","\"Then the only thing awaiting the Crimson Thunder Palace will be destruction.\"","Many within the Crimson Thunder Palace felt extremely unwilling deep inside especially the disciples and elders who had suffered heavily during the battle.","Some looked toward Fei Ling with resentment hidden within their eyes.","After all, in their opinion, this entire calamity had indeed begun because of her and the Fei Clan.","If not for the Fei Clan joining the Neutral Alliance...","If not for Fei Ling asking for Bai Zihan’s help...","How could the Crimson Thunder Palace have fallen into such a miserable state?","The Crimson Thunder Palace had lost all face today.","Many were feeling a deep resentment towards Fei Ling after Bia Zihan asked whether she was satisfied or not?","If she wasn’t satisfied after all this, they can only say that her grudge is as deep as an ocean and she won’t be satisfied until they were destroyed.","However, the moment Bai Zihan calmly uttered those words, everyone’s thoughts instantly changed.","The meaning behind those words could not have been clearer.","Whether the Crimson Thunder Palace survived or not...","Would now depend entirely upon Fei Ling’s satisfaction.","At that moment, the resentment within many people’s hearts disappeared completely, replacing it with fear.","Because everyone understood clearly that Bai Zihan was absolutely capable of destroying them if he wished.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader’s expression changed repeatedly.","Then, without the slightest hesitation, he directly knelt.","BANG!","His knees smashed heavily against the ruined ground.","The sudden action stunned many disciples.","After all, this was the dignified Sect Leader of the Crimson Thunder Palace.","A peak expert who normally stood above countless people within the empire.","Yet now, he had abandoned all pride completely.","The Sect Leader lowered his head toward Fei Ling immediately.","\"Miss Fei!\"","His voice no longer carried the dignity of a sect master.","Instead, it was filled with nervousness and sincerity.","\"The Crimson Thunder Palace was wrong! We were blinded by greed and arrogance!\"","He quickly continued before Fei Ling could even respond.","\"From today onward, the Crimson Thunder Palace is willing to fully compensate the Fei Clan for all losses!\"","\"We are also willing to assist the Fei Clan in every possible way! And I personally swear that the Crimson Thunder Palace will never again make any move against the Fei Clan!\"","His voice became increasingly serious.","\"Not only that, we are willing to protect the Fei Clan no matter what happens.\"","\"As long as the Crimson Thunder Palace still exists, no one will be allowed to bully the Fei Clan again!\"","The surrounding Crimson Thunder Palace elders’ expressions twitched slightly upon hearing those words.","Protect the Fei Clan under their banner?","Previously, they had looked down upon the Fei Clan completely.","Yet now, their Sect Leader was voluntarily lowering their status before them.","However, no one dared object.","Because Bai Zihan was still standing there calmly watching everything.","Meanwhile, Yu Longxuan’s expression had already become extremely ugly.","His fists clenched tightly beneath his sleeves.","Humiliation burned fiercely within his chest.","However, the moment he sensed Bai Zihan’s indifferent gaze land upon him, his heart immediately trembled.","At the same time, the Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader and several elders also looked toward him anxiously.","Their meaning was obvious.","If he still refused now and angered Bai Zihan further, then the Crimson Thunder Palace might truly be finished today.","At that point, all blame would naturally fall upon him.","Yu Longxuan gritted his teeth so hard that faint cracking sounds could almost be heard.","Finally—","BANG!","He unwillingly knelt as well.","His expression looked incomparably ugly.","\"...The matter regarding the Fei Clan...\"","Yu Longxuan forced the words out slowly.","\"It was because of the struggle for the throne.\"","His voice sounded extremely stiff.","\"I was blinded by ambition and failed to consider the consequences properly.\"","The humiliation within his heart nearly made him cough blood.","Yet he still lowered his head slightly toward Fei Ling.","\"I apologize!\"","The surrounding atmosphere instantly became strange.","Countless people stared blankly at the scene before them.","A Sect Leader of a peak sect.","A prince of the empire.","Both kneeling before Fei Ling simultaneously.","Trying desperately to appease her.","At this moment, Fei Ling herself was completely dumbfounded.","Her beautiful eyes widened slightly as she looked at the kneeling figures before her.","Even now, she still found everything difficult to believe.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader possessed status comparable to the Sect Leader of the Heavenly Sword Sect.","Someone she normally could only look up toward from afar.","As for Yu Longxuan, he was one of the empire’s princes.","A figure capable of shaking countless clans with a single command.","Yet now, both of them were kneeling before her in fear.","Trying desperately to gain her forgiveness.","Fei Ling suddenly felt as though everything before her resembled a dream.","And deep down, she understood clearly, this was all because of one person.","Her gaze unconsciously shifted toward Bai Zihan standing calmly in the skies.","At this moment, Bai Zihan’s expression remained indifferent from beginning to end.","As though forcing a prince and a peak sect leader to kneel was merely something insignificant to him.","(Thank you!)","Fei Ling silently spoke within her heart as she looked toward Bai Zihan.","Her emotions had already become extremely complicated.","Previously, whenever she looked at Bai Zihan, the first thing she felt was annoyance.","Especially because of his shameless teasing and flirtatious attitude toward her.","In her eyes back then, Bai Zihan was simply an arrogant and somewhat lecherous young master.","Yet now, that same person had personally brought the Bai Clan to stand behind her when the Fei Clan was at its most desperate moment.","Not only did he help them, he directly crushed the Crimson Thunder Palace and forced even the Seventh Prince to kneel before her.","Fei Ling had never expected Bai Zihan of all people would help her to such an extent.","And after today’s display of power, she was absolutely certain of one thing.","At least during the struggle for the throne, no one would dare target the Fei Clan again.","Not unless they wished to end up like the Crimson Thunder Palace.","Thinking about this, Fei Ling’s gaze unconsciously softened slightly as she looked at Bai Zihan.","For some reason...","The more she looked at him now, the more handsome he seemed.","Then Fei Ling’s eyes shifted toward the kneeling Yu Longxuan and the Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader.","Both figures lowered their heads before her with completely different attitudes from before, especially Yu Longxuan.","If Bai Zihan were in her position, he would definitely never let such an opportunity go so easily.","At the very least, he would squeeze every possible benefit from them before stopping.","However, Fei Ling was still Fei Ling.","Although she felt satisfied and somewhat exhilarated, she still understood reality clearly.","The current situation existed because of Bai Zihan.","This was borrowed power.","And although the Crimson Thunder Palace and Yu Longxuan were kneeling now, they still possessed terrifying status and influence within the empire.","If she pushed too far, who could guarantee they would not secretly retaliate in the future once this matter passed?","Especially Yu Longxuan.","No matter what, he was still a prince.","Thinking this, Fei Ling slowly took a deep breath before finally speaking.","\"This is already more than enough.\"","Her voice was soft, yet it echoed clearly throughout the battlefield.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader immediately revealed an expression of relief.","Even Yu Longxuan secretly relaxed slightly.","Meanwhile, Fei Ling turned toward Bai Zihan seriously.","Then she cupped her hands gently.","\"Thank you, Junior Brother.\"","This time, her gratitude was completely sincere.","Without Bai Zihan, the Fei Clan would likely have already fallen into despair by now.","At this moment, Bai Zihan looked toward Fei Ling briefly.","Seeing the complicated emotions within her eyes, the corners of his lips curved upward faintly.","Then he calmly nodded.","\"Since Senior Sister Fei is satisfied...\"","His gaze slowly swept across the kneeling Crimson Thunder Palace experts.","\"I shall spare you once!\""]},{"number":606,"title":"Chapter 606: The Uncontrollable Variable","paragraphs":["Every prince and princess immediately received reports of the Bai Clan attacking the Crimson Thunder Palace.","After all, during the struggle for the throne, each faction constantly kept spies watching one another.","Countless expressions changed drastically after receiving the news.","Some princes and princesses secretly felt relieved.","Fortunately, they had restrained themselves previously and did not rashly move against the Neutral Alliance clans.","Otherwise, the current situation of the Crimson Thunder Palace might very well have become their own.","Others, however, were shocked beyond belief.","None of them had expected the Bai Clan to go this far for the Fei Clan.","Launching a direct assault against a Top Sect over a First-Rate Clan?","Such behavior was practically unheard of within the empire.","Originally, many believed Bai Zihan would at most issue a warning or force the Crimson Thunder Palace to compensate the Fei Clan.","But instead, The Bai Clan directly mobilized their army and attacked.","Naturally, despite the shock, many factions also felt delighted inwardly.","After all, the Crimson Thunder Palace stood firmly on the Seventh Prince’s side.","Seeing one of their rivals suffer such a devastating blow was naturally something worth celebrating.","Soon after, another piece of information arrived.","And the moment the various princes and princesses saw it, even the calmest among them nearly lost composure.","Fourteen Immortal Realm experts.","Five Earth Immortals!","Nine Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators!","The moment that lineup became known, the entire Imperial Family seemed to fall into temporary silence.","Not to mention, that not every Immortal Realm Cultivator was present like Bai Ren or Bai Chu.","That meant what the Bai Clan brought out wasn’t even their full force.","One clan possessed such terrifying strength?","Inside the First Prince’s residence, the atmosphere had already become incomparably heavy.","Yu Zidi slowly lowered the intelligence report within his hand.","His expression looked extremely gloomy despite his takeover of the Imperial Court.","Looking at the strength of the Bai Clan, it is definitely almost invincible and there was no one who could compete with them in the Desolate Heaven Empire.","The more Yu Zidi thought about it, the colder his heart became.","If the Bai Clan continued developing at this speed, then even after he became Emperor, he might only remain Emperor in name.","The true authority of the empire might gradually shift elsewhere.","Thinking this, a cold light flashed across Yu Tiancheng’s eyes.","\"The Bai Clan...\"","He slowly tightened his grip over the report.","\"They absolutely cannot continue growing unchecked.\"","His determination to suppress the Bai Clan burned even stronger. No matter whether he would need help or not, he must have the Vermillion Pill Empire deal with the Bai Clan.","With the two Empires working together, he refuses to believe that he can’t handle a single Clan.","Many people quickly received another report afterward.","The Crimson Thunder Palace had been defeated completely.","The Seventh Prince was forced to kneel.","The entire sect was nearly destroyed.","Although many were not surprised by the result after seeing the Bai Clan’s terrifying lineup, their hearts still trembled once the outcome was confirmed.","However, some people secretly felt pity.","\"What a shame! If Bai Zihan had completely destroyed the Crimson Thunder Palace or killed Yu Longxuan directly, it would have been even better.\"","Since that wasn’t achieved, this meant that the Seventh Prince was still in the race for the throne.","Although the Crimson Thunder Palace suffered huge losses, they were still a Top Sect and many Princes and Princesses didn’t have the power to compete even with such an injured force.","Still, regardless of personal thoughts, one thing became completely clear to everyone after this battle.","The Bai Clan could no longer be provoked casually.","Not a single prince or princess dared think of targeting the Neutral Alliance clans anymore.","***","Far away from the chaos surrounding the Crimson Thunder Palace, inside an elegant palace hidden beneath the quiet moonlight, the atmosphere remained calm and tranquil.","Soft incense drifted slowly through the room.","A beautiful woman dressed in luxurious crimson robes sat beside a jade table quietly drinking tea.","Her movements were graceful and refined.","As though nothing within the outside world could truly disturb her emotions.","This person was naturally the Ninth Princess, Yu Feiyan.","Or perhaps more accurately—","Qin Lingxiao!","A subordinate dressed in black robes knelt respectfully before her while reporting everything that had occurred at the Crimson Thunder Palace in detail.","From the Bai Clan’s mobilization...","To the overwhelming suppression...","And finally, the Seventh Prince kneeling beneath Bai Zihan’s pressure.","Only after the report completely ended did silence return to the room once more.","Yu Feiyan slowly placed her teacup down.","A faint ripple finally appeared within her otherwise calm eyes.","\"This Bai Clan...\"","Her voice sounded soft and thoughtful.","\"They are much stronger than our previous reports suggested.\"","The subordinate immediately lowered his head further.","\"Yes, Your Highness. Our earlier investigations indeed did not uncover strength at this level.\"","His expression also looked somewhat grave.","\"Especially the number of Immortal Realm experts.\"","The subordinate hesitated briefly before continuing carefully.","\"There are only two possibilities. Either the Bai Clan concealed their true strength, so much so that we were deceived previously Or their growth truly occurred within this recent period.\"","Between the two, they thought that it was more likely to be the former than the latter.","However, they also can’t deny the possibility because of the Mu Clan who has recently broken through and is able to produce Grade-7 pills.","With their help, there was a possibility that the Bai Clan had become much stronger during this period.","But just Grade-7 pills weren’t enough to make such a big difference.","After all, growth of this magnitude within such a short period of time was simply too terrifying.","Even with the Qin Clan’s support, they didn’t think that any Clan could grow as much as the Bai Clan did in recent periods.","Yu Feiyan gently tapped her fingers against the jade table.","Her beautiful eyes narrowed faintly.","Whether it was concealment or sudden growth, neither possibility was good news.","Because regardless of the process, the result remained the same.","The Bai Clan was becoming too powerful.","And unlike the other ambitious factions within the empire, the Bai Clan was even more difficult to predict.","Especially Bai Zihan himself.","Thinking about him, a faint smile slowly formed on Yu Feiyan’s lips.","In the long centuries she had lived, she had encountered countless geniuses.","Peerless talents.","Monstrous cultivators.","Scheming rulers.","Even heaven-defying figures capable of shaking entire eras.","Yet Bai Zihan was the first person she genuinely found difficult to see through.","The more Qin Lingxiao observed him, the more interested she became.","Her beautiful eyes gradually deepened.","\"Interesting...\"","She softly murmured.","\"Very interesting!\"","The subordinate remained kneeling silently.","He did not dare interrupt her thoughts.","After a long while, Qin Lingxiao finally smiled faintly once more.","Qin Lingxiao slowly leaned back against her chair.","The faint smile upon her lips deepened slightly.","Originally, when she first arrived within the Desolate Heaven Empire, she had viewed this mission as little more than a simple task.","A remote empire.","To someone of her status and background, such a place should have been easy to manipulate.","Yet now, things had become far more interesting than she expected.","A trace of amusement flashed across Qin Lingxiao’s eyes.","\"Who would have thought...\"","She softly muttered.","\"That a remote empire like this could actually produce such surprises.\"","Her fingers lightly tapped against the jade table rhythmically.","Bai Zihan!","The Bai Clan!","The Mu Clan!","The increasingly unstable situation within the empire.","Everything was gradually moving beyond her initial expectations.","For countless years, almost everything around Qin Lingxiao had remained within her calculations and expectations.","Very few things could genuinely surprise her anymore.","Yet this time...","The Desolate Heaven Empire had unexpectedly become one of those rare exceptions.","Soon, however, the amusement within her eyes gradually faded slightly.","Her expression became thoughtful once more.","Then she suddenly asked calmly:","\"When can Father send more people?\"","Asking for reinforcements...","For Qin Lingxiao herself, this was already somewhat embarrassing.","After all, before arriving here, she had been completely confident in handling everything personally.","But now, the situation has changed.","If she wanted to continue operating silently without exposing her true strength too early...","Then she needed more support.","The subordinate lowered his head respectfully before answering carefully.","\"It may still take some time, Young Miss. Patriarch Qin currently cannot move too openly.\"","His expression became slightly solemn.","\"The other Great Clans have already begun paying close attention to our movements.\"","Qin Lingxiao slowly nodded.","Naturally, she already understood this clearly.","Which was exactly why the Qin Clan could not move recklessly.","Otherwise, once the other Great clans noticed something first, the situation would become troublesome.","After remaining silent briefly, Qin Lingxiao asked another question.","\"Then how many people have already infiltrated the Desolate Heaven Empire?\"","The subordinate answered immediately.","\"Approximately 5!\"","Hearing this number, Qin Lingxiao’s beautiful brows frowned slightly.","Five people from the Central Continent have already infiltrated the Desolate Heaven Empire.","That just means more variables have arrived.","After a long moment, Qin Lingxiao slowly exhaled.","Then she suddenly laughed softly.","\"Looks like we’ll need to speed up this stupid struggle for the throne.\"","Her beautiful eyes narrowed faintly.","\"Otherwise...\"","A dangerous glint flashed across them briefly.","\"Others may end up reaping the rewards for my hard work.\""]},{"number":607,"title":"Chapter 607: The Third Prince’s Offensive","paragraphs":["Within only a few days after the destruction of the Crimson Thunder Palace’s prestige, the situation throughout the empire changed once more.","And this time, the one making the largest moves was the Ninth Princess.","Yu Feiyan’s faction suddenly began expanding at astonishing speed.","One force after another fell beneath her control.","Third-rate sects.","Second-rate clans.","Even several First-Rate Clans eventually chose to submit.","Her expansion speed was so fast that it shocked countless people.","Unlike the Seventh Prince’s previous methods, however, Yu Feiyan’s approach appeared far more refined and efficient.","Almost all forces seemed to willingly join her faction after a single discussion.","They even seemed willing to throw away their lives for her cause, which many found strange.","After all, many forces that are forced to submit would naturally hold grudges against the prince or princess they followed, even if they outwardly obeyed.","And if the opportunity ever appeared, they would immediately flee.","Most of the time, they also would not give their full effort because, in the end, they were forced into submission.","However, the Ninth Princess’s forces were different.","It was as though every one of them was ready to give everything, including their lives.","Such loyalty normally could not be achieved unless both sides had worked together for many years and built deep trust.","Naturally, many people also quickly noticed something strange.","Throughout all her expansion...","Yu Feiyan intentionally avoided every force belonging to the Neutral Alliance.","All of them remained completely untouched despite lying directly within several regions Yu Feiyan expanded through.","Others believed that the Ninth Princess wanted to avoid confronting the Bai Clan and ending up like the Seventh Prince.","But Bai Zihan knew that with Qin Lingxiao’s abilities, if she truly wished to bring a clan under her control, she could easily make them willingly submit.","There would be no need to confront the Neutral Alliance directly.","After all, if the other party willingly joined her, then what justification could the Neutral Alliance use to interfere?","Yet she wasn’t doing that.","Instead, she deliberately avoided the Neutral Alliance altogether.","Perhaps she wanted to avoid being targeted by the Bai Clan.","Or perhaps she wanted others to lower their guard by making it seem as though she feared the Bai Clan.","Despite that, her faction continued growing larger and larger.","However, what surprised many people even more was the reaction of the other princes and princesses.","Or rather—","The lack of reaction.","Originally, countless people believed the First Prince, Third Prince, or Fourth Princess would immediately move to suppress Yu Feiyan’s rapidly growing influence.","Yet unexpectedly...","None of them did.","Instead, they also suddenly began expanding aggressively themselves.","The First Prince rapidly annexed multiple sects and clans loyal to weaker princes.","The Third Prince launched several swift offensives across the western regions.","It was as though the strongest contenders had silently reached some kind of understanding.","Rather than clashing against each other immediately...","They first chose to eliminate the weaker competitors.","And under the pressure of these monsters, the smaller princes and princesses quickly collapsed one after another.","Some were forced to submit.","Others abandoned their territories and fled entirely.","As for several unfortunate ones, even their fate became unknown.","Perhaps they had already died silently somewhere within the shadows of the throne war.","Within only a short period of time, the struggle for the throne had already entered an entirely new stage.","The weak were rapidly being eliminated.","And eventually, only five remained standing within the struggle for the throne.","The First Prince!","The Third Prince!","The Fourth Princess!","The Seventh Prince!","And the Ninth Princess.","These five had become the final competitors for the empire’s supreme seat.","However, although the Seventh Prince still technically remained within the race, most people already believed he had effectively lost.","After all, the blow suffered at the Crimson Thunder Palace had been far too severe.","His greatest supporter had nearly been destroyed entirely by the Bai Clan.","Even now, the Crimson Thunder Palace still remained in recovery.","Their prestige had also fallen tremendously after being publicly crushed beneath the Bai Clan’s feet.","Meanwhile, while the Seventh Prince struggled to recover, the other competitors had all expanded rapidly.","Compared to them, Yu Longxuan now looked increasingly weak.","And in the current situation, weakness itself was a crime.","Especially because despite his decline, the Seventh Prince still possessed many clans and sects beneath his banner.","To the other competitors, those forces were no longer viewed as allies of the Seventh Prince.","They were prey.","And among the remaining competitors, the Third Prince was the first to move.","Inside a massive camp, Yu Wenzhao calmly stared at the map before him.","Several regions beneath the Seventh Prince’s control had already been marked clearly.","A faint cold smile appeared upon his face.","For a long time already, he had been eyeing Yu Longxuan’s territory.","Especially because the territories controlled by both sides bordered each other closely.","Originally, Yu Wenzhao still maintained some caution because of the Crimson Thunder Palace’s existence.","After all, he had once believed himself to possess the advantage, only to still suffer defeat.","That experience had made him much more cautious.","But now?","The Crimson Thunder Palace had already been crippled by the Bai Clan.","This was the perfect opportunity.","\"How unfortunate for Seventh Brother...\"","Yu Wenzhao softly muttered.","The current Seventh Prince no longer possessed the qualifications to continue competing equally against the top contenders.","Soon afterward, the Third Prince’s forces officially launched their offensive.","One clan after another loyal to the Seventh Prince was attacked.","Some chose to surrender immediately after seeing the overwhelming pressure.","Others resisted briefly before being crushed.","Within only a few days, multiple territories formerly under Yu Longxuan’s influence changed ownership entirely.","The Seventh Prince’s faction began shrinking rapidly.","And the most terrifying part was that the other remaining competitors did not interfere.","The First Prince remained silent.","The Fourth Princess continued consolidating her own forces.","The Ninth Princess merely watched calmly while continuing her own expansion.","No one intended to help Yu Longxuan or stop the Third Prince.","Only the Crimson Thunder Palace remained.","Everything else beneath the Seventh Prince’s banner had already been devoured completely by the Third Prince.","And now, the Third Prince’s eyes finally landed upon the Crimson Thunder Palace itself.","Yu Wenzhao’s gaze remained fixed upon the region occupied by the Crimson Thunder Palace.","Behind him stood numerous experts.","The pressure filling the hall alone was enough to suffocate ordinary cultivators.","Compared to before, the Third Prince’s forces had clearly expanded tremendously.","Especially after annexing large portions of the Seventh Prince’s territory.","At this moment, his side alone already possessed:","One Earth Immortal Realm expert!","Seven Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators!","And numerous Great Ascension Realm elders.","Such a lineup was already enough to crush most top factions within the empire.","Not to mention, the current Crimson Thunder Palace was no longer at its peak.","Under normal circumstances, Yu Wenzhao’s current force would absolutely be enough to destroy the Crimson Thunder Palace completely.","However, Yu Wenzhao still did not act recklessly.","Because no matter how weakened the Crimson Thunder Palace had become...","An injured camel was still larger than a horse.","The Crimson Thunder Palace was still a Top Sect with thousands of years of foundation.","No one knew exactly how many hidden cards they still possessed.","Especially cornered beasts were often the most dangerous.","Yu Wenzhao had already learned that lesson once before.","He would not underestimate anyone again.","The Heaven Suppression Pavilion elder beside him slowly spoke.","\"Your Highness, the Crimson Thunder Palace is already severely weakened. Most of their experts suffered injuries during the Bai Clan battle.\"","\"If we attack now, victory should not be difficult.\"","The Heaven Suppression Pavilion elders were excited since this was a golden opportunity.","By defeating the Crimson Thunder Palace, not only would that increase their chances of winning the throne, but the Heaven Suppression Pavilion would also become even more powerful.","Perhaps by then, it might even become the number one sect within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Thinking about that, many of them felt that joining the Third Prince had truly been the correct decision.","Yu Wenzhao nodded slightly.","\"However, the Crimson Thunder Palace is already desperate. If we pressure them too heavily, they may choose mutual destruction instead.\"","Although the Crimson Thunder Palace was weakened, if a Top Sect truly fought desperately before destruction, even the victor would suffer heavy losses.","And right now, the throne war has already reached its final stage.","The remaining competitors were not easy opponents.","The First Prince!","The Fourth Princess!","The Ninth Princess!","At this stage, any major losses could become fatal later.","Yu Wenzhao slowly narrowed his eyes.","Thinking this, he slowly tapped the table.","\"We will attack!\"","His voice echoed calmly.","\"But not recklessly. We will surround the Crimson Thunder Palace first. Cut off all their external support.\"","His eyes gradually turned cold.","\"Pressure them continuously and only when they can no longer resist...\"","Yu Wenzhao’s lips slowly curved upward faintly.","\"Then we finish them in one strike!\""]},{"number":608,"title":"Chapter 608: A Broken Throne Dream","paragraphs":["Inside the Crimson Thunder Palace, the atmosphere had already become incomparably oppressive.","Ever since the Third Prince began his offensive, attacks constantly erupted across the surrounding territories.","Although the Third Prince’s forces never launched a full-scale assault directly against the Crimson Thunder Palace, everyone understood clearly what Yu Wenzhao was trying to do.","He was exhausting them slowly.","Like a predator cornering wounded prey.","BOOM!","Another explosion echoed outside one of the outer defensive regions.","Several Crimson Thunder Palace disciples hurried back while covered in blood.","\"They retreated again!\"","An elder’s expression immediately darkened further.","Again!","Every single time, it was the same.","The Third Prince’s forces would suddenly launch attacks from several directions, pressure them heavily, force them to mobilize experts...","Then immediately withdraw before a decisive clash could occur.","At first, many within the Crimson Thunder Palace were furious.","However, after several days passed, that fury gradually transformed into exhaustion and helplessness.","Because everyone knew the truth.","Yu Wenzhao was intentionally dragging things out.","And unfortunately, it was working perfectly.","The Crimson Thunder Palace had already suffered enormous losses after the Bai Clan battle.","Many elders were still injured.","Countless disciples remained mentally shaken.","Resources had also been depleted tremendously.","Under such circumstances, constantly remaining on high alert while facing endless harassment only worsened their condition further.","Yet despite understanding everything clearly, there was nothing they could do.","Attack the Third Prince directly?","That would simply mean walking straight into a trap.","Yu Wenzhao was obviously waiting for exactly that.","But if they remained inside the sect and continued defending passively, then their eventual defeat was inevitable.","A heavy silence filled the main hall.","Many elders clenched their fists unwillingly.","Their expressions looked incomparably ugly.","Everyone understood the current situation clearly.","There was no longer any way to turn things around.","However, no one dared say those words aloud because Yu Longxuan was still present.","The Seventh Prince sat quietly at the highest seat within the hall.","Compared to before, his entire aura had changed drastically.","The arrogance and confidence he once possessed had almost completely disappeared.","What remained now was exhaustion and bitterness.","For a long time, Yu Longxuan remained completely silent.","The hall was so quiet that even breathing could be heard clearly.","Finally—","Sigh!","A deep sigh slowly escaped his mouth.","Then Yu Longxuan slowly raised his head.","His voice sounded somewhat hoarse.","\"Let’s just surrender!\"","The moment those words fell, the entire hall instantly erupted into chaos.","\"Prince!\"","Several elders immediately stood up in shock.","Even the Crimson Thunder Palace disciples widened their eyes in disbelief.","Surrender?","Those words had never once existed within Yu Longxuan’s vocabulary before.","This was the same Seventh Prince who refused to bow even when facing Bai Zihan and the Bai Clan’s overwhelming suppression.","Even when the Crimson Thunder Palace was nearly destroyed...","Even when he himself had been forced to kneel publicly...","Yu Longxuan still never admitted defeat.","Yet now, he was personally telling them to surrender.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader’s expression changed repeatedly.","\"Your Highness...\"","His voice trembled slightly.","Yu Longxuan slowly closed his eyes.","At this moment, he finally understood something clearly.","He no longer possessed any chance at the throne.","None at all!","Originally, even after the Bai Clan incident, a small part of him still believed he could recover somehow.","After all, he still possessed the Crimson Thunder Palace.","He still possessed supporters.","He still possessed influence.","But now?","Reality had crushed those final illusions completely.","The Third Prince was devouring his remaining forces rapidly.","And most importantly, the Crimson Thunder Palace itself was already broken.","Even if they survived this crisis somehow, they no longer possessed the qualifications to compete against the remaining princes and princesses within the throne war.","Yu Longxuan slowly clenched his fists tightly.","Blood dripped faintly from his palms.","Humiliation!","Unwillingness!","Hatred!","All of it churned violently within his heart.","Yet in the end, it all transformed into helplessness.","Surrendering was their only option.","At least, the Crimson Thunder Palace wouldn’t be affected too much.","If they surrendered, Yu Wenzhao would not destroy the Crimson Thunder Palace.","He still needed the Crimson Thunder Palace.","For the remaining throne war, he required every bit of strength he could gather. So, if the Crimson Thunder Palace surrendered, he would merely force them to join his side.","Otherwise, if things were pushed to the extreme, the Crimson Thunder Palace could still resist desperately and inflict heavy losses upon him.","The Crimson Thunder Palace might have been crippled heavily, but it still possessed thousands of years of foundation.","There was simply no reason for him to destroy the Crimson Thunder Palace completely.","However, Yu Longxuan’s expression gradually became colder.","It was a different story for himself though.","A faint self-mocking smile appeared on his face.","As long as he remained alive, he would always remain a potential threat.","Even if he had already lost the fight for the throne, no ruler would willingly leave behind a prince who could still claim the throne.","So, his fate would either be death or something worse.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader’s expression became extremely complicated.","He naturally understood that surrendering truly was the best outcome for the sect.","Otherwise, continuing this battle would only lead to destruction sooner or later.","But for Yu Longxuan, this decision was undoubtedly cruel.","After all, the moment the Crimson Thunder Palace surrendered, it would essentially abandon the Seventh Prince completely.","The Sect Leader hesitated briefly before asking solemnly,","\"Your Highness... are you certain?\"","Yu Longxuan remained silent for several moments.","Then he slowly nodded.","\"I am!\"","His voice carried exhaustion, but also resolution.","\"There is no other choice left.\"","The Sect Leader closed his eyes briefly.","Then after a long silence, he finally sighed deeply.","\"...Very well.\"","The moment those words fell, many elders revealed complicated expressions.","Some felt relief.","Others felt guilt.","But no one objected.","The Crimson Thunder Palace could still survive, but only if they surrendered now.","The Sect Leader slowly turned his head toward one of the Grand Elders standing nearby.","The Sect Leader cupped his hands solemnly.","\"Grand Elder, I ask you to personally escort His Highness away from the Empire.\"","The Immortal Ascension Grand Elder fell silent briefly before nodding heavily.","\"I understand!\"","Yu Longxuan quietly watched everything unfold.","His expression became increasingly bitter.","Once upon a time, countless experts willingly gathered beneath his banner.","He believed himself destined to ascend the throne.","Yet now, he had reached the point where he needed to flee like a defeated dog.","The contrast was almost laughable.","But deep within his heart, another figure unconsciously appeared once more.","Bai Zihan!","Yu Longxuan slowly lowered his head.","If not for that battle...","If not for provoking the Bai Clan...","Would things really have ended like this?","Well, who knows?","The Grand Elder slowly stepped forward.","His aged face looked solemn as he cupped his hands toward Yu Longxuan.","\"Your Highness...\"","His deep voice echoed softly within the hall.","\"We should leave now.\"","Yu Longxuan remained silent briefly.","Then he slowly nodded.","\"...Alright!\"","There was no hesitation anymore.","No anger.","No struggle.","Yu Longxuan slowly swept his gaze across the familiar hall one final time.","This place once gathered countless ambitious experts beneath him.","Everyone believed he possessed a real chance to ascend the throne.","But now?","Everything had crumbled completely.","Then without another word, Yu Longxuan turned and walked away.","The Grand Elder followed closely behind him.","Soon, both figures gradually disappeared into the deeper regions of the Crimson Thunder Palace.","Watching their departure, the Sect Leader slowly closed his eyes.","A heavy sigh escaped his mouth.","Then his expression gradually became firm once more.","Now that the Seventh Prince had left, it was time for the Crimson Thunder Palace to survive.","The Sect Leader immediately began issuing orders.","\"All disciples are to stand down. No one is allowed to provoke the Third Prince’s forces.\"","Numerous elders quickly nodded.","However, they still did not surrender immediately.","They needed to give Yu Longxuan enough time to escape far away.","If they surrendered right now, the Third Prince might immediately send people to search for him.","Catching him now would be easy.","But if an hour passed first, then tracking him down would become nearly impossible unless someone knew his destination beforehand.","Thus, another hour passed quietly.","Outside the Crimson Thunder Palace, the Third Prince’s forces launched another round of attacks as usual.","Several experts descended from the skies while pressuring the outer defensive formations continuously.","BOOM!","A massive explosion shook the mountains.","The Third Prince’s cultivators immediately prepared themselves for another prolonged confrontation.","However, this time, something was different.","The defensive formations of the Crimson Thunder Palace slowly weakened.","Then gradually dispersed completely.","Countless gazes immediately sharpened.","Soon afterward, numerous figures flew out from within the Crimson Thunder Palace.","At the front stood the Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader alongside several elders.","Seeing this scene, many of the Third Prince’s forces immediately became vigilant.","Their expressions turned cold.","They thought the Crimson Thunder Palace had finally decided to launch a desperate counterattack.","Several Great Ascension experts even began circulating their Qi fully.","However, contrary to everyone’s expectations, The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader suddenly stopped in midair.","Then before countless stunned gazes...","He slowly cupped his hands and bowed deeply toward the Third Prince’s army.","\"The Crimson Thunder Palace...\"","His voice echoed clearly across the battlefield.","\"...Surrenders!\""]},{"number":609,"title":"Chapter 609: The Prince Who Lost Everything","paragraphs":["The moment the Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader publicly declared their surrender, the atmosphere within the Third Prince’s camp immediately erupted.","Countless disciples and elders revealed excited expressions.","Some even laughed openly.","\"We won!\"","\"The Crimson Thunder Palace surrendered!\"","\"Hahaha! The Seventh Prince is finished!\"","...","For many of them, this was an enormous victory.","The Crimson Thunder Palace was a Top Sect that had stood proudly within the empire for thousands of years.","Now, it had finally lowered its head before the Third Prince.","This meant that Yu Wenzhao’s influence would rise to an entirely new level.","Even the Immortals from the Heaven Suppression Pavilion looked extremely delighted.","After all, once the Crimson Thunder Palace joined their side, the Third Prince’s overall strength would increase tremendously.","Meanwhile, high above the battlefield, Yu Wenzhao himself also revealed a faint smile.","However, unlike the others, his eyes still remained cold and cautious.","He did not lower his guard in the slightest.","Because he understood clearly that a wounded beast was often the most dangerous before death.","The Crimson Thunder Palace had surrendered too easily according to his expectations.","That alone made him wary.","Yu Wenzhao slowly narrowed his eyes before calmly giving an order.","\"Seal their meridians first!\"","The excited atmosphere immediately quieted slightly.","Several elders quickly cupped their hands.","\"Yes, Your Highness!\"","Soon afterward, multiple elders stepped forward cautiously toward the Crimson Thunder Palace elders and Grand Elders.","Their qi circulated fully.","Clearly, they remained prepared for a sudden ambush at any moment.","Even Yu Wenzhao’s gaze never left the Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader.","After all, if the other party truly intended to fight desperately now, the losses would still be severe.","However—","To everyone’s surprise, no one resisted.","Not even slightly.","The Crimson Thunder Palace elders quietly allowed their meridians to be sealed one after another.","Even the Grand Elders remained silent throughout the process.","Seeing this scene, many of the Third Prince’s experts secretly relaxed.","Yu Wenzhao’s eyes flickered faintly.","It seemed the Crimson Thunder Palace had truly given up.","As for the ordinary disciples, Yu Wenzhao did not bother sealing them.","They were simply too weak to threaten him and far too numerous to waste time sealing individually.","And right now, he did not wish to waste unnecessary time.","Soon afterward, Yu Wenzhao personally led his forces into the Crimson Thunder Palace.","Behind him followed numerous experts alongside the surrendered elders who now resembled prisoners of war more than respected elders of a prestigious sect.","The once lofty Crimson Thunder Palace now appeared incomparably bleak.","Soon, the group entered the main hall.","Yu Wenzhao’s gaze immediately swept across the surroundings sharply.","Then his brows slowly furrowed.","Because one person was missing.","Yu Longxuan!","The Third Prince’s expression gradually turned cold.","He immediately looked toward the Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader.","\"Where is Seventh Brother?\"","The atmosphere instantly became tense once more.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader lowered his head slightly before answering honestly.","\"His Highness... has already abandoned the Crimson Thunder Palace and fled.\"","His voice sounded bitter.","\"That is also the reason why we chose to surrender.\"","Silence filled the hall briefly.","Yu Wenzhao narrowed his eyes.","Abandoned them?","He didn’t know whether those words were true or if they planned for him to escape.","But regardless of the reasoning behind it, one fact remained unchanged.","Yu Longxuan had escaped.","And Yu Wenzhao absolutely could not allow that.","A cold light flashed across his eyes instantly.","\"Find him!\"","His voice echoed sharply throughout the hall.","\"Whether dead or alive, I want Seventh Brother brought before me!\"","The surrounding experts immediately bowed.","\"Yes, Your Highness!\"","In an instant, multiple figures shot out from the Crimson Thunder Palace at terrifying speed.","Search teams immediately spread throughout the surrounding regions.","Meanwhile, Yu Wenzhao slowly stood within the hall silently.","His expression looked incomparably cold.","He had already reached this stage.","There was absolutely no way he would leave behind any future problems.","Several hours quickly passed.","Search teams continuously returned one after another from every direction surrounding the Crimson Thunder Palace.","However, every single report carried the same result.","Nothing!","\"There are no traces of the Seventh Prince.\"","\"We searched the northern regions thoroughly. No fluctuations were left behind.\"","\"The southern search team also found nothing.\"","Even the Immortal Ascension experts sent personally by Yu Wenzhao returned empty-handed.","Inside the main hall, the atmosphere gradually became somewhat heavy.","Soon, one Heaven Suppression Pavilion elder slowly spoke solemnly.","\"Your Highness, the Seventh Prince was most likely escorted away personally by an Immortal Realm expert skilled in spatial movement.\"","\"After all, who knows how many hours have already passed since they left. If the other party continuously tore through space while erasing their traces, tracking them now would be almost impossible.\"","The surrounding elders nodded grimly.","That explanation made the most sense.","Once an Immortal Realm cultivator fully concealed themselves while escaping through spatial tears, finding them afterward would become extraordinarily difficult unless one knew their exact destination beforehand.","At this point, even the remaining qi traces had already dissipated completely.","Yu Wenzhao quietly listened to the reports.","His eyes narrowed faintly.","However, contrary to everyone’s expectations, he did not become furious.","Instead, he remained surprisingly calm.","After several moments of silence, Yu Wenzhao slowly spoke.","\"It doesn’t matter.\"","His tone sounded indifferent.","Yu Longxuan had already lost everything.","His forces had all been taken away, including the Crimson Thunder Palace.","What threat could he still pose now?","Now, he was merely a fugitive prince without any foundation remaining.","Even if he survived, it would be difficult for him to rise again.","Yu Wenzhao slowly leaned back against his seat.","(Still...)","A dangerous light flashed across his eyes.","(If he dares show himself again in the future, then I will kill him personally!)","Soon afterward, Yu Wenzhao no longer wasted thoughts on Yu Longxuan.","Instead, his attention shifted toward the Crimson Thunder Palace experts standing below.","Although they had surrendered, Yu Wenzhao naturally would not trust them completely so easily.","However, he was already testing them, and during the past several hours, they had done nothing suspicious, proving they truly had no hidden agenda.","Yu Wenzhao’s expression gradually became imposing once more.","\"You only have two choices.\"","His calm voice echoed clearly throughout the hall.","\"Follow me wholeheartedly from today onward...\"","\"Or the Crimson Thunder Palace will disappear entirely from this empire.\"","The Crimson Thunder Palace Sect Leader lowered his head slowly.","\"We understand.\"","His voice sounded bitter yet respectful.","\"From today onward, the Crimson Thunder Palace is willing to follow Your Highness.\"","The surrounding elders also lowered their heads one after another.","No one resisted.","Because they had already known this would be their only choice the moment they surrendered.","Yu Wenzhao quietly observed them for several moments before finally nodding faintly.","Then he slowly turned his gaze toward the distant horizon outside the hall.","His eyes gradually sharpened.","The Seventh Prince had already fallen.","Now, only the true competitors remained.","The First Prince!","The Fourth Princess!","The Ninth Princess!","Among them, the one he wanted to crush the most was naturally the First Prince.","A cold smile slowly appeared on Yu Wenzhao’s face.","\"First Brother...\"","His voice echoed softly within the hall.","\"Soon you will be next!\"","***","Far away, two figures moved rapidly through the endless skies.","Space itself distorted repeatedly around them.","Each step crossed countless miles instantly.","The surrounding scenery blurred continuously as mountains, rivers, and forests flashed past beneath them at terrifying speed.","The one leading was naturally the Crimson Thunder Palace Grand Elder.","His expression remained extremely solemn.","Even now, he did not dare lower his guard in the slightest.","Every so often, he would directly tear apart space once more before changing directions abruptly.","At the same time, he continuously erased the qi fluctuations left behind by their movements.","Clearly, he feared the Third Prince’s forces tracking them down.","Meanwhile, behind him, Yu Longxuan followed silently.","Unlike before, the lofty aura surrounding the Seventh Prince had almost completely disappeared.","At this moment, he looked more like a defeated cultivator wandering aimlessly through the world.","Only after several more hours passed did the Grand Elder finally slow down gradually.","The surrounding area had already become completely unfamiliar.","Towering mountain ranges stretched endlessly beneath the night sky.","Not a single trace of human presence could be sensed nearby.","The Grand Elder carefully swept his divine sense across the surroundings several times before finally exhaling deeply in relief.","\"We should be safe now, Your Highness.\"","His aged voice sounded somewhat tired.","\"We have already traveled far enough. Even if the Third Prince sent Immortal Realm experts after us, they should no longer be able to track our traces.\"","Yu Longxuan remained silent briefly before slowly nodding.","\"...Good!\"","However, despite those words, his eyes still looked somewhat empty.","The Grand Elder glanced toward him silently.","Naturally, he understood the Seventh Prince’s current state very well.","After all, Yu Longxuan had spent countless years preparing for the throne.","Everything he did...","Everything he lived for...","All of it revolved around becoming Emperor someday.","That goal had long since become the center of his life.","But now?","Everything he had lived for had collapsed completely.","Even if he survived...","What reason did he still have to continue living?"]},{"number":610,"title":"Chapter 610: Yu Wenzhao’s Perfect Opportunity","paragraphs":["The Crimson Thunder Palace Grand Elder slowly exhaled heavily as he sat down against the tree trunk.","His face looked visibly pale.","Continuously tearing through space for such a long period while erasing their traces had exhausted an enormous amount of his qi.","Meanwhile, beside him, Yu Longxuan stood quietly beneath the night sky.","His expression remained somewhat absent-minded.","The Grand Elder glanced toward him before sighing softly.","\"Your Highness, once we recover, we can continue moving farther away from the empire.\"","Yu Longxuan nodded silently.","However, before either of them could speak further, a calm voice suddenly echoed through the forest.","\"So... you were hiding here?\"","The atmosphere instantly froze.","Yu Longxuan’s pupils contracted violently.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Grand Elder shot to his feet immediately.","BOOM!","His remaining qi erupted instinctively around him as his expression changed drastically.","\"Who?!\"","His voice echoed sharply through the forest.","At this moment, his heart had already sunk completely.","(Impossible!)","He had personally erased all traces along the way.","How could someone still track them here?","And worse—","After exhausting himself so heavily, he could barely display twenty percent of his full strength now.","If the opponent was an Immortal Realm expert, then they had absolutely no chance of escaping.","The surrounding forest remained silent briefly.","Then slowly, several figures emerged from the darkness.","The moment Yu Longxuan and the Grand Elder saw those faces, both of their expressions changed completely.","\"You?!\"","Yu Longxuan’s eyes widened in disbelief.","\"You... how could it be—\"","Unfortunately—","The newcomers gave them no chance to continue speaking.","BOOM!!!","A terrifying killing intent instantly erupted.","The entire forest trembled violently.","The Crimson Thunder Palace Grand Elder roared furiously as he tried to resist.","However, in his heavily weakened state, he simply could not withstand the overwhelming assault.","Blood exploded through the air.","Yu Longxuan’s expression twisted violently.","\"No—!\"","Before he could finish speaking, a cold blade pierced directly through his chest.","His body froze instantly.","His eyes widened unwillingly.","The aura surrounding the Seventh Prince rapidly dissipated.","Beside him, the Grand Elder’s body also crashed heavily onto the ground.","Silence returned to the forest once more.","Only the smell of blood lingered beneath the ancient tree.","The several figures quietly stood there for a moment.","Then one of them slowly stepped forward and carefully checked both corpses personally.","After confirming that their souls and life aura had completely vanished, he finally nodded slightly.","\"They’re dead.\"","Only then did the group finally relax.","Without another word, the figures quickly disappeared back into the darkness.","Soon, the forest became silent once more.","As though nothing had ever happened there at all.","***","Inside the Crimson Thunder Palace, the atmosphere had completely changed compared to before.","Now, the entire sect had fallen under the Third Prince’s control.","Yu Wenzhao stood at the highest point of the Crimson Thunder Palace overlooking the massive sect below.","Behind him stood numerous experts from both his original faction and the newly surrendered Crimson Thunder Palace.","Over the past few days, Yu Wenzhao had moved extremely quickly.","Not only did he fully consolidate the Crimson Thunder Palace into his faction, but he also directly took control of many of the sect’s resources and treasures.","Naturally, although the Crimson Thunder Palace elders felt bitter seeing thousands of years of accumulated wealth gradually being absorbed away, none of them dared object.","Because compared to destruction, this outcome was already far better.","Meanwhile, after fully integrating the Crimson Thunder Palace’s remaining strength, the Third Prince’s faction expanded once more.","At this moment, his side now possessed:","Two Earth Immortal Realm experts!","And nearly fifteen Immortal Realm cultivators overall!","Not to mention the countless Great Ascension Realm experts beneath them.","Just this lineup alone was already enough to make countless factions despair.","Even Yu Wenzhao himself gradually felt increasing confidence.","Compared to before, his current power had already risen tremendously.","At this stage, aside from the Top Three Clans and Sects, almost no force within the empire could suppress him completely anymore.","Inside the grand hall, numerous experts stood respectfully below.","Many of them carried excited expressions, especially the Heaven Suppression Pavilion elders.","After swallowing the Seventh Prince’s remaining foundation whole, their side had become one of the absolute strongest forces remaining within the throne war.","At this moment, a massive map floated before Yu Wenzhao.","Several territories across the empire had already been marked clearly.","The remaining competitors.","The First Prince.","The Fourth Princess.","The Ninth Princess.","Yu Wenzhao’s gaze slowly swept across each territory carefully.","However, his eyes only paused briefly upon the First Prince’s territory before moving away.","A faint cold smile appeared on his face.","\"The First Prince...\"","Yu Wenzhao softly muttered.","\"I’ll save him for last!\"","After all, among the remaining competitors, the First Prince still possessed the strongest foundation publicly.","If Yu Wenzhao clashed with him now, even victory would likely come at an enormous cost.","And at the current stage of the throne war, unnecessary losses were unacceptable, especially when there were still easier targets remaining.","Yu Wenzhao’s gaze slowly shifted elsewhere.","Toward the territories belonging to the Fourth Princess and Ninth Princess.","Yu Qingya has the support of The Frost Lily Pavilion!","One of the strongest sects within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Its foundation was extremely deep and mysterious.","In terms of overall strength, the Frost Lily Pavilion was almost equal to the Heaven Suppression Pavilion supporting Yu Wenzhao.","Neither side truly possessed an overwhelming advantage.","However, that was before the Crimson Thunder Palace joined him.","Now, everything was different.","Yu Wenzhao slowly leaned back against his seat.","With the Crimson Thunder Palace integrated into his faction, his current strength had already surpassed the Fourth Princess’s side by a noticeable margin.","Two Earth Immortals!","Nearly fifteen Immortal Realm experts.","With such terrifying power gathered beneath him, even the Frost Lily Pavilion would struggle to stop him now.","If he truly wished to crush Yu Qingya, it would no longer be difficult.","Still, Yu Wenzhao’s gaze gradually shifted once more.","Toward the Ninth Princess’s territory.","Yu Feiyan!","Her expansion speed had simply been too abnormal.","One force after another willingly joined beneath her banner almost effortlessly.","Even now, Yu Wenzhao still could not fully understand how she achieved it.","That unknown factor naturally made him wary.","However, after carefully analyzing her faction repeatedly, Yu Wenzhao still discovered one major weakness.","The Ninth Princess lacked top-level experts.","Unlike him or the Fourth Princess, Yu Feiyan did not possess an Earth Immortal Realm cultivator beneath her command.","And within the current stage of the throne war, Earth Immortals were absolute pillars capable of determining victory or defeat.","No matter how strange her methods were, without enough peak experts supporting her, she would eventually be crushed by overwhelming force.","Thinking about this, Yu Wenzhao slowly narrowed his eyes.","Compared to the heavily fortified First Prince or the Frost Lily Pavilion-backed Fourth Princess, the Ninth Princess appeared to be the easier target.","A faint smile slowly appeared on his face.","\"We’ll deal with Yu Feiyan first!\"","The surrounding elders immediately exchanged glances.","Many nodded secretly in agreement.","After all, although the Ninth Princess’s growth was alarming, her foundation still appeared weaker than the others.","If they moved quickly enough, they could likely eliminate her before she became an even greater problem.","However, just as Yu Wenzhao was preparing to issue further orders—","Suddenly, a figure rushed hurriedly into the hall.","\"Your Highness!\"","The man’s voice sounded urgent.","He quickly knelt before Yu Wenzhao.","\"Urgent news!\"","Yu Wenzhao’s eyes narrowed faintly.","\"Speak!\"","The expert swallowed slightly before answering quickly.","\"The Ninth Princess has made their move! She personally led her forces and attacked the Frost Lily Pavilion!\"","The entire hall instantly fell silent.","\"What?!\"","Several elders exclaimed immediately.","Even Yu Wenzhao’s expression changed slightly.","The Frost Lily Pavilion?","Yu Feiyan attacked Yu Qingya first?","For a moment, even Yu Wenzhao himself looked somewhat stunned.","Because no matter how he viewed the situation, the Fourth Princess should have been one of the hardest opponents to deal with.","Yet the Ninth Princess had directly chosen to attack her first.","Was she crazy?","Or...","Did she possess some kind of confidence no one else knew about?","Yu Wenzhao’s eyes gradually became serious.","The moment the news settled fully within the hall, the atmosphere immediately changed.","Originally, many elders still felt confused by Yu Feiyan’s sudden actions.","But after thinking carefully, numerous people quickly reacted.","And soon, excitement appeared across several faces.","Because regardless of Yu Feiyan’s intentions, one fact remained undeniable.","The Ninth Princess and Fourth Princess were now fighting each other.","Which meant both sides would inevitably suffer losses.","Inside the hall, one Heaven Suppression Pavilion elder suddenly laughed loudly.","\"Hahaha! Excellent!\"","\"No matter who wins, both sides will definitely be weakened heavily afterward.\"","\"The Frost Lily Pavilion is not an easy opponent even for the Ninth Princess.\"","...","As more people thought about it, the brighter their expressions became.","This was practically the perfect opportunity.","Originally, Yu Wenzhao still needed to carefully consider which opponent to attack first.","But now?","The Ninth Princess had solved that problem for him herself.","Yu Wenzhao slowly leaned back against his seat.","A faint smile gradually appeared on his face as well.","\"Excellent!\"","His eyes flickered sharply.","No matter who gained the advantage in the end, both sides would undoubtedly suffer damage.","And at that moment, he would make his move.","A true hunter never rushed carelessly into battle.","Instead, they waited for the perfect moment to strike.","Yu Wenzhao slowly stood up from his throne-like seat.","His robes fluttered lightly despite the still air.","\"We will move as well!\"","The surrounding experts immediately became serious.","Yu Wenzhao’s lips curved upward coldly.","\"Let the Ninth Princess and Fourth Princess weaken each other first. Once one side begins gaining the upper hand...\"","A dangerous light flashed across his eyes.","\"We will descend and destroy both of them at the same time!\"","The entire hall immediately erupted.","\"Your Highness is wise!\"","\"With two Earth Immortals and nearly fifteen Immortal Realm experts, no one will be able to stop us!\"","\"Hahaha! Then this throne war is already decided!\""]},{"number":611,"title":"Chapter 611: Yu Feiyan Makes Her Move","paragraphs":["Three days ago!","Inside the Frost Lily Pavilion, the atmosphere remained calm and serene as ever.","Snowflakes drifted slowly from the sky while countless icy mountains stood beneath the clouds like immortal blades piercing the heavens.","At the highest palace within the sect, Yu Qingya quietly sat beside a frozen lake.","Her beautiful eyes calmly observed the chessboard before her.","Across from her sat the Frost Lily Pavilion Master.","Several elders also stood nearby silently.","Not long ago, news regarding the Third Prince’s actions had already reached them.","Yu Wenzhao had officially begun devouring the Seventh Prince’s forces.","When Yu Qingya first received the news, she immediately realized the danger.","If Yu Wenzhao completely digested the Seventh Prince’s foundation smoothly, his strength would rise to an extremely troublesome level.","By then, her faction would struggle to suppress him.","Thus, Yu Qingya had originally intended to move immediately.","She planned to become the third party watching from behind the shadows.","Once Yu Wenzhao and the Seventh Prince exhausted each other further, she would descend directly and reap the benefits herself.","After all, this was the perfect opportunity.","Otherwise, once the Third Prince fully absorbed the Crimson Thunder Palace, he would become far too powerful to handle later.","Thus, the Frost Lily Pavilion had already begun gathering experts from her faction.","However, before they could even mobilize fully, another piece of news suddenly arrived.","\"The Ninth Princess has mobilized her forces toward the Frost Lily Pavilion!\"","The moment those words were spoken, even the surrounding elders became briefly stunned.","Yu Qingya herself also paused slightly.","Although her expression remained calm outwardly, a trace of genuine surprise still flickered deep within her eyes.","Yu Feiyan?","Coming to attack her?","Before the Battle for the Throne, Yu Qingya barely remembered the Ninth Princess aside from knowing that lowly blood flowed within her veins and that she was considered a disgrace.","Previously, even looking directly into her eyes would have been impossible for Yu Feiyan.","(Just how did she change this much?)","But there was no point dwelling on that now.","For a brief moment, silence filled the frozen hall.","Clearly, even the Frost Lily Pavilion had not expected this development.","After all, among the remaining competitors, the Frost Lily Pavilion publicly possessed one of the strongest foundations remaining.","Under normal circumstances, the Ninth Princess should have been avoiding them instead.","Yet now, Yu Feiyan had personally chosen to attack them first.","One elder frowned slightly.","\"Could this be a trap?\"","Another elder shook his head calmly.","\"Regardless of her intentions, attacking us directly is foolish.\"","Soon, the Frost Lily Pavilion Master slowly spoke.","\"Perhaps... but this may not necessarily be a bad thing.\"","The surrounding elders immediately looked toward him.","The Pavilion Master’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Originally, they planned to act as the third party between Yu Wenzhao and the Seventh Prince.","However, no matter how weak the Ninth Princess’s faction appeared compared to them, if they diverted too much of their strength, they might not be able to handle both situations simultaneously.","Compared to the Ninth Princess, dealing with the Third Prince was far more important.","But ignore Ninth Princess’s advance?","Although regrettable, they all knew their best option now was to abandon their plan to target the Third Prince and focus fully on the Ninth Princess who was approaching them.","Thinking about this, the Frost Lily Pavilion Master calmly asked,","\"How strong are Yu Feiyan’s current forces?\"","Soon, intelligence reports were quickly presented.","Several elders carefully reviewed the information.","After a while, faint smiles gradually appeared across numerous faces.","\"No Earth Immortal Realm experts.\"","\"Only around five Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators overall.\"","\"As for the rest, not worth mentioning.\"","...","The Frost Lily Pavilion remained extremely calm after learning the details.","Because compared to them, Yu Feiyan’s foundation truly appeared lacking.","The Frost Lily Pavilion alone possessed an Earth Immortal expert.","Not to mention multiple Immortal Ascension cultivators and countless elite disciples.","No matter how strange Yu Feiyan’s rise had been recently, absolute strength still determined everything eventually.","At least—","That was what they believed.","Soon afterward, discussions quickly concluded.","The Frost Lily Pavilion would abandon their previous plans entirely.","Instead of targeting Yu Wenzhao now, they would focus fully on the Ninth Princess first.","\"If Yu Feiyan dares come here personally... then we’ll bury her here completely!\"","Several elders nodded one after another.","Clearly, they all viewed this as an enormous opportunity.","If they could eliminate the Ninth Princess now, the throne war would immediately shrink once again.","And more importantly, Yu Feiyan’s rapidly expanding forces would all become resources for the Frost Lily Pavilion instead.","At the center of the hall, Yu Qingya quietly listened to the discussion.","She slowly nodded.","\"Very well!\"","A cold light gradually appeared within her eyes.","(I want to see what you are hiding, Yu Feiyan!)","***","And just as the intelligence reports claimed—","The Ninth Princess’s forces began advancing toward the Frost Lily Pavilion.","However, strangely enough, she did not appear hurried at all.","This was no surprise attack.","No attempt to move swiftly before the Frost Lily Pavilion could prepare.","Instead, her forces advanced steadily and calmly across the empire like they didn’t care that Yu Qingya would know about their attack.","At first, Yu Qingya and the Frost Lily Pavilion did not think much about it.","After all, from their perspective, the Ninth Princess was merely walking directly into a trap.","But soon—","New reports continuously arrived one after another.","\"The Cloud River Sect has joined the Ninth Princess!\"","\"The White Stone Clan has submitted!\"","\"The Golden Flame Pavilion has defected!\"","...","Inside the Frost Lily Pavilion, the atmosphere gradually became strange.","Because those forces...","Originally belonged to them.","Or more accurately—","They had all previously supported the Fourth Princess’s faction.","Yet now, as Yu Feiyan advanced across the territories, those clans and sects unexpectedly switched allegiance one after another.","And the most unbelievable part was that there barely seemed to be any fighting.","The reports consistently described the same thing.","Yu Feiyan would arrive.","Then after a brief meeting...","The entire clan or sect would willingly submit.","No battle.","No resistance.","No bloodshed.","Almost as if they had become bewitched.","Inside the frozen hall, several elders’ expressions had already become somewhat ugly.","\"This makes no sense.\"","\"The White Stone Clan has followed us for years.\"","\"And the Cloud River Sect Master is known for his stubborn personality. He should never surrender so easily.\"","Even Yu Qingya herself gradually frowned.","Some of those clans truly were extremely loyal to her faction.","And others, even if they lacked loyalty, still should not have been easy to sway.","Yet Yu Feiyan barely seemed to spend any effort convincing them.","And afterward, those same people immediately became completely obedient to her faction.","It was as though something invisible had quietly changed their minds entirely.","This naturally made Yu Qingya increasingly wary.","At first, she viewed Yu Feiyan’s forces with some contempt.","No Earth Immortal.","Only around five Immortal Ascension cultivators.","Compared to the Frost Lily Pavilion and her other forces, the difference should have been overwhelming.","But now, as the Ninth Princess continued advancing, her forces were continuously expanding at an astonishing speed.","Every territory she passed through seemed to become part of her faction effortlessly.","The army behind her grew larger and larger.","According to the reports, many newly joined clans and sects displayed fanatical loyalty almost immediately.","As if they truly believed Yu Feiyan would become the future ruler of the empire without question.","But it wasn’t just the Fourth Princess’s faction being devoured.","Even forces belonging to the Third Prince and First Prince were absorbed without hesitation.","The only ones spared were those belonging to the Neutral Alliance.","It took the Ninth Princess more than three days after the Fourth Princess first received reports of her advance.","Finally—","The Frost Lily Pavilion saw the Ninth Princess’s forces arrive.","Countless figures filled the snowy plains outside the sect.","Banners fluttered beneath the freezing winds while powerful auras spread endlessly across the horizon.","However, strangely enough, the atmosphere did not resemble an army preparing for an immediate assault at all.","No experts charging forward.","No killing intent erupting toward the Frost Lily Pavilion.","Instead, Yu Feiyan’s forces calmly stopped outside the sect as though they were merely visiting another faction.","At the center of the massive army stood Yu Feiyan herself.","Behind her stood countless experts and sect leaders who had recently joined her faction.","Many among them originally belonged to the Fourth Princess.","Yet now, every single one stood behind Yu Feiyan obediently without the slightest hesitation.","High above the Frost Lily Pavilion, countless icy formations illuminated the sky.","The Frost Lily Pavilion experts had already gathered completely.","At the front stood Yu Qingya herself.","Beside her stood the Frost Lily Pavilion Master alongside numerous elders.","Their gazes remained cold as they stared toward the approaching army below.","Yu Qingya quietly observed the Ninth Princess carefully.","The more she looked, the stranger she felt.","Because the current Yu Feiyan felt completely unfamiliar to her.","It was as though the person standing before her now was no longer the same Ninth Princess she once remembered.","\"You sure took your time coming here.\"","Her voice echoed coldly across the snowy battlefield.","Yu Feiyan merely smiled faintly.","Meanwhile, Yu Qingya’s gaze slowly shifted behind Yu Feiyan.","Toward the former subordinate clans and sects who had betrayed her faction recently.","All of them now stood respectfully behind the Ninth Princess as though following her was the most natural thing in the world.","Seeing this scene, several Frost Lily Pavilion elders could no longer suppress their anger.","One elder immediately stepped forward furiously.","\"Traitors!\"","Her voice thundered across the battlefield.","\"The Frost Lily Pavilion supported your sects for years, yet you dare betray the Fourth Princess now?!\"","Another elder’s expression turned incomparably ugly.","\"Have you all forgotten who protected your clans all these years?!\"","Their voices carried both fury and disbelief.","Because even now, many of them still could not understand why these clans suddenly defected so easily.","However, the reactions from those former allies were even stranger.","None of them showed guilt.","None appeared ashamed.","Instead, they merely looked calmly toward the Frost Lily Pavilion elders.","Almost as though they genuinely did not understand why the others were angry.","One sect master slowly stepped forward before speaking respectfully,","\"The Ninth Princess is the rightful future ruler of the empire.\"","His tone sounded completely natural.","\"As her subjects, following her is only proper.\"","The Frost Lily Pavilion elders’ expressions immediately changed further.","Because the man speaking now was previously one of Yu Qingya’s most loyal supporters.","Yet now, he spoke as though abandoning the Fourth Princess was the most obvious decision imaginable.","Another clan leader also nodded calmly.","\"We merely followed the will of Heaven.\"","\"There is nothing shameful about that.\"","The surrounding Frost Lily Pavilion experts gradually felt chills rising within their hearts.","This was no longer normal loyalty.","These people almost looked brainwashed.","These people truly believed what they were saying.","There was no hesitation.","No unwillingness whatsoever.","It was as though the moment they joined Yu Feiyan’s faction, all doubts within their hearts had completely disappeared.","\"Fourth Sister, how about we have a talk?\"","Yu Feiyan asked.","Yu Qingya immediately became wary, as did the surrounding elders.","If it were anyone else, perhaps they would not have thought much of it.","But Yu Feiyan was different.","Who knows what kind of ability she has to make so many of their loyal followers betray them?","\"What? Scared?\"","Yu Feiyan asked calmly.","\"Don’t worry. You can bring your Sect Leader and Grand Elders. I merely want to speak with you personally one last time before our clash.\"","Yu Qingya looked toward Yu Feiyan and then toward the Frost Lily Pavilion elders beside her.","No matter what strange tricks Yu Feiyan possessed, Yu Qingya still did not believe they could overcome the combined strength of an Earth Immortal Realm expert and multiple Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators.","Moreover, this situation could actually benefit them.","If they managed to capture Yu Feiyan directly, then her entire faction would likely collapse immediately afterward.","No matter how Yu Qingya thought about it, there seemed to be no reason to reject the request.","\"Okay!\"","Yu Qingya replied coldly.","\"But only for ten minutes.\""]},{"number":612,"title":"Chapter 612: Visitors from Beyond the Empire","paragraphs":["Just as chaos was brewing across the Desolate Heaven Empire, an entirely different scene was unfolding within the Imperial Capital.","The throne war continued to shake countless territories.","The Third Prince was rapidly expanding.","The Fourth Princess and Ninth Princess stood on the verge of conflict.","The First Prince remained hidden while silently accumulating strength.","Every major force within the empire had already become caught within the growing storm.","Yet amidst all of this, three figures leisurely walked through the bustling streets of the capital.","Two of them appeared to be ordinary middle-aged men.","Their clothing was simple.","Their auras were restrained completely.","From the outside, they looked no different from ordinary guards accompanying a wealthy young master.","However, if any true expert were present, they would immediately discover something horrifying.","The surrounding qi unconsciously avoided the two men.","Even space itself seemed strangely stable around them.","As for the young man between them, his appearance was handsome and refined.","He wore luxurious robes embroidered with golden patterns that ordinary cultivators would never dare wear openly.","His expression carried obvious disdain.","As he observed the bustling capital around him, his brows became increasingly furrowed.","\"Tsk!\"","The young man clicked his tongue.","A look of disappointment appeared on his face.","\"This is the capital of the so-called Desolate Heaven Empire?\"","His voice carried unconcealed contempt.","\"What a backward place.\"","The nearby pedestrians naturally heard his insult, but judging by his appearance, they knew they could not afford to offend this young master.","Why bother risking their lives for a few words?","In this period of time, everyone knew that the law would be weakest and to rely on that to keep you safe is more like a dream.","The young man continued shaking his head.","\"The Qi is thin. The cultivation standards are laughable.\"","\"And these buildings...\"","His gaze swept across the magnificent imperial streets.","\"They look like villages compared to home.\"","The two middle-aged men exchanged glances.","Neither appeared surprised by his attitude.","Clearly, they were already accustomed to it.","One of them smiled faintly.","\"Young Master, there is no need to lower yourself by comparing this place to our homeland. This empire is merely a remote corner of the Continent.\"","The other bodyguard nodded.","\"Indeed! Once the Young Master completes this mission successfully, your contribution will be immense. By then, your position within the clan will become unshakable.\"","\"For the sake of the bigger picture, I hope the Young Master can endure this hardship.\"","Hearing those words, the young man’s expression softened slightly.","However, it disappeared just as quickly.","His mood still did not improve.","Instead, he snorted coldly.","\"Hmph! I know that already. If not for this mission, do you think I would willingly come to such a place?\"","His gaze drifted toward the distant Imperial Palace.","A faint look of disgust surfaced once more.","\"Forget the Qi. Even the air here feels dirty.\"","The two bodyguards smiled helplessly.","They could understand his frustration.","After all, compared to the place they came from, the Desolate Heaven Empire truly was insignificant.","Yet the clan’s orders were absolute.","No matter how unwilling they were, they still had to complete the task assigned to them.","The young master folded his hands behind his back and continued walking through the capital.","The young master’s mood only worsened.","At first, he merely frowned.","Then he began clicking his tongue repeatedly.","Soon afterward, every single thing around him seemed to become an eyesore.","Complaint after complaint poured from his mouth without pause.","The nearby bodyguards remained silent.","Neither bothered responding.","After all, they had accompanied him for many years.","They knew his temperament well.","The more dissatisfied he became, the more he would complain.","Finally—","The young master stopped walking entirely.","\"No!\"","He waved his hand impatiently.","\"I’ve had enough.\"","His face was filled with annoyance.","\"Walking around this place is exhausting. Go find a carriage.\"","One of the bodyguards immediately cupped his hands.","\"As you command, Young Master!\"","Without another word, he turned and disappeared into the crowd.","Meanwhile, the young master remained standing in place.","His expression grew increasingly unpleasant.","The mission was already irritating enough.","Now they had spent days wandering around this backward empire while obtaining almost nothing useful.","Naturally, his patience was rapidly reaching its limit.","After several moments of silence, he suddenly spoke again.","This time, his tone carried obvious irritation.","\"Where is that bitch Qin Lingxiao?\"","The old bodyguard beside him immediately frowned.","The young master continued speaking without restraint.","\"She should know where that place is, right? If she knows, shouldn’t we just capture her and interrogate her?\"","\"Why are we wasting so much time here? Wouldn’t that solve everything immediately?\"","The old bodyguard nearly laughed from disbelief.","Capture Qin Lingxiao?","Interrogate her?","The young master spoke as though he were discussing some ordinary cultivator.","The old man could only shake his head helplessly.","Who was Qin Lingxiao?","Did he truly think she was some random genius from a small empire?","Someone they could simply seize and question whenever they wished?","If that were possible, their clan would never have sent them here personally.","The old man’s gaze became somewhat complicated.","Qin Lingxiao’s background alone was enough to make countless major powers think twice.","She herself wasn’t someone who could be defeated so easily. Even an empire was destroyed simply because it offended her.","Even within their own clan, many elders would hesitate before provoking her unnecessarily.","Yet this young master casually spoke of capturing and interrogating her.","The old man could only shake his head again.","\"Young Master.\"","His tone became slightly more serious.","\"We still don’t know her whereabouts.\"","The young master frowned.","Just then—","The bodyguard who had left earlier returned.","Behind him followed an extremely luxurious carriage pulled by four snow-white spiritual beasts.","The young master’s eyes immediately brightened.","Finally! At least something in this empire looked barely acceptable.","Without hesitation, he stepped inside.","As the carriage began moving through the capital streets, the old bodyguard gazed toward the distant horizon.","Soon, the three entered the carriage.","As it slowly moved through the capital streets, the young master lazily leaned against his seat.","For several moments, silence filled the carriage.","Then suddenly, the young master sat upright.","His eyes lit up.","\"I’ve figured it out!\"","The two old men immediately looked over.","The young master spoke confidently.","\"Looking around aimlessly is useless. We should just ask the locals.\"","The two old men stared at him.","One of them helplessly replied,","\"Young Master, the locals don’t know anything. If they knew, someone would have found it long ago.\"","The young master waved dismissively.","\"Nonsense. There are countless people in this empire. Someone must know.\"","The old man rubbed his forehead.","Before he could speak again, the young master had already issued another order.","\"Bring me one.\"","The two old men exchanged another glance.","Then one of them sighed.","A moment later—","A passerby walking outside suddenly felt an invisible force wrap around him.","He didn’t know why, but although he had intended to continue straight ahead, he unknowingly began walking toward a luxurious carriage.","Inside the carriage, the curtain slowly opened.","The young master looked down at him.","The gaze resembled that of a deity looking upon a mortal.","Arrogant.","Indifferent.","Unquestionably superior.","In an irritated tone, he asked:","\"You!\"","The passerby hurriedly bowed.","\"Y-Yes?\"","Just from the carriage and the clothes the other party was wearing, he could tell that this was someone of extremely high status.","Someone like him dared not be impolite toward such a person.","The young master crossed his arms.","\"Which sect is the strongest in this empire?\"","The man didn’t even need to think.","\"Heaven Sword Sect!\"","The answer came instantly.","The young master raised an eyebrow.","\"Oh? Where is this sect?\"","The man immediately pointed toward the distant horizon as he briefly told the general direction.","The young master listened quietly.","Then he nodded.","\"Good!\"","The passerby secretly sighed in relief.","However, before he could leave, the young master had already turned toward the two old men.","\"These lowly people might not have the slightest idea, but wouldn’t the strongest sect know? Even if they don’t know fully, they should have an idea.\"","The two old men remained silent.","While they did not necessarily believe the Heaven Sword Sect would know, it was still better to ask a force that had existed in this empire for thousands of years than to continue searching blindly themselves.","Besides, even if they did not know, they could simply have the Heaven Sword Sect help search for it.","A faint smile finally appeared on the young master’s face.","\"Let’s go. To this so-called strongest sect.\"","His eyes narrowed slightly.","\"If anyone in this empire knows something, then it should be their Sect Leader.\"","The carriage immediately changed direction.","Under the watchful eyes of countless confused citizens, it shot into the sky and disappeared toward the north.","Meanwhile, neither the young master nor the two old men noticed that, in a quiet corner of the capital, an old beggar slowly lifted his head.","His cloudy eyes watched the departing carriage.","Then the old beggar lowered his head once more and continued drinking his cheap wine as though nothing had happened."]},{"number":613,"title":"Chapter 613: An Outsider Steps Into the Heaven Sword Sect","paragraphs":["The flying carriage tore across the skies at astonishing speed.","Four snow-white spiritual beasts pulled it forward while streams of wind continuously parted before them.","Inside the carriage, the young master sat lazily with one leg crossed over the other.","His expression remained impatient.","Fortunately, after obtaining the general direction from the passerby, the journey became much smoother.","Along the way, whenever they encountered cultivators, the two old men casually gathered information.","And just as expected, the Heaven Sword Sect was famous throughout the empire.","Almost everyone knew where it was located.","Thus, after several hours of travel, the carriage finally arrived at its destination.","Far ahead, massive palaces stood among the mountains while disciples continuously moved between the peaks.","A gigantic stone sword seemed to support the very heavens themselves.","For ordinary people, the sight was magnificent, filling them with awe upon witnessing such a scene.","However, the young master’s expression only became more disdainful.","\"Tsk!\"","He looked at the towering mountain range.","\"So this is the strongest sect in the Desolate Heaven Empire?\"","His tone was full of disappointment.","\"It’s smaller than some of our clan’s outer branch compounds.\"","The two old men smiled bitterly.","Naturally, they did not disagree.","Compared to their clan, the Heaven Sword Sect truly was insignificant.","Still—","At least they had finally found the place.","Thinking about being one step closer to completing his mission, the young master’s mood improved slightly.","\"Let’s go down.\"","The carriage slowly descended toward the main entrance of the sect.","Meanwhile, The Heaven Sword Sect disciples guarding the mountain gate immediately noticed the unfamiliar carriage.","Their expressions instantly became vigilant.","After all, they couldn’t recognize the carriage that was descending.","Soon, the carriage landed before the gate.","Several Heaven Sword Sect guards stepped forward.","One of them cupped his fists politely.","\"Welcome to the Heaven Sword Sect! May I ask for your identities and purpose for visiting?\"","The young master immediately frowned.","His eyes turned cold.","(A mere gate guard... Actually dared to question him?)","A killing intent instantly flashed across his eyes.","In his view, such a weak ant wasn’t even qualified to speak to him.","Forget questioning him.","The guard should be kneeling the moment he appears.","Just as he was about to raise his hand, the two old men immediately sensed his intentions.","One quickly transmitted his voice.","\"Young Master, please calm down.\"","The other hurriedly added,","\"This is merely a minor inconvenience. There is no need to create unnecessary complications.\"","\"If we start killing people immediately, we will attract a lot of attention.\"","The young master’s face darkened, clearly unhappy.","However, after a moment, he slowly lowered his hand.","\"Hmph!\"","Seeing this, the two old men secretly sighed in relief.","\"The Young Master truly possesses a broad and magnanimous heart.\"","The other nodded repeatedly.","\"Indeed! Such tolerance is worthy of admiration.\"","The young master proudly lifted his chin.","Naturally, he accepted the compliments without hesitation.","However, The Heaven Sword Sect guard’s expression had already become increasingly ugly.","The entire exchange had occurred right before him.","These people acted as though refraining from killing him was some great act of mercy.","Arrogant.","Utterly arrogant.","And this was the Heaven Sword Sect, The strongest sect in the empire.","How could outsiders behave so insolently before their gates?","The guard’s eyes gradually turned cold.","His voice became noticeably colder.","\"Once again, I will ask. State your identities. And what business do you have with the Heaven Sword Sect?\"","Behind him, dozens of disciples immediately formed ranks.","If these strangers refused to cooperate, the Heaven Sword Sect was fully prepared to treat them as enemies.","The atmosphere at the mountain gate became increasingly tense.","Dozens of Heaven Sword Sect disciples stood ready.","Qi quietly gathered around them.","Meanwhile, inside the carriage, the young master merely looked at them with undisguised contempt.","The old man beside him inwardly sighed.","Arguing with gate guards was meaningless.","Thus, he simply stepped forward and calmly replied,","\"We have business with your Sect Leader.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, several disciples almost laughed out loud.","Even the lead guard’s expression became strange.","Their Sect Leader?","These people wanted to meet their Sect Leader?","The guard carefully examined the three once more.","Certainly, their carriage was extraordinary.","Their clothing was expensive.","And their bearing suggested they came from a powerful background.","But so what?","Who was the Heaven Sword Sect Leader?","The number one sword cultivator within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","The leader of the strongest sect in the entire empire.","Even kings, clan patriarchs, and sect masters could not simply demand an audience whenever they wished.","Yet these strangers arrived at the mountain gate and immediately requested to meet him?","The guard sneered.","\"You want to meet the Sect Leader?\"","His tone carried obvious mockery.","\"Do you think our Sect Leader is some roadside merchant that anyone can visit?\"","Several disciples behind him chuckled.","\"Our Sect Leader has matters concerning the empire to handle every day. Why would he waste his time meeting random strangers?\"","The guard’s gaze became even colder.","\"Stop dreaming. Turn around and leave!\"","Inside the carriage, the young master’s expression immediately darkened.","The killing intent in his eyes surged once more.","However, before he could erupt, the old man raised a hand slightly.","The old man looked toward the guards.","His expression remained calm.","However, he already understood that continuing this conversation would achieve nothing.","After all, they truly had no token, invitation, or status recognized by the Heaven Sword Sect.","To these disciples, they were merely unknown outsiders.","Thus—","The old man no longer wasted words.","He simply raised his hand casually.","A small motion.","Nothing more.","The Heaven Sword Sect disciples frowned.","Then their expressions suddenly froze.","The guard’s pupils lost focus.","The disciples behind him became motionless.","One after another, they stood completely still.","Like puppets whose souls had abruptly departed.","No resistance.","No struggle.","No warning signs whatsoever.","The dozens of disciples simply remained standing there silently.","The old man withdrew his hand.","\"Let’s go!\"","The spiritual beasts immediately pulled the carriage forward.","The Heaven Sword Sect disciples offered no response.","They merely stood there blankly as the carriage passed through the mountain gate.","To others, it almost appeared as though the disciples had willingly allowed the carriage to enter.","Several minutes later, the guard suddenly blinked.","Confusion appeared in his eyes.","\"Huh?\"","The disciples behind him gradually recovered as well.","One after another, they looked around in bewilderment.","\"What happened?\"","\"Why are we standing here?\"","\"Wasn’t there... something just now?\"","The guard frowned deeply.","A strange sense of unease appeared in his heart.","He felt as though he had forgotten something important.","Yet no matter how hard he tried to remember, his mind remained completely blank.","After several moments, he shook his head.","\"Forget it!\"","Perhaps he had merely become distracted.","Unfortunately, none of them noticed that far within the Heaven Sword Sect, a luxurious flying carriage was already moving toward the inner regions of the sect.","And even fewer people realized that three extremely dangerous guests had just entered the strongest sect in the empire completely unnoticed.","Eventually, the carriage came to a stop at the docking station.","The three figures stepped out.","The young master folded his hands behind his back.","The two old men followed closely behind.","Since they had already entered the sect, finding the Sect Leader naturally became their next objective.","Fortunately, that turned out to be much easier than expected.","The Heaven Sword Sect was not some hidden organization.","Visitors arrived frequently.","Many major clans, sects, and imperial officials often came to seek audiences with the Sect Leader.","Thus, when the two old men casually asked for directions, nobody found it strange.","Several disciples even pointed out the location enthusiastically.","One of the old men nodded.","\"It seems our task will be easier than expected.\"","The other smiled faintly.","\"Indeed! At least we already know where the Sect Leader of Heaven Sword Sect resides.\"","For once, something had gone smoothly.","Thus, the group began walking toward the Sect Leader’s office.","However, after only a short distance, they noticed something unusual.","Large numbers of disciples were rushing toward the same direction.","Some were running.","Others were flying.","Several even abandoned their cultivation sessions midway and hurried off excitedly.","The atmosphere was extremely lively.","\"Quickly! We’ll be late!\"","\"I heard Senior Sister Chu already arrived!\"","\"Hurry!\"","Excited voices continuously echoed throughout the sect.","Even the young master could not help becoming curious.","His brows rose slightly.","Could this be related to his mission?","After all, they had traveled across an entire empire searching for clues.","Anything unusual immediately attracted his attention.","Seeing the young master’s interest, one of the old men immediately reached out and stopped a passing disciple.","The disciple looked anxious.","Clearly, he wanted to leave immediately. However, he found that he seemed to not be able to leave even if he wanted to.","The old man smiled politely.","\"Little friend. What happened?\"","\"Why is everyone in such a hurry?\"","The disciple blinked.","He looked at the three strangely.","\"You don’t know?\"","His expression was genuinely surprising.","At the moment, almost the entire Heaven Sword Sect was discussing this matter.","How could there still be people unaware of it?","However, he was in too much of a hurry to question them further.","Thus, he immediately answered.","\"Senior Sister Chu Ziyan is about to fight Senior Sister Bai Xueqing!\""]},{"number":614,"title":"Chapter 614: The Young Master’s First Shock!","paragraphs":["The disciple’s eyes immediately lit up when he saw that the three seemed completely unaware.","For some reason, he suddenly felt like explaining.","Perhaps it was because both names carried too much weight within the Heaven Sword Sect, or perhaps because he simply enjoyed talking.","\"Senior Sister Bai Xueqing and Senior Sister Chu Ziyan are the two greatest geniuses of our generation within the Heaven Sword Sect.\"","\"No! Not just the Heaven Sword Sect. They are peerless geniuses throughout the entire Desolate Heaven Empire.\"","His voice became increasingly animated.","\"Many people even believe both of them possess the qualifications to stand at the very peak of the world someday.\"","The young master’s eyebrow twitched slightly.","(The peak of the world?)","The disciple continued speaking enthusiastically.","\"Although most people believe Senior Sister Bai Xueqing is stronger, nobody dares underestimate Senior Sister Chu Ziyan.\"","The disciple looked toward the distant arena excitedly.","\"I need to go! You’re lucky to come across such an opportunity. You all should come watch as well.\"","\"You won’t regret it!\"","The moment he finished speaking, he immediately rushed away.","Within seconds, he disappeared into the crowd.","The young master looked in the direction the disciple had left.","Then he suddenly snorted.","\"Hmph!\"","His face was full of disdain.","\"Peerless geniuses? The peak of the world?\"","His voice carried obvious mockery.","\"Did they ask me?\"","In his eyes, a genius from the Desolate Heaven Empire was no different from a genius among ants.","To be called peerless geniuses who could one day stand at the peak, they should at least possess talent comparable to his own, which he believed was impossible.","The young master continued sneering.","\"These people are making such a huge commotion. I bet those two are only Nascent Soul Realm cultivators.\"","\"To think they dare call such people peerless geniuses.\"","The two old men did not comment.","Truthfully, they also did not think much of this empire’s younger generation.","However, one of them stroked his beard thoughtfully.","\"Still, Young Master, this level of excitement throughout an entire sect isn’t normal.\"","The second old man nodded.","\"Indeed! Since we have already arrived, watching their battle may not be a bad thing.\"","\"We can also evaluate the standards of the younger generation within the Desolate Heaven Empire.\"","The young master crossed his arms.","If it had not been for the countless hours he spent sitting in the carriage bored out of his mind, he would not have even spared them a glance.","But now that he was extremely bored, he thought that no matter how weak these ants were, watching them fight might at least improve his mood.","It would be even better if they were pretty.","After a brief pause, he nodded.","\"Fine! Let’s take a look. If nothing else, it should help pass the time.\"","The two old men naturally had no objections.","Thus, the three followed the massive flow of disciples.","The further they walked, the larger the crowd became.","Thousands.","Then tens of thousands.","Almost every disciple within the Heaven Sword Sect seemed to be heading toward the same destination.","Eventually, an enormous arena appeared before them.","Countless seats surrounded it.","Excited discussions filled the air.","The atmosphere was extremely lively.","The three quickly entered alongside the crowd.","However, the young master’s expression immediately darkened again.","Because they were not escorted anywhere special.","No exclusive VIP seating was prepared.","Thus, after entering, they simply found ordinary seats among the countless disciples.","The young master stared at the surrounding crowd.","Then at his seat.","Then at the countless Heaven Sword Sect disciples sitting nearby.","His face twitched.","\"I... am sitting here?\"","His voice sounded almost unbelievable.","One old man coughed awkwardly.","The other looked away.","The young master’s expression became uglier and uglier.","Back home, wherever he went, he occupied the highest seat.","The best seat.","Yet now, he was sitting shoulder-to-shoulder with what he considered a bunch of insignificant ants.","His mood instantly worsened.","\"This place truly is a backward region.\"","He grumbled.","\"Not even basic hospitality exists.\"","The two old men wisely remained silent.","At least this time, the young master merely complained.","Compared to killing someone, that was already a very good outcome.","Soon afterward, the discussions throughout the arena gradually intensified.","More and more disciples arrived.","The arena rapidly became packed as excited discussions echoed from every direction.","\"Who do you think will win?\"","\"Senior Sister Bai, obviously!\"","\"Not necessarily. Senior Sister Chu also has a good chance.\"","The discussions continued noisily around him, which he initially ignored entirely until—","\"Didn’t you hear the latest rumors?\"","\"What rumors?\"","\"It’s said that Senior Sister Bai already broke through to the Void Refinement Realm!\"","The moment those words entered his ears, the young master’s expression froze.","His scoffing stopped abruptly.","Not only him—","Even the two old men beside him became stunned.","For a moment, all three wondered whether they had misheard.","Void Refinement Realm?","One of the old men’s mouths twitched slightly.","Meanwhile, another disciple excitedly joined the discussion.","\"I heard that too!\"","\"Senior Sister Chu might have broken through as well!\"","\"Even if she hasn’t yet, she’s definitely standing at the peak of the Spirit Severing Realm.\"","\"Otherwise, why would she challenge Senior Sister Bai?\"","The surrounding disciples nodded repeatedly.","Clearly, many people believed this speculation.","The young master slowly turned his head.","His eyes were filled with disbelief.","(Void Refinement Realm?)","The three exchanged glances.","For the first time since arriving in the Desolate Heaven Empire, their expressions became somewhat strange.","One old man frowned.","\"Isn’t this bragging a little too much?\"","His voice was low.","The second old man nodded silently.","Even he found it difficult to believe.","Void Refinement Realm!","That was no joke.","After thinking briefly, one of the old men turned toward a nearby disciple.","\"Hello!\"","The disciple looked over curiously.","\"What is it?\"","The old man smiled politely.","\"Little friend, may I ask something?\"","The disciple nodded.","\"These two geniuses everyone keeps discussing... How old are they? And what cultivation realms are they actually in?\"","The old man had already begun making assumptions.","Perhaps these were disciples who were already on the verge of becoming elders.","That would make far more sense.","After all, the Void Refinement Realm was not some common cultivation stage.","Even in the Central Glorious Continent, such cultivators would still be considered formidable, especially if they were still a disciple.","The disciple immediately looked at him strangely.","As though he had just asked whether the sky was blue.","\"You don’t know?\"","His expression became even more peculiar.","Within the Desolate Heaven Empire, even people who had never visited the Heaven Sword Sect knew Bai Xueqing’s name.","Still, he answered.","\"Senior Sister Bai and Senior Sister Chu are both only twenty years old this year.\"","Silence.","The old man’s smile froze.","The second old man’s eyes widened slightly.","The young master himself sat motionless.","For several seconds, none of them spoke.","Then—","\"Twenty?\"","The young master finally muttered.","His voice sounded somewhat hoarse.","His eyes were filled with disbelief.","Twenty?","Void Refinement Realm?","Even if the rumors were exaggerated, that still meant they were at least in the Spirit Severing Realm.","His mind momentarily became blank.","Back home, he had always been praised as a heaven-defying genius.","His clan elders constantly praised his talent.","His peers envied him.","His juniors worshipped him.","At twenty years old, he had not disappointed their expectation and entered the Spirit Severing Realm.","Even that achievement had shocked countless people.","Yet now...","He was hearing that two disciples from what he considered a backward empire had possibly reached the Void Refinement Realm at roughly the same age.","The young master’s hands unconsciously clenched.","(Impossible!)","His first reaction was disbelief.","There was no way.","How could a place like the Desolate Heaven Empire produce geniuses superior to him?","The disciple beside them, however, simply continued speaking.","\"Junior Sister Bai was already able to defeat Void Refinement Realm cultivators before. She must have become even more terrifying now.\"","\"With the Mu Clan supporting her, there should be no shortage of high-quality pills.\"","\"Don’t forget that Chu Ziyan is also Bai Zihan’s fiancée. She must receive similar resources as well.\"","\"Even if they haven’t broken through yet, they will definitely reach the Void Refinement Realm within a few months.\"","The young master listened quietly.","The more he listened, the less certain he became.","Originally, he had viewed everything here with contempt.","The empire was weak.","The sect was small.","Its disciples were ants.","Its geniuses were probably mediocre.","Yet now, a seed of doubt had appeared within his heart.","However, until he witnessed everything with his own eyes, he still refused to believe it completely.","Then suddenly—","A wave of cheers erupted from one side of the arena.","\"Senior Sister Bai and Senior Sister Chu are here!\"","The crowd instantly became restless.","Countless heads turned simultaneously.","Even the young master and the two old men looked over.","The two old men silently observed the two girls.","Even they had to admit... These two young women were extraordinary.","Beside them, the young master sat completely still.","His eyes remained fixed upon them.","His expression had become somewhat strange.","The arrogance.","The disdain.","The contempt.","For a brief moment, all of it seemed to disappear.","His gaze lingered on Bai Xueqing.","Then shifted toward Chu Ziyan.","Then back again.","His eyes widened slightly.","His heartbeat unconsciously accelerated.","A single thought surfaced within his mind and he couldn’t stop himself from blurting it out.","\"Beautiful!\""]},{"number":615,"title":"Chapter 615: The Young Master’s Fascination","paragraphs":["The moment those words left his mouth, the two old men were unable to remain calm.","Because they understood him far too well.","This was not a casual compliment nor was it simple admiration.","The young master was genuinely captivated.","His gaze remained fixed upon the arena.","Upon the two women standing opposite one another.","The more he looked, the more shocked he became.","Back in the Central Glorious Continent, he had seen countless beauties.","Saintesses!","Princesses!","Daughters of supreme clans!","Women whose beauty was renowned across entire regions.","Yet somehow... The two women before him did not lose out to any of them.","In fact—","If he was being honest with himself, they might even surpass many of those famous Saintesses renowned for their beauty.","\"How can such a place hide beauties like these?\"","The young master muttered unconsciously.","His eyes never left the arena.","The two old men exchanged glances.","Both could see the surprise in each other’s eyes.","They had followed the young master for many years.","Naturally, they knew how proud he was.","Even when facing famous Saintesses from the Central Glorious Continent, he rarely offered praise.","Most of the time, he merely nodded dismissively.","Yet now...","He was openly expressing admiration.","This alone spoke volumes.","One of the old men looked toward the arena once more.","Then he inwardly sighed.","Truthfully, he could not entirely blame the young master.","The two young women truly were exceptional.","Their appearances were flawless.","Their temperaments were even more extraordinary.","One was cold and ethereal like an immortal fairy descended from the heavens.","The other was elegant and graceful while possessing an unyielding sharpness hidden beneath her beauty.","Standing together, they naturally drew every gaze in the arena.","No wonder the entire Heaven Sword Sect had gathered.","For a moment, the old man even jokingly wondered whether the crowd had come for the battle or simply to admire the two women.","Meanwhile, the young master remained completely focused on the arena.","Unable to look away.","A strange light gradually appeared within his eyes.","Then as though he had suddenly reached a decision.","He spoke.","\"I want them!\"","The two old men blinked.","For a moment, they thought they had misheard.","The young master continued calmly.","\"I want both of them as my wives.\"","The two old men nearly choked.","One of them hurriedly transmitted his voice.","\"Young Master! Please remember our mission.\"","The second old man immediately nodded.","\"This matter is far more important than personal affairs.\"","However, the young master merely waved his hand dismissively.","His gaze remained fixed upon Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan.","\"Who said I’m neglecting my duties? I’ll complete the mission. Does that somehow prevent me from pursuing women?\"","The two old men became speechless.","After a moment of consideration, they slowly nodded.","Objectively speaking...","The young master was not entirely wrong.","If the rumors were true and these two truly possessed such extraordinary talent, then their talent would indeed make them worthy candidates for the young master’s wives.","Although becoming the young master’s main wife would likely be impossible.","After all, the clan already had plans to arrange a marriage with a major power of equal standing.","Such unions involved countless interests.","They were not something that could be changed casually.","However, taking such talented and beautiful women as concubines was not entirely out of the question.","In fact, many powerful young masters did precisely that.","The young master’s gaze toward the arena grew increasingly possessive.","In his mind, the matter already seemed settled.","Meanwhile—","Neither Bai Xueqing nor Chu Ziyan had the slightest idea what was happening within the audience.","Nor would they have cared even if they knew.","At that moment, their entire attention was focused upon one another.","Bai Xueqing stood calmly upon one side of the arena.","However, as her gaze swept across the surrounding stands, a faint frown appeared on her face.","Seeing her expression, Chu Ziyan immediately understood what she was thinking.","A trace of embarrassment appeared on her beautiful face.","\"Sorry.\"","Chu Ziyan smiled helplessly.","\"I didn’t think it would become this big.\"","She glanced around the arena.","Truthfully, she was also somewhat surprised.","When she had recently broken through, she simply wanted to test her newfound strength.","After all, opportunities to find a suitable opponent were extremely rare.","Among the younger generation, there were very few people qualified to exchange blows with her.","Coincidentally, Bai Xueqing had also recently advanced.","Thus, Chu Ziyan had proposed a duel.","Bai Xueqing naturally agreed.","The two of them were perhaps the most suitable opponents for one another within the entire Heaven Sword Sect.","Not only were their cultivation realms similar, but both possessed extraordinary combat strength.","Testing their breakthroughs through battle would undoubtedly be beneficial for both.","As a result, they requested the use of the arena.","Neither had expected the news to spread so quickly, nor had they expected nearly the entire sect to appear.","Even many disciples and elders who were supposedly in seclusion had emerged.","The scale had become somewhat ridiculous.","Chu Ziyan rubbed her forehead.","\"Somehow the news leaked, and then everyone found out.\"","Her expression became increasingly helpless.","Bai Xueqing followed her gaze.","Thousands upon thousands of disciples filled the seats.","The noise was deafening.","The excitement was obvious.","After all, these were the two greatest geniuses of the Heaven Sword Sect.","Perhaps even the entire empire.","Seeing this scene, Bai Xueqing merely shook her head.","\"Ignore them.\"","Her voice remained calm.","\"There is no need to pay attention to them.\"","Although she was somewhat displeased by the attention, there was nothing that she or Chu Ziyan could do about it.","Besides, if people wanted to watch, they could watch.","She was not someone unaccustomed to attention.","Ever since childhood, she had attracted countless gazes.","The same was true for Chu Ziyan.","Long ago, they had both become accustomed to attracting attention wherever they went.","Chu Ziyan laughed softly.","\"I suppose you’re right.\"","The two exchanged a glance.","The smiles faded.","Their expressions gradually became serious.","Meanwhile, within the audience, countless disciples immediately noticed the change.","The discussions rapidly quieted down.","Everyone understood.","The battle was about to begin!"]},{"number":616,"title":"Chapter 616: Bai Xueqing Vs Chu Ziyan!","paragraphs":["Clang!","Two swords collided.","A sharp metallic cry echoed throughout the arena.","The next instant—","Both figures vanished.","Clang! Clang! Clang!","Sword lights erupted across the arena as Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan exchanged blows at astonishing speed.","To ordinary disciples, the two had already become little more than blurs.","One moment they appeared on the eastern side of the arena.","Next, they were already clashing in the west.","Their movements were fluid and elegant.","Many disciples couldn’t even keep up with their speed.","Yet everyone could tell that neither of them was fighting seriously.","No technique had been unleashed.","This was merely a warm-up.","A simple exchange to gauge one another’s current strength.","Even so, the spectators could not help but feel shocked.","\"So fast!\"","\"They’re stronger than before!\"","\"Much stronger!\"","...","Discussions immediately erupted.","Many of the disciples present had witnessed them fighting against the Demonic Forces.","Others had watched them in the last Dragon and Phoenix Competition.","Because of that, they understood more clearly than anyone how terrifying this improvement was, especially those who had only seen them during the Dragon and Phoenix Competition.","For cultivators, only a short amount of time had passed, yet the growth displayed by the two women was almost unbelievable.","Rather than having their Cultivation slow down due to having reached a higher realm, they have rather increased further.","Their swords collided repeatedly.","Every exchange was cleaner, faster, sharper,","Soon, the cultivation auras surrounding the two women became impossible to conceal.","Late Spirit Severing Realm!","The moment that realization spread through the arena, countless people sucked in cold breaths.","Even some elders revealed expressions of astonishment.","This strength had already surpassed many elders within the sect.","Among the audience, the young master sat motionless.","The two old men beside him were equally silent.","Late Spirit Severing Realm!","They had viewed the Desolate Heaven Empire as a backward region, yet the geniuses standing before them had surpassed even their young master.","At twenty years old, their young master had only entered the Spirit Severing Realm.","These two women had already reached it’s late stages.","The gap was obvious and impossible to deny.","Not to mention, their young master was able to achieve that largely thanks to all the resources poured into him since young.","The two of them, on the other hand, shouldn’t have much resources compared to what the Young Master had.","The young master’s expression grew increasingly complicated.","Then slowly, that complexity transformed into something else.","Possessiveness!","The stronger the two women appeared, the more determined he became.","Such beauty.","Such talent.","Such cultivation.","In his eyes, they were becoming increasingly worthy of him.","Upon the arena—","Clang!","Another sword collision echoed.","The two women separated.","Bai Xueqing landed lightly upon the ground.","Chu Ziyan touched down several dozen meters away.","Although the difference was small, Bai Xueqing appeared to possess a slight advantage.","A faint smile appeared on Bai Xueqing’s face.","\"Ziyan, you’ve really become strong.\"","Her praise was completely sincere.","Chu Ziyan had always been slightly weaker than her.","After receiving the cultivation technique Bai Zihan had given her, Bai Xueqing had believed her cultivation speed would leave most of her generation far behind.","The improvement she experienced had been extraordinary.","Yet somehow, Chu Ziyan had still managed to keep pace.","Even now, she was able to exchange hundreds of blows without falling behind.","Although Bai Xueqing was not fighting at full strength, it was still a pleasant surprise.","Across from her, Chu Ziyan smiled.","\"And you’re as powerful as ever.\"","She adjusted her grip on her sword.","\"If I don’t start getting serious soon, I reckon I might be defeated before I even get to see your true strength.\"","Her tone was light, yet her eyes were filled with determination.","More than anyone else, Chu Ziyan understood the gap between them.","Bai Xueqing was probably the most talented person she would ever meet besides Bai Zihan.","But understanding the gap and accepting defeat were two entirely different things.","She had never been someone who surrendered simply because victory was difficult, nor had she ever believed losing was natural.","If there was a mountain before her, she would climb it.","If there was a stronger opponent, she would challenge them.","That was precisely why she had reached her current level.","A powerful aura surged from Chu Ziyan’s body.","Boom!","A vast wave of Qi erupted outward.","The arena trembled slightly.","The pressure surrounding her instantly began rising.","Countless disciples immediately widened their eyes.","\"What is happening?!\"","\"Her aura is still increasing!\"","\"No way...\"","Even some elders stood up abruptly.","Then a subtle yet unmistakable transformation occurred.","The Qi surrounding Chu Ziyan seemed to undergo a qualitative change.","Early Void Refinement Realm!","Absolute silence!","For a brief moment, the entire arena became quiet.","Then chaos erupted.","\"Void Refinement Realm!\"","\"She actually broke through!\"","\"My heavens!\"","\"She’s only twenty!\"","The audience exploded into uproar.","Although many had speculated.","Although rumors had already spread.","Speculation and reality were completely different things.","A twenty-year-old Void Refinement cultivator.","Such a thing was almost unheard of within the Desolate Heaven Empire unless you include Bai Zihan.","Among the audience, the young master’s pupils contracted violently.","His expression completely changed.","Not only him.","Even the two old men were visibly shaken.","\"Impossible...\"","One of them muttered subconsciously.","The other stared at Chu Ziyan without blinking.","Even in the Central Glorious Continent, such talent would be enough to shake countless factions.","Meanwhile, upon the arena, even Bai Xueqing appeared surprised.","Her beautiful eyes widened slightly.","Though only for a brief second.","Then a smile appeared on her face.","\"Ziyan, congratulations!\"","Her voice carried sincere happiness.","She truly was surprised.","Breaking through to the Void Refinement Realm was no small matter.","Even Bai Xueqing had not expected Chu Ziyan to reach this step so quickly.","She genuinely did not know how Chu Ziyan had managed it.","Across from her, Chu Ziyan smiled.","\"Thank you, but I don’t think this means I’ve caught up to you.\"","Bai Xueqing chuckled softly.","Then a powerful aura erupted from her body as well.","Boom!","The pressure immediately swept across the arena.","The surrounding Qi instantly became restless.","Early Void Refinement Realm!","The entire Heaven Sword Sect fell silent.","Everyone stared blankly.","Then chaos erupted once more.","\"Senior Sister Bai also broke through!\"","\"My heavens!\"","\"Two Void Refinement Realm cultivators at twenty years old!\"","Countless disciples nearly lost their minds.","Many people had expected Bai Xueqing to be stronger.","Many had believed the rumors, yet witnessing it personally was still shocking beyond words.","Across the arena, Chu Ziyan merely smiled.","She showed no surprise whatsoever.","Clearly, she had already guessed the outcome.","If she could break through,","Then Bai Xueqing, who had always been one step ahead, naturally could as well.","However, the reactions of everyone else were completely different.","Especially the young master and the two old men.","They sat there motionless.","Their minds were in turmoil.","Earlier, discovering that both women had reached the Late Spirit Severing Realm had already exceeded their expectations.","Now—","Void Refinement Realm!","The young master unconsciously clenched his fists.","In the history of the Central Glorious Continent, only a handful of individuals had achieved something comparable.","Every single one of those people had eventually become legendary figures.","Monsters among monsters.","Existences capable of shaking entire regions.","Yet today, in a place he had repeatedly called a backward empire, he had encountered not one but two.","The two old men exchanged glances.","Both could see the shock within the other’s eyes.","Perhaps... they had underestimated the Desolate Heaven Empire far more than they realized.","Meanwhile, in the arena, neither Bai Xueqing nor Chu Ziyan paid attention to the commotion.","Their eyes remained locked on one another.","The warm-up was over.","Now, the real battle is finally going to begin!"]},{"number":617,"title":"Chapter 617: Two Void Refinement Geniuses","paragraphs":["The moment both women revealed their Void Refinement Realm cultivation, the atmosphere throughout the arena completely changed.","No one doubted their strength anymore.","The only question remaining was—","Who was stronger?","Upon the arena, Bai Xueqing’s eyes narrowed slightly.","A faint smile appeared on her face.","\"Since we’ve both broken through, there is no need to hold back anymore.\"","Chu Ziyan smiled.","\"Exactly what I was thinking.\"","The next moment—","Both vanished.","Boom!","The ground beneath their feet shattered.","Clang!","Another collision echoed.","However, this time, the force generated was several times greater than before.","Shockwaves swept outward.","The protective formations around the arena immediately activated.","Countless disciples widened their eyes.","Such power was already enough to threaten ordinary Void Refinement cultivators, yet neither side showed any signs of stopping.","Suddenly, Bai Xueqing’s figure retreated.","\"Nine Shadows Flowing Light Sword!\"","Whoosh!","A brilliant sword light erupted.","Then one Bai Xueqing became two.","Two became four.","Four became nine.","Nine identical figures appeared throughout the arena.","Every single one radiated the same aura.","The same presence.","For a moment, even many elders found it difficult to determine which one was real.","The audience immediately erupted.","\"I can’t tell which one is real!\"","\"The Nine Shadows Flowing Light Sword!\"","\"Senior Sister Bai has reached an even higher level of mastery!\"","The nine figures moved simultaneously.","Sword lights flashed from every direction.","Chu Ziyan instantly found herself surrounded. Still, she remained completely calm.","\"Trying to confuse me?\"","A crimson glow emerged around her.","The temperature of the surrounding air rapidly increased.","Her sword slowly rose.","Then countless crimson flower petals appeared. Each petal contained terrifying sword qi.","\"Crimson Petal Tempest!\"","The petals exploded outward like a raging storm.","Thousands of crimson petals filled the arena.","They spun violently in every direction.","Slash! Slash! Slash!","The nine shadows were instantly struck.","One after another, they shattered.","Exploding into fragments of light.","Chu Ziyan understood that trying to differentiate real from fake is almost impossible. Rather it was better to destroy every single one of them.","The audience gasped.","\"She broke it!\"","\"Chu Ziyan destroyed all nine shadows!\"","\"What terrifying control!\"","The crimson storm continued sweeping across the battlefield.","At the last moment, Bai Xueqing’s real body emerged from among the shattered shadows.","Clang!","The two swords collided once more.","A violent shockwave exploded outward.","Neither side gave ground.","Neither side yielded.","The battle only became more intense.","Sword light after sword light illuminated the arena.","One moment Bai Xueqing attacked.","The next Chu Ziyan counterattacked.","Techniques continuously erupted.","Every exchange carried enough power to seriously injure ordinary Void Refinement cultivators.","The audience could no longer remain calm.","Even the elders revealed solemn expressions.","\"Their cultivation realms are already shocking enough.\"","\"But what’s truly terrifying is their mastery over their clan techniques.\"","\"Their comprehension of their techniques is equally monstrous.\"","\"I suspect both of them have already reached Greater Mastery.\"","The surrounding elders immediately fell silent.","Greater Mastery!","The higher the grade of a technique, the more difficult it was to comprehend.","The Chu Clan’s technique was a high-grade Earth Grade Technique while Bai Xueqing’s was a Heaven Grade Technique.","Even Minor Mastery would greatly increase the strength of a technique compared to Beginner Mastery, let alone Greater Mastery.","Among the audience, even the two old men accompanying the young master became increasingly serious.","Originally, they had only been shocked by the girls’ cultivation.","Now, they were beginning to realize something even more frightening.","These two were not merely talented in cultivation.","Their combat foundations were also absurdly solid.","Meanwhile, the young master’s gaze never left the arena.","The possessiveness in his eyes only deepened.","And as the battle continued to escalate, neither Bai Xueqing nor Chu Ziyan showed any intention of stopping.","Clang!","Another collision shook the arena.","Sword qi erupted in every direction as Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan separated once more.","Both stood several hundred meters apart.","Although the battle appeared evenly matched...","Although Chu Ziyan had managed to keep up until now...","She knew that Bai Xueqing was still holding back.","It was merely a feeling and had no proof.","Yet having known Bai Xueqing for so many years, she trusted her instincts.","Chu Ziyan was almost certain that Bai Xueqing still possessed strength she had yet to reveal.","However, she felt no frustration, anger, or resentment.","If she could not force Bai Xueqing to reveal her full strength, then it simply meant she was not worthy of seeing it yet.","The fault would lie with herself, not Bai Xueqing.","Besides, the Chu Clan’s techniques had always been weaker than the Bai Clan’s.","The fact that she could stand here and exchange blows equally with Bai Xueqing was already something she was proud of.","However, being satisfied with herself did not mean she was satisfied with losing.","If she wanted victory, then she needed to surpass her limits.","Boom!","A powerful Qi erupted from Chu Ziyan.","The surrounding spiritual energy also began gathering toward her sword.","The crimson glow around her intensified.","The next moment, Chu Ziyan raised her sword toward the heavens.","Countless waves of Qi gathered above her.","The sky itself seemed to tremble.","\"Heaven Severing Tide!\"","Endless streams of sword qi erupted behind her like a raging sea awakened by a storm.","Layer upon layer of azure tides surged across the arena, each carrying enough force to split mountains apart.","In the end, all of those tides merged into a single heaven-cleaving sword ray that descended with unstoppable momentum.","\"Heaven Grade Technique!\"","\"What terrifying power!\"","The massive azure tide descended.","The sheer pressure caused the arena’s defensive formation to tremble violently.","Among the audience, the young master’s expression finally changed.","His previous arrogance had long disappeared.","Even he had to admit that this attack was powerful.","Very powerful.","Perhaps if he were unprepared, he might even suffer serious injuries from such an attack.","However, Bai Xueqing remained calm.","Her gaze quietly observed the incoming attack.","Then she slowly raised her sword.","A familiar scene appeared within her mind.","An attack capable of freezing heaven and earth.","Back when Feilian had possessed her body, Bai Xueqing had personally experienced that power.","Although she could never replicate it perfectly, over time, she had continuously practiced.","Again.","And again.","And again.","Using nothing but memories, fragments of feelings, and her own comprehension.","Eventually, she succeeded.","A cold aura spread outward. The temperature throughout the arena plummeted.","Frost began appearing upon the ground.","Then Bai Xueqing swung her sword.","\"Icebound Severing Sword!\"","The world seemed to freeze.","A magnificent ice-blue sword light erupted forward.","Everything in its path instantly froze.","The arena.","The air.","Even the surrounding Qi itself.","The young master’s eyes widened.","The two old men immediately sat upright.","Their expressions completely changed.","Boom!","The two techniques collided.","The resulting explosion shook the entire Heaven Sword Sect.","A deafening roar echoed across countless mountain peaks.","The arena’s defensive formation lit up brilliantly.","Violent shockwaves spread in every direction.","Countless disciples were forced to shield their eyes.","Even some elders had to circulate their Qi to protect themselves.","The two old men stared at the battlefield with solemn expressions.","One of them slowly spoke.","\"That technique...\"","His voice contained disbelief.","\"Could it be a High-Grade Heaven Grade Technique?\"","The second old man frowned.","His eyes remained fixed upon the remnants of the ice-blue sword light.","\"Perhaps?\"","Then he hesitated.","For a brief moment, an absurd thought appeared in his mind.","\"It almost feels like...\"","He paused.","Then shook his head.","Impossible.","Absolutely impossible.","\"For a moment, I thought it felt similar to a Saint Grade Technique.\"","The first old man’s expression immediately changed.","Then he shook his head as well.","\"That is impossible.\"","Even in the Central Glorious Continent, Saint Grade Techniques were treasures capable of shaking entire regions.","Countless major powers fought over them.","How could such a technique appear in a place like the Desolate Heaven Empire?","And even if it somehow existed, how could a mere Void Refinement cultivator utilize it?","Even Great Ascension Realm cultivators struggled to use such techniques.","Only those within the Immortal Realm could truly unleash their full power.","Meanwhile, within the battlefield, the outcome had already become clear.","The gigantic crimson tidal wave cracked apart.","Then shattered.","Boom!","The remaining ice-blue sword light continued forward.","Its power had weakened significantly, yet it still carried terrifying force.","Chu Ziyan’s pupils contracted.","Whoosh!","Her figure instantly disappeared.","The ice-blue sword light swept past her previous location.","A moment later—","Boom!","The ground behind her exploded.","A massive frozen trench stretched across the arena.","The audience collectively sucked in cold breaths.","Chu Ziyan landed several hundred meters away.","A few strands of hair drifted down beside her.","Her breathing had become slightly heavier.","Across from her, Bai Xueqing stood calmly.","Although the two had already fought fiercely, it seemed the battle had yet to end.","However, before they could continue—","Clap! Clap! Clap!","A sudden applause echoed throughout the arena.","\"Wonderful!\"","A voice filled with arrogance rang out clearly.","\"You two are good enough to become this young master’s wives!\"","The young master slowly stepped into the arena."]},{"number":618,"title":"Chapter 618: Long Haotian","paragraphs":["\"What?!\"","\"Who the hell is that?!\"","\"Where did this idiot come from?\"","\"Has he gone insane? You dare say such things to Senior Sister Bai and Senior Sister Chu?!\"","...","Countless disciples immediately erupted in fury.","Many were so angry they nearly jumped from their seats, wanting to teach him a lesson.","The battle between Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan had reached its most exciting point, yet someone had actually interrupted it.","And not only interrupted it, he had spoken such shameless words.","Within the Heaven Sword Sect, Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan possessed extremely high status and were admired as role models.","Yet this stranger had appeared out of nowhere and declared that both women should become his wives.","It was simply absurd.","Upon the arena, Bai Xueqing slowly turned her gaze toward the newcomer.","Her eyes narrowed slightly.","The surrounding temperature seemed to drop several degrees.","She carefully scrutinized the young man.","Unfortunately, she did not recognize him, nor did she recognize the clothing he wore.","However, she could feel that he wasn’t weak by any means.","Although he had hidden it quite well, she felt something similar to what she felt when facing Bai Zihan.","More importantly, the confidence he displayed did not appear fake.","Still, his words were extremely offensive which made her very displeased.","Beside her, Chu Ziyan’s expression had also become cold, particularly after hearing him.","After all, she already had a fiancé.","The entire empire knew this. The man was either ignorant or simply did not care.","Neither possibility improved her opinion of him.","Meanwhile, the young master stood proudly in the center of the arena.","As though completely unaware of the hostility surrounding him or perhaps he simply did not care.","His gaze swept across Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan.","The more he looked, the more satisfied he became.","Excellent.","Truly excellent!","The young master’s smile widened.","\"Stop that insolent man!\"","A furious shout interrupted him.","Several Heaven Sword Sect elders rose into the sky.","Their expressions were extremely ugly.","One of the elders pointed toward the arena entrance.","\"You dare disrupt a duel and insult our disciples in the sect?\"","\"Leave immediately!\"","The young master merely glanced at them before laughing.","A trace of contempt appeared in his eyes.","Two figures suddenly appeared beside him.","The surrounding space immediately distorted.","They casually released a trace of their aura.","Only a trace yet the result was immediate.","Boom!","An overwhelming pressure descended upon the arena.","The Heaven Sword Sect elders’ expressions instantly changed.","Their bodies stiffened and all fell on the ground.","Since even the elders were in such a situation, there was no need to elaborate on weaker disciples.","They all felt the pressure.","An aura far beyond Void Refinement Realm.","Far beyond the Great Ascension Realm.","An aura that stood at the peak of countless cultivators’ dreams.","Immortal Realm!","The faces of the Heaven Sword Sect elders immediately paled.","One elder’s voice trembled.","\"Immortal...\"","Another swallowed hard.","\"Two Immortal Realm experts...\"","The surrounding disciples became deathly silent.","The countless insults instantly disappeared.","Fear replaced anger.","Shock replaced outrage.","However, not everyone was completely intimidated.","After all, it wasn’t as though the Heaven Sword Sect lacked one.","As the number one sect in the empire, when had they ever been bullied?","Was two Immortal Realm Cultivators enough to bully their sect?","An elder in the Great Ascension Realm stepped forward.","Although he was still far inferior to an Immortal Realm expert, he managed to withstand the pressure to a certain extent.","His expression was grave as he looked toward the two old men.","Then toward the arrogant young master.","\"Do you know where you are?\"","The elder’s gaze sharpened.","\"This is the Heaven Sword Sect. No matter who you are, you should respect the rules of our sect.\"","Everyone knew the elder was already being extremely polite.","After all, the other side possessed two Immortal Realm experts.","If not for that, would he even be conversing with them?","They would have already subdued them and thrown them into the sect prison.","The young master merely glanced at him.","Then he scoffed.","\"Hmph!\"","His eyes were filled with disdain.","\"A mere Great Ascension Realm cultivator dares lecture me?\"","He waved his hand dismissively.","\"As expected of a backward region. You people truly don’t know your place.\"","The young master continued indifferently.","\"This young master is offering these two women a great opportunity. Who are you to interfere?\"","His tone carried absolute arrogance.","As though everyone present should be grateful.","The elder still wanted to say more, but the two old men immediately suppressed him.","It was already bad enough that their young master had made such a scene and attracted so much attention.","If these elders angered him and he killed one of them, the matter would spiral completely out of control.","Thankfully, the young master completely ignored the elder after he was suppressed.","Instead, he turned toward Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan.","A confident smile appeared on his face.","He clasped his hands behind his back.","Standing proudly in the center of the arena.","\"My name is Long Haotian.\"","His gaze swept over the two women.","\"I have taken a liking to both of you. Therefore, I am willing to give you the opportunity to become my wife.\"","Many disciples stared blankly.","Some were so angry that their faces turned red.","The man’s tone made it sound as though he were bestowing an incredible blessing.","As though becoming his wife was some unimaginable fortune.","The expressions of Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan instantly became colder.","Their moods, which had already been terrible, became even worse.","Chu Ziyan’s eyes were completely devoid of warmth.","\"I already have a fiancé.\"","Her voice was cold and sharp.","\"The entire Desolate Heaven Empire knows this.\"","She looked directly into Long Haotian’s eyes.","\"So stop dreaming.\"","The blunt rejection immediately caused many disciples to feel refreshed.","Some nearly applauded.","Long Haotian’s smile froze slightly.","Clearly, he had not expected such a direct refusal, nor had he expected her to already have a fiancé.","Bai Xueqing also stepped forward.","Her icy gaze landed upon him.","\"You seem to think having Immortal Realm experts behind you makes you some great figure.\"","Her voice remained calm, yet everyone could hear the coldness hidden beneath it.","\"But it is impossible between us!\"","The arena instantly erupted.","\"Well said!\"","\"Senior Sister Bai!\"","\"Hahaha!\"","\"That’s right!\"","\"Who is this idiot to dream of marrying Bai Xueqing? Doesn’t he know that the Bai Clan doesn’t lack Immortal Realm cultivators? He is merely dreaming!\"","The disciples who had been suppressing their anger immediately cheered despite them being suppressed by the two old men’s aura.","Long Haotian’s expression gradually darkened.","For the first time in his life, he had been rejected without the slightest hesitation.","There were countless women of various backgrounds and talents who begged to be with him.","Now that he was offering such an opportunity, rather than being grateful, they dared to refuse him.","But he wasn’t too angry.","He believed it was simply because of their ignorance.","Because they didn’t know who he was.","If they knew he was the heir of the Long Clan, one of the strongest clans in the Central Glorious Continent, he was certain they would regret their decision and beg him.","In the Central Glorious Continent, merely hearing his name was enough for countless people to recognize him immediately.","But here, it seemed that no one had the slightest idea who he was despite him already revealing his name.","\"It seems like you don’t know who I am.\"","There was no need to say more.","In his eyes, the other party was simply ignorant.","Then—","Boom!","A terrifying aura erupted from his body.","The cultivation he had been suppressing was instantly unleashed.","Immortal Realm!","The entire arena fell silent once more.","Who would have thought that such a shameless person would possess such a high cultivation realm?","Countless disciples stared at Long Haotian with widened eyes.","The pressure radiating from his body was simply too overwhelming.","Immortal Realm!","Many people found it difficult to connect that terrifying cultivation with the arrogant young man standing before them.","After all, Long Haotian did not appear particularly old.","In fact, he looked only a few years older than Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan.","Yet he had already stepped into the Immortal Realm.","Such talent was enough to leave countless people speechless.","The Heaven Sword Sect disciples quickly searched their memories.","However, no matter how hard they tried, none of them recognized him.","Not a single person had ever heard of Long Haotian.","This only made the situation stranger.","If someone possessed such monstrous talent, there was no way he should be unknown.","A person like this should have shaken the entire empire long ago.","The only conclusion everyone could reach was obvious.","He was not from the Desolate Heaven Empire, perhaps not even the nearby Empire.","Many people immediately recalled his earlier words.","His arrogant attitude.","His contempt toward the Heaven Sword Sect.","His complete disregard for Chu Ziyan’s engagement to Bai Zihan.","Everything suddenly made sense.","If he was not from the Desolate Heaven Empire, they wouldn’t know about them.","That was why he behaved so recklessly.","Although many disciples hated him, they could not deny one thing.","Long Haotian was terrifying.","Terrifyingly talented.","Terrifyingly powerful.","An Immortal Realm cultivator at such a young age was something they had never even imagined.","No matter how angry they were, they understood the reality before them.","Among everyone present, there was likely no one capable of defeating Long Haotian, not to mention the two old men.","Even the Great Ascension Realm elders who had stepped forward earlier fell silent.","The difference in cultivation was simply too great.","Meanwhile, Long Haotian enjoyed the shocked expressions surrounding him.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","This was the reaction he had expected.","This was the reaction he was accustomed to seeing.","Fear!","Shock!","Awe!","That was how people usually responded after learning who he truly was.","His gaze slowly returned to Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan.","In his mind, now that they had witnessed his cultivation, their attitudes would undoubtedly change.","After all, throughout his life, very few women had been able to remain indifferent after discovering his identity and talent.","Unfortunately for him, the expressions of Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan remained completely unchanged.","Neither showed surprise.","Neither showed admiration.","And neither showed the slightest intention of reconsidering.","Instead, their gazes grew even colder than before."]},{"number":619,"title":"Chapter 619: An Immortal Realm Suitor","paragraphs":["Long Haotian immediately felt awkward.","Because things were not proceeding the way he had imagined.","In fact, they were progressing in the exact opposite direction.","Originally, after revealing his cultivation, he had expected a completely different reaction from Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan.","Shock!","Admiration!","Excitement!","Perhaps even gratitude.","Instead, Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan were still staring at him as though he were some annoying pest that had wandered into their duel.","Not a single trace of admiration could be seen on either woman’s face.","If the two of them were pretending, then they deserved the best actress award.","Long Haotian’s brow twitched slightly.","(It shouldn’t be like this...)","He was genuinely confused.","Back in the Central Glorious Continent, countless women chased after him.","There were daughters of powerful clans and prestigious sects.","Whenever his identity and cultivation were revealed, most people immediately changed their attitude.","They became respectful and would practically throw themselves into his arms.","As a result, Long Haotian had never actually learned how to pursue women.","There had never been any need.","His background alone was enough.","And if not that, then he also possessed top-tier talent.","So now, for perhaps the first time in his life, none of his usual methods were working.","Long Haotian found himself at a complete loss.","If those things failed...","Then what exactly was he supposed to do?","He genuinely had no idea.","After thinking for a moment, he quickly reached a conclusion.","(They must be embarrassed.)","His eyes brightened slightly.","That had to be it!","There was simply no other explanation.","After all, how could women not be moved by someone like him?","The problem definitely wasn’t him.","It had to be them.","Perhaps they were shy about accepting his confession because there were too many people watching.","The more Long Haotian thought about it, the more reasonable it sounded.","Meanwhile, Bai Xueqing’s expression grew increasingly cold.","If she knew what Long Haotian was currently thinking, she would probably stab him immediately.","Beside her, Chu Ziyan was no different.","The two women exchanged a glance.","Neither bothered concealing their disgust.","In fact, their feelings were becoming more obvious by the second.","The man had interrupted their duel.","Insulted them.","Ignored their rejection.","Acted as though they were possessions.","And somehow still believed he was doing them a favor.","Their impressions of him had already dropped below zero.","Unfortunately, Long Haotian completely failed to understand.","Instead, he smiled confidently.","\"As expected.\"","He nodded to himself.","\"You don’t need to be embarrassed.\"","Long Haotian continued speaking.","\"I understand!\"","His tone was unusually gentle.","\"You’ve probably never met someone as great as me before.\"","The disciples nearly choked.","Just what made him think that?","They didn’t know just how much one needed to be thick skinned to be so narcissistic.","Chu Ziyan’s eyelids twitched.","Bai Xueqing’s grip on her sword tightened.","Yet Long Haotian remained completely oblivious.","Bai Xueqing finally spoke. Her voice was colder than ice.","\"Are you done?\"","Long Haotian blinked.","His eyes immediately lit up.","\"So you agree?\"","His tone even carried a hint of excitement.","As though he had finally received the answer he wanted.","Bai Xueqing stared at him.","For a brief moment, she genuinely wondered whether this man understood the language she was speaking.","The veins on her forehead almost twitched.","If Long Haotian had not possessed Immortal Realm cultivation and two Immortal Realm protectors standing behind him, she would have already rushed forward and slapped him several times.","Bai Xueqing was not foolish. She knew very well that she was no match for him.","Thus, she could only suppress her anger.","Though her voice became even colder.","\"Agree? I am rejecting you.\"","She pointed toward Chu Ziyan.","\"Ziyan is already engaged.\"","Then she pointed toward herself.","\"And I have no intention of marrying anyone.\"","Her rejection could not have been any clearer.","Unfortunately, Long Haotian’s expression immediately darkened.","His previously cheerful mood vanished.","\"Engaged?\"","His eyes narrowed.","\"To whom?\"","It seems like finally something has entered his brain.","The tone in his voice was unpleasant.","Very unpleasant!","\"Is he stronger than me?\"","\"Hmph! An engagement is merely an engagement. It can be canceled.\"","His tone sounded extremely natural.","As though canceling someone else’s engagement was no different from deciding what to eat for lunch.","Then his eyes flashed coldly.","\"And if he refuses, I’ll simply teach him a lesson until he agrees.\"","For the first time in years, Bai Xueqing felt that there was someone more arrogant than Bai Zihan.","But even Bai Zihan had never managed to make her feel this level of disgust.","Bai Xueqing realized something.","Talking to Long Haotian was completely pointless.","At this point, she could only wait for the Sect Grand Elders to appear.","Otherwise, this farce would likely continue forever.","Just then—","A loud voice suddenly echoed from the audience.","\"If you’re asking who it is, then I can tell you!\"","Everyone turned toward the source.","His face was filled with excitement.","The disciple pointed toward Chu Ziyan.","\"Senior Sister Chu’s fiancé is Bai Zihan, the younger brother of Bai Xueqing!\"","The entire arena immediately became noisy again.","They knew why the person had decided to answer Long Haotian’s question.","Because he was from the Shen Clan.","Everyone knew about the hatred between the Shen Clan and Bai Zihan.","Shen Liang had been crippled by Bai Zihan, and Bai Zihan had also publicly humiliated them.","Not to mention, Bai Zihan had significantly weakened the Shen Clan’s influence within the Heaven Sword Sect until a new Sect Leader was appointed.","The Shen Clan knew they couldn’t defeat the Bai Clan.","But that didn’t mean the hatred had disappeared.","Now that someone was looking for trouble with Bai Zihan, how could the Shen Clan pass up such an opportunity?","Although he didn’t recognize Long Haotian, one could tell that he got incredible background.","Even if he couldn’t do anything to Bai Zihan, just making trouble for them was good enough.","The Shen Clan disciple wasn’t finished.","He pointed toward Bai Xueqing next.","\"And Senior Sister Bai once publicly declared something as well. Senior Sister Bai said long ago that if anyone wishes to marry her, they must first defeat her younger brother!\"","The moment those words fell, Long Haotian immediately brightened.","If it was simply defeating someone, then that was easy.","Moreover, after learning that it involved defeating Bai Xueqing’s younger brother, he thought it would be even easier.","Since Bai Xueqing was already unparalleled in talent, he subconsciously assumed that Bai Zihan’s cultivation must be lower than hers.","Not only could that fulfill the condition to marry Bai Xueqing, but he could also force Bai Zihan to break his engagement with Chu Ziyan.","He suddenly felt that things had become very easy and convenient.","(I shouldn’t be too harsh on him though.)","Long Haotian thought generously.","After all, if everything went according to plan, Bai Zihan would become his brother-in-law.","Naturally, he should show some mercy and give him some face.","Of course, that was assuming Bai Zihan obediently canceled the engagement.","Otherwise, he would have no choice but to teach him a harsh lesson.","One shouldn’t covet the women that he has eyes on!","Thinking of this, Long Haotian almost laughed.","He truly felt that he was being exceptionally benevolent.","Meanwhile, Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan looked at him as though he had lost his mind.","Long Haotian, however, didn’t seem to notice those gazes.","Instead, he turned toward Bai Xueqing.","\"Is it true?\"","His eyes were shining.","\"...\"","Bai Xueqing remained silent.","Her expression did not change. However, inwardly, she felt somewhat helpless.","Back then, she truly had not thought much about making that statement.","Why would she?","Within the Desolate Heaven Empire, there was practically nobody among the younger generation capable of defeating Bai Zihan.","Even many older cultivators would struggle.","As for those ancient Immortal Realm experts who had lived for thousands of years?","They obviously would not shamelessly run over to challenge Bai Zihan simply to marry her.","And even if some old lunatic actually tried such a thing, she could simply reject him based on age alone.","With her status and background, who would dare force the issue?","Unfortunately, reality always found ways to surprise people.","Who could have imagined that a young Immortal Realm cultivator would suddenly appear?","Seeing Bai Xueqing remain silent, Long Haotian’s smile widened.","In his eyes, silence was basically confirmation.","However, before he could say anything further, several voices suddenly rang out from the audience.","\"It’s true!\"","\"Senior Sister Bai really said that!\"","\"I was there when she said it!\"","\"Everyone in the Desolate Heaven Empire knows about it!\"","...","While many admired Bai Xueqing, not everyone did.","Just like those from the Shen Clan, there were people who disliked her for various reasons.","Clan conflicts.","Personal grudges.","Jealousy.","And many other reasons.","Now that there was an opportunity to make things difficult for Bai Xueqing and Bai Zihan, they immediately jumped at the chance.","Upon hearing confirmation from so many people, Long Haotian laughed again.","\"Hahaha!\"","His laughter echoed throughout the arena.","Excellent!","Truly excellent!","This was even easier than he had imagined.","He looked toward Bai Xueqing.","Then toward Chu Ziyan.","\"In that case, the matter is settled.\"","His tone sounded as though everything had already been decided.","\"I’ll defeat Bai Zihan. Then you, Bai Xueqing, must marry me!\"","His gaze shifted toward Chu Ziyan.","\"And after that, I’ll have him cancel his engagement with you as well.\""]},{"number":620,"title":"Chapter 620: Seeking Bai Zihan","paragraphs":["Long Haotian’s smile grew wider and wider.","The more he thought about it, the more perfect the situation seemed.","In his mind, the matter was already settled.","He merely needed to find this Bai Zihan, defeat him, and then everything would naturally proceed according to plan.","\"Bai Xueqing, don’t worry. Since he is your brother, I will go easy on him.\"","Many disciples immediately revealed ugly expressions when they heard those words.","The way he spoke was simply too arrogant.","It was as though Bai Zihan had already lost.","As though the battle had already happened.","As though the outcome had already been decided.","Moreover, going easy on Bai Zihan?","Well, good luck with that.","Meanwhile, the two old men behind him exchanged glances.","Neither looked particularly pleased.","Truthfully speaking, they were already dissatisfied with how much attention Long Haotian had attracted.","Their mission was very important.","The clan had specifically sent them to the Desolate Heaven Empire for a reason.","Yet ever since arriving, Long Haotian had done everything except focus on that mission.","First, he interrupted the duel between Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan.","Then he publicly declared his intention to marry them.","Now he wanted to challenge some unknown person.","If they were to do so right now, it would waste much of their time that could be invested into their mission.","Moreover, if this continued, their presence might become known throughout the entire empire.","That was the exact opposite of what they wanted.","Unfortunately, who was Long Haotian?","Once he made a decision, changing his mind was nearly impossible.","The two old men had watched him grow up.","They understood him better than anyone.","Trying to stop him now would be like trying to stop a flood with bare hands.","The first old man finally decided to try.","\"Young Master, our mission should take priority.\"","Long Haotian waved his hand dismissively.","\"It won’t take long.\"","The old man’s eyelid twitched.","The second old man also tried.","\"Young Master, attracting unnecessary attention may not be beneficial.\"","Long Haotian laughed.","\"Attention?\"","His expression was filled with confidence.","\"What attention is there to fear? Moreover, do you think others don’t already know about our presence here?\"","The two old men immediately became speechless.","Although he was merely saying those things because he didn’t want to stop but thinking about it carefully, he was not entirely wrong.","While they hoped to remain unnoticed, they already knew such a thing was nearly impossible.","Especially now that Long Haotian had made such a commotion, their presence had most likely already been exposed.","Meanwhile, Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan watched him in complete disgust.","The more he spoke, the worse their impression became.","This man had not even met Bai Zihan.","He had never exchanged a single blow with him.","He didn’t even know what kind of person Bai Zihan was.","Yet he was already speaking as though victory was guaranteed.","It was ridiculous.","Bai Xueqing’s eyes narrowed slightly.","A faint sneer almost appeared on her face.","Defeat Bai Zihan?","Did he really think it was that simple?","He was even saying that he would go easy on him.","She truly wanted to see whether he would still say those words after actually fighting Bai Zihan.","Beside her, Chu Ziyan shared similar thoughts.","Her expression remained cold.","Yet inwardly, she almost felt amused.","Wanting to challenge Bai Zihan?","Just listening to Long Haotian’s words alone made it obvious that he was simply an ignorant person who had no idea what kind of monster he was about to provoke.","Long Haotian’s confidence only continued to grow.","He looked toward the two women.","\"Where is Bai Zihan?\"","His voice echoed throughout the arena.","\"I’ll go find him right now.\"","Neither Bai Xueqing nor Chu Ziyan answered.","\"...\"","In fact, both women looked at him as though he were an idiot.","Why would they help him?","Unfortunately, their silence could not stop him.","\"I know where he is!\"","The very same disciple from the Shen Clan shouted excitedly.","\"If the Young Master wishes to find Bai Zihan, I can lead the way!\"","Long Haotian’s eyes immediately brightened.","\"Oh?\"","A smile appeared on his face.","\"You know where he is?\"","The Shen Clan disciple immediately nodded.","\"I do!\"","Long Haotian laughed loudly.","\"Hahaha! Excellent!\"","He was becoming increasingly pleased with this disciple.","First, he had informed him about Chu Ziyan’s fiancé.","Then he had revealed Bai Xueqing’s condition.","And now he was willing to lead him directly to Bai Zihan.","This was truly a helpful person.","Long Haotian had always disliked owing favors.","Since the other party had helped him repeatedly, naturally he should be rewarded.","With a casual flick of his wrist, a jade bottle flew through the air.","Whoosh!","The Shen Clan disciple instinctively caught it.","Long Haotian spoke casually.","\"Take it! A reward for your assistance.\"","The Shen Clan disciple was stunned.","He had not expected a reward.","Truthfully, he had only spoken up because he wanted to make things difficult for Bai Zihan.","However, when he opened the bottle and examined its contents, his eyes nearly popped out of their sockets.","His breathing instantly became hurried.","Inside were several pills.","Grade-7 Pills!","The disciple’s entire body trembled.","Even some nearby elders widened their eyes after sensing the aura coming from the bottle.","Grade-7 Pills!","And Long Haotian had casually thrown them out as a reward.","As though they were completely worthless.","The Shen Clan disciple immediately sucked in a cold breath.","His heart pounded wildly.","What kind of background did Long Haotian possess?","Even Top Clan like Zhao and Li Clan treated Grade-7 Pills as priceless treasures.","Yet Long Haotian handed them out like candy.","The disciple’s attitude changed almost instantly.","The scheming look in his eyes disappeared.","In its place appeared genuine respect.","No—","Reverence!","He hurriedly bowed respectfully.","\"Thank you, Young Master!\"","His voice was filled with excitement.","At this moment, his thoughts were racing wildly.","Perhaps...","This was an opportunity.","An opportunity far greater than he had ever imagined.","If he could make a connection with someone like Long Haotian, his position within the Shen Clan would rise dramatically.","Perhaps even becoming the heir would no longer be impossible.","The more he thought about it, the more excited he became.","Meanwhile, Long Haotian nodded in satisfaction.","Yes!","This was the normal reaction.","This was how people normally responded to him.","Not like Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan.","Looking at the disciple, Long Haotian smiled.","\"Very good. Lead the way.\"","The Shen Clan disciple immediately straightened his back.","\"Yes, Young Master Long!\"","Then Long Haotian turned toward the two old men.","\"Bring them with us.\"","The two old men frowned.","\"Young Master...\"","Long Haotian waved his hand dismissively.","\"No need to say anything.\"","His gaze landed upon Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan.","A confident smile appeared on his face.","\"I want them to witness it personally. Witness how I defeat Bai Zihan.\"","His voice carried absolute certainty.","As though the outcome had already been decided.","The two old men inwardly sighed.","As expected, their young master had become completely invested in this matter.","At this point, there was no stopping him.","Better to quickly finish this and continue with their mission.","Just as the two old men were about to move—","A calm voice suddenly echoed throughout the arena.","\"There is no need.\"","The voice was neither loud nor domineering.","Yet the moment it appeared, the entire arena instantly fell silent.","\"I am already here!\""]},{"number":621,"title":"Chapter 621: The Beginning of Long Haotian’s Misfortune","paragraphs":["Bai Zihan had instructed Kong Zhanhong long ago to keep an eye on various suspicious individuals entering the Desolate Heaven Empire.","And that naturally included Long Haotian and his two bodyguards.","The three had been on his radar ever since they appeared in the Capital with their luxurious carriage.","From the very beginning, they had been suspected to be outsiders. And clearly, that judgment had not been mistaken.","Of course, they were not the only suspicious individuals.","There were also several other groups suspected to have come from outside the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Through the intelligence network Kong Zhanhong had painstakingly built over the years, reports continuously flowed in from every major city.","Thus, Bai Zihan learned about Long Haotian’s movements almost immediately.","Including the moment they departed from the Capital and headed toward the Heaven Sword Sect.","The moment Bai Zihan received that report, his closed eyes slowly opened.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"Heaven Sword Sect...\"","Although he did not know why they were going there, he immediately realized that this was an excellent opportunity.","Because the current Sect Leader, Han Sha, was under his control.","If he wished to move against someone inside the Heaven Sword Sect, things would become much easier with Han Sha’s cooperation.","As for what he intended to do with them was simple.","Capture them and interrogate them.","No matter how much he observed them, Bai Zihan still could not determine their true objective.","He knew they were searching for something.","That much was obvious.","Yet what exactly they sought remained unclear.","Therefore, he planned to capture them and interrogate them personally.","After all, people from the Central Glorious Continent won’t travel thousands upon thousands of miles for trivial matters.","There had to be a reason.","Something important enough to attract their interest toward the Desolate Heaven Empire.","And if such a thing truly existed then Bai Zihan needed to know exactly what it was.","Bai Zihan held no personal hostility toward the three.","But unfortunately for them, they had chosen to head toward a place where it would become very easy for him to deal with them.","After making his decision, Bai Zihan immediately issued an order.","\"Summon Grand Elder Bai Ren and Grand Elder Bai Chu.\"","Bai Zihan had no intention of mobilizing the entire Bai Clan.","Not only would that be unnecessary, but it would also alert the enemy.","Besides, the Heaven Sword Sect itself already possessed more than enough manpower.","Thus, he only chose to bring the two strongest Bai Clan Grand Elders.","Because he knew very well that the three outsiders would not be simple opponents.","Their cultivation might even rival Qin Lingxiao.","Therefore, he naturally could not be careless.","Soon afterward, Bai Zihan quietly arrived at the Heaven Sword Sect and followed the three toward the Sect Arena.","Bai Zihan frowned slightly.","\"The arena?\"","His expression became somewhat strange.","At that moment, Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan were currently engaged in their duel.","Why would these outsiders head there?","To watch a fight?","Bai Zihan genuinely found it difficult to understand.","\"Do they have that much free time?\"","He honestly wondered.","Thus, accompanied by Bai Ren and Bai Chu, he quietly entered the arena.","To avoid attracting attention, he concealed his appearance and suppressed his aura.","From beginning to end, nobody noticed his arrival.","Then he silently watched everything unfold.","Truthfully speaking, he did not pay much attention to the duel itself.","Instead, most of his focus remained on Long Haotian and the two old men.","Then Long Haotian suddenly interrupted the duel.","And publicly declared that Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan were worthy of becoming his wives.","Bai Zihan stood silently within the crowd.","\"...\"","For a moment, he genuinely became speechless.","Then he nearly face-palmed.","He had spent so much effort trying to determine Long Haotian’s objective.","Was this really it?","Was marrying women truly his purpose?","It didn’t seem likely.","Yet somehow, the man’s focus had completely shifted toward Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan.","Bai Zihan suddenly felt disappointed.","Beside him, Bai Ren and Bai Chu’s expressions immediately darkened.","A terrifying pressure flickered within their eyes.","The moods of the two elders instantly became terrible.","Someone had appeared out of nowhere and publicly declared his intention to marry a princess of the Bai Clan.","Who gave him such courage?","And worse, Long Haotian was not merely targeting Bai Xueqing.","He was also targeting Chu Ziyan, Bai Zihan’s fiancée.","Yet this stranger openly declared that he wanted to take her for himself.","The two elders were already suppressing the urge to rush out and teach him a lesson.","Had it not been for Bai Zihan stopping them, they likely would have acted long ago.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan remained calm.","He simply continued watching.","One thing after another.","The rejection.","The arguments.","The arrogant declarations.","The increasingly shameless behavior.","And finally, Long Haotian decided that he would defeat him personally.","He would force Bai Zihan to cancel the engagement.","Then marry Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan himself.","Bai Zihan rubbed his forehead.","Even he was beginning to feel mentally exhausted.","\"This fellow...\"","For the first time in a long while, Bai Zihan genuinely did not know what to say.","Eventually, Long Haotian demanded to know his whereabouts.","Then he declared that he would personally go find him.","Bai Zihan sighed softly.","At that point, there was no longer any reason to remain hidden.","After all, this was an excellent opportunity.","Thus, Bai Zihan finally stepped forward.","His gaze landed directly upon Long Haotian.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","Then his calm voice echoed throughout the arena.","\"There is no need. I am here!\"","The moment the voice echoed throughout the arena, countless gazes immediately turned toward him.","Long Haotian’s eyes narrowed slightly.","His gaze carefully swept over Bai Zihan.","Then he turned toward the Shen Clan disciple beside him.","Long Haotian pointed toward the approaching figure.","\"Is he Bai Zihan?\"","The Shen Clan disciple instinctively stiffened.","The moment his eyes landed on Bai Zihan, a trace of fear flashed across them.","His scalp instantly went numb.","His heartbeat accelerated.","After all, this was Bai Zihan.","Hatred was one thing.","Fear was another.","If Bai Zihan were absent, he naturally dared to scheme against him.","But now that Bai Zihan was personally standing before him...","The pressure was entirely different.","Still, after glancing toward Long Haotian and remembering the terrifying cultivation and background behind him, the disciple forcibly steadied himself.","He immediately nodded vigorously.","\"Y-Yes! That’s Bai Zihan!\"","\"There is absolutely no mistake!\"","Upon receiving confirmation, Long Haotian’s eyes instantly brightened.","A smile spread across his face.","Excellent!","Truly excellent!","Originally, he had planned to waste time searching for Bai Zihan personally.","Instead, the man had delivered himself directly to him.","What could be more convenient?","Long Haotian’s mood instantly improved.","At the very least, Bai Zihan had saved him the trouble of searching.","Thus, Long Haotian burst into laughter.","\"Hahaha!\"","His laughter echoed throughout the arena.","Then he looked directly toward Bai Zihan.","His eyes shone with excitement.","\"Good! You’ve arrived at exactly the right time!\"","His tone carried genuine satisfaction.","As though Bai Zihan had just done him an enormous favor.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan merely glanced at Long Haotian.","Then his gaze shifted toward the two old men standing behind him.","His eyes lingered on them briefly.","The two old men immediately felt a faint sense of discomfort.","Most people would become nervous when facing two Immortal Realm experts.","Yet Bai Zihan looked at them as though he were calmly evaluating ordinary cultivators.","The feeling was extremely strange.","Meanwhile, Long Haotian remained completely oblivious.","He pointed toward Bai Xueqing.","Then toward Chu Ziyan.","His actions were so natural that they almost appeared reasonable.","\"I’ll keep this simple.\"","Long Haotian continued confidently.","\"Your sister and your fiancée have both caught my eye.\"","Bai Ren’s eyelid twitched violently.","Bai Chu’s face darkened completely.","Long Haotian, however, continued speaking without noticing anything unusual.","\"So I need you to do two things.\"","He raised one finger.","\"First. Allow me to marry your sister.\"","Then he raised a second finger.","\"Second. Cancel your engagement with Chu Ziyan, so that I can marry her.\"","His tone remained completely serious.","As though these were perfectly reasonable requests.","\"Of course, I will compensate you generously!\""]},{"number":622,"title":"Chapter 622: Do you even deserve that?","paragraphs":["Bai Zihan looked at Long Haotian quietly, then a faint smile appeared on his face.","Long Haotian immediately noticed it.","His mood improved slightly.","(As expected, he is quite happy to hear his generous proposal.)","He thought.","After all, who wouldn’t be happy?","He was the heir of a Top Clan from the Central Glorious Continent.","His talent was unparalleled.","His background was monstrous.","His future was limitless.","To become his brother-in-law was an opportunity countless people could only dream of.","In Long Haotian’s eyes, this was no different from a chicken transforming into a phoenix.","Naturally, he thought that Bai Zihan should be delighted.","Thus, Long Haotian waited confidently for Bai Zihan’s response.","Then Bai Zihan finally spoke.","\"Do you even deserve that?\"","Silence!","The smile on Long Haotian’s face froze instantly.","Long Haotian blinked.","Then his expression slowly darkened.","\"What did you say?\"","His voice became noticeably colder.","Bai Zihan merely smiled.","\"Are your ears also malfunctioning now?\"","His gaze swept over Long Haotian leisurely.","Then he shook his head slightly.","\"Toad dreaming about eating swan meat!\"","The surrounding disciples immediately lowered their heads.","Many were desperately suppressing their laughter.","Meanwhile, Long Haotian’s face became increasingly ugly.","\"You!\"","His voice contained a warning.","\"I advise you to think carefully before speaking. Do you know who this young master is?\"","Immortal Realm pressure subtly leaked from his body.","Many disciples immediately felt their breathing become difficult, yet Bai Zihan remained completely unaffected.","Long Haotian continued coldly.","\"You should understand your position. I am already giving you plenty of face!\"","His expression became increasingly arrogant.","\"Don’t mistake my goodwill for weakness.\"","Then he sneered.","\"Don’t refuse a toast only to be forced to drink a forfeit!\"","His eyes flashed coldly.","\"I sincerely advise you not to choose the second option.\"","The threat was obvious.","Everyone present could hear it clearly.","Long Haotian took another step forward. His aura surged slightly.","\"Because once I start using force...\"","His gaze locked onto Bai Zihan.","\"You won’t like the outcome.\"","Countless eyes turned toward Bai Zihan.","Waiting for his reaction.","Waiting to see whether he would back down.","However, Bai Zihan simply smiled.","\"I see!\"","Long Haotian thought he had finally understood.","A trace of satisfaction appeared on his face.","Unfortunately, Bai Zihan’s next words immediately shattered that illusion.","\"Then I’d quite like to see it.\"","Long Haotian stared at him.","Bai Zihan met his gaze calmly.","As though he genuinely wanted to see what Long Haotian could do.","Long Haotian felt something was wrong.","The confidence before him did not seem fake, yet that was impossible.","No matter how talented Bai Zihan was, he should be younger than Bai Xueqing.","Meanwhile, he was already an Immortal Realm expert.","The difference between them should have been insurmountable.","Behind Long Haotian, the two old men narrowed their eyes.","While they found Bai Zihan strange, their focus was on Bai Ren and Bai Chu.","They didn’t know why, but those two gave them a feeling of threat, almost as though they were as strong as they were.","However, they shook their heads. They didn’t think that should be possible.","They were two of the strongest cultivators in the Central Glorious Continent.","How could people from such a remote place possess strength comparable to theirs?","Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan silently watched everything unfold.","Previously, when Long Haotian had revealed his Immortal Realm cultivation, both of them had been somewhat worried.","After all, regardless of how arrogant he was, his strength was real.","However, the moment Bai Zihan appeared, those worries quietly disappeared.","The two women understood him far too well, especially that expression.","That calm smile and relaxed demeanor.","When Bai Zihan acted like this, it usually meant one thing.","Everything was already under control.","At least, that was what Chu Ziyan believed.","Looking at Bai Zihan’s back, the coldness in her eyes gradually softened.","Meanwhile, Bai Xueqing’s thoughts were on different things.","While she also trusted Bai Zihan completely, she knew her younger brother better than almost anyone.","Therefore, something immediately felt suspicious.","The timing was too perfect.","Not only had Bai Zihan appeared at exactly the right moment, he had also brought Grand Elder Bai Ren and Grand Elder Bai Chu with him.","That was definitely not a coincidence.","Bai Xueqing’s eyes narrowed slightly.","(He’s planning something.)","The thought immediately surfaced in her mind.","She knew that Bai Zihan never acted without purpose.","Still, regardless of what Bai Zihan was planning, one thing was certain.","Long Haotian had already become his target.","And once Bai Zihan set his sights on someone...","Their fate was usually not very pleasant.","Unfortunately, the person in question remained completely unaware.","Long Haotian’s expression became uglier and uglier.","The more Bai Zihan spoke, the angrier he became.","In his eyes, he had already shown tremendous generosity.","He had even considered treating Bai Zihan as a future brother-in-law.","Yet instead of gratitude, he received mockery.","Long Haotian felt that his goodwill had been completely trampled upon.","His expression darkened.","\"So be it!\"","His voice became cold.","\"Since you refuse to recognize what’s good for you...\"","A terrifying aura surged from his body.","The surrounding air immediately became heavy.","\"Then I can only do this the hard way.\"","Immortal Realm pressure swept across the arena.","Many disciples instantly felt their blood qi fluctuate.","Some weaker disciples even turned pale.","Long Haotian’s gaze looked down upon Bai Zihan.","Arrogant and domineering.","Like a ruler looking down upon a mortal.","Then his voice echoed throughout the entire arena.","\"Bai Zihan! I challenge you! Do you dare accept it?\"","The moment those words fell, the entire Heaven Sword Sect erupted.","Countless disciples immediately became excited.","Fear?","There was definitely fear.","After all, Long Haotian was an Immortal Realm cultivator.","But excitement quickly overwhelmed it.","Because opportunities like this were simply too rare.","An Immortal Realm battle!","Many cultivators could spend their entire lives without witnessing one.","And now they might witness it with their own eyes.","Moreover, one of the participants was Bai Zihan.","The legendary genius of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","The man who had overturned countless impossible situations.","The man whose strength nobody could accurately measure.","Instantly, everyone’s attention became focused.","Even the elders could not remain calm.","The atmosphere reached an unprecedented level.","The atmosphere inside the Heaven Sword Sect’s arena reached its peak.","Countless eyes were fixed upon Bai Zihan.","Would he accept? Or would he refuse?","After all, his opponent was an Immortal Realm cultivator.","Bai Zihan merely stood there calmly.","Outwardly, his expression remained unchanged.","Internally, however, he was already weighing several considerations.","Agreeing had several benefits.","The first was time.","Han Sha had already received his instructions, but mobilizing the Heaven Sword Sect’s forces still required time.","The longer Long Haotian remained occupied, the better.","A duel would naturally buy him that time.","The second reason was curiosity.","Bai Zihan had heard countless legends regarding the Central Glorious Continent.","He wanted to see for himself whether those stories were exaggerated or true.","He knew that there was a high chance of war between the Desolate Heaven Empire and the Central Glorious Continent.","So, it was a good idea to learn about their strengths.","And now, a perfect test subject had conveniently delivered himself to his doorstep.","The third reason...","Bai Zihan glanced at Long Haotian.","Then a faint smile appeared on his face.","He simply wanted to beat him up.","The fellow was truly irritating.","Thus, after a brief moment of silence, Bai Zihan finally nodded.","\"Sure, why not!\"","A confident smile appeared on Long Haotian’s face.","Then he suddenly raised a hand.","\"Wait!\"","Long Haotian looked toward Bai Zihan.","\"If we’re going to fight, then let’s make things more interesting.\"","Bai Zihan raised an eyebrow.","\"Oh?\"","Long Haotian clasped his hands behind his back.","His expression was full of confidence.","\"Let’s make a bet!\"","Long Haotian pointed toward Chu Ziyan.","\"If I win.\"","His voice echoed throughout the arena.","\"You will dissolve your engagement with her.\"","The moment those words fell, Chu Ziyan’s expression instantly became cold.","Yet Long Haotian remained completely serious.","Bai Zihan did not immediately agree.","Instead, he looked at Long Haotian.","Then he casually asked,","\"And if you lose?\"","Long Haotian blinked.","For a brief moment, he genuinely froze.","Lose?","The word felt unfamiliar.","The possibility had never crossed his mind.","After all, he was Long Haotian.","He was an Immortal Realm cultivator.","How could he lose to someone from the Desolate Heaven Empire?","The very idea sounded absurd.","Thus, after a short pause, Long Haotian laughed loudly.","\"Hahaha!\"","His laughter was filled with absolute confidence.","Then he proudly declared,","\"If I lose?\"","He spread his arms.","\"Then name your price!\"","His voice thundered throughout the arena.","\"Anything you wish!\"","The two old men behind him immediately frowned.","Their expressions changed slightly.","Unfortunately, Long Haotian either failed to notice or simply didn’t care.","His confidence had already reached its peak.","After all, in his mind, there was only one outcome to this battle.","Victory!","Therefore, making promises cost him nothing.","As long as Bai Zihan accepts his bet!"]},{"number":623,"title":"Chapter 623: The Fish Takes the Bait","paragraphs":["Bai Zihan did not answer immediately.","Although he had already made his decision internally, he still needed to appear somewhat reluctant.","Several moments passed before Bai Zihan finally nodded.","\"Very well!\"","Long Haotian’s smile widened.","However, before he could speak, Bai Zihan continued.","\"But verbal agreements are cheap.\"","The smile on Long Haotian’s face paused slightly.","Bai Zihan looked at him and spoke leisurely.","\"If you’re serious about this wager, then make a Heavenly Vow.\"","The entire arena instantly fell silent.","Even Long Haotian’s expression stiffened slightly.","A Heavenly Vow?","The smile on his face immediately became somewhat forced.","Unlike ordinary promises, Heavenly Vows were not things cultivators made lightly, especially powerful cultivators.","Breaking such a vow could result in terrifying consequences.","Long Haotian’s eyes narrowed.","Behind him, the expressions of the two old men immediately changed.","\"Young Master!\"","\"A mere native from a remote empire is not worth making a Heavenly Vow over.\"","Although they believed Long Haotian would win, neither of them liked unnecessary risks.","After all, Heavenly Vows were not jokes.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan merely smiled as he looked at Long Haotian.","\"What?\"","His tone was filled with mockery.","\"Scared of losing?\"","The moment those words fell, Long Haotian’s face darkened.","Bai Zihan had struck precisely where it hurt the most.","Long Haotian’s pride!","The two old men inwardly cursed.","Sure enough, Long Haotian’s expression immediately became ugly.","\"Scared?\"","He almost laughed.","\"Me?\"","A powerful aura erupted from his body.","His eyes burned with anger.","\"How could this young master possibly lose?\"","Bai Zihan shrugged.","\"Then why hesitate?\"","The simple sentence instantly shattered the last traces of Long Haotian’s hesitation.","His pride simply would not allow him to back down, especially in front of Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan.","Long Haotian immediately sneered.","\"Fine! A Heavenly Vow it is!\"","Then he looked at Bai Zihan.","\"But if I make one, you will make one as well.\"","His eyes narrowed.","\"I don’t trust your words either.\"","Bai Zihan smiled.","\"Of course!\"","His agreement came so quickly that Long Haotian was momentarily stunned.","Naturally, Long Haotian had no way of knowing that Bai Zihan cared very little about Heavenly Vows.","After surviving Heavenly Tribulations before, he was no longer particularly fearful of them, even if he were to break one.","Not to mention, he had absolutely no intention of losing.","Thus, under countless gazes, the two stepped forward.","Long Haotian raised his hand. His voice echoed throughout the arena.","\"I, Long Haotian, swear upon Heaven and Earth. If I lose this battle, I shall fulfill one request made by Bai Zihan.\"","Seeing this, Bai Zihan smiled as he also raised his hand.","His voice remained calm.","\"I, Bai Zihan, swear upon Heaven and Earth. If I lose this battle, I shall dissolve my engagement with Chu Ziyan.\"","There was no turning back now.","Long Haotian’s confidence returned instantly.","In fact, it became even stronger than before.","Now that the Heavenly Vow had been established, victory would bring him everything he wanted.","Thinking about it, he could not help but smile.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan was equally satisfied.","Everything was proceeding exactly as planned.","The fish had already swallowed the bait.","Now all that remained was reeling it in.","The two old men behind Long Haotian exchanged uneasy glances.","For some reason, they could not shake the feeling that something was wrong.","Unfortunately, it was already too late.","The Heavenly Vow had been made.","There was no withdrawing now.","At the center of the arena, Long Haotian slowly stepped forward.","Immortal Realm aura surged from his body like a tidal wave.","Across from him, Bai Zihan remained calm.","A faint smile lingered on his face.","Long Haotian’s eyes blazed with excitement.","The Heavenly Vow had already been established.","The bet had been set.","Everything was in place.","A magnanimous expression appeared on his face.","\"Bai Zihan!\"","His tone became unexpectedly generous.","\"Although you have agreed to this fight, I don’t wish for others to say that I bullied you.\"","Long Haotian continued.","\"After all, I am already in the Immortal Realm.\"","He clasped his hands behind his back.","\"If you wish, I can suppress my cultivation to match yours.\"","Long Haotian wasn’t finished.","\"I can also refrain from using my artifacts.\"","With Bai Zihan’s background, he probably possessed an Earth Grade Artifact at best.","Meanwhile, Long Haotian possessed several Top Grade Heaven Grade Artifacts personally bestowed upon him by his clan.","If he revealed them now, Bai Zihan might lose all confidence before the battle even began.","Moreover, defeating a weakling with his full cultivation and artifacts felt somewhat excessive.","At least in Long Haotian’s mind.","He was giving Bai Zihan plenty of face.","Thus, he proudly continued,","\"How about it? This young master is more than willing to give you a handicap.\"","Bai Zihan looked at Long Haotian quietly.","Truthfully speaking, under normal circumstances, he would gladly agree.","Why wouldn’t he?","If an enemy voluntarily weakened himself, only a fool would refuse.","Unfortunately, today was different.","Bai Zihan actually wanted to see the true standards of the Central Glorious Continent.","He wanted to know how strong they really were.","If Long Haotian suppressed himself, there would be little point.","Thus, Bai Zihan slowly shook his head.","\"Cut the crap. Come at me with your full strength.\"","Then a mocking smile appeared on his face.","\"You can talk about handicaps after you manage to land a punch on me.\"","Long Haotian’s expression froze.","The smile on his face slowly disappeared.","Then—","Crack!","A faint cracking sound echoed.","Several veins bulged on his forehead.","His fists clenched tightly.","Land a punch?","This fellow was actually questioning whether he could even touch him?","Long Haotian gritted his teeth.","His eyes became increasingly dangerous.","In his mind, Bai Zihan had become the most irritating person he had ever met.","This fellow simply refused to appreciate kindness.","No matter what he said, Bai Zihan always found a way to mock him.","Finally, Long Haotian’s patience reached its limit.","Long Haotian stared directly at Bai Zihan.","His eyes burned with anger.","\"Fine!\"","His voice echoed throughout the arena.","\"If that’s what you want, then don’t blame me later.\"","Bai Zihan merely smiled.","Long Haotian felt his blood pressure rise even further.","This fellow was smiling again.","At this point, he desperately wanted to wipe that smile off Bai Zihan’s face.","Thus, he no longer wasted words.","His fighting intent surged toward the heavens.","\"Let’s fight!\""]},{"number":624,"title":"Chapter 624: Long Haotian Vs Bai Zihan!","paragraphs":["The ground beneath Long Haotian’s feet exploded.","His figure instantly disappeared.","Countless disciples widened their eyes.","Too fast!","Even many elders could barely follow his movements.","All they could see was a blurry streak tearing through the arena.","Whoosh!","Long Haotian’s figure appeared directly in front of Bai Zihan.","His lips curled upward.","A sneer appeared on his face.","(As expected!)","Bai Zihan was still standing there without even having time to react.","Long Haotian inwardly laughed.","(He can’t even keep up with my speed. Let’s see you talk after taking this punch!)","The difference between the Immortal Realm and lower realms was enormous.","No matter how talented Bai Zihan was, there was no way he could react.","Long Haotian raised his fist.","His punch shot directly toward Bai Zihan’s face.","Unfortunately—","Before his fist could even arrive, another fist suddenly appeared in his vision.","Long Haotian’s pupils contracted.","\"What?!\"","The next moment—","Bang!!!","A terrifying impact erupted.","Long Haotian felt as though a mountain had smashed into his face.","His entire body instantly lost control.","Blood sprayed from his mouth.","Then his figure shot backward like a cannonball.","Bang!","The arena shook violently. Dust and rubble filled the air.","Silence!","Absolute silence!","Everyone stared blankly at the scene before them.","Nobody could comprehend what had just happened.","A moment ago, Long Haotian appeared impossibly fast.","A moment later, he had been punched across the arena.","The two old men behind him froze.","Their eyes widened. Their calm expressions completely disappeared.","\"Impossible!\"","The first old man blurted out.","The second old man’s face changed dramatically.","Their divine senses instantly swept toward Bai Zihan.","The result made their hearts tremble.","Great Ascension Realm!","Bai Zihan was actually a Great Ascension Realm cultivator!","Their minds shook violently.","(How old was he?)","Not only had he reached the Great Ascension Realm at such an age, he had also sent Long Haotian flying with a single punch.","Even if Long Haotian had underestimated Bai Zihan and held back, that should still have been impossible.","Even ordinary Immortal Realm cultivators might not be capable of such a thing.","Meanwhile, Bai Ren and Bai Chu remained calm.","Neither looked surprised.","To them, this outcome was perfectly normal.","In fact, if Bai Zihan had been the one sent flying, that would have been truly shocking.","Boom!","The pile of rubble suddenly exploded.","A figure shot out.","Long Haotian immediately reappeared.","His clothes were somewhat disheveled.","A clear fist mark could be seen on his face.","His expression was filled with disbelief.","He stared at Bai Zihan.","As though looking at a monster.","\"You...\"","His voice trembled slightly.","Genuine shock appeared on his face.","\"You...\"","Long Haotian pointed at him.","Then finally blurted out,","\"You’re in the Great Ascension Realm?!\"","Bai Zihan might have been able to deceive others before, but once a battle against an Immortal Realm cultivator began, hiding his cultivation became nearly impossible.","Not to mention, Bai Zihan had not even attempted to conceal his aura when he struck.","The entire arena exploded into chaos.","\"What?!\"","\"Great Ascension Realm?!\"","\"Clan Leader Bai is in the Great Ascension Realm?!\"","\"How is that possible?!\"","Countless disciples nearly screamed.","Even many elders were stunned.","Previously, it was already shocking enough that Bai Zihan had reached the Void Refinement Realm.","Yet less than a year had passed, and now he had entered the Great Ascension Realm.","What kind of cultivation speed was that?","Everyone felt as though lightning had struck their minds.","A Great Ascension Realm cultivator!","Under twenty years old!","Many elders suddenly felt that they had cultivated their entire lives for nothing.","Meanwhile, Long Haotian continued staring at Bai Zihan.","His mind was in complete disorder.","Originally, he had assumed Bai Zihan would be at most in the Nascent Soul Realm.","Perhaps Soul Formation Realm if he was exceptionally talented.","That alone would already qualify him as a top genius, even in the Central Glorious Continent.","Yet reality had viciously slapped him across the face.","Not only was Bai Zihan a Great Ascension Realm cultivator, he was powerful enough to send an Immortal Realm expert flying with a single punch.","Even if Long Haotian had been caught off guard, that should still have been extremely difficult.","After all, his physique was one of the top physiques within his clan.","Long Haotian’s expression twisted.","Even now, he still could not understand it.","How?","How had Bai Zihan sent him flying with a single punch?","His face still throbbed painfully.","The pain was so intense that even speaking caused the muscles in his face to twitch.","For a brief moment, he almost doubted reality.","He couldn’t remember the last time someone had hit him this hard.","In fact, even when his father personally beat him during training, it had never hurt this much.","The more he thought about it, the uglier his expression became.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan merely glanced at him casually.","Even though Bai Zihan could have taken advantage of the situation to attack him, it seems like he has no intention of doing that.","It was as if he didn’t care about the duel nor took it seriously.","That attitude immediately infuriated Long Haotian.","His fists clenched.","His teeth ground together.","That arrogance should have belonged to him!","Not Bai Zihan!","He was the Immortal Realm cultivator.","Yet somehow...","The roles had become completely reversed.","\"Looks like you overestimated yourself.\"","Bai Zihan’s gaze swept across Long Haotian.","Then he leisurely added,","\"You can’t even withstand a single punch of mine.\"","Long Haotian’s face instantly turned red.","Not from embarrassment but from anger.","\"Don’t get cocky!\"","His roar echoed throughout the arena.","\"That was only because you caught me off guard!\"","Immortal Realm aura exploded from his body.","The rubble around him instantly shattered.","His eyes burned with fury.","\"The real battle starts now!\"","Shing!","A sharp sword cry suddenly echoed throughout the arena.","Long Haotian took out his sword from his storage ring.","\"Heaven Grade Artifact!\"","\"No! It’s a Top Grade Heaven Grade Sword!\"","Shock appeared on countless faces.","Even many elders revealed expressions of envy.","Such a weapon would be considered a supreme treasure and even those at the very Top had them.","Yet such a young man has it. This only made others certain that Long Haotian’s background must be terrifying.","Long Haotian gently stroked the blade.","A trace of pride appeared on his face.","This sword had accompanied him for years.","Countless geniuses had fallen beneath it.","Today would be no exception.","His gaze locked onto Bai Zihan.","\"Let’s see how long you can remain arrogant.\"","Whoosh!","Long Haotian vanished.","Sword light filled the sky.","A golden streak split the air and instantly arrived before Bai Zihan.","The sword descended.","Space itself seemed to distort under its edge.","Long Haotian sneered.","This attack was completely different from before.","This time, he was serious.","This time, Bai Zihan would understand the difference between them.","Unfortunately, Bai Zihan’s expression didn’t change at all.","Shing!","A sword cry echoed. A silver blade appeared in Bai Zihan’s hand as well.","Then—","Bang!","The two swords collided.","Terrifying shockwaves exploded outward.","The arena trembled violently.","Long Haotian’s sneer instantly froze.","His pupils contracted.","The attack had been blocked. Not even a step backward.","The sword in Bai Zihan’s hand remained steady.","As though blocking the attack had required no effort whatsoever.","Long Haotian’s eyes widened.","His gaze immediately landed on Bai Zihan’s sword.","Then his expression changed.","His mind blanked.","Because he could clearly sense it.","The sword in Bai Zihan’s hand... was actually on the same level as his own.","A Top Grade Heaven Grade Sword!","\"Impossible!\"","Long Haotian blurted out.","His voice was filled with disbelief.","\"How can you possess a Top Grade Heaven Grade Sword?!\"","The surrounding elders were equally stunned.","Their eyes nearly popped out of their sockets.","Another Top Grade Heaven Grade Artifact?","In the entire Desolate Heaven Empire, such treasures could almost be counted on one hand.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan merely glanced at his sword.","Then at Long Haotian.","A playful smile appeared on his face.","\"What?\"","His tone was filled with amusement.","\"Did you think only you could have one?\""]},{"number":625,"title":"Chapter 625: One Sword Breaks His Dao Heart","paragraphs":["Long Haotian’s expression remained ugly.","Of course, he didn’t think he was the only person in the world who possessed a Top Grade Heaven Grade Artifact.","What truly shocked him was that someone like Bai Zihan had one.","His eyes narrowed, then he coldly snorted.","\"Don’t become overconfident just because you possess a Top Grade Heaven Grade Sword. You are still nothing before me!\"","Boom!","Immortal Realm Qi erupted once more.","Long Haotian stepped forward.","His sword swept through the air.","A dazzling golden sword light instantly slashed toward Bai Zihan.","At the same time, a sharp aura suddenly erupted from his body.","The surrounding sword cultivators immediately felt their own swords tremble slightly.","Long Haotian’s lips curved upward.","A proud smile appeared on his face.","This was his true confidence.","Half-Step Sword Intent!","Although he had not fully comprehended Sword Intent, he had already stepped through the door.","He was only half a step away.","Within the younger generation of the Central Glorious Continent, this achievement was already enough to make countless geniuses despair.","The two old men nodded slightly.","Their expressions eased somewhat.","Although Long Haotian was difficult to deal with and stubborn to his core, his talent was something nobody could deny.","One old man silently sighed.","Long Haotian’s temperament may be flawed, but his talent is undoubtedly heaven-defying.","Half-Step Sword Intent at such an age.","Given another decade or two, he would likely truly comprehend Sword Intent.","By then, there won’t be many who could be compared to him.","This was what it meant to be favored by the heavens.","Slash! Slash!","Long Haotian’s attacks became increasingly fierce.","Each strike carried traces of Half-Step Sword Intent.","The power behind every attack multiplied dramatically.","The difference between possessing Sword Intent and lacking it was like the difference between heaven and earth.","Even Half-Step Sword Intent was enough to crush countless sword cultivators.","The surrounding Heaven Sword Sect disciples stared in awe.","Most of them were sword cultivators.","Thus, they could feel the terror of Long Haotian’s swordsmanship more clearly than anyone.","Yet—","Clang! Clang! Clang!","Every attack was blocked.","Bai Zihan’s figure remained steady.","His sword moved calmly.","Neither hurried nor slow.","No matter how fierce Long Haotian’s attacks became, he seemed unable to gain even the slightest advantage.","Eventually, Bai Zihan became somewhat disappointed.","His expression turned indifferent.","Then he casually spoke.","\"If that’s all you’ve got...\"","Clang!","Another attack was effortlessly deflected.","\"...then you might as well give up.\"","The words almost caused Long Haotian to cough up blood.","He was already using Half-Step Sword Intent!","Yet Bai Zihan was speaking as though he were some ordinary cultivator.","Rage exploded within Long Haotian’s chest.","\"You arrogant—\"","Before he could finish, Bai Zihan moved.","Whoosh!","His figure suddenly disappeared.","Long Haotian’s pupils contracted.","Fast!","The next moment, a silver sword light appeared before him.","Instinctively, Long Haotian raised his sword to block.","Clang!!!","A deafening explosion rang out.","Long Haotian was forced backward several steps.","His arms trembled.","His expression changed.","Something was wrong.","Very wrong.","The pressure from Bai Zihan’s sword had changed completely.","Whoosh!","Another sword strike arrived.","Then another.","Then another.","Each strike was faster than the last.","Each strike was sharper than the last.","Soon, Long Haotian found himself completely suppressed.","The confident smile on his face had long disappeared.","Meanwhile, the two old men behind him gradually frowned.","Their eyes became increasingly serious.","At first, they thought Long Haotian was merely being pushed back due to carelessness.","Then they noticed something.","An aura that every sword cultivator dreamed of obtaining.","The first old man’s eyes widened.","\"No...\"","The second old man’s breathing abruptly stopped.","\"That aura...\"","Their gazes locked onto Bai Zihan’s sword.","Then both of them froze.","Complete disbelief appeared on their faces.","Sword Intent!","Not Half-Step Sword Intent.","Actual Sword Intent!","The first old man’s voice trembled slightly.","\"S-Sword Intent...\"","The second old man’s eyes widened to their limit.","His heart shook violently.","Impossible!","This should be impossible.","How old was Bai Zihan?","Even in the Central Glorious Continent, countless old sword cultivators spent centuries pursuing Sword Intent without success.","Yet this young man had already comprehended it.","And not merely touched its edge.","He had truly stepped into the realm of Sword Intent.","Meanwhile, Long Haotian finally noticed it as well.","The moment realization struck him, his entire body almost froze.","His eyes nearly popped out of their sockets.","The sword in Bai Zihan’s hand descended once more.","Wrapped in a sharp aura capable of splitting everything before it.","Long Haotian’s voice trembled.","\"Sword Intent?!\"","His mind almost went blank.","This was no longer Half-Step Sword Intent.","This was the real thing.","A complete level above him.","And what neither Long Haotian nor the two old men dared imagine was that Bai Zihan’s Sword Intent wasn’t merely Basic Sword Intent at all.","If they knew the truth, their minds would likely collapse on the spot.","However, Bai Zihan wasn’t interested in ending this fight too quickly and had no intention of using his Intermediate Sword Intent.","In fact, even using Basic Sword Intent might already have been excessive.","\"When will you finally learn?\"","Bai Zihan’s calm voice echoed across the arena.","\"You aren’t the only person who can have something.\"","His sword descended once more.","Clang!","Long Haotian instinctively raised his weapon to block.","The impact forced him backward several steps, yet he barely noticed.","His attention was no longer focused on the battle.","Instead, his eyes remained fixed on Bai Zihan’s sword.","Sword Intent!","Genuine Sword Intent.","Even now, he found it difficult to believe.","His Half-Step Sword Intent had always been one of his greatest sources of pride.","It was proof of his talent.","Proof of his hard work.","Proof that he stood above countless geniuses of his generation.","Throughout the Central Glorious Continent, there were not many who could compare to him in the Dao of the Sword.","At least, that was what he had always believed.","Yet now...","Reality had given him a vicious slap across the face.","A youth less than half his age.","A cultivator from a remote empire he had previously looked down upon.","Someone who had already accomplished what he himself had been striving to achieve.","The impact was simply too great.","His confidence was crumbling.","His pride was being shattered piece by piece.","And Long Haotian had never possessed a particularly steady heart to begin with.","His path had always been smooth.","His talent had always carried him forward.","His background had always protected him.","Whenever he encountered obstacles, others solved them for him.","Whenever he desired something, it was handed to him.","Thus, although his cultivation was high, his state of mind was far weaker than it should have been.","Now that he had encountered someone who completely surpassed his expectations, the flaw immediately revealed itself.","His thoughts became chaotic.","His sword became unstable.","His focus drifted.","Even while fighting, his mind remained occupied by the same question.","How?","How was this possible?","How could someone like Bai Zihan possess Sword Intent?","Whoosh!","A sword light flashed past his shoulder.","Long Haotian hurriedly retreated.","A strand of hair floated through the air.","Only then did he realize how close he had come to injury.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan shook his head slightly.","Disappointment flashed through his eyes.","Originally, he had been somewhat interested in Long Haotian.","After all, this was supposedly a top genius from the Central Glorious Continent.","Someone nurtured by a powerful clan.","Someone who should have possessed a firm Dao Heart, yet the reality before him was completely different.","The moment Long Haotian discovered that Bai Zihan possessed Sword Intent, his mentality had begun collapsing.","In a life-and-death battle, such a reaction was fatal.","If Bai Zihan had truly intended to kill Long Haotian, he would have been dead several times by now.","Yet Long Haotian remained completely unaware.","The gap between them was far larger than he imagined.","Bai Zihan inwardly sighed.","Apart from his cultivation realm, Long Haotian had shown nothing particularly impressive.","His combat instincts were average.","His mentality was fragile.","His battle awareness was lacking.","Even his swordsmanship was overly reliant on brute force, despite being fortunate enough to comprehend Half-Step Sword Intent.","Compared to Chong Sheng...","The difference was enormous.","Bai Zihan’s eyes narrowed slightly.","The image of Chong Sheng appeared in his mind.","Someone whose cultivation, talent, combat experience, mentality, and Dao Heart had all been tempered to an extraordinary degree.","Even while facing impossible odds, Chong Sheng had remained calm.","Although Chong Sheng ultimately fell beneath his sword, Bai Zihan had needed to give everything he had to accomplish it.","It seemed that there was indeed a huge difference between a top genius and someone worthy of being called a Heaven Chosen.","The only area in which Long Haotian surpassed Chong Sheng was cultivation, and even that was largely because Long Haotian had been supplied with abundant resources and had enjoyed far more time to cultivate.","Meanwhile, Chong Sheng had possessed very few resources by comparison and very little time to grow.","Then again, Chong Sheng had been a reincarnated cultivator, so perhaps the comparison wasn’t entirely fair.","Still...","Even his sister Bai Xueqing possessed a far stronger mentality than Long Haotian, and she wasn’t even a Heaven Chosen.","Clang!","Their swords collided once more.","This time, Long Haotian was directly forced backward dozens of meters.","His arms trembled violently.","Bai Zihan remained standing in place.","He didn’t move back even a single step.","Looking at Long Haotian’s increasingly unstable expression, Bai Zihan could not help but shake his head again.","\"If you don’t want to fight, then just give up!\""]},{"number":626,"title":"Chapter 626: Long Haotain’s Power","paragraphs":["Long Haotian’s grip on his sword tightened until his knuckles turned white.","Give up?","Those words burned through him like acid.","Long Haotian of the Long Clan.","A recognized genius of the Central Glorious Continent.","Someone who had comprehended Half-Step Sword Intent at an age when most cultivators were still struggling with the foundations of their Dao.","He had never surrendered.","Not once in his entire life.","The word simply did not exist in his vocabulary.","\"Don’t... patronize me!\"","He roared.","Qi erupted from his body in a violent torrent.","Every last bit of his cultivation surged forward without restraint.","The two old men behind him tensed instinctively, yet neither moved.","The first old man’s hand rose halfway.","Then stopped.","The second old man glanced at him.","A silent exchange passed between them.","Then the second old man exhaled and settled back where he stood.","( Let him fight! )","It wasn’t indifference.","Quite the opposite.","They had both lived long enough to recognize something important.","Long Haotian’s greatest flaw had never been his talent.","His talent was extraordinary.","His technique was refined.","His cultivation, backed by the Long Clan’s resources, was formidable.","The flaw was his fragile heart.","In moments exactly like this one.","When the world refused to bend to his expectations.","When something stood before him that he could not simply overpower.","Long Haotian’s heart cracked.","And a cracked heart, left untempered, would one day shatter completely.","Every path beyond the Immortal Realm required a Dao Heart that could not be broken.","Until now, Long Haotian had never encountered anyone who could surpass his talent the way Bai Zihan did.","The first old man thought that Bai Zihan from a remote empire is the whetstone Long Haotian has always needed.","Perhaps today’s humiliation would become the most valuable lesson the Long Clan could ever provide him.","Thus, they remained where they stood.","Meanwhile, Long Haotian roared again and charged.","Whoosh!","He crossed the distance instantly.","Golden Immortal Qi ignited around his body like a second skin.","His sword swept downward in a vicious arc.","\"Heaven Sundering Blaze—First Form!\"","Boom!","The technique erupted.","A Mid Heaven Grade Martial Art!","One of the Long Clan’s most prized sword techniques.","The air itself seemed to ignite as a pillar of blazing golden sword light descended toward Bai Zihan like a falling sun.","The surrounding Heaven Sword Sect disciples scrambled backward.","The heat alone was enough to burn their robes.","Even several elders straightened slightly.","That was genuine power.","The full force of an Immortal Realm cultivator unleashing a Mid Heaven Grade technique was not something just anyone could receive head-on.","Bai Zihan tilted his head slightly.","His expression remained unchanged.","Then he raised the Eternal Spirit Sword.","Clang!","The impact was enormous.","The arena floor cracked beneath Bai Zihan’s feet.","Not because he had been pushed back.","But because he had absorbed the force and redirected it downward.","The blazing golden light split around him like water flowing around a stone before dispersing into the air.","Long Haotian landed several paces away.","His teeth clenched tightly.","(He blocked it? That technique had been blocked?)","Whoosh!","He circled left.","Then slashed right.","Two feints.","One killing strike.","\"Heaven Sundering Blaze—Second Form!\"","Three waves of sword light erupted.","Each one stronger than the last.","Each one faster than the previous strike.","Each one carrying greater destructive power.","The second old man’s eyes widened slightly.","Regardless of the outcome, Long Haotian’s mastery of Heaven Sundering Blaze was undeniably exceptional.","Bai Zihan watched the three sword waves approach.","Then he moved.","Whoosh!","One smooth step.","The first wave passed harmlessly beside him.","A slight twist of his wrist redirected the second wave.","The attack spun sideways and crashed into the arena wall.","Boom!","A massive crack spread across the stone.","The third wave arrived.","Clang!","Bai Zihan met it directly.","Not with brute force.","But with the Eternal Flowing Water Sword Art.","His blade curved like flowing water.","The incoming force was swallowed whole.","The attack vanished as though it had fallen into a bottomless river.","Long Haotian stumbled forward.","The rebound from his own strike nearly disrupted his footing.","He recovered instantly yet his breathing had become heavier.","Not from exhaustion. His Immortal Realm cultivation possessed more than enough endurance.","No! It was something else.","He stared at Bai Zihan.","At the calm eyes looking back at him.","There was neither contempt nor excitement.","Only amusement.","It was as though this battle wasn’t even worth taking seriously.","As though Bai Zihan could end it whenever he wished.","\"How dare you look down on me!\"","Long Haotian lunged forward again.","This time, he abandoned Heaven Sundering Blaze entirely.","The Immortal Qi surrounding his body changed.","Long Haotian planted his feet firmly.","His sword slowly rose before him.","Every cultivator present felt something tighten in their chest.","An instinctive warning.","A primal sense of danger.","The technique had not even been released.","Yet the pressure gathering around Long Haotian’s body surpassed anything seen previously.","The two old men remained completely still.","No surprise appeared on their faces.","Only recognition.","The first old man exhaled softly.","(So he’s using that.)","They had wondered whether he would.","Part of them had hoped he wouldn’t need to.","Yet here it was.","Dragon Burial Slash!","The Long Clan’s most closely guarded Technique.","A technique only taught to those who had made great contributions to the clan Or to the Clan Leaders.","Long Haotian had received it personally on the day his father acknowledged him as the heir of the Long Clan.","A Saint Grade Technique!","The only Saint Grade Technique possessed by the Long Clan.","The first old man glanced toward Bai Zihan.","Although Bai Zihan had impressed them greatly, he knew this was the end.","Even Earth Immortals would suffer if struck directly by this attack.","Let alone Bai Zihan, who was only in the Great Ascension Realm.","The fight was over!","And with it, Long Haotian’s Dao Heart would be restored.","The humiliation.","The struggle.","The doubt.","The eventual victory.","A complete tempering.","Everything they could have hoped for.","Long Haotian’s eyes blazed with confidence.","\"I want to see how you block this!\"","Long Haotian declared.","Bai Zihan looked at him calmly.","He could feel it.","The technique had not even been released yet, yet he could already tell how powerful it would be.","(If I take this head-on...)","His grip on the Eternal Spirit Sword shifted slightly.","Even with his physique, if the attack landed directly, he might suffer serious injuries.","He wasn’t completely certain.","But one thing was obvious.","This attack was on an entirely different level from anything he had faced before.","At last, Long Haotian had finally demonstrated something worthy of being called a genius of the Central Glorious Continent.","With this technique alone, Long Haotian could walk sideways among his generation without fearing many opponents.","A smirk appeared on Bai Zihan’s face.","\"Nine Shadows Flowing Light Sword!\"","Whoosh!","Nine afterimages erupted outward simultaneously.","Nine identical figures appeared.","Each carried the same aura.","The same Qi signature.","The same presence.","Nine Bai Zihans.","Long Haotian’s eyes snapped left then right.","He immediately released a pulse of Immortal Qi.","Nothing!","All nine felt identical.","His expression changed.","Previously, when he had seen Bai Xueqing use this technique, he hadn’t thought much of it.","He believed that with his divine sense, he could easily identify the real body.","But now?","He couldn’t tell them apart at all.","Then they moved.","All nine figures stepped outward simultaneously.","Each moving in a different direction.","Within moments, they had spread throughout the arena.","Some stood near the walls.","Some near the arena’s edge.","Some halfway up the stone steps.","All nine perfectly spaced apart.","Long Haotian’s eyes swept across the battlefield.","His grip tightened.","The Dragon Burial Slash was still building within him.","But the targets had multiplied.","And he had no idea which one was real.","The nine figures watched him with identical expressions.","Then one tilted its head.","\"What happened?\"","The voice came from the left.","Long Haotian spun around.","\"Couldn’t tell us apart?\"","Another voice sounded behind him.","\"You were so confident a moment ago.\"","This one came from above.","One shadow leaned casually against a railing with his sword resting on his shoulder.","\"I want to see how you block this.\"","Another one repeated Long Haotian’s earlier words mockingly.","Long Haotian’s eyes twitched.","\"You—\"","\"Still charging up?\"","One shadow asked conversationally.","\"Take your time. We’re not going anywhere.\"","\"Well,\" another shadow said thoughtfully, \"some of us might be going somewhere. It’s getting a bit crowded here.\"","Long Haotian’s Qi surged violently.","\"Stop talking!\"","\"All of us?\" one asked.","\"Or just some of us?\" another added.","\"He might need to be more specific,\" a third remarked.","Long Haotian stood frozen at the center of the arena.","A Saint Grade Technique coiled within him like a loaded crossbow without a target.","Nine identical Bai Zihans surrounded him.","Leaning against walls.","Standing on steps.","Watching him as though he were a mildly interesting insect.","Bai Zihan’s calculation had been simple from the very beginning.","A Saint Grade Technique from someone at Long Haotian’s cultivation level could only be used once.","Maybe twice if he was willing to pay a severe price afterward.","So don’t get hit.","It was that simple.","The moment Long Haotian revealed a technique capable of genuinely threatening him, the answer became obvious.","Make him unable to use it.","Then wait.","One figure near the arena wall examined his fingernails idly.","\"Anytime now.\"","Long Haotian’s jaw clenched so tightly that it was a miracle his teeth hadn’t shattered.","But no matter how angry he got, there was no way for him to differentiate those Nine Shadows."]},{"number":627,"title":"Chapter 627: Dragon Burial Slash!","paragraphs":["The two old men’s expressions had become increasingly ugly.","They could naturally see what Bai Zihan was trying to do.","He wasn’t confronting the Dragon Burial Slash head-on.","He was stalling.","Dragging out the fight until Long Haotian exhausted himself maintaining the technique.","And the most frustrating part?","It was working.","Long Haotian’s cultivation might be high, but a Saint Grade Technique was not something he could maintain indefinitely.","Every second consumed an enormous amount of Immortal Qi.","The first old man’s eyes narrowed.","His divine sense spread outward.","The second old man did the same.","The nine figures scattered throughout the arena appeared identical.","To ordinary cultivators, they were impossible to distinguish.","However, the two old men were far from ordinary cultivators.","Their divine senses swept through the battlefield repeatedly.","No wonder, Long Haotian couldn’t tell these clones apart.","Even the two of them were having hard time differentiating the real one, not to mention, Long Haotian.","Only after expending Qi and taking a few seconds, were they finally able to locate Bai Zihan.","Then—","The first old man’s eyes flashed.","(Found him!)","Almost simultaneously, the second old man reached the same conclusion.","The real Bai Zihan was standing casually near one corner of the arena.","\"Young Master! Three o’clock!\"","\"The one near the eastern wall!\"","Long Haotian’s eyes immediately snapped toward that location.","At the same time, mocking laughter erupted.","\"Hahaha! Seriously?\"","\"Are they helping him?\"","\"Even in a duel between juniors, they still have to give him answers?\"","\"How shameless!\"","\"Forget genius. Without his elders helping him, he can’t even tell who’s real!\"","\"Hahaha! I guess this is the strength of an Immortal Realm genius?\"","The laughter grew louder.","Although nobody explicitly accused the two old men of cheating, the meaning was obvious.","This was a duel between the two, and although the old man didn’t physically intervene, it has similar implications.","The two old men’s expressions immediately darkened. Their faces burned with embarrassment.","Under normal circumstances, they would never interfere.","However, they had no choice.","If Long Haotian continued wasting Qi, the Dragon Burial Slash would collapse on its own.","By then, if Long Haotian truly lost, who knew what would happen to his Dao Heart?","They only want to temper Long Haotain’s Dao heart, not completely break it apart.","Unfortunately, they had been too eager to help and had blurted it out aloud rather than silently transmitting the message.","Long Haotian’s face alternated between red and green.","His grip tightened.","The mocking voices entered his ears one after another.","Each sentence felt like a slap across his face.","Every word stabbed directly into his pride.","For a brief moment, he even wanted to turn around and yell at the two old men.","However, he couldn’t really blame them either.","After all, if he weren’t in trouble, they wouldn’t have needed to intervene at all.","Moreover, without their help, he truly wouldn’t have been able to identify Bai Zihan.","He would have continued wasting Qi like an idiot while Bai Zihan played with him.","That realization only made the humiliation even greater.","Veins bulged across his forehead.","His eyes became bloodshot.","The Saint Grade Technique within him grew increasingly unstable.","Then his gaze locked onto Bai Zihan.","Murderous intent erupted.","\"Bai Zihan...\"","His voice sounded like it had been squeezed through clenched teeth.","The surrounding temperature seemed to drop.","(Only by killing you...)","The pressure emanating from the Dragon Burial Slash skyrocketed.","Long Haotian’s eyes burned with madness.","(...can I wash away today’s humiliation!)","The accumulated power finally erupted.","The sky darkened.","An enormous golden dragon phantom appeared behind Long Haotian.","The dragon opened its eyes.","A terrifying dragon roar echoed throughout the Heaven Sword Sect.","ROAR!","The pressure was simply too terrifying.","Long Haotian raised his sword.","The dragon phantom followed the movement.","Golden light illuminated the heavens.","At this moment, Long Haotian no longer cared about winning elegantly.","He no longer cared about preserving face.","He only wanted one thing.","To crush Bai Zihan completely.","\"DRAGON BURIAL SLASH!\"","His roar shook the heavens.","Then the sword descended.","The enormous dragon phantom roared and lunged toward Bai Zihan.","Everything in its path shattered.","Even space itself seemed to distort beneath the overwhelming force.","The two old men stared intently.","Their hearts settled slightly.","(This attack should be enough.)","No matter how monstrous Bai Zihan was.","No matter how shocking his talent.","He was still only in the Great Ascension Realm.","Against a fully unleashed Saint Grade Technique, how could he possibly survive?","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan was also preparing himself.","Originally, he had intended to see whether Long Haotian would actually release the technique.","Unfortunately, the two old men had interfered.","Now that his position had been exposed, he had no choice but to deal with Long Haotian’s technique head-on.","Just as Bai Zihan tightened his grip on the Eternal Spirit Sword, a familiar voice suddenly echoed inside his mind.","\"We are ready!\"","Bai Zihan’s eyes flickered.","It was Han Sha.","It seemed that the preparations he had ordered were finally complete.","A faint smile appeared on Bai Zihan’s face.","Perfect timing.","He had already seen enough of Long Haotian’s strength.","And now that Han Sha and the others were prepared, there was no need to drag things out.","Across the battlefield, the enormous golden dragon roared as it descended.","Its pressure crushed everything in its path.","The sky trembled.","The earth shattered.","Even space itself seemed unable to endure its might.","Long Haotian’s eyes were filled with madness.","\"Die!\"","His roar shook the heavens.","The Dragon Burial Slash surged forward with unstoppable momentum.","At that moment, Bai Zihan finally moved.","His eyes became incomparably sharp.","The playful expression that had remained throughout the battle completely disappeared.","An overwhelming aura erupted from his body.","Great Ascension Realm Qi exploded outward.","The surrounding spiritual energy instantly became chaotic.","His sword slowly rose.","The Eternal Spirit Sword emitted a clear cry as Sword Intent surged.","The surrounding sword cultivators felt their own swords trembling violently.","Even the two old men felt their expressions change.","A sense of danger suddenly appeared within their hearts.","Bai Zihan’s gaze remained fixed on the approaching dragon.","\"Fate Severing Slash!\"","A terrifying sword light appeared.","The moment it appeared, countless cultivators felt an indescribable chill run through their souls.","As though nothing in heaven or earth could escape its edge.","Then the two attacks collided.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The entire Heaven Sword Sect shook violently.","An explosion unlike anything before erupted between the two techniques.","The arena instantly collapsed.","Even the very formation protecting the disciples and elders were shattered without a shred of resistance.","Countless disciples were thrown to their knees.","Some weaker cultivators directly coughed up blood.","Even the sect elders had to circulate their cultivation to resist the shockwave.","Bai Xueqing’s expression changed.","Chu Ziyan’s face turned pale.","The force generated by the collision was so terrifying that both women nearly lost their footing.","Fortunately, Bai Ren casually waved his sleeve, and a protective barrier instantly appeared around them.","Meanwhile, the two old men behind Long Haotian were no longer calm.","Their eyes widened.","Complete disbelief appeared on their faces.","They stared at the battlefield as though they had seen a ghost.","Because Bai Zihan’s technique was actually competing against the Dragon Burial Slash.","A Saint Grade Technique!","Not only was it competing, it was gradually gaining the upper hand.","The golden dragon phantom roared furiously, yet the silver sword light continued advancing.","The dragon’s body began to crack.","The cracks spread rapidly.","Then—","Boom!!!","The dragon phantom exploded.","Golden fragments filled the sky.","The Dragon Burial Slash had been destroyed.","And the silver sword light didn’t stop.","It continued forward, straight toward Long Haotian.","Long Haotian’s pupils contracted to the size of needles.","His face instantly lost all color.","\"No!\"","Long Haotian’s mind went completely blank.","The scene before him felt unreal.","His strongest attack.","The technique he had always been proud of.","The Saint Grade Technique bestowed upon him by the Long Clan.","Dragon Burial Slash!","Destroyed.","His eyes remained fixed on the exploding dragon phantom.","For a brief moment, he completely forgot where he was.","Forgot about the duel.","Forgot about the countless spectators watching him.","His mind repeatedly echoed with the same thought.","(How? How did it lose?)","Unfortunately, reality did not care about his confusion.","The silver sword light continued advancing.","Fast.","Relentless.","Merciless.","It was already directly before him.","Only then did Long Haotian’s instincts finally scream.","Danger!","His pupils contracted violently.","A cold chill surged from the soles of his feet to the top of his head.","Without hesitation, his hand shot toward his storage ring.","A bronze shield instantly appeared.","A Heaven Grade defensive artifact.","One of the life-saving treasures given to him by his clan.","\"Protect me!\"","Long Haotian roared.","The shield immediately expanded.","Layers of defensive runes erupted from its surface.","A massive barrier formed before him.","Then—","BANG!!!","The Fate Severing Slash arrived."]},{"number":628,"title":"Chapter 628: Two Golden Immortal Cultivators","paragraphs":["For several moments after the collision, nobody could see anything.","The entire battlefield had been swallowed by dust, rubble, and violent Qi fluctuations.","The remnants of the Fate Severing Slash continued tearing through the air.","The ground remained cracked and shattered.","Everyone stared toward the center of the explosion.","\"Did Bai Zihan’s attack hit him?\"","\"Has that arrogant guy died?\"","Then a figure slowly emerged from the dust cloud.","Cough! Cough!","Long Haotian was in an extremely miserable state.","The Heaven Grade shield he had used to block the attack was completely destroyed.","The defensive armor beneath his robes had also suffered severe damage.","Deep cracks covered its surface.","Fresh blood stained his chest.","Although the slash had not penetrated deeply, the wound was enough to make anyone understand how close he had come to death.","Long Haotian lowered his head.","His gaze remained fixed on the blood.","His body trembled slightly.","Not from pain but from fear.","For the first time in his life, he had truly felt death so clearly.","If he had been even a fraction slower...","If he hadn’t brought out the Heaven Grade shield in time...","If he had relied solely on his defensive armor...","Then he might not be standing here right now.","The more he thought about it, the colder his body became.","His previous arrogance had completely disappeared.","When death stood before a person, reality inevitably seeped into their bones, no matter how arrogant and ignorant one was.","Long Haotian slowly raised his head.","His eyes landed on Bai Zihan.","This time, there was no longer any trace of contempt within them, only fear.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan remained completely calm.","He hadn’t held back much, thinking that Long Haotian could protect himself, and indeed, he was able to do so.","Though if he had died, Bai Zihan wouldn’t have thought much about it either.","That would simply mean that Long Haotian amounted to only this much. As for the information he wanted, those two old men should suffice.","Well, Long Haotian surviving was good news.","Bai Zihan believed that getting information out of an arrogant young man would be much easier than getting it from those old fossils.","Whoosh!","Bai Zihan suddenly disappeared.","Bang!","A hand directly grabbed Long Haotian’s head.","The next moment, Long Haotian’s face smashed violently into the ground.","The shattered arena cracked even further. Dust exploded outward.","Long Haotian’s body struggled instinctively.","Unfortunately, Bai Zihan’s strength was far beyond what he could currently resist.","His head remained firmly pinned to the ground.","Then—","Shing!","The Eternal Spirit Sword appeared at his neck.","The sharp edge rested against his skin.","A thin line of blood immediately appeared.","Bai Zihan’s calm voice entered his ears.","\"Don’t move!\"","Long Haotian’s entire body froze because he knew this wasn’t an empty threat.","If he moved, Bai Zihan would genuinely kill him.","The entire arena fell into dead silence.","Everyone stared blankly.","Although everyone had known about Bai Zihan’s strength, his opponent this time was an Immortal Realm cultivator with a mysterious and profound background.","Yet Bai Zihan, against all odds, emerged victorious.","And it was such a dominant victory, that one might believe that it was Bai Zihan that was in the Immortal Realm, not his opponent.","Others could only shake their heads, once again being reminded of why Bai Zihan was considered an unparalleled genius throughout their history.","Meanwhile, cold sweat appeared on the faces of many spectators who previously made things difficult for Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan, especially the Shen Clan disciple who had previously wanted to lead Long Haotian into the Bai Clan.","Soon, the two old men finally recovered from their shock.","Their expressions changed drastically.","\"Release Young Master Immediately!\"","However, Bai Zihan didn’t even give them a glance and simply ignored them.","The two old men’s expressions darkened.","Things had turned for the worse, and the two old men now wanted to regain control of the situation as quickly as possible.","Terrifying pressure erupted from their bodies.","The Golden Immortal Realm aura surged upward like a tsunami.","Unlike Long Haotian’s aura, this pressure possessed an entirely different level of oppression.","It was as though heaven itself had descended.","The surrounding space trembled.","Many disciples instantly collapsed to their knees.","Even numerous elders felt their bodies grow heavy and were forced down.","Some found themselves unable to breathe.","\"What... What is this pressure?\"","A Heaven Sword Sect elder’s face turned pale.","\"So powerful and unfathomable!\"","\"This pressure... Even the Grand Elders don’t possess such terrifying pressure!\"","The surrounding crowd erupted into panic.","Some had previously encountered Earth Immortal experts, yet the pressure before them felt even more terrifying.","The difference wasn’t small; it was enormous.","The two old men’s eyes remained fixed on Bai Zihan.","Killing intent slowly emerged.","At this point, they no longer cared about appearances.","The Young Master had been captured.","Nothing else mattered.","One of the old men stepped forward.","His voice carried overwhelming pressure.","\"Since you refuse to listen when we speak politely...\"","Golden Immortal Qi surged around him.","\"...then don’t blame us for being impolite.\"","The second old man also took a step forward.","His gaze was icy.","\"Release the Young Master immediately. Otherwise, you’ll bear the consequences.\"","However, before either of them could make a move—","Two figures suddenly appeared in front of them.","Bai Ren!","Bai Chu!","The two old men frowned.","\"Move aside!\"","The first old man spoke coldly.","His tone allowed no room for refusal.","However, Bai Ren suddenly laughed.","\"Pfft! Hahaha...\"","His laughter echoed across the battlefield.","Then he pointed toward Bai Zihan.","\"You want to harm our Young Master?\"","His smile gradually disappeared.","\"I’m afraid we can’t allow that.\"","Beside him, Bai Chu’s expression remained indifferent.","His cold gaze landed upon the two old men.","\"Our Young Master won fair and square. Behave yourselves.\"","The two old men nearly exploded from anger.","\"Fair and square, my ass!\"","One of them directly cursed.","His face darkened completely.","\"You weaklings don’t get to decide that.\"","Boom!","Golden Immortal pressure erupted from his body.","The terrifying aura surged directly toward Bai Ren and Bai Chu.","His intention was simple.","Force them to retreat.","Make them understand the difference between them.","Unfortunately, nothing happened.","Bai Ren remained standing where he was.","Bai Chu did not move either.","Neither showed the slightest reaction.","The old man’s pupils contracted.","Surprise flashed through his eyes.","However, he quickly suppressed it.","Without hesitation, he launched his attack.","Whoosh!","His figure disappeared.","The next moment, his fist appeared before Bai Ren.","The fist carried enough power to shatter mountains.","Space itself seemed unable to withstand the pressure.","Then a hand casually reached out.","Grab!","The old man’s fist stopped completely.","Bai Ren had caught it effortlessly.","As though he had merely caught a child’s punch.","Bai Ren looked at the old man.","Then he grinned.","\"That’s all?\"","The smile on his face became increasingly mocking.","\"You and your Young Master really are the same.\"","The old man’s eyes widened.","The second old man’s expression changed dramatically.","At this point, they finally realized something was terribly wrong.","Finally, they could sense Bai Ren and Bai Chu’s cultivation.","Their expressions instantly changed.","\"Golden Immortal!\"","The first old man blurted out.","The second old man’s eyes widened to their limits.","\"You...\"","His voice trembled slightly.","\"You’re Golden Immortals too?!\"","Although it sounded like a question, neither of them actually needed an answer.","The truth was already before them.","An Earth Immortal could never stop a Golden Immortal so casually.","Nor could an Earth Immortal remain completely unaffected by their pressure.","Not to mention, the Qi that they emitted at the moment, it clearly showed that they were in the Golden Immortal Realm as well.","Everything suddenly made sense.","The reason Bai Ren and Bai Chu had remained calm despite their pressure.","It was all because they possessed the same cultivation realm as them.","Their minds shook violently.","(This was impossible!)","Before arriving in the Desolate Heaven Empire, the Long Clan had already investigated the Desolate Heaven Empire thoroughly.","The Earth Immortal Realm should have been the limit.","That should have been the strongest level of cultivation in this backwater region.","Yet now, the first two true experts they encountered were both Golden Immortals.","What kind of joke was this?","The two old men exchanged glances.","Both could see the disbelief in the other’s eyes.","Had the Long Clan’s intelligence network made a mistake?","Or had they accidentally stumbled upon a hidden force that had remained concealed for countless years?","Meanwhile, Bai Ren continued holding the old man’s fist.","His grin widened.","\"What’s wrong? You looked pretty confident a moment ago.\"","Beside him, Bai Chu slowly folded his arms.","His expression remained cold.","\"You wanted to bully our Young Master with your cultivation?\"","His eyes narrowed.","\"You’ll have to get past us first.\"","Looking at the two, they knew that their plan to swiftly rescue Long Haotain and kill Bai Zihan had failed.","Even if they can beat the two of them, before they could do that, their young master might already meet his end by Bai Zihan’s sword."]},{"number":629,"title":"Chapter 629: Between A Rock And A Hard Place","paragraphs":["The two old men’s expressions remained grim.","For a moment, neither side moved.","Although Bai Ren and Bai Chu had revealed themselves as Golden Immortals, the two old men gradually calmed down.","Panic would solve nothing.","The first old man took a deep breath.","His gaze shifted toward Long Haotian, who was still pinned beneath Bai Zihan’s sword.","Then his eyes flashed subtly.","A silent message was conveyed.","Give up!","The second old man did the same.","They had both lost their composure because Long Haotian’s life appeared to be at risk, but after calming down, they finally realized that there shouldn’t be any real danger to his life.","It was merely a duel.","It shouldn’t lead to Long Haotian’s death.","They had simply panicked. Otherwise, they would never have become so worked up.","Long Haotian’s face twisted slightly.","Under the pressure of the Eternal Spirit Sword resting against his neck, he eventually clenched his teeth and nodded.","He had already lost anyway.","Seeing this, the two old men relaxed somewhat.","In their eyes, the situation was still salvageable.","After all, there wasn’t any true life-and-death grudge between the two sides.","The duel had simply gone badly.","Yes, Long Haotian’s wager had been disrespectful towards Bai Zihan.","Yes, they had become overly aggressive afterward.","But Bai Zihan had agreed to the duel himself.","At the end of the day, it was merely a contest between juniors.","Surely Bai Zihan would release Long Haotian now.","That was the most reasonable outcome.","\"I give up. You win!\"","Long Haotian admitted through his gritted teeth.","Unfortunately for him, Bai Zihan made no move to withdraw his sword.","Bai Zihan asked, his sword still resting at Long Haotian’s neck.","\"What is your purpose for coming here?\"","The question was simple.","Yet the moment it was spoken, the expressions of all three people changed.","Long Haotian froze.","The two old men’s pupils contracted.","Their hearts skipped a beat.","How could Bai Zihan possibly know they had come here for something?","The first old man’s thoughts raced.","The second old man’s gaze sharpened.","But both immediately reached the same conclusion.","It had to be a coincidence.","What Bai Zihan probably suspected was that Long Haotian might be targeting him under the guise of pursuing Chu Ziyan and Bai Xueqing.","They didn’t believe Bai Zihan had any idea about their true purpose in the Desolate Heaven Empire.","There was no way.","The Long Clan’s mission had been kept extremely confidential.","Even within the clan itself, very few people knew the truth.","Meanwhile, Long Haotian quickly regained his composure.","Although his face remained pale, he immediately forced a confused expression onto it.","\"What are you talking about?\"","His voice sounded somewhat stiff.","\"I don’t understand what you mean.\"","Long Haotian’s expression did not change in the slightest.","\"You don’t understand?\"","Bai Zihan’s sword pressed slightly closer to his neck.","A tiny stream of blood trickled down.","Long Haotian’s body instantly stiffened.","Then Bai Zihan calmly reminded him.","\"Did you forget the Heavenly Vow you made?\"","The moment those words were spoken, Long Haotian’s face changed.","The two old men’s expressions also darkened.","The condition they had all dismissed because they never believed Long Haotian would lose.","Yet now, he had lost.","And the vow was still binding.","Bai Zihan’s gaze remained fixed on Long Haotian.","His voice became colder.","\"I made a bet that you would do anything I ask, and what I want is for you to answer my questions truthfully.\"","Bai Zihan said. With that condition in place, if Long Haotian dared to avoid answering or attempted to deceive him, he would be struck by Heavenly Tribulation.","\"I’ll ask again! Why did you come to the Desolate Heaven Empire?\"","The last trace of composure vanished from Long Haotian’s face.","This time, there was no room for misunderstanding.","Bai Zihan knew.","He wasn’t guessing.","He wasn’t fishing for information due to some misunderstanding.","He already knew that they had come to the Desolate Heaven Empire for a mission.","He was asking because he already knew there was something worth asking about.","The two old men exchanged glances.","Shock gradually appeared in their eyes.","Their hearts sank.","It didn’t seem as though Bai Zihan was making a random guess.","Rather, he already knew they had come here for some purpose.","Long Haotian’s forehead began to sweat.","He couldn’t possibly answer.","If he did, the Long Clan would never let him off easily.","The mission involved interests far greater than himself.","But if he lied?","Then he would be struck by Heavenly Tribulation.","Even with his arrogance, he knew what happened to those struck by Heavenly Tribulation.","Most died. Those who survived often became crippled.","\"...\"","Long Haotian remained silent.","His fists clenched tightly.","The Heavenly Vow hung over his head like an executioner’s blade.","He couldn’t answer.","The mission concerned the Long Clan’s greatest interests.","If he revealed it, even if he survived today, the clan would never forgive him.","Perhaps even his status as heir would be revoked.","Even with his talent, that position was not untouchable.","Yet if he lied...","The Heavenly Vow would immediately react and Heavenly Tribulation would descend.","That outcome was no better.","Thus, he could only remain silent and try to delay things.","His only hope now rested on the two old men.","As long as they rescued him, he wouldn’t need to answer anything.","The two old men naturally understood this as well.","Since matters had reached this point, there was no point hiding anything.","The first old man looked directly at Bai Zihan.","His voice became significantly colder.","\"Young man. You already know who we are. Then you should also understand that antagonizing us will not benefit you.\"","The second old man nodded.","\"The Long Clan is not something your Bai Clan can afford to offend.\"","His gaze swept across the Heaven Sword Sect.","Then across the entire Desolate Heaven Empire.","A trace of arrogance appeared in his eyes.","\"Not just your Bai Clan. Even this entire empire. If our Long Clan wishes it, we can erase it from existence.\"","The surrounding crowd’s expressions changed.","Although the statement sounded incredibly arrogant, the pressure the two old men had displayed earlier suggested it might not be an empty threat.","Perhaps they truly possessed such power.","\"Release the Young Master and assist us. The rewards you receive will be far beyond your imagination.\"","The two old men first tried intimidation and then offered benefits.","Knowing that Bai Zihan was aware of their background, they felt that he wouldn’t want to offend them too deeply.","They also knew a little about the Bai Clan, which was hailed as the strongest clan in the Desolate Heaven Empire.","With the Bai Clan’s help, they might be able to complete their mission much more easily.","Therefore, they offered rewards to Bai Zihan in exchange for his cooperation.","Since Bai Zihan knew their background, they believed he would be able to see the benefits of their offer.","As for whether they would actually reward him afterward...","The two old men inwardly sneered.","After all, Bai Zihan had dared to threaten the Young Master’s life and interfere with their mission.","He would be fortunate if they chose not to destroy his clan completely afterward.","Unfortunately, Bai Zihan looked completely uninterested.","His expression didn’t change at all.","Instead, he pressed the Eternal Spirit Sword slightly deeper against Long Haotian’s neck.","A thin stream of blood flowed down.","Long Haotian’s entire body stiffened.","Bai Zihan spoke calmly.","\"Forget Heavenly Tribulation.\"","His voice was indifferent.","\"If you don’t answer...\"","His gaze locked onto Long Haotian.","\"You won’t survive what comes next.\"","Long Haotian’s face instantly turned pale.","The two old men’s expressions darkened.","At this point, they finally realized something.","Bai Zihan wasn’t bluffing, nor was he afraid of them.","From the very beginning, he had intended to get answers.","One way or another.","The first old man slowly exhaled.","His eyes became icy.","\"It seems negotiation is impossible.\"","The second old man nodded.","\"We’ll take the Young Master and leave.\"","The first old man agreed.","\"This place is far more complicated than we anticipated.\"","Their original confidence had already disappeared.","Golden Immortals.","Two of them.","Such a force should not have existed in the Desolate Heaven Empire.","The information they possessed was completely wrong.","However, that only made them more determined to leave.","As long as they escaped today, they could report everything back to the clan.","Compared to the true power of the Long Clan, the forces present here were insignificant.","At that time...","The first old man glanced at Bai Ren.","Then at Bai Chu.","Finally, his gaze landed on Bai Zihan.","A cold light flashed through his eyes.","(We’ll see if you’re still this arrogant then.)","Boom!","Golden Immortal Qi erupted.","The two old men moved simultaneously.","Terrifying pressure swept across the battlefield.","The surrounding space distorted.","Their target was obvious.","Long Haotian!","They intended to rescue him by force.","Unfortunately—","Before either of them could approach—","Bai Ren smiled.","Bai Chu’s eyes narrowed.","The two Golden Immortals of the Bai Clan stepped forward at the same time.","Boom!!!","Four Golden Immortal auras collided directly above the ruined arena."]},{"number":630,"title":"Chapter 630: Even Golden Immortals Must Yield","paragraphs":["The clash between the four Golden Immortals instantly pushed the battlefield into chaos.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Terrifying shockwaves spread in every direction.","The heavens trembled.","The earth cracked.","Even the surrounding space showed signs of distortion under the overwhelming pressure.","Their Cultivation was similar, however, it was easy to see that the two elders from the Long Clan were stronger than Bai Ren and Bai Chu.","Although Bai Ren and Bai Chu had successfully broken through to the Golden Immortal Realm with the help of the pills provided by Bai Zihan, they were still newly advanced Golden Immortals.","Compared to the two elders of the Long Clan, their foundation was naturally weaker.","After all, the two old men had spent countless years in the Golden Immortal Realm.","Their understanding of cultivation, combat experience, and mastery of their techniques far surpassed what Bai Ren and Bai Chu currently possessed.","As the battle continued, Bai Ren and Bai Chu gradually found themselves being pushed back.","However, being pushed back did not mean being defeated.","If the Long Clan’s Elders want to rescue Long Haotain, it is almost impossible with Bai Ren and Bai Chu.","The Long Clan elders’ faces darkened.","While exchanging blows with Bai Ren, the first old man coldly shouted,","\"Are you two insane? You’ve only just entered the Golden Immortal Realm!\"","His voice thundered across the battlefield.","\"You still have a future ahead of you, yet you’re willing to throw everything away for a junior?\"","The second old man also spoke coldly.","\"That Bai Zihan is young and ignorant. But you two should understand the consequences of your actions.\"","His eyes flashed with killing intent.","\"Do you know how many Golden Immortals exist within the Long Clan? Our clan has stood at the peak of the Central Glorious Continent for countless years.\"","\"Can your Bai Clan withstand our wrath?\"","The threat was obvious.","The expressions of Bai Ren and Bai Chu became slightly more serious.","Truthfully speaking, the words did carry weight.","A clan capable of casually sending out multiple Golden Immortals was undoubtedly terrifying.","However, neither of them showed any fear.","Bai Ren directly laughed.","\"Stop talking nonsense.\"","Boom!","His fist collided with the first old man’s palm.","The resulting shockwave shattered a nearby mountain peak.","Then Bai Ren grinned.","\"Our Clan Leader has already made his decision. We simply follow it.\"","Beside him, Bai Chu nodded.","His voice remained cold and indifferent.","\"Since the Young Master wants answers...\"","His gaze locked onto the two old men.","\"Then nobody is taking Long Haotian away.\"","The two Long Clan elders were instantly furious.","\"You foolish idiots!\"","The first old man roared.","\"You don’t understand what you’re provoking!\"","However, before either side could continue arguing, several powerful auras suddenly appeared.","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","Soon, dozens of experts appeared around the ruined arena led by Han Sha.","The Grand Elders and Elders of the Heaven Sword Sect!","Nearly all of the Heaven Sword Sect’s high-level experts had arrived.","The moment they landed, they immediately surrounded the entire battlefield.","The Heaven Sword Sect disciples became increasingly shocked.","Meanwhile, Han Sha’s expression remained ugly.","Originally, he had been extremely dissatisfied when Bai Zihan ordered him around.","Being commanded—or more accurately, threatened—by a junior naturally made him uncomfortable.","However, knowing he had no ability to disobey, he could only obediently follow Bai Zihan’s instructions.","Only now did he finally understand why Bai Zihan had specifically ordered every available Grand Elder and Elder to gather here.","Because the opponents they were facing were far more terrifying than anyone had imagined.","Han Sha’s gaze swept across the battlefield.","His scalp immediately went numb.","The pressure radiating from the four combatants made even him feel suffocated.","Beside him stood one of the Earth Immortal Grand Elders.","The old man had originally been calmly stroking his beard.","However, after sensing the auras in the sky, his hand froze.","Several strands of beard were accidentally ripped out.","His eyes widened in disbelief.","His body even trembled slightly.","Others might merely be guessing, but as an Earth Immortal himself, he understood exactly what he was sensing.","His voice trembled.","\"T-This...\"","His face was filled with shock.","Then he slowly swallowed.","\"T-They are Golden Immortals!\"","The moment those words left his mouth, silence descended.","Everyone froze.","Han Sha’s eyes widened.","The surrounding Elders and Grand Elders stood completely stunned.","Golden Immortals?","Those legendary experts that should only exist within the Central Glorious Continent?","Many people felt their hearts nearly stop.","And then another terrifying thought appeared in their minds.","If the two Long Clan elders were Golden Immortals...","Then that meant Bai Ren and Bai Chu were also Golden Immortals.","The entire crowd collectively sucked in a cold breath.","Just when did the Bai Clan become so terrifying?","Previously when they had fought against the Demonic Force, Bai Ren and Bai Chu were both in Earth Immortal.","Now they have advanced to the legendary Golden Immortal Realm?","Their gazes slowly turned toward Bai Zihan.","The young man was still standing calmly with his sword resting against Long Haotian’s neck.","Bai Zihan’s voice suddenly rang across the battlefield.","\"Enough!\"","His tone was cold and carried unquestionable authority.","The Eternal Spirit Sword remained pressed firmly against Long Haotian’s neck.","Bai Zihan’s gaze swept across the two old men.","\"You are surrounded.\"","His voice echoed clearly.","\"The Heaven Sword Sect’s Grand Elders and Elders are here. You can’t defeat Elder Ren or Elder Chu.\"","\"My sword is at your Young Master’s throat.\"","He paused briefly before narrowing his eyes.","\"So I suggest you stop while you can.\"","A terrifying killing intent flashed through his eyes.","\"Otherwise, the consequences will be yours to bear.\"","The two old men’s expressions darkened.","Their eyes immediately turned icy.","The first old man glared at Bai Zihan.","\"You won’t dare!\"","Their confidence did not come from arrogance alone.","It came from the Long Clan.","The Long Clan’s status was simply too terrifying.","No force within the Desolate Heaven Empire could withstand its wrath.","Even if Bai Zihan was a peerless genius, surely he wouldn’t be foolish enough to truly kill Long Haotian.","Since Bai Zihan knew their background, they thought he wouldn’t dare do it.","However, Bai Zihan did not waste words arguing.","Instead—","Shing!","The Eternal Spirit Sword suddenly moved.","The blade sank slightly deeper into Long Haotian’s neck.","Fresh blood immediately flowed out.","Long Haotian’s entire body stiffened.","His pupils shrank violently.","For a moment, he could clearly feel death pressing against his throat.","A cold chill surged through every inch of his body.","He was terrified.","\"You two, stop!\"","Long Haotian shouted immediately.","His voice no longer carried any arrogance.","Only panic remained.","\"Elders! Stand down!\"","The two old men froze.","Long Haotian’s face had already turned pale.","Cold sweat covered his forehead.","His body was trembling uncontrollably.","At this moment, he no longer doubted Bai Zihan.","This lunatic would actually kill him.","The two old men exchanged glances.","Then they slowly looked around.","Bai Ren!","Bai Chu!","The Heaven Sword Sect’s Grand Elders!","The surrounding Elders.","They had already sealed every possible escape route.","Their hearts gradually sank.","Only now did they fully realize the truth.","From beginning to end...","Bai Zihan had already prepared everything.","Whether Long Haotian had provoked him or not...","Whether the duel happened or not...","It seemed they had already stepped into Bai Zihan’s grasp the moment they entered the Desolate Heaven Empire.","The more they thought about it, the colder they felt.","The first old man stared at Bai Zihan.","His gaze became increasingly complicated.","Shock!","Frustration!","Unwillingness!","And finally, resignation.","Who would have thought?","They were Golden Immortal experts respected wherever they went.","Yet today, they had been forced into a corner by a junior.","A junior whose cultivation had not even reached the Immortal Realm.","They knew that if they did as Bai Zihan said, there was a high possibility that all three of them would be captured, and the Long Clan might not even know how they died.","But if they dared resist any longer, Bai Zihan didn’t seem willing to patiently wait for them to escape.","He might kill Long Haotian if they dared to take his words lightly.","If they could escape, then perhaps it wouldn’t be too bad.","Although the Long Clan might lose its heir and genius, there were still many who could replace him.","But the problem was that even if they tried to escape, with so many experts present and two Golden Immortals blocking their path, escaping would not be easy and carried a high chance of failure.","The Long Clan elders slowly released the Immortal Qi surrounding their bodies.","The violent Golden Immortal pressure disappeared.","The overwhelming pressure that had suffocated everyone finally dissipated.","Countless disciples immediately felt relief wash over them.","Many nearly collapsed from exhaustion.","The two old men raised their hands.","A clear gesture of surrender.","\"We will not resist.\"","The first old man spoke slowly.","His eyes never left Bai Zihan.","\"We admit defeat.\"","The second old man nodded.","\"We only ask that you do not harm the Young Master.\""]},{"number":631,"title":"Chapter 631: Yu Wenzhao Makes his Move","paragraphs":["At the same time, the Heaven Suppression Pavilion began mobilizing.","The Crimson Thunder Palace also moved.","Yu Wenzhao wasn’t going to waste a God-given opportunity. He intended to devour both Yu Feiyan’s and Yu Qingya’s forces.","The enormous Third Prince’s faction began moving at full speed.","Yu Wenzhao did not leave many forces behind. Almost all of his elite experts were brought along.","Though he merely intended to wait. Wait until the perfect moment arrives before making his move.","High above the clouds, Yu Wenzhao stood at the front of the massive fleet.","The two Earth Immortal experts followed closely behind him.","One belonged to the Heaven Suppression Pavilion.","The other came from the Crimson Thunder Palace.","The pressure radiating from both men was enough to make ordinary cultivators tremble.","Behind them stood nearly fifteen Immortal Realm experts.","The lineup was absolutely terrifying.","Yu Wenzhao’s hands rested behind his back.","The wind whipped through his robes.","His expression remained calm.","Everything was proceeding exactly according to plan.","\"Your Highness.\"","One elder stepped forward respectfully.","\"At our current speed, we should arrive near the Frost Lily Pavilion in less than 12 hours.\"","Yu Wenzhao nodded.","\"Good! However, there is no need to be in a hurry.\"","Right now, the battle between Yu Feiyan and Yu Qingya should have just begun.","He would need to wait for a few days before the two sides completely lose all their strength.","He wasn’t planning to intervene until both sides suffered heavy casualties.","The thought made him smile faintly.","No matter how capable Yu Feiyan was.","No matter how mysterious her recent rise had been.","She simply lacked the foundation to challenge the Frost Lily Pavilion directly.","And Yu Qingya?","Even if she won, she would undoubtedly pay a heavy price.","By then, both sides would become his prey.","And he would become the hunter.","The massive fleet of the Third Prince continued advancing through the skies of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","At the very front of the fleet, Yu Wenzhao stood calmly with his hands behind his back.","His gaze remained fixed toward the distant horizon.","Everything was proceeding exactly as he expected.","No, it was going even better than he had expected.","However, just as the fleet continued its advance—","Whoosh!","A figure suddenly shot toward the front of the fleet.","It was one of the scouts sent ahead.","The man’s expression appeared somewhat strange.","Yu Wenzhao immediately noticed it.","His brows furrowed slightly.","The scout quickly landed before him and knelt.","\"Your Highness!\"","Yu Wenzhao spoke calmly.","\"Report!\"","The scout immediately answered.","\"Your Highness, the situation at the Frost Lily Pavilion appears different from what we expected.\"","The Heaven Suppression Pavilion’s Earth Immortal expert narrowed his eyes.","\"What do you mean?\"","The scout quickly lowered his head.","\"There are no signs of a large-scale battle.\"","Silence fell.","The expressions of numerous experts froze.","\"No signs of battle?\"","One elder immediately frowned.","The scout nodded.","\"Yes. The Frost Lily Pavilion remains intact with no major signs of battle. There wasn’t even a scratch on their walls.\"","The more he spoke, the stranger everyone’s expressions became.","Even Yu Wenzhao’s eyes narrowed.","This was impossible.","According to every report they had received, Yu Feiyan had personally led her forces toward the Frost Lily Pavilion.","Even if neither side achieved victory, there should at least have been signs of conflict.","Yet now...","Nothing?","The scout continued.","\"Furthermore...\"","He hesitated.","\"The Ninth Princess’s forces cannot be found either.\"","\"What?\"","Several elders blurted out simultaneously.","The scout lowered his head further.","Neither side appeared to be fighting, and even Yu Feiyan’s army was nowhere to be seen.","Maybe hiding a few hundreds might have been easy but tens of thousands? That is almost impossible.","The fleet gradually became quiet.","Everyone exchanged confused glances.","This was completely different from what they had imagined.","\"What is going on?\"","\"Could the battle have already ended?\"","\"Impossible! How could a war between two Princesses end in merely one or two days? And without any signs of battle?\"","\"Could Lily Frost Pavilion already have their walls repaired?\"","The Frost Lily Pavilion wasn’t some weak faction, nor was Yu Feiyan’s rapidly expanding force.","Even if one side won, the battle should have lasted far longer.","\"Could Princess Yu Feiyan have retreated?\"","The suggestion caused several people to pause.","It wasn’t impossible.","However, the Heaven Suppression Pavilion’s Earth Immortal expert quickly shook his head.","\"No! If she intended to retreat, why mobilize such a large force in the first place?\"","\"And according to our intelligence, she truly did head toward the Frost Lily Pavilion. So, how can there be no conflict?\"","If it had been only a single report, perhaps there might have been a mistake.","But almost everyone in the vicinity knew that Princess Yu Feiyan had headed toward the Frost Lily Pavilion, and it was widely believed she intended to wage war.","That information absolutely could not be false.","The surrounding experts slowly nodded.","Something was definitely wrong.","Yu Wenzhao remained silent for a long time.","His gaze gradually turned colder.","Originally, he had believed everything was under control.","Now, however, the situation has suddenly become unclear.","And uncertainty was something he disliked greatly.","Finally, he spoke.","\"Continue investigating.\"","The scout immediately lowered his head.","\"Yes, Your Highness!\"","Yu Wenzhao’s eyes narrowed.","\"I want information from every nearby sect, clan, city, and trading post.\"","His voice became colder.","\"Find out whether Yu Feiyan truly arrived at the Frost Lily Pavilion. Find out whether she left.\"","\"And most importantly...\"","A dangerous light flashed across his eyes.","\"Find out what happened during these past few days.\"","The surrounding experts immediately straightened.","\"Understood!\"","Several scouts quickly departed.","Whoosh! Whoosh!","One figure after another disappeared into the distance.","***","Several hours passed!","The Third Prince’s massive fleet continued hovering above the clouds.","No one was relaxed. The strange reports from earlier had already placed everyone on edge.","Even Yu Wenzhao no longer appeared as relaxed as before.","His eyes remained fixed toward the direction of the Frost Lily Pavilion.","Finally—","Whoosh!","Multiple figures rapidly approached from different directions.","The scouts had returned.","The moment they appeared, countless gazes immediately turned toward them.","Yu Wenzhao spoke first.","\"Report!\"","The leading scout immediately knelt.","\"Your Highness, we have thoroughly investigated every major city, sect, clan, and trading post surrounding the Frost Lily Pavilion.\"","Yu Wenzhao narrowed his eyes.","\"And?\"","The scout hesitated briefly before speaking.","\"The Ninth Princess and her forces indeed headed toward the Frost Lily Pavilion.\"","The surrounding experts nodded.","At least that part matched their intelligence.","However, the scout’s expression became increasingly strange.","\"But there are no reports of any large-scale battle.\"","Silence descended.","The scout continued.","\"None of the nearby sects heard sounds of battle.\"","\"In a battle of such magnitude, the sounds should have spread for hundreds or even thousands of miles. Yet no one heard anything.\"","The more he spoke, the stranger the situation sounded.","The scout quickly lowered his head.","\"This subordinate personally verified the information multiple times. All nearby witnesses reported the same thing.\"","\"Princess Yu Feiyan’s forces arrived but then... nothing happened.\"","The elders’ expressions stiffened.","Nothing happened?","How was that possible?","The Frost Lily Pavilion and Yu Feiyan’s faction together numbered countless cultivators.","If they truly fought, the surrounding region should have been shaken for thousands of miles.","Yet now there was no evidence of conflict whatsoever.","Another scout stepped forward.","\"This subordinate also investigated. The Ninth Princess definitely did not retreat.\"","Yu Wenzhao’s gaze sharpened.","\"Are you certain?\"","\"Yes, Your Highness!\"","The scout answered immediately.","\"Numerous witnesses personally saw Yu Feiyan’s forces heading toward the Frost Lily Pavilion.\"","\"After that, however...\"","His voice became uncertain.","\"No one knows where they went.\"","The surrounding experts stared at him.","A strange atmosphere immediately spread throughout the fleet.","\"If they didn’t fight and they didn’t retreat, then where did tens of thousands of cultivators go?\"","A Heaven Suppression Pavilion elder suddenly spoke.","\"Could the Frost Lily Pavilion have concealed the entire battlefield somehow?\"","The two Earth Immortals exchanged glances.","Then both shook their heads.","Even for an Earth Immortal Realm expert, concealing a war of that scale would be extremely difficult.","Not impossible.","But highly improbable.","Especially when neither side possessed enough Earth Immortal experts to maintain such a massive concealment.","Another elder spoke.","\"Could Princess Yu Qingya have surrendered?\"","Immediately afterward, he shook his own head.","That sounded even more ridiculous.","They were talking about Yu Qingya.","Even before the Emperor himself, she would never surrender so easily.","The more everyone thought about it, the more confused they became.","Even Yu Wenzhao’s brows gradually furrowed.","Something was wrong.","The situation before him no longer made sense.","According to all logic, the Frost Lily Pavilion and Yu Feiyan should already have been engaged in a fierce battle.","Yet reality completely contradicted those expectations.","\"Just what is going on here?\"","Yu Wenzhao wondered.","However, no matter how much they racked their brains, no answer came to them.","\"Your Highness, what shall we do?\""]},{"number":632,"title":"Chapter 632: Invading Frost Lily Pavilion","paragraphs":["Yu Wenzhao did not act immediately.","Instead, he chose to wait.","The massive fleet remained hidden among the clouds surrounding the Frost Lily Pavilion’s territory.","Countless scouts continuously came and went.","Information flowed in without interruption.","Yet the more reports Yu Wenzhao received, the more confused he became.","There was absolutely nothing.","Even stranger, neither Yu Qingya nor Yu Feiyan made any movements afterward.","It was as though both sides had vanished from the world simultaneously.","Inside the flagship, the atmosphere had gradually become heavy.","Many elders were beginning to grow impatient.","\"Your Highness, this cannot continue.\"","The surrounding experts nodded.","They had mobilized nearly the entirety of their elite forces.","Remaining idle indefinitely was simply unrealistic.","By now, even the Frost Lily Pavilion must have already become aware of their presence.","\"Regardless of what happened, the Frost Lily Pavilion is still there. If the Fourth Princess remains inside, then she is still our enemy.\"","\"Even if the Ninth Princess never attacked them, we originally intended to deal with the Frost Lily Pavilion eventually.\"","His eyes flashed coldly.","\"The only difference is that we expected them to be weakened first.\"","Everyone looked toward Yu Wenzhao.","Meanwhile, Yu Wenzhao stood before the massive map.","His eyes remained fixed upon the Frost Lily Pavilion’s territory.","Truthfully speaking, he disliked this situation.","He preferred certainty.","He preferred understanding every variable before acting.","Yet after an entire day of investigation, he still had no answers.","No matter how many scouts he sent.","The result remained the same.","Yu Feiyan had arrived.","Yu Qingya had remained inside.","Then something happened.","After that, everything became a blank.","Yu Wenzhao slowly narrowed his eyes.","A dangerous light flickered within them.","Eventually, he let out a cold laugh.","\"Interesting.\"","The surrounding experts immediately became attentive.","Yu Wenzhao slowly turned around.","\"Since we cannot discover the truth from outside...\"","His gaze swept across everyone present.","\"Then we’ll uncover it ourselves.\"","The expressions of numerous elders brightened.","The Heaven Suppression Pavilion’s Earth Immortal smiled faintly.","\"Your Highness intends to attack?\"","Yu Wenzhao nodded.","\"That’s right.\"","His voice remained calm.","\"Whether Yu Feiyan attacked them or not changes very little. The Frost Lily Pavilion was always one of our targets.\"","Originally, he had hoped to devour both Yu Feiyan and Yu Qingya after they weakened each other.","Unfortunately, things had not unfolded according to his expectations.","However, that did not mean he intended to retreat.","Quite the opposite.","His current strength gave him enormous confidence.","Two Earth Immortals!","Nearly fifteen Immortal Realm experts!","Countless Great Ascension cultivators!","The combined foundations of the Heaven Suppression Pavilion and the Crimson Thunder Palace.","Such a force was already enough to crush most powers within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Even if the Frost Lily Pavilion remained at full strength, Yu Wenzhao still did not believe he would lose.","At worst, the losses would simply be somewhat greater.","That was all!","The Crimson Thunder Palace’s Earth Immortal immediately laughed.","\"Hahaha! That’s more like it.\"","His eyes shone fiercely.","Although their own prince lost, by contributing to the Third Prince, their position in the future won’t be too low.","\"With our current strength, why should we fear them?\"","The Heaven Suppression Pavilion experts also nodded one after another.","The confusion from earlier gradually disappeared.","After all, no matter how mysterious the situation appeared, absolute strength remained absolute strength.","Unless the Frost Lily Pavilion suddenly produced several additional Earth Immortal experts, there was no reason for them to fear anything.","Yu Wenzhao slowly raised his hand.","The entire hall immediately fell silent.","His expression became cold.","\"Pass down my orders.\"","Every expert straightened immediately.","\"The fleet will advance immediately. We head directly toward the Frost Lily Pavilion.\"","A powerful aura erupted from Yu Wenzhao’s body.","His robes fluttered violently.","A sharp light flashed through his eyes.","\"If Yu Qingya is there, we destroy her.\"","\"If Yu Feiyan is there...\"","\"We destroy her as well.\"","A cold smile appeared on his face.","The smile widened.","\"This throne war may very well end today.\"","The surrounding experts immediately became excited.","Indeed, if they could also take Frost Lily Pavilion, then the First Prince won’t have anything against them.","\"Your Highness is wise!\"","\"Hahaha! No matter what schemes they are plotting, they cannot withstand our strength!\"","\"Today, the Frost Lily Pavilion will fall!\"","Soon, the massive fleet began moving once more.","Countless flying ships surged forward.","The clouds split apart.","The heavens trembled.","Like a terrifying storm descending upon the world, the Third Prince’s faction advanced directly toward the Frost Lily Pavilion.","***","The massive fleet soon arrived above the Frost Lily Pavilion.","Thousands of flying ships covered the sky.","The clouds were torn apart.","The sunlight itself seemed blocked by the overwhelming force gathered overhead.","Countless disciples within the Frost Lily Pavilion looked up nervously.","Many of them had never witnessed such a terrifying army before.","The pressure alone was enough to make weaker cultivators struggle to breathe.","At the center of the fleet, Yu Wenzhao stood with his hands clasped behind his back.","His gaze swept across the Frost Lily Pavilion below.","The entire sect was protected by layers of icy formations.","Despite that, compared to Yu Wenzhao’s forces, those formations would not last long.","Yet strangely enough, everything appeared calm.","There was no sign of panic.","No frantic mobilization.","No experts rushing around preparing for war.","It was as though they had already expected his arrival.","That only deepened the unease within Yu Wenzhao’s heart.","However, he quickly suppressed it.","No matter what secrets they were hiding, absolute power would crush them eventually.","Slowly, he stepped forward.","His voice echoed across the heavens.","\"Yu Qingya!\"","The sound rolled throughout the entire Frost Lily Pavilion.","\"I have arrived.\"","His eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Come out and greet me.\"","Silence!","No one appeared.","The entire Frost Lily Pavilion remained motionless.","Yu Wenzhao frowned.","Several moments passed.","Still nothing.","The Heaven Suppression Pavilion’s Earth Immortal coldly snorted.","\"They’re stalling.\"","\"Your Highness, give the order. We can break their mountain gate in less than an hour.\"","The surrounding experts nodded.","Their patience was also beginning to wear thin.","Meanwhile, Yu Wenzhao’s eyes gradually became colder.","His patience had already been stretched by the strange events of the past few days.","Now even Yu Qingya refused to show herself.","Finally, he slowly raised his hand.","A terrifying aura began gathering around him.","The experts behind him immediately prepared themselves.","The fleet entered combat formation.","It appeared that a full-scale assault would begin at any moment.","However, just as Yu Wenzhao was about to issue the order—","Whoosh!","A figure suddenly appeared above the Frost Lily Pavilion.","The surrounding space rippled slightly.","Then a beautiful woman dressed in icy blue robes stepped forward.","Yu Qingya!","Her expression remained calm.","As though she wasn’t facing the most powerful army remaining in the throne war.","The moment she appeared, Yu Wenzhao’s expression softened slightly.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"So you were here after all.\"","Yu Qingya merely looked at him quietly.","Neither side spoke for several moments.","Then Yu Wenzhao slowly laughed.","\"Qingya. Looking at the situation before us, I believe you should understand reality better than anyone.\"","He gestured toward the countless flying ships behind him.","The overwhelming force assembled beneath his banner.","Two Earth Immortals.","Nearly fifteen Immortal Realm experts.","A lineup capable of crushing almost anything within the empire.","Yu Wenzhao’s smile widened.","\"Surrender!\"","His voice echoed clearly across the battlefield.","\"There is no point resisting. You know as well as I do that the Frost Lily Pavilion cannot stop me.\"","His gaze became sharp.","\"If you submit now, perhaps I can still show some mercy.\"","Silence followed.","Yu Qingya remained expressionless.","She neither accepted nor refused.","Her reaction made Yu Wenzhao frown slightly.","Something felt off.","She wasn’t angry.","She wasn’t fearful.","She wasn’t even tense.","Before Yu Wenzhao could continue speaking, another voice suddenly echoed from behind Yu Qingya.","\"Third Brother.\"","The smile on Yu Wenzhao’s face instantly froze.","His pupils contracted violently.","That voice...","Whoosh!","A second figure slowly emerged beside Yu Qingya.","Yu Feiyan!","The entire battlefield instantly fell silent.","Every expert behind Yu Wenzhao froze.","The Heaven Suppression Pavilion elders stared blankly.","The Crimson Thunder Palace experts widened their eyes.","Yu Wenzhao’s expression changed completely.","Yu Feiyan standing beside Yu Qingya?","For several moments, nobody spoke.","The scene before them completely shattered every conclusion they had reached during the past few days.","Yu Wenzhao slowly looked at Yu Qingya.","Then at Yu Feiyan.","Then back again.","His mind raced rapidly.","Countless possibilities flashed through his head.","Finally, he spoke.","His voice was noticeably colder than before.","\"What is going on here?\"","Neither princess answered immediately.","Yu Feiyan merely smiled faintly.","Meanwhile, Yu Qingya’s calm gaze remained fixed on him.","Seeing the two of them standing together, a terrible feeling suddenly appeared within Yu Wenzhao’s heart.","(Did they perhaps form an alliance?)","He couldn’t help but think so.","But that wasn’t the frightening part.","The frightening part was another possibility.","Could Yu Feiyan’s attack on the Frost Lily Pavilion have been nothing more than a trap designed to lure him here from the very beginning?"]},{"number":633,"title":"Chapter 633: The Alliance He Never Expected","paragraphs":["The more Yu Wenzhao thought about it, the more his expression darkened.","At first, the idea sounded absurd.","Yu Feiyan and Yu Qingya working together?","Of all the remaining competitors for the throne, they all should be enemies.","Sooner or later, they would inevitably have to fight one another.","There was simply no way around it.","Yet as Yu Wenzhao replayed the events of the past several days in his mind, the impossible gradually became the most reasonable explanation.","His eyes slowly narrowed.","If Yu Feiyan and Yu Qingya had truly formed an alliance...","Then everything suddenly made sense.","Why had there been no battle?","Why had the Frost Lily Pavilion remained completely intact?","Why had no one heard the sounds of fighting?","Why had Yu Feiyan’s forces seemingly vanished from the world?","The answer was simple!","There had never been a battle in the first place.","Yu Feiyan’s forces had likely entered the Frost Lily Pavilion.","Hidden within the sect’s territory, they naturally would not be visible to outside observers.","Likewise, if both sides were allies rather than enemies, there would be no chaos.","The strange blank period that had confused him for days suddenly became far easier to explain.","Yet that only created another question.","Why?","Why would Yu Qingya agree?","Why would Yu Feiyan trust her?","Both of them were competitors for the throne.","Even if they joined forces today, they would eventually become enemies tomorrow.","No matter how Yu Wenzhao viewed it, such an alliance should have been extremely unlikely.","However, whether he understood their reasons no longer mattered.","Because the reality was standing directly before him.","Yu Qingya was there.","Yu Feiyan was there.","And neither showed the slightest hostility toward the other.","Could they have planned to work together to deal with him?","The one with the greatest chance of becoming Emperor!","This seemed to be the likely reason as to why even though two of them were also enemies but had to form an alliance.","After all, Yu Wenzhao believes that among the competitors, there was truly no one who could defeat him now.","Perhaps that realization has pushed Yu Qingya and Yu Feiyan to form a temporary alliance.","The surrounding experts of the Heaven Suppression Pavilion and Crimson Thunder Palace were also gradually reaching the same conclusion.","Their expressions became increasingly ugly.","\"If they truly joined forces, then their combined strength is no joke.\"","\"They might have intentionally lured us in as well. Who knows what trump card they might have prepared?\"","They slowly realized that the lamb to be slaughtered wasn’t so easy to do now.","Yu Wenzhao slowly exhaled.","Originally, he had intended to hunt weakened prey.","Instead, it appeared he had arrived before two fully intact factions.","And perhaps, two factions that had deliberately allowed him to come.","His eyes swept across Yu Feiyan and Yu Qingya once more.","Neither princess appeared nervous. Neither showed fear despite being surrounded by his overwhelming army.","That alone was enough to make Yu Wenzhao wary.","However, only for a moment.","Soon, the coldness within his eyes returned.","Alliance?","So what?","Even if the two had truly joined forces, it did not change everything.","It merely changed the difficulty of the battle.","His current foundation was not what it had been before.","The Crimson Thunder Palace had already fallen into his hands.","His faction now possessed two Earth Immortal Realm experts.","Nearly fifteen Immortal Realm cultivators.","Countless Great Ascension Realm experts.","Even if Yu Feiyan and Yu Qingya combined their strength, defeating him would not be easy.","Perhaps the losses would be greater than expected.","Perhaps the battle would become more troublesome.","But he still did not believe he would lose.","Slowly, Yu Wenzhao smiled.","It was no longer the relaxed smile from earlier.","This smile was colder, sharper, and more dangerous.","\"So that’s how it is.\"","His voice echoed across the battlefield.","Yu Qingya remained silent.","Yu Feiyan merely smiled faintly.","Seeing their reactions, Yu Wenzhao became even more certain.","His gaze swept across both women.","Although he remained confident in victory, Yu Wenzhao had no intention of fighting both factions at the same time if it could be avoided.","After all, victory and effortless victory were two completely different things.","The current situation was troublesome precisely because Yu Feiyan and Yu Qingya appeared united.","If he could break that unity...","Then everything would become much easier.","A faint smile appeared on Yu Wenzhao’s face.","His expression gradually relaxed.","His gaze moved between the two women.","\"So the two of you truly joined forces?\"","Neither Yu Qingya nor Yu Feiyan replied.","Yu Wenzhao did not seem bothered.","Instead, he slowly shook his head.","\"Though I must admit, I never expected the Fourth Sister to make such a foolish choice.\"","His eyes settled on Yu Qingya.","\"After all, there is only one throne.\"","Yu Wenzhao continued.","\"You are competitors. Even if the two of you defeat me today...\"","His smile widened slightly.","\"What then?\"","His voice echoed across the sky.","\"Will you continue being loving sisters forever?\"","A few experts behind him chuckled softly.","Yu Wenzhao’s tone became increasingly mocking.","\"Don’t be ridiculous. The moment I fall, the alliance between the two of you will lose its purpose.\"","\"Eventually, one of you will sit upon the throne and the other will kneel.\"","His gaze locked onto Yu Qingya.","\"Or perhaps die.\"","Silence!","Yu Qingya’s expression remained unchanged.","His eyes swept across the Frost Lily Pavilion below.","\"Fourth Sister.\"","His voice became softer.","\"Have you truly thought this through?\"","He slowly gestured toward the Frost Lily Pavilion.","\"This is your foundation. The Frost Lily Pavilion has supported you for years.\"","\"If war breaks out here today, who do you think will suffer the greatest losses?\"","His eyes narrowed.","\"The Frost Lily Pavilion!\"","Yu Wenzhao paused briefly before speaking again.","\"And when the dust settles?\"","His gaze shifted toward Yu Feiyan.","\"The greatest beneficiary won’t be you. It will be the Ninth Sister.\"","The expressions of several Frost Lily Pavilion elders changed slightly.","Yu Wenzhao immediately noticed it.","A faint smile appeared.","He pressed forward relentlessly.","\"Think about it carefully. Right now, Yu Feiyan is standing inside your territory.\"","\"Her forces are inside your sect. You possess the advantage.\"","His voice became increasingly persuasive.","\"If you act now...\"","His finger pointed toward Yu Feiyan.","\"You may very well be able to capture her and her forces with ease.\"","The surrounding Heaven Suppression Pavilion experts immediately understood what Yu Wenzhao was doing.","They remained silent.","Allowing him to continue.","Yu Wenzhao’s gaze remained fixed upon Yu Qingya.","\"At that point, your strength may even rival mine. Your chances of becoming the next Emperor would increase tremendously.\"","The battlefield fell silent once more.","Countless gazes turned toward Yu Qingya.","Even some Frost Lily Pavilion disciples subconsciously looked toward her.","After all, Yu Wenzhao’s words were not entirely unreasonable.","There truly was only one throne.","Sooner or later, Yu Feiyan and Yu Qingya would have to become enemies.","At least, that was what everyone believed.","Even Yu Wenzhao himself became increasingly confident.","No alliance was truly unbreakable, especially one built between rivals.","Yet, to everyone’s surprise—","Yu Qingya’s expression did not change in the slightest.","It was as though Yu Wenzhao’s words had completely failed to affect her.","Finally, she spoke.","Her voice was calm, almost indifferent.","\"I have no interest in the throne.\"","The moment those words left her mouth, the entire battlefield froze.","Yu Wenzhao’s smile immediately stiffened.","The Heaven Suppression Pavilion elders stared blankly.","Even many Frost Lily Pavilion disciples looked shocked.","For a brief moment, complete silence descended upon the battlefield.","Yu Wenzhao frowned.","\"You what?\"","This might be the biggest joke he had ever heard.","Yu Qingya had no interest in the throne?","Then what was she doing gathering various forces, including the Frost Lily Pavilion?","Why hadn’t she withdrawn before the battle for the throne began?","Yu Qingya’s gaze remained calm.","\"I said...\"","Her eyes slowly moved toward Yu Feiyan.","\"I have no interest in becoming Emperor.\"","Shock flashed across countless faces.","Yu Wenzhao stared at her as though he had misheard.","The throne war had already reached this stage.","Yet now she was claiming she never cared about the throne?","Yu Qingya continued.","Her voice remained steady.","\"The rightful owner of the throne...\"","She looked directly at Yu Feiyan.","\"...is the Ninth Sister.\"","Boom!","The statement struck everyone like a thunderbolt.","The Heaven Suppression Pavilion experts were completely stunned.","The Crimson Thunder Palace elders froze.","Even Yu Wenzhao’s pupils contracted.","Meanwhile, Yu Feiyan merely smiled softly.","At that moment, the atmosphere became incomparably strange.","Because everyone could hear it clearly.","Yu Qingya’s words contained neither reluctance nor unwillingness.","They were genuine.","Yu Wenzhao suddenly understood something.","If Yu Qingya truly had no desire for the throne...","Then the greatest weakness in his entire plan no longer existed.","There would be no betrayal.","No internal conflict.","No struggle for power between the two women.","At least not in the way he had anticipated.","That means that he might need to fight against the forces of the two princesses!"]},{"number":634,"title":"Chapter 634: Dangerous Variable","paragraphs":["Among the countless disciples of the Frost Lily Pavilion, confusion had already reached its peak.","No one understood what was happening.","Everything that had happened over the past few days felt completely surreal.","When news first arrived that the Ninth Princess was marching toward the Frost Lily Pavilion, the entire sect had immediately entered a state of preparation.","Many disciples had believed a great battle was about to erupt.","After all, Yu Feiyan was one of the remaining contenders for the throne.","And the Frost Lily Pavilion stood firmly behind the Fourth Princess.","The two sides should have been enemies.","There should have been bloodshed.","There should have been war.","Yet the reality that followed was nothing like what anyone expected.","Many disciples still remembered the day Yu Feiyan arrived.","The Ninth Princess had entered their territory personally.","Not only that, she had requested to meet the Fourth Princess directly.","At the time, countless disciples had secretly mocked her.","Some believed she had come to negotiate.","Others believed she had come to surrender.","A few even thought she had gone mad.","After all, entering enemy territory personally was simply too reckless, especially when she didn’t even bring a single guard with her.","From their perspective, once Yu Feiyan stepped into the sect, her life was already in the Fourth Princess’s hands.","Yet shortly afterward, when she emerged from the Hall, something had changed.","The Pavilion Master’s attitude toward Yu Feiyan had changed.","The elders’ attitudes had also changed.","Even the usually cold and aloof Fourth Princess seemed different.","And before long, an even more shocking order arrived.","The Ninth Princess’s forces were permitted to enter the Frost Lily Pavilion.","At the time, countless disciples thought they had misheard.","Yu Feiyan’s army?","Entering the sect?","The very same army that should have been their enemy?","Yet the order came directly from the Fourth Princess and the Sect Master.","No one dared disobey.","Thus, tens of thousands of cultivators entered the Frost Lily Pavilion peacefully.","Not as prisoners or captives, but as guests.","Moreover, there was no announcement or whatsoever.","Naturally, this only caused even greater confusion.","Many disciples secretly discussed the matter and believed a temporary alliance must have been formed.","Others speculated that the Fourth Princess intended to cooperate with the Ninth Princess to deal with the Third Prince and First Prince.","That explanation seemed quite reasonable.","After all, Yu Wenzhao’s rise had become increasingly threatening.","With the Crimson Thunder Palace added to his side, he had become the strongest contender publicly.","If the Fourth Princess and Ninth Princess joined forces temporarily, perhaps they could suppress him together.","Although unusual, such an arrangement was not impossible.","Others even thought that perhaps the Ninth Princess must have surrendered and was working for their Princess.","At least, those were some of the conclusions that many made until now.","\"The rightful owner of the throne is the Ninth Sister.\"","Yu Qingya announced.","Countless disciples stared at the Fourth Princess in shock.","Her words continued to echo within their minds.","Many disciples stood completely frozen. Some even wondered whether they had heard incorrectly.","They were fellow disciples and knew the Fourth Princess personality quite well.","And her ambition to become the Emperor has never been concealed as well.","So they were utterly confused when the Fourth Princess had declared that she had no interest in becoming Emperor.","Not only that, she openly acknowledged Yu Feiyan as the rightful heir.","The shocking part was not only Yu Qingya herself.","The Elders, The Pavilion Master and the senior leaders of the Frost Lily Pavilion haven’t objected either.","They remained standing quietly behind Yu Qingya as though everything she had just said was something that they agreed as well.","Just what the hell happened during that meeting?","What exactly had Yu Feiyan done to them?","No one knew, and no one dared ask.","Because regardless of their confusion, there was one fact they all understood.","The people standing above them had already made their decision.","And the will of the Pavilion Master and the Fourth Princess was absolute.","No matter what they personally thought.","No matter how unbelievable everything seemed.","They would just need to obey.","Meanwhile, Yu Wenzhao’s gaze never left Yu Feiyan.","The wariness within his eyes deepened noticeably.","At first, he had only viewed Yu Feiyan as an unpredictable variable.","A troublesome opponent with some strange methods.","But now, he was beginning to reevaluate her entirely.","Yu Qingya, one of the most talented princesses of the current generation.","Proud, cold, and aloof.","Even among the imperial princes and princesses, she was infamous for being stubborn and never yielding to anyone.","Yet this very same woman had openly acknowledged Yu Feiyan as Emperor.","The more Yu Wenzhao thought about it, the more dangerous Yu Feiyan appeared.","His eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Ninth Sister...\"","His voice carried none of its previous mockery.","Only vigilance remained.","\"It seems you’ve hidden yourself quite well.\"","Countless eyes turned toward Yu Feiyan.","Facing the attention of the entire battlefield, she merely blinked innocently.","A trace of confusion even appeared on her face.","\"What do you mean, Third Brother?\"","Her tone sounded completely sincere.","If not for the fact that Yu Qingya and Frost Lily Pavilion Elders were all acting submissive, one might even think that someone wronged Yu Feiyan.","Yu Wenzhao’s eyes narrowed immediately.","\"Hahaha...\"","The laughter gradually faded. The killing intent within his eyes became increasingly obvious.","\"Ninth Sister! I truly underestimated you.\"","The atmosphere immediately became heavier.","Yu Feiyan simply smiled.","Yu Wenzhao continued staring directly at her.","Originally, among all the remaining competitors, Yu Feiyan had been the one he paid the least attention to.","She had been little more than an afterthought.","Yet now, the situation has reversed completely.","No matter how cunning and powerful the First Prince and Fourth Princess were, they were still people whom Yu Wenzhao deeply understood.","Although he wouldn’t claim to know everything about them, he knew enough to know just how much preparation he needed to deal with them.","But Yu Feiyan?","The more he tried to read her, the more confused he became.","It was even more confusing when he compared her timid and cowardly demeanor of the past to her current self.","Whether something had happened to make her change or she had been pretending before, it didn’t matter.","The current Yu Feiyan was someone he could not see through.","She was a variable.","A very dangerous variable!","And dangerous variables needed to be eliminated immediately.","A faint killing intent leaked from Yu Wenzhao’s body.","The surrounding temperature, which was already very low, seemed to drop even more.","His eyes locked onto Yu Feiyan.","\"I never thought you could subdue the Fourth Sister so easily.\"","The words echoed clearly across the battlefield.","Yu Wenzhao intentionally used the word \"subdue\" to humiliate Yu Qingya.","Yu Wenzhao wanted to see if there was any reaction from Yu Qingya when he used those words, but there was still no retort and objection for her.","Which only made the situation even more frightening.","Just what had Yu Feiyan done to make Yu Qingya become so submissive?","However, Yu Wenzhao no longer intended to waste time in thinking about such a question whose answer he won’t be able to come up with.","His instincts were screaming warnings.","Every moment Yu Feiyan remained alive felt increasingly dangerous.","The First Prince could wait.","The Fourth Princess could also wait.","But this Ninth Princess, he suddenly felt, could not.","Slowly, Yu Wenzhao raised his hand.","The smile vanished completely from his face.","\"Get ready!\"","Boom!","A terrifying aura erupted from his body.","The sky trembled violently.","The clouds shattered apart.","Behind him, the two Earth Immortal Realm experts immediately stepped forward.","Their cultivation exploded outward without restraint.","The pressure descended upon heaven and earth.","Many weaker cultivators felt their legs shaking uncontrollably.","Yet the terrifying pressure did not stop there.","One Immortal Realm expert after another released their aura.","Nearly fifteen Immortal Realm cultivators stood proudly behind Yu Wenzhao.","The heavens darkened.","The spiritual Qi of the entire region became chaotic.","The massive fleet began shifting formation.","Countless flying ships moved simultaneously.","Killing intent flooded the sky.","The Third Prince’s army had finally revealed its fangs.","Yu Wenzhao’s voice echoed throughout the battlefield.","\"Ninth Sister. You have become far too dangerous.\"","A frightening light flashed within his eyes.","\"Today...\"","His aura exploded once more.","\"I will personally eliminate you!\"","And for the first time since arriving at the Frost Lily Pavilion, Yu Wenzhao finally prepared to unleash the full strength of his faction.","The terrifying pressure of nearly fifteen Immortal Realm experts blanketed the heavens.","Killing intent churned throughout the battlefield.","Countless cultivators unconsciously held their breath.","Everyone could feel it.","War was about to begin.","Yet in the center of it all, the person standing at the heart of the storm showed not the slightest trace of panic.","Yu Feiyan blinked.","Then she sighed.","\"Third Brother! Why are you in such a hurry?\"","Yu Wenzhao’s expression remained cold.","Yu Feiyan shook her head helplessly.","She looked genuinely aggrieved.","\"And here I was hoping to have a good talk before the fight.\""]},{"number":635,"title":"Chapter 635: Have a Tea","paragraphs":["The corners of Yu Wenzhao’s mouth twitched.","A talk? Was she serious?","Yu Feiyan smiled brightly.","\"How about this?\"","She casually produced a jade tea cup from her storage ring.","\"Let’s calm down first.\"","A stream of spiritual water appeared.","Moments later, fragrant tea leaves floated within the cup.","The rich aroma immediately spread through the air. One could immediately tell that this tea wasn’t ordinary tea and was probably very beneficial to one’s body.","Yu Feiyan raised the cup slightly.","\"Would Third Brother like to discuss things over tea?\"","Yu Wenzhao stared at her.","Then his expression darkened further.","Talk?","Tea?","Did she think he was an idiot?","His gaze subconsciously drifted toward Yu Qingya.","The Fourth Princess stood calmly behind Yu Feiyan.","There was not the slightest dissatisfaction on her face.","The scene only strengthened the suspicions already growing within his heart.","Yu Qingya was not someone who could be persuaded through mere words.","He knew exactly what kind of person she was.","Even when facing their Imperial Father, she had never been the type to lower her head easily.","Yet now she was standing behind Yu Feiyan as though everything was perfectly natural.","The more Yu Wenzhao thought about it, the more absurd it seemed.","Some kind of secret technique?","Soul manipulation?","Mind control?","Perhaps the person had been replaced with someone who looked like her?","Whatever it was, he had no intention of finding out personally.","Yu Wenzhao’s eyes narrowed.","\"I have no interest in drinking tea with you.\"","His voice was cold.","Yu Feiyan blinked.","\"Really?\"","She looked somewhat disappointed and hurt.","\"I have some excellent tea.\"","\"No!\"","Yu Wenzhao’s answer was immediate. Not a shred of hesitation existed within his voice.","Yu Feiyan looked around, then she sighed dramatically.","\"Third Brother.\"","She shook her head.","\"You aren’t scared of me, are you?\"","The moment those words left her mouth, countless cultivators nearly choked.","Scared?","The Third Prince?","The current strongest contender for the throne?","Yu Wenzhao’s expression immediately darkened.","Yu Feiyan continued innocently.","\"It would be understandable, of course.\"","A smile slowly appeared on her face.","\"I mean, if you’re afraid of being alone with me, you can bring all your elders.\"","She pointed toward the Immortal Realm experts behind him.","\"Bring them all!\"","A few cultivators almost coughed blood.","Yu Feiyan continued speaking seriously.","\"Actually, I can come over to your side instead. Would that make Third Brother feel safer?\"","The atmosphere instantly became strange.","Many people looked at Yu Feiyan as though she had lost her mind.","Cross over to the enemy’s side?","Personally?","Who would suggest such a thing?","Yet Yu Feiyan seemed completely sincere.","\"If you’re worried about being outnumbered, I can come alone.\"","She nodded thoughtfully.","\"That should put your mind at ease.\"","Yu Wenzhao’s face grew darker with every sentence.","The veins on his forehead visibly twitched.","Yu Feiyan was openly provoking him, though her expression remained completely innocent.","Yu Wenzhao, however, wasn’t stupid. He could easily see through her scheme.","Though he didn’t understand what gave her the confidence to believe she would be able to act if she came alone.","Even then, he wasn’t going to play right into her hands.","He had the advantage, and there was no need to risk his life.","Yu Wenzhao stared at her for several long moments.","\"You think this is fear?\"","Yu Feiyan nodded honestly.","\"It certainly looks that way.\"","Crack!","A vein pulsed near his temple.","For perhaps the first time in years, he felt the urge to strangle someone personally.","Unfortunately, that urge was precisely why he refused to approach her.","She was deliberately provoking him, so that he might approach her but he wasn’t going to fall for that.","Yu Wenzhao slowly rose to his feet.","His robes billowed violently.","The killing intent surrounding him intensified.","\"No! We don’t have anything to discuss with each other. Either you submit, or I will force you to submit!\"","The smile disappeared from Yu Feiyan’s face.","For a brief moment, disappointment appeared within her eyes.","\"A pity.\"","She lowered the tea cup.","\"I thought we could settle things peacefully.\"","Yu Wenzhao’s aura surged once more.","The heavens rumbled.","His gaze remained fixed firmly upon Yu Feiyan.","\"Whatever tricks you possess. Whatever methods you used on Fourth Sister. They will not work on me.\"","Yu Wenzhao said.","The moment those words fell, Yu Wenzhao raised his hand.","His expression was cold and absolute.","\"Attack!\"","Boom!","The atmosphere instantly exploded.","The countless cultivators standing behind Yu Wenzhao erupted into motion as though they had been waiting for this very command.","In truth, many of them had.","Ever since arriving at the Frost Lily Pavilion, they had been restraining themselves.","Now they no longer needed to.","Killing intent flooded the sky.","Thousands upon thousands of cultivators surged forward simultaneously.","The massive fleet shifted formation.","Countless flying ships lit up with dazzling light.","Array cannons emerged from their hulls.","The air itself distorted under the immense concentration of power.","Many cultivators felt their blood boil with excitement.","Finally!","The battle had begun.","\"Kill!\"","\"Capture the Ninth Princess!\"","\"Destroy the Frost Lily Pavilion!\"","Roars shook the heavens.","At the front of the army, several Immortal Realm experts attacked first.","Their figures transformed into streaks of light.","Mountain-sized palms descended from above.","Sword lights stretched across the sky.","Spears capable of piercing the heavens shot forward.","The entire battlefield seemed on the verge of collapse.","Amidst all the chaos, Yu Feiyan remained calm.","She simply stood there holding her tea cup.","The fragrant aroma continued drifting through the air.","As though the battle unfolding before her had nothing to do with her.","Behind her, however, Yu Qingya had already moved.","The Fourth Princess slowly raised her hand.","Her expression remained as cold as ever.","\"Prepare for battle!\"","Her voice spread throughout the Frost Lily Pavilion.","Instantly, the entire sect came alive.","The elders stepped forward.","The disciples entered their assigned positions.","Countless formation masters activated prepared arrays.","The Frost Lily Pavilion’s Grand Guardian Formation was activated at full power.","The incoming attacks arrived almost immediately.","Boom! Boom!","A cannon blast hit the formation, followed by a giant palm slammed into the barrier.","The heavens shook violently.","Shockwaves swept across hundreds of kilometers yet the barrier merely rippled and did not break.","Another Immortal Realm attack followed.","Then another.","And another.","Boom! Boom! Boom! Boom!","The entire sky seemed to explode continuously.","An endless torrent of attacks crashed against the Frost Lily Pavilion’s defenses.","The barrier trembled violently.","The surrounding space fractured repeatedly.","Many disciples turned pale from the terrifying pressure, but the formation still endured.","Countless Frost Lily Pavilion disciples immediately erupted into cheers.","\"It blocked it!\"","\"The formation held!\"","\"As expected of our Frost Lily Pavilion Grand Formation!\"","...","Meanwhile, Yu Wenzhao’s forces were also not in a bad mood, as they had already expected this.","Just like when attacking the Crimson Thunder Palace, they had been prepared to play the long game.","The formation could protect them for now, but for how much longer?","Meanwhile, Yu Feiyan took a small sip of tea.","Then she sighed softly.","\"What a waste!\"","The people around her blinked.","Yu Feiyan looked at the countless attacks crashing against the barrier.","\"I spent all that effort brewing good tea.\"","She shook her head regretfully.","\"And Third Brother wouldn’t even try a cup.\"","Then a sinister smile appeared on her face.","\"Looks like I can only resort to force then!\""]},{"number":636,"title":"Chapter 636: Opening the Gates of War","paragraphs":["Yu Feiyan did not move immediately and neither did Yu Wenzhao.","The two simply watched each other from opposite sides of the battlefield.","One stood before the Frost Lily Pavilion.","The other sat upon his throne aboard the flagship.","Both appeared completely calm and completely confident.","Neither seemed worried in the slightest.","The ongoing assault continued without interruption.","Attack after attack crashed into the Frost Lily Pavilion’s Grand Guardian Formation.","Violent explosions echoed endlessly yet neither side paid much attention to it.","Because everyone understood that this was merely the beginning.","The true battle would only begin after the formation fell.","The Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal stood with his hands behind his back.","Beside him stood the Crimson Thunder Palace’s Earth Immortal.","Neither had any intention of participating in the assault against the formation.","There was no need.","The formation would eventually fall under the combined efforts of so many cultivators.","Why waste their strength now?","Their true opponents were elsewhere.","The two Earth Immortals occasionally glanced toward the Frost Lily Pavilion.","More specifically, toward the Frost Lily Pavilion’s own Earth Immortal ancestor.","Once the defensive formation was broken, the real battle would begin.","Although they held a numerical advantage of two against one, neither dared to be negligent.","Earth Immortal Realm experts were not existences that could be underestimated.","At their level, a single mistake could prove fatal.","Thus, both sides remained patient.","Hours gradually passed.","The sun slowly shifted across the sky.","The endless bombardment never ceased.","Yet the Frost Lily Pavilion’s Grand Guardian Formation continued to endure.","At first, many cultivators were excited then got impatient.","Then gradually they became bored.","The battlefield gradually entered a strange stalemate.","Yet strangely enough, neither Yu Wenzhao nor Yu Feiyan appeared concerned.","Both continued waiting calmly.","As though each possessed complete confidence in whatever was about to happen.","Eventually, Yu Feiyan suddenly stood up.","The movement attracted quite a few gazes, but no one paid it much attention.","Yu Feiyan calmly glanced toward the cultivators under her command, then she spoke.","\"Everyone, prepare yourselves.\"","The moment those words left her mouth, the cultivators belonging to Yu Feiyan’s faction visibly straightened.","Their eyes lit up.","Their spirits rose.","Finally!","For days now, they had been eager to fight.","Originally, they had followed Yu Feiyan with the intention of attacking the Frost Lily Pavilion.","Instead, before they could even draw their weapons, their Princess had somehow convinced the Fourth Princess to join her side.","As a result, they had spent the past several days doing absolutely nothing.","Now, however, things were finally different.","Their Princess had finally given an order.","Which meant action was coming.","Excitement immediately spread through their ranks.","Weapons appeared.","Auras rose.","Countless cultivators began preparing themselves.","Yu Feiyan looked toward Yu Qingya.","\"Fourth Sister.\"","Yu Qingya turned toward her.","\"What is it?\"","Yu Feiyan smiled.","\"In a while, deactivate the formation when I give a signal.\"","The moment those words left her mouth, Yu Qingya’s expression changed slightly.","Even several Frost Lily Pavilion elders widened their eyes.","Deactivate the formation?","Now?","The entire reason they had been able to resist was because of the Grand Guardian Formation.","Without it, they would immediately be exposed to Yu Wenzhao’s overwhelming forces.","Yu Qingya frowned.","\"Ninth Sister.\"","Her voice grew serious.","\"This is not a good idea.\"","She glanced toward Yu Wenzhao’s army.","\"The Third Brother has many powerful cultivators under his command. There are nearly fifteen Immortal Realm experts.\"","\"Without the formation, we will immediately lose our greatest advantage.\"","Unlike before, Yu Qingya did not blindly agree.","This was war.","The lives of countless disciples were involved.","Even if she trusted Yu Feiyan, she could not simply ignore such concerns.","The surrounding elders immediately nodded in agreement.","Clearly, they shared the same opinion.","However, Yu Feiyan merely smiled.","There was not the slightest worry on her face.","\"I know.\"","Yu Qingya looked at her.","Yu Feiyan casually took another sip of tea.","Then she spoke calmly.","\"Don’t worry. I have a plan.\"","The confidence in her voice was absolute.","For some reason, the moment those words left her mouth, the surrounding tension seemed to lessen slightly.","Yu Qingya stared at her for several moments.","In the end, she sighed softly.","After a brief silence, Yu Qingya nodded reluctantly.","\"Very well!\"","Her answer immediately caused several elders to become anxious yet before they could speak, Yu Qingya raised her hand.","The elders immediately fell silent.","If Yu Qingya had already made her decision, there was little they could do to change it.","Meanwhile, on the opposite side of the battlefield, Yu Wenzhao observed the entire exchange from afar.","Although he could not hear their conversation, he could tell that something had changed.","His eyes narrowed slightly.","A faint sense of unease surfaced within his heart once more.","And for reasons he could not explain, the sight of Yu Feiyan smiling calmly made that unease grow even stronger.","On Yu Wenzhao’s side, many cultivators had already begun to assume that the situation would continue like this for a while longer.","The Frost Lily Pavilion would hide behind its Grand Guardian Formation.","They would continue attacking.","Eventually, the formation would weaken.","Then collapse.","After that, the true battle would begin.","However, the next development completely caught them off guard.","Yu Feiyan suddenly raised her hand.","Her calm voice echoed across the battlefield.","\"Now.\"","The moment the word left her mouth, Yu Qingya immediately responded.","The massive Grand Guardian Formation that had protected the Frost Lily Pavilion for hours suddenly began to dim.","Within moments, the formation was completely deactivated.","The battlefield froze.","Even the endless bombardment seemed to pause momentarily.","Countless eyes widened in disbelief.","\"What?!\"","\"They deactivated their formation?!\"","\"Why would they do that?\"","\"Is it a trap?\"","\"Have they gone mad?\"","Confused cries erupted everywhere.","Even many Frost Lily Pavilion disciples felt their hearts skip a beat.","Although they had received prior instructions, seeing the formation actually disappear still made them nervous.","On the opposite side, many of Yu Wenzhao’s subordinates were equally stunned.","The development was simply too strange.","At the center of the army, Yu Wenzhao’s eyes narrowed.","He did not immediately issue an attack order.","Instead, he maintained his caution.","His gaze locked firmly onto Yu Feiyan.","The Ninth Princess still stood there calmly, not a trace of panic appeared on her face.","If this was truly a mistake, why wasn’t she worried?","If this was desperation, why did she seem so relaxed?","No!","There had to be something else.","Thus, Yu Wenzhao remained patient.","The army behind him also refrained from moving recklessly.","The entire battlefield entered an awkward silence.","Yu Feiyan smiled.","The next moment, her voice thundered across the battlefield.","\"Kill them!\"","Boom!","Countless cultivators from Yu Feiyan’s faction erupted into motion.","For days they had been waiting.","For days they had been suppressing their battle intent.","Now they no longer needed to hold back.","A deafening roar erupted from their ranks.","\"Kill!\"","Thousands upon thousands of cultivators surged forward.","At the same time, the Frost Lily Pavilion’s forces also moved.","Yu Qingya’s eyes turned cold.","Her sword appeared in her hand.","\"Attack!\"","The Frost Lily Pavilion disciples immediately followed.","The elders soared into the sky.","Formation masters abandoned their defensive positions.","The entire sect transformed from a fortress into an army.","Two massive forces charged forward simultaneously.","The sight stunned countless spectators.","No one had expected the defenders to launch the first offensive.","They were actually charging directly toward Yu Wenzhao’s superior army."]},{"number":637,"title":"Chapter 637: The Ninth Princess Watches","paragraphs":["Even the two Earth Immortal experts on Yu Wenzhao’s side frowned.","Had they gone insane?","Meanwhile, Yu Wenzhao’s eyes flashed sharply.","Although surprised, his response was immediate.","A cold smile appeared on his face.","\"So that’s your plan?\"","His voice echoed throughout the battlefield.","\"If you wish to die, I will grant your wish!\"","He raised his hand.","The next moment, his own army exploded into action.","\"Meet them head-on!\"","He believed that in a head-on fight, his army should emerge victorious easily.","Of course, he didn’t underestimate his opponents.","However, on his side were two Earth Immortals, while on Yu Feiyan and Yu Qingya’s side, there was only one.","After they defeated the Frost Lily Pavilion’s Earth Immortal, then no matter how many casualties the other side suffered, two Earth Immortals could easily make up for that difference.","Hence, he wasn’t in the least afraid of a head-on clash.","BOOOM! BOOOM!","The two massive armies finally collided head-on.","Countless cultivators charged into battle.","Sword lights filled the sky.","Spears pierced through the clouds.","Powerful techniques erupted one after another.","Explosions echoed endlessly throughout the battlefield.","The entire region descended into chaos almost instantly.","A crimson sea of flames swept across the battlefield.","Moments later, a torrent of icy lotus petals descended from above.","The two attacks collided violently.","BOOM!","The resulting shockwave flattened mountains in the distance.","Cultivators from both sides continuously unleashed their strongest techniques.","The sky became a dazzling display of colors as countless different forms of Qi intertwined together.","The battlefield resembled the end of the world.","Far above the battlefield, three terrifying auras suddenly erupted.","BOOOM!","The heavens shook violently.","The Earth Immortal ancestor of the Frost Lily Pavilion stepped forward.","At almost the same moment, the Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal and the Crimson Thunder Palace’s Earth Immortal moved as well.","Space distorted around them.","Even the Immortal Ascension Realm experts below instinctively retreated.","No one dared remain too close.","The battle of Earth Immortals had begun.","Several Frost Lily Pavilion Grand Elders immediately rose into the sky.","Their cultivation erupted without reservation.","Clearly, they intended to assist their ancestor.","However—","\"Stop!\"","A calm voice echoed through their minds.","The Frost Lily Pavilion’s Earth Immortal ancestor did not even turn around, but her command immediately froze the Grand Elders in place.","\"Ancestor...\"","One of the Grand Elders clenched his fists.","\"We can help!\"","The old woman finally glanced toward them.","Her expression remained calm.","\"No!\"","The Grand Elders fell silent.","The truth was that what she said wasn’t entirely accurate.","Three peak Immortal Ascension Realm experts joining forces might actually be able to stall an Earth Immortal temporarily.","However, that assistance would come at a cost.","The Frost Lily Pavilion only possessed a handful of Immortal Ascension Realm experts, and even with Yu Feiyan’s forces added to theirs, their numbers were still inferior to Yu Wenzhao’s.","If three of their strongest experts left the battlefield, who would stop the others?","One or two remaining behind would be insufficient.","Yet if three or more stayed behind, the balance below could be maintained.","The Grand Elders slowly lowered their heads.","\"Leave them to me!\"","The Grand Elders hesitated briefly before eventually retreating.","Soon, only three figures remained standing high above the battlefield.","One against two!","The Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal looked at the Frost Lily Pavilion ancestor.","A mocking smile gradually appeared on his face.","For a moment, he simply observed her.","Then he chuckled.","\"Su Binglan!\"","His voice carried across the heavens.","\"Did you ever imagine that things would come to this?\"","The Frost Lily Pavilion ancestor, Su Binglan remained silent.","Judging by Heaven Suppression Earth immortal, one could tell that there is a story between the two.","The Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal continued.","\"A thousand years ago, your Frost Lily Pavilion stood at the height of its glory. You looked down upon countless forces. Your reputation shook the entire empire.\"","His smile widened.","\"And now?\"","He slowly spread his arms.","\"Your sect is under siege, with your disciples fighting for their lives. And you...\"","His gaze sharpened.","\"Are standing alone before two Earth Immortals.\"","The Crimson Thunder Palace’s Earth Immortal merely watched quietly.","He too was someone whose chosen side had lost in this battle for the throne.","However, if he made sufficient contributions, there shouldn’t be much impact on his sect afterward.","In any case, no matter how one looked at it, the Frost Lily Pavilion was at a disadvantage.","\"If you wish to reminisce about the past, I can accompany you after the battle.\"","The Frost Lily Pavilion’s Earth Immortal spoke without any emotion on her face.","Despite facing two Earth Immortals, she didn’t seem afraid at all.","The Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal raised an eyebrow.","Su Binglan slowly lifted her sword.","A terrifying sword intent instantly pierced the heavens.","\"But first...\"","Her eyes turned cold.","\"Let’s see whether you can survive!\"","BOOOM!","A terrifying wave of sword Qi erupted across the sky.","A chilling aura swept across the heavens.","The temperature plummeted at an astonishing rate.","Ice spread through the air.","Ice crystals appeared throughout the battlefield.","Even the clouds overhead began freezing.","The world itself seemed on the verge of turning into a frozen wasteland.","Countless cultivators shivered involuntarily.","Many weaker experts immediately retreated further away.","The battle between Earth Immortals was simply too terrifying.","Yet despite the overwhelming cold, the Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal and the Crimson Thunder Palace’s Earth Immortal remained completely unaffected.","The Qi surrounding their bodies naturally repelled the invading frost.","Their expressions did not change in the slightest.","The Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal laughed.","\"Good!\"","His aura erupted.","BOOOM!","A massive phantom mountain materialized behind him.","The heavens trembled.","An oppressive force descended upon the entire battlefield.","At the same time, the Crimson Thunder Palace’s Earth Immortal made his move.","Crack! Crack! Crack!","Countless crimson bolts of lightning tore through the sky.","The thunderous roar shook heaven and earth.","The destructive power contained within each bolt was enough to annihilate ordinary Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators instantly.","Su Binglan’s expression remained calm.","Her sword moved as a sea of frost erupted.","Thousands of sword lights shot toward her opponents.","BOOOM! BOOOM! BOOOM!","Violent explosions continuously erupted across the sky.","The surrounding heavens seemed unable to withstand the pressure.","The battle immediately entered a fierce stalemate.","However, everyone could see the disadvantage she faced.","One against two.","No matter how powerful she was, no matter how confident she appeared, the numerical disadvantage was simply too great.","Every exchange forced her to defend against attacks from two different directions.","Every move consumed far more Qi than her opponents.","Gradually, the pressure began to accumulate.","Yet neither of the two Earth Immortals felt any joy.","Because although they held the advantage, defeating an Earth Immortal was never easy, especially one as powerful as the Frost Lily Pavilion ancestor.","If she chose to fight desperately, both of them could suffer severe injuries.","They could only take their time, slowly chipping away at her strength and eventually defeating her.","Far below, the situation on the main battlefield was remarkably similar.","The armies collided like two raging oceans.","Cultivators fell every moment as blood stained the sky.","With the ferocity of the battle, the balance gradually tilted toward one side.","Yu Wenzhao’s side was winning.","The advantage in numbers was simply too obvious.","The advantage in experts was equally apparent.","Nearly fifteen Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators rampaged throughout the battlefield.","Everywhere they passed, immense pressure followed.","Although the Frost Lily Pavilion and Yu Feiyan’s forces fought fiercely, they were gradually being pushed back.","The disparity between the two sides slowly became visible.","High above the battlefield, Yu Qingya’s beautiful face remained calm, yet her eyes had become increasingly solemn.","If not for having depleted some of Qi from attacking their Grand Formation, Yu Wenzhao force might be even more powerful.","Still the situation was not very optimistic.","Even with both armies combined, they still struggled to match Yu Wenzhao’s faction.","Not far away, several Frost Lily Pavilion elders were already fighting bitter battles against multiple opponents.","Meanwhile, Yu Wenzhao sat calmly atop his flagship.","His gaze swept across the battlefield.","The corners of his mouth slowly rose.","This was the outcome he had expected.","A direct confrontation favored him.","The longer the battle continued, the greater his advantage would become.","Sooner or later, the enemy lines would collapse.","Sooner or later, the Frost Lily Pavilion’s Earth Immortal would be overwhelmed.","And once that happened, the battle would be over.","However, for some reason, Yu Wenzhao still couldn’t relax.","His gaze instinctively drifted toward a certain figure.","Yu Feiyan!","The Ninth Princess remained astonishingly calm.","She wasn’t even participating in the fighting.","Instead, she stood quietly atop the city wall.","A cup of tea remained in her hand.","She occasionally took a sip as though she were merely watching a performance.","There was not the slightest trace of anxiety on her face.","Not even as her side appeared to be slowly losing ground.","The sight caused Yu Wenzhao’s brows to furrow.","The battle was proceeding exactly as logic dictated.","Exactly as he had expected.","And yet, the calmer Yu Feiyan appeared, the more uneasy he became."]},{"number":638,"title":"Chapter 638: Yu Feiyan makes her move","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, atop the Flying Ship, Yu Wenzhao’s attention never completely left Yu Feiyan.","Although the battle was proceeding favorably for him, he remained vigilant.","Thus, even while commanding the army, he had deliberately surrounded himself with layers of protection.","Several Great Ascension Realm experts remained nearby at all times.","Numerous defensive treasures had already been activated.","Formation barriers quietly surrounded the Flying Ship.","Yu Wenzhao did not care what others thought.","Coward?","Paranoid?","Overly cautious?","He didn’t care.","As long as he obtained the throne, none of those opinions mattered.","He had already learned his lesson from his failed attack on Yu Longxuan. Being more prepared was always better than not being prepared.","Far away, Yu Feiyan quietly finished the last sip of tea.","The empty cup disappeared into her storage ring.","She glanced around the battlefield.","The Earth Immortals were fighting each other.","The Immortal Ascension Realm experts were also occupied.","A smile appeared on her face.","Whoosh!","Her figure suddenly vanished.","The movement was so subtle that almost nobody noticed.","Even Yu Qingya only sensed a slight fluctuation before Yu Feiyan disappeared completely.","A moment later—","Behind Yu Wenzhao’s throne.","Space distorted slightly.","A figure silently emerged.","Yu Feiyan clasped her hands behind her back and smiled.","\"You are quite a cautious one.\"","Her voice suddenly sounded behind him.","\"Unlike your sister.\"","The smile on her face widened.","Yu Wenzhao’s pupils instantly contracted.","His entire body stiffened.","A chill ran down his spine.","How?","When?","The place was protected by numerous defensive artifacts, so how had Yu Feiyan infiltrated it?","And instantaneously at that?","He had been keeping an eye on her throughout the battle.","One moment she was far away.","The next moment, she was standing behind him.","Before he could even turn around, he instinctively leaped forward.","\"Protect me!\"","His furious roar shook the Flying Ship.","Several Great Ascension Realm guards immediately reacted.","However, it was already too late.","The moment Yu Feiyan appeared, the outcome had already been decided.","Or more accurately, the moment Qin Lingxiao decided to act.","Standing behind Yu Feiyan, Qin Lingxiao smiled faintly.","The reason she had patiently waited until now was precisely because she did not wish to expose her full strength.","Therefore, only after all of the Immortal Realm cultivators on Yu Wenzhao’s side were occupied did she finally make her move.","Against a few Great Ascension Realm cultivators, she naturally did not need to reveal her Golden Immortal cultivation.","Late Great Ascension Realm strength was already more than enough.","Yu Feiyan casually stepped forward, and her hand shot out.","Grab!","She seized Yu Wenzhao by the collar.","The Third Prince of the empire.","One of the strongest contenders for the throne yet at this moment, he had been caught as easily as a chicken.","\"Release me!\"","Yu Wenzhao roared immediately.","The initial shock quickly transformed into fury.","\"Do you know what you’re doing?!\"","His voice echoed throughout the Flying Ship.","\"If you release me now, I can still pretend this never happened! Otherwise...\"","Threat after threat poured from his mouth.","Unfortunately, Yu Feiyan appeared completely uninterested.","She merely looked at him.","Then she tilted her head slightly.","\"You seem scared.\"","Yu Wenzhao nearly choked.","Scared?","Of course he was scared!","Someone had somehow appeared behind him without triggering a single defensive formation.","Even now, he still couldn’t understand how it had happened.","The flying ship was protected by numerous defensive treasures.","Several layers of formations.","Multiple Great Ascension Realm experts.","Yet Yu Feiyan had appeared behind him as though none of it existed.","The situation was absurd.","However, Yu Wenzhao forced himself to remain calm.","He wasn’t completely panicked yet.","So what if she had managed to infiltrate?","Now she was trapped in the center of his forces.","From another perspective, wasn’t this simply delivering herself into his hands?","The more Yu Wenzhao thought about it, the calmer he became.","Even then, he tried to break free.","However, no matter how hard he struggled, he couldn’t escape her grip.","His Soul Formation Realm cultivation erupted.","Boom!","Qi surged through his body.","Yet Yu Feiyan’s hand didn’t move even slightly.","It felt as though an entire mountain was pressing down upon him.","His face changed completely.","A defensive artifact activated automatically.","Golden light erupted around him.","Nothing happened.","Another artifact activated.","Then another.","Then another.","One treasure after another attempted to protect him.","Yet none of them managed to make Yu Feiyan even twitch.","Yu Feiyan continued holding him effortlessly, as though she hadn’t even noticed.","Confusion appeared in Yu Wenzhao’s eyes.","How?","Just how strong was she?","However, he quickly suppressed those thoughts.","There was still no need to panic.","His guards were already moving.","Several Great Ascension Realm experts charged forward simultaneously.","\"Release His Highness!\"","\"How dare you!\"","\"Die!\"","The attacks arrived instantly, yet Yu Feiyan didn’t even look at them.","With one hand holding Yu Wenzhao by the collar, she casually waved the other.","Boom!","The nearest Great Ascension Realm expert was sent flying.","Before he could even scream, he crashed through multiple sections of the Flying Ship.","Another expert arrived.","Boom!","He was sent tumbling through the air like a broken rag doll.","A third attacked.","Then a fourth.","Then a fifth.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","One after another, they were effortlessly swatted away.","The entire scene looked absurd.","These weren’t ordinary cultivators.","These were Great Ascension Realm experts, existences capable of ruling top cities.","Yet before Yu Feiyan, they looked no different from ants.","Yu Wenzhao’s eyes widened further with every passing second.","Yu Feiyan dealt with his strongest experts below the Immortal Realm with only one hand.","It was simply too absurd.","Yu Wenzhao stared at her.","Then his gaze slowly changed.","No!","This wasn’t right.","This wasn’t the Yu Feiyan he knew.","The Ninth Princess had always been timid, cowardly, and weak.","Even if she had hidden some strength, there should have been limits.","Perhaps if she were at the Spirit Severing Realm, it might be understandable.","After all, Bai Zihan had also risen rapidly from his meager cultivation to stand among the younger generation’s strongest.","But this?","Great Ascension Realm?","A Great Ascension Realm cultivator capable of treating other Great Ascension Realm experts like children?","That was ridiculous.","That was impossible.","Unless, a terrifying thought surfaced within his mind.","His face paled.","His eyes locked onto Yu Feiyan.","\"Who are you?\"","His voice trembled slightly.","\"You are not the Ninth Princess I know.\"","Yu Feiyan blinked innocently.","Yu Wenzhao continued staring at her.","The more he looked, the stronger his conviction became.","His instincts were screaming.","Everything finally made sense.","The sudden change in personality.","The sudden confidence.","The ability to subdue Yu Qingya.","The impossible strength.","This wasn’t Yu Feiyan.","It couldn’t be.","His gaze became increasingly certain.","\"You are not her!\"","Yu Wenzhao growled.","\"Who are you?!\"","For the first time since the battle began, Yu Wenzhao felt that he had finally uncovered the truth.","The woman before him was an imposter.","And his instincts told him that possibility was far more likely than believing the timid Ninth Princess had somehow become this terrifying existence overnight.","Yu Wenzhao’s accusation was met with nothing more than a smile.","Qin Lingxiao looked down at him as though she were looking at an interesting child.","Far from being alarmed by having her identity questioned, she appeared completely unconcerned.","Yu Wenzhao was already in her hand.","What difference did exposure make now?","Could he escape?","Obviously not!","Thus, Qin Lingxiao merely smiled and said nothing.","Meanwhile, the commotion atop the Flying Ship did not go unnoticed.","Although the battle remained chaotic, the fluctuations erupting from the command ship were simply too obvious.","Boom!","Another Great Ascension Realm guard was sent flying.","Part of the Flying Ship exploded.","Formation barriers shattered.","The disturbance immediately attracted attention.","Many experts from Yu Wenzhao’s faction instinctively turned their heads.","\"What happened?\"","\"That direction...\"","\"Isn’t that His Highness’s Flying Ship?\"","Even the Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators fighting nearby couldn’t help glancing over.","Something was clearly wrong.","Then one of Yu Wenzhao’s guards finally reacted.","His face pale with panic, he immediately crushed a communication talisman.","The message spread throughout the battlefield.","\"The Third Prince has been captured!\"","\"The Ninth Princess has captured His Highness!\"","The message echoed through countless communication channels.","For a brief moment, the entire battlefield froze.","Even cultivators in the middle of combat nearly forgot to continue attacking.","Captured?","The Third Prince?","Everyone felt as though they had misheard.","How was that possible?","Yu Wenzhao was protected by numerous Great Ascension Realm experts along with defensive formations.","Even an Earth Immortal cultivator shouldn’t have been able to infiltrate it so easily.","Yet somehow, he had been captured?","The shock spread like a tsunami.","\"What?! Captured?!\"","\"Impossible!\"","\"How did she get there?\"","The reactions were immediate.","Confusion, disbelief and shock.","No one understood what had happened.","Even the Immortal Ascension Realm experts fighting in the sky became distracted.","Far above, the Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal frowned.","The Crimson Thunder Palace’s Earth Immortal looked toward the Flying Ship.","Even Su Binglan’s eyes flickered slightly.","On the battlefield below, the Frost Lily Pavilion disciples and Yu Feiyan’s forces erupted.","\"The Third Prince has been captured!\"","\"Hahaha! Victory is ours!\"","The morale of Yu Feiyan and Yu Qingya’s alliance exploded.","Every cultivator felt as though they had been injected with endless energy.","Their battle intent soared as their attacks became fiercer.","Their momentum became unstoppable.","Originally, they had been gradually pushed back.","Now, they charged forward instead.","The battlefield instantly reversed."]},{"number":639,"title":"Chapter 639: Yu Wenzhao Captured!","paragraphs":["The cheers from Yu Feiyan’s side continued spreading across the battlefield.","Many on Yu Wenzhao’s side still refused to believe it.","How could such a thing happen?","Surely there had been some mistake.","However, their doubts did not last long.","Whoosh!","A figure suddenly emerged from the shattered Flying Ship.","It was Yu Feiyan, and in her hand was Yu Wenzhao.","The Third Prince was being dragged through the air by his collar.","His robes were disheveled and his expression ugly.","No matter how much humiliation burned within him, there was nothing he could do.","The moment the two appeared above the battlefield, countless eyes widened.","\"It’s really His Highness!\"","\"The Third Prince was actually captured!\"","\"How is this possible?! What are his guards doing?\"","This time, there was no room for doubt.","Everyone could see it with their own eyes.","The impossible had happened.","Yu Feiyan had truly captured Yu Wenzhao.","The morale of Yu Wenzhao’s forces immediately plummeted.","Far above, the Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal naturally noticed the development.","His expression changed instantly.","The mockery and confidence from earlier vanished completely.","\"Impossible!\"","His eyes locked onto Yu Wenzhao.","The Third Prince truly had been captured.","A chill immediately crept into his heart.","If Yu Wenzhao died, everything would be over.","The Heaven Suppression Sect had already committed itself to Yu Wenzhao’s faction.","If the Third Prince fell now, the sect would inevitably suffer tremendous losses afterward.","Without hesitation, he made a decision.","He looked toward the Crimson Thunder Palace’s Earth Immortal.","\"Keep Su Binglan occupied!\"","His aura erupted.","\"I’m going to rescue His Highness!\"","The Crimson Thunder Palace’s Earth Immortal frowned because he knew that Su Binglan was stronger than him.","Without another Earth Immortal, it would be difficult to fight against her.","However, after only a moment’s hesitation, he nodded.","\"Very well!\"","The Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal immediately prepared to break away from the battle.","Unfortunately, someone stood in his path.","A sword appeared before him.","The surrounding temperature plummeted once more.","Su Binglan stood silently between him and Yu Feiyan.","Her expression remained calm.","\"You wish to leave? Have you asked for my permission?\"","The Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal’s face darkened.","\"Move aside!\"","His aura exploded violently.","However, Su Binglan’s sword intent only grew sharper.","\"Don’t be in such a hurry. If you want to leave, you have to go through me!\"","Her icy gaze fell upon him.","The Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal gritted his teeth.","A terrifying pressure erupted from his body, yet Su Binglan did not retreat even half a step.","Although she was at a disadvantage against two opponents, with Yu Wenzhao captured, she didn’t think this fight would last much longer.","At that moment, Yu Feiyan’s voice suddenly echoed throughout the battlefield.","\"Everyone stop!\"","Countless cultivators turned toward her.","Yu Feiyan smiled faintly then she casually lifted Yu Wenzhao higher.","The Third Prince’s expression immediately darkened.","A terrifying force restrained him completely.","No matter how much he struggled, he couldn’t break free.","Yu Feiyan looked toward the Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal.","Then toward the Crimson Thunder Palace’s Earth Immortal.","Then toward the countless cultivators below.","Her smile widened slightly.","\"I believe everyone should calm down.\"","The battlefield gradually fell silent.","Even the ongoing clashes began slowing because everyone understood what was happening.","Yu Feiyan lightly patted Yu Wenzhao’s shoulder.","The gesture nearly made him cough blood from humiliation.","Then she spoke casually.","\"If anyone takes another step...\"","Her tone remained relaxed.","Yet the meaning behind her words caused countless hearts to tremble.","\"I’ll kill him!\"","Silence!","The Heaven Suppression Sect’s Earth Immortal froze.","The Crimson Thunder Palace’s Earth Immortal’s expression changed.","Yu Wenzhao was already completely within her control.","If she truly wished to kill him, no one present could stop her in time.","Yu Feiyan smiled.","Meanwhile, Yu Wenzhao’s face had become ashen.","For the first time since the battle began, he truly understood the severity of his situation.","Before, he had believed that rescue was inevitable.","That his guards would save him.","That the Earth Immortals would save him.","That his army would save him.","But now, reality was staring him directly in the face.","His life was no longer in his own hands.","One thought from Yu Feiyan.","One movement of her fingers.","And everything could end.","The battlefield remained deathly silent.","The moment Yu Wenzhao was captured, the battle had fundamentally changed.","And if he died here today, this war for the throne might very well end alongside him.","The Third Prince’s face had become increasingly ugly.","Humiliation.","Anger.","Frustration.","All of it churned within his heart.","Never in his life had he imagined that he would one day be held up like a hostage before an entire battlefield.","Yet despite his situation, Yu Wenzhao did not give up.","He continued struggling.","Boom!","His cultivation erupted once more.","Qi surged violently through his meridians.","Unfortunately, it was of no use at all.","Yu Feiyan’s grip remained completely unmoving.","No matter how hard he struggled, he couldn’t escape.","However, Yu Wenzhao was not someone who would surrender easily.","His gaze swept across the battlefield.","He could already see the hesitation spreading through his army.","Many cultivators had stopped fighting.","The morale of his army that had once filled the battlefield was rapidly declining.","The moment Yu Wenzhao saw this, alarm bells immediately rang within his heart.","No!","This could not continue.","If the army surrendered now, everything would be over.","Years of preparation.","Years of planning.","Years of sacrifices.","All of it would vanish.","His eyes immediately turned fierce.","\"Do not surrender!\"","His voice thundered across the battlefield.","The sudden roar startled countless cultivators.","Even Yu Feiyan glanced at him.","Yu Wenzhao ignored her.","His gaze remained fixed on his army.","\"Continue fighting!\"","His voice echoed through heaven and earth.","\"No one is allowed to stop!\"","Many of his subordinates hesitated.","\"Your Highness...\"","One of the elders didn’t know whether they should listen since Yu Wenzhao might be killed if they failed to do as Yu Feiyan said.","Yu Wenzhao immediately cut him off.","\"This is an order!\"","The authority within his voice returned.","The bearing of a prince once more appeared.","\"Do you think she dares kill me?\"","The question caused many people to pause.","Indeed!","Yu Wenzhao was not an ordinary cultivator.","He was an imperial prince.","One of the empire’s most important figures.","Killing him would have enormous consequences.","Yu Wenzhao quickly noticed the change in their expressions.","His confidence grew.","\"She won’t!\"","He laughed coldly.","\"She captured me because she wants leverage. If she kills me, she loses her greatest bargaining chip.\"","Many cultivators gradually calmed down.","The logic sounded reasonable.","He glanced toward the sky.","The two Earth Immortals.","Nearly fifteen Immortal Ascension Realm experts.","An army that still outnumbered the enemy.","The advantages hadn’t disappeared simply because he had been captured.","As long as they remained calm, they could still turn the situation around.","At least, that was what Yu Wenzhao desperately wanted everyone to believe, including himself.","Because beneath his confident appearance, a tiny seed of fear had already taken root.","The truth was that even he wasn’t completely certain.","Would Yu Feiyan really not kill him?","Logically speaking, she shouldn’t.","Rationally speaking, she wouldn’t.","Yet he also knew that this wasn’t the same Yu Feiyan he once knew or whether she is Yu Feiyan at all.","Still, he had no choice but to persist.","The throne was within reach.","He had come too far to abandon it now.","Qin Lingxiao merely looked at Yu Wenzhao with amusement.","The Third Prince was still trying to salvage the situation.","Still trying to convince both himself and his subordinates that everything remained within his grasp.","Qin Lingxiao did not care, though.","Whether the battle continued for another hour or another month made little difference to her.","It didn’t affect her plans at all.","Thus, while Yu Wenzhao continued issuing orders, Qin Lingxiao simply listened with a faint smile.","Almost as though she were watching an amusing performance.","Just as she was thinking this—","Swish!","A figure suddenly appeared beside her.","If others looked at her, no one would recognize her despite her formidable strength.","After all, she was not from the Desolate Heaven Empire.","She was one of the experts Qin Lingxiao had brought from her clan.","The woman appeared unusually serious, even somewhat anxious.","The moment Qin Lingxiao saw her expression, her brows rose slightly.","Very few things could make her look like this.","The woman immediately bowed.","\"Miss!\"","Qin Lingxiao nodded casually.","\"What is it?\"","Her tone remained relaxed.","Even now, she could not think of anything that would truly trouble her.","\"A problem has arisen.\"","Qin Lingxiao remained calm.","\"Oh?\"","The woman took a deep breath.","\"Long Haotian has been captured.\"","The smile on Qin Lingxiao’s face immediately froze.","For the first time since appearing on the battlefield, genuine surprise flashed through her eyes.","\"...What?\"","The subordinate quickly continued.","\"Not only him.\"","Her voice became increasingly grave.","\"The two elders accompanying him have also been captured.\""]},{"number":640,"title":"Chapter 640: Golden Immortals Revealed","paragraphs":["Qin Lingxiao was stunned when she heard those words.","Long Haotian being captured could be somewhat explained if he had been acting alone because he was only in the Immortal Ascension Realm.","There were a few forces she could think of that might be capable of subduing him despite all the artifacts he possessed.","But the two elders from the Long Clan?","They were in the Golden Immortal Realm just like her.","In this Desolate Heaven Empire, there shouldn’t be anyone capable of subduing them.","Qin Lingxiao stared at the subordinate.","\"Explain!\"","The subordinate didn’t dare waste any time and immediately began recounting what had transpired at the Heaven Sword Sect.","She spoke about how Long Haotian had gone there, attempted to marry Bai Xueqing and Chu Ziyan, and eventually ended up challenging Bai Zihan.","(Long Haotian lost?!)","When Qin Lingxiao heard that, she couldn’t help but be surprised.","Although she disliked Long Haotian and looked down on him, his talent and strength were something she had to acknowledge.","But that same Long Haotian lost against Bai Zihan?","\"Bai Zihan...\"","She had to admit that he was someone she couldn’t properly see through, possessing a talent that seemed blessed by the heavens themselves.","Since she was here, there was no way she hadn’t investigated Bai Zihan.","Yet the more she investigated, the more surprised she became.","Just three years ago, Bai Zihan had seemingly been stuck at the Core Formation Realm.","Yet within three years, he had managed to ascend all the way to the Great Ascension Realm.","Such talent was virtually unheard of, even in the Central Glorious Continent.","Moreover, with only Great Ascension Realm cultivation, he had been able to defeat Long Haotian, who was in the Immortal Ascension Realm and possessed numerous high-grade artifacts.","No matter how Qin Lingxiao looked at it, Bai Zihan was abnormal.","Yet before she could continue thinking, the subordinate spoke again.","\"Miss, there is more important information.\"","Qin Lingxiao looked up.","The subordinate hesitated briefly.","Then she lowered her voice.","\"The Bai Clan possesses Golden Immortal experts.\"","Qin Lingxiao froze.","\"...What?\"","\"The Bai Clan possesses two Golden Immortals.\"","Silence!","For the first time since arriving in the Desolate Heaven Empire, Qin Lingxiao genuinely lost her composure.","Her eyes widened.","\"How can that be?!\"","The subordinate lowered her head.","\"I personally confirmed it.\"","Qin Lingxiao’s thoughts became chaotic.","Everything she had investigated.","Everything she knew.","Everything the Central Glorious Continent knew.","All of it seemed completely wrong.","The Bai Clan should have possessed only Earth Immortals.","A force barely worth mentioning on the scale of the Central Glorious Continent.","Yet now?","Not only had they produced Bai Zihan.","Not only had they defeated Long Haotian.","They also possessed two Golden Immortal experts.","Although such a lineup was still insufficient to compete with the truly dominant powers of the Central Glorious Continent, they were no longer a force that could be underestimated.","Qin Lingxiao’s expression gradually darkened.","A bad feeling appeared in her heart.","\"Where are Long Haotian and his elders now?\"","Her voice became noticeably more serious.","If they had died after the battle, things would be much simpler.","Unfortunately, reality rarely followed one’s wishes.","The subordinate hesitated.","Then she answered.","\"Bai Zihan captured them.\"","Qin Lingxiao’s pupils contracted.","Captured?","Not killed.","That was even worse.","Because it meant Bai Zihan could potentially obtain information from them.","The subordinate hesitated once more.","This time, she appeared somewhat nervous.","\"Miss...\"","Qin Lingxiao immediately noticed.","\"What else?\"","The subordinate took a deep breath.","\"It appears that Bai Zihan already has a general idea that people from the Central Glorious Continent have infiltrated the Desolate Heaven Empire.\"","The moment those words left her mouth, Qin Lingxiao’s expression changed completely.","\"What?!\"","A genuine alarm appeared in her eyes.","That secret should never have been exposed.","Qin Lingxiao’s mind raced rapidly.","How much did he know?","Who told him?","Had the captured elders revealed something?","The more she thought about it, the more unsettled she became.","Meanwhile, hanging from Qin Lingxiao’s hand, Yu Wenzhao listened with a bewildered expression.","Much of the conversation exceeded his understanding, but a few points remained firmly in his mind.","Golden Immortals.","The Central Glorious Continent.","These matters were far beyond the scope of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","And one particular detail struck him like lightning.","The Bai Clan possessed two Golden Immortal cultivators.","Yu Wenzhao’s eyes widened.","His breathing momentarily stopped.","Golden Immortals!","Existences above Earth Immortals.","Existences that the entire Desolate Heaven Empire had never produced.","The strongest beings in the empire were merely Earth Immortals, yet the Bai Clan possessed two experts beyond that realm.","The revelation left him speechless.","If only...","If only he had obtained the Bai Clan’s support.","If only Bai Zihan had stood on his side.","Then everything would have been different.","With two Golden Immortals supporting him, what throne struggle would even remain?","What Heaven Suppression Sect?","What Crimson Thunder Palace?","What rival princes and princesses?","All opposition would have been crushed effortlessly.","The throne would already belong to him.","Moreover, he was now completely certain that this Yu Feiyan before him was an imposter from the Central Glorious Continent.","No wonder she had been able to infiltrate his Flying Ship so easily despite its numerous defensive mechanisms.","Qin Lingxiao was silent for a long time, completely ignoring the battle being fought around her.","She had thought she could take her time and watch these people destroy one another.","But it seemed she no longer had that luxury.","Qin Lingxiao remained silent for a long time.","The battlefield around her continued shaking from countless clashes.","Her thoughts were entirely elsewhere.","The Bai Clan.","Two Golden Immortals.","Long Haotian’s capture.","And most importantly, the possibility that Bai Zihan already knew about the infiltration from the Central Glorious Continent.","That last point was the most dangerous of all.","Qin Lingxiao slowly closed her eyes.","When she opened them again, the hesitation had disappeared.","She had made her decision.","This battle no longer mattered.","She needed to go to the Bai Clan immediately.","She needed to rescue Long Haotian and the two elders.","And she needed to ensure that no information leaked.","Beside her, Yu Wenzhao suddenly felt a chill run through his body.","His instincts screamed danger.","The look in Qin Lingxiao’s eyes had changed.","Gone was the amusement.","Gone was the casual indifference.","His face immediately paled.","\"N-No...\"","Qin Lingxiao’s hand moved.","She grabbed him by the throat.","The sudden pressure caused Yu Wenzhao’s eyes to widen.","He immediately struggled.","Fear filled his face.","Previously, he had convinced himself that Qin Lingxiao would not dare kill him.","After all, he was an imperial prince.","A candidate for the throne.","A valuable hostage.","But now?","After hearing everything?","After realizing that this woman was likely an existence from the Central Glorious Continent?","His confidence shattered completely.","For the first time, he truly believed he could die.","\"Wait!\"","Yu Wenzhao’s voice became frantic.","\"I can help you! I can become your ally!\"","\"I can give you all my resources! I can—\"","His words became increasingly desperate.","The proud Third Prince who had once looked down upon countless people now resembled a drowning man grasping at his final straw.","Unfortunately, Qin Lingxiao did not care.","Her gaze remained indifferent.","In her eyes, Yu Wenzhao’s value had already reached its limit.","The throne struggle no longer interested her.","His ambitions no longer interested her.","Right now, there was only one thing that mattered.","The Bai Clan!","Yu Wenzhao saw the indifference in her eyes.","His heart instantly sank.","\"No!\"","His voice became shrill.","\"Please! I don’t want to die! Spare me! I’ll do anything!\"","Unfortunately, his pleading accomplished nothing.","Qin Lingxiao tightened her grip.","Crack!","The sound echoed clearly across the battlefield.","Yu Wenzhao’s eyes widened.","His body suddenly went limp.","The desperate struggle ceased instantly.","Not only had his neck been broken, but his soul had also been annihilated.","There was no possibility of saving him.","The Third Prince of the Desolate Heaven Empire had died completely.","Qin Lingxiao casually released her hand.","The corpse fell from the sky.","Whoosh!","Hundreds of meters.","Thousands of eyes followed it downward.","Thud!","The body crashed into the battlefield below.","Silence!","For several moments, nobody reacted.","Their minds simply refused to process what they had just witnessed.","Then—","\"Your Highness!\"","A horrified scream erupted.","Several cultivators rushed toward the fallen body.","One elder immediately inspected him.","Moments later, his face turned deathly pale.","His hands trembled.","The surrounding cultivators stared at him anxiously.","\"Well?! How is His Highness?!\"","The elder slowly lifted his head.","His voice was filled with despair.","\"His Highness is dead.\"","Silence!","The elder’s voice trembled.","\"His soul has been extinguished. There is no way to save him.\"","The moment those words spread, the entire battlefield erupted.","\"What?!\"","\"Dead?!\"","\"His Highness is dead?!\"","Countless cultivators stared at the corpse.","Disbelief!","Shock!","Horror!","None of them had expected Qin Lingxiao to actually kill him.","He was a prince.","An imperial heir.","Yet she had killed him without the slightest hesitation.","Above the battlefield, furious roars erupted.","\"You monster!\"","\"How dare you!\"","\"You killed His Highness!\"","Numerous cultivators glared at Qin Lingxiao with bloodshot eyes.","However, their anger quickly gave way to confusion.","Then uncertainty.","Then helplessness.","Because what now?","Yu Wenzhao was dead.","The very person they had pledged loyalty to.","The man they had followed through countless battles.","The candidate they hoped would become Emperor.","He was completely gone.","Even if they continued fighting—","For what?","Moreover, what benefit would they gain?","Nothing!","The army’s morale, which had already been wavering, completely collapsed.","Many cultivators exchanged uncertain glances.","Above all, Qin Lingxiao merely glanced toward the distant horizon.","Her thoughts were already elsewhere.","\"We need to go to the Bai Clan!\""]},{"number":641,"title":"Chapter 641: True God","paragraphs":["Deep within one of the Bai clan’s heavily guarded underground chambers, there were three new prisoners.","Long Haotian and the two Golden Immortal elders of the Long Clan.","Their expressions were ugly.","Earth-grade artifact shackles bound their wrists, ankles, and even their necks.","The artifacts continuously suppressed the circulation of Qi within their bodies.","However, Bai Zihan knew better than anyone that such measures alone were far from sufficient.","These were Golden Immortal Cultivators.","A moment of carelessness could lead to disaster.","Although the Bai Clan also has Bai Ren and Bai Chu, Bai Zihan didn’t want to take any chances.","Thus, after bringing them back to the Bai Clan, Bai Zihan had personally sealed their meridians.","Bai Zihan instructed the guards to also seal their meridians every hour.","Only then did Bai Zihan feel somewhat reassured.","Inside the chamber, Bai Zihan sat calmly across from Long Haotian.","His fingers lightly tapped the armrest of his chair.","Tap! Tap!","The rhythmic sound echoed through the room.","Long Haotian’s expression darkened.","He naturally understood why he had been brought here.","Interrogation!","Unfortunately for Bai Zihan, Long Haotian had already made up his mind.","As long as he refused to answer, there was nothing Bai Zihan could do.","The Heavenly Vow remained hanging above his head. If he lied, Heavenly Tribulation would descend immediately.","But he also couldn’t afford to tell his clan’s secret mission to Bai Zihan as who knows what kind of consequence he would need to face.","Thus, silence was his safest choice.","Bai Zihan looked at him.","\"Let’s start with something simple.\"","Long Haotian remained silent.","Bai Zihan wasn’t surprised.","\"Why did the Long Clan come to the Desolate Heaven Empire?\"","Silence!","\"What are you looking for?\"","Silence!","Long Haotian simply closed his eyes.","His expression practically screamed that he would not answer anything.","Bai Zihan narrowed his eyes slightly.","Truthfully, there was something that had already been bothering him for quite some time.","The Heavenly Vow!","By all logic, Long Haotian should have already suffered divine punishment.","After all, he had clearly violated parts of the vow.","Yet until now...","Nothing.","No punishment whatsoever.","The heavens remained completely silent.","Bai Zihan couldn’t help feeling annoyed.","When he had broken the Heavenly Vow, Heaven had immediately tried to strike him dead.","Now Long Haotian violated it and somehow nothing happened.","The more Bai Zihan thought about it, the more irritated he became.","\"So the heavens are deliberately targeting me?\"","He muttered.","He thought that previously because he survived against heavenly Tribulation, that’s why Heaven tribulation deliberately worked against him.","Or it might even be because of his villain identity that Heaven didn’t want to assist him with his goal.","Anyways, it seems like threatening Long Haotian with the heavenly vow wouldn’t work.","Bai Zihan stared at Long Haotian.","Several seconds passed.","Then Bai Zihan slowly stood up and began walking toward Long Haotian.","\"Answer me while I am being nice, otherwise you might face fate worse than heavenly Tribulation!\"","Long Haotian suddenly felt a bad premonition.","A moment later—","\"AAAAAAAHHHHHHHHH!\"","A miserable scream echoed throughout the chamber.","The two elders jumped from the chamber next door as they heard their young master’s scream which was similar to that of a pig.","Long Haotian’s body convulsed violently.","His face twisted beyond recognition.","Every muscle in his body trembled uncontrollably.","Bai Zihan has basically mastered the art of torture. Targeting body organs which could generate the most pain while leaving not much injury.","Torture is all about trying to keep the culprit alive while making them suffer as much as possible.","\"Question one. Why did you come here?\"","Long Haotian gritted his teeth.","\"I won’t—\"","\"AAAAAAAHHHHHHHHH!\"","Another scream erupted.","This one was even louder than before.","Long Haotian’s entire body was shaking.","Tears had already begun forming in his eyes.","Bai Zihan nodded thoughtfully.","\"Still refusing?\"","Several more seconds passed.","Then—","\"AAAAARRRRRGGGGGHHHHHHH!\"","The chamber shook from the scream.","Long Haotian nearly collapsed.","Bai Zihan looked somewhat disappointed.","\"Your endurance isn’t very impressive.\"","Long Haotian’s face twitched.","Endurance?","What endurance?!","The pain Bai Zihan inflicted seemed to target every nerve, every meridian, and every corner of his soul simultaneously.","It was pure torture.","The kind of torture that made death seem merciful.","Bai Zihan sighed.","\"I fear that you might die before you give me the answer I want.\"","Long Haotian’s eyes immediately widened.","What kind of language was this?","Can’t you just stop if you think you are going to kill me?","Bai Zihan slowly raised his hand again.","The moment Long Haotian saw it, his expression changed dramatically.","\"WAIT!\"","Bai Zihan paused.","Long Haotian’s breathing became rapid.","His earlier confidence had completely disappeared.","His pride had vanished.","His stubbornness had vanished.","Everything had vanished.","All that remained was panic.","\"I’ll talk!\"","The words came out almost instantly.","Bai Zihan blinked as he looked at Long Haotian.","\"That was fast.\"","Long Haotian nearly coughed blood.","Fast?","It had only taken a few moments for Bai Zihan to completely destroy his resolve.","At this point, Heavenly Tribulation suddenly seemed far less terrifying than whatever Bai Zihan was doing to him.","Bai Zihan smiled pleasantly and returned to his seat.","\"Excellent!\"","He crossed his legs leisurely.","\"Now,\"","His eyes narrowed.","\"Let’s start from the beginning.\"","***","The reason Long Haotian had come to the Desolate Heaven Empire was actually very simple.","He was searching for a legacy.","However, it was not an ordinary legacy.","Rather, it was a legacy rumored to belong to a True God.","As for what realm a True God actually represented, no one knew.","The title had appeared only a handful of times throughout countless years of recorded history.","Even among the oldest forces of the Central Glorious Continent, information regarding True Gods was scarce.","Most regarded it as little more than a myth.","After all, even Immortal Emperors had long vanished from the world.","Although traces of their existence could still be found throughout history, no living cultivator had ever witnessed one.","Yet the legends surrounding True Gods were even more mysterious.","All believed that a True God stood above the Immortal Emperor Realm.","Others believed it was merely another title for an Immortal Emperor.","There were even those who claimed that True Gods did not belong to the cultivation system at all.","Regardless of the truth, one fact remained universally accepted.","If True Gods truly existed, they were beings far beyond ordinary understanding.","Existences capable of living for millions of years without exhausting their lifespan.","Existences capable of overlooking countless eras while empires rose and fell beneath them.","Existences whose power could not be measured by their current standards.","Throughout all recorded history, only a single individual was suspected of reaching such a stage.","A figure whose existence bordered between history and legend.","Over countless generations, many supreme powers attempted to uncover the truth.","Unfortunately, none succeeded.","Gradually, it has been forgotten by the time.","The legend of the True God gradually faded into obscurity.","Even among the supreme powers of the Central Glorious Continent, very few still took the story seriously.","At least, that had been the case until several thousand years ago.","An ancient ruin suddenly emerged.","Its appearance shook the entire Central Glorious Continent.","The ruins contained treasures beyond imagination.","Heaven-defying artifacts.","Rare resources that had vanished from the world long ago.","Even Golden Immortals and Supreme Immortals were driven mad by the discoveries.","The moment news spread, countless factions descended upon the ruins.","What followed was an exploration and war that lasted for a long period of time inside the ruin.","Yet despite all the bloodshed, the greatest treasure hidden within the ruins was not a cultivation technique or an artifact.","It was a map!","A seemingly ordinary map.","However, everyone could tell that whatever the map was pointing to, the treasure within should be even greater than what was found in the ruins.","Many believe that it must be the legacy very likely belonging to the legendary True God.","After all, the treasure within the ruins already was beyond imagination, so the treasure that the Map continued must be higher.","Of course, if someone had managed to obtain the complete map, they might have been able to locate the legacy directly.","Unfortunately, reality rarely unfolded so smoothly.","The moment the map appeared, the entire Central Glorious Continent descended into chaos.","Every major faction wanted it.","Every supreme power believed they were destined to obtain the inheritance.","And thus, another war erupted.","This conflict was even more intense than the battle over the ruins themselves.","Golden Immortals fell.","Supreme Immortals severely injured.","Ancient clans and immortal sects shed rivers of blood.","Everyone fought desperately for ownership of the map.","In the end, no single faction succeeded.","Instead, during the final struggle, the map was torn apart.","The complete map was divided into multiple fragments.","Different pieces fell into the hands of different powers.","Although everyone possessed only a portion of the treasure, no one was willing to hand theirs over.","Thus, the complete map disappeared from the world.","For countless years afterward, the various factions secretly studied their respective fragments.","Most discovered very little.","After all, a single fragment could not reveal the whole picture.","However, the supreme powers of the Central Glorious Continent were not simple.","Through countless deductions, ancient divination methods, and comparisons with historical records, some gradually managed to uncover clues.","Although no one could determine the exact location of the legacy, they were able to identify a general region.","And that discovery shocked everyone.","The location pointed toward the Eastern Continent.","More specifically, somewhere within the vicinity of the Desolate Heaven Empire."]},{"number":642,"title":"Chapter 642: True God!","paragraphs":["Because the Map had been torn into many pieces, determining the specific location was almost impossible.","As for setting aside their differences and working together?","That was even more impossible.","They had previously cooperated only to deal with the Demonic Cultivator leader because of his extraordinary strength.","But after that, they immediately returned to fighting one another.","Of course, there were others who attempted to cooperate by exchanging their pieces of the Map.","However, many were deceived with false maps, while others discovered that the information they obtained was incomplete or insignificant.","The discovery that the Map pointed toward the Eastern Continent and the Desolate Heaven Empire had only recently become known to the Long Clan.","On the other hand, some clans might have learned of it much earlier.","The Qin Clan, for example, definitely knew and had already sent their people.","This was the reason why Long Haotian and Qin Lingxiao had tried to keep a low profile and avoid attracting unnecessary attention.","\"Oh, a True God’s legacy?\"","The information Long Haotian had provided was not entirely surprising to Bai Zihan.","He knew that these top forces from the Central Glorious Continent would not come here without reason.","Either it was a powerful legacy or some priceless resource such as an exceptionally rich spirit vein.","Only such things could attract the attention of the top powers of the Central Glorious Continent.","Now he had his answer.","A True God’s legacy!","Bai Zihan leaned back in his chair, his expression calm as he quietly processed everything Long Haotian had told him.","He carefully turned the concept over in his mind.","True God!","He honestly wasn’t sure what to make of the title itself.","Was it a cultivation realm beyond the Immortal Emperor Realm?","Or was it simply what people called someone whose strength had reached a level beyond ordinary comprehension?","Perhaps it truly was the realm above the Immortal Emperor.","Bai Zihan didn’t particularly care about the answer right now.","Realm or title, it made little practical difference.","What mattered was that it was definitely something capable of making someone the most powerful person in the world.","Bai Zihan’s thoughts continued to churn.","Numerous questions naturally followed.","How many fragments of the Map were currently within the Desolate Heaven Empire?","More importantly, did anyone already possess a more precise location, or were they all still operating based on a general region?","The answer to the latter was probably easy to guess.","Since no one had shown any signs of obtaining the legacy, it was safe to assume that nobody possessed its exact location.","Or perhaps the torn Map simply wasn’t capable of pinpointing it.","Then how was he supposed to find it?","He didn’t even possess a fragment of the Map.","In fact, he couldn’t be entirely certain that Long Haotian was telling the truth, although it was highly likely.","Still, if he had to search the entire Desolate Heaven Empire blindly, then even if he mobilized every force within the empire, he might not be able to locate it.","Just then—","\"True God’s legacy?\"","A familiar voice sounded within his mind.","\"That is definitely interesting.\"","Bai Zihan’s entire body stiffened for a brief moment.","Then—","\"Feilian!\"","The word escaped his mouth far louder than intended.","His voice echoed throughout the chamber.","Long Haotian flinched violently, his already frayed nerves snapping to full alert before immediately relaxing again as his body reminded him that moving was painful.","Bai Zihan cleared his throat, forced his expression back into composure, and briefly glanced toward Long Haotian.","The Long Clan’s young master was far too exhausted and broken to care about what had just happened.","He remained slumped against the wall with the defeated posture of a man whose dignity had been thoroughly dismantled over the past several hours.","Well, even if he noticed, so what?","Bai Zihan turned his attention inward.","His voice became quiet, contained entirely within his consciousness.","(Feilian. Have you recovered?)","A brief silence followed.","The kind of silence Bai Zihan had was not sure he would ever break again.","For months, he had spoken into that silence and received no response.","Day after day.","Week after week.","He had known she was still there.","He could faintly sense her presence lingering within the Soul-Confining Artifact like a dying ember refusing to extinguish completely.","But knowing she was alive and hearing nothing from her were two entirely different things.","As the weeks stretched into months, the guilt within his heart only grew heavier.","If not for his stubbornness and refusal to listen, she might never have ended up in such a state.","(Feilian?)","He called again, this time more carefully.","His voice carried a trace of guilt and softness that he rarely showed.","A familiar laugh echoed within his consciousness.","It was faint and gentle.","Yet to Bai Zihan, it sounded clearer than any voice in the world.","\"I am fine.\"","Feilian’s voice carried its usual calmness.","\"It seems you’ve caused quite a bit of trouble while I was asleep.\"","Bai Zihan’s expression relaxed slightly.","\"Feilian!\"","She was truly awake.","\"When did you recover?\"","Bai Zihan asked.","\"A few days ago.\"","Bai Zihan was stunned.","\"A few days? Then why didn’t you say anything?\"","Feilian sounded amused.","\"I had only recovered enough to regain consciousness. I was still weak.\"","Bai Zihan nodded in understanding.","The truth was that after awakening, Feilian had not immediately revealed herself because she wanted to observe Bai Zihan.","She wanted to understand everything she had missed.","And what she discovered left her increasingly astonished.","Bai Zihan had already reached the Great Ascension Realm.","Not only that, but he had become capable of defeating Immortal Realm cultivators.","As an Immortal Emperor, Feilian had witnessed countless prodigies throughout her life.","Yet Bai Zihan’s growth still exceeded everyone she had ever known.","The more she learned about what had happened during her absence, the more unbelievable it became.","It seemed that while she had been recovering, Bai Zihan had not wasted a single day.","If anything, his progress had become even more terrifying than before.","She had originally intended to remain silent for several more days.","However, the moment she heard mention of the True God’s legacy, she could no longer restrain her curiosity.","\"You truly surprised me. You have become much stronger.\"","A trace of satisfaction entered her voice.","Bai Zihan smiled slightly.","Then his expression became complicated.","After a moment of silence, he spoke.","\"I’m sorry!\"","Immortal Emperor Feilian became quiet.","Bai Zihan lowered his gaze.","\"If not for me, you wouldn’t have ended up like that.\"","The memory remained vivid in his mind.","If he had remained calm.","If he had listened.","If he had not allowed anger and emotion to control him.","Things might have unfolded very differently.","Feilian remained silent for several moments.","Then she sighed softly.","\"I told you before. I do not blame you.\"","Her voice was gentle.","However, it quickly became serious.","\"That said, you must remember this lesson.\"","Bai Zihan listened carefully.","Immortal Emperor Feilian continued.","\"This cultivation world is merciless. The moment emotions cloud your judgment, you become vulnerable.\"","Her tone gradually sharpened.","\"Many geniuses die not because they lack talent or strength.\"","\"They die because they allow emotion to dictate their actions. Once that happens, death is usually not far away.\"","Bai Zihan nodded slowly.","\"I understand!\"","This time, he genuinely engraved those words into his heart.","Only after hearing his response did Feilian sound satisfied.","\"Good!\"","A brief silence followed.","Then Bai Zihan suddenly remembered something.","His eyes brightened.","Without hesitation, he opened his storage ring.","Several jade bottles appeared in his hand.","The moment they emerged, a rich medicinal fragrance filled the chamber.","Inside were several Grade-7 and Grade-8 soul-nourishing pills.","Medicines specifically designed to strengthen souls and restore spiritual damage.","The moment Feilian sensed them, she froze.","\"...\"","Several seconds passed.","Then—","\"Where did you get those?\"","For perhaps the first time since awakening, genuine shock entered her voice.","Bai Zihan blinked.","\"I refined them.\"","Silence!","Within the Soul-Confining Artifact, Feilian stared at the pills in disbelief.","Grade-7 pills.","Grade-8 pills.","And not ordinary pills either.","Soul-nourishing pills were notoriously difficult to refine.","The ingredients alone were priceless.","The control required over both flame and Qi during refinement was extraordinary.","Even many high-ranking alchemists failed repeatedly when attempting such pills.","Yet Bai Zihan was calmly telling her that he had refined them himself.","Feilian had known Bai Zihan long enough to understand one thing.","He did not lie about matters like this.","If he said he refined them, then he truly had.","Which only made the situation even more absurd.","Bai Zihan wasn’t even an alchemist when she last saw him.","When exactly had he become a Grade-8 Alchemist?","Her mind was already in turmoil.","Even during her era, Grade-8 Alchemists possessed terrifying status.","Numerous major powers competed to recruit them.","Countless experts owed them favors.","Their influence often surpassed their actual cultivation.","As for Immortal Emperors?","They naturally stood above everyone.","But outside of Immortal Emperors, very few people would willingly offend a Grade-8 Alchemist.","Such individuals were simply too valuable.","Too well-connected.","Yet now...","A young man who had not even reached the Immortal Realm was casually telling her that he could refine Grade-8 pills.","The more she thought about it, the more ridiculous it sounded.","Even in her era—","Even among the greatest geniuses she had ever seen—","There had never been someone like Bai Zihan."]},{"number":643,"title":"Chapter 643: Dao Manifestation Realm!","paragraphs":["Feilian remained silent for a moment before one of the Grade-7 Soul-Nourishing Pills vanished from the jade bottle.","A moment later, it appeared within the Soul-Confining Artifact.","Without hesitation, Feilian consumed it.","Boom!","The medicinal energy immediately spread throughout her soul.","A warm sensation enveloped her entire being.","The effect was almost instantaneous.","The soul power that had been weakened and depleted for months rapidly recovered.","Streams of soul power flowed through her damaged soul, nourishing every corner that had previously been exhausted.","For a brief moment, Immortal Emperor Feilian felt as though a dry riverbed had finally received rainfall after a long drought.","Her aura visibly strengthened.","Even Bai Zihan could sense the change.","The previously faint presence within the Soul-Confining Artifact suddenly became much clearer.","\"Hm?\"","Bai Zihan’s eyes brightened.","\"Is it working well?\"","Immortal Emperor Feilian nodded.","\"It is very effective.\"","In truth, it was even more effective than she had imagined.","She had seen and taken various kinds of pills throughout her life, but she felt that Bai Zihan’s pills were even better than those she had taken when she was alive.","For a brief moment, Feilian found herself staring at the remaining pills.","A dangerous temptation appeared within her heart.","She wanted another one.","The effects were simply too good.","Unfortunately, she quickly suppressed the thought.","Although the pills could restore her soul, her current condition remained unstable.","Absorbing too much energy too quickly could easily become harmful instead.","Recovery required patience.","Thus, after consuming a single Grade-7 Soul-Nourishing Pill, Immortal Emperor Feilian resisted the temptation and stopped.","(There is no need to rush.)","She thought.","A brief silence followed.","Then Immortal Emperor Feilian spoke again.","\"Now,\"","Her tone became more serious.","\"Let’s return to the matter of what he said. Did he say that the True God’s legacy was in this Empire?\"","Bai Zihan nodded.","After hearing Long Haotian’s explanation, countless questions had already formed within his mind.","And if anyone in the world could answer them, it would undoubtedly be this Empress Feilian.","After all, she had once ruled the world as an Immortal Emperor for tens of thousands of years.","If a True God truly existed, surely she would know something.","Bai Zihan immediately asked,","\"Do you know what a True God is?\"","Within the Soul-Confining Artifact, Immortal Emperor Feilian became quiet.","\"No!\"","Bai Zihan blinked.","He had not expected that answer.","Bai Zihan frowned slightly.","Even Empress Feilian didn’t know?","\"However, while I do not know what a True God truly is, I do have some ideas.\"","Bai Zihan immediately became attentive.","Within the Soul-Confining Artifact, Empress Feilian’s voice gradually became more solemn.","\"Most cultivators believe that the Immortal Emperor Realm is the end of cultivation. That it is the absolute peak.\"","\"They are wrong.\"","Empress Feilian continued calmly.","\"The reason they think so is simple. Immortal Emperors are the strongest beings they have ever known.\"","\"Throughout countless years, no one has surpassed that realm. Naturally, people assume it is the final destination.\"","A faint sigh escaped her.","\"However, only those who have actually stepped into the Immortal Emperor Realm understand the truth.\"","\"The Immortal Emperor Realm is not the end. It is merely the beginning.\"","If word of such a statement spread throughout the world, countless cultivators would likely go mad.","Immortal Emperor!","A realm that existed only in legends.","Yet according to Feilian, it was merely the beginning.","\"The moment one enters the Immortal Emperor Realm, their perception undergoes a fundamental transformation.\"","\"You begin to perceive things that ordinary cultivators cannot. You begin to perceive the Laws of the universe itself.\"","\"Countless Laws exist throughout the universe. They form the very foundation of reality.\"","Bai Zihan listened carefully.","While many people might find this shocking and unbelievable, Bai Zihan was different.","As someone who possessed memories of countless cultivation novels from his previous life, how could he not be familiar with such concepts?","Of course, although he was not particularly surprised, Feilian’s words confirmed that this world also possessed Laws similar to those described in the cultivation novels he had once read.","\"At the peak of the Immortal Emperor Realm, one may begin to perceive these Laws.\"","Feilian paused briefly before continuing.","\"Only after completely mastering a Law can one take the next step.\"","\"The Dao Manifestation Realm!\"","A realm beyond the Immortal Emperor Realm.","A realm Bai Zihan had never heard mentioned before.","Immortal Emperor Feilian’s voice carried a trace of reverence.","\"At that stage, a cultivator no longer merely understands a Law. They become capable of manifesting it and controlling them at will.\"","\"They can directly utilize the Law as naturally as breathing. They can alter reality according to their will.\"","\"Mountains can become oceans.\"","\"Day can become night.\"","\"Life can become death.\"","\"Death can become life.\"","\"For many civilizations, such existences were already equivalent to gods.\"","A faint smile appeared in Feilian’s voice.","\"In fact, the True God that these people are referring to is likely a Dao Manifestation cultivator.\"","If such a realm truly existed, then calling its cultivators gods was hardly an exaggeration.","\"Unfortunately, nobody in my era ever reached the Dao Manifestation Realm. Therefore, I cannot say with certainty whether such a realm truly exists.\"","As someone who had stood at the peak of the Immortal Emperor Realm, her desire was naturally to ascend further.","However, despite tens of thousands of years of cultivation and despite her extraordinary talent, she had only managed to perceive fragments of the Laws.","Until the very end, she had never broken through.","These conclusions were the result of tens of thousands of years of research, exploration, and countless records recovered from ancient ruins.","Several moments passed before she spoke again.","\"Throughout all recorded history, there was only one individual who was believed to have reached the Dao Manifestation Realm.\"","\"A person whose existence blurred the line between history and legend. A person whose name still appears within the oldest records.\"","Bai Zihan unconsciously leaned forward.","\"Who?\"","Empress Feilian slowly answered.","\"Dao Sovereign Xuan Tianyu!\"","Bai Zihan tried to remember whether he had ever heard that name before.","However, no matter how much he searched his memories, nothing surfaced.","Then again, considering that the world viewed the Immortal Emperor Realm as the peak of cultivation, it was hardly surprising.","Otherwise, the forces from the Central Glorious Continent would not be calling Dao Manifestation cultivators as True Gods.","\"The so-called True God’s legacy...\"","Feilian’s voice became unusually firm.","\"It must be his legacy.\"","Although she could not be completely certain, throughout the endless history of this world, whenever the topic of someone surpassing the Immortal Emperor Realm arose, only one name ever appeared.","Dao Sovereign Xuan Tianyu!","Even during Feilian’s era, that name had already been nearly forgotten.","Very little information remained regarding him.","The only consistent descriptions portrayed him as an existence of unimaginable power, capable of bending the world itself according to his will.","As a peak Immortal Emperor, Feilian had once searched extensively for anything related to Dao Sovereign Xuan Tianyu.","After all, any clue regarding him might have become her key to breaking through into the next realm.","Unfortunately, despite all her efforts, she had gained almost nothing beyond scattered fragments of information.","Therefore, when Long Haotian mentioned the map and the possible existence of the legacy, she had been both surprised and excited.","Even if it was not Dao Sovereign Xuan Tianyu’s legacy, it could still belong to another Dao Manifestation Realm cultivator.","Thinking about that, Feilian could not help becoming excited.","Perhaps the thing she had failed to achieve in her previous life, she might finally be able to achieve in this one.","But of course, first she needs to know whether the map that Long Haotian mentioned was legit or they had been scammed.","Empress Feilian gradually calmed herself.","The excitement in her heart did not disappear, but she knew that excitement alone was meaningless.","The first thing they needed to determine was whether Long Haotian’s information was genuine.","After all, throughout history, countless false inheritances had appeared.","Even she couldn’t find out anything about the Dao Manifestation Realm, so how can these people get their hands on their legacy?","Thus, before becoming excited about a possible Dao Manifestation Realm legacy, they first needed to confirm whether the map actually existed and whether it was a map of Dao Manifestation realm legacy.","After thinking for a moment, Feilian spoke.","\"Ask him about the map.\"","Although just a piece of the map won’t be able to track down the location, she could check whether it belongs to Dao Manifestation Realm Cultivator.","Bai Zihan nodded.","His gaze immediately shifted toward Long Haotian.","The latter instinctively shivered.","\"Long Haotian.\"","Long Haotian immediately straightened.","\"What?\"","Bai Zihan leaned forward slightly.","\"The map.\"","Long Haotian’s expression froze.","\"The piece of the map your Long Clan possesses. Where is it?\"","The moment those words left Bai Zihan’s mouth, Long Haotian’s expression changed.","That was one of the most important secrets of the Long Clan.","Naturally, there was no way he could casually reveal it.","Unfortunately for him, Bai Zihan slowly raised a hand.","The familiar hand.","The same hand that had nearly made him wish for death not long ago.","Long Haotian’s pupils contracted violently.","A cold chill ran down his spine.","Bai Zihan smiled.","\"Think carefully before answering.\"","Long Haotian nearly cried.","A short while ago, Bai Zihan had suddenly become cheerful after speaking to whoever was inside his artifact.","Long Haotian had thought that perhaps the interrogation was finally over.","Perhaps Bai Zihan had forgotten about him.","Perhaps his suffering had ended.","Yet now?","The nightmare had returned.","Long Haotian stared at Bai Zihan.","Then at the raised hand.","Then back at Bai Zihan.","For a brief moment, a thought appeared in his mind.","(Is this guy suffering from some kind of mental illness?)","His moods changed too quickly.","One moment he was smiling happily by himself.","The next moment he was threatening torture again.","Long Haotian immediately buried the thought deep within his heart.","He wasn’t suicidal.","If Bai Zihan somehow learned what he was thinking, another round of torture would probably begin immediately.","Thus, Long Haotian obediently answered.","\"The map isn’t with me.\"","Bai Zihan narrowed his eyes.","\"Where is it?\"","Long Haotian swallowed.","\"It remains within the Long Clan Estate. My father ordered it to be guarded. Only a handful of core elders are permitted to view it.\""]},{"number":644,"title":"Chapter 644: More Clues","paragraphs":["After a few moments, Bai Zihan shook his head.","Trying to obtain the Long Clan’s map fragment was unrealistic.","Just to verify whether the Map was connected to a Dao Manifestation Realm cultivator, the price was too great.","Not to mention, at his current level, that was almost impossible.","Not worth it at all.","The actions of the various forces from the Central Glorious Continent had already provided sufficient proof.","A force like the Long Clan would not dispatch its young master and two Golden Immortal protectors unless they were fairly certain.","Likewise, the Qin Clan would not secretly infiltrate the Desolate Heaven Empire for no reason.","The fact that these forces had already begun moving was enough.","Whether it was truly the legacy of Dao Sovereign Xuan Tianyu or not hardly mattered.","At the very least, it was undoubtedly a treasure capable of shaking the entire cultivation world.","Thinking of this, Bai Zihan’s expression gradually became serious.","The arrival of the Central Glorious Continent was inevitable.","Right now, only a handful of forces who possessed map fragments knew about the treasure pointing toward the Desolate Heaven Empire.","But that situation would not last forever.","As those forces continued to make their moves, it would inevitably be noticed by others.","And when that happened, the Desolate Heaven Empire would no longer be peaceful.","A faint pressure settled over Bai Zihan’s heart.","He knew better than anyone how terrifying the Central Glorious Continent truly was.","The Bai Clan might dominate the Desolate Heaven Empire.","It might even dominate the surrounding regions.","But compared to the true overlords of the Central Glorious Continent?","The gap remained enormous.","Just capturing Long Haotian and his two protectors had already demonstrated that fact.","To achieve that victory, the Bai Clan had mobilized nearly all of its strongest experts.","Bai Ren.","Bai Chu.","And numerous elders.","If not for Long Haotian becoming a hostage and forcing the two Golden Immortal elders to restrain themselves, there was a very real possibility that both of them could have escaped.","Golden Immortals were simply too difficult to capture.","Yet those two elders were not even considered top-tier experts within the Long Clan.","As far as he knew, top forces also had Supreme Immortals among their ranks.","Just one of them should be enough to flatten the entire Desolate Heaven Empire.","If the Long Clan truly decided to mobilize its full strength...","The Bai Clan would not be able to stop them.","Not even close.","And the Long Clan was only one force among countless powerful factions in the Central Glorious Continent.","The more Bai Zihan thought about it, the clearer the situation became.","Even if he united every cultivator within the Desolate Heaven Empire...","Even if he somehow convinced neighboring empires and sects to cooperate...","It still might not be enough.","The difference in power was simply too great.","\"Forget it. Those map fragments are meaningless unless enough of them are pieced together.\"","Even if he somehow obtained the Long Clan’s fragment, it would not change much.","At best, it would merely confirm some of Long Haotian’s words.","At worst, it would provoke a terrifying force from the Central Glorious Continent.","Within the prison cell, Long Haotian looked at Bai Zihan with a trace of regret.","In truth, a part of him had actually hoped Bai Zihan would become arrogant and think he could barge into the Long Clan.","If Bai Zihan truly decided to head toward the Long Clan to seize the map fragment...","He would be delivering himself right into the Long Clan’s hands.","Unfortunately, Bai Zihan was clearly not that stupid.","Seeing Bai Zihan stand up and prepare to leave, Long Haotian suddenly became anxious.","\"Wait! Bai Zihan! Where are you going?! Release me!\"","His voice echoed through the chamber.","Now that he had already revealed everything he knew, Long Haotian naturally assumed Bai Zihan would let him go.","After all, from his perspective, Bai Zihan had already obtained the information he wanted.","Bai Zihan stopped at the entrance and slowly turned around.","A strange expression appeared on his face.","\"Release you?\"","He blinked.","\"Did I ever say I was going to release you?\"","Long Haotian froze.","The smile on Bai Zihan’s face widened slightly.","Long Haotian’s expression immediately darkened.","No!","Bai Zihan had never once promised such a thing.","\"B-But I already answered your questions!\"","Long Haotian protested.","\"And I appreciate your cooperation.\"","Bai Zihan nodded seriously.","Long Haotian nearly coughed blood.","Cooperation?","If not for the torture and the fear of being struck by Heavenly Thunder, would he have revealed those things?","Bai Zihan looked at Long Haotian as though he were looking at an idiot.","Release him?","Impossible!","The moment Long Haotian stepped outside the Bai Clan, his first action would undoubtedly be contacting the Long Clan.","Not only would Golden Immortals arrive.","Supreme Immortals might descend as well.","Bai Zihan could not afford such a risk.","\"Bai Zihan. You should think carefully. The Long Clan is not someone you can afford to offend.\"","His voice became increasingly threatening.","\"If you release me now, I can still pretend none of this happened. I can still forgive you.\"","Bai Zihan stared at him silently.","Then he laughed.","It was the laugh of someone who found the statement absurd.","Forgive him?","(As if!)","If Long Haotian could truly forgive him after all the torture he had gone through, Bai Zihan would admit that Long Haotian possessed a Buddha’s heart.","Did Long Haotian truly think he was a three-year-old child?","The moment he was released, he would definitely inform his clan, and revenge would be inevitable.","Even if Long Haotian swore otherwise, Bai Zihan would never believe him.","Perhaps a Heavenly Vow could have provided some assurance.","Unfortunately, Bai Zihan’s eyes narrowed slightly.","The Heavens seemed determined to oppose him, and even when others broke Heavenly Vows, nothing happened.","He could not trust Heavenly Vows at all.","\"Nice try! But please say something more believable next time.\"","Bai Zihan waved dismissively and turned around.","Long Haotian’s eyes widened.","\"BAI ZIHAN!\"","Long Haotian roared.","\"YOU CAN’T KEEP ME HERE FOREVER! THE LONG CLAN WILL FIND ME!\"","\"YOU’RE FINISHED!\"","His furious voice echoed throughout the underground prison.","Bai Zihan did not even bother looking back.","\"Now that’s more believable.\"","His footsteps gradually faded into the distance.","The heavy prison door closed behind him.","Within the Soul-Confining Artifact, Feilian spoke once more.","\"What are you planning to do next?\"","Bai Zihan raised an eyebrow.","Empress Feilian’s tone became more serious.","\"You already made your move against Long Haotian. You should have prepared yourself to face the consequences.\"","Bai Zihan remained silent.","Naturally, he understood what she meant.","She also agreed to keeping Long Haotian imprisoned. Releasing him is not an option.","However, imprisoning him does not mean Bai Zihan can avoid confrontation with the Long Clan.","The disappearance of their young master and two Golden Immortal elders would not go unnoticed forever.","Perhaps weeks or if they are lucky, a few months.","Sooner or later, the Long Clan will eventually realize that something is wrong.","And what if there are other members of the Long Clan who are also in the Desolate Heaven Empire.","If that is the case, it will not take them long to discover what happened. Only days!","And since Bai Zihan captured Long Haotian publicly before every Heaven Sword Sect, the Long Clan will know who the culprit is without needing much investigation.","Bai Zihan also knew that.","He had already considered that possibility.","The moment he decided to capture Long Haotian, he had accepted that the matter would eventually reach the Long Clan.","The only uncertainty was when.","\"So? How do you intend to deal with them?\"","Bai Zihan’s footsteps did not stop.","\"Gather more clues about this True God’s legacy.\"","Bai Zihan’s eyes gradually sharpened.","The Long Clan is a future problem.","The True God’s legacy is the opportunity in front of me.\"","The current situation was obvious.","The Bai Clan was too weak.","The Desolate Heaven Empire was too weak.","Compared to the Central Glorious Continent, they were insignificant.","His own growth speed was already monstrous.","With the System’s assistance, he had achieved things that countless cultivators could never accomplish in their entire lives.","Even his clan has become very strong, perhaps unrivaled in the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Yet even then... catching up to the Long Clan within a few weeks was unrealistic.","His and his clan’s growth was already highest.","No matter how absurd the System was, some things simply required time.","The Long Clan had accumulated power for countless generations.","They possessed Golden Immortals.","Supreme Immortals.","Resources beyond imagination.","The gap was simply too large.","Thus, there was only one option left.","The True God’s legacy.","A faint light flashed within Bai Zihan’s eyes.","If he could obtain it before the forces of the Central Glorious Continent, everything would change.","If he could obtain the legacy of Dao Realm Cultivator, then there should be nothing in this world that he should fear!"]},{"number":645,"title":"Chapter 645: The Princess’s Inquiry","paragraphs":["Bai Zihan fell into deep thought as he walked through the underground corridors.","The prison door had already closed behind him.","Long Haotian’s furious shouting gradually faded into the distance.","Yet Bai Zihan paid it no attention.","His mind was occupied by a far more important matter.","The True God’s legacy!","Or perhaps more accurately—","The legacy of a Dao Manifestation Realm cultivator.","If Feilian’s speculation was correct, then only by obtaining that inheritance could their fate change.","Not only would it solve the immediate crisis posed by the Central Glorious Continent, but it might also grant him the qualifications to stand above the countless supreme powers of the Central Glorious Continent.","The problem was obvious.","How was he supposed to find it?","Even those people with the map couldn’t find it, and his only lead was that it was somewhere within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Bai Zihan rubbed his forehead.","Without the map, locating the legacy was practically impossible.","There were only two methods available to him.","The first was to find others who knew more than Long Haotian.","As this thought surfaced, several figures immediately appeared in Bai Zihan’s mind.","They were the people from the Central Glorious Continent who had recently entered the Desolate Heaven Empire, just like Long Haotian.","Unfortunately, Bai Zihan quickly shook his head.","Even if he captured them, the possibility of obtaining useful information seemed rather low.","From everything he had observed so far, these people appeared just as clueless as Long Haotian.","They were constantly moving throughout the empire.","Searching here and investigating there without any clear direction.","If they truly possessed accurate information, they would have already headed straight toward the inheritance site.","Instead, they seemed to be blindly searching.","Which meant the first option was unreliable.","That left only the second method.","A massive search.","A search conducted on a scale large enough to cover the entire Desolate Heaven Empire.","The more people involved, the greater the chance of discovering clues.","Bai Zihan’s eyes narrowed slightly.","And suddenly, a thought flashed through his mind.","The throne war!","More specifically, Qin Lingxiao.","Bai Zihan’s footsteps slowed.","A strange expression appeared on his face.","(Perhaps that is her objective as well?)","Previously, he had never fully understood Qin Lingxiao’s actions.","Why disguise herself as Yu Feiyan?","Why participate in the struggle for the imperial throne?","For someone from the Qin Clan, such things should have been meaningless.","Unless she needed authority.","Authority over the entire empire.","If Qin Lingxiao successfully became Emperor, she could mobilize countless officials, sects, clans, merchants, and cultivators.","She could command the resources of an entire nation.","More importantly, she could use all of them to search for clues related to the True God’s legacy.","The more Bai Zihan thought about it, the more reasonable it seemed.","After all, searching an empire the size of the Desolate Heaven Empire with only a handful of experts was hopeless.","But using hundreds of millions?","That was a different matter entirely.","Of course, this was merely speculation.","He had no proof.","Still...","The possibility certainly existed.","Bai Zihan’s eyes flickered thoughtfully.","Just as he stepped out of the Bai Clan’s prison—","\"Clan Leader Bai!\"","A voice suddenly rang out.","The voice carried obvious nervousness and urgency.","Bai Zihan immediately recognized it.","Yu Feiyan!","Or more accurately, Qin Lingxiao.","His brows rose slightly.","A moment later, several Bai Clan guards hurried over.","Their faces were pale.","\"Clan Leader! We apologize!\"","The leading guard lowered his head immediately.","\"We tried to stop her, but...\"","\"She forced her way through.\"","\"We were unable to stop her.\"","Bai Zihan looked past them.","Standing not far away was Qin Lingxiao.","Her breathing was slightly uneven.","Her expression was tense.","Far more tense than Bai Zihan had ever seen before.","The moment their eyes met, Qin Lingxiao immediately stepped forward.","\"Clan Leader Bai!\"","Her voice was unusually serious.","\"I need to speak with you.\"","Bai Zihan narrowed his eyes.","He knew why Qin Lingxiao was here.","It was likely because of Long Haotian.","Not because he thought she cared about him, but because she wanted to prevent information from being leaked.","Unfortunately for her, he already knew everything.","He immediately sent messages to Grand Elder Bai Chu and Bai Ren.","Bai Zihan waved toward the guards.","\"You may leave.\"","Bai Zihan ordered, knowing there was nothing they could do against someone like Qin Lingxiao.","Rather, they would only get in his way.","\"Yes, Clan Leader!\"","The guards quickly withdrew.","Even though they were worried about Bai Zihan’s safety, they wouldn’t dare delay his command.","Soon, only Bai Zihan and Qin Lingxiao remained.","Qin Lingxiao quickly composed herself.","The nervousness that had briefly appeared on her face vanished almost instantly.","By the time she reached Bai Zihan, she had already returned to the calm and elegant demeanor of the Ninth Princess.","She bowed slightly.","\"My apologies, Clan Leader Bai. I came without notice and even forced my way past your guards.\"","A faint smile appeared on her face.","\"I hope Clan Leader Bai will not take offense.\"","Bai Zihan smiled politely.","\"Princess Yu is being too courteous. If you came personally, then you must have had a reason.\"","\"I naturally do not mind.\"","Qin Lingxiao nodded inwardly.","As expected.","No matter the situation, Bai Zihan always remained calm and gave nothing away.","Well, that was simply what Qin Lingxiao believed because she was trying to read Bai Zihan’s expression.","But if Bai Xueqing were here, she would say that this demeanor alone already revealed many things.","Bai Zihan remaining calm despite Yu Feiyan forcefully breaking in meant that he was cautious of her and likely regarded her as a powerful opponent.","Otherwise, with the Bai Clan’s current strength, Bai Zihan would not take anyone seriously.","Even if it were the Emperor himself, he would likely throw him into the Bai Clan’s prison if he dared to force his way into the Bai Clan.","The fact that Bai Zihan did not do so meant that he knew he could not—or that the price would be too high.","But Qin Lingxiao knew none of this and simply believed that Bai Zihan was always like this.","Taking a slow breath, Qin Lingxiao finally arrived at the real reason for her visit.","\"There is indeed a reason.\"","A trace of hesitation appeared on her face as she spoke carefully.","\"I heard that recently, someone claiming to be a young master from the Central Glorious Continent entered the Desolate Heaven Empire.\"","Her eyes remained fixed on Bai Zihan.","Observing every tiny movement.","Every subtle reaction.","\"Furthermore, I heard Clan Leader Bai captured him.\"","Silence!","Qin Lingxiao stared at Bai Zihan.","Trying to read him.","Trying to determine how much he knew.","Trying to determine whether Long Haotian was still alive.","Unfortunately...","As always...","Bai Zihan’s expression revealed absolutely nothing.","His face remained calm and indifferent.","Like a tranquil lake without the slightest ripple.","After a brief pause, Bai Zihan nodded.","\"There was indeed such a person.\"","Qin Lingxiao’s pupils contracted slightly.","Bai Zihan continued calmly.","\"I captured someone called Long Haotian who dared to harass my fiancée and sister. Although whether that is his real name or merely an alias used to deceive others, I cannot say.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, Qin Lingxiao’s heart skipped a beat.","But judging by Bai Zihan’s words, it seemed he still didn’t know Long Haotian’s true identity.","A thousand thoughts flashed through her mind.","However, none of them appeared on her face.","Instead, she deliberately showed confusion.","\"Long Haotian?\"","She frowned slightly.","\"The name sounds unfamiliar.\"","Then her expression gradually changed.","A trace of concern appeared.","\"But if he was protected by such powerful guards, then his background must be extraordinary.\"","Bai Zihan nodded.","\"I assume so. He continued threatening me until the very end.\"","Qin Lingxiao almost laughed.","Of course he would threaten.","Back in the Central Glorious Continent, he wouldn’t even need to say anything.","Just his name alone would make others submit.","Still...","What she truly cared about was not Long Haotian himself.","It was something else.","Her gaze sharpened slightly.","\"Then...\"","She paused.","Choosing her words carefully.","\"Did Clan Leader Bai obtain any other information from him?\"","Her tone sounded casual.","Almost indifferent.","As though she were merely curious.","However, her eyes remained locked onto Bai Zihan.","Bai Zihan smiled faintly.","\"What kind of information does Princess Yu mean?\"","Qin Lingxiao’s heart tightened slightly.","Still not revealing anything.","This man truly was difficult to deal with.","She maintained her calm expression.","\"For example, why he came to the Desolate Heaven Empire?\"","Qin Lingxiao carefully observed Bai Zihan’s face.","If Long Haotian had remained silent...","Then everything would be simple.","She could leave immediately.","Perhaps even find a way to rescue that fool later.","But if Long Haotian had talked...","A dangerous light flashed through her eyes.","Only for an instant.","Yet within that instant, a trace of killing intent appeared.","It vanished almost immediately.","So quickly that even most Immortal Realm cultivators would have failed to notice it.","Unfortunately for her, Bai Zihan noticed.","Within the Soul-Confining Artifact, Feilian’s voice sounded tense.","(She wants to kill you!)","Bai Zihan’s eyes narrowed imperceptibly.","(I know.)","He replied inwardly.","Qin Lingxiao’s thoughts were racing.","That stupid Long Haotian revealing his face and identity at the Heaven Sword Sect had already been a foolish decision.","And now he had gotten himself captured?","If Long Haotian had revealed the truth...","Then the situation had become completely out of control.","The fewer people who knew about the legacy, the better.","Every additional person meant another competitor.","More importantly, every additional person increased the risk of the information spreading further.","If Bai Zihan knew...","Then she would have no choice but to kill him.","Not only him.","Everyone who knew.","The thought was ruthless.","Yet Qin Lingxiao was not going to hesitate!"]},{"number":646,"title":"Chapter 646: The Secret Worth Killing For","paragraphs":["If it had been before, Bai Zihan would have done everything possible to avoid provoking Qin Lingxiao.","After all, she has reached the Golden Immortal Realm.","She was a Heaven Chosen One.","An existence whose status and strength far exceeded anything the Desolate Heaven Empire could produce.","Such a person was not someone he could have handled.","Even if the entire Bai Clan joined forces, the outcome would have been uncertain.","But now things are different.","The Bai Clan and Bai Zihan were no longer the same as they had been months ago.","The Bai Clan have Golden Immortal now and the number of Immortal Realm cultivators are increasing day by day.","Bai Zihan’s cultivation had already stepped into the Great Ascension Realm.","His physique had been refined by Heavenly Tribulation as well.","Although he still could not defeat Qin Lingxiao, he was no longer so weak that she could casually kill him with a wave of her hand.","At the very least, she would not be able to kill him instantly.","Because of that, Bai Zihan no longer felt the same pressure he once did when facing someone like her.","Of course, that did not mean he underestimated her.","Qin Lingxiao was not Long Haotian.","Qin Lingxiao was a Heaven Chosen who undoubtedly possessed numerous trump cards.","Seeing that she dared come here alone, knowing that he has already captured two Golden Immortals showed her confidence.","As these thoughts flashed through his mind, Bai Zihan merely continued looking at her.","The silence stretched on.","A trace of anger rose within Qin Lingxiao’s heart.","This Bai Zihan truly knew how to frustrate people.","She had already hinted at her question several times.","Yet he still refused to reveal anything.","For a brief moment, the impulse to act directly surfaced within her mind.","Fortunately, she quickly suppressed it.","This was not the time to allow emotions to cloud her judgment.","Taking a slow breath, Qin Lingxiao calmed herself.","When she spoke again, she was once more the elegant Ninth Princess of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","\"Clan Leader Bai!\"","Her voice became softer.","\"I only ask because I am concerned for the Empire.\"","Qin Lingxiao continued.","\"Recently, I have learned a little about the Central Glorious Continent.\"","A trace of worry appeared on her face.","\"And I have also heard of the Long Clan. From what I understand, they are one of the great powers of the Central Glorious Continent.\"","\"If that Long Haotian truly comes from the Long Clan...\"","She paused briefly.","\"Which I believe he does, considering the strength of his protectors, then this could be viewed as a provocation against the Long Clan.\"","Qin Lingxiao sighed softly.","A worried expression appeared on her beautiful face.","\"Clan Leader Bai, have you considered the consequences?\"","\"The Desolate Heaven Empire cannot withstand the wrath of a force like the Long Clan.\"","\"If they discover that their young master has been captured and imprisoned here, the consequences could be disastrous for the Desolate Heaven Empire.\"","Everything she said sounded perfectly reasonable coming from the princess of the empire.","Yet beneath those words lay an entirely different purpose.","Qin Lingxiao had already realized that obtaining answers directly from Bai Zihan was almost impossible.","This man was simply too cautious.","Too difficult to read.","Since she could not determine whether Long Haotian had revealed the truth to him, she would have to question Long Haotian personally.","Only then could she know the extent of the damage.","Only then could she decide who needed to die.","Her eyes flickered slightly.","\"Perhaps...\"","She spoke carefully.","\"There may still be a way to resolve this matter peacefully.\"","Bai Zihan finally raised an eyebrow.","Qin Lingxiao immediately continued.","\"If Clan Leader Bai is willing, perhaps the Imperial Family can take custody of him. We can verify his identity and, if he truly is from the Long Clan, negotiate with them directly.\"","A faint smile appeared on her face.","\"That would also reduce the pressure on the Bai Clan. It is, after all, a matter that concerns the entire Empire.\"","On the surface, her proposal sounded reasonable, even considerate.","But both Bai Zihan and Feilian instantly understood her true objective.","She wanted Long Haotian.","Only then could she personally determine whether the secret of the True God’s legacy had been exposed.","A faint smile appeared on Bai Zihan’s face before he casually waved his hand.","\"Princess Yu worries too much.\"","Bai Zihan continued leisurely.","\"That person is nothing more than an impostor and a liar trying to establish dominance through fabricated stories.\"","\"What Long Clan from the Central Glorious Continent?\"","He shook his head.","\"He is clearly bluffing. With his strength, it would not be surprising if he were merely some wandering fraud pretending to possess a great background.\"","Bai Zihan calmly continued.","\"Princess, I believe you have been misinformed. I personally fought against him.\"","\"He was nothing like the geniuses said to come from the Central Glorious Continent.\"","A look of disappointment appeared on his face.","\"Honestly, I was rather underwhelmed. Even his guards were not particularly impressive.\"","\"Princess, rest assured. These people are merely swindlers trying to create trouble by borrowing someone else’s identity.\"","Silence!","The corner of Qin Lingxiao’s eye twitched.","A vein bulged slightly on her forehead.","Impostor?","Liar?","Swindler?","For the first time in many years, Qin Lingxiao felt the urge to curse someone.","Long Haotian was the direct heir of the Long Clan.","One of the most prestigious Heaven Chosen of the Central Glorious Continent.","An Immortal Realm genius!","The two elders accompanying him were Golden Immortals.","Yet Bai Zihan was describing them as if they were roadside scammers.","Who would believe such nonsense?","Unfortunately, Qin Lingxiao understood exactly what Bai Zihan was doing.","He was pretending.","Pretending Long Haotian’s identity was insignificant.","Pretending the Long Clan did not exist.","Pretending there was no reason whatsoever for the Imperial Family to become involved.","Everything pointed toward one conclusion.","Bai Zihan had absolutely no intention of handing Long Haotian over.","Taking a slow breath, Qin Lingxiao forcibly suppressed the irritation in her heart.","\"Clan Leader Bai.\"","Her voice became slightly heavier.","\"I believe you should reconsider. The Central Glorious Continent is not a place that can be provoked lightly.\"","\"If those people truly come from the Long Clan...\"","She looked directly into Bai Zihan’s eyes.","\"Then the consequences will be severe. The current Bai Clan may be powerful within the Desolate Heaven Empire.\"","\"But compared to the true overlords of the Central Glorious Continent...\"","She slowly shook her head.","\"The difference is simply too great!\"","Qin Lingxiao’s tone carried genuine seriousness.","Regardless of her personal objectives, the Long Clan was indeed a terrifying existence.","If they truly mobilized their strength, the Bai Clan would have little chance of survival.","Unfortunately, Bai Zihan merely smiled.","\"Thank you for your concern, Princess.\"","His tone remained polite.","However, his attitude left no room for discussion.","\"But I have my own considerations.\"","Qin Lingxiao’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Bai Zihan continued calmly.","\"If those people truly come from some great force and decide to make a move against me in the future...\"","A confident smile appeared on his face.","\"Then I will naturally take responsibility myself. There is no need for Princess Yu to concern herself with such matters.\"","The atmosphere immediately became heavier.","Qin Lingxiao stared at Bai Zihan.","Bai Zihan looked back calmly.","Neither side backed down.","At that moment, Qin Lingxiao understood something clearly.","No matter what she said today...","No matter how reasonable her arguments sounded...","Bai Zihan would never hand Long Haotian over.","A trace of frustration appeared within her heart.","Things had become troublesome.","Qin Lingxiao’s expression remained calm.","Not a single flaw could be found.","Yet beneath that calm exterior, her thoughts were anything but peaceful.","She could not leave Long Haotian in Bai Zihan’s hands.","That was simply not an option.","If Long Haotian had not yet revealed the secret of the True God’s legacy, then she needed to rescue him as quickly as possible.","Every moment he remained imprisoned increased the possibility of something going wrong.","After all, Long Haotian might be foolish, arrogant, and reckless, but his status was undeniable.","He was the direct heir of the Long Clan.","If she rescued him now, the Long Clan would undoubtedly owe her a tremendous favor.","A favor from one of the supreme forces of the Central Glorious Continent.","Such a thing carried enormous value.","However...","That was only the best-case scenario.","A cold light flashed deep within Qin Lingxiao’s eyes.","What if Long Haotian had already spoken?","What if Bai Zihan already knew about the map fragments?","What if he already knew about the True God’s legacy?","The moment that possibility surfaced, her heart sank.","Because if that was the case...","Then the situation became far more troublesome.","The fewer people who knew about the inheritance, the better.","Every additional person represented another competitor.","Most importantly, if news of the True God’s legacy reached the wider cultivation world, countless forces would descend upon the Desolate Heaven Empire.","At that point, even the Qin Clan would lose their advantage.","Her fingers unconsciously tightened beneath her sleeve.","If Bai Zihan truly knew...","Then she would have no choice.","Not because she hated him.","Not because she held any personal grudge.","But because she could not allow such information to spread.","Bai Zihan would have to die."]},{"number":647,"title":"Chapter 647: The Princess Reveals Her Hand","paragraphs":["However...","Qin Lingxiao’s brows furrowed slightly.","Killing Bai Zihan was not as simple as killing an ordinary cultivator.","Bai Zihan was the Clan Leader of the Bai Clan, being one of the most influential figures in the entire Desolate Heaven Empire.","His reputation had already reached unprecedented heights.","If he suddenly died... the entire empire would be shaken.","If Bai Zihan died after meeting her then suspicion would naturally fall upon her.","Or rather, upon Yu Feiyan.","After all, she was currently wearing Yu Feiyan’s identity.","The moment Bai Zihan died, investigations would begin.","And once those investigations started, it would not be difficult to discover that Yu Feiyan had come to the Bai Clan shortly before his death.","Even if no evidence existed.","Even if nobody could prove anything.","Suspicion alone would be enough.","A faint headache formed.","Because the consequences would be her losing the throne war.","Her gaze flickered slightly.","Everything she had done coming to the Desolate Heaven Empire would be for naught.","Only after obtaining the throne could she mobilize the Empire’s countless forces to search for clues regarding the True God’s legacy.","Qin Lingxiao silently weighed the benefits and costs.","Killing Bai Zihan would solve one problem.","But it might create ten more.","The price was simply too great.","Yet if Bai Zihan truly knew about the True God’s legacy...","For a moment, even Qin Lingxiao found herself trapped in a dilemma.","Across from her, Bai Zihan calmly watched her.","Although he could not read minds, he had a fairly good idea of what she was thinking.","And the more he thought about it, the more amused he became.","Did Qin Lingxiao truly believe things were still the same as before?","Did she think he was still that insignificant cultivator who could only struggle helplessly before a Golden Immortal?","A faint smile appeared on Bai Zihan’s face.","Back then, perhaps.","Back then, Qin Lingxiao could have killed him with a single finger.","But now?","The situation had changed.","Even if Qin Lingxiao truly wanted to kill him...","Could she actually accomplish it?","\"Heh!\"","Bai Zihan almost burst out laughing.","The matter of whether he lived or died was no longer entirely in her hands.","\"Princess.\"","Bai Zihan suddenly spoke.","\"If there is nothing else, I shall take my leave.\"","Qin Lingxiao’s eyes immediately sharpened.","\"Wait!\"","The words escaped her mouth almost instantly.","She stepped forward.","\"Clan Leader Bai, this matter does not concern only the Bai Clan. It concerns the entire Desolate Heaven Empire. You must think carefully!\"","Her voice carried obvious urgency.","Even now, she still hoped Bai Zihan would change his mind.","If he simply handed Long Haotian over...","Many problems could be resolved.","At the very least, she could determine exactly how much information had been leaked.","Unfortunately...","\"There is nothing more to discuss regarding this matter.\"","Bai Zihan’s tone was calm and decisive, leaving no room for negotiation.","Qin Lingxiao’s expression stiffened slightly.","Bai Zihan turned around.","He had no intention of continuing the conversation.","Likewise, he had no intention of directly confronting Qin Lingxiao.","Although his confidence had increased greatly, he was not arrogant enough to underestimate a Golden Immortal Cultivator.","If a battle erupted now, the Bai Clan would inevitably suffer losses.","That was something he wished to avoid.","Unfortunately...","Qin Lingxiao seemed to have finally reached her own conclusion.","A trace of coldness flashed through her eyes.","Her voice became slightly heavier.","\"Clan Leader Bai, this is my final warning.\"","Bai Zihan stopped walking.","Behind him, Qin Lingxiao continued.","\"If Long Haotian remains imprisoned here, disaster will eventually descend upon the Desolate Heaven Empire.\"","\"By then, it will not only be the Bai Clan that suffers. The entire Empire will pay the price.\"","Her tone sounded righteous and concerned.","As though she were genuinely worried about the Empire’s future.","Yet beneath those words lay a naked threat.","Bai Zihan also knew that it wasn’t like she cared about the Empire but just worked that Long Haotian might leak the information about True God’s legacy.","Unfortunately, he has already leaked them.","The surrounding air gradually became colder.","Qin Lingxiao’s eyes narrowed.","If Bai Zihan refused to listen...","Then perhaps there was only one option left.","A terrifying aura quietly began gathering within her body.","In that instant, countless thoughts flashed through her mind.","Kill him and deal with the aftermath later.","Perhaps someone could impersonate him temporarily.","Perhaps the truth could be concealed.","Golden Immortal energy silently surged.","The surrounding spiritual qi trembled.","And then she moved.","Boom!","A palm shot forward.","The strike was swift.","The terrifying power contained within it was enough to instantly annihilate an ordinary Great Ascension cultivator countless times over.","Even mountains would collapse beneath such a blow.","Qin Lingxiao’s eyes remained cold.","She thought that she already gave Bai Zihan plenty of chances to avoid death but he didn’t know how to appreciate her kindness.","As her attack descended, she was already calculating how to handle the chaos that would follow.","As for whether he would survive, that didn’t even cross her mind.","She was also busy thinking about her next move.","How to hide Bai Zihan’s death.","How to suppress the Bai Clan or if possible make use of them.","How to—","Suddenly.","Laughter echoed through the courtyard.","\"Hahahahahaha!\"","The laughter was loud and wild, almost crazed.","Qin Lingxiao’s pupils contracted.","Because the owner of that laughter was Bai Zihan.","Boom!","The rubble exploded outward.","Broken stones and shattered earth flew in every direction.","Bai Zihan slowly stepped out from the crater left behind by Qin Lingxiao’s attack.","Blood dripped down from his forehead.","A crimson trail ran along the side of his face.","Several tears had appeared in his robes, and more blood stained his sleeves and chest.","His condition was clearly far from unharmed.","Yet he was very much still standing.","Bai Zihan wiped the blood from the corner of his mouth and looked at Qin Lingxiao.","The grin on his face only widened.","As though the injuries covering his body were completely insignificant.","To be honest, Qin Lingxiao’s casual attack was more powerful than any technique he has been hit with.","However, still then apart from minor injuries and bleeding, nothing serious happened.","Qin Lingxiao was beyond stunned.","Not only had he survived, he was laughing.","As if he had just witnessed something incredibly amusing.","As if her attack was nothing more than a joke.","\"You! How did you survive that?\"","Although she didn’t utilize her full power, believing that she was already using more than what she should to deal with the Great Ascension Realm cultivator.","Even Long Haotian with all his artifacts would have been left on deathbed.","While Bai Zihan has defeated Long Haotian, she subconsciously never believed that Bai Zihan had beaten him fair and square.","Still then, even if it had not killed him, it should have very well crippled him.","Bai Zihan slowly turned around, his eyes locked onto hers.","A grin spread across his face.","\"So...\"","His voice echoed through the air.","\"You’ve finally shown your true colors!\"","The moment those words fell, several terrifying auras erupted around her.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","The heavens shook.","The earth trembled.","And Qin Lingxiao’s expression finally changed.","Qin Lingxiao’s expression finally changed.","(I’ve been surrounded!)","The realization struck her immediately.","Was it because she had been inattentive?","Had she allowed her guard to drop while focusing on Bai Zihan?","No.","That explanation didn’t make sense.","As a Golden Immortal, her divine sense far surpassed everyone present within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Yet until this very moment, she didn’t even know that she was surrounded by so many people.","One after another, powerful figures emerged from the shadows.","Some appeared atop rooftops.","Others descended from the sky.","Several simply stepped out from hidden locations throughout the Bai Clan.","Their gazes were all fixed upon Qin Lingxiao.","Cold and Hostile, Filled with killing intent.","Among them stood Bai Chu and Bai Ren.","And numerous Bai Clan Grand Elders.","Each of them radiated powerful auras of Immortal Realm.","Perhaps none of them alone could threaten Qin Lingxiao.","But together?","That was a different matter entirely.","Bai Chu took a step forward.","His aged eyes were icy.","\"Even though you are a Princess, the Bai Clan is not a place where you can act wildly.\"","His voice carried no respect whatsoever, only anger.","Another elder immediately followed.","\"You dared to attack our Clan Leader.\"","His expression was grim.","\"That means you are prepared to become an enemy of the Bai Clan.\"","Boom!","Several auras locked onto Qin Lingxiao simultaneously.","The surrounding atmosphere instantly became oppressive.","Qin Lingxiao narrowed her eyes.","Just from their expressions alone, she could tell that this matter had already become extremely ugly.","These people were furious.","If given the opportunity, they would not hesitate to kill her.","Of course...","The Bai Clan elders were not fools either.","The fact that Qin Lingxiao had managed to injure Bai Zihan with a single strike was enough to reveal many things.","Bai Zihan was no ordinary Great Ascension cultivator.","Everyone present knew that better than anyone.","Yet despite that, Qin Lingxiao had still sent him flying and drawn blood with what appeared to be a casual attack.","Such strength was impossible for an ordinary Immortal Realm cultivator.","Bai Ren’s expression became increasingly solemn.","His gaze remained fixed on Qin Lingxiao.","Judging from the aura she had briefly revealed...","There was only one possibility.","Golden Immortal Realm!","A true Golden Immortal had been hiding within the Desolate Heaven Empire this entire time.","And she had been masquerading as the Ninth Princess.","None of them understood how such a thing was possible.","Nor did they understand why Yu Feiyan possessed such terrifying strength.","But one thing was certain.","The woman standing before them was far more dangerous than any of them had previously imagined."]},{"number":648,"title":"Chapter 648: The Enchantress","paragraphs":["Bai Zihan casually dusted off the dirt on his robes.","Then he looked at Qin Lingxiao.","\"Princess Yu.\"","His smile widened slightly.","\"Why don’t you surrender obediently?\"","The moment those words fell, Qin Lingxiao’s face darkened.","Surrender?","A Golden Immortal Heaven Chosen from the Qin Clan surrendering to a group of cultivators from the Desolate Heaven Empire?","The mere thought was absurd.","Yet what truly angered her was the situation itself.","Everything had spiraled completely out of control.","She had come here intending to verify whether Long Haotian had leaked information.","Instead, she had exposed herself.","More importantly, she had fallen into Bai Zihan’s trap.","\"This is all your fault!\"","Qin Lingxiao suddenly bellowed.","Her beautiful face was filled with anger.","If he had obediently handed Long Haotian over, none of this would have happened.","\"Looks like Princess Yu isn’t going to listen when I’m being polite. Elders, please.\"","Boom!","The moment the command was given, the atmosphere changed completely.","Bai Ren immediately stepped forward.","His immortal aura erupted.","Beside him, Bai Chu moved as well.","His expression was icy as killing intent surged from his body.","The two strongest experts of the Bai Clan instantly positioned themselves at the very front.","Behind them, numerous elders moved into formation.","In the blink of an eye, Qin Lingxiao found herself surrounded from every direction.","The Bai Clan had clearly come prepared.","There was not the slightest opening.","Bai Ren’s eyes narrowed.","\"Princess or not. You attacked our Clan Leader.\"","Bai Chu coldly continued.","\"Today, you must give the Bai Clan an explanation.\"","Boom!","Dozens of powerful auras locked onto Qin Lingxiao simultaneously.","The pressure in the air became suffocating.","Qin Lingxiao slowly swept her gaze across the encirclement.","Then her eyes stopped on Bai Zihan.","The anger within them was almost tangible.","The next moment—","Boom!","A terrifying aura erupted from her body.","\"You dare!\"","Qin Lingxiao’s voice echoed across the Bai Clan.","Her beautiful face was filled with fury.","For someone of her status, being forced into such a situation inside a remote empire was an enormous humiliation.","Yet despite her anger, her mind remained calm.","Because Qin Lingxiao understood one thing.","Trying to defeat everyone present through brute force was unrealistic.","Even for her.","There were simply too many opponents.","Two Golden Immortals and numerous Immortal Realm cultivators.","Therefore, she needed another method.","As Bai Ren and Bai Chu advanced, a strange light flickered deep within Qin Lingxiao’s eyes.","Her physique quietly activated.","Invisible fluctuations spread outward which are almost impossible to detect.","She wasn’t trying to overpower them.","She was trying to influence them.","Manipulate and control them.","Among everyone present, Bai Ren and Bai Chu were naturally her primary targets.","If she could affect even one of them, the situation would immediately change.","However, she was well-aware of how difficult it was to influence another Golden Immortal Realm.","Golden Immortals possessed powerful souls and stable Dao Hearts, especially cultivators who had survived countless years of cultivation.","Still Qin Lingxiao was not discouraged.","While instantly bewitching the might not be possible, however over time, she can accomplish it.","She only needed time, a few minutes.","As long as she could survive long enough, her techniques would gradually take effect.","Her eyes filled with hatred as they landed on Bai Zihan.","Everything was because of him.","If not for Bai Zihan, she would never have exposed herself.","Never have fallen into such a predicament.","Fortunately, if she succeeded today, perhaps this entire incident could still be buried.","Meanwhile, from the rear of the formation, Bai Zihan quietly observed the battle.","His expression remained calm.","Even he had to admit it.","Qin Lingxiao truly deserved her title as a Heaven Chosen One.","Despite being surrounded by overwhelming numbers.","Despite facing two Golden Immortals and countless Immortal experts.","She still maintained her defenses flawlessly.","She refused to fall.","Refused to reveal weakness.","However, Bai Zihan also noticed something else.","She was buying time.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","(Still trying to use those abilities?)","Others might not understand what she was doing but Bai Zihan already knew the nature of her methods.","However, there was no need to worry about him.","After all, he already knew who his enemy was.","How could he possibly come unprepared?","Clank! Clank!","A long silver whip danced through the battlefield.","The weapon moved like a living serpent.","Sometimes soft.","Sometimes sharp.","Sometimes impossibly unpredictable.","Each strike carried terrifying Golden Immortal power.","Bai Chu’s sword collided with it.","Sparks exploded.","Boom!","A shockwave swept through the surroundings.","Before Bai Chu could continue, Bai Ren appeared from another direction.","A massive palm descended from above.","Qin Lingxiao twisted her body.","The whip lashed outward.","Boom!","Another collision erupted.","The heavens trembled.","The earth cracked.","Several Bai Clan elders immediately followed up.","Immortal techniques descended from every direction.","For a moment, Qin Lingxiao seemed completely engulfed yet she somehow escaped every fatal attack.","Again.","And again.","And again.","Her combat instincts were astonishing.","Even Bai Ren’s expression gradually became serious.","This woman was dangerous!","Clank!","The whip swept across the battlefield once more.","Qin Lingxiao forced back two elders before retreating several hundred meters.","A bead of sweat slowly formed on her forehead.","Her breathing had begun to grow heavier.","Even for her, fending off so many Immortal Realm cultivators simultaneously was far from easy.","The pressure continued increasing as Qin Lingxiao kept enduring.","She knew that all she needed was time.","Just a little more time.","And the entire battlefield would become hers.","Boom! Clank! Boom!","The battlefield continued to shake.","One minute passed.","Then another.","Then another.","Qin Lingxiao continued retreating while exchanging blows with the Bai Clan experts.","Her whip danced through the air like a silver dragon.","Every strike carried enough power to severely wound ordinary Immortal Realm cultivators.","Yet the Bai Clan experts refused to back down.","Bai Ren attacked relentlessly.","Bai Chu followed closely behind.","The other elders constantly coordinated with one another.","Their attacks arrived in endless waves.","Not giving Qin Lingxiao even a moment to breathe.","As time passed, Qin Lingxiao’s expression gradually became uglier.","(Something was wrong.)","Her abilities should have begun producing results by now.","Even if Bai Ren and Bai Chu possessed strong souls capable of resisting her influence, the other Bai Clan elders should not have been able to do the same.","Especially those in the Immortal Ascension Realm.","Under normal circumstances, some of them should already be showing signs of hesitation.","Yet none of it happened.","Not a single person slowed down.","Not a single person showed mercy.","Not a single person displayed any abnormalities.","Instead, they seemed even more determined than before.","Boom!","A sword strike narrowly missed her shoulder.","Qin Lingxiao immediately retreated.","Her eyes flickered.","Another minute passed.","Still nothing.","At this point, even Qin Lingxiao began doubting herself.","(How?)","For the first time since the battle began, genuine confusion appeared in her eyes.","(How is this possible?)","Her physique had never failed her before.","Even those stronger than her would gradually be affected if given enough time.","Yet here...","Absolutely nothing.","She glanced toward Bai Chu.","The old man’s sword was still swinging toward her neck without the slightest hesitation.","Then Bai Ren.","The Golden Immortal’s attacks only seemed to be growing fiercer.","There wasn’t even the smallest trace of influence.","Not even a crack.","Qin Lingxiao’s heart sank.","Then her gaze swept toward the Immortal Ascension elders.","Surely—","Surely at least one of them should have succumbed by now.","Yet what she saw nearly made her cough blood.","The elders were looking at her with expressions filled entirely with vigilance and hostility.","One of them even shouted,","\"Don’t let up!\"","\"She’s weakening!\"","Immediately, several attacks intensified.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Qin Lingxiao was forced back hundreds of meters.","The disbelief in her heart grew stronger.","(How? How did they avoid my seduction techniques?)","(How are they still attacking me?)","(How can they still bear to beat me down like this?)","Her confidence was beginning to crack.","For years, her physique had been one of her greatest advantages.","Countless geniuses.","Countless experts.","Countless enemies.","All had eventually fallen under its influence.","Yet the Bai Clan seemed completely immune.","At that moment, a familiar laugh sounded from the rear.","\"Hahaha...\"","Qin Lingxiao immediately turned.","There stood Bai Zihan.","His robes were stained with blood.","Yet the smile on his face was as irritating as ever.","He looked at her as though he had already expected this outcome from the beginning.","And indeed, he did. Ever since the incident at the Royal banquet where he almost succumbed to Qin Lingxiao’s charm, he knew how dangerous it was.","Hence why he had already made preparations, giving artifacts to resist her charm and mind control.","He also has made pills of Qin Lingxiao which can be eaten to clear one’s mind and heart.","Therefore, it definitely won’t be easy for Qin Lingxiao to seduce any Bai Clan Member."]},{"number":649,"title":"Chapter 649: Petals That Concealed the Sky","paragraphs":["Bai Zihan’s laughter continued to echo across the battlefield.","To Qin Lingxiao, that laughter sounded incomparably irritating.","Her anger only grew stronger.","Boom!","She lashed her whip forward, forcing back several Bai Clan elders before retreating once more.","Her beautiful face had long since lost its usual composure.","How could she not be angry?","She was Qin Lingxiao.","A Supreme existence from the Central Glorious Continent.","A genius who was able to reach the Golden Immortal realm in under two hundred years.","A woman whose very existence could overturn kingdoms and manipulate countless geniuses like puppets.","Back in the Central Glorious Continent, even powerful sect masters and clan leaders had to remain wary of her.","Yet now?","She was being forced into such a miserable state by a mere Bai clan.","If someone had told her this before entering the Desolate Heaven Empire, she would have laughed in their face.","Previously, she had always believed that if not for fear of attracting the attention of other forces from the Central Glorious Continent, she alone could easily dominate the entire Desolate Heaven Empire.","Yet reality had slapped her in the face.","She wasn’t facing the entire empire.","She was only facing the Bai Clan.","And still, she was being pushed back step after step.","Boom!","Another attack descended.","Qin Lingxiao deflected it with her whip.","Yet her thoughts remained chaotic.","Most importantly, she couldn’t understand why these people weren’t under her control.","Her physique along with her clan’s secret arts should have already made them into her obedient puppets.","Even if Bai Ren and Bai Chu possessed powerful Dao Hearts, what about the others?","What about the Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators?","Why were they also completely unaffected?","Why did none of them seem affected?","Why did none of them show the slightest trace of confusion?","How could she possibly accept that?","The more she thought about it, the more furious she became.","And eventually, her gaze landed upon the source of that infuriating laughter.","Bai Zihan!","Standing in the distance.","Blood still stained his robes with his injuries which had not fully healed.","Yet he looked as relaxed as ever.","As though everything remained completely under his control.","The sight nearly made Qin Lingxiao grit her teeth.","Her instincts screamed that whatever was happening had to do with Bai Zihan.","He must have done something.","\"Bai Zihan!\"","Her voice exploded across the battlefield.","Qin Lingxiao’s beautiful eyes burned with anger.","She no longer cared about maintaining the image of the elegant Ninth Princess.","In the distance, Bai Zihan merely looked at her.","There wasn’t the slightest trace of fear on his face.","Instead, he clicked his tongue.","\"Tsk! Tsk!\"","He slowly shook his head.","\"Princess, did you really think that just because you possess some strength, you can do whatever you want here?\"","Bai Zihan spread his arms.","His gaze swept across the entire battlefield.","\"This is the Bai Clan.\"","His voice suddenly became colder.","\"And since you dared to bare your fangs at me, then you should be prepared to face the consequences.\"","Boom!","As if responding to his words, another wave of attacks descended.","All of them surged toward Qin Lingxiao from every direction.","The pressure immediately increased once again.","Even Bai Zihan had to admit it.","Qin Lingxiao was impressive.","No! More than impressive.","She was currently facing two Golden Immortals.","Along with numerous Earth Immortals and Immortal Ascension cultivators.","Yet she still stood her ground.","Although she was being pushed back continuously, she had yet to truly collapse.","Such strength was enough to make even Bai Ren and Bai Chu take her seriously.","Of course...","Part of the reason was because neither Bai Ren nor Bai Chu had used their true trump cards.","Neither of them had unleashed Fate Severing Slash, their most powerful technique in their arsenal.","If they had done so from the beginning, Qin Lingxiao’s situation would have become far more dangerous.","Perhaps even fatal.","However, Bai Zihan had already instructed them beforehand.","Do not use it unless absolutely necessary.","The reason was simple, Bai Zihan still did not wish to kill Qin Lingxiao.","At least not yet.","The moment Qin Lingxiao died, there was a high chance that the Qin Clan would know.","If that forced the Qin Clan to go all out, then there was another headache right there.","More importantly, Qin Lingxiao was a Heaven Chosen.","Someone like her undoubtedly possessed countless life-saving treasures and hidden trump cards.","Bai Zihan wasn’t completely certain they could truly kill her.","Rather than recklessly exhausting themselves attempting to finish her off, it was better to preserve their strength.","Who knows what kind of trump card it would be?","Perhaps Qin Clan Supreme Immortal might make his entry.","If a greater threat appeared later, Bai Ren and Bai Chu would still need sufficient qi to fight.","Unfortunately, Qin Lingxiao knew none of this.","From her perspective, everyone present was genuinely trying to kill her.","Boom!","A sword narrowly brushed past her shoulder, followed by a palm strike which she barely dodged.","The constant pressure was enough to drive ordinary cultivators into despair.","Yet Qin Lingxiao’s eyes only became colder.","She wasn’t afraid but she was certainly furious.","Her gaze locked onto Bai Zihan.","The hatred within her eyes became increasingly obvious.","\"Bai Zihan!\"","Her voice was filled with killing intent.","\"You will regret this!\"","The moment those words fell, Qin Lingxiao suddenly stopped retreating.","Instead, she closed her eyes.","The surrounding battlefield seemed to freeze for an instant.","A strange aura emerged from her body.","It wasn’t violent nor was it destructive.","Instead, it felt ethereal and dreamlike.","Bai Zihan’s expression immediately became serious.","At the center of the battlefield, Qin Lingxiao slowly opened her eyes.","A strange fragrance suddenly spread across the battlefield.","Colorless and Invisible yet it permeated the surrounding area with astonishing speed.","Even the qi barriers erected by the Bai Clan elders failed to stop or notice it.","The fragrance passed through them as though they did not exist.","For a brief moment, several elders felt their minds become hazy.","Their eyes lost focus.","Countless scenes began surfacing within their consciousness.","Power.","Immortality.","Lost loved ones.","Unfulfilled regrets.","Their deepest desires manifested before them like beautiful dreams.","Bai Zihan’s expression immediately changed.","\"Don’t breathe in!\"","His voice exploded across the battlefield.","\"She’s using some kind of technique!\"","The Bai Clan elders instantly reacted.","Unlike the others, Bai Zihan remained completely unaffected.","The Saint-Grade Mind-Protecting Artifact protected his mind at all times.","If Qin Lingxiao’s abilities could not affect him from close range, they certainly would not affect him from such a distance.","Hearing his warning, Bai Ren and Bai Chu immediately sealed their senses except their sight.","The other elders quickly followed.","Those who had briefly fallen into a daze abruptly also woke up from Bai Zihan’s voice.","Their expressions became ugly.","Although the technique did not seem particularly destructive, it had successfully bought Qin Lingxiao several precious seconds.","And for someone like her, a few seconds were enough.","Qin Lingxiao’s eyes flashed coldly.","A mysterious seal formed between her fingers.","The next moment, her body began to dissolve into countless flower petals.","An endless storm of petals erupted outward as they scattered across the sky.","Each petal carried Qin Lingxiao’s aura.","For a brief instant, it seemed as though thousands of Qin Lingxiaos had appeared simultaneously.","\"Stop her!\"","Bai Ren roared.","Boom!","His divine sense erupted outward.","Sweeping across the battlefield yet the result caused his expression to sink.","Nothing.","Every petal seemed real.","Every petal seemed fake.","By the time the Bai Clan elders destroyed the sea of flowers, Qin Lingxiao herself had already vanished without a trace.","The petals gradually faded into light.","Leaving behind an empty battlefield.","Bai Ren frowned deeply.","Even with his Golden Immortal cultivation, he could not locate her.","It was as though she had disappeared from existence itself.","A moment later, Bai Chu landed beside Bai Zihan.","\"Clan Leader.\"","His voice was solemn.","\"Should we pursue her?\"","The surrounding elders immediately looked over.","Yu Feiyan revealed terrifying strength today.","Allowing such an enemy to escape was naturally dangerous.","However, Bai Zihan simply shook his head.","\"No!\"","The answer came without hesitation.","Bai Zihan looked toward the direction where Qin Lingxiao had disappeared.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","(Heaven Chosen are really not so easy to kill.)","He knew that If they chase her, the best outcome is that they fail to find her.","But the worst outcome is that they lose their lives.","Who hasn’t read a cultivation novel where the Main Character is chased by villains?","Either the Main Character successfully escapes or manages to counterattack.","There are also instances where his/her powerful friend, family or bodyguard appears and beats the villains.","If he orders the Elders to chase, there is a high chance that the result might be one of these.","Anyways, there is no need to take such a risk.","Moreover, from the very beginning, he had never intended to capture Qin Lingxiao anyway."]},{"number":650,"title":"Chapter 650: The Price of Defeat","paragraphs":["Thousands of flower petals drifted through the air.","They danced silently beneath the night sky before gradually converging toward a distant mountain range far from the Bai Clan.","The petals gathered.","Until finally, a figure emerged.","Qin Lingxiao stumbled forward.","Her face was pale.","Her breathing was heavy.","Several wounds covered her body.","Blood stained portions of her robes.","The elegant and noble appearance she usually maintained had long since disappeared.","For a moment, she simply stood there in silence.","Taking deep breaths.","Trying to stabilize the chaotic qi within her body.","Her eyes flickered with disbelief.","She could not even remember the last time she had been injured to such an extent.","Back in the Central Glorious Continent, even when competing against other powerful individuals, very few people had ever managed to force her into such a miserable state.","Yet today...","She had suffered this at the hands of the Bai Clan.","A trace of unwillingness appeared in her eyes.","She had greatly underestimated the Bai Clan.","Greatly underestimated Bai Zihan.","She had believed that even if the Bai Clan had grown stronger, it should still have been insignificant before her.","Instead, reality had taught her a painful lesson.","Not only had she failed to achieve her objective.","She had also exposed her true cultivation and even revealed part of her abilities.","The next time Bai Zihan faced her, he would undoubtedly be even more vigilant.","Just then, several figures rushed over from the shadows.","The moment they saw Qin Lingxiao’s condition, their expressions changed drastically.","\"Master!\"","\"What happened?!\"","The shock in their voices was impossible to hide.","Their eyes widened.","Some even suspected they were seeing things.","After all, Qin Lingxiao was a Golden Immortal.","A top genius of the Qin Clan.","Who in the Desolate Heaven Empire could possibly injure her to this extent?","Yet the evidence was right before them.","Qin Lingxiao waved her hand dismissively.","Clearly not wishing to discuss the matter.","The subordinates immediately lowered their heads.","None dared to question her further.","Qin Lingxiao’s gaze turned toward the distant direction of the Bai Clan.","A cold light flashed through her eyes.","\"From now on...\"","Her tone became noticeably more serious.","\"Exercise greater caution when dealing with the Bai Clan.\"","The subordinates immediately straightened.","\"Yes, Master!\"","Qin Lingxiao continued.","\"And send more people to watch them.\"","Her eyes narrowed.","\"Especially Bai Zihan.\"","\"Understood!\"","They answered without hesitation.","Qin Lingxiao slowly withdrew her gaze from the direction of the Bai Clan.","Her expression remained cold.","(As for Long Haotian...)","There was nothing she could do anymore.","His fate was now completely in Bai Zihan’s hands.","The same was true for the information regarding the True God’s legacy.","Whether it remained secret or became exposed was no longer something she could control.","A trace of frustration flashed through her eyes.","From the very beginning, she had wanted to prevent exactly this situation.","Unfortunately, things had spiraled beyond her expectations.","Still, Qin Lingxiao did not completely lose hope.","Long Haotian might be arrogant and foolish.","But he was not stupid enough to casually reveal information about the True God’s legacy.","Even the Long Clan would not spare Long Haotian if he dared to divulge information regarding the True God’s legacy.","At least, that was what she believed.","Of course...","She also had no idea what methods the Bai Clan might possess to force him to reveal the information.","Unfortunately, those matters were already beyond her control.","Thinking about them now would accomplish nothing.","At that moment, one of her subordinates hesitated before speaking.","\"Master...\"","Qin Lingxiao glanced toward him.","The subordinate immediately lowered his head.","\"Should we request additional support from the clan?\"","The others remained silent; however, many secretly agreed.","After witnessing Qin Lingxiao’s condition, anyone could tell that something had gone wrong.","Not only had she failed to bring back Long Haotian, but she had also returned injured.","If the Bai Clan truly possessed such strength, then perhaps someone stronger from the Qin Clan was needed.","The moment those words left his mouth—","Qin Lingxiao’s gaze turned icy.","The subordinate’s body stiffened.","A terrifying pressure descended upon him.","Cold sweat instantly appeared on his forehead.","He immediately realized his mistake.","Request support?","Wouldn’t that mean admitting failure?","Wouldn’t that mean telling the clan that she was struggling against a force from the Desolate Heaven Empire?","Qin Lingxiao had always been one of the Qin Clan’s proudest geniuses, someone who had never needed much assistance when carrying out her missions.","How could she willingly ask for support?","The subordinate immediately lowered his head further.","\"This subordinate spoke carelessly.\"","Qin Lingxiao looked away.","She did not bother responding.","The silence itself was already an answer.","A moment later, Qin Lingxiao stepped forward.","Her figure transformed into a streak of light.","Without another word, she shot toward the horizon.","Her destination was clear.","The Frost Lily Pavilion!","***","Meanwhile, at the Frost Lily Pavilion, the battle had already come to an end.","With Yu Wenzhao’s death, there was no longer any reason for the conflict to continue.","The moment news of his death spread across the battlefield, the resistance from his forces rapidly collapsed.","Without him, how could anyone continue to contend for the throne?","They had lost.","Meanwhile, Yu Feiyan’s allies were confused by her sudden departure.","One moment, everything was already in her hands and victory was inevitable.","The next moment, she had suddenly left as though something of utmost importance had occurred.","Princess Yu Qingya also did not understand the situation.","She only knew that Yu Feiyan had left in a hurry after receiving some sort of urgent information.","As for where she had gone or what she was doing, Yu Qingya had no clue.","Fortunately, none of that affected the overall outcome.","The victory had already been decided.","And so, Yu Qingya continued carrying out the task that was nearly completed.","The surrender of Yu Wenzhao’s forces.","Compared to the earlier fighting, this process progressed surprisingly smoothly.","Yu Wenzhao’s forces surrendered almost immediately, knowing that the war was a lost cause.","No one attempted anything foolish.","No one attempted to continue resisting.","The reason was simple.","They understood their situation.","Most importantly, they still wished to survive.","A defeated force had no right to make demands.","They could only hope that the victors would show mercy.","Thus, maintaining a cooperative attitude became their best option.","Only then could they minimize future punishment.","Many of them also possessed a clear understanding of the current state of the battle for the throne.","The last opponent still remained.","The First Prince, Yu Zidi!","Because of this, many former supporters of Yu Wenzhao secretly felt relieved.","Yu Feiyan still needed capable subordinates if she wished to ensure her eventual victory.","She could not afford to purge everyone who had once served Yu Wenzhao.","They knew that Princess Yu Feiyan would definitely recruit them, and this was even more true for powerful experts.","They were not overly worried about losing their lives because they knew that Princess Yu Feiyan would most likely want them as allies or subordinates.","This reality greatly reduced their worries.","The Earth Immortal from the Heaven Suppression Pavilion slowly stepped forward before cupping his fists toward Yu Qingya.","\"This old man greets Princess Qingya.\"","His attitude was far more respectful than before.","There was not the slightest trace of arrogance left.","After witnessing Yu Wenzhao’s death and the collapse of his faction, he understood better than anyone which direction the wind was blowing.","The Heaven Suppression Pavilion had already placed its bet.","Unfortunately, they had chosen the wrong side.","Now, the only thing left to do was minimize their losses.","\"This old man is willing to pledge loyalty to Her Highness, the Ninth Princess.\"","His voice echoed throughout the hall.","\"The Heaven Suppression Pavilion is also willing to cooperate fully with Her Highness’s future plans.\"","The Earth Immortal himself remained calm.","He knew that there might not be any immediate benefits from this declaration.","However, there was one thing he was certain of.","Showing loyalty and submission now would greatly increase the chances of preserving both his life and the future of the Heaven Suppression Pavilion.","Moreover, his eyes flickered slightly.","The throne war was not over.","The First Prince still stood in the way.","If he could demonstrate sufficient value during the upcoming conflict, perhaps not only would the Heaven Suppression Pavilion survive, but its status might even rise further.","After all, Prince Yu Wenzhao was dead, but his ambition was still very much alive.","Not far away, the Earth Immortal from the Crimson Thunder Palace stepped forward as well.","His actions were much the same.","They had never possessed any true loyalty toward the Third Prince in the first place and had only chosen to serve Yu Wenzhao after he defeated their Seventh Prince.","Now that Yu Feiyan had emerged victorious, they saw little reason not to change their allegiance once again.","\"This old man is also willing to serve Her Highness.\"","At the front of the hall, Yu Qingya quietly observed everything.","After hearing the declarations from the two Earth Immortals, she merely gave a slight nod.","She did not make any promises.","The reason was simple.","She did not know what Yu Feiyan’s intentions were.","As someone serving Yu Feiyan, everything that happened had to proceed according to Yu Feiyan’s wishes.","If Yu Feiyan wished to accept these people, then they would be accepted.","If Yu Feiyan wished to kill them, then so it would be.","This was their fate!"]},{"number":651,"title":"Chapter 651: Shadows from the Central Continent","paragraphs":["As time passed...","Whether they were former subordinates of Yu Wenzhao or long-time supporters of Yu Feiyan, all eyes remained fixed upon Yu Qingya.","After all, the person who would truly decide their future had yet to return.","Then—","A powerful aura approached from the distance.","Several experts immediately raised their heads.","Yu Qingya’s eyes brightened slightly.","A moment later, a streak of light descended from the sky.","Yu Feiyan appeared.","The moment she landed, countless gazes focused upon her.","Yu Qingya immediately stepped forward.","A trace of concern flashed through her eyes.","As one of Yu Feiyan’s loyal followers, she naturally noticed the injuries.","Although Qin Lingxiao had already concealed much of the damage and changed into fresh robes, several subtle traces remained.","Her complexion was slightly pale.","Her aura was somewhat unstable.","It was clear she had experienced a fierce battle.","\"Ninth Sister, what happened?\"","Yu Qingya’s voice was filled with concern.","Her eyes swept across Yu Feiyan’s pale complexion and the faint traces of injuries she had failed to completely conceal.","Unfortunately, Qin Lingxiao merely waved her hand dismissively.","Clearly, she had no intention of discussing the matter, just as before.","\"Has everything been settled?\"","A faint smile appeared on Yu Qingya’s face.","\"Ninth Sister, rest assured.\"","She gestured toward the gathered forces.","\"The aftermath has already been handled. The remaining forces have surrendered.\"","\"The major factions have also expressed their willingness to cooperate.\"","A trace of pride could not help but enter her voice.","Qin Lingxiao followed her gaze.","Her eyes swept across the battlefield.","The surrendered forces.","The various experts.","The Earth Immortals.","The remaining supporters of Yu Wenzhao.","Everyone stood quietly.","Seeing this, Qin Lingxiao gave a slight nod.","Objectively speaking, everything had gone perfectly.","Yu Wenzhao was dead, and his faction had collapsed.","The Ninth Princess’s influence had expanded tremendously.","The throne war was now entering its final stage.","Yet for some reason...","Qin Lingxiao felt no joy.","Instead, her thoughts drifted back toward the Bai Clan.","Toward that humiliating defeat.","The more she thought about it, the more agitated she became.","Fortunately, she quickly suppressed those emotions.","Now was not the time.","Her gaze shifted toward the former members of Yu Wenzhao’s faction.","Many of them immediately lowered their heads.","Others revealed nervous expressions.","There was both anticipation and fear.","No one knew how Yu Feiyan intended to deal with them.","Would she purge them?","Punish them?","Or accept them?","The atmosphere instantly became tense.","Qin Lingxiao slowly stepped forward.","Her voice echoed throughout the hall.","\"You all made the wrong choice.\"","The former supporters of Yu Wenzhao immediately felt their hearts tighten.","Qin Lingxiao continued calmly.","\"You chose to stand beside Yu Wenzhao and go against me.\"","No one dared to respond.","However, before panic could spread, her tone suddenly changed.","\"Fortunately for you, the battle for the throne is not over. The First Prince still remains.\"","Many people secretly released a breath of relief.","Qin Lingxiao’s eyes swept across the crowd.","\"I will give you an opportunity. An opportunity to make amends.\"","The hall instantly became quiet.","Everyone listened carefully.","\"I will judge your future according to your contributions in the war against the First Prince. If you perform well...\"","Qin Lingxiao paused briefly.","\"Then I will not hold your previous actions against you.\"","The moment those words fell, many people immediately revealed expressions of joy.","They quickly bowed.","\"Thank you, Your Highness!\"","\"This subordinate will certainly do his utmost!\"","\"We are willing to serve Your Highness!\"","...","Voices rang out one after another.","Even the former supporters of Yu Wenzhao became visibly excited.","After all, what they feared most was retaliation.","Now that Yu Feiyan had given them a path forward, they naturally seized it immediately.","Qin Lingxiao merely nodded.","Her expression remained calm yet inwardly, her thoughts were elsewhere.","(I need to finish this quickly.)","A cold light flashed through her eyes.","The situation had already changed.","Bai Zihan might now possess information regarding the True God’s legacy.","Even if he did not know everything, he knew far more than before.","Furthermore, more and more forces from the Central Glorious Continent were entering the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Every day that passed meant more competitors.","A trace of pressure appeared in Qin Lingxiao’s heart.","She had come here carrying the expectations of the Qin Clan.","Failure was unacceptable.","If she returned empty-handed after all this time...","The disappointment from the clan would be immense.","(No! That could not happen.)","Her fists slowly tightened beneath her sleeves.","No matter what happened...","No matter who stood in her way...","She had to obtain the True God’s legacy.","She had to succeed.","***","Meanwhile, back at the Bai Clan, Bai Zihan had already put the matter of Qin Lingxiao aside.","At least temporarily.","The moment she escaped, Bai Zihan immediately returned to fulfilling his duties as Clan Leader.","After all, regardless of how dangerous Qin Lingxiao was, there was little point dwelling on a battle that had already ended.","The more important matter was preparing for what came next.","Bai Zihan knew very clearly that the situation within the Desolate Heaven Empire was changing rapidly.","The Central Glorious Continent had already begun extending its influence into this land.","The first thing he planned to do was increase the Bai Clan’s overall strength.","Fortunately, resources were not a problem.","The Mu Clan continuously supplied large quantities of pills.","Furthermore, Bai Zihan himself could already refine Grade-8 pills.","Whether it was cultivation resources, breakthrough pills, healing pills, or tempering pills, the Bai Clan possessed an advantage that countless other forces could only dream of.","As a result, Bai Zihan intended to direct even more resources toward the clan’s cultivation.","He wanted the Bai Clan’s strength to rise as quickly as possible.","The stronger the Bai Clan became, the better they could withstand the approaching storm.","The second matter concerned intelligence.","Bai Zihan planned to have Kong Zhanhong increase surveillance throughout the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Particularly regarding the foreigners who had recently begun appearing.","He was already keeping an eye on them, and Bai Zihan wanted to increase that surveillance even further.","Moreover, he was also instructed to investigate the Desolate Heaven Empire for anything unusual or suspicious.","Bai Zihan did not tell Kong Zhanhong about the True God’s legacy because there was little benefit in doing so, even if he knew.","Furthermore, Bai Zihan himself did not know what the inheritance looked like, so he could not give Kong Zhanhong any specific instructions.","Therefore, Bai Zihan told him to focus on anything that appeared suspicious or resembled an inheritance.","All he could do was provide Kong Zhanhong with a vague direction and hope that something useful eventually surfaced.","After all, if the True God’s legacy truly existed somewhere within the empire, clues would inevitably appear sooner or later.","This would inevitably increase the cost as more people are required to be recruited.","Fortunately, money is also not a problem for Bai Zihan.","Thirdly, Bai Clan experts were deployed to keep an eye on the First Prince’s movements.","Now that Qin Lingxiao had defeated both Yu Qingya and Yu Wenzhao, her final target would undoubtedly be Yu Zidi.","After defeating him, she could ascend to the throne.","But Bai Zihan had no intention of allowing her to achieve that.","He had various methods of interfering, but first, it remained unknown whether she could truly defeat the First Prince in the first place.","Well, with her strength, it probably would not be too difficult.","And finally...","Bai Zihan intended to focus on improving his own strength.","In the past, his current cultivation could almost be considered invincible within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","But that was only before the arrival of the Central Glorious Continent’s forces.","With Long Haotian and his two elders’ arrival, it had already become clear that such forces could easily expand their presence here.","As more and more forces arrived and no longer felt the need to hide their intentions, it was certain that even more powerful individuals would appear.","Perhaps even Supreme Immortals might show up.","A trace of pressure surfaced in Bai Zihan’s heart.","His current strength was no longer sufficient.","Not if he wished to stand against Heaven Chosen like Qin Lingxiao.","Not if he wished to contend with the countless powerful experts now entering the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Not if he wished to seize the True God’s legacy for himself.","A faint smile appeared on Bai Zihan’s face.","Fortunately, he possessed advantages that nobody else did.","His gaze landed upon the familiar items in the System Shop.","The 10× Cultivation Card!","The 100× Cultivation Card!","Previously, Bai Zihan had been reluctant to spend his points, hoping to save them for a truly desperate situation.","But now that things had come to this, he knew that unless he rapidly increased his strength, no matter what artifacts or treasures he purchased, they would only serve as temporary solutions.","If he wished to survive the coming storm...","If he wished to crush enemies like Qin Lingxiao beneath his feet...","Then he needed greater strength.","As quickly as possible.","A cold light flashed through Bai Zihan’s eyes.","The era in which the Bai Clan dominated the Desolate Heaven Empire was coming to an end.","A far larger stage was beginning to reveal itself.","And Bai Zihan intended to stand at its very peak."]},{"number":652,"title":"Chapter 652: The Rising Tension","paragraphs":["After making all the necessary arrangements, Bai Zihan officially entered seclusion.","The Bai Clan also became unusually quiet.","From the outside, it almost seemed as though the Bai Clan had withdrawn from the world’s affairs.","However, the Bai Clan might have become quiet.","The outside world certainly had not.","In fact, the entire Desolate Heaven Empire was in an uproar.","Rumors spread at an astonishing speed.","No!","At this point, it was difficult to tell whether they were merely rumors or actual news.","The topic on everyone’s lips was naturally the Bai Clan.","More specifically, the two Grand Elders of the Bai Clan.","Bai Ren!","Bai Chu!","According to numerous witnesses, the two elders had displayed strength far beyond the Immortal Realm.","Many people even claimed that both of them had reached the legendary Golden Immortal Realm.","A realm that had never before appeared within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","At first, countless people dismissed the stories as exaggerations.","There had never been a single person who successfully survived the Heavenly Tribulation, and there were no Grade-8 pills to assist them.","As a result, many cultivators did not even attempt ascension, believing that remaining an Earth Immortal was far better than pursuing something seemingly impossible.","Now, how could two Golden Immortals suddenly appear within the Bai Clan?","Yet as more witnesses came forward...","And as more details emerged...","The skepticism gradually began to disappear.","Especially after reports surfaced that their opponent had also possessed Golden Immortal-level strength.","Soon, discussions erupted throughout the empire.","\"If those rumors are true, then who can stop the Bai Clan now?\"","\"Forget the Desolate Heaven Empire. Even the entire Eastern Region might fall beneath their influence.\"","\"Two Golden Immortals...\"","\"Just hearing those words is enough to make one’s scalp tingle.\"","\"The Bai Clan was already the strongest force in the empire. Now they’ve become even more terrifying.\"","Countless cultivators felt their hearts tremble.","The Bai Clan had already been viewed as an invincible giant.","Now, that giant has risen to an entirely new level.","Many people could not even imagine what force within the Eastern Region could still compete with them.","Naturally, the major powers became increasingly cautious.","The Li-Zhao Alliance, which was once arrogant and even believed that although they could not defeat the Bai Clan, they would not lose to them either, had become quiet.","There were no more provocations from them.","Whether it was a sign of submission or evidence that they were planning something behind closed doors, no one knew.","At the same time, another piece of news shook the empire.","The death of Yu Wenzhao!","The Third Prince’s fall had officially been confirmed.","And the person responsible was none other than the Ninth Princess herself.","The moment this information spread, public opinion exploded.","Many people were shocked.","Many were frightened.","Others began openly criticizing her.","After all, regardless of political struggles, Yu Wenzhao was still her brother.","Yet she had personally killed him.","As a result, countless rumors began circulating.","\"Yu Feiyan is too ruthless.\"","\"She even killed her own brother without hesitation.\"","\"If she becomes the Emperor, what will happen to the rest of us?\"","\"Such a person is far too dangerous.\"","...","Some even began referring to her as a bloodstained princess.","Others called her a heartless monster willing to sacrifice anyone for power.","While those actions could certainly be criticized, they were also being deliberately blown out of proportion.","After all, whenever there was a battle for the throne, bloodshed inevitably followed.","Many intelligent individuals quickly realized that someone was deliberately fanning the flames.","And when people considered who benefited the most from damaging Yu Feiyan’s reputation, the answer became obvious.","The First Prince, Yu Zidi.","At this stage of the throne war, only two true contenders remained.","Yu Feiyan and Yu Zidi.","Yu Zidi’s faction quietly pushed the narrative throughout the empire.","Stories portraying Yu Feiyan as cold-blooded.","Stories portraying her as a calculating schemer devoid of emotion.","Stories portraying her as a woman willing to sacrifice family, allies, and subjects alike in pursuit of power.","The campaign was relentless and surprisingly effective.","After all, the death of Yu Wenzhao was real.","The facts themselves provided ample ammunition.","Yu Zidi’s supporters merely needed to guide public opinion in the desired direction.","As the rumors spread farther and farther, the atmosphere within the empire gradually became more tense.","Many citizens now hold negative impressions of Yu Feiyan.","Compared to Yu Feiyan, many felt that Yu Zidi, who was known for being kind and compassionate, should become the next Emperor.","The situation continued to escalate.","And this time, the Imperial Court itself officially stepped onto the stage.","Soon, a decree was issued from the capital.","The contents spread throughout the empire at astonishing speed.","The Imperial Court openly condemned the Ninth Princess.","According to the decree, Yu Feiyan had violated imperial law by personally killing a member of the Imperial Family.","Regardless of the circumstances.","Regardless of the political struggle.","Yu Wenzhao had still been a prince of the empire.","His death at the hands of Yu Feiyan was declared a serious crime.","The decree demanded that Yu Feiyan immediately return to the capital and submit herself to investigation and punishment.","Furthermore, she was ordered to comply with the judgment of the Imperial Court.","If she refused, the Court would be forced to act according to the law.","The announcement immediately caused another wave of discussion across the empire.","Many commoners were shocked.","Many cultivators sneered.","And many major powers simply watched in silence.","After all, everyone knew one thing.","Yu Feiyan would never comply.","And indeed—","Yu Feiyan’s response arrived.","Or more accurately...","There was no response at all.","The Ninth Princess completely ignored the decree.","She neither defended herself nor acknowledged the Court’s authority.","It was as though the order did not exist.","The Court naturally could not tolerate such a blatant challenge to their authority.","Soon afterward, a second decree was issued.","This time, the tone became far harsher.","Yu Feiyan was officially declared a criminal of the empire.","Anyone assisting her would be viewed as aiding a criminal.","Any force supporting her would be subject to investigation.","The Court further condemned her followers and accused them of participating in rebellion against the empire.","The news immediately spread throughout every corner of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Although it still caused shock, the reaction was far less dramatic than expected.","Because many people had already anticipated this outcome.","After all, everyone knew who currently controlled the Imperial Court.","Yu Zidi!","Thus, the Court’s actions did not surprise the major powers.","The real question was something else.","Could the Court actually enforce its decree?","That was where opinions began to differ.","Many experts simply shook their heads.","The Court might possess authority, but authority alone was not enough.","Yu Feiyan was no longer the same princess she had once been.","Behind her stood three of the empire’s top sects.","Numerous major clans.","Countless experts.","Even if the Imperial Family mobilized its forces along with its military power, capturing Yu Feiyan would still be extremely difficult.","In fact, many believed the Court lacked the strength to do so altogether.","The decree sounded impressive.","But without sufficient power to enforce it, it was little more than words on paper.","Naturally, Yu Zidi’s camp understood this as well.","They were not foolish enough to believe a single decree could eliminate Yu Feiyan.","That was never the true objective.","The real goal was public opinion.","The real goal was legitimacy.","The real goal was to stir the emotions of the public.","If Yu Feiyan could be branded as a criminal in the minds of the people, then Yu Zidi would gain the moral high ground.","Every accusation.","Every decree.","Every public condemnation.","Was merely another weapon in the battle for the throne.","A weapon without bloodshed.","Yet one that could be just as dangerous.","While Yu Zidi’s faction continued doing everything in its power to smear Yu Feiyan’s reputation, something unexpected happened.","Yu Feiyan did nothing.","No public response or clarification.","No attempt to defend herself before the people.","Of course, many understood that such efforts would likely be meaningless anyway.","Once public opinion had been stirred to such a degree, a few explanations would not be enough to reverse it.","Still, people had expected something.","At the very least, they expected retaliation.","Yet none came.","Even more surprisingly, Yu Feiyan did not immediately move against Yu Zidi.","This left countless people confused.","After all, from the perspective of the outside world, Yu Feiyan now possessed overwhelming advantages.","Many believed that if she truly wished to do so, she could easily defeat Yu Zidi and seize the throne for herself.","At least, that was what most people believed.","Yet Yu Feiyan remained unusually quiet.","It was almost as if she were waiting for something or perhaps wary of something.","This strange silence only made people increasingly uneasy.","Even Yu Zidi’s supporters felt somewhat unsettled.","After all, an enemy who openly attacked was far easier to deal with than an enemy who remained hidden.","Days passed.","Then weeks.","The atmosphere throughout the empire became increasingly tense.","Everyone knew that the final confrontation was approaching.","Yet neither side made any significant move.","The calm before the storm stretched on endlessly.","Many cultivators even began speculating whether both sides were secretly gathering strength for a decisive battle.","Others wondered if some unseen force was influencing the situation from the shadows.","Rumors appeared every day with theories emerging one after another.","As time passed, the tension only continued to build.","Eventually...","It reached its peak.","And then—","Nothing happened.","Several more weeks passed.","The anticipated war never came.","The empire remained trapped in a strange state of uncertainty.","Until one day.","A decree suddenly emerged from the Imperial Capital.","After consultation with the ministers, military officials, and representatives of the common people—","The next Emperor of the Desolate Heaven Empire would be Yu Zidi!"]},{"number":653,"title":"Chapter 653: Baiting the Ninth Princess","paragraphs":["\"Heh!\"","Qin Lingxiao looked at the invitation sent by the Imperial Court.","More specifically, the invitation to Yu Zidi’s coronation ceremony.","It had been distributed to almost all of the major forces, including many clans and sects under her command.","Of course, for a big event such as the coronation of Desolate Heaven Empire’s Emperor, it wasn’t limited to just Desolate Heaven Empire.","The surrounding nation has also received the invitation including Empires like Vermillion Pill Empire and Falling Star Empire.","A faint sneer appeared on Qin Lingxiao’s face.","She barely needed a glance to understand what it was.","A very obvious trap.","Yu Zidi was trying to lure her into making a move.","If she did nothing, then once the coronation was completed, Yu Zidi would officially become the Emperor of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","At that point, any action she took afterward could easily be branded as rebellion.","Whether she cared about such labels was another matter entirely.","However, legitimacy was still important, especially when trying to unite forces beneath a single banner.","Otherwise, even if she got the throne, if those people under her couldn’t obey what she says, then what she did until now would be useless.","Qin Lingxiao lightly tapped the invitation against the table.","Her eyes remained calm.","These were merely some small tricks from Yu Zidi.","Unfortunately, she had little choice but to take the bait.","A cold light flashed through her eyes.","She could not afford to continue delaying.","It has already been a month since she suffered at the Bai Clan.","Every additional day increased the chances of more forces from the Central Glorious Continent becoming aware that the True God’s legacy is in the Desolate Heaven Empire.","That was something she wished to avoid at all costs.","The fewer competitors, the better.","However, Qin Lingxiao was unable to take any swift action against Yu Zidi.","She has various methods by which she could have instantly gotten the throne.","For example, assassinating Yu Zidi which was probably the most efficient and quick.","Unfortunately, that idea had quickly reached a dead end because she could not find him at all.","No matter how many people she sent.","No matter how extensive her intelligence network became.","Yu Zidi’s whereabouts remained a mystery.","She did not even know whether he was currently within the Imperial Capital or hidden somewhere else entirely.","It was as though he had vanished from the world.","So, even if she wanted to take any direct action against Yu Zidi, she couldn’t.","As for infiltrating his faction and gradually taking control of his forces just as she did previously, that was even less practical.","The process was far too slow because of various officials and factions that the First Prince is allied with.","Unlike Yu Wenzhao or Yu Qingya, as far she knows, Yu Zidi didn’t have a single major backing which if lost, he would lose.","Rather his backing were all the important officials of the Imperial Court who had a lot of connections.","If she were to start by taking his allies, it would require her to personally interact with numerous officials and influential figures.","Doing so would only risk exposing herself to greater traps.","Yu Feiyan was confident in her strength. After all, she was a Golden Immortal Realm cultivator.","But she was not arrogant enough to believe she could do whatever she wanted.","The lesson from the Bai Clan was still fresh in her mind.","If she encounters another unexpected obstacle just like the Bai Clan, then her plans will be for naught and she might end up suffering at the First Prince’s hand.","Her eyes narrowed slightly.","Yu Zidi was not a simple opponent.","Many people thought that those old monsters who had lived for thousands of years were wise and omniscient.","In Yu Feiyan’s opinion, that was just bullshit.","Most of them had spent the majority of their lives in seclusion.","When it came to schemes and political maneuvering, many of them were surprisingly lacking.","They might not be as good as the shopkeeper aunties on the street.","Many cultivators who spents most of their time in seclusion think that larger fists equal greater truth.","The people truly proficient at scheming were often those born into royal families.","People like Yu Zidi.","Individuals who had been immersed in political struggles from the moment they were born.","Every smile concealed intentions.","Every word carried hidden meanings.","Every action served a purpose.","Compared to them, many powerful cultivators seemed almost straightforward and naive.","Although they might possess higher cultivation, more often than not, they ended up losing against such scheming individuals.","Fortunately, Yu Feiyan was not one of those cultivators who relied solely on strength.","She understood various schemes to a certain extent due to her dealings with various royal families in the Central Glorious Continent.","Yet even so, she could not fully grasp what Yu Zidi was planning, nor could she predict what cards he still held in reserve.","However, just his decision to hide and not confront her directly showed just how cautious he is.","He might try to smear her reputation and whatnot but he has been avoiding direct confrontation and also revealing his position.","Qin Lingxiao slowly placed the invitation back onto the table.","Her gaze became firm.","In the end...","There was only one option.","She would need to attend.","The coronation ceremony was the one occasion where Yu Zidi would be forced to appear before her.","That might be the only opportunity for her to deal with him directly.","Otherwise, if she missed that chance as well, who knew for long he would go into hiding?","But she also knew that since he was making his appearance and even dared to give her force the invitation, he must have something planned.","\"One month...\"","Although it was a bit long, since she could not find him, she had no choice but to attend the so-called coronation and deal with him there.","***","Two months passed since Bai Zihan entered seclusion.","The only reason Bai Zihan finally emerged from seclusion was because today was the day of Yu Zidi’s coronation.","The day the First Prince was supposed to ascend the throne and become the next Emperor of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Naturally, Bai Zihan had already been informed when the invitation was first delivered to the Bai Clan.","At the time, he had been somewhat surprised, though not particularly shocked.","After all, from Yu Zidi’s perspective, this was indeed the best move available.","Force Yu Feiyan to make a choice.","Either allow him to become Emperor or come and stop him.","Simple and effective.","That was, of course, only if Yu Feiyan were not Qin Lingxiao in disguise and did not possess Golden Immortal cultivation.","Aside from that matter, there had been nothing urgent enough to warrant interrupting Bai Zihan’s cultivation.","As a result, he had remained in seclusion for another entire month.","Although only two months had passed in the outside world, for Bai Zihan, the cultivation wasn’t limited to just that two months.","With effects of the 100× Cultivation Card and the 10× Cultivation Card, he was cultivating for more than two months.","To others, it had only been sixty days.","To Bai Zihan, however, it felt more like two to three years of cultivation.","The benefits were naturally enormous.","Of course, the price was equally enormous.","His System Points had been consumed at an alarming rate.","After checking his remaining balance, even Bai Zihan could not help but feel somewhat helpless.","Only a little over ten thousand points remained.","Compared to the mountain of points he once possessed, the current amount was almost insignificant.","Still...","Bai Zihan did not regret it.","Resources existed to be used.","What mattered was the result and the result was extremely satisfactory.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","He slowly opened his eyes.","[ \"System!\" ]","*************************","[ Host Info ]","Host: Bai Zihan","Age: 20","Cultivation Realm: Great Ascension (Late)","Constitution: Primordial Chaos Body","Supreme Dao Bone","Martial Arts:","Nine Shadows Flowing Light Sword (Major Mastery)","Eternal Flowing Water Sword (Greater Mastery)","Fate Severing Slash (Greater Mastery)","Heaven’s Mandate Reversal (Minor Mastery)","*************************","In these two months, he had been able to break through from the Early Great Ascension Realm to the Late Great Ascension Realm.","That was an increase of two minor realms.","Not only that, he had also practiced his martial arts, but he was only able to increase the mastery of Heaven’s Mandate Reversal technique by one level.","As for the others, it seemed that he would need much more intensive practice if he wished to improve them further.","Well, there was no time for that right now.","Not only did he need to attend the coronation, but he also needed to earn a few more points.","Considering what might happen during the upcoming coronation, Bai Zihan was certain that many opportunities would present themselves for him to earn System Points, which he could then use for cultivation."]},{"number":654,"title":"Chapter 654: The Gathering of Powerful Delegations","paragraphs":["As the day of the coronation drew nearer, the entire Desolate Heaven Empire became increasingly lively.","Among all the places within the empire, none was busier than the Imperial Capital.","The streets were cleaned daily.","New decorations were hung throughout the city.","The main avenues leading toward the Imperial Palace were lined with imperial guards standing at attention.","Everywhere one looked, preparations for the coronation were underway.","After all, regardless of the ongoing struggle for the throne, if everything proceeded smoothly, the empire would soon welcome its new Emperor.","Naturally, such an occasion could not be treated lightly.","Invitations had long since been sent across the Eastern Region.","Not only to the major forces within the Desolate Heaven Empire but also to neighboring empires.","Various royal delegations had already begun making their way toward the Imperial Capital.","For several days, flying ships continuously descended outside the capital.","The number of experts entering the city increased by the hour.","The Imperial Capital, which was already prosperous, became even more crowded than before.","Countless discussions could be heard throughout inns, restaurants, and tea houses.","\"So, the First Prince is finally becoming Emperor.\"","\"After all this chaos, the throne finally has an owner.\"","\"I just hope the empire can return to peace.\"","Many ordinary citizens secretly sighed in relief.","To them, they did not particularly care who became Emperor.","What they wanted was peace and stability.","Years of internal conflict had already caused enough unrest.","If the empire could finally settle down, that would naturally be the best outcome.","Of course...","Not everyone shared that optimism.","\"What about the Ninth Princess?\"","\"Do you really think she’ll simply accept this?\"","After everything that had happened, very few believed Yu Feiyan would willingly watch Yu Zidi ascend the throne.","\"Impossible! She’s willing to kill the Third Prince, her own third brother. If she’s willing to go that far, why would she stop now?\"","\"She truly wants the throne, she won’t simply hand it over.\"","\"Then why hasn’t she attacked the First Prince yet?\"","\"Didn’t everyone say she defeated both Yu Qingya and Yu Wenzhao within a very short period? If she’s truly that powerful, why has Yu Zidi remained completely unharmed until now?\"","His words caused many people to become thoughtful.","\"Perhaps... she’s afraid?\"","\"That’s right. If she truly possessed overwhelming strength, she would have marched straight into the Imperial Capital long ago.\"","\"Instead, she’s remained completely silent. Maybe the First Prince possesses hidden trump cards which she is scared of.\"","Many people nodded.","After all, Yu Zidi had remained calm throughout the entire struggle for the throne.","Not only had he never shown the slightest panic, but he had even publicly announced his coronation.","If he lacked confidence, would he really dare to do something so bold?","Of course, not everyone held the same opinion.","\"No. I don’t think it’s that simple.\"","\"Someone like the Ninth Princess definitely has her own plans.\"","\"She’s probably just waiting for the right opportunity.\"","The discussions grew increasingly heated.","Would Yu Feiyan appear at the coronation?","Or would she simply watch Yu Zidi become Emperor?","No one knew the answer.","Yet everyone understood one thing.","If Yu Feiyan truly intended to make a move...","Then the upcoming coronation would very likely become the final battlefield in the struggle for the throne.","As the number of distinguished guests arriving at the Imperial Capital continued to increase, the city’s security became noticeably tighter.","The number of guards patrolling the streets increased severalfold.","Elite imperial troops were stationed at every major intersection.","The city gates were heavily guarded day and night.","Even the skies above the capital were constantly patrolled by cultivators from the Imperial Family.","After all, this coronation was unlike any held before.","Not only would the major forces of the Desolate Heaven Empire be present.","Delegations from neighboring empires were also expected to attend.","The sheer number of powerful cultivators gathering within the Imperial Capital was unprecedented.","No one could predict what might happen during their stay.","For that reason, the Imperial Guards remained on constant alert.","Many ordinary citizens also became increasingly nervous.","Even numerous ministers within the Imperial Court shared similar concerns.","However...","The person at the center of all this, Yu Zidi, appeared to hold an entirely different opinion.","In previous generations, whenever foreign delegations visited the Desolate Heaven Empire, strict regulations had always been enforced.","Every empire was limited in the number of experts it could bring.","After all, allowing too many powerful foreign cultivators to enter the Imperial Capital at once posed an obvious security risk.","If something unexpected happened, the consequences would be unimaginable.","Yet this time...","Those restrictions had completely disappeared.","Not only did Yu Zidi abolish the previous limitations, but he personally announced that every visiting empire was free to bring as many experts as they wished.","According to him, the larger the delegation...","The greater the respect they were showing toward the Desolate Heaven Empire and its newly ascended Emperor.","This decision immediately caused an uproar within the Imperial Court.","Many experienced ministers were alarmed.","During one court session, an elderly minister stepped forward and respectfully cupped his fists.","\"Your Highness, this official believes such a decision is inappropriate.\"","\"If numerous foreign experts are allowed to enter the Imperial Capital without restriction, it could pose a serious threat to the empire’s national security.\"","Another minister quickly stepped forward in agreement.","\"Your Highness, this official also believes the previous regulations should remain in place.\"","\"Should an accident occur during the coronation, the consequences would be beyond imagination.\"","A third minister added solemnly,","\"Your Highness, this matter also concerns your own safety.\"","\"If too many foreign experts gather within the capital, protecting Your Highness will become significantly more difficult.\"","Voices of opposition echoed throughout the hall.","Nearly all the veteran ministers shared the same concern.","To them, this was simply too dangerous for the security of the nation and Yu Zidi’s security.","However...","Seated upon the throne, Yu Zidi merely smiled faintly.","His expression remained calm from beginning to end.","He slowly swept his gaze across the court before speaking leisurely.","\"You worry too much. The coronation is a celebration for the entire Eastern Region.\"","\"The more distinguished guests who attend, the greater the honor bestowed upon the Desolate Heaven Empire.\"","He paused briefly before continuing,","\"If they are willing to bring more experts to witness my ascension, then that only proves the importance they place upon this occasion.\"","\"Why should We refuse such sincerity?\"","The ministers exchanged uneasy glances.","Several wanted to continue persuading him.","Yet seeing Yu Zidi’s unwavering attitude, they ultimately swallowed the words that had reached their lips.","None of them understood why Yu Zidi insisted on making such a risky decision.","Yu Zidi’s decision quickly spread beyond the borders of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Naturally, the various neighboring empires did not hold back.","One powerful delegation after another began making its way toward the Imperial Capital.","The scale of their entourages far exceeded anything seen in previous coronation ceremonies.","Some empires dispatched several Earth Immortals.","Others sent entire groups of elite cultivators.","There were even forces that treated the journey almost like a military expedition.","Among them all, none attracted more attention than the Vermillion Pill Empire.","The moment news of its delegation spread, the entire Imperial Capital erupted into discussion.","The Vermillion Pill Empire had dispatched five of its ten strongest cultivators.","Along with them came numerous renowned elders, protectors, and elite experts.","The size of the delegation was astonishing.","When people learned of it, they could not help but gasp.","\"Five of the Top Ten?\"","\"Is this really just for a coronation ceremony?\"","\"That force alone is enough to sweep through an ordinary empire.\"","Many people secretly felt their scalps go numb.","If someone claimed that the Vermillion Pill Empire had no other intentions besides attending the ceremony...","Almost no one would believe it.","Nor was the Vermillion Pill Empire the only one.","The other neighboring empires had likewise dispatched lineups that far exceeded normal diplomatic standards.","Although they all claimed to be attending to congratulate the new Emperor...","The sheer number of experts accompanying each delegation made that explanation difficult to accept.","The atmosphere within the Imperial Capital became increasingly tense.","The veteran ministers naturally noticed this as well.","During another court session, several ministers once again stepped forward.","\"Your Highness!\"","An elderly minister respectfully cupped his fists.","\"The number of foreign experts entering the Imperial Capital has already exceeded all previous records.\"","\"The Vermillion Pill Empire alone has dispatched five of its ten strongest cultivators.\"","\"If something unexpected were to happen...\"","Before he could finish speaking, another minister also stepped forward.","\"Your Highness, this official requests that the previous restrictions be reinstated immediately.\"","\"It is still not too late.\"","Even the Military Commander of the Imperial Family took a step forward.","His expression was unusually solemn.","\"Your Highness.\"","\"This subordinate has defended the Imperial Capital for hundreds of years.\"","\"But never have I witnessed so many foreign experts gathering within the city.\"","\"If they harbor any ill intentions...\"","He paused briefly before continuing.","\"The Imperial Capital may fall into complete chaos.\"","The hall became completely silent.","Nearly every minister shared the same concern.","Their worries were no longer hypothetical.","The foreign experts were already arriving in overwhelming numbers.","Yet...","Yu Zidi did not even seem interested in listening.","He casually waved his hand.","\"Enough!\"","A single word immediately silenced the entire court.","His expression remained as calm as ever.","\"There is no need to discuss this matter any further.\"","The ministers looked at one another.","Many still wished to persuade him.","However, seeing Yu Zidi’s unquestionable attitude, they ultimately remained silent.","None of them could understand what their future Emperor was thinking.","It was as though...","He actually welcomed the arrival of all those powerful foreign experts."]},{"number":655,"title":"Chapter 655: Humiliation Within the Imperial Capital","paragraphs":["The arrival of the foreign delegations quickly changed the atmosphere within the Imperial Capital.","At first, everything was normal for the coronation of the new Emperor.","It was likely with thousands flocking to the Imperial Capital especially the merchants.","With Imperial Capital about to receive lots of people, how can merchants miss such an opportunity to make money?","The residents of the Capital were also preparing to receive a lot of guests and celebrate such a grand occasion.","Then various delegations also entered the city under the escort of the Imperial Guards.","The Imperial Court treated every guest with the highest level of courtesy.","However...","As more and more experts arrived, problems gradually began to surface.","Many of the foreign delegation cultivators behaved as though the Imperial Capital belonged to them.","Some rode their spirit beasts directly through the busiest streets, forcing ordinary citizens to scramble out of the way.","Others openly released portions of their cultivation aura simply because they disliked being surrounded by crowds.","They seemed to have put no laws in their eyes and deliberately did whatever they pleased.","Entire marketplaces became chaotic wherever they passed.","No one dared offend them.","After all, they represented foreign empires.","Any conflict involving them could easily escalate into a diplomatic incident.","More importantly...","Everyone knew that Yu Zidi himself had personally welcomed these delegations.","Offending them was, in a sense, equivalent to disrespecting the Emperor-to-be.","Who would dare shoulder such responsibility?","Not to mention...","Among the countless experts within the Imperial Capital, only a handful possessed the strength to contend against these cultivators.","Most citizens simply endured in silence.","Even the Imperial Guards were forced to suppress their anger.","Many times, they witnessed foreign cultivators openly disregarding imperial regulations.","Yet after recognizing the insignias on their robes, they could only grit their teeth and step aside.","Not only could they do nothing to these people, but they also had to offer apologies instead.","One incident after another spread throughout the city.","At one of the capital’s most famous restaurants, dozens of cultivators from a neighboring empire occupied the entire upper floor.","They ordered nearly every signature dish.","Rare spirit wine flowed endlessly and expensive spiritual beast meat was served plate after plate.","By the end of the banquet, the cost was enough to bankrupt an ordinary cultivator several times over.","Yet when the owner nervously presented the bill, one of the foreign cultivators merely laughed.","\"We came here to honor your future Emperor. Our very presence is already giving this restaurant face.\"","\"You still expect us to pay?\"","The restaurant owner turned pale.","He wanted to argue.","But after sensing the terrifying aura released by the other party, he swallowed his words.","In the end...","He could only force a bitter smile while watching them leave.","Not a single gold coin was paid.","When he later reported the matter to the nearby Imperial Guards, the guards exchanged helpless looks.","One captain sighed deeply.","\"We understand your grievances but they are official delegations. We cannot act without orders from above.\"","The restaurant owner could only lower his head in despair.","Similar incidents occurred throughout the city.","Some foreign cultivators occupied entire inns without paying.","Others casually seized cultivation rooms after claiming they were too small for people of their status.","There were even those who openly pushed local cultivators aside simply because they wished to walk first.","Resentment quietly accumulated among the people.","Many citizens no longer understood Prince Yu Zidi’s decision.","\"What exactly is His Highness planning?\"","\"Why allow these people to act however they please?\"","\"This is our Imperial Capital, not theirs.\"","\"Our own people are being bullied while the Imperial Guards can only stand by. Are they here to serve us or them?\"","The complaints grew louder with each passing day.","When had they ever suffered such humiliation?","They were the strongest empire in the Eastern Region, and it should have been these people who behaved carefully while in their territory, not the other way around.","This was all due to Yu Zidi’s orders. Otherwise, if the Desolate Heaven Empire truly wished to deal with these foreigners, would they be able to resist?","How could they still continue to act so domineering?","Therefore, as resentment toward these foreign delegations increased, so did the resentment toward Prince Yu Zidi.","Meanwhile, the foreign cultivators became increasingly arrogant.","Having encountered no resistance whatsoever, many of them gradually stopped treating the Desolate Heaven Empire with respect.","So they began to view the Imperial Capital of Desolate Heaven Empire as little more than a backward empire hosting them.","After all, most of these people were here to support Yu Zidi, and they were well aware that no matter what they did, unless it became too outrageous, there would be no repercussions.","Inside one of the luxurious restaurants, several cultivators sat leisurely around a table.","Their robes bore the unmistakable emblem of the Tianyu Empire.","\"So this is the famous Desolate Heaven Empire? I expected something far grander.\"","\"Their citizens don’t even dare meet our eyes. Earlier, I walked through the busiest street. The moment they sensed my aura, everyone scattered like frightened sheep.\"","The room erupted into laughter.","\"What’s there to be surprised about?\"","\"This trip is merely a formality. The coronation itself is of little importance. Our true objective lies elsewhere. Don’t forget that!\"","The room immediately fell silent as they nodded.","Every member of the delegation understood exactly what he meant.","After enjoying their meal, the members of the Tianyu Empire slowly rose from their seats.","They chatted and laughed among themselves as though they had completely forgotten about the bill.","Just as they reached the entrance, the restaurant manager suddenly rushed forward.","His eyes were already red, on the verge of crying.","He bowed repeatedly.","\"S-Seniors...\"","His voice trembled.","\"Please... This humble one begs you. You don’t have to pay the full amount.\"","\"I-I can even give you a fifty percent discount.\"","Tears gradually welled up in his eyes.","\"Our restaurant is only a small business. If we lose this much money...\"","\"We’ll go bankrupt!\"","His body bent even lower.","There was no trace of dignity left.","He could only beg.","The surrounding customers quietly watched the scene.","Many clenched their fists, yet none dared step forward.","The Tianyu cultivators looked at one another before bursting into laughter.","One of them stepped forward.","His face was filled with contempt.","\"Bankrupt? What does that have to do with us?\"","He looked down at the kneeling manager as though looking at an insect.","\"You should be thanking us. It is your restaurant’s fortune that we chose to dine here.\"","The manager’s expression turned even paler.","\"S-Senior...\"","Before he could finish—","Bang!","The Tianyu Empire cultivator casually kicked him.","The manager’s frail body was sent tumbling several meters across the floor before crashing into a nearby table.","Plates shattered.","Blood trickled from the corner of his mouth.","\"You dare continue pestering us?\"","The Tianyu Empire cultivator sneered.","\"Know your place!\"","With that, the Tianyu delegation walked out of the restaurant as though nothing had happened.","The entire hall fell deathly silent.","Every customer stared at their departing backs.","Some were furious.","Some felt humiliated.","Others simply lowered their heads.","Not a single person dared stop them.","Even the Imperial Guards stationed outside merely watched silently.","Their fists clenched so tightly that veins bulged across their hands.","Yet in the end...","They still did nothing.","The Tianyu cultivators merely laughed louder.","To them...","This was exactly how the weak should behave.","Just then—","As the delegation arrogantly strode down the street, the cultivator leading them suddenly bumped into someone.","Thud!","The collision wasn’t particularly hard.","However, the Tianyu Empire cultivator’s eyes immediately became enraged.","His mood was already sour from the restaurant manager who dared demand money from him and now someone dared bump into him.","He slowly turned around.","He opened his mouth, preparing to shout.","\"You blind—\"","Slap!!","A crisp slap echoed throughout the entire street.","The Tianyu Empire cultivator’s words abruptly stopped.","His body spun violently through the air before crashing into a nearby stall.","Wood splintered.","Several tables collapsed.","Blood mixed with broken teeth scattered across the ground.","The bustling street instantly became silent.","Everyone froze.","An even angrier voice suddenly rang out.","\"Damn it! Who is blind enough to bump into this young master?\"","A handsome young man slowly withdrew his hand.","His luxurious white robes fluttered gently in the wind.","His expression was filled with obvious displeasure.","It was...","Bai Zihan!","He glanced at the dust-covered Tianyu cultivator lying on the ground before slowly shifting his gaze toward the rest of the delegation.","His eyes were cold.","\"You dare bump into this young master? You even dirtied my robes.\"","He casually brushed the sleeve of his robe before looking back at them.","\"Compensate me!\"","His voice was calm, yet it carried unquestionable dominance.","\"Otherwise...\"","A faint smile slowly appeared on Bai Zihan’s face.","\"...don’t even think about leaving this place unscathed.\""]},{"number":656,"title":"Chapter 656: A Slap Across the Tianyu Empire’s Face","paragraphs":["The Tianyu Empire cultivator slowly climbed to his feet.","His face was swollen.","Blood dripped from the corner of his mouth.","For a brief moment...","He simply stood there blankly.","(Who am I? Where am I?)","He was one of the strongest members of the Tianyu Empire delegation, an Immortal Ascension Realm cultivator.","Even if he had been caught completely off guard, he should never have been sent flying so effortlessly by a slap.","The surrounding Tianyu cultivators also wore expressions of disbelief.","An Immortal Ascension had been sent tumbling across half the street without the slightest ability to resist.","Only after several breaths did he finally recover.","The confusion in his eyes instantly transformed into boundless rage.","His expression twisted ferociously.","\"How dare you!\"","His furious roar echoed through the street.","\"Do you know who I am?!\"","Boom!","His Immortal Ascension aura erupted without reservation.","An overwhelming pressure swept across the surroundings.","Nearby cultivators hurriedly retreated.","Many ordinary citizens turned pale under the terrifying pressure.","The Tianyu cultivator took a step forward.","His eyes were filled with murderous intent as he glared at Bai Zihan.","\"You actually dared to attack me! I’ll—\"","Bai Zihan frowned.","His expression darkened.","Instead of showing the slightest fear, he became even angrier.","\"What? You still have the nerve to shout?\"","He pointed at the Tianyu cultivator with an expression full of righteous indignation.","\"You bumped into this young master first. And now you’re yelling at me?\"","The Tianyu cultivator was completely stunned.","Even the surrounding crowd watched everything with excitement.","After all, they had been suffering under these foreign delegations, and finally someone was putting them in their place.","Who here didn’t know the reputation of Bai Zihan?","Even if his recent achievements had cast Bai Zihan in a new light, who didn’t know about his previous behavior?","He was unreasonable, quick to anger, and if you caught his attention, one could only pray for their safety.","Everyone looked at Bai Zihan.","Then they looked at the Tianyu cultivator whose face was still swollen from a single slap.","No matter how they looked at it...","The one who had suffered seemed to be the Tianyu cultivator.","Yet Bai Zihan continued as though he had suffered an enormous injustice.","\"I was originally in a good mood today. But after being bumped into by trash like you...\"","\"My mood has completely been ruined.\"","He coldly stretched out a hand.","\"Compensation.\"","The Tianyu cultivator laughed from extreme anger.","\"Compensation? You still dare ask me for compensation?\"","Bai Zihan nodded matter-of-factly.","\"Naturally. You damaged this young master’s mental state, dirtied my robes, and wasted my precious time.\"","He casually looked at the Tianyu delegation.","\"I won’t make things difficult for you. Hand over a Heaven-Grade Artifact. I’ll consider this matter settled!\"","Silence!","Not only the Tianyu delegation, even the surrounding citizens were dumbfounded.","A Heaven-Grade Artifact?","Just because someone bumped into him?","Everyone stared blankly at Bai Zihan.","The Tianyu cultivators looked at one another.","For the first time in their lives, they felt as though they had met a true master.","They had spent the past several days bullying others.","Eating without paying.","Occupying inns.","Seizing cultivation rooms.","Throwing their weight around everywhere they went.","Yet compared to the young man before them, everything they had done suddenly seemed insignificant.","At most, they extorted some gold coins.","This fellow... was directly demanding a Heaven-Grade Artifact!","One merely had to know the value of such an item to understand how outrageous the request was.","Even within powerful empires, a Heaven-Grade Artifact was considered an extremely valuable treasure.","Who in their right mind would hand one over simply because of a minor collision?","Not to mention, it was Bai Zihan who clearly bumped into him.","The Tianyu cultivator trembled with rage.","His face alternated between red and green.","\"You...\"","He pointed at Bai Zihan.","\"You dare extort me?\"","Bai Zihan’s eyebrows immediately rose.","\"Extort?\"","His expression instantly turned cold.","\"So you’re saying... you have no intention of compensating me?\"","A dangerous smile slowly appeared on Bai Zihan’s face.","\"Very good! It seems words alone won’t solve this.\"","The Tianyu Empire cultivator laughed hysterically.","\"Hahaha!\"","His laughter echoed throughout the street.","He looked at Bai Zihan as though he were staring at a complete fool.","\"You want to solve this with force?\"","He slowly cracked his neck.","A cruel smile spread across his face.","\"Good! I also want to see exactly how you intend to solve this.\"","In his eyes, Bai Zihan had already dug his own grave.","An Immortal Ascension Realm expert was not someone a mere youth should provoke.","Regardless of his background, daring to challenge him in public was nothing short of courting death.","The other members of the Tianyu Empire delegation also revealed amused expressions.","Their earlier humiliation had left all of them seething with anger.","Now...","It seemed they finally had an opportunity to wash away that humiliation.","As long as they crippled—or even killed—this arrogant youth, no one would dare mock the Tianyu Empire again.","Several of them even folded their arms, already anticipating the upcoming battle.","However...","Just as the Immortal Ascension Realm cultivator was about to make his move, one of the elders standing behind the group suddenly narrowed his eyes.","His gaze remained fixed on Bai Zihan’s face.","A trace of uncertainty flashed across his expression.","Then...","His pupils suddenly contracted.","His expression changed drastically.","\"Chen Muyang!\"","His shout exploded through the street.","\"Stop!\"","The Immortal Ascension Realm cultivator, Chen Muyang, halted in confusion.","His face was still filled with anger.","Although he was dissatisfied at being interrupted, the one who had spoken possessed a higher status and greater strength than him.","Suppressing his temper, he turned around.","\"Elder Fu. What is the meaning of this?\"","His voice was still filled with obvious irritation.","\"I have already been humiliated. Why are you stopping me?\"","Elder Fu ignored his complaint.","Instead, his eyes remained fixed on the young man standing opposite them.","His expression became increasingly solemn.","After several breaths, he finally spoke.","\"...He is Bai Zihan.\"","The moment those three words fell...","The laughter instantly disappeared.","The smiles on everyone’s faces froze.","Even Chen Muyang’s expression stiffened.","\"Bai... Zihan?\"","Several members of the delegation instinctively repeated the name.","Although very few of them had ever seen Bai Zihan in person, every single one of them had heard his name.","Not only had he accomplished countless feats that seemed almost unbelievable, but he was also the genius who had defeated Feng Xuanye.","Feng Xuanye, who was considered the greatest genius of the Tianyu Empire and perhaps even the entire Eastern Region.","Bai Zihan was the very person who had defeated Feng Xuanye despite being less than half his age.","More importantly, before leaving the Tianyu Empire, they had all received strict instructions.","Under no circumstances were they to provoke Bai Zihan or anyone from the Bai Clan.","At least not before the various foreign delegations had fully assembled and joined forces.","The reason was simple.","Recent rumors regarding the Bai Clan were simply too shocking.","Rumors claimed that the Bai Clan possessed two Golden Immortal Realm experts.","Whether those rumors were true or false remained uncertain.","But even if they were exaggerated, the Bai Clan’s previously demonstrated strength was already terrifying enough.","Based on the Bai Clan’s previously demonstrated strength alone, even if the Tianyu Empire delegation fought together, they still would not be able to handle the Bai Clan.","For that reason, before departing, the higher-ups had repeatedly warned them.","Avoid conflict.","Do not provoke the Bai Clan.","Even if the Bai Clan provokes you first... endure it.","Wait until the other empires arrive before making any move.","Only after the various forces joined hands would they possess sufficient confidence.","Who would have thought...","The very person they had been repeatedly warned about would suddenly appear before them...","And even take the initiative to confront them.","Immediately, the expressions of the Tianyu Empire cultivators became extremely unsightly, especially Chen Muyang’s.","The rage on his face froze.","It was gradually replaced by helplessness.","And finally...","Reluctant acceptance.","His fists clenched tightly beneath his sleeves.","The veins on the back of his hands bulged visibly.","He wanted nothing more than to smash Bai Zihan into the ground.","Yet he did not dare.","The orders issued before leaving the Tianyu Empire echoed repeatedly in his mind.","Under no circumstances were they to provoke the Bai Clan.","Should he act now, he would not only ruin the Tianyu Empire’s plans but would also have to bear the consequences upon returning.","Thinking of the punishment awaiting him, Chen Muyang forcibly swallowed the anger burning within his heart.","He took a deep breath before coldly snorting.","\"Hmph! I’ll let you off this time.\"","His unwilling voice spread throughout the street.","The surrounding spectators were instantly stunned.","Many blinked in disbelief.","Over the past several days, these foreign cultivators had been nothing short of arrogant and overbearing.","Even when they were clearly in the wrong, they refused to yield even a single step.","Yet now...","Bai Zihan had slapped one of them in public.","Demanded a Heaven-Grade Artifact as compensation, and openly threatened them.","Despite all that, the Tianyu Empire delegation was actually backing down.","Many people could not help but secretly gasp.","\"This is Bai Zihan! Even the Tianyu Empire doesn’t dare offend him.\"","\"The Bai Clan’s reputation truly isn’t something ordinary people can compare to.\"","Quite a few citizens suddenly felt an indescribable sense of satisfaction.","Previously, they had been powerless against these foreign delegations.","No matter how much they were bullied, they could only endure.","Now...","The roles had completely reversed.","The Tianyu Empire delegation was now the one forced to swallow its anger.","Unable to retaliate.","Unable to vent.","Just like they themselves had been forced to do these past several days.","\"Heh?\"","Bai Zihan let out a disdainful chuckle.","\"You’ll let me off?\"","He looked at Chen Muyang as though he had just heard the greatest joke in the world.","\"Who do you think you are?\"","His gaze gradually turned cold.","\"I’ll say this one last time. Until you compensate this young master with a Heaven-Grade Artifact...\"","\"...don’t even think about moving an inch!\""]},{"number":657,"title":"Chapter 657: The Tianyu Empire Backs Down","paragraphs":["Bai Zihan stood with his hands behind his back.","His expression remained calm.","Yet there was not the slightest regard for the identities or cultivation of the people standing before him.","The Tianyu Empire cultivators’ expressions darkened even further.","At this moment, Elder Fu slowly stepped forward.","Unlike Chen Muyang, he still maintained his composure.","He cupped his fists slightly.","\"Young Master Bai. This matter was indeed our fault. My Tianyu Empire is willing to apologize.\"","\"I hope Young Master Bai can be magnanimous and forgive this offense.\"","His tone was neither servile nor arrogant.","Instead, it was extremely sincere.","After all, provoking the Bai Clan now would benefit no one.","Unfortunately, Bai Zihan merely glanced at him.","\"Magnanimous?\"","He chuckled.","\"I’m not.\"","Bai Zihan continued leisurely,","\"Since it was your fault, compensate me. Otherwise...\"","He pointed casually toward the street behind them.","\"None of you are leaving.\"","The atmosphere instantly became heavy.","Even Elder Fu’s expression gradually darkened.","He had already lowered his stance considerably yet Bai Zihan refused to give him even the slightest bit of face.","Still, he forcibly suppressed the anger in his heart.","After taking a deep breath, he spoke once more.","\"Young Master Bai. A Heaven-Grade Artifact is simply too precious. My Tianyu Empire is willing to compensate you with an Earth-Grade Artifact instead.\"","\"I hope Young Master Bai can let this matter end here.\"","The surrounding spectators could not help but gasp.","An Earth-Grade Artifact!","Although it could not compare to a Heaven-Grade Artifact, it was still an extremely precious treasure.","For most cultivators, obtaining even one Earth-Grade Artifact during their entire lifetime was already considered a tremendous fortune.","Using such an item merely as compensation for accidentally bumping into someone...","That was already an unimaginable concession.","Many people secretly felt that Elder Fu had already shown sufficient sincerity.","However, Bai Zihan shook his head with displeasure.","\"No! I said a Heaven-Grade Artifact. Not an Earth-Grade Artifact. If you cannot understand human language...\"","\"I don’t mind teaching you.\"","The smiles on the Tianyu Empire cultivators’ faces completely disappeared.","At this point...","Anyone could see that Bai Zihan was deliberately making things difficult for them.","He had no intention of accepting any compromise.","Chen Muyang could no longer endure it.","His eyes blazed with fury.","\"Bai Zihan!\"","His shout echoed throughout the street.","\"Don’t go too far! We are here to attend the coronation of the new Emperor! We are honored guests personally invited by His Majesty!\"","He stared directly at Bai Zihan.","His voice carried an unmistakable warning.","\"If you continue causing trouble for us, have you considered the consequences of offending your future Emperor?\"","The surrounding crowd instinctively held their breath.","Everyone understood the meaning behind Chen Muyang’s words.","He was using Yu Zidi’s name to pressure Bai Zihan.","If it were anyone else, they might truly have hesitated.","Unfortunately for him, the person standing before him was Bai Zihan.","As if he gave a damn about offending Yu Zidi, who, in his eyes, could be killed whenever he pleased.","Bai Zihan’s expression gradually turned impatient.","He looked at Elder Fu as though he were looking at an annoying fly.","\"I’ve already wasted enough time talking. I’ve decided. I’m done being civil.\"","Snap!","Bai Zihan casually snapped his fingers.","The crisp sound echoed throughout the street.","The next instant—","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","Several terrifying figures silently appeared around Bai Zihan.","The surrounding crowd was startled.","The expressions of the Tianyu Empire delegation changed dramatically.","Every newcomer radiated an incomparably powerful aura.","Earth Immortals!","Every single one of them was an Earth Immortal Realm expert.","Standing at the very front was an elderly man dressed in plain white robes.","His hands rested casually behind his back.","A leisurely smile hung on his face as though he were merely watching an entertaining play.","It was none other than Bai Ren.","Seeing Bai Ren appear, Bai Zihan casually pointed toward the Tianyu Empire delegation.","\"They refuse to compensate me. What do you think we should do?\"","Bai Ren chuckled.","His tone was calm, yet every word carried unquestionable dominance.","\"If Clan Leader says they should compensate, then they should compensate. If they refuse...\"","He slowly swept his gaze across the Tianyu Empire delegation.","The smile on his face remained unchanged.","\"...then they needn’t leave.\"","His voice was gentle.","Yet the meaning behind those words caused everyone’s hearts to tremble.","The other Bai Clan elders nodded without the slightest hesitation.","Their expressions remained completely indifferent.","It was as though surrounding the Tianyu Empire delegation was the most natural thing in the world.","Seeing this scene, Elder Fu’s pupils contracted.","He had originally believed the Bai Clan elders would at least persuade Bai Zihan to calm down.","Instead...","Not a single one of them questioned Bai Zihan’s actions.","They simply stood behind him without hesitation.","Elder Fu’s expression became increasingly grim.","He took a deep breath before speaking in a solemn voice.","\"Fellow Daoists, I hope the Bai Clan will think carefully. We represent the Tianyu Empire. This time, we have come as honored guests to attend the coronation of the Desolate Heaven Empire’s new Emperor.\"","\"If anything happens to us here...\"","He paused before continuing.","\"The Tianyu Empire will never let this matter rest.\"","His tone was no longer as polite as before.","The warning hidden within his words was unmistakable.","However...","Neither Bai Ren nor the other Bai Clan elders showed the slightest reaction.","It was as though they had heard nothing.","Outwardly, Elder Fu remained calm.","Inwardly, however, he was already extremely alarmed.","His gaze repeatedly swept across the Bai Clan experts.","The more he observed, the heavier his heart became.","The number of Earth Immortal Realm experts alone already far exceeded their own.","And then there was Bai Ren.","No matter how carefully Elder Fu tried to perceive him, he could not sense Bai Ren’s cultivation at all.","He was immediately reminded of the terrifying rumors that Grand Elder Bai Ren had already ascended to the Golden Immortal Realm.","Thinking of the rumors that had spread throughout the Eastern Region...","Rumors that the Bai Clan possessed two Golden Immortal Realm experts...","Cold sweat unconsciously appeared on Elder Fu’s back.","Moreover, even if Bai Ren were not a Golden Immortal Realm expert, the current lineup alone was already enough to overwhelm the Tianyu Empire delegation.","If both sides truly fought...","The outcome was obvious to everyone present.","The Tianyu Empire delegation would stand no chance.","Just as the atmosphere grew increasingly tense...","Another voice suddenly rang out from the crowd.","\"Fellow Daoists of the Bai Clan, there is no need to make matters so unpleasant.\"","Everyone instinctively turned toward the source of the voice.","A group of cultivators slowly approached from the end of the street.","\"The Vermillion Pill Empire!\"","Someone in the crowd immediately recognized the emblem.","Whispers instantly spread throughout the street.","\"They’re here!\"","\"This is going to become even more troublesome.\"","The Tianyu Empire delegation’s gloomy expressions immediately brightened.","A smile appeared on Elder Fu’s face.","The newcomers stopped a short distance away.","Leading them was an elderly man with white hair and sharp eyes.","Although his aura was restrained, no one dared underestimate him.","He calmly glanced between the Bai Clan and the Tianyu Empire before speaking.","\"Everyone has come to the Desolate Heaven Empire to attend His Majesty’s coronation. Why ruin the atmosphere over such a trivial misunderstanding?\"","His tone was gentle.","However, everyone present understood one thing.","The Vermillion Pill Empire had chosen to stand beside the Tianyu Empire.","The white-haired elder nodded slightly before turning back toward Bai Zihan.","\"Young Master Bai. Today’s matter should end here. The Tianyu Empire has already expressed its willingness to compensate you with an Earth-Grade Artifact.\"","\"That should be sufficient.\"","Several experts behind him slowly stepped forward.","It was a mix of Earth Immortal Realm and Immortal Ascension Realm experts.","Seeing this, the Tianyu Empire delegation immediately straightened their backs.","The confidence that had disappeared moments ago gradually returned.","With the Vermillion Pill Empire standing beside them, the disparity between the two sides no longer seemed so overwhelming.","Although the Bai Clan still possessed the advantage...","It was no longer an insurmountable one.","At least, that was what they believed.","Chen Muyang sneered inwardly.","(So what if it’s the Bai Clan? Now let’s see whether you still dare remain so arrogant.)","Many of the surrounding spectators also became nervous.","Just moments ago, it had seemed the Tianyu Empire delegation was completely cornered.","Now, with the arrival of the Vermillion Pill Empire...","The situation had changed yet again.","However...","Facing the additional experts...","Bai Zihan’s expression did not change in the slightest.","He merely glanced lazily at the newcomers before letting out a faint chuckle.","\"Who do you think you are to say what I should accept?\"","The white-haired elder frowned slightly.","Bai Zihan slowly swept his gaze across both delegations.","\"Are you planning to compensate this young master on their behalf? If not...\"","He casually folded his arms.","\"Then don’t interrupt while this young master is collecting his compensation.\"","His attitude was every bit as domineering as before.","There wasn’t the slightest intention of backing down.","The smile on the white-haired elder’s face gradually disappeared.","The expressions of the Vermillion Pill Empire experts also darkened.","They had personally stepped forward to mediate.","Yet Bai Zihan had rejected them without giving them the slightest bit of face.","The atmosphere instantly became even heavier.","One side was the Bai Clan.","The other consisted of both the Tianyu Empire and the Vermillion Pill Empire.","The confrontation that had originally involved only two forces had suddenly expanded.","The surrounding streets quickly became packed with spectators.","Even the Imperial Guards no longer dared approach.","Instead, they hurriedly dispatched messengers toward the Imperial Palace.","Such a disturbance was no longer something they were qualified to handle."]},{"number":658,"title":"Chapter 658: Two Empires? Beat them All!","paragraphs":["Seeing Bai Zihan remain completely unyielding even after the arrival of two imperial delegations...","The surrounding spectators could not help but inwardly gasp.","It wasn’t one or two clans that he was going against, but two entire empires.","Yet Bai Zihan was now facing both of them at the same time.","They represented two of the strongest empires in the Eastern Region.","Despite that, Bai Zihan showed not the slightest intention of giving them face.","Instead, his attitude became even more domineering.","It was as though the greater the pressure placed upon him, the more overbearing he became.","Many citizens could not help but admire him inwardly.","Only someone like Bai Zihan would dare act so recklessly before two imperial delegations.","On the opposite side, Elder Fu exchanged a glance with the white-haired elder from the Vermillion Pill Empire.","Neither of them spoke.","Yet both understood the meaning in each other’s eyes.","Bai Zihan had no intention of letting them leave peacefully.","Negotiation had completely failed.","The white-haired elder slowly stepped forward.","The smile on his face had long since disappeared.","He looked directly at Bai Zihan before speaking coldly,","\"It seems you do not know what’s good for you. Don’t blame us then.\"","Boom!","The white-haired elder no longer concealed his cultivation.","His Earth Immortal Realm aura erupted outward.","The surrounding buildings trembled violently.","Countless spectators hurriedly retreated in alarm.","At the same time, the experts behind him also stepped forward.","One after another, terrifying auras rose into the sky.","The Tianyu Empire delegation naturally did the same.","In an instant, dozens of powerful cultivators released their cultivation simultaneously.","The entire street seemed unable to withstand the overwhelming pressure.","The white-haired elder remained calm.","Since a clash seemed inevitable, he might as well use this opportunity to probe the Bai Clan’s true strength.","The recent rumors surrounding the Bai Clan had simply been too unbelievable.","Two Golden Immortal Realm experts?","He refused to believe such absurd claims.","Even if the rumors were true...","Surely the combined strength of the Vermillion Pill Empire and the Tianyu Empire would be enough to compete against the Bai Clan.","His eyes narrowed.","(Let’s see... just how strong your Bai Clan truly is.)","However, before anyone from the Bai Clan moved, Bai Ren casually took a single step forward.","His leisurely smile never disappeared.","He simply glanced at the two imperial delegations.","There wasn’t even the slightest fluctuation in his emotions.","Then...","Boom!","An indescribably terrifying pressure descended upon the entire street.","The moment Bai Ren released his aura, it felt as though the heavens themselves had suddenly collapsed.","The Earth Immortal Realm experts from both empires immediately felt an overwhelming pressure descend upon them.","Their expressions changed drastically.","The auras they had proudly released were instantly suppressed.","It was as though insignificant candles had encountered the blazing sun.","One by one, the Earth Immortal Realm experts involuntarily took several steps backward.","The white-haired elder’s pupils shrank violently.","His face instantly turned pale.","\"T-This is...\"","As an Earth Immortal himself, he understood better than anyone what this terrifying pressure represented.","This was not merely someone slightly stronger than him.","This was an existence that had completely surpassed his level.","A cold chill instantly spread through his entire body.","Golden Immortal...","Beside him, Elder Fu’s expression was no better.","Cold sweat continuously dripped down his forehead.","His legs trembled uncontrollably.","Although he desperately tried to maintain his composure, his body instinctively warned him of the danger before him.","The Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators fared even worse.","Many of their faces had already turned deathly pale.","Several weaker cultivators found themselves unable to even circulate their spiritual energy under Bai Ren’s overwhelming pressure.","Only the Earth Immortal Realm experts could remain standing.","Even then, their breathing had become noticeably heavier.","The earlier confidence displayed by the two imperial delegations had completely vanished without a trace.","Bai Zihan looked at the two imperial delegations with complete indifference.","Seeing their earlier arrogance disappear beneath Bai Ren’s pressure, he merely curled his lips.","He slowly shook his head.","\"What a disappointment.\"","Then, without another word, Bai Zihan casually waved his hand.","\"Beat them!\"","He ordered.","\"Yes, Clan Leader!\"","The Bai Clan elders answered almost simultaneously.","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","Without the slightest hesitation, they charged toward the two imperial delegations.","Boom!","The street instantly erupted into chaos.","However, the earth-shattering battle everyone had imagined never happened.","Instead, what unfolded before everyone’s eyes was an utterly one-sided beating.","Bang!","An Earth Immortal from the Tianyu Empire was sent crashing through several buildings with a single punch.","Boom!","A Vermillion Pill Empire elder was struck squarely in the face before being kicked into the ground.","Crack!","Another expert barely managed to raise his defensive artifact before it was shattered by a Bai Clan elder’s fist.","Miserable cries continuously echoed throughout the street.","The spectators stared with wide eyes.","No one had expected such an outcome.","This wasn’t a battle.","It was outright one sided bullying.","Bai Ren alone stood before the strongest experts from both empires.","He never even attacked seriously.","Simply by casually flicking his fingers, he was easily able to suppress his opponents.","Every attempt they made to resist was effortlessly crushed.","The remaining Bai Clan elders, meanwhile, no longer had any opponents worthy of concern.","With Bai Ren suppressing the strongest experts, the others naturally had an easy time.","Moreover, even without Bai Ren’s assistance, the Bai Clan elders still possessed overwhelming advantages.","After months of consuming high-grade pills and cultivating with the Bai Clan’s abundant resources, their strength had risen far beyond what ordinary Earth Immortals could compare to.","As for the Tianyu Empire delegation...","Although their combat strength was respectable, they were still inferior to the Bai Clan elders.","The Vermillion Pill Empire delegation fared even worse.","Their cultivation realms were undoubtedly high.","However, much of that cultivation had been accumulated through the empire’s abundant pills.","While their cultivation was certainly high, their combat ability was another matter entirely.","Against opponents of similar cultivation, they were naturally at a disadvantage.","Much less against the battle-hardened Bai Clan elders.","Bang!","\"Argh!\"","Another Vermillion Pill Empire elder was punched directly into the street, leaving behind a massive crater.","Chen Muyang was even more miserable.","His face was already swollen beyond recognition.","Every time he tried to stand, another Bai Clan elder would send him flying once more.","His entire body ached unbearably.","Seeing the situation spiraling completely out of control, Elder Fu hurriedly shouted,","\"Stop! We admit defeat! We were wrong! I will compensate you.\"","\"Today is the auspicious day of His Majesty’s ascension! If this fighting continues, it will be viewed as disrespect toward the future Emperor!\"","The white-haired elder from the Vermillion Pill Empire also shouted anxiously,","\"Young Master Bai! Please show mercy!\"","\"We are official delegations invited to attend the coronation! If this matter grows any larger, it will damage the dignity of the Desolate Heaven Empire itself!\"","\"Surely you don’t wish to be accused of disrupting the coronation!\"","Their voices were filled with urgency.","Gone was the arrogance they had displayed only moments earlier.","Now...","All they wanted was for the beating to end.","Unfortunately, Bai Zihan remained completely unfazed by their words.","\"They’re still talking.\"","He glanced at the Bai Clan elders.","\"It seems you haven’t beaten them hard enough.\"","\"Yes, Clan Leader!\"","The Bai Clan elders immediately understood.","Boom!","Their attacks became even fiercer.","\"AHHH!\"","Painful screams continuously rang throughout the street.","The surrounding spectators watched with numb expressions.","No matter how Elder Fu and the white-haired elder pleaded, Bai Zihan acted as though he had heard nothing.","Of course, Bai Zihan had no intention of killing them.","These people still had their uses.","However, a severe lesson was still absolutely necessary.","Thus, the beatings continued without mercy.","Only after both imperial delegations had been beaten into a thoroughly miserable state did the Bai Clan elders finally slow their attacks.","Just then—","\"STOP!\"","A thunderous shout echoed across the street.","Dozens of Imperial Guards rapidly rushed over.","Leading them was a middle-aged man clad in golden armor.","His imposing aura swept across the surroundings as he stepped forward.","It was none other than the Captain of the Imperial Guards.","The Captain of the Imperial Guards frowned deeply as his gaze swept across the scene before him.","The sight was truly miserable.","The once-proud delegations of the Tianyu Empire and the Vermillion Pill Empire were in complete disarray.","Many of their robes had been torn to shreds.","Several experts were covered in dust.","Quite a few had swollen faces and bruises covering their bodies.","Some were so badly beaten that they were almost beyond recognition.","The Captain could not help but inhale sharply.","He had not expected the Bai Clan to beat two imperial delegations into such a pitiful state.","Just how powerful was the Bai Clan currently?","Could they have surpassed the combined might of Desolate Heaven Empire as well?","The Captain couldn’t help but shudder at such thought."]},{"number":659,"title":"Chapter 659: Compensation Increased","paragraphs":["The moment Elder Fu and the white-haired elder noticed the arrival of the Imperial Guards, their eyes immediately lit up.","They hurriedly stepped forward.","\"Captain!\"","Elder Fu cupped his fists with an aggrieved expression.","\"We came to the Desolate Heaven Empire as honored guests to attend His Majesty’s coronation. Yet this is how your empire treats its guests?\"","The white-haired elder also spoke indignantly,","\"Your Empire personally invited us. Instead of protecting your guests, you’ve allowed us to be humiliated in broad daylight.\"","\"If word of this spreads... what will the various empires think of the Desolate Heaven Empire?\"","The Captain’s expression became even uglier.","Regardless of who was right or wrong, these people were still foreign delegations officially invited by the Imperial Court.","Allowing them to be beaten into this state would undoubtedly damage the empire’s reputation.","Suppressing the frustration in his heart, the Captain turned toward Bai Zihan.","For a brief moment, a trace of anger flashed through his eyes.","However, the moment he saw Bai Ren standing quietly behind Bai Zihan...","His expression immediately softened.","He knew exactly who he was facing.","Taking a deep breath, the Captain cupped his fists politely.","\"Clan Leader Bai, I ask that you please calm down.\"","His tone remained extremely courteous.","\"Today is a joyous occasion for the Desolate Heaven Empire. Our empire will soon welcome its new Emperor.\"","\"I hope Clan Leader Bai can show His Majesty some face and allow today’s matter to end here.\"","The surrounding spectators all looked toward Bai Zihan.","Most people felt that, after the Captain had personally intervened, Bai Zihan would surely back down.","After all, this was already giving the Imperial Court sufficient face.","However, Bai Zihan merely glanced at the Captain.","His expression remained as indifferent as ever.","\"Show him face?\"","He let out a faint chuckle.","\"Hehe, does Yu Zidi even deserve that?\"","His words caused countless people to suck in cold breaths.","The Captain’s smile stiffened.","For Bai Zihan to casually address the First Prince by his name was already a tremendous sign of disrespect, not to mention what he had just said.","It was now obvious to everyone that Bai Zihan did not care in the slightest about Yu Zidi, who was about to become the new Emperor.","The Captain wanted to reprimand Bai Zihan.","But he knew doing so would only escalate the situation further, which would ultimately ruin the First Prince’s plans.","Bai Zihan continued calmly as he casually pointed toward Chen Muyang.","\"He bumped into me and should compensate me.\"","The reason Bai Zihan gave was incredibly trivial compared to the enormous commotion he had caused.","The Captain naturally understood that Bai Zihan was deliberately making things difficult for them.","Still, he quickly calmed himself and nodded.","\"That is naturally reasonable. I believe both delegations are also willing to offer compensation.\"","The Captain only wanted to end this matter as quickly as possible.","Elder Fu and the white-haired elder immediately nodded repeatedly.","\"As long as this matter can end peacefully, we are willing to compensate.\"","They no longer wished to remain here for even another moment.","Elder Fu even thought that giving away one Heaven-Grade Artifact was preferable to continuing to deal with Bai Zihan.","Although anger surged within his heart, he secretly consoled himself.","Once the coronation was over and their plan was set into motion, not only would he recover the Heaven-Grade Artifact...","He would also exact revenge upon the Bai Clan.","Bai Zihan slowly nodded.","He raised four fingers.","\"Then I’ll make things simple. Four Heaven-Grade Artifacts, and I won’t pursue this matter any further.\"","The moment those words left his mouth...","Elder Fu, who had just been about to take out a Heaven-Grade Artifact, froze.","His outstretched hand stiffened in midair.","He blinked, wondering if he had heard incorrectly.","\"...Four?\"","Even the white-haired elder’s expression became blank for a moment.","Chen Muyang’s eyes widened in disbelief.","\"What? You previously said only one Heaven-Grade Artifact! How did it become four?\"","Bai Zihan looked at him as though the answer was obvious.","\"That was then. This is now.\"","He shrugged casually.","\"When this young master was being generous, you refused. So naturally, the compensation has increased.\"","His tone was completely matter-of-fact, as though it were the most reasonable thing in the world.","He then pointed toward the white-haired elder from the Vermillion Pill Empire.","\"As for the extra two Heaven-Grade Artifacts...\"","\"That’s because your Vermillion Pill Empire insisted on meddling in someone else’s business.\" You’ve also caused this young master considerable emotional distress.\"","The white-haired elder nearly coughed up a mouthful of blood.","Emotional distress?","What emotional distress?","From beginning to end, Bai Zihan had been the one beating them into the ground!","If anyone should be compensated for emotional distress...","It should have been them!","The surrounding spectators also wore strange expressions.","Many wanted to laugh but did not dare.","Others nearly choked trying to hold back their laughter.","Everyone knew Bai Zihan was clearly making things difficult for them.","Yet...","No one dared say a word.","After all...","The biggest fist made the rules.","And right now, the Bai Clan possessed the biggest fist.","The white-haired elder’s face turned ashen.","His voice became noticeably colder.","\"Young Master Bai. Isn’t this nothing more than blatant robbery?\"","\"We will never agree to such outrageous terms!\"","The moment he finished speaking—","Boom!","An overwhelming pressure suddenly descended upon him.","Bai Ren had not moved.","He merely glanced at the white-haired elder.","Yet his terrifying aura instantly focused entirely upon him.","The white-haired elder’s face changed dramatically.","His breathing stagnated.","His knees nearly buckled beneath the overwhelming pressure.","He staggered backward several steps before barely managing to steady himself.","Cold sweat instantly drenched his back.","He immediately shut his mouth.","Not daring to utter another word.","Beside him, Elder Fu’s expression became increasingly unsightly.","He inwardly cursed Bai Zihan countless times.","Yet faced with Bai Ren’s overwhelming strength, he could only suppress every trace of dissatisfaction.","After taking a deep breath, Elder Fu turned toward Chen Muyang.","\"Take it out!\"","Chen Muyang froze.","\"E-Elder Fu...\"","\"Take out your Heaven-Grade Artifact.\"","Elder Fu’s tone left no room for discussion.","\"It was your recklessness that caused today’s incident. You should bear part of the responsibility.\"","Chen Muyang’s face became incomparably ugly.","He possessed only a single Heaven-Grade Artifact, and now he had to give it away.","It had accompanied him for many years.","Giving it away was like cutting off a piece of his own flesh.","He inwardly felt utterly wronged.","In his opinion, it had clearly been Bai Zihan who bumped into him first before turning around to accuse him and demand compensation.","However, seeing Elder Fu’s unwavering gaze, he ultimately clenched his teeth.","With an expression full of unwillingness, he slowly retrieved the Heaven-Grade Artifact from his storage ring.","Elder Fu also gritted his teeth.","He took out another Heaven-Grade Artifact of his own.","Two Heaven-Grade Artifacts quietly floated before them.","His gaze then shifted toward the white-haired elder.","The meaning could not have been clearer.","The remaining two...","Naturally had to be provided by the Vermillion Pill Empire.","The white-haired elder’s face darkened to an unprecedented degree.","He had originally stepped forward to help the Tianyu Empire.","To mediate the conflict.","Yet now...","The Vermillion Pill Empire had somehow become one of the victims.","Not only had they failed to resolve the matter, they were now expected to hand over two Heaven-Grade Artifacts.","His expression became increasingly unsightly.","Several elders behind him also wore gloomy expressions.","Many of them could not help but cast dissatisfied glances toward the Tianyu Empire delegation.","(We came here to help you. And now we’re the ones paying the price?)","(If not for your people provoking Bai Zihan first, why would we have become involved in this mess?)","The more they thought about it, the more aggrieved they felt.","On the other side, the members of the Tianyu Empire delegation naturally understood Bai Zihan’s reasoning.","Originally, they had been the only ones involved.","At worst, they would probably have had to surrender one or perhaps two Heaven-Grade Artifacts.","However, the moment the Vermillion Pill Empire chose to interfere...","Bai Zihan had immediately doubled the compensation.","By Bai Zihan’s own words...","The additional compensation was for the Vermillion Pill Empire’s needless meddling.","From that perspective, the extra two Heaven-Grade Artifacts had nothing to do with the Tianyu Empire.","Naturally, they should be paid by the Vermillion Pill Empire.","For a brief moment, neither side was willing to speak.","The white-haired elder’s face twitched slightly.","He inwardly cursed Bai Zihan countless times.","Yet, under Bai Ren’s terrifying gaze, he ultimately swallowed every complaint.","Slowly, he reached toward his waist.","With obvious reluctance, he removed the Heaven-Grade defensive artifact he had worn for many years.","His fingers lingered on it for a long moment before he finally tossed it forward.","One Heaven-Grade Artifact.","Gone.","His heart bled.","Then he turned toward one of the Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators whom he disliked the most within the delegation.","\"Hand over your Heaven-Grade sword.\"","The old man’s expression immediately changed.","That Heaven-Grade sword was his greatest treasure.","He had obtained it only after countless years of effort.","Giving it away now... was no different from cutting out a piece of his own heart.","However, seeing the white-haired elder’s gloomy expression, he knew there was no room for refusal.","He also knew that if he stubbornly refused and forced the elder to choose someone else instead, that person would undoubtedly harbor deep resentment toward him.","After a long silence, he bitterly sighed.","With trembling hands, he slowly withdrew the Heaven-Grade sword from his storage ring.","The brilliant blade gleamed under the sunlight.","His face was filled with unwillingness as he reluctantly handed it over.","The white-haired elder accepted the sword without another word.","Soon, Four Heaven-Grade Artifacts floated quietly in midair.","The surrounding spectators stared at the four priceless treasures with wide eyes.","Even many Earth Immortal Realm experts swallowed involuntarily.","Four Heaven-Grade Artifacts...","Such wealth was enough to make countless major powers go mad with envy.","Yet today, they had all become compensation for a single collision."]},{"number":660,"title":"Chapter 660: Extorting Four Heaven-Grade Artifacts!","paragraphs":["The four Heaven-Grade Artifacts floated quietly before Bai Zihan.","With a casual wave of his sleeve, all four treasures disappeared into his storage ring.","Only then did a satisfied smile appear on his face.","\"See?\"","Bai Zihan clasped his hands behind his back and looked at the two imperial delegations.","\"If you were going to hand them over anyway, you should have done so from the beginning.\"","He sighed as though he were deeply disappointed in them.","\"But no... You insisted on getting yourselves beaten first.\"","He shook his head repeatedly.","\"Tell me. Was it worth it?\"","The members of the Tianyu Empire and Vermillion Pill Empire delegations almost coughed up blood.","Bai Zihan stood there lecturing them as though they had brought everything upon themselves.","Bai Zihan continued in a tone resembling that of an elder teaching juniors.","\"You people are still too impulsive. When encountering problems, you should learn to resolve them peacefully.\"","\"Violence isn’t the answer.\"","Hearing those words, countless people twitched involuntarily.","Violence wasn’t the answer?","Who was the one who had ordered, ’Beat them!’ only moments ago?","Yet not a single person dared point that out.","After all, the person speaking was Bai Zihan.","After lecturing them for quite some time, Bai Zihan finally nodded in satisfaction.","\"Fortunately, this young master has always been broad-minded and kind-hearted. I never like holding grudges.\"","He generously waved his hand.","\"Since you’ve sincerely compensated me, I’ll graciously forget everything that happened today.\"","The corners of Elder Fu’s mouth twitched violently.","Forget?","From beginning to end, they had been the ones beaten black and blue.","Now Bai Zihan was acting as though he were the victim showing mercy.","Before Elder Fu could say anything, Bai Zihan suddenly smiled warmly.","\"Since we’re all heading to the Imperial Palace anyway, why don’t we travel together? We can chat along the way and build friendships.\"","The smiles on Elder Fu and the white-haired elder instantly froze.","The two of them almost instinctively took a step backward.","\"No need!\"","Elder Fu rejected the proposal without the slightest hesitation.","\"Our Tianyu Empire delegation still has other matters to attend to. We’ll head to the palace ourselves.\"","The white-haired elder nodded repeatedly.","\"The Vermillion Pill Empire is the same. We won’t trouble Clan Leader Bai.\"","The speed of their refusal left everyone speechless.","It was as though they feared Bai Zihan would suddenly change his mind and demand another Heaven-Grade Artifact if they stayed another moment.","Without waiting for Bai Zihan’s reply, Elder Fu immediately cupped his fists.","\"We’ll take our leave!\"","As soon as he finished speaking, he hurriedly led the Tianyu Empire delegation away.","The white-haired elder moved even faster.","Almost as though fleeing, he led the Vermillion Pill Empire experts in the opposite direction.","In the blink of an eye, both imperial delegations had disappeared from the street.","The surrounding spectators watched their retreating figures with peculiar expressions.","Who would have imagined...","Two mighty imperial delegations would one day flee from someone as though avoiding a plague.","Bai Zihan watched them leave before clicking his tongue in disappointment.","\"What a pity. I thought we could become great friends.\"","The Captain of the Imperial Guards silently complained inwardly.","(Friends? What kind of friends extort Heaven-Grade Artifacts?)","Fortunately, those two delegations had escaped quickly enough.","Otherwise, who knew what excuse Bai Zihan would come up with next?","Suppressing the thoughts in his heart, the Captain stepped forward and respectfully cupped his fists.","\"Clan Leader Bai. The coronation ceremony is about to begin. I ask that you make your way to the Imperial Palace as soon as possible.\"","Although his tone remained respectful, there was a trace of urgency hidden within it.","He truly hoped Bai Zihan would head straight to the palace.","If he continued wandering through the capital...","The Captain genuinely feared that the remaining imperial delegations might also become victims of Bai Zihan’s \"compensation.\"","Bai Zihan nodded casually.","\"Very well! This young master was planning to head there anyway.\"","With that, he waved his hand.","\"Let’s go!\"","Surrounded by Bai Ren and the Bai Clan elders, Bai Zihan leisurely walked toward the Imperial Palace, leaving behind a street full of stunned spectators who would likely remember today’s absurd spectacle for the rest of their lives.","***","At the Imperial Palace!","The Imperial Palace had long since been decorated with expensive decor.","Dragon carvings and phoenix sculptures adorned every hall, radiating imperial majesty.","Countless palace guards stood motionless on either side of the grand avenue leading toward the ceremonial plaza.","Their expressions were solemn.","Today, the Desolate Heaven Empire would welcome its new Emperor.","Naturally, this was an event that attracted countless powerful factions.","The enormous ceremonial plaza was already bustling with guests.","Delegations from every major empire, powerful clans, prestigious sects, and renowned merchant associations had already begun taking their seats.","Everywhere one looked...","Powerful auras intertwined throughout the palace grounds.","Many experts quietly observed the newcomers while secretly evaluating the strength of every faction present.","From time to time, another delegation would arrive through the palace gates.","Each arrival drew the attention of everyone nearby.","\"They’re from the Azure Cloud Empire.\"","\"The representatives of the Heaven Sword Sect have also arrived.\"","Quiet discussions spread throughout the plaza.","However, before long, another commotion arose near the palace entrance.","\"The Tianyu Empire has arrived!\"","\"The Vermillion Pill Empire is here as well!\"","Many people immediately turned toward the entrance.","Two imperial delegations slowly walked into the palace.","The powerful auras of numerous Immortal Ascension Realm and Earth Immortal Realm experts spread throughout the surroundings.","Their arrival immediately attracted countless gazes.","However, after only a brief glance, many people’s expressions became rather strange.","Although the two delegations tried their best to maintain their dignity, their faces were extremely gloomy.","It was as though every single one of them had just swallowed an entire basket of sour apples.","Not only that, several experts still had swollen cheeks.","Others had black eyes.","Some even walked with a noticeable limp despite trying to conceal it.","Although they had already consumed healing pills, the injuries inflicted by the Bai Clan were not something that could disappear completely within such a short period of time.","The sharp-eyed experts present noticed everything.","\"...\"","A brief silence followed.","Then someone quietly laughed.","\"Hahaha... Brother Chen, what happened to your face?\"","A cultivator from another empire looked at Chen Muyang with obvious amusement.","\"Weren’t you perfectly fine when you entered the capital a few days ago?\"","Another elder smiled.","\"Could it be that the Tianyu Empire encountered some terrifying demonic beast outside the city?\"","Someone immediately shook his head.","\"What kind of demonic beast could beat an entire imperial delegation into this state?\"","The surrounding guests chuckled.","Many of them deliberately lowered their voices yet cultivators at their level naturally heard every single word.","Chen Muyang’s face darkened even further.","His fists clenched tightly.","If not for the Imperial Palace being the venue of today’s ceremony, he would already have exploded in anger.","The white-haired elder from the Vermillion Pill Empire was no better.","His expression remained gloomy throughout.","Every time someone glanced toward the Heaven-Grade defensive artifact that had once hung from his waist, his heart began bleeding once again.","The atmosphere around the two delegations was incomparably oppressive.","No one within either group had any intention of speaking.","Before the discussions could continue much longer, another announcement rang through the palace.","\"The Bai Clan has arrived!\"","The entire plaza suddenly fell silent.","Countless heads immediately turned toward the entrance.","Compared to the arrival of the two imperial delegations, the Bai Clan’s appearance caused an even greater stir.","Bai Zihan slowly walked through the palace gates with his hands clasped behind his back.","Behind him followed Bai Ren and the Bai Clan elders.","Each step they took seemed calm and unhurried.","Yet the invisible pressure they radiated caused many experts to unconsciously become serious, especially Bai Ren.","Although he completely restrained his aura, no one dared underestimate him.","After all, the recent rumors surrounding the Bai Clan had spread throughout the entire Eastern Region.","Golden Immortal Realm experts!","Whether true or false, no one was willing to gamble their lives finding out.","Many powerful experts immediately rose to greet them.","\"Greetings, Clan Leader Bai.\"","\"Clan Leader Bai, it has been a long time.\"","\"Hahaha! Congratulations on the Bai Clan’s recent prosperity.\"","One after another, Clan leaders and sect masters took the initiative to greet Bai Zihan.","Even other Empire delegations showed remarkable courtesy.","None of them dared display the slightest arrogance.","After all, the Bai Clan’s current influence was no longer what it had once been.","Their terrifying military strength alone was already enough to make countless factions think twice.","More importantly, they also possessed the support of the Mu Clan.","Not far away, Mu Qingyuan and the Mu Clan elders had already arrived.","The Mu Clan’s current reputation had likewise reached unprecedented heights.","Since producing a Grade Seven Grandmaster Alchemist, their influence had expanded dramatically throughout the Eastern Region.","Countless factions had attempted to establish closer ties with them over the past several months.","Some wished to purchase pills, others hoped to form alliances.","Many even offered astonishing prices simply to secure future cooperation.","Yet, no matter who came.","No matter what conditions they offered.","Mu Qingyuan always gave the same answer.","\"If it concerns cooperation or any significant transaction, discuss it with the Bai Clan.\"","Those simple words had shocked countless powerful factions.","Everyone understood their meaning.","Despite the Mu Clan’s unprecedented prestige...","Despite now possessing a Grade Seven Grandmaster Alchemist...","The Mu Clan still willingly placed the Bai Clan first.","They were openly acknowledging the Bai Clan’s position.","No one present believed Mu Qingyuan had been forced into such a decision.","If anything, it only demonstrated just how deep the relationship between the two clans had become.","As Bai Zihan entered the ceremonial plaza, countless gazes followed him.","Some were filled with admiration.","Some with fear.","Others with undisguised curiosity.","Yet among the Tianyu Empire and Vermillion Pill Empire delegations, the expressions on everyone’s faces became incomparably ugly.","Especially after seeing Bai Zihan calmly accepting greetings from every direction as though nothing had happened earlier.","The corners of Chen Muyang’s eyes twitched violently.","He silently swore to himself.","(Enjoy your arrogance while you still can...)","(Once the coronation ends...)","(Everything will change!)"]},{"number":661,"title":"Chapter 661: The Storm at the Coronation","paragraphs":["Bai Zihan slowly swept his gaze across the enormous ceremonial plaza.","His eyes calmly passed over one powerful faction after another.","Some were familiar faces.","Others, he had never seen before.","Every so often, someone would respectfully nod toward him.","Bai Zihan merely acknowledged them with a faint nod before shifting his attention elsewhere.","Still, there was no Imperial Family within sight.","No empress or queen and obviously no Yu Qingya or Yu Feiyan.","He continued surveying the plaza.","Before long, his eyes landed upon a familiar figure.","A beautiful woman dressed in blue stood quietly beside the delegation of the Falling Star Empire.","Her posture was straight, her expression vigilant.","It was Mingzhe, the personal bodyguard of Empress Sun Yaoqing.","Ever since Sun Yaoqing had successfully ascended the throne of the Falling Star Empire, he had maintained contact with them.","The Falling Star Empire would occasionally send intelligence regarding their Empire.","However, none of them concerned the mysterious organization Bai Zihan had been searching for.","That hidden force remained as elusive as ever.","Still, maintaining ties with the Falling Star Empire had never been a bad investment.","After all, under Sun Yaoqing’s rule, the empire had undergone tremendous changes.","She had introduced numerous reforms that bridge the inequality between noble and commoners.","Of course, those very reforms also kept her incredibly busy.","She had entrusted Mingzhu with representing the Falling Star Empire.","Without another thought, Bai Zihan walked toward their delegation.","Seeing him approach, Mingzhu immediately stood up.","She respectfully cupped her fists.","\"Clan Leader Bai!\"","There wasn’t the slightest trace of arrogance in her demeanor, only genuine respect.","To both her and the Falling Star Empire, Bai Zihan was no ordinary ally.","Without his assistance, Sun Yaoqing would never have seized the throne so smoothly.","More importantly, when the Demonic Cultivator Chong Sheng had threatened the empire, it had been Bai Zihan who had ultimately resolved the crisis.","They also helped them when negotiating with the Mu Clan for the pills.","As a result, their Empire is flourishing compared to before.","The favor he had shown the Falling Star Empire was simply too great.","Not to mention, the Bai Clan’s current strength had already become terrifying enough that no empire dared treat them lightly.","Bai Zihan smiled faintly before returning the greeting.","\"Commander Mingzhu. I trust everything has been well in the Falling Star Empire?\"","Mingzhu nodded.","\"Thanks to Clan Leader Bai’s previous assistance, everything has been progressing smoothly. The reforms Her Majesty introduced have already begun producing remarkable results.\"","Bai Zihan nodded in satisfaction.","\"Well, that’s good.\"","After exchanging a few pleasantries, Bai Zihan suddenly stepped half a pace closer.","His voice became almost inaudible as he whispered something in Mingzhu’s ear.","Mingzhu’s eyes widened in surprise and then bowed thankfully.","\"Many thanks for informing me, Clan Leader Bai!\"","With that, Bai Zihan turned around and leisurely walked back toward the Bai Clan’s seating area.","Bai Ren and the other elders quietly followed behind him.","Soon, Bai Clan members took their seats.","The moment Bai Zihan sat down, countless hidden gazes once again converged upon him.","Yet Bai Zihan ignored every single one of them.","The atmosphere within the ceremonial plaza gradually became solemn.","The quiet discussions that had filled the surroundings slowly died away.","One after another, the guests returned to their seats.","Even the experts who had been secretly observing one another withdrew their gazes.","Everyone understood.","The coronation was about to begin.","A deep, ancient bell suddenly rang throughout the Imperial Palace.","Dong!","The sound echoed across the capital like rolling thunder.","It was followed by a second...","Then a third...","Dong! Dong! Dong!","Nine consecutive bell chimes reverberated through heaven and earth, signifying the arrival of the empire’s most sacred ceremony.","At the same time, hundreds of palace attendants lined both sides of the grand avenue.","Imperial Guards stood like statues, their spears pointed toward the heavens.","Their movements were perfectly synchronized.","Moments later, an elderly eunuch stepped onto the towering ceremonial platform.","His sharp voice spread throughout the plaza.","\"His Imperial Highness, the First Prince...\"","\"Yu Zidi!\"","As his announcement echoed through the palace, majestic music filled the air.","The grand palace gates slowly opened.","Countless gazes instantly turned toward the entrance.","A young man dressed in a magnificent golden imperial robe slowly walked forward.","Nine golden dragons were embroidered upon his robes, each one seemingly alive beneath the sunlight.","A purple-gold crown rested upon his head.","His expression was calm.","Every step he took was steady and dignified.","Behind him followed numerous members of the Imperial Family, civil officials, military generals, and palace attendants.","There were also the queens and the Empress.","The entire procession exuded unparalleled imperial majesty.","\"The coronation is finally beginning!\"","Quiet whispers spread throughout the crowd.","Many representatives from the various empires rose to their feet as a gesture of courtesy.","Yu Zidi continued walking until he reached the center of the ceremonial platform.","There, a magnificent golden throne stood upon a raised dais.","Above it fluttered the imperial banner of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","However, Yu Zidi did not immediately ascend the throne.","Instead, he turned toward the heavens.","His expression became solemn.","The elderly eunuch once again raised his voice.","\"The coronation ceremony...\"","\"Begins!\"","Immediately afterward, another group of palace attendants stepped forward carrying an ancient golden altar.","The altar was carved with countless mysterious runes.","At its center rested a jade tablet bearing the names of the previous emperors of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Yu Zidi slowly approached the altar.","Taking three sticks of incense from a nearby attendant, he lit them before respectfully bowing toward the ancestral tablet.","One bow...","Two bows...","Three bows...","After completing the rites, he carefully placed the incense into the bronze censer before the altar.","The elderly eunuch loudly proclaimed,","\"His Imperial Highness pays homage to the imperial ancestors!\"","\"May the imperial lineage prosper for ten thousand generations!\"","The surrounding officials immediately bowed.","\"May the empire prosper for ten thousand generations!\"","Their voices merged into one, shaking the entire palace.","The atmosphere became increasingly solemn.","After paying respects to the imperial ancestors, Yu Zidi turned toward the towering throne.","Step by step...","He ascended the golden stairs.","Every movement drew the attention of countless spectators.","Once he reached the summit, he slowly turned around.","His gaze swept across the entire ceremonial plaza.","Representatives from countless empires...","Prestigious sects...","Powerful clans...","Merchant associations...","All had gathered beneath his eyes.","The elderly eunuch took a scroll adorned with golden dragon patterns before loudly announcing,","\"By the will of Heaven and the blessings of the imperial ancestors...\"","\"Today, the First Prince, Yu Zidi shall inherit the Imperial Throne of the Desolate Heaven Empire!\"","Thunderous applause immediately erupted throughout the ceremonial plaza.","Many guests politely clapped in congratulations.","Thunderous applause echoed throughout the ceremonial plaza.","Many guests rose to their feet and offered their congratulations.","Everything seemed to be proceeding exactly as planned.","However, just as the elderly eunuch was about to continue the ceremony—","A cold, commanding voice suddenly echoed across the palace.","\"Stop!\"","The single word resounded like thunder.","The applause abruptly ceased.","Everyone instinctively turned toward the voice.","Countless eyes widened.","Another group had arrived.","Walking at the front were two stunning women.","One was dressed in elegant azure robes, her temperament graceful yet imposing.","The other wore crimson robes that radiated nobility and authority.","They were none other than the Fourth Princess, Yu Qingya and the Ninth Princess, Yu Feiyan.","Behind them stood an imposing army of experts.","The uniforms of the Crimson Thunder Palace fluttered in the wind.","Experts from the Frost Lily Pavilion stood with cold expressions.","The Heaven Suppression Sect had likewise dispatched numerous elders.","Alongside them were representatives from several powerful clans and sects who had openly chosen to stand behind the two princesses.","The moment they entered, the atmosphere throughout the ceremonial plaza instantly became suffocating.","Anyone with discerning eyes could tell at a glance, these people had not come to congratulate Yu Zidi.","\"They’re here...\"","\"They actually came.\"","\"I knew today’s coronation wouldn’t proceed so smoothly.\"","Whispers immediately spread throughout the crowd.","Representatives from the various empires quietly exchanged glances.","Everyone understood.","The true battle for the throne was finally beginning.","On the ceremonial platform, Yu Zidi quietly looked toward the entrance.","Surprisingly, there was neither anger nor panic on his face.","Instead, a faint smile slowly appeared.","It was as though he had already expected this outcome.","Or perhaps, he had been waiting for it all along.","He leisurely descended a few steps from the throne before smiling warmly.","\"Fourth Sister!\"","\"Ninth Sister!\"","\"You’ve finally arrived.\"","His tone remained as gentle and courteous as ever.","Anyone unfamiliar with the situation might have mistaken them for siblings meeting after a long separation.","His smile widened.","\"Are you here to congratulate this elder brother on today’s coronation?\"","The entire plaza fell silent.","Everyone stared at the three royal siblings.","Yu Qingya’s beautiful face immediately turned cold.","She had long since grown sick of Yu Zidi’s hypocritical appearance.","Always smiling.","Always courteous.","Always pretending to be a benevolent elder brother.","Yet behind that smiling face, countless schemes and conspiracies lurked in the shadows.","\"Hmph!\"","Yu Qingya let out a cold snort.","\"Drop the act, Yu Zidi.\"","Her voice was filled with unconcealed disdain.","\"I’m already tired of seeing that fake smile of yours.\"","Yu Zidi merely smiled without saying anything.","Seeing his expression, Yu Qingya’s eyes grew even colder.","She took a step forward.","Her clear voice echoed throughout the ceremonial plaza.","\"You...\"","\"Are not worthy of becoming Emperor!\"","The imperial officials immediately erupted into outrage.","\"Preposterous!\"","An elderly minister stepped forward, his face flushed with anger.","\"How dare you utter such rebellious words!\"","Another military general glared at Yu Qingya.","\"Your Highness! Even if you are a princess, we cannot allow such disrespect toward His Majesty!\"","A civil official pointed angrily toward the two princesses.","\"Today is the Desolate Heaven Empire’s most sacred ceremony!\"","\"Yet you dare create trouble before the representatives of countless empires?\"","\"Are you trying to make the Desolate Heaven Empire a laughingstock?\"","Another elder shouted furiously,","\"You are disgracing the Imperial Family before the entire Eastern Region!\"","\"Do you realize the consequences of your actions?\"","One accusation after another echoed throughout the palace.","Many imperial officials glared at Yu Qingya and Yu Feiyan with undisguised hostility.","Yet...","Neither princess showed the slightest intention of retreating.","Yu Qingya merely looked at them with cold eyes.","While beside her, Yu Feiyan remained completely silent."]},{"number":662,"title":"Chapter 662: The Battle for the Imperial Throne","paragraphs":["Before the imperial officials could continue their condemnation, several women seated behind the imperial family slowly rose to their feet.","They were the queens of the late Emperor.","Standing at the very front was the Empress Dowager, her face filled with displeasure.","She looked coldly at Yu Qingya and Yu Feiyan.","\"Enough!\"","Her voice carried unquestionable authority.","\"This is the coronation of the new Emperor. You are both daughters of the Imperial Family.\"","\"Do not make a spectacle of yourselves before the distinguished guests of the Eastern Region.\"","One of the senior queens also stepped forward.","\"Yu Qingya. You’ve gone too far.\"","\"Today is the empire’s most important ceremony. Even if you have grievances, this is neither the time nor the place.\"","Another queen shifted her gaze toward Yu Feiyan.","Unlike the others, her eyes carried unconcealed contempt.","\"So you’ve finally dared to show yourself.\"","\"We thought you had at least learned your place after hiding for so many years.\"","Her words grew increasingly sharp.","\"You are still the same timid little girl.\"","\"Don’t think that gathering a few followers gives you the qualifications to compete for the throne.\"","Another queen sneered.","\"Know your place.\"","\"You’re nothing more than an insignificant princess.\"","\"Don’t force us to teach you palace etiquette again.\"","Their voices became increasingly oppressive.","Years of living within the imperial palace had naturally cultivated an imposing aura.","In the past, such pressure alone would have been enough to scare shy Yu Feiyan.","Almost instinctively, Yu Feiyan’s delicate body trembled slightly.","It was an involuntary reaction born from years of oppression within the palace.","She had endured their ridicule and suppression since childhood.","Those memories were not so easily erased.","However, just as the invisible pressure was about to descend upon her—","A slender hand gently reached out.","It stopped before Yu Feiyan.","Standing before her was the ordinary-looking attendant who had accompanied her into the palace.","She lowered her head respectfully.","Yet the moment she stepped forward, the oppressive atmosphere surrounding Yu Feiyan instantly disappeared without a trace.","Her expression remained calm from beginning to end.","From his seat, Bai Zihan quietly watched the scene unfold.","His gaze lingered on the attendant for only a brief moment before the corners of his lips curved upward ever so slightly.","Others might not recognize her but he naturally did.","The attendant was none other than Qin Lingxiao.","As for the young woman standing behind her, that was the real Yu Feiyan.","Bai Zihan quickly understood Qin Lingxiao’s intentions.","Originally, she had always disguised herself as Yu Feiyan.","However, today was different.","This was the final stage of the struggle for the throne.","No one could guarantee that Yu Zidi had not prepared methods to verify Yu Feiyan’s identity.","After everything that had happened between the Imperial Family and the Bai Clan, it would not have been strange if Yu Zidi had already begun suspecting something.","If Qin Lingxiao continued impersonating Yu Feiyan and her disguise was exposed, their entire plan could collapse at the final moment.","Instead, bringing the real Yu Feiyan while personally acting as her attendant was undoubtedly the safest choice.","If anyone attempted to verify Yu Feiyan’s identity, they would only find the genuine princess.","Furthermore, should Qin Lingxiao ultimately need to eliminate Yu Zidi herself, doing so as an attendant would attract far less political backlash than if the act were committed by Yu Feiyan.","In every aspect, this arrangement was far more advantageous.","Bai Zihan inwardly nodded.","But of course, along with the advantages, there were also disadvantages.","For one, if Yu Feiyan was killed, which would be much easier, then she no longer could take her identity and use them.","Well, it wasn’t a big disadvantage as she could take the identity of Yu Qingya but then again, Yu Qingya might also get killed.","On the opposite side, Yu Qingya paid no attention whatsoever to the queens’ accusations.","She merely glanced at them before letting out a cold laugh.","\"Petty tricks.\"","She looked directly at Yu Zidi.","\"Stop hiding behind these women.\"","Her voice was filled with ridicule.","\"And as for you all...\"","She slowly swept her gaze across the queens.","\"A group of old women who know nothing beyond eating, sleeping, and squabbling within the inner palace. You should stop interfering in matters beyond your understanding.\"","The queens’ expressions instantly froze.","The next moment, their faces became livid with rage.","\"Impudent!\"","\"Yu Qingya!\"","\"How dare you speak to your elders in such a manner!\"","\"You’ve become utterly lawless!\"","One queen pointed at her with trembling fingers.","\"No wonder you dare rebel against your elder brother.\"","\"You don’t even possess the most basic respect for your elders!\"","The entire plaza instantly became even noisier.","Many guests secretly exchanged glances.","No one had expected Yu Qingya to insult the queens so directly.","On the ceremonial platform, Yu Zidi merely sighed softly.","His face was filled with helplessness.","\"Fourth Sister...\"","He smiled bitterly.","\"Must your words be so hurtful? I’ve always treated you as my beloved younger sister.\"","\"If there is something I’ve done wrong... you may tell me. I’ll gladly correct myself.\"","His expression was sincere enough to move many of the unaware officials.","He slowly spread his hands.","\"But if you say I’m unfit to become Emperor...\"","\"Then tell everyone...\"","\"Who do you believe is worthy?\"","Without the slightest hesitation, Yu Qingya immediately turned toward the crimson-robed figure beside her.","She raised her hand.","\"I nominate the Ninth Sister, Yu Feiyan.\"","\"She is the one truly qualified to inherit the throne of the Desolate Heaven Empire.\"","The plaza erupted into an uproar.","\"What nonsense!\"","\"Yu Feiyan?\"","\"She’s utterly incompetent!\"","\"How could someone like her possibly govern an empire?\"","\"She has neither achievements nor prestige.\"","\"What qualifications does she possess to compete with His Majesty?\"","One of the queens looked at Yu Feiyan with complete disdain.","\"Don’t forget your own identity.\"","\"Your bloodline is already tainted.\"","\"You are merely the daughter of a lowly servant.\"","\"An illegitimate daughter. The late Emperor was already generous enough to acknowledge your existence and grant you the title of Princess.\"","\"You should have been grateful. Instead, you’ve become greedy enough to covet the Imperial Throne?\"","Her voice grew increasingly cold.","\"You truly don’t know your place.\"","Several imperial officials immediately echoed her words.","\"An illegitimate princess has no right to inherit the throne!\"","\"Her bloodline isn’t even worthy of entering the ancestral temple!\"","\"Allowing her to remain within the Imperial Family was already an act of supreme benevolence!\"","\"She should be thanking the Imperial Family instead of pushing her luck!\"","One accusation after another rang throughout the ceremonial plaza.","The contempt in their voices was undisguised.","To them, Yu Feiyan had never been a legitimate contender.","Yu Qingya’s face turned ice-cold.","She looked at the queens and the imperial officials with unconcealed disgust.","\"You old women...\"","Her voice echoed throughout the ceremonial plaza.","\"Your opinions mean nothing.\"","She slowly swept her gaze across the officials standing beneath the ceremonial platform.","\"And you old fossils as well. You’ve spent your entire lives flattering those in power.\"","\"You’ve watched corruption spread across every corner of the Desolate Heaven Empire.\"","\"You’ve watched innocent people suffer while filling your own pockets yet now you dare lecture us about qualifications?\"","Her eyes burned with fury.","\"The Desolate Heaven Empire has become what it is today because of people like you!\"","The expressions of the imperial officials immediately darkened.","\"Impudent!\"","\"How dare you slander the court!\"","\"Utter nonsense!\"","Several ministers shouted angrily.","However, Yu Qingya ignored every one of them.","She raised the longsword in her hand.","\"It doesn’t matter whether you acknowledge Ninth Sister or not.\"","\"Because today...\"","Her voice suddenly became incomparably domineering.","\"We shall purify the Desolate Heaven Empire of its filth!\"","Boom!","An overwhelming aura erupted from Yu Qingya’s body.","Her cultivation surged toward the heavens.","The spiritual energy throughout the entire ceremonial plaza instantly became violent.","At almost the same moment—","Boom!","The experts behind the two princesses no longer concealed themselves.","Terrifying auras rose one after another.","The Crimson Thunder Palace experts stepped forward first.","Lightning crackled around their bodies.","The surrounding air trembled violently beneath their immense cultivation.","Next, the Frost Lily Pavilion revealed its strength.","Elegant women dressed in snow-white robes slowly walked forward.","Cold qi spread across the plaza.","The surrounding temperature rapidly dropped.","Thin layers of frost even began forming upon the stone floor.","Then the Heaven Suppression Sect released its own terrifying pressure.","Several Earth Immortal Realm experts stood side by side.","Their expressions were solemn as they stared toward Yu Zidi’s faction.","Behind them, experts from numerous clans and sects also stepped forward.","From his seat, Bai Zihan simply watched everything unfold.","His fingers lightly tapped the armrest of his chair.","His expression remained calm from beginning to end.","It was as though the confrontation before him had nothing to do with him whatsoever.","Likewise, the Bai Clan elders remained completely relaxed.","Not a trace of nervousness could be seen on any of their faces.","Their indifference has made many covert observers secretly more vigilant.","Meanwhile, the representatives from the various empires who had been completely unaware of today’s events immediately became flustered.","Many delegation leaders hurriedly transmitted voice messages to their subordinates.","Some secretly activated defensive artifacts.","Others quietly prepared escape routes.","No one wished to become collateral damage in a battle involving multiple Earth Immortal Realm experts.","Several merchant association representatives had already begun calculating which direction offered the fastest route out of the ceremonial plaza.","The atmosphere became increasingly chaotic.","Unlike them, the Tianyu Empire delegation remained remarkably calm.","Elder Fu slowly narrowed his eyes.","A cold smile appeared on his face.","The humiliation they had suffered earlier flashed through his mind.","His gaze instinctively drifted toward Bai Zihan.","(Enjoy yourself while you still can. Soon...)","(You’ll discover today’s humiliation won’t go unanswered.)","Beside them, the white-haired elder from the Vermillion Pill Empire also slowly stepped forward.","The Heaven-Grade defensive artifact that had accompanied him for centuries was already gone, causing his heart to ache every time he remembered Bai Zihan.","His expression was gloomy beyond comparison.","\"Everyone.\"","He quietly transmitted his voice.","\"Prepare yourselves.\"","One after another, the experts of both empires silently began circulating their qi.","The peaceful coronation ceremony had already come to an end.","What followed would determine the fate of the entire Desolate Heaven Empire!"]},{"number":663,"title":"Chapter 663: The New Emperor’s Last Shield?","paragraphs":["The experts behind Yu Qingya and Yu Feiyan instantly erupted into motion.","The Earth Immortal Realm experts shot into the sky like streaks of light.","Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators followed closely behind.","Terrifying Qi swept across the entire Imperial Palace.","Meanwhile, the queens who had been acting so arrogantly only moments earlier instantly lost all composure.","Seeing numerous countless cultivators charging toward the ceremonial platform, their faces turned deathly pale.","Other than their status, their cultivation was meager. Even a Nascent Soul cultivator could kill them with a single finger.","One queen shrieked,","\"P-Protect us!\"","Another queen no longer maintained her noble bearing.","She hurriedly retreated behind the Imperial Guards.","\"Guards! What are you standing there for?!\"","\"Stop them!\"","The Empress Dowager’s complexion also changed drastically.","She had never expected Yu Qingya to truly attack.","\"Quickly! Protect me!\"","Fear appeared in the eyes of those women who had spent decades enjoying luxury within the palace.","Their previous arrogance had vanished completely.","All that remained was fear and panic.","Standing upon the ceremonial platform, Yu Zidi quietly observed everything.","However, contrary to most people’s expectations, not only did he show no fear, the corners of his mouth slowly lifted into a faint smile.","(Excellent!)","He had actually hoped Yu Qingya and Yu Feiyan would be the first to attack.","Only then...","Would they appear to be the aggressors before the countless witnesses gathered today.","Now, the entire Eastern Region had personally witnessed the two princesses launching an assault during the coronation.","Even if he personally strangled them to death, it would still be considered righteous.","Yu Zidi slowly shook his head.","\"Fourth Sister...\"","\"Ninth Sister...\"","\"You’ve disappointed me.\"","His voice carried genuine regret.","\"So, in the end, you’ve chosen to rebel.\"","He inwardly sneered.","(You really believed my only support consisted of a few military commanders and several insignificant noble clans?)","(How naïve! To think you’d launch an assault so confidently...)","At the forefront of Yu Feiyan’s forces, two Earth Immortal Realm experts burst forward.","One hailed from the Heaven Suppression Sect.","The other was from the Crimson Thunder Palace.","Capturing Yu Zidi...","Such a contribution would undoubtedly be the greatest achievement of today’s battle.","If they could accomplish it, then not only would their sects be spared, but they might also be heavily rewarded.","Without hesitation, the two accelerated once more.","Their terrifying cultivation instantly locked onto Yu Zidi.","Boom!","The surrounding space trembled violently.","The Heaven Suppression Sect elder respectfully cupped his fists while continuing forward.","\"Your Highness, I’m afraid you’ll have to come with us.\"","Although his actions were decisive, his tone remained polite.","The Crimson Thunder Palace elder also smiled faintly.","\"We mean no disrespect. If possible, we hope Your Highness won’t resist.\"","As if they were only following the orders of the Ninth Princess.","The two reached out simultaneously.","Their immense qi sealed the surrounding space.","Yu Zidi seemed completely trapped.","Many spectators subconsciously held their breath.","Could it be...","The battle would end before it had truly begun?","However, just as the two Earth Immortals were about to reach Yu Zidi, a calm voice suddenly echoed across the plaza.","\"That’s enough!\"","The next instant, a figure silently appeared before Yu Zidi.","No one saw how he had arrived.","It was as though he had always been standing there.","An elderly man dressed in plain gray robes calmly folded his hands behind his back.","The attacks of the two Earth Immortals came to an abrupt halt.","An invisible force completely blocked their advance.","Neither could move another inch.","Their expressions changed dramatically.","\"You...\"","The gray-robed elder calmly looked at them.","\"Don’t think you can kill the Emperor before me!\"","The entire ceremonial plaza instantly fell silent.","A moment later, countless cries of astonishment erupted.","\"Royal Ancestor Xuande!\"","\"It’s actually Ancestor Xuande!\"","\"He intervened!\"","Even the imperial officials looked stunned.","Everyone in the Desolate Heaven Empire knew of Xuande.","He was the strongest backing of the Imperial Family and was regarded as the Royal Ancestor, having served generations of the Yu Imperial Family.","However, what surprised them wasn’t his presence, but the fact that he never interfered in any affairs apart from matters concerning the survival of the Imperial Family.","As for the struggle for the throne, he neither cared nor supported any prince or princess.","Yet now, he had personally stepped forward.","And he was protecting Yu Zidi, which clearly showed his stance.","The Heaven Suppression Sect elder’s expression became solemn.","The Crimson Thunder Palace elder also frowned deeply.","Both knew that Xuande wasn’t a weak opponent.","Even if they outnumbered him, taking him down would not be an easy task.","However, neither of them showed the slightest intention of retreating.","After all...","Not far behind them, Frost Lily Pavilion’s Earth Immortal Ancestor, Su Binglan, slowly stepped forward.","Her white robes fluttered gently despite the absence of any wind.","An icy aura silently spread throughout the surroundings.","The temperature of the entire ceremonial plaza noticeably dropped.","Xuande was definitely more powerful individually, but could he stop three Earth Immortals?","The three Earth Immortals quietly formed a triangle around Xuande.","More importantly, their greatest advantage had never been these three Earth Immortals.","It was their overall strength.","Behind them stood the combined forces of the Crimson Thunder Palace, Heaven Suppression Sect, Frost Lily Pavilion, and numerous allied clans.","Their overall military strength vastly surpassed Yu Zidi’s visible forces.","Even if Xuande managed to stall the three of them, how long could Yu Zidi’s remaining subordinates survive?","Sooner or later, he would inevitably fall into their hands.","As for the chance that other guests might help Yu Zidi, they didn’t think they would.","Most of the major clans and sects that had not chosen a side until now had deliberately remained neutral throughout the entire struggle for the throne.","There was no reason for them to suddenly throw themselves into such a dangerous conflict at the very last moment.","As for the delegations from the other empires, that possibility was even less likely.","Why would they interfere in the internal throne struggle of another empire?","If anything, many would probably be delighted to see the Desolate Heaven Empire descend into civil war.","The greater the chaos, the more advantageous it would be for the surrounding empires.","Behind Yu Feiyan, Qin Lingxiao still made no move.","She quietly stood in the guise of an ordinary attendant, her gaze calmly sweeping across the battlefield before finally settling upon one particular group.","The Bai Clan!","Among everyone gathered within the Imperial Palace, if there was anyone capable of overturning today’s situation through sheer strength alone, it was undoubtedly the Bai Clan.","Even Xuande, she wasn’t overly concerned about.","With her strength, it would only take a few moves to defeat him.","However, if the Bai Clan elders interfered, then her strength would amount to nothing.","Therefore, she wanted to see what the Bai Clan’s attitude was.","Fortunately, the Bai Clan remained seated.","They didn’t display the slightest intention of intervening.","Seeing this, Qin Lingxiao secretly relaxed slightly.","Based on everything she had observed, the Bai Clan had never shown any interest in involving themselves in the Imperial Family’s struggle for the throne.","As long as no one provoked them, they generally remained spectators.","However, a trace of regret still flashed across Qin Lingxiao’s eyes.","She couldn’t help but think back to the incident involving Long Haotian.","Back then, she had impulsively demanded that Bai Zihan hand Long Haotian over to her.","That single decision had unnecessarily created friction between herself and the Bai Clan.","Had she not made that demand, she would have felt far more confident proceeding with today’s plan.","Even knowing that the Bai Clan possessed Golden Immortal Realm experts, she could have acted without much concern.","Now, although the Bai Clan appeared content to watch from the sidelines, there was no telling when they might decide to make a move against Yu Feiyan, believing her to be the same person who had previously invaded the Bai Clan.","So, for now, since her force could easily take on Yu Zidi, Qin Lingxiao decided to watch queitly from the sideline.","And indeed, even without Qin Lingxiao making a move, the battle was heavily in Yu Feiyan’s favor.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Terrifying explosions continuously echoed across the Imperial Palace.","At the center of the battlefield, Xuande was being completely suppressed.","Facing the combined attacks of three Earth Immortal Realm experts, he had no opportunity to retaliate.","He was forced into a purely defensive position.","Boom!","Another powerful attack slammed into his Heaven-Grade defensive artifact.","The golden barrier shook violently.","Xuande’s face turned increasingly pale.","The only reason he had not been defeated was because he had completely abandoned offense.","Like a turtle retreating into its shell, he hid behind his defensive artifact, pouring all of his Qi into maintaining its protective barrier.","Every attack he received further depleted his Qi.","It was only a matter of time before his defenses collapsed.","Meanwhile, the rest of the battlefield was no better.","Although Yu Zidi had dispatched a large number of Imperial Guards and loyal military forces to hold the line...","They stood no chance against the combined might of the three top sects.","The Heaven Suppression Sect.","The Crimson Thunder Palace.","The Frost Lily Pavilion.","Backed by numerous allied clans, they steadily overwhelmed the imperial forces.","One defensive line after another collapsed.","Imperial Guards fell in large numbers.","The once orderly formation rapidly descended into chaos.","The battlefield was completely one-sided.","To the countless spectators watching from afar, Yu Zidi had already lost."]},{"number":664,"title":"Chapter 664: Yu Zidi allies","paragraphs":["Indeed, In one swift sweep, Yu Zidi’s forces were pushed onto the defensive.","The once orderly imperial army was steadily collapsing under the relentless assault of Yu Feiyan’s force.","Every passing moment brought heavier casualties.","Victory seemed to be slipping further and further away.","However, Yu Zidi’s expression remained remarkably composed.","He was not without other preparations.","Quietly, he circulated his Qi and transmitted a message toward two distant groups seated among the honored guests.","Clan Leader Li!","Clan Leader Zhao!","Right now, he wanted to keep those foreign delegations a secret when dealing with the Bai Clan.","The Bai Clan...","That was the true obstacle standing before his path to becoming Emperor.","As for Yu Feiyan’s forces, Yu Zidi had never considered them worthy of deploying every one of his hidden cards.","The Li-Zhao Alliance alone should have been more than sufficient to suppress them.","After all, both clans had brought numerous experts today.","Combined with their allied forces, turning the tide of the battlefield should have been an effortless task.","Thus, to Yu Zidi, this battle was already as good as won.","His real concern had never been Yu Feiyan.","It was Bai Zihan.","It was the Bai Clan.","Only after eliminating every one of Yu Feiyan’s supporters would he reveal his remaining strength and force the Bai Clan into submission.","That had always been his plan.","However, several breaths passed.","Nothing happened.","Yu Zidi’s brows furrowed almost imperceptibly.","There was no reply.","Neither Clan Leader Li nor Clan Leader Zhao responded to his transmission.","Even more strangely, neither clan showed the slightest intention of joining the battle.","Their experts remained quietly seated.","Their expressions were calm, as though the fierce battle unfolding before them had nothing to do with them at all.","Yu Zidi’s pupils narrowed slightly.","(What’s going on? Why aren’t they moving?)","He immediately sent another transmission.","Still...","Silence!","The Li Clan remained motionless.","The Zhao Clan did the same.","Not a single cultivator stepped forward.","Yu Zidi immediately sent another transmission.","\"Clan Leader Li! Clan Leader Zhao! Why are you still sitting there? Move at once!\"","His voice carried an unmistakable hint of urgency.","Yet...","Nothing.","No response.","No acknowledgment.","The Li Clan remained seated.","The Zhao Clan did the same.","It was as though they had never received his message.","Yu Zidi’s calm expression finally began to crack.","His brows gradually knitted together.","He couldn’t understand it.","Everything had already been agreed upon beforehand.","The Li-Zhao Alliance was supposed to intervene the moment the situation became unfavorable.","Why were they refusing to move now?","Did something happen?","Or...","Had they changed their minds?","Yu Zidi instinctively rejected the latter possibility.","Neither clan had any reason to betray him.","They would only profit after helping him, becoming even more prominent clans.","He gritted his teeth.","Although countless questions filled his mind, he no longer had the luxury of finding answers.","Yu Feiyan’s forces were advancing at an alarming pace.","The Imperial Guards were steadily being pushed backward.","Several defensive lines had already collapsed.","If this continued, the enemy would soon reach the ceremonial platform itself.","There was no longer any point in hiding his remaining trump cards.","With a gloomy expression, Yu Zidi circulated his qi once more.","This time, his spiritual transmission spread toward every foreign delegation present within the Imperial Palace.","The Tianyu Empire!","The Vermillion Pill Empire!","The Azure Cloud Empire!","And every other empire that had secretly reached an agreement with him.","\"Everyone... it’s time.\"","Upon receiving Yu Zidi’s message, the various foreign delegations subtly frowned.","Their expressions became somewhat displeased.","This...","Was not what they had agreed upon.","Their agreement with Yu Zidi had always been clear.","Their purpose was to help suppress the Bai Clan.","Not to involve themselves in Yu Zidi’s struggle against Yu Feiyan.","After all, the internal conflict of the Desolate Heaven Empire had little to do with them.","Helping Yu Zidi seize the throne was merely a convenient byproduct.","The Bai Clan...","That was their true objective.","Several delegation leaders exchanged silent glances.","Although dissatisfied, none openly refused.","Before leaving their respective empires, each of them had received the same instruction from their emperors.","Cooperate with Yu Zidi as much as possible...","...provided it did not harm their own interests.","Now that Yu Zidi had personally requested their assistance, ignoring him outright was no longer an option.","The various foreign delegations quickly reached a decision.","If Yu Zidi fell here, then every arrangement they had painstakingly made over the past months would become meaningless.","Their true objective had always been the Bai Clan.","However, without Yu Zidi ascending the throne, they would lose their greatest ally within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Although reluctant...","They had little choice but to act.","Whoosh!","One figure after another rose into the air.","Experts from the Tianyu Empire...","The Vermillion Pill Empire...","The Azure Cloud Empire...","And the other allied empires slowly stepped onto the battlefield.","The sudden appearance of so many powerful experts immediately attracted everyone’s attention.","However, none of them immediately attacked.","Instead, Elder Fu stepped forward first.","He cupped his fists toward Yu Qingya and Yu Feiyan.","\"Princesses.\"","His tone was calm and courteous.","\"This is an internal affair of the Desolate Heaven Empire. Our various empires have no desire to interfere.\"","The white-haired elder from the Vermillion Pill Empire also nodded.","\"Indeed. We merely hope both sides can give us some face. After all, today was meant to be a joyous occasion.\"","\"If possible, postpone your conflict until after the foreign delegations have departed. Otherwise...\"","He paused briefly.","\"We may have no choice but to intervene in order to preserve order.\"","His words immediately made many onlookers nod inward.","That sounded perfectly reasonable.","After all...","Why should foreign guests become involved in another empire’s internal struggle?","From their perspective, it was only natural to ask both sides to stop fighting until they had left.","Many spectators even felt the foreign delegations were acting quite fairly.","However...","Yu Qingya merely let out a cold scoff.","\"Give you face?\"","Her eyes scanned the various foreign experts with undisguised contempt.","\"Stop pretending. We already know about the shady deal between all of you and Yu Zidi.\"","The moment those words fell...","Many expressions changed slightly.","However, the delegation leaders remained astonishingly calm.","Not a trace of panic appeared on their faces.","Elder Fu frowned slightly.","\"Fourth Princess. I don’t understand what you’re talking about.\"","The white-haired elder also calmly shook his head.","\"It seems you’ve misunderstood something. We merely wish to prevent unnecessary bloodshed.\"","The others likewise wore expressions of complete innocence.","Anyone who did not know the truth would genuinely believe they were impartial mediators.","Yu Qingya’s eyes turned colder.","\"You really are shameless. But it doesn’t matter.\"","She had never expected them to confess it in public.","After all, doing so would only disgrace both themselves and Yu Zidi.","Without wasting another word on them, Yu Qingya suddenly raised her hand.","\"Continue the attack! Anyone who stands in our way...\"","\"Is an enemy!\"","Boom!","At her command, Yu Feiyan’s forces erupted once more.","The Earth Immortal Realm experts charged forward without the slightest hesitation, treating the newly arrived foreign experts no differently than Yu Zidi’s own forces.","Foreign delegations frowned upon hearing Yu Qingya’s uncompromising response.","They had already offered a way for both sides to back down gracefully.","Yet Yu Qingya had rejected it without the slightest hesitation.","Since that was the case...","There was nothing more to say.","Boom!","One terrifying aura after another erupted.","The strongest experts from every foreign delegation immediately soared into the sky.","The Tianyu Empire moved first.","The Vermillion Pill Empire closely followed.","Then came the Azure Cloud Empire.","One Earth Immortal...","Two...","Three...","The number continued to rise.","Each imperial delegation had dispatched four or five Earth Immortal Realm experts for the coronation.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Heaven and earth trembled.","The terrifying pressure generated by so many Earth Immortal Realm experts instantly swept across the Imperial Palace.","In a flash, the entire situation had been overturned.","Originally, Yu Feiyan’s side possessed the absolute advantage.","But now...","Everything was different.","The Heaven Suppression Sect.","The Crimson Thunder Palace.","The Frost Lily Pavilion.","Together, they possessed only three Earth Immortal Realm experts.","Even including Xuande, there were merely four Earth Immortals present on the battlefield.","Meanwhile...","The foreign delegations alone had dispatched well over ten Earth Immortal Realm experts.","The difference in strength was simply too enormous.","It wasn’t something that could be bridged through strategy or courage.","Many people subconsciously looked toward Yu Feiyan’s camp.","Could they withstand such a terrifying lineup?","The answer was obvious.","No!","They couldn’t.","Against more than ten Earth Immortal Realm experts...","Three Earth Immortals stood no chance whatsoever.","The advantage Yu Feiyan had painstakingly established vanished almost instantly.","The smiles on Yu Zidi’s face, however, became increasingly brilliant.","Although the Li-Zhao Alliance had unexpectedly refused to act, the foreign delegations had ultimately stepped forward.","With such an overwhelming disparity in strength...","He could no longer imagine any possible way for Yu Feiyan to turn the tables."]},{"number":665,"title":"Chapter 665: The Foreign Empires Enter the Fray","paragraphs":["The sudden reversal caused the expressions of everyone on Yu Feiyan’s side to change.","The overwhelming pressure of more than ten Earth Immortal Realm experts instantly descended upon the battlefield.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Terrifying auras shook the heavens.","The newly arrived foreign experts immediately intercepted the Heaven Suppression Sect, the Crimson Thunder Palace, and the Frost Lily Pavilion’s Earth Immortals.","The battle balance had completely shifted.","Many of Yu Feiyan’s subordinates clenched their fists.","They had never expected the foreign delegations to openly support Yu Zidi.","Although they had suspected some form of cooperation, witnessing more than ten Earth Immortals personally stepping onto the battlefield still left their hearts sinking.","\"This is bad!\"","\"We’re completely suppressed!\"","\"If this continues...\"","Their morale visibly wavered.","Even Yu Qingya’s expression became somewhat grim.","The foreign empires had hidden their intentions well.","The moment they made their move, they had completely overturned the battlefield.","However...","Unlike everyone else, Qin Lingxiao remained remarkably calm.","There wasn’t the slightest ripple in her eyes.","Slowly, she raised one hand.","Her indifferent voice quietly echoed.","\"It’s your turn.\"","The moment her words fell, five figures silently emerged from different corners of the Imperial Palace.","None of them had appeared through the main entrance.","It was as though they had materialized out of thin air.","Each wore black robes.","Each had their face completely concealed beneath dark masks.","Not a single strand of hair was visible.","The only thing the crowd could sense was the terrifying pressure radiating from their bodies.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Five overwhelming Earth Immortal Realm auras erupted simultaneously.","The entire Imperial Palace trembled violently.","\"What?!\"","\"Another five Earth Immortals?!\"","\"Where did they come from?!\"","Countless spectators cried out in disbelief.","Even the foreign delegation leaders’ expressions changed.","Without giving anyone time to react, the five masked Earth Immortals shot into the sky.","Like five black meteors, they directly intercepted the advancing foreign experts.","Boom!","The heavens exploded.","Violent shockwaves swept across the battlefield as Earth Immortal clashed against Earth Immortal.","The terrifying collision instantly tore apart layers of clouds above the Imperial Palace.","The entire sky seemed on the verge of collapsing.","The five masked Earth Immortals immediately engaged the foreign experts in fierce combat.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","One terrifying collision after another echoed across the skies.","Qi surged wildly as dazzling techniques illuminated the heavens.","The foreign experts’ expressions gradually turned solemn.","As they exchanged blows with the masked figures, the same question arose in each of their minds.","(Who are they?)","Before arriving at the Desolate Heaven Empire, their empires had thoroughly investigated every major faction.","Every Earth Immortal Realm expert within the empire had been carefully documented.","The Royal Ancestor Xuande.","Su Binglan of the Frost Lily Pavilion.","The Earth Immortals of the Heaven Suppression Sect.","The Crimson Thunder Palace.","Even several hidden old monsters from the major clans.","They knew them all.","So who were these five masked Earth Immortals?","From the technique they used, they couldn’t find anything out.","The uncertainty only made foreign experts more cautious.","However, despite their shock, they had little choice.","Since they had already stepped onto the battlefield, there was no turning back.","Boom!","Another violent collision shook the heavens as the Earth Immortals fought with increasing intensity.","Meanwhile, the smile on Yu Zidi’s face finally disappeared.","His expression gradually stiffened.","He had believed that once the foreign delegations intervened, suppressing Yu Feiyan’s forces would be effortless.","After all, more than ten Earth Immortal Realm experts were enough to overwhelm almost any force in the Eastern Region.","Yet...","Who could have imagined, Yu Feiyan still possessed another hidden force.","Five Earth Immortal Realm experts!","Yu Zidi’s heart gradually sank.","Just how many hidden cards did Yu Feiyan still possess?","His fists unconsciously tightened.","Without hesitation, he once again circulated his Qi.","His spiritual transmission shot toward the Li Clan and Zhao Clan.","\"Clan Leader Li!\"","\"Clan Leader Zhao!\"","\"Move now! If this continues, everything will be ruined!\"","Several breaths passed.","Still...","Nothing.","No reply.","No movement.","The Li Clan remained seated.","The Zhao Clan remained equally motionless.","Not a single expert rose from their seats.","\"...\"","Yu Zidi’s face darkened completely.","\"Dammit!\"","He could no longer suppress his anger.","With a loud shout, he slammed his foot against the ceremonial platform.","Bang!","The solid stone beneath him instantly shattered into countless pieces.","His expression became incomparably gloomy.","He thought that he has prepared everything meticulously","Yet at the most critical moment, Li and Zhao Clan, upon whom he had placed considerable expectations, had completely ignored his calls for help.","They had betrayed him at this critical moment.","Although Yu Feiyan had revealed another five Earth Immortal Realm experts, the disparity in strength had not completely disappeared.","The foreign delegations still possessed the numerical advantage in terms of Earth Immortals.","With well over ten Earth Immortal Realm experts on the battlefield, they continued to outnumber Yu Feiyan’s side.","However...","Numbers alone did not determine everything.","The five masked Earth Immortals were far from ordinary.","Together with the Heaven Suppression Sect elder, the Crimson Thunder Palace elder, and Su Binglan, they firmly held the foreign experts at bay.","Neither side could gain a decisive advantage in a short period of time.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Violent explosions continuously echoed across the heavens as Earth Immortal fought Earth Immortal.","Meanwhile, the battle below raged just as fiercely.","Although Yu Feiyan’s side was at a disadvantage in terms of Earth Immortal Realm experts, their forces overwhelmingly outnumbered Yu Zidi’s in every other realm.","Immortal Ascension Realm.","Great Ascension Realm.","Void Refinement Realm.","Everywhere across the battlefield, Yu Feiyan’s troops steadily pressed forward.","The Imperial Guards desperately resisted, but under the combined assault of the three great sects and their allied forces, they were gradually forced backward.","For a time...","Neither side could truly claim the upper hand.","The battle had entered a complete stalemate once again.","...","Standing quietly behind Yu Feiyan, Qin Lingxiao calmly surveyed the battlefield.","Her indifferent gaze slowly swept across the various factions before finally settling upon one group.","The Bai Clan!","Bai Zihan remained leisurely seated in his chair.","One hand rested casually upon the armrest while the other held a teacup.","His expression was calm.","It was as though the fierce battle unfolding before him was nothing more than an entertaining performance.","Not once had he shown the slightest intention of intervening.","Seeing this, Qin Lingxiao silently relaxed.","At least for now, the Bai Clan had no intention of participating in this conflict.","Her gaze then slowly shifted away.","It landed upon the ceremonial platform.","Yu Zidi!","By now, the once heavily guarded platform had become noticeably emptier.","Most of the Imperial Guards had already rushed onto the battlefield.","Even Xuande was occupied fighting three Earth Immortals.","Only a handful of loyal guards still remained beside Yu Zidi.","Qin Lingxiao’s eyes narrowed slightly.","(Now is the perfect opportunity.)","There was no need to continue wasting time in this chaotic battlefield.","As long as Yu Zidi died, everything would immediately come to an end.","Without Yu Zidi, no one else possessed the legitimacy or influence to compete for the throne.","Yu Feiyan would naturally become the rightful ruler of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Without another word, Qin Lingxiao turned toward one of the Immortal Ascension Realm experts beside her.","\"Protect Her Highness.\"","The cultivator immediately cupped his fists.","\"Yes!\"","Receiving the order, he immediately stepped closer to Yu Feiyan, vigilantly guarding her surroundings.","The next moment, Qin Lingxiao disappeared.","There wasn’t the slightest fluctuation of Qi.","No sound.","No warning.","She simply vanished from where she stood.","When she appeared again, she was already standing before Yu Zidi.","Only a few steps separated them.","Without the slightest warning, Qin Lingxiao struck.","There was no flashy technique.","No earth-shattering martial art.","She simply raised a single finger.","Yet the instant it descended, space itself seemed to distort.","An invisible force pierced straight toward Yu Zidi’s forehead with terrifying speed.","It was a strike meant to kill.","The few Imperial Guards beside Yu Zidi hadn’t even realized what was happening.","Only when the attack was already inches away did Yu Zidi’s instincts scream in warning.","His pupils shrank to pinpoints.","(Not good!)","Boom!","Just before Qin Lingxiao’s finger reached him, a brilliant golden barrier suddenly erupted around Yu Zidi.","Countless profound runes rapidly spread across the translucent shield.","A terrifying defensive aura burst forth.","Bang!","Qin Lingxiao’s strike landed squarely upon the barrier.","The entire Imperial Palace trembled violently.","Crack! Crack!","Spiderweb-like fractures instantly spread across the golden barrier.","Within a single breath, the Heaven-Grade defensive artifact reached its limit.","Boom!","The barrier exploded into countless fragments of golden light that scattered throughout the sky.","Although it shattered, it had successfully blocked Qin Lingxiao’s fatal strike.","Yu Zidi was blasted backward several dozen meters before barely managing to stabilize himself.","His face had turned completely pale.","Cold sweat drenched his back.","Only now did he clearly see the person who had attacked him.","His eyes widened in horror.","\"You...! Yu Feiyan’s attendant...\"","He had finally realized it.","The attendant who had remained beside Yu Feiyan all this time was the one who had nearly taken his life.","Had it not been for the Top-Grade Heaven-Grade defensive artifact he took from the treasury, he would already be a corpse.","The thought alone sent chills through his entire body.","Meanwhile, Qin Lingxiao looked at the shattered fragments of the barrier with slight surprise.","A Top-Grade Heaven-Grade defensive artifact!","Even within the Central Glorious Continent, such treasures were far from common.","Still, her expression quickly returned to indifference.","It changed nothing.","Without anyone capable of stopping her, Yu Zidi was merely delaying the inevitable.","Whether it took one strike or ten, the outcome would remain exactly the same."]},{"number":666,"title":"Chapter 666: A Threat Against the Bai Clan","paragraphs":["Qin Lingxiao’s expression remained indifferent.","The instant the golden barrier shattered, she stepped forward once more.","There was no hesitation.","Whoosh!","Her figure blurred.","Another killing strike descended.","Yu Zidi’s face turned deathly pale.","He no longer cared about conserving his treasures.","With a wave of his sleeve, another defensive artifact flew into the air.","A jade mirror.","Buzz!","A brilliant silver barrier unfolded before him.","Bang!","Qin Lingxiao’s attack landed.","Crack!","The mirror instantly split in half before exploding into countless fragments.","However...","It had bought Yu Zidi another breath of time.","Without waiting for Qin Lingxiao’s next strike, Yu Zidi frantically took out another treasure.","A crimson talisman.","Boom!","A blazing wall of flames erupted between the two.","Qin Lingxiao merely waved her sleeve.","The flames dispersed instantly.","Bang!","The talisman disintegrated into ashes yet another treasure was destroyed.","Yu Zidi’s hands trembled.","Another artifact appeared.","Then another.","Every single one was an extremely precious defensive treasure.","Normally, any one of them would be enough to make countless major powers fight to the death.","Now...","Yu Zidi shattered them one after another without the slightest hesitation.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Each defensive artifact barely survived a single strike before exploding apart.","None of them could withstand Qin Lingxiao.","Yet...","Each one bought him another fleeting moment.","Qin Lingxiao frowned slightly.","She hadn’t expected Yu Zidi to possess so many life-saving treasures.","It seems like he has already raided the treasury of the Imperial Family.","Still...","It was meaningless.","No matter how many defensive artifacts he possessed, they would eventually run out.","The outcome would not change.","Meanwhile, Yu Zidi’s breathing had become increasingly ragged.","His robes were soaked with cold sweat.","His heart pounded wildly.","For the first time in his life, he felt death so close.","His mind screamed only one thing.","(I must live!)","However...","Even in such a desperate situation, another thought remained deeply rooted within his heart.","(The throne... I cannot lose the throne!)","To surrender?","To admit defeat?","To hand the empire over to Yu Feiyan?","Such thoughts never once crossed his mind despite being overwhelming .","To Yu Zidi...","The throne was no different from his own life.","If he gave it up, then even living would become meaningless.","His eyes frantically swept across the battlefield, desperately searching for anyone capable of saving him.","Xuande?","Still going against other Earth Immortals.","The foreign experts?","Occupied by the masked Earth Immortals.","The Imperial Guards?","Already overwhelmed plus they aren’t powerful enough.","No one...","Then his gaze suddenly froze.","It landed upon a distant platform.","The Bai Clan!","More specifically, Bai Zihan.","At this very moment, Bai Zihan still sat leisurely in his seat, calmly sipping tea as though the life-and-death battle before him had nothing to do with him.","Yu Zidi’s eyes instantly brightened.","Without the slightest hesitation, he shouted across the battlefield.","\"Clan Leader Bai!\"","His voice echoed throughout the Imperial Palace.","\"I trust the Bai Clan has no intention of watching the Desolate Heaven Empire fall into chaos!\"","He forcibly suppressed the panic in his heart.","His expression quickly regained the dignity expected of an Emperor.","\"I hereby invite the Bai Clan to assist in suppressing these rebels! As long as the Bai Clan lends me its strength today, this Emperor guarantees that the Bai Clan shall forever remain the foremost clan of the Desolate Heaven Empire!\"","\"The Imperial Family will stand with the Bai Clan for generations to come!\"","Even while facing death, Yu Zidi’s tone never sounded pleading.","Instead, it carried the confidence of a ruler extending an offer.","Hearing those words, Bai Zihan finally looked toward Yu Zidi.","\"Heh...\"","A faint chuckle escaped his lips.","Even at a time like this, Yu Zidi still insisted on maintaining the appearance of a righteous Emperor.","More importantly, from where did Yu Zidi find the confidence to believe the Bai Clan would help him?","Did he truly think Bai Zihan was unaware of why so many powerful foreign delegations were allowed within the Desolate Heaven Empire?","Still Bai Zihan showed no intention of exposing Yu Zidi nor did he bluntly reject him.","He simply placed his teacup down before speaking calmly.","\"Your Majesty. This matter appears to be a dispute between members of the Imperial Family.\"","\"As a member of the Neutral Alliance, the Bai Clan has no intention of interfering in the battle of the throne.\"","He slightly cupped his fists.","\"Please forgive us for being unable to offer assistance.\"","His tone was courteous and polite without the slightest hint of hostility.","Yet...","Yu Zidi’s expression immediately darkened.","He could naturally hear the meaning hidden beneath Bai Zihan’s words.","Neutral Alliance.","Unable to interfere.","Every sentence sounded reasonable.","Yet every sentence amounted to the same answer.","The Bai Clan would not help him.","Yu Zidi’s eyes gradually turned bloodshot.","\"Battle for the throne?\"","He suddenly roared.","\"What battle for the throne?! I have already ascended the throne! I am the legitimate Emperor of the Desolate Heaven Empire!\"","He pointed furiously toward Yu Feiyan and Yu Qingya.","\"They are rebels! They are attempting to murder their Emperor!\"","\"This is no longer a dispute between siblings! This is rebellion!\"","His furious voice echoed throughout the Imperial Palace.","He stared directly at Bai Zihan.","\"So tell me...\"","\"Will the Bai Clan truly stand by and watch rebels overthrow the legitimate Emperor?\"","However, Bai Zihan remained seated.","His expression did not change in the slightest.","Neither did he rise from his chair.","Seeing Bai Zihan remain completely indifferent, the last trace of hope in Yu Zidi’s heart shattered.","Silence lingered for a brief moment.","Then Yu Zidi suddenly laughed.","\"Hahaha...\"","The laughter gradually grew louder.","\"Hahahahaha!\"","It echoed throughout the battlefield.","Everyone frowned.","His laughter carried an unmistakable hint of madness.","After laughing for several breaths, Yu Zidi slowly lifted his head.","His eyes were filled with coldness.","He looked directly at Bai Zihan.","\"So this is the Bai Clan’s final decision?\"","Bai Zihan simply looked at him calmly without answering.","Seeing that silence, Yu Zidi’s expression twisted.","\"Good! Very good! You’ll regret this, Bai Zihan!\"","His voice became increasingly sinister.","\"You really think remaining neutral will keep the Bai Clan safe? You’ve made the greatest mistake of your life!\"","Yu Zidi’s lips slowly curled into a cold smile.","\"If you refuse to help this Emperor today then the Bai Clan is doomed.\"","Bai Zihan’s expression did not change in the slightest.","Instead, a faint smile appeared on his face.","\"Oh?\"","He looked at Yu Zidi with apparent curiosity.","\"And what exactly does Your Majesty mean by that?\"","His tone remained as calm as ever.","It was as though he genuinely couldn’t understand Yu Zidi’s confidence.","Not only Bai Zihan, even Qin Lingxiao temporarily halted her attacks.","She withdrew several steps, her beautiful eyes narrowing slightly as she looked toward Yu Zidi.","She, too, wanted to hear his answer.","After all, even with her Golden Immortal Realm cultivation, taking down the Bai Clan wasn’t easy.","Yet...","Yu Zidi, a mere Prince of the Desolate Heaven Empire, actually dared to declare that the Bai Clan was doomed.","Where did such confidence come from?","If he truly possessed another hidden trump card capable of threatening the Bai Clan then she didn’t mind delaying his death for a little longer.","After all, if Yu Zidi could weaken or even destroy the Bai Clan for her, that would save her a great deal of trouble.","The other Foreign Delegation wanted to stop Yu Zidi from uttering another word.","They didn’t want others to know what they had done nor dealing with the Yu Zidi.","Moreover, negotiating with the Bai Clan and saying that he will help them, whether that is true or not, they obviously didn’t like it.","They had come here to deal with the Bai Clan and if Yu Zidi intended to protect him then...","Anyways, since nothing has been confirmed, they still didn’t do anything for now.","Yu Zidi slowly wiped the blood from the corner of his mouth.","Then he laughed.","\"Hahaha... Bai Zihan, you truly know nothing.\"","His gaze swept across the members of the Bai Clan before returning to Bai Zihan.","Yu Zidi continued with a cold smile.","\"The moment today’s coronation began, the Imperial Army, together with the armies of every foreign empire present here, had already surrounded the Bai Clan.\"","Yu Zidi’s smile widened.","\"By now, your Bai Clan should already be engulfed in flames. The combined armies of the Imperial Family and the foreign empires are more than enough to reduce your entire clan territory to ashes.\"","He stared directly into Bai Zihan’s eyes.","\"You should understand what that means.\"","Yu Zidi’s voice gradually became colder.","\"So I’ll give you one final chance. Help this Emperor suppress these rebels. The moment you do, I will immediately send an order for every army surrounding the Bai Clan to withdraw.\"","His eyes flashed with menace.","\"But if you refuse...\"","He paused deliberately.","A sinister smile spread across his face.","\"...then by the time this battle ends, the Bai Clan will have already disappeared from the Desolate Heaven Empire forever.\""]},{"number":667,"title":"Chapter 667: Threatening The Bai Clan!","paragraphs":["Yu Zidi’s declaration immediately sent shockwaves throughout the Imperial Palace.","Countless spectators stared at him with wide eyes.","Many of them were completely dumbfounded.","Moments ago, Yu Zidi had been desperately trying to seek the Bai Clan’s assistance.","Yet now, instead of pleading, he was openly threatening them.","The Bai Clan!","Who were they?","Throughout the entire Eastern Region, the Bai Clan stood at the very peak.","Even the rulers of the various empires would think twice before provoking them.","Yet Yu Zidi, an almost crowned Emperor who had yet to secure his own throne, actually dared to threaten the Bai Clan in public.","Many people found it difficult to believe.","After all, he couldn’t even suppress Yu Feiyan’s rebellion.","Where exactly did he find the confidence to provoke the Bai Clan?","Could it be...","He truly possessed another terrifying trump card? Or had the pressure driven him completely insane?","Yu Zidi’s confidence seemed far too great to be mere bluffing.","Yu Zidi suddenly turned toward Qin Lingxiao.","His expression became incomparably cold.","\"You!\"","He pointed directly at her.","\"I advise you to stop now.\"","His voice carried the commanding tone of an Emperor.","\"Capture Yu Feiyan and submit to this Emperor.If you do... I may still show mercy and spare your life.\"","His arrogant words echoed throughout the battlefield.","Many people couldn’t help exchanging strange glances.","Even now, Yu Zidi was still speaking from a position of absolute superiority.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan remained seated exactly where he was.","He leisurely lifted his teacup.","Took a slow sip.","Then calmly placed it back onto the table.","His expression never changed from beginning to end.","It was as though Yu Zidi’s threats...","His declaration...","His confidence...","None of it was worth even the slightest attention.","Seeing Bai Zihan’s indifferent attitude, the veins on Yu Zidi’s forehead bulged.","His expression cracked.","He was threatening them, yet Bai Zihan still treated him as though he didn’t even exist.","That calm, unconcerned expression was even more humiliating than an outright refusal.","Yu Zidi clenched his fists so tightly that cracking sounds echoed from his fingers.","His eyes burned with rage.","\"Bai Zihan!\"","He roared furiously.","\"Are you looking down on this Emperor? You think I’m bluffing?\"","His breathing became increasingly heavy.","\"I’ve already told you... The Bai Clan’s fate is in my hands! Yet you still dare ignore me?\"","The more Bai Zihan remained silent, the more furious Yu Zidi became.","To him, Bai Zihan’s silence was the greatest form of contempt.","Finally, seeing that Bai Zihan remained completely uninterested, Yu Zidi no longer bothered to hide anything.","A sinister smile slowly spread across his face.","\"So... You still refuse to believe this Emperor?\"","He slowly swept his gaze across everyone present before looking back at Bai Zihan.","\"Very well! Then this Emperor will tell everyone exactly what I mean.\"","His voice echoed throughout the Imperial Palace.","\"At this very moment... The Bai Clan is already under siege. The Imperial Army has joined forces with the armies of every empire standing behind me.\"","\"Their target is the Bai Clan.\"","The entire plaza instantly fell silent.","Many people immediately understood what Yu Zidi meant.","Today’s coronation had drawn nearly every important expert of the Bai Clan to the Imperial Palace.","Its remaining defenses would naturally be much weaker than usual.","Meanwhile, the foreign delegations hadn’t merely brought experts.","They had secretly mobilized their own armies as well.","Together with the Imperial Army of the Desolate Heaven Empire, they had launched an assault upon the Bai Clan while everyone’s attention was focused on the coronation.","It was a carefully prepared conspiracy.","One meant to destroy the Bai Clan in a single stroke.","The expressions of countless spectators immediately changed.","However, rather than admiring Yu Zidi’s schemes, many looked at him with open contempt, especially the officials and cultivators of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","As the future Emperor, instead of protecting one of the empire’s strongest pillars, he had secretly colluded with foreign empires to destroy it.","This wasn’t merely a political struggle.","It was betrayal.","Betrayal of his own people.","Betrayal of his own empire.","Many people unconsciously frowned.","Even those who had originally supported Yu Zidi couldn’t help feeling a trace of disappointment.","An Emperor who relied upon outsiders to eliminate his own subjects...","Could such a person truly be worthy of ruling the Desolate Heaven Empire?","However, Yu Zidi didn’t care in the slightest.","He could clearly feel the contemptuous gazes directed toward him.","But so what?","Initially, he had intended to keep everything hidden.","After destroying the Bai Clan, he would simply fabricate a suitable explanation or extricate himself from the situation.","Then he would continue presenting himself as a benevolent Emperor loved by his people.","Unfortunately, things had not unfolded according to his expectations.","Yu Feiyan’s force’s strength had greatly exceeded his calculations.","One hidden card after another had appeared.","She had transformed from someone he believed he could suppress effortlessly into the greatest threat to his throne.","Under such circumstances, there was no longer any reason to continue hiding the truth.","As long as he secured victory today, history would be written by him.","The victors would decide what was true and what was false.","Thinking of this, Yu Zidi looked directly at Bai Zihan.","A cold smile appeared on his face.","\"So, Bai Zihan! You have two choices. Continue standing there and watch.\"","\"And by the time this battle ends, you’ll receive news that the Bai Clan has been erased from the Desolate Heaven Empire.\"","\"Or... Fight for this Emperor. Help me suppress Yu Feiyan and her followers. If you do...\"","\"I’ll immediately order every army surrounding the Bai Clan to withdraw.\"","Yu Zidi’s eyes flashed with confidence.","He no longer believed Bai Zihan could remain so calm.","After all, the Bai Clan’s fate was no longer in Bai Zihan’s hands.","It was in his.","At least, that is what he believed.","Even after hearing Yu Zidi’s revelation, Bai Zihan’s expression did not change in the slightest.","Not a trace of panic.","Not a hint of anger.","Instead a faint smirk slowly appeared on his face.","He calmly looked at Yu Zidi before gently shaking his head.","\"Yu Zidi, it seems you’ve misunderstood something.\"","He leisurely stood up from his chair.","His voice remained as calm as ever.","\"Do you really think.my Bai Clan is that weak?\"","Not far away, Qin Lingxiao narrowed her eyes.","She had been quietly listening the entire time.","If what Yu Zidi had said was true then perhaps one of her greatest headaches would finally disappear.","If the combined armies of five empires truly succeeded in destroying them, then not only would one enormous obstacle vanish, she could also rescue Long Haotian.","The secret about True God’s legacy would be protected.","Even the Bai Clan who might have extracted the information would perish. Indeed, that would be the best ending.","She couldn’t help praising Yu Zidi for his ruthlessness and decisiveness.","Although what Yu Zidi had done was utterly disgraceful for someone about to become Emperor.","From her perspective, it was undoubtedly beneficial.","She hoped his plan would succeed.","Of course she also understood another meaning behind Yu Zidi’s words.","He wasn’t merely threatening Bai Zihan, he was threatening her as well.","If the Bai Clan truly fell...","Then once those combined armies returned to the capital, her own situation would become far more dangerous.","However, whether Yu Zidi himself would still be alive by the time they returned remained another matter entirely.","Hearing Bai Zihan’s question, Yu Zidi merely let out a cold scoff.","\"Stop pretending. I know the Bai Clan isn’t weak.\"","He stared directly into Bai Zihan’s eyes.","\"But can the Bai Clan survive against the combined armies of five empires? Can you?\"","\"The Bai Clan has absolutely no chance.\"","Bai Zihan still kept smiling.","Then he calmly extended one hand.","\"If that’s truly the case then take out your transmission jade. Ask your commander. See whether the Bai Clan has already been destroyed.\"","The moment those words fell, Yu Zidi couldn’t help sneering inwardly.","(Still pretending?)","He naturally believed Bai Zihan remained so calm because he simply didn’t believe him.","Very well!","Since that was the case, he would let Bai Zihan hear it with his own ears.","Without hesitation, Yu Zidi took out a communication jade.","His spiritual sense immediately entered it.","A moment later, his voice echoed into the jade.","\"Report the situation. Has the Bai Clan been captured?\"","His tone sounded calm.","Captured...","Was merely a pleasant way of putting it.","In truth, his orders had never been to capture anyone.","He had ordered the combined armies to completely eradicate the Bai Clan.","Leave no survivors.","By now, even if the slaughter had not completely finished, half of the Bai Clan should already have been reduced to rubble.","At that point, he could generously promise Bai Zihan that, should he submit immediately, the remaining survivors would be spared.","As for whether he intended to keep such a promise afterward, Yu Zidi merely sneered inwardly.","(Even if I don’t kill him... There are plenty of people who will.)","The foreign empires!","The Li-Zhao Alliance!","None of them will allow the Bai Clan to continue existing. And with their current strength, they surely won’t survive."]},{"number":668,"title":"Chapter 668: Changed Sides?","paragraphs":["Apart from those still locked in fierce combat, almost everyone else unconsciously fell silent.","Even many of the experts who were fighting, also diverted some of their attention to listen.","Everyone wanted to know the outcome.","Has the Bai Clan truly fallen? Or...","Had they somehow survived the combined assault of more than five empires?","Either answer would shake the entire Eastern Region.","If the Bai Clan had truly been destroyed, then the Desolate Heaven Empire would forever lose its strongest pillar.","The balance of power across the Eastern Region would be rewritten overnight.","However, if the Bai Clan had actually repelled the combined armies then no force throughout the entire Eastern Region would dare provoke them ever again.","After such a battle, even the foreign empires would have to think carefully before facing the Bai Clan’s inevitable retaliation.","Either result would send shockwaves throughout the world.","The battlefield gradually became eerily quiet.","Everyone waited.","Then a weak, exhausted voice finally emerged from the communication jade.","\"Y-Your Highness! There... there is a huge emergency!\"","The voice was hoarse.","It sounded as though its owner had barely escaped with his life.","\"We... Our forces...\"","\"...have almost been wiped out!\"","The moment those words echoed across the Imperial Palace, Yu Zidi’s smug smile instantly froze.","The entire battlefield fell into complete silence.","One could hear a pin drop.","Everyone stared blankly at the communication jade.","Yu Zidi’s pupils violently contracted.","His face immediately darkened.","\"Nonsense!\"","He roared furiously.","\"Is this the time for jokes?! I asked whether the Bai Clan had been destroyed!\"","\"Answer this Emperor!\"","However, the trembling voice from the jade immediately replied.","\"Y-Your Highness! T-This subordinate wouldn’t dare joke about something like this...\"","\"What I said... is the truth.\"","\"Our army alongside the Vermillion Pill, Tianyu, Azure Cloud and Jade River Empire is almost eradicated.\"","Yu Zidi’s expression twisted.","\"What?!\"","His voice carried both disbelief and fury.","\"Impossible! How can the combined armies of several empires lose to a single clan?\"","\"It doesn’t make any sense!\"","His breathing became increasingly frantic.","Even if the Bai Clan truly possessed the rumored two Golden Immortal Realm experts...","Could two individuals really overturn an army consisting of tens of thousands of cultivators?","Not to mention, one of the two rumored Golden Immortal Cultivators is here in the Imperial Palace.","That was impossible!","Then the voice from the jade spoke once more.","This time, it carried unconcealed fear.","\"I-It... It isn’t just the Bai Clan...\"","Yu Zidi suddenly froze.","\"What did you say?\"","The voice swallowed hard before continuing.","\"T-The Li Clan and the Zhao Clan as well...\"","\"They’re helping the Bai Clan!\"","Boom!","Those words struck everyone present like a bolt from the blue.","Another earth-shattering piece of news had just been revealed.","The Li Clan!","The Zhao Clan!","The very same two clans that had ignored every one of Yu Zidi’s pleas for help...","Were actually helping the Bai Clan?","Yu Zidi’s body stiffened.","His trembling gaze slowly shifted away from the communication jade.","It landed directly upon the Li Clan and Zhao Clan delegations seated among the honored guests.","The two clan leaders remained seated.","Neither attempted to deny the accusation.","Neither looked surprised.","Instead, their expressions were complicated.","There was reluctance.","There was guilt.","Yet there wasn’t the slightest intention of refuting the words coming from the communication jade.","If what had just been reported were false, by now, they would have already stood up to denounce the commander for slandering their clans.","They would have immediately cleared their names before everyone present.","But... Nothing.","Neither Clan Leader Li nor Clan Leader Zhao uttered a single word.","Their silence was the clearest admission.","Yu Zidi’s expression gradually froze.","His mind suddenly connected everything.","No wonder...","No wonder they had ignored every one of his transmissions.","No wonder they had remained seated despite repeatedly urging them to attack.","It wasn’t because of hesitation nor because of pride.","It was because... They had already switched sides.","In all of his calculations, in every possible outcome he had envisioned...","Never...","Not even once...","Had he imagined that the two clans he trusted the most would betray him.","The Bai Clan!","He had always believed that every major power feared and hated the Bai Clan.","He had thought that when the decisive moment arrived, everyone would unite against them.","Instead, the very allies upon whom he had placed the greatest expectations had abandoned him and chosen to stand beside the Bai Clan.","His lips trembled violently.","\"Y-You...\"","He pointed a shaking finger toward the two clan leaders.","His eyes were bloodshot.","\"You actually betrayed me! You backstabbed this Emperor! You disgraceful traitors!\"","His furious roar echoed throughout the Imperial Palace.","\"How did I not see that you two were a bunch of cowards.\"","For a brief moment, Clan Leader Li and Clan Leader Zhao lowered their heads.","A trace of guilt flashed across their faces.","After all, Yu Zidi had indeed placed considerable trust in them.","However, that guilt quickly disappeared.","Yu Zidi had long since stopped treating them with respect.","Now, after being publicly humiliated before the entire Eastern Region, the last remnants of their hesitation vanished.","Clan Leader Zhao slowly stood up.","His expression turned cold.","\"Betray you?\"","He let out a mocking laugh.","\"Your Highness... No...\"","He deliberately corrected himself.","\"Yu Zidi! You speak as though we owe you something.\"","Clan Leader Li also rose to his feet.","His gaze was equally indifferent.","\"You ask why we didn’t help you?\"","\"Then let me ask you something.\"","\"What reason do we have to help you?\"","Yu Zidi’s expression twisted.","Clan Leader Zhao continued without waiting for an answer.","\"You haven’t even secured the throne. You are not yet the Emperor. You are merely another prince fighting for succession.\"","\"If you can’t even win your own battle for the throne... What qualifications do you have to demand our loyalty?\"","His words struck Yu Zidi like sharp blades.","Clan Leader Li sneered.","\"The late Emperor is dead. The new Emperor has yet to be decided.\"","\"So why should we continue treating you with respect due to an Emperor? You couldn’t even defeat your own sisters.\"","\"And you still expect everyone else to stake their clans’ futures on you?\"","His voice became increasingly contemptuous.","\"If you can’t even protect yourself... Then what value do you have to us?\"","The expressions of countless spectators changed.","The Li Clan and Zhao Clan had completely torn away all pretense.","There was no longer any room for reconciliation.","From this moment onward... their alliance with Yu Zidi had officially come to an end.","There was, in fact, only one reason why the Li Clan and Zhao Clan had ultimately been forced to help the Bai Clan.","The Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art!","It had become the most sought-after cultivation technique throughout the empire.","Its reputation had spread like wildfire.","It is a High-Grade Earth Rank cultivation technique, nearly everyone has free access to it as well.","For ordinary cultivators who could only afford mediocre techniques, the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art increased their cultivation speed by nearly tenfold.","To countless loose cultivators and smaller clans, it was nothing short of a heavenly blessing.","However, this is also better than almost every cultivation technique in the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Naturally, the Li Clan and Zhao Clan could not remain indifferent.","Even Li Jianhong and Zhao Wutian had been tempted.","Initially, both patriarchs had remained extremely cautious.","They had repeatedly warned the clan elders.","\"No one is permitted to cultivate it without permission. Investigate it first.\"","Yet... Nothing.","The technique appeared completely flawless.","Not only that, every disciple who cultivated it advanced at astonishing speed.","Their foundations became more stable.","Their spiritual qi became purer.","Their breakthroughs became noticeably easier.","Everything pointed toward one conclusion.","It was an extraordinary cultivation technique.","As more time passed, the warnings issued by Li Jianhong and Zhao Wutian gradually lost their effect.","After all, actions always spoke louder than suspicion.","Nothing had happened.","One month.","Two months.","Three months.","Every cultivator who practiced the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art experienced only benefits.","No abnormalities appeared whatsoever.","Eventually, even the clan elders began persuading their patriarchs.","\"Patriarch, perhaps we’ve been overly cautious.\"","\"The technique has already spread throughout the empire.\"","\"If there were truly a problem, someone would have discovered it by now.\"","Li Jianhong remained silent.","Zhao Wutian hesitated.","However, the temptation became increasingly difficult to resist.","Every day they watched their disciples rapidly improve.","Every day they saw their rivals becoming stronger.","Could they really continue standing still?","Even without asking their Clan Leader, many have already begun cultivating the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art themselves.","Especially the Li Clan who is more obsessed with strength.","Even Li Jianhong himself began to cultivate the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art himself.","And with him taking the lead, the Li clan has no reason to hold themselves back.","One elder after another began cultivating it.","Then the core disciples.","Then the inner elders.","Eventually, nearly every expert within the Li Clan and Zhao Clan practiced the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","Little did they know...","From the very moment they began cultivating that technique, their fate had already slipped into Bai Zihan’s hands."]},{"number":669,"title":"Chapter 669: Dealing with The Li Clan","paragraphs":["Bai Zihan had long since learned of the secret alliance between the Li-Zhao Clan and Yu Zidi.","After all, there were numerous spies planted within both clans, the most valuable of whom was Han Sha, the new Sect Leader of the Heaven Sword Sect.","No matter how carefully they tried to conceal their plans, they couldn’t hide them from Bai Zihan.","Even so, even if Bai Zihan hadn’t known about their alliance, he still wouldn’t have been concerned about them.","With the Bai Clan’s current strength, the Li Clan and Zhao Clan were nothing in his eyes.","He could crush them whenever he wished.","Still, Bai Zihan had done nothing to them even though he had the strength to destroy them.","There were two reasons why they were still standing.","The first was the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","Bai Zihan understood human nature all too well.","No cultivator could resist the temptation of cultivating faster, especially not someone like Li Jianhong.","The Li Clan was obsessed with strength.","Even if they suspected there might be something wrong with the technique, they would still be tempted to cultivate it.","Even if they initially remained cautious, Bai Zihan knew they would eventually succumb to temptation.","All he needed to do was wait.","And just as he had expected, many experts from both clans eventually cultivated the technique.","The most important among them was Li Jianhong himself.","As for Zhao Wutian, he remained cautious and never cultivated the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","Even so, it didn’t matter whether Zhao Wutian avoided cultivating it.","Many of the Zhao Clan’s other experts had already done so.","The moment that happened...","Those two clans had effectively become Bai Zihan’s possessions.","Whenever he wished, he could claim them.","The second reason was that the Li Clan and Zhao Clan still had value.","The Bai Clan’s enemies were no longer limited to those within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","There were also foreign powers lurking beyond its borders.","Sooner or later, those empires would make their move.","When that day came, the Bai Clan would naturally require additional manpower.","Rather than destroying the Li Clan and Zhao Clan beforehand, it was far more beneficial to leave them intact.","When those foreign powers eventually came knocking, Bai Zihan could make use of both clans.","Even if they couldn’t defeat the Bai Clan’s enemies, they could at least exhaust them or buy valuable time.","Today, it was time to prove their worth.","Yu Zidi’s plan had truly been ingenious.","Using the coronation ceremony to draw away some of the Bai Clan’s strongest experts...","Then secretly mobilizing the combined armies of multiple empires to surround the Bai Clan’s territory.","Under normal circumstances, such a strategy would have succeeded against almost any force within the Eastern Region.","It was undoubtedly the best opportunity anyone could hope for.","Unfortunately, there was one fatal flaw. Their strength simply wasn’t enough to deal with the Bai Clan.","Not to mention, he has prepared a few pawns to deal with them.","***","A luxurious flying ship slowly descended outside the Li Clan.","Only two people stepped down.","Bai Zihan and Bai Ren!","The moment the guards recognized the young man dressed in white, the entire Li Clan was thrown into an uproar.","\"B-Bai Zihan!\"","\"What is he doing here?\"","\"He only brought one elder?\"","Some Li Clan members became nervous, while others revealed expressions of delight.","In their eyes, Bai Zihan had practically delivered himself to their doorstep.","If they could seize him here...","Wouldn’t the Bai Clan lose its greatest genius?","Some even secretly circulated their Qi.","As long as the Clan Leader gave the order, they would immediately surround Bai Zihan.","Yet not everyone shared the same thoughts.","Many Li Clan members who had previously dealt with Bai Zihan felt an inexplicable chill run down their backs.","After witnessing everything Bai Zihan had accomplished over the past several months, none of them believed he would recklessly place himself in danger.","Still, regardless of what they thought, no one dared act without orders.","The guards quickly stepped forward and respectfully cupped their fists.","\"Clan Leader Bai! What brings you to the Li Clan today?\"","Bai Zihan merely smiled.","\"I’ve come to visit Clan Leader Li. I have something important to discuss with him.\"","The guards glanced at one another before immediately sending someone to report the matter.","...","Inside the main hall.","Li Jianhong listened quietly as the guard finished his report.","\"Bai Zihan came with only one Grand Elder?\"","A strange smile slowly appeared on his face.","He had expected Bai Zihan to remain within the Bai Clan after everything that had happened.","Yet, unexpectedly, the young man had come personally.","To the Li Clan.","To his territory.","An elder beside him immediately lowered his voice.","\"Clan Leader! This is a rare opportunity. If we seize Bai Zihan now...\"","Before he could finish speaking, Li Jianhong slowly raised his hand.","The hall immediately fell silent.","His eyes narrowed thoughtfully.","Then the corners of his mouth gradually lifted.","\"Invite him in.\"","Li Jianhong smiled faintly.","\"Since Clan Leader Bai has come all this way... how could we refuse him entry?\"","The guard quickly bowed.","\"Understood!\"","After the guard departed, the smile on Li Jianhong’s face gradually disappeared.","His eyes became incomparably cold.","(Bai Zihan... I’ve waited for an opportunity like this for a very long time.)","If there was ever a chance to eliminate him, he absolutely could not let it slip away.","Bai Zihan had personally walked into the Li Clan with only a single elder accompanying him.","Such an opportunity might never appear again.","Quietly, Li Jianhong crushed a communication jade hidden within his sleeve.","An order spread throughout the Li Clan.","At once, several secluded elders slowly opened their eyes.","Formation Masters silently activated the clan’s grand formation.","Everything happened in complete silence.","On the surface, the Li Clan remained peaceful and welcoming.","Yet beneath that calm exterior, an invisible net had already begun tightening around Bai Zihan.","Moments later, Bai Zihan stepped into the grand hall alongside Bai Ren.","Li Jianhong rose from his seat with a warm smile, as though greeting an old friend.","\"Hahaha! Clan Leader Bai! To what do I owe the pleasure of this unexpected visit?\"","\"I will give you one chance to submit to me.\"","Bai Zihan spoke calmly.","Li Jianhong’s smile froze.","\"...What?\"","For a brief moment, he wondered if he had misheard.","Silence!","The entire hall became deathly quiet.","Every Li Clan elder stared blankly at Bai Zihan.","Several breaths later—","\"Hahaha!\"","An elder suddenly burst into loud laughter.","The laughter quickly spread throughout the hall.","\"Hahaha!\"","\"What arrogance!\"","\"Has this brat gone insane?\"","\"He actually wants the Li Clan to submit?\"","Even the more composed elders couldn’t help but shake their heads.","Their eyes were filled with ridicule.","Submit?","The Li Clan was one of the top clans of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Its heritage stretched back thousands of years.","Countless generations had built its current glory.","Yet Bai Zihan had casually walked into their territory and demanded that they surrender.","It was simply laughable.","Li Jianhong also chuckled.","However, unlike the others, his smile gradually carried a trace of disappointment.","He slowly shook his head.","\"I had thought Clan Leader Bai was a rather intelligent person. But now... It seems I overestimated you.\"","His eyes narrowed slightly.","\"To utter such foolish words, I truly don’t know whether to admire your courage or pity your stupidity.\"","He slowly rose from his seat.","The atmosphere inside the hall instantly turned icy.","\"Since you’ve come all this way and even asked my Li Clan to surrender...\"","\"Then don’t blame us for keeping you here forever.\"","Boom!","The moment his words fell, terrifying auras erupted throughout the hall.","One after another.","Li Clan elders slowly stood.","Great Ascension Realm.","Immortal Ascension Realm.","Earth Immortal Realm.","Powerful killing intent instantly locked onto Bai Zihan.","The temperature within the hall seemed to plummet.","However, despite everyone surrounding him, not a single person attacked immediately.","Their eyes repeatedly swept toward Bai Ren.","After all, Bai Ren’s reputation had already spread throughout the empire.","No one dared underestimate him.","More importantly, this was Bai Zihan.","None of them believed he would recklessly enter the Li Clan without some hidden confidence.","For several moments, both sides remained motionless.","The hall fell into an eerie silence.","The other elders gradually became impatient.","They had observed Bai Zihan carefully.","Yet nothing happened.","No hidden experts appeared.","No reinforcements arrived.","It was still only Bai Zihan and Bai Ren.","Finally, one hot-tempered elder lost his patience.","\"Hmph! I refuse to believe he has any trick capable of overturning the situation!\"","Boom!","His cultivation exploded as he shot toward Bai Zihan.","Several other elders immediately followed behind him.","In an instant, several powerful cultivators charged across the hall.","Their terrifying pressure caused the surrounding space to tremble.","Yet before any of them could come within several meters of Bai Zihan—","Their expressions suddenly changed.","Thump!","One elder abruptly stopped mid-stride.","His eyes widened.","\"...My... heart...\"","An indescribable pain erupted from deep within his chest.","It felt as though an invisible hand had suddenly clenched his heart.","\"Aghhh!\"","He screamed and collapsed onto the floor.","Thud!","Another elder fell to his knees.","Then another.","Then another.","Within a single breath, every elder who had rushed toward Bai Zihan clutched their chests in agony.","Their faces turned deathly pale.","Cold sweat poured from their foreheads.","\"Aaaaah!\"","\"My heart!\"","\"W-What is happening?!\"","\"It hurts!\"","They rolled across the ground in unbearable pain.","Some desperately circulated their Qi in an attempt to suppress whatever was happening.","Others frantically swallowed healing pills.","None of it worked.","The strange pain only grew stronger.","The sudden scene stunned everyone remaining inside the hall."]},{"number":670,"title":"Chapter 670: Suppressing the Li Clan","paragraphs":["Li Jianhong’s expression instantly changed as he watched his elders fall one after another without any apparent reason.","\"What happened?!\"","None of the fallen elders had been struck.","No one had attacked them.","Yet they had collapsed simultaneously as though afflicted by some invisible curse.","Even Bai Ren’s eyes flashed with surprise.","Initially, he hadn’t understood what Bai Zihan was trying to accomplish by coming to the Li Clan with only him as company.","But now...","He finally understood where Bai Zihan’s confidence came from.","(What did he use?)","Even Bai Ren couldn’t understand.","Was it some kind of poison?","A poison that couldn’t be detected?","That was the only explanation he could think of.","Li Jianhong arrived at the same conclusion almost instantly.","\"It must be poison!\"","Without the slightest hesitation, he flipped his hand.","A jade bottle appeared.","He immediately swallowed several antidote pills.","Grade-6 Detoxification Pills!","The highest-grade antidote the Li Clan possessed.","The surrounding elders reacted just as quickly.","One after another, they hurriedly consumed their own antidotes.","For a brief moment, relief appeared on many of their faces.","Since they had seen through Bai Zihan’s trick, then there was nothing to fear.","However, the next moment—","\"Ugh!\"","Li Jianhong’s pupils violently contracted.","A heart-piercing pain suddenly erupted from deep within his chest.","It was several times stronger than before.","His body stiffened.","Thud!","He fell heavily onto both knees.","Large beads of cold sweat instantly covered his forehead.","His breathing became ragged.","\"W-What...\"","\"How...\"","His face was filled with disbelief.","The Grade-6 Detoxification Pill was completely ineffective.","Impossible!","A Grade-6 antidote could neutralize virtually every poison below Grade 6.","Even if it encountered a Grade-7 poison, it should at least suppress its effects to a considerable degree.","Yet...","Nothing changed.","The pain continued to intensify.","It was as though he had swallowed nothing at all.","Around him, the other elders experienced exactly the same fate.","One after another, they collapsed onto the floor.","Cries of agony echoed throughout the hall.","\"Aaaagh!\"","\"It still hurts!\"","\"My meridians...\"","\"What kind of poison is this?!\"","No matter how desperately they circulated their Qi...","No matter how many antidotes they swallowed...","Nothing worked.","Within moments, every Li Clan expert who had cultivated the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art had collapsed.","Only two elders remained standing.","Both were Great Ascension Realm cultivators.","Both wore pale expressions as they instinctively retreated several steps.","Bai Zihan glanced at them before calmly withdrawing his gaze.","He didn’t expect everyone to cultivate the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","Perhaps they had remained suspicious or perhaps they simply hadn’t found the opportunity.","Either way, it didn’t matter much.","Two Great Ascension Realm cultivators alone posed no threat whatsoever.","Even Bai Zihan himself could easily suppress them.","Not to mention, Bai Ren still stood quietly behind him.","This was precisely why Bai Zihan had brought Bai Ren with him, to deal with the individuals who had never cultivated the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","Meanwhile, Li Jianhong struggled to lift his head.","His eyes were bloodshot.","Fear, confusion and overwhelming fury filled his gaze.","He glared at Bai Zihan.","\"You! What... did you do to us?!\"","His voice was almost a roar.","Every elder inside the hall stared at Bai Zihan with the same question.","Bai Zihan merely smiled faintly.","\"You don’t need to know.\"","He calmly looked at everyone present.","\"You only need to know one thing.\"","\"Your lives are now in my hands. If I wish...\"","\"I can take them whenever I please.\"","Those words immediately reminded everyone of a similar incident.","The Ancient Ruins!","After obtaining the inheritance of the Immortal Emperor by Bai Xueqing, Bai Zihan had threatened every major power.","He claimed he could kill any of their geniuses... whenever he wished.","At that time, almost everyone had dismissed it as an empty threat.","Until he killed geniuses from the sect that has made their move against them.","No one knew how.","No one could stop it.","The unknown had become their greatest fear.","And now, that same nightmare had descended upon the Li Clan.","The only difference was that this time...","It wasn’t their juniors.","It was them.","Li Jianhong’s face turned deathly pale.","He frantically examined every inch of his body.","His spiritual sense swept through his dantian.","His meridians.","His sea of consciousness.","His blood.","Again and again.","He searched for poison.","For cursed seals.","For anything unusual.","He still found... nothing.","The same was true for every other elder.","No matter how many times they inspected themselves...","No matter how thoroughly they searched, they couldn’t discover the source of their suffering.","Yet Bai Zihan could suppress them with a single thought.","The more they failed to understand it, the greater the fear growing inside their hearts became.","Li Jianhong’s breathing became increasingly ragged.","His entire body trembled uncontrollably.","Cold sweat soaked his robes as he struggled to endure the unbearable agony.","Bai Zihan calmly looked at everyone before speaking once more.","\"So, have you decided?\"","His gaze slowly swept across every elder lying on the ground.","\"Will the Li Clan submit?\"","Silence!","However, the silence itself was the answer.","Not a single person nodded.","Not a single person agreed.","Even after reaching such a miserable state, they still refused.","After all, they were the Li Clan.","One of the three greatest clans of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","For countless years, they had stood at the peak of the empire.","Although they acknowledged the Bai Clan’s superiority, they believed the difference between them wasn’t insurmountable.","Perhaps the Bai Clan was stronger... but only by a little.","Yet now, without even exchanging a single real blow, they were being forced to bow their heads because of one mysterious move.","How could they possibly accept such humiliation?","Li Jianhong clenched his teeth.","Veins bulged across his forehead.","He desperately circulated his Qi, attempting to suppress the strange force tormenting him.","The other elders did the same.","Boom! Boom!","Powerful spiritual Qi erupted throughout the hall.","However, it was completely useless.","No matter how much Qi they mobilized, the pain remained.","If anything, it only became worse.","Seeing their futile resistance, Bai Zihan’s eyes gradually turned cold.","\"You stubborn old bones...\"","He slowly shook his head.","\"It seems that unless you truly suffer, you simply won’t learn.\"","The moment those words fell—","\"Aaaaaaaah!\"","An incomparably miserable scream erupted from Li Jianhong’s mouth.","Then the other elders also followed.","The pain increased severalfold.","It no longer felt like someone was merely squeezing his heart.","Instead, it was as though countless invisible needles were repeatedly piercing his very soul.","Every elder inside the hall let out heart-wrenching screams.","\"Aaaagh!\"","\"Stop!\"","\"It hurts!\"","Several elders slammed their heads against the stone floor in a desperate attempt to distract themselves from the agony.","Others clawed at their own chests until blood flowed freely.","Some even wished they could knock themselves unconscious.","Unfortunately, they couldn’t.","Their consciousness remained incomparably clear.","Every second of agony was experienced in its entirety.","Ten minutes passed...","To those Li Clan elders, those ten minutes felt longer than an entire lifetime.","No...","Longer than a hundred lifetimes.","By the end, every trace of resistance had disappeared from their eyes.","Their pride...","Their dignity...","Their unwillingness...","Everything had been completely crushed beneath that unbearable torment.","Many had already begging to be spared and had completely surrendered.","Li Jianhong lay weakly on the ground.","His body twitched slightly.","His eyes had long since lost their previous arrogance.","They now contained nothing but terror.","He would rather die once than endure that pain ever again.","Bai Zihan calmly walked forward.","He stopped before Li Jianhong.","Looking down at the once-proud Clan Leader, he asked the same question again.","\"So, do you surrender?\"","The pain coursing through their bodies left them with only one possible answer.","There was no room for hesitation.","No room for pride.","No room for resistance.","Li Jianhong’s body trembled violently.","His lips quivered uncontrollably.","The moment Bai Zihan repeated the question, whatever dignity he had desperately clung to completely collapsed.","\"I... I surrender!\"","His answer came almost instantly.","He didn’t dare delay even a single breath longer.","\"Our Li Clan surrenders!\"","His voice echoed throughout the hall.","Although he tried to maintain the bearing expected of a Clan Leader, there was nothing dignified left about his appearance.","His robes were soaked with sweat.","His hair hung in complete disarray.","His face had long since become deathly pale.","He lay kneeling on the ground like a defeated prisoner.","The once lofty Clan Leader of the Li Clan no longer possessed even a trace of his former arrogance.","Only endless fear remained.","The moment those words left his mouth, the unbearable agony abruptly vanished.","It disappeared as suddenly as it had come.","\"...!\"","Li Jianhong’s eyes widened.","He greedily inhaled mouthful after mouthful of air.","His entire body went limp as he collapsed onto the floor.","Only after the pain disappeared did he realize that every inch of his body had already been drenched in cold sweat.","His robes clung tightly to his skin.","His heartbeat was still wildly out of control.","He had escaped.","He had finally escaped that nightmare.","Around him, the other Li Clan elders experienced the same thing.","The horrifying pain that had tormented them for what felt like countless lifetimes vanished without warning.","One after another, they collapsed weakly onto the ground, gasping for breath as though they had just been pulled back from the gates of hell.","Bai Zihan looked at the scene before him before letting out a faint chuckle.","He slowly shook his head.","\"People truly are strange. When offered the easy path...\"","\"They refuse to walk it. They insist on choosing the difficult one instead.\""]},{"number":671,"title":"Chapter 671: Spies in Li Clan?","paragraphs":["Bai Zihan’s casual remark made the Li Clan elders’ faces twitch uncontrollably.","Easy path?","The corners of Li Jianhong’s mouth trembled.","He wanted nothing more than to point at Bai Zihan and curse him.","What easy path?","You walked into our clan and demanded we surrender!","Who in their right mind would agree to such a ridiculous demand?","Had their positions been reversed, even Li Jianhong himself would have laughed the other party out of the hall.","Yet not a single elder dared utter those thoughts aloud.","The pain from moments ago still lingered vividly within their memories.","Merely recalling it caused their souls to shudder.","They had finally understood one terrifying truth.","The Li Clan had lost.","Not to the Bai Clan.","But to Bai Zihan alone.","From beginning to end, the Bai Clan hadn’t even made a move.","Bai Ren had stood quietly behind Bai Zihan without lifting a single finger.","Everything had been accomplished by Bai Zihan himself.","The thought made every elder feel a deep sense of despair.","How were they supposed to fight someone like this?","They didn’t even know what method Bai Zihan had used.","They couldn’t defend against it.","They couldn’t remove it.","They couldn’t even discover its existence.","Their lives had unknowingly fallen into Bai Zihan’s hands long ago.","At that moment, Bai Zihan’s gaze slowly shifted.","It landed upon the only two elders still standing inside the hall.","The two Great Ascension Realm elders who had never cultivated the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","The smile on Bai Zihan’s face gradually disappeared.","His eyes narrowed slightly.","The hall instantly became silent again.","Those two elders stiffened.","An inexplicable sense of unease rose within their hearts.","Bai Zihan quietly observed them for several moments before asking a seemingly ordinary question.","\"Who do you work for?\"","\"...\"","The two elders looked visibly confused.","\"Clan Leader Bai...\"","One of them forced out a smile.","\"We don’t understand what you mean.\"","Bai Zihan remained expressionless.","He didn’t immediately respond.","Instead, countless thoughts flashed through his mind.","The Li Clan...","A clan obsessed with strength.","If anyone in the Desolate Heaven Empire desired greater cultivation speed the most, it would undoubtedly be them.","Especially after witnessing the miraculous effects of the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","There should have been no reason for these two elders to reject it.","Unless it wasn’t because they were cautious but because someone had specifically ordered them not to cultivate it.","The Zhao Clan remaining cautious was understandable.","But the Li Clan?","That simply didn’t fit their nature.","The more Bai Zihan thought about it, the more suspicious these two became.","Seeing that they continued pretending to be ignorant, Bai Zihan calmly spoke again.","\"Elder Ren!\"","The instant those two words left his mouth—","Boom!","An incomparably terrifying pressure suddenly descended upon the entire hall.","The space itself seemed to freeze.","The expressions of the two elders changed drastically.","\"What—?!\"","Before either of them could react...","Bang!","Both were forcibly driven to their knees.","Crack!","The stone floor beneath them instantly shattered.","Fresh blood trickled from the corners of their mouths.","Their bodies trembled violently beneath the overwhelming pressure.","Golden Immortal!","How could mere Great Ascension Realm cultivators possibly resist the aura of a Golden Immortal?","It was like asking ants to withstand the weight of an entire mountain.","The difference was simply too great.","\"No...\"","\"I-I can’t move...\"","The two elders desperately circulated their cultivation.","Every vein bulged across their bodies.","Their spiritual Qi erupted wildly.","It accomplished absolutely nothing.","The pressure remained as immovable as heaven itself.","Bai Ren still hadn’t taken a single step.","His expression remained indifferent, as though suppressing two Great Ascension Realm cultivators required no more effort than pressing down two insects.","The surrounding Li Clan elders watched the scene with numb expressions.","Some unconsciously swallowed.","Others lowered their heads.","Several couldn’t stop their bodies from trembling.","\"...Monsters...\"","One elder muttered subconsciously.","\"They’re all monsters...\"","Another bitter smile appeared on Li Jianhong’s face.","If it wasn’t Bai Zihan terrifying them with methods beyond comprehension...","Then it was Bai Ren effortlessly suppressing Great Ascension Realm experts without even moving.","Only now did they truly understand how laughable their previous ambitions had been.","They had actually believed they could challenge the Bai Clan.","Challenge this Bai Clan?","The thought alone now seemed utterly absurd.","Li Jianhong’s expression became increasingly complicated as Bai Ren was bullying two juniors.","Initially, he had thought Bai Zihan was merely venting his anger.","But now...","Seeing Bai Zihan’s calm expression, even Li Jianhong couldn’t help but become suspicious.","Could it be...","Is there really something wrong with them?","Bai Zihan slowly turned his gaze toward Li Jianhong.","\"Tell me about them.\"","Li Jianhong didn’t dare hide anything.","He immediately cupped his fists.","\"Yes!\"","He pointed toward the two kneeling elders.","\"They aren’t members of the Li Clan by blood.\"","Bai Zihan remained silent, signaling him to continue.","Li Jianhong quickly explained.","\"They joined the Li Clan several hundred years ago. At that time, both were merely wandering cultivators.\"","\"They repeatedly rendered great services to the Li Clan.\"","\"They once presented our clan with an Earth-Grade Artifact. It greatly strengthened the clan’s foundation.\"","\"They also contributed countless resources over the years. When our Li Clan encountered a life-and-death crisis several centuries ago, both of them fought desperately alongside us.\"","\"They suffered severe injuries protecting many of our clansmen. Because of their contributions, they gradually earned the trust of the clan.\"","\"Eventually... They were promoted to elders.\"","As Li Jianhong, Bai Zihan found everything suspicious.","Giving away an Earth-Grade Artifact?","Even many direct descendants of the Li Clan would hesitate before making such a sacrifice.","Earth-Grade Artifacts weren’t ordinary treasures.","For independent cultivators, they were often their greatest life-saving cards.","Who would willingly hand one over to the clan which isn’t even tied by blood?","He slowly looked toward the two kneeling elders.","Both maintained confused expressions as if being wronged.","As though they had no idea why Bai Zihan suspected them.","They were acting remarkably well.","Unfortunately, that was precisely what made Bai Zihan suspicious.","The Li Clan was different from the Zhao Clan.","The Zhao Clan was cautious by nature.","Its members valued schemes over brute strength.","If two Zhao Clan elders had refused to cultivate the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art, Bai Zihan wouldn’t have found it strange.","But the Li Clan?","That was another matter entirely.","The Li Clan pursued strength above everything else.","Their entire clan had nearly gone mad over the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","Even Li Jianhong himself couldn’t resist cultivating it after months of observation.","Yet these two elders hadn’t touched it.","That alone was enough to raise Bai Zihan’s suspicions.","Bai Zihan inwardly sighed.","(If only I had something like Heavenly eyes to see the truth or lie.)","There were indeed several similar items in the System Store.","Artifacts capable of detecting lies.","Physique like Truth-Seeking Heavenly Eyes.","Even pills that forced absolute honesty.","Unfortunately, each one cost an absurd amount of System Points.","For now, he could only rely on observation.","Bai Zihan calmly met the gaze of the two elders.","Neither avoided his eyes.","Instead, they looked back with expressions of bewilderment.","As though they were the victims.","Bai Zihan chuckled inwardly.","(Good composure. It seems you aren’t ordinary elders after all.)","Bai Zihan remained silent.","His gaze never left the two kneeling elders.","For a long moment, the hall was deathly quiet, broken only by the heavy breathing of the Li Clan elders who had only just recovered from their torment.","Had he guessed wrong?","Even Bai Zihan began to question his own speculation.","The Li Clan was indeed obsessed with strength.","Perhaps these two simply had their own reasons for avoiding the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","Perhaps he had become overly suspicious.","However, suspicion alone was enough.","Bai Zihan had never been the type to leave hidden dangers behind simply because he lacked certainty.","He slowly looked toward Bai Ren.","\"Elder Ren!\"","Bai Ren immediately understood.","He took a single step forward.","Boom!","An overwhelming Golden Immortal aura descended upon the two Great Ascension Realm elders like an entire mountain.","Crack! Crack!","The stone floor beneath their knees instantly fractured.","The two elders groaned as every bone in their bodies creaked violently.","Their faces turned pale.","Yet they stubbornly gritted their teeth.","\"We... don’t understand what Clan Leader Bai is talking about...\"","\"Please... don’t falsely accuse us...\"","Bai Zihan’s expression remained unchanged.","\"Continue!\"","Bai Ren nodded.","Without another word, he increased the pressure.","Boom!","\"Aaaagh!\"","The two elders let out agonized screams.","Blood slowly trickled from the corners of their mouths.","Their muscles trembled uncontrollably as the terrifying pressure crushed them from every direction.","Even so, neither of them admitted anything.","Minutes passed.","Their bones cracked one after another.","Fresh blood stained their robes.","Even the surrounding Li Clan elders couldn’t bear to watch.","Bai Zihan’s brows furrowed slightly.","(Had I overthought it?)","Just as that thought flashed through his mind—","\"No...\"","One of the elders suddenly let out a trembling cry.","His body shook violently.","His face had become utterly bloodless.","\"I... I’ll talk...\"","The other elder immediately turned toward him with widened eyes.","\"What are you doing?!\"","\"Shut up!\"","The first elder seemed to have completely broken down.","His eyes were filled with terror.","\"I don’t want to die!\"","\"I don’t want to die!\"","He repeatedly slammed his forehead against the ground.","\"I’ll tell you everything!\"","The surrounding Li Clan members stared at him in complete disbelief.","Li Jianhong’s pupils contracted sharply.","\"What...?\"","The elder raised his head toward Bai Zihan.","His voice trembled violently.","\"I was... sent here ...by the Zhao Clan.\"","Silence!","Every Li Clan elder stared blankly at the kneeling man.","Li Jianhong’s expression froze.","His mind went completely blank.","The elder continued between terrified breaths.","\"Please... Please spare me... I was only following orders.\"","The other elder’s expression changed drastically.","\"You traitor!\"","His eyes instantly became filled with killing intent.","Without hesitation, he forcefully broke through Bai Ren’s suppression for a brief instant and lunged toward the confessing elder.","\"You deserve to die!\"","Boom!","Before he could move more than a single step, Bai Ren casually flicked his finger.","Bang!","The elder was blasted backward like a broken kite.","He crashed heavily against a distant pillar before falling to the floor, coughing up several mouthfuls of blood.","His cultivation was instantly sealed.","Seeing that violent reaction, Bai Zihan’s eyes narrowed.","He had obtained his answer.","If the first confession could still have been questioned, the second elder’s desperate attempt to silence him had confirmed everything."]},{"number":672,"title":"Chapter 672: Zhao Clan’s Turn","paragraphs":["The truth wasn’t anything unusual.","The Zhao Clan’s plan had begun centuries ago.","Like every major power, the Zhao Clan had naturally planted spies within the Li Clan.","However, unlike ordinary intelligence gathering, the Zhao Clan had been far more ambitious.","Rather than merely infiltrating disciples or servants, they had carefully selected a group of cultivators with clean backgrounds.","Each of them received resources, guidance, and fabricated identities before being sent into the Li Clan separately.","Their objective was simple.","Become true members of the Li Clan.","Every one of them repeatedly made contributions to the clan.","Some donated precious treasures.","Some completed dangerous missions.","Others risked their lives protecting Li Clan members during major conflicts.","Everything they did served a single purpose.","To earn the Li Clan’s complete trust.","Only after gaining sufficient merit would they slowly climb the clan hierarchy.","The process took centuries.","Many failed along the way.","Some died in battle before reaching important positions.","Others were eliminated during internal struggles.","A few abandoned the mission altogether.","By the end, only the two before Bai Zihan had successfully become elders of the Li Clan.","Li Jianhong’s expression became increasingly unsightly the more he learned.","He could accept spies from hostile factions.","Every major power engaged in such practices.","That was simply part of survival within the cultivation world.","However, the Zhao Clan was different.","For countless years, the Li Clan and Zhao Clan had been close allies.","They had shared interests, exchanged resources, and maintained a united front before the Bai Clan’s rise.","Yet all that time, the Zhao Clan had secretly nurtured spies within the highest ranks of the Li Clan.","Even elder positions had been infiltrated.","The realization filled Li Jianhong with both humiliation and fury.","It also made him realize one terrifying fact.","The Zhao Clan had never truly trusted the Li Clan.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan remained remarkably calm.","To him, the revelation wasn’t particularly surprising.","In fact, it perfectly matched Zhao Wutian’s personality.","Unlike the Li Clan, which preferred solving problems through strength, the Zhao Clan excelled at long-term planning.","Even as allies, Zhao Wutian would never place complete trust in another clan.","Alliances existed only because of shared interests.","The moment those interests disappeared, former allies could easily become the next enemies.","Once the Bai Clan was removed, the Li Clan and Zhao Clan would inevitably compete for supremacy over the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Preparing in advance for that possibility was exactly the sort of decision the Zhao Clan would make.","Bai Zihan had no intention of dwelling on the matter further.","The internal schemes between the Li Clan and Zhao Clan were ultimately insignificant to him.","The Li Clan had fallen under his control.","The next destination naturally became the Zhao Clan.","Unlike his visit to the Li Clan, however, this time Bai Zihan had no intention of going with only Bai Ren.","What interested him now was finishing today’s business.","He slowly turned around.","His gaze landed upon Li Jianhong.","\"It’s time to pay the Zhao Clan a visit.\"","The moment those words were spoken, Li Jianhong immediately understood Bai Zihan’s intention.","His expression became complicated.","The Zhao Clan... Was about to suffer the same fate as the Li Clan.","Bai Zihan looked at him indifferently.","\"Li Jianhong. Get ready. You’re coming with me.\"","***","The Zhao Clan had become unusually busy.","Today was the coronation of the new Emperor.","They were already making their final preparations before departing for the Imperial Capital.","No one doubted that today’s ceremony would remain peaceful.","Yu Feiyan still possessed considerable influence.","There was an overwhelming chance that she would appear to contest the throne.","When that happened, the Zhao Clan would naturally stand beside Yu Zidi.","Many disciples were discussing the matter excitedly.","At that moment, a guard hurriedly rushed through the clan gates.","His expression looked rather strange.","Before anyone could question him, he loudly announced the unexpected visitors.","\"Clan Leader! The Li Clan has arrived! And...\"","His voice paused slightly.","\"Bai Zihan has come with them.\"","Silence!","\"...What?\"","Several elders frowned.","Bai Zihan...","Together with the Li Clan?","How could those two possibly appear together?","For a brief moment, nobody could make sense of the situation.","However, some of the quicker-witted elders suddenly revealed delighted expressions.","Their eyes brightened.","\"The Li Clan succeeded?\"","\"They captured Bai Zihan?\"","\"It must be!\"","One elder nodded repeatedly.","\"Otherwise, why would Bai Zihan appear alongside Li Jianhong?\"","\"It seems the Li Clan acted before us.\"","The more they thought about it, the more reasonable it sounded.","After all, the Li Clan had always desired Bai Zihan’s death just as much as they did.","Capturing him alive before heading to the Imperial Capital wasn’t impossible.","Many Zhao Clan members couldn’t help but smile.","If Bai Zihan had truly fallen into their hands, then the Bai Clan had effectively lost its greatest pillar.","Soon afterward, the news reached Zhao Wutian.","Inside the main hall, Zhao Wutian was similarly surprised.","\"The Li Clan... and Bai Zihan?\"","He frowned briefly before slowly smiling.","\"It seems Li Jianhong has accomplished something extraordinary.\"","Without further delay, he ordered both parties to be invited inside.","Moments later, the main hall doors slowly opened.","Bai Zihan leisurely walked inside with Bai Ren behind him.","Beside them, Li Jianhong quietly entered the hall.","Several Li Clan elders followed closely behind.","The moment Zhao Wutian saw them, he immediately stood and laughed heartily.","\"Hahaha! It seems you’ve already taken care of Bai Zihan before today’s great event.\"","His laughter echoed throughout the hall.","Many Zhao Clan elders nodded in agreement.","Some even looked toward Bai Zihan with smug expressions.","However, as Zhao Wutian continued laughing, his smile gradually froze.","Something...","Didn’t seem right.","Li Jianhong showed no trace of accomplishment.","Instead, his face was gloomy.","His expression was incomparably ugly.","More importantly, the resentment in his eyes wasn’t directed toward Bai Zihan.","It was directed at Zhao Wutian.","Meanwhile, Bai Zihan stood calmly in the middle of the hall.","A faint smile rested on his face.","There wasn’t the slightest sign of someone who had been captured.","The strange atmosphere immediately caused Zhao Wutian’s heart to tighten.","His smile slowly disappeared.","An uneasy feeling suddenly surfaced within him.","Before he could ask anything—","Li Jianhong suddenly stepped forward.","His eyes burned with unconcealed fury.","He glared directly at Zhao Wutian.","The resentment that had accumulated throughout the journey finally erupted.","\"You...\"","Li Jianhong’s voice was ice-cold.","\"What exactly did you mean by planting your people inside my Li Clan?\"","The entire Zhao Clan hall instantly fell silent.","Every Zhao Clan elder’s expression changed.","Zhao Wutian’s pupils contracted for only a brief moment before immediately returning to normal.","A veteran schemer like him naturally wouldn’t admit to such a matter so easily.","Instead, he frowned deeply, as though he had heard something completely absurd.","\"What are you talking about?\"","His tone carried genuine confusion.","\"What people?\"","Before Li Jianhong could continue, several Zhao Clan elders also stepped forward.","One of them coldly glanced toward Bai Zihan before speaking.","\"Clan Leader Li, don’t tell me you’ve actually believed the words of an outsider?\"","Another elder nodded.","\"Bai Zihan is famous for his schemes.\"","\"If he truly said such things, then his intention is obvious.\"","\"He wishes to sow discord between our two clans. Once we begin doubting each other, the greatest beneficiary would naturally be the Bai Clan.\"","Several elders immediately voiced their agreement.","The more they thought about it, the more reasonable it seemed.","They wanted to shift the blame of having planted the spies to Bai Zihan sowing discord between their clan.","Meanwhile, Zhao Wutian slowly sighed.","A look of helplessness appeared on his face.","\"Brother Li. If there truly are misunderstandings between us...\"","\"We can settle them after today’s business.\"","His gaze calmly swept toward Bai Zihan.","Then a faint smile appeared.","\"Right now, Bai Zihan has already fallen into our hands. What are a few spies compared to him?\"","His tone remained composed.","\"If the Zhao Clan has truly wronged the Li Clan in this matter...\"","\"I am willing to compensate you afterward.\"","He deliberately avoided addressing the accusation directly.","Instead, he shifted the focus toward Bai Zihan.","In Zhao Wutian’s eyes, Li Jianhong wouldn’t make such a scene unless he was absolutely certain.","But as long as Bai Zihan had been captured, everything else became insignificant.","However, Li Jianhong suddenly laughed.","\"Hahaha...\"","The laughter echoed strangely throughout the hall.","It was neither triumphant nor mocking.","Instead, it was filled with bitterness.","He looked at Zhao Wutian as though looking at a complete fool.","\"What capture?\"","Li Jianhong slowly shook his head.","The ridicule in his eyes became increasingly obvious.","\"You think we could capture him?\"","The smile on Zhao Wutian’s face gradually stiffened.","Li Jianhong’s laughter abruptly ceased.","He looked directly into Zhao Wutian’s eyes.","His next sentence instantly caused the entire hall to fall silent.","\"The Li Clan has already surrendered to Bai Zihan!\""]},{"number":673,"title":"Chapter 673: The Zhao Clan’s Disbelief","paragraphs":["Shock!","Utter shock!","The moment those words left Li Jianhong’s mouth, the entire Zhao Clan hall erupted into complete chaos.","\"What?!\"","\"The Li Clan surrendered?\"","\"How could that ever happen?!\"","Countless Zhao Clan elders shot to their feet.","Some stared at Li Jianhong.","Others stared at Bai Zihan.","The expressions on their faces were filled with utter disbelief.","Even though those words had come from Li Jianhong’s own mouth, they still couldn’t bring themselves to believe them.","The Li Clan’s entire philosophy revolved around pursuing strength.","Even if they were to be destroyed, they would rather perish than surrender to someone else.","Meanwhile, Zhao Wutian remained rooted to his spot.","His eyes were fixed upon Li Jianhong.","Although he had heard every single word clearly, his mind simply couldn’t process them.","\"...What did you say?\"","His voice had unconsciously become hoarse.","Li Jianhong merely looked at him.","There wasn’t the slightest trace of impatience on his face.","After all, he knew just how absurd his words sounded.","Taking a deep breath, he slowly repeated himself.","\"The Li Clan... has surrendered.\"","Silence lasted only for an instant.","Then—","Boom!","Another wave of commotion swept through the hall.","\"No! Absolutely impossible!\"","\"Clan Leader Li, enough. This isn’t the time for jokes.\"","\"The coronation is about to begin. We don’t have time to entertain such nonsense.\"","Several Zhao Clan elders immediately denied it.","The Li Clan...","One of the Three Great Clans of the Desolate Heaven Empire...","Submitting without a fight?","Who would possibly believe such a thing?","Li Jianhong smiled bitterly.","There wasn’t the slightest amusement on his face.","Instead, he slowly spread his hands.","\"Do I look like I’m joking?\"","His voice was calm, almost helpless.","The hall gradually became quiet again.","Only now did everyone truly observe Li Jianhong.","Li Jianhong looked completely helpless and unwilling.","He had also positioned himself half a step behind Bai Zihan.","That position represented both status and his stance.","A subordinate naturally stood behind his superior.","No Clan Leader would willingly place himself in such a position unless he had truly submitted to another.","Zhao Wutian naturally noticed it as well.","His pupils shrank.","A terrifying thought suddenly surfaced in his mind.","(No...)","Before he could continue thinking, overwhelming anger surged through him.","He abruptly took a step forward.","His gaze locked firmly onto Li Jianhong.","\"Li Jianhong!\"","His voice thundered throughout the hall.","\"Have you gone mad?\"","The pressure of an Earth Immortal Realm expert burst forth uncontrollably.","The surrounding air instantly became heavy.","\"How could you possibly submit to Bai Zihan? You are the Clan Leader of the Li Clan!\"","\"One of the Three Great Clans of the Desolate Heaven Empire! You would rather bow your head to a junior than fight?\"","His face was filled with both anger and incomprehension.","No matter how talented Bai Zihan was...","No matter how powerful the Bai Clan had become...","He simply could not understand how someone like Li Jianhong could willingly surrender.","Li Jianhong looked at Zhao Wutian with a complicated expression.","There was pity, helplessness and also a trace of sympathy.","He knew exactly what Zhao Wutian was thinking.","After all, only a short while ago, he had thought the exact same thing, wanting to take care of Bai Zihan.","But one move was enough to make the Li Clan submit.","Even now, he still couldn’t comprehend how Bai Zihan had accomplished it.","With a single thought, Bai Zihan could reduce the entire Li Clan to a state worse than death.","Li Jianhong had searched every inch of his body countless times.","He still found nothing.","The other Li elders had done the same.","The result remained unchanged.","The source of Bai Zihan’s control was completely beyond their understanding.","As long as Bai Zihan possessed that mysterious method, Li Jianhong could no longer see any path for the Li Clan to oppose him.","That was precisely why he pitied Zhao Wutian though he also thought he deserved it for planting spies in his clan.","Soon, the Zhao Clan would understand that same despair.","Unfortunately, Zhao Wutian neither understood nor was willing to understand why Li Jianhong was making such an expression.","To him, Li Jianhong’s behavior was simply madness.","Since reasoning no longer worked, there was only one solution left.","His eyes turned cold.","\"Capture Bai Zihan!\"","The order echoed throughout the main hall.","Boom!","The Zhao Clan experts immediately erupted with terrifying auras.","One after another, elders stepped forward.","Several Earth Immortal Realm experts locked onto Bai Ren.","Meanwhile, the remaining elders fixed their killing intent upon Bai Zihan.","So what if the Li Clan had surrendered?","In Zhao Wutian’s eyes, that merely meant Li Jianhong had lost his mind.","The situation itself had not changed.","Bai Zihan had still voluntarily walked into the Zhao Clan’s territory.","He had brought only Bai Ren with him.","Such an opportunity was simply too precious to let slip away.","No matter what tricks Bai Zihan possessed...","As long as they captured him first, everything would come to an end.","\"Li Clan!\"","Bai Zihan spoke.","\"You know what you should do.\"","The moment those words fell—","Boom!","Li Jianhong took the first step forward.","Without the slightest hesitation, he stood directly before Bai Zihan.","The Li Clan elders also moved almost simultaneously.","One after another, they formed a protective wall around Bai Zihan and Bai Ren.","Their weapons remained lowered, yet their intentions were unmistakable.","Anyone wishing to touch Bai Zihan would first have to pass through them.","The sudden scene instantly froze the Zhao Clan.","Even Zhao Wutian’s expression stiffened. Then his face darkened completely.","An uncontrollable rage surged through his chest.","He truly couldn’t understand.","The Li Clan had surrendered.","Fine!","Although he couldn’t accept it, that was ultimately their own decision.","But now, they were actually protecting Bai Zihan?","It was a betrayal of the Zhao Clan.","His furious gaze swept across every Li Clan elder.","\"What are you doing?\"","His voice boomed throughout the hall.","\"Have all of you gone insane? You actually intend to stand against the Zhao Clan?\"","The Li Clan elders remained silent.","Seeing that, Zhao Wutian’s anger only intensified.","He wanted the Li Clan to stop protecting Bai Zihan, even if they had no intention of helping the Zhao Clan.","Because if the Li Clan truly chose to protect Bai Zihan, then today’s battle would become far more troublesome.","The Zhao Clan would undoubtedly win on its own territory.","But victory would come at a tremendous cost.","A cost he was unwilling to pay especially with the imperial coronation about to begin.","He stared directly at Li Jianhong.","His voice became noticeably calmer.","\"Even if your Li Clan has chosen to surrender, I won’t interfere. But must you truly protect him?\"","\"Step aside! The Zhao Clan’s grievance is with Bai Zihan alone.\"","\"As long as you don’t interfere, I won’t hold today’s events against the Li Clan.\"","Unfortunately, the Li Clan didn’t move an inch.","Nor did they show any sign of retreating.","It seemed as though they were prepared to stand with Bai Zihan to the very end if necessary."]},{"number":674,"title":"Chapter 674: The Price of Temptation","paragraphs":["\"Good! Good!\"","Zhao Wutian’s face twisted with fury.","\"The Li Clan has truly chosen to side with the Bai Clan!\"","His voice boomed throughout the entire hall.","\"If that’s your decision, then don’t blame the Zhao Clan for what comes next!\"","At this point, Zhao Wutian no longer cared why the Li Clan had made such a choice.","Whether they had been threatened...","Bribed...","Or had simply lost their minds...","None of it mattered anymore.","The moment they chose to stand before Bai Zihan, they had become enemies of the Zhao Clan.","There was no middle ground.","No room for reconciliation.","Boom!","Without another word, Zhao Wutian waved his hand.","The Zhao Clan experts immediately charged forward.","Terrifying spiritual pressure swept across the hall.","The Earth Immortal Realm experts targeted Bai Ren.","Meanwhile, the remaining elders rushed directly toward the defensive line formed by the Li Clan.","Although they had hesitated earlier because of Li Jianhong’s shocking move, they were no longer willing to delay.","However, before either side could even clash—","Thud!","One Zhao Clan elder suddenly stumbled.","His face twisted violently.","He clutched his chest with both hands.","\"W-What...\"","Before he could finish speaking—","Thud!","Another elder collapsed.","Then another.","Then another.","Within only a few breaths, several Zhao Clan experts had fallen onto the floor.","Every one of them wore expressions of unbearable agony.","\"Aaaaah!\"","\"My heart!\"","\"W-What’s happening?!\"","\"It hurts!\"","Their miserable screams instantly echoed throughout the hall.","The charging Zhao Clan experts abruptly stopped in their tracks.","Confusion immediately replaced the killing intent on their faces.","\"What happened?\"","\"They haven’t even attacked yet!\"","\"Why are they collapsing?\"","The sudden scene looked eerily familiar to Li Clan.","Li Jianhong couldn’t help narrowing his eyes.","He immediately recognized those expressions.","They were exactly the same as they had been not long ago.","But just like before, he hadn’t seen Bai Zihan make any move, nor had he sensed any abnormality that could have caused such a thing.","At the same time, the other Li Clan members secretly felt a sense of satisfaction.","Now the Zhao Clan was experiencing the same despair they had gone through earlier.","Unlike the Li Clan, however, the Zhao Clan had always been considerably more cautious.","Although the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art possessed astonishing effects, not every Zhao Clan expert had immediately chosen to cultivate it.","Many had remained suspicious.","Others preferred waiting longer before making their decision.","As a result, only a little over half of the Zhao Clan experts present had cultivated the technique.","Compared to the Li Clan, the Zhao Clan had undoubtedly been much more vigilant.","Unfortunately, even they ultimately couldn’t resist the temptation of rapidly increasing their cultivation.","The Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art was simply too attractive.","In the end, more than half of the Zhao Clan’s experts had still fallen for it.","Now, they were paying the price.","The remaining Zhao Clan experts instinctively retreated several steps.","None of them dared continue their charge.","Instead, they stared nervously at their companions rolling across the ground.","Fear gradually surfaced within their eyes.","No one knew what had happened.","No one saw Bai Zihan make a move.","Yet several elders had suddenly lost all ability to fight.","The unknown was always the most terrifying.","Several Zhao Clan elders immediately began checking the fallen cultivators.","Some inspected their meridians.","Others searched for poison.","A few even used their spiritual sense to probe every inch of their bodies.","The result was exactly the same as the Li Clan’s.","Nothing!","There wasn’t the slightest abnormality yet the elders continued screaming in unbearable agony.","The bizarre scene caused every remaining Zhao Clan expert to hesitate.","No one dared take another step forward.","Their cautious nature had completely taken over.","Until they understood exactly what had happened, none of them were willing to risk becoming the next person writhing on the ground.","Zhao Wutian’s expression darkened to the extreme.","His gaze swept across the elders writhing on the ground before finally settling on Bai Zihan.","\"What did you do?\"","Then his eyes shifted toward the Li Clan.","He noticed their expressions.","There was no surprise, only sympathy.","Some elders even subconsciously revealed bitter smiles.","It was the expression of someone who had experienced the exact same nightmare.","In that instant, everything connected.","Zhao Wutian’s pupils shrank.","\"So that’s it...\"","He finally understood.","He finally understood why the Li Clan had surrendered.","It wasn’t because they lacked backbone nor because they feared the Bai Clan’s strength.","It was because they had experienced the same mysterious method.","The same despair.","The same pain.","Faced with an enemy capable of reducing them to such a state without even lifting a finger, what choice had they truly been given?","Meanwhile, Li Jianhong was also observing the Zhao Clan.","However, his attention wasn’t on those who had fallen.","It was on those who remained standing.","His brows gradually furrowed.","Only about half of the Zhao Clan experts had collapsed.","The others, including Zhao Wutian himself, remained completely unaffected.","At first, Li Jianhong couldn’t understand why.","But after carefully looking at those still standing, a terrifying possibility suddenly emerged within his mind.","His breathing unconsciously became heavier.","(The cultivation technique...)","He immediately remembered it.","The Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art!","He knew that, with Zhao Wutian’s personality, he wouldn’t cultivate the technique until he was absolutely certain it was safe.","However, he and the other Li Clan members had cultivated it without much restraint.","Previously, those Zhao Clan spies had also remained unaffected.","The reason was likely because they, too, had followed Zhao Wutian’s instructions and refrained from cultivating the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","Li Jianhong suddenly felt a chill run down his spine as a terrifying realization slowly took shape within his mind.","(So that’s how it is...)","If his speculation was correct, then everyone who had cultivated the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art had unknowingly fallen under Bai Zihan’s control.","The thought alone was enough to make his scalp turn numb.","However, Li Jianhong wisely remained silent.","He had no intention of voicing his speculation.","What benefit would there be in exposing it?","Would it improve his own situation?","No!","It would only offend Bai Zihan further.","If anything, the more he understood the truth, the less willing he became to oppose him.","Because that truth was far more terrifying than he had initially imagined.","The Li Clan!","The Zhao Clan!","The other clans!","Countless sects throughout the Desolate Heaven Empire!","Over the past several months, the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art had spread across the entire empire like wildfire.","Too many cultivators had practiced it.","Even cultivators from powerful backgrounds had regarded it as their greatest opportunity.","Many people who hadn’t cultivated the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art felt they were falling behind in cultivation.","As a result, more and more people chose to cultivate it.","If even he, the Li Clan Leader, had been unable to resist the temptation, then who else could?","Then, if his speculation was truly correct...","Bai Zihan’s influence no longer stopped at the Li Clan or Zhao Clan.","It extended throughout the entire Desolate Heaven Empire.","The Li-Zhao Alliance!","The Bai Clan Alliance!","Even the Imperial Family’s cultivators...","There was a very real possibility that many of them had already cultivated the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","If so...","Then Bai Zihan’s hand already rested upon more than half of the empire’s cultivation world.","Perhaps... Even more.","The more Li Jianhong thought about it, the colder his heart became.","He could no longer fathom just how deeply Bai Zihan’s influence had penetrated the Desolate Heaven Empire.","His grasp over the empire was likely far greater than anyone had ever imagined.","At that moment, the final trace of unwillingness hidden deep within Li Jianhong’s heart completely disappeared.","Before such a person, resistance was meaningless.","Just like an ant whose life rested in another’s hand, he finally understood that he no longer possessed even the qualification to resist."]},{"number":675,"title":"Chapter 675: The Zhao Clan’s Defeat","paragraphs":["Although Zhao Wutian was far more cunning than Li Jianhong and normally would have connected the clues much faster, the overwhelming shock before him prevented him from thinking clearly.","Moreover, unlike Li Jianhong, Zhao Wutian had no idea that the Li Clan had widely cultivated the Heavenly Mandate Assimilation Art.","He naturally couldn’t connect everything to that cultivation technique.","The only thing on his mind was that the Li Clan must have experienced the exact same mysterious method and had been forced into submission.","However, Zhao Wutian still believed they had the upper hand in this situation.","Although more than half of the Zhao Clan’s experts had fallen, the remaining half still stood ready for battle.","Those who remained should be more than enough to deal with the Li Clan’s forces.","As long as these remaining forces remained unaffected by whatever trick Bai Zihan had used, he still believed that victory was within his reach.","His eyes instantly turned cold.","\"Attack!\"","The remaining Zhao Clan experts erupted into motion once again.","Every cultivator who remained unaffected charged directly toward Bai Zihan.","Seeing the Zhao Clan move once more, the Li Clan experts immediately stepped forward.","Boom!","Both sides collided head-on.","Powerful Qi exploded throughout the hall.","Sword Qi, palm techniques, and countless treasures filled the sky.","\"Don’t let them near Clan leader Bai!\"","The Li Clan fought desperately to maintain the defensive line before Bai Zihan.","Now that Li Jianhong had discovered the truth, he was more desperate to show how sincere they were.","He knew that going against the Bai Clan was virtually impossible, so it was better for him to make a more favorable impression on Bai Zihan as much as he could.","This situation was the perfect opportunity to prove both his sincerity and that the Li Clan had truly submitted and willing to do everything Bai Zihan commands.","And also to show just how useful they were. They resisted the Zhao Clan’s attack with everything they had.","However, this was the Zhao Clan’s territory.","No matter how powerful the Li Clan might be, how could they possibly contend against the Zhao Clan on its own territory?","More and more Zhao Clan experts continued gathering from every direction.","Even if the Li Clan resisted with everything they had, they simply couldn’t block every attack.","Sooner or later, someone would break through.","Zhao Wutian naturally understood this as well.","His eyes remained fixed upon Bai Zihan.","No matter what tricks Bai Zihan had up his sleeve, as long as that didn’t affect everyone, they still had a chance.","Previously, they had remained cautious, thinking they might also collapse like those Zhao Clan members.","But they hadn’t.","That gave Zhao Wutian even more confidence.","Unfortunately, he hadn’t included one person in his calculations.","Bai Ren!","The old man, who had remained silent from beginning to end, finally took a single step forward.","Boom!","The instant his foot landed upon the ground, an overwhelming aura burst forth.","Golden Immortal Realm!","The terrifying pressure descended upon the entire Zhao Clan like a collapsing heaven.","Every Zhao Clan expert felt their breathing stagnate.","Before anyone could react—","Bai Ren vanished.","His figure appeared before the strongest Zhao Clan Earth Immortal, Zhao Wujin, almost instantly.","Zhao Wujin was both startled and terrified.","He had witnessed firsthand just how powerful Bai Ren was when he slew the Half-Qilin with that Saint-Grade Sword.","If Bai Ren used the same method again, Zhao Wujin knew he wouldn’t survive.","Fortunately, Bai Ren had no intention of bullying them too much and didn’t even draw the Saint-Grade Sword.","One palm descended.","Boom!","Zhao Wujin spat out a mouthful of blood before being blasted through several walls.","Before the others could recover from their shock—","Bai Ren appeared again.","Another punch.","Another Earth Immortal was sent crashing into the ground.","Every strike was simple.","Every strike was direct.","Yet every strike carried an irresistible force.","No one could withstand even a single move.","Within only a few breaths, every one of the Zhao Clan’s Earth Immortals had been defeated.","Some lay unconscious.","Others could no longer even stand.","The remaining Zhao Clan elites immediately lost all courage.","Even their strongest Earth Immortals couldn’t withstand a single move.","How could they, who were far weaker, possibly resist?","Even if they somehow managed to keep Bai Ren occupied, the Li Clan traitors were no easy opponents either.","Within moments, the once chaotic battlefield had become deathly silent.","Only one person remained standing before Bai Zihan.","Zhao Wutian!","His face had long since lost its previous confidence.","Instead, it was filled with disbelief.","More than half of his experts were still writhing on the ground in unbearable agony.","The remaining elites had already been defeated by Bai Ren and those traitorous Li Clan members.","The enormous Zhao Clan had been brought to the brink of defeat in only a matter of minutes.","Zhao Wutian slowly turned his gaze toward Bai Zihan.","The young man remained standing exactly where he had been from the very beginning.","There wasn’t the slightest hint of panic or surprise on his face.","It was as though everything unfolding before him had already been calculated long ago.","Seeing that calm expression, Zhao Wutian slowly closed his eyes.","A bitter smile appeared on his face.","He understood now that there had never been a chance from the very beginning.","The mysterious method that had instantly crippled more than half of the Zhao Clan’s experts, combined with Bai Ren’s overwhelming strength...","The outcome had already been decided the moment Bai Zihan stepped through the Zhao Clan’s gates.","Even if he had prepared countless more schemes...","Even if the Zhao Clan had activated every hidden trump card...","None of it would have changed the result.","Against absolute strength and an incomprehensible method, every calculation became meaningless.","Slowly, Zhao Wutian let out a long sigh.","The unwillingness within his heart gradually disappeared.","He was a smart man.","Perhaps not the strongest.","But smart enough to recognize when resistance had become completely pointless.","Continuing this battle would only cause more damage to the Zhao Clan, and it would accomplish nothing.","Moreover, he understood that even if he surrendered, Bai Zihan wouldn’t destroy the Zhao Clan.","The Li Clan was the perfect example standing before him.","That alone was enough for Zhao Wutian to understand one thing.","Bai Zihan had a use for them.","Otherwise, with the Bai Clan’s current strength, erasing either the Li Clan or the Zhao Clan would not have been particularly difficult.","Since that was the case, there was no reason to throw away the Zhao Clan’s future over meaningless pride.","If this had merely been a contest between equals, Zhao Wutian would have fought until the very end.","He would never willingly bow his head.","But this wasn’t a battle between equals.","This was a battle against someone who had already rendered resistance meaningless before the fight had truly begun.","There was nothing left to struggle against.","Without another moment of hesitation, Zhao Wutian slowly lowered his head.","The remaining Zhao Clan elders watched silently.","No one spoke.","No one objected.","Their strongest experts had already fallen.","More than half of their forces were writhing on the ground.","The rest had been completely suppressed.","They understood just as clearly as Zhao Wutian did.","The Zhao Clan had lost completely.","Bai Zihan quietly watched Zhao Wutian.","After several moments, he gave a slight nod.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","He appreciated intelligent people, especially those who knew when to give up.","Such people saved him considerable time.","Otherwise, he would have had to waste even more effort convincing them.","Since Zhao Wutian had already made the correct decision himself, things became much simpler.","Meanwhile, Li Jianhong, who stood beside Bai Zihan, suddenly felt a surge of grievance.","His eyelids twitched uncontrollably.","He looked toward Zhao Wutian, then back toward Bai Zihan.","His heart suddenly felt extremely wronged.","He had suffered through what he could only describe as a living nightmare.","His entire clan had been tortured until every shred of dignity had been stripped away.","Only after enduring pain that felt worse than death had he finally surrendered.","Yet Zhao Wutian...","This fellow hadn’t even experienced a fraction of that torment.","He had simply taken one look at the situation, realized he couldn’t win, and surrendered immediately.","Then Bai Zihan actually accepted it without any torture.","The more Li Jianhong thought about it, the more wronged he felt.","He had originally believed Zhao Wutian would be forced to experience the exact same nightmare as the Li Clan.","He had even looked forward to watching the Zhao Clan scream in agony just as they had.","Instead, Zhao Wutian had escaped all of it simply by surrendering early.","For the first time in many years, Li Jianhong genuinely felt that life was unfair.","He couldn’t help thinking that perhaps he should have been smarter and surrendered the moment he realized he had lost.","(Dammit! All that suffering... for nothing.)"]},{"number":676,"title":"Chapter 676: Assault on the Bai Clan","paragraphs":["After settling the matter of the Zhao Clan, Bai Zihan wasted no time.","Bai Zihan calmly issued his first command.","\"The Li Clan and Zhao Clan will immediately dispatch most of your elite cultivators. They are to secretly guard the Bai Clan!\"","Neither Li Jianhong nor Zhao Wutian understood why they needed to protect the Bai Clan.","The current Bai Clan was already the strongest force within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","With Bai Ren alone standing guard, who could possibly threaten them?","Even after losing a portion of their strength today, the Bai Clan could still suppress any single force within the empire.","The order simply didn’t make sense.","However, neither of them dared question Bai Zihan.","They merely nodded obediently.","Whatever Bai Zihan wanted, they would do.","Bai Zihan then issued his second order.","\"Neither the Li Clan nor the Zhao Clan will interfere in today’s coronation. You will not provide Yu Zidi with any assistance.\"","Those words caused both Clan Leaders to freeze.","Their expressions changed noticeably.","The Li Clan and Zhao Clan had secretly supported Yu Zidi from the very beginning.","Very few people knew of this arrangement.","In fact, even many of their closest allies remained completely unaware.","The cooperation had been kept under the highest level of secrecy.","Yet Bai Zihan seemed to have already known about it all along.","After everything they had experienced today, however, this revelation no longer surprised them as much.","Compared to the mysterious method capable of controlling their lives, knowing about their secret alliance seemed almost insignificant.","Neither of them objected.","They simply accepted the order.","Deep inside, both silently sighed.","Without the support of the Li Clan and Zhao Clan, Yu Zidi had virtually no chance against Yu Feiyan.","At least, that was what they believed.","Neither of them had any idea that several foreign powers would eventually help Yu Zidi.","They had underestimated him too much, believing that once Yu Zidi took the throne, they would be able to control him.","After issuing the necessary arrangements, Bai Zihan left the remaining matters to the two Clan Leaders.","Orders quickly spread throughout both clans.","Once everything had been arranged, Bai Zihan, Bai Ren, Li Jianhong, Zhao Wutian, and the remaining experts finally departed toward the Imperial Capital.","Meanwhile, far away from them, a different force had already begun moving.","The moment Bai Zihan and the Bai Clan’s strongest experts left for the coronation, numerous hidden cultivators emerged from the shadows.","One after another.","They gathered with astonishing speed.","Rows of flying ships slowly appeared above the horizon.","Among them were the armies of the Desolate Heaven Empire, experts from the Vermilion Pill Empire, the Tianyu Empire, and the Azure Moon Empire.","The massive coalition advanced silently toward a single destination.","The Bai Clan!","***","The commander of the Imperial Army stood at the front of the massive coalition.","His sharp eyes remained fixed upon the distant Bai Clan.","A jade communication token slowly dimmed in his hand.","The latest report had finally arrived.","\"Bai Zihan has already departed. He has taken Bai Ren and a large number of Bai Clan experts with him to the Imperial Capital.\"","A faint smile appeared on his face.","Everything was proceeding exactly according to plan.","The Bai Clan had undoubtedly become weaker.","Although it still remained the strongest power within the Desolate Heaven Empire, that superiority was now meaningless.","After all, this was not a battle between two factions.","It was the combined might of four empires.","The Desolate Heaven Empire!","The Vermilion Pill Empire!","The Tianyu Empire!","The Azure Moon Empire!","Together, they possessed overwhelming superiority in both numbers and experts.","How could they possibly lose?","No one believed such a thing was possible.","Still, none of them acted immediately.","Patience remained essential.","They continued observing the Bai Clan from afar.","Minutes slowly passed.","Half an hour.","Then another half hour.","An entire hour slipped by.","Finally, the commander slowly raised his hand.","\"There is no need to wait any longer.\"","A cold smile spread across his face.","\"This is the perfect opportunity.\"","His raised hand suddenly dropped.","\"Attack!\"","Boom!","The countless flying ships instantly accelerated.","Like a dark tide covering the heavens, the coalition army surged toward the Bai Clan.","Their killing intent shook the sky itself.","Within moments, they arrived before the Bai Clan’s gates.","The Bai Clan had naturally discovered them long ago.","The alarm bells had already sounded throughout the entire clan.","An enormous defensive formation suddenly rose into the sky.","A massive barrier enveloped the entire Bai Clan.","Seeing the barrier appear, many experts from the four empires laughed.","\"A defensive formation? So what?\"","One Earth Immortal sneered.","\"The Bai Clan truly thinks a mere formation can stop us?\"","Another expert looked at the barrier with disdain.","\"It won’t even last a minute.\"","Facing the combined assault of so many experts, what could a defensive formation possibly accomplish?","Without hesitation, the commander waved his hand.","\"Break it!\"","Boom!","Countless attacks exploded simultaneously.","The sky itself seemed to collapse beneath the overwhelming bombardment.","Wave after wave of terrifying attacks continuously struck the barrier.","The entire formation trembled violently.","However, one minute passed.","The barrier remained intact.","Three minutes passed.","Still intact.","Five minutes.","Nothing changed.","Ten minutes later...","The enormous formation continued standing proudly above the Bai Clan.","Not even a visible crack had appeared.","The laughter from the coalition army gradually disappeared.","Instead, confusion spread through their ranks.","\"What kind of formation is this?\"","One Earth Immortal frowned deeply.","\"This isn’t a Grade-6 Formation. If it were, it should have shattered long ago.\"","Another expert stared fixedly at the glowing barrier.","His expression became increasingly grave.","\"Could it be... a Grade-7 Formation?\"","The suggestion immediately caused countless people to shake their heads.","Impossible!","The Eastern Continent simply did not possess anyone capable of establishing a Grade-7 Formation.","Such a formation should never exist here.","Even so, no one could explain the current situation.","After a brief silence, the commander calmly spoke.","\"It doesn’t matter. Even if it truly is a Grade-7 Formation... it cannot withstand us forever.\"","Everyone immediately nodded.","That was indeed the truth.","No formation possessed infinite power.","As long as they continued their relentless bombardment, sooner or later the barrier would collapse.","Thus, the attacks continued.","Inside the Bai Clan, Bai Tianheng calmly stood atop the wall.","Around him, countless Bai Clan cultivators silently watched the continuous bombardment.","No trace of panic could be seen on anyone’s face.","Everything had unfolded exactly as Bai Zihan had predicted.","The only thing that surprised Bai Tianheng was Yu Zidi’s courage.","He truly had not expected Yu Zidi to secretly collude with foreign empires in order to attack the Bai Clan.","Such a decision was no different from inviting wolves into one’s home.","Even if Yu Zidi eventually obtained the throne, the Desolate Heaven Empire would undoubtedly pay an enormous price.","Still, none of that mattered anymore.","Bai Tianheng calmly watched the coalition army continue wasting their Qi.","He had no intention of stopping them.","The more power they exhausted attacking the formation, the easier the battle afterward would be.","Time slowly passed.","Under the relentless bombardment, the barrier finally began to flicker.","Tiny ripples appeared across its surface.","Soon, several faint cracks gradually spread through the protective barrier.","Seeing this, excitement immediately erupted throughout the coalition army.","\"It’s breaking!\"","\"Keep attacking!\"","\"We’re almost through!\""]},{"number":677,"title":"Chapter 677: Reinforcements From The Li and Zhao Clans","paragraphs":["Inside the Bai Clan, Bai Tianheng finally smiled.","He slowly raised his hand.","\"Deactivate the formation.\"","The order immediately spread throughout the clan.","The enormous defensive barrier slowly dissolved into countless streams of spiritual light before disappearing completely.","The sudden disappearance of the barrier delighted the coalition forces.","\"So they’ve finally given up!\"","\"They’ve exhausted the formation!\"","Without another word, the coalition army charged forward.","Like a flood breaking through a dam, countless cultivators rushed toward the Bai Clan.","At the very same moment, Bai Tianheng slowly drew his weapon.","His calm voice echoed throughout the battlefield.","\"Kill!\"","Boom!","The Bai Clan gates burst open.","Countless Bai Clan experts surged forward like dragons leaving the sea.","The two great armies finally collided head-on.","Boom!","The instant the two armies collided, the entire battlefield descended into chaos.","Explosions echoed continuously across the sky.","Countless techniques illuminated the heavens as though thousands of stars had fallen upon the battlefield.","The coalition army possessed an overwhelming numerical advantage.","Wave after wave of cultivators surged relentlessly toward the Bai Clan.","Whenever one cultivator fell, another immediately took his place.","However, the moment the battle truly began, the coalition quickly discovered something unexpected.","The Bai Clan’s individual strength far exceeded their estimates.","Moreover, every Bai Clan cultivator seemed capable of fighting opponents above their cultivation realm.","Although greatly outnumbered, the Bai Clan showed no signs of being overwhelmed.","Instead, every charge launched by the coalition was met head-on.","Boom!","High above the battlefield, Bai Chu erupted into motion.","The moment he entered the battlefield, an Earth Immortal from the Tianyu Empire was immediately forced back.","Before the latter could stabilize himself, a brilliant sword light pierced through the sky.","Blood sprayed everywhere.","The Earth Immortal’s body exploded into countless fragments.","He had not even managed to exchange three moves.","Before the surrounding experts could recover from their shock—","Boom!","Bai Chu’s figure flashed once again.","Another Earth Immortal from the Azure Moon Empire was sent crashing toward the ground.","The moment he struck the earth, Bai Chu’s sword descended.","The Earth Immortal perished instantly.","Bai Chu moved across the battlefield like an unstoppable war god.","Within only a short time, several Earth Immortal experts had already fallen beneath his sword.","The coalition commanders’ expressions changed drastically.","\"This monster...\"","\"Stop him!\"","\"If this continues, he’ll slaughter all of us!\"","Without hesitation, more Earth Immortal experts rushed toward Bai Chu.","One...","Three...","Five...","Even that was not enough.","Only after ten Earth Immortal experts joined forces did Bai Chu’s terrifying momentum finally slow.","The ten surrounded him from every direction, unleashing their strongest techniques without holding anything back.","Even then, none of them dared become careless nor did they think they could kill him.","Simply keeping a Golden Immortal occupied was already an enormous achievement.","Meanwhile, battles erupted throughout every corner of the battlefield.","The coalition gradually realized another shocking fact.","The Bai Clan possessed far more Immortal Realm experts than they had anticipated.","However, reality proved otherwise.","Earth Immortals continuously emerged from within the Bai Clan.","Immortal Realm experts joined the battlefield one after another.","The battle gradually turned into a brutal war of attrition.","Still, the coalition army retained one undeniable advantage.","Numbers!","They possessed cultivators from four different empires.","Their total force exceeded the Bai Clan’s by several times.","Although the Bai Clan’s quality was superior, quantity itself eventually became a weapon.","The coalition commanders remained confident.","\"As long as this continues...\"","\"The Bai Clan will eventually exhaust themselves.\"","\"No matter how powerful they are, they cannot fight forever.\"","Many experts nodded in agreement.","The Bai Clan had indeed exceeded every expectation.","But in the end...","There were simply too many enemies.","As long as they continued pressing the attack without giving the Bai Clan a chance to recover...","Victory would eventually belong to the coalition or so they believed.","The battle continued to rage across the Bai Clan.","Explosions echoed endlessly.","Blood stained the earth.","Although the coalition still possessed the advantage in numbers, the fierce resistance of the Bai Clan had already exceeded every expectation.","Just then—","Rumble!","The sound of countless flying ships approaching suddenly echoed from the distance.","Everyone instinctively looked toward the horizon.","Rows upon rows of flying ships rapidly approached the battlefield.","The sudden appearance of the unknown force immediately alarmed both sides.","No one knew whose side the newcomers intended to support.","At the front of the coalition army, the commander of the Imperial Army narrowed his eyes.","Soon, he recognized the banners completely.","A smile gradually appeared on his face.","\"So it’s them.\"","He immediately raised his hand.","\"Don’t attack them!\"","He thought that it might be reinforcement for the Bai Clan, but seeing the Li Clan and Zhao Clan banners, he felt relieved.","Before long, the Li Clan and Zhao Clan fleets arrived before the battlefield.","Leading them were several elders from both clans.","The commander looked toward them.","\"What are you doing here?\"","Although he knew that these two clans were allies, their unexpected appearance still kept him on guard.","One of the Zhao Clan elders immediately stepped forward.","He respectfully cupped his fists.","\"We have come under His Highness Yu Zidi’s secret orders. Our mission is to assist the coalition army and destroy the Bai Clan.\"","Hearing those words, the commander’s final trace of suspicion disappeared.","After all, everyone in the Desolate Heaven Empire knew that the Li Clan and Zhao Clan had been sworn enemies of the Bai Clan for countless years.","Moreover, he was well aware that both clans secretly supported Yu Zidi.","It wasn’t strange for Yu Zidi to summon them at such a crucial moment.","Looking at the current battlefield, the commander couldn’t help but nod inwardly.","Although the coalition still held the advantage, the Bai Clan’s strength had greatly exceeded their expectations.","Every additional ally would reduce their losses and increase their chances of success.","His expression softened considerably.","\"Very well! Join the attack immediately.\"","The Li Clan and Zhao Clan elders nodded.","Without another word, their armies immediately advanced.","Countless cultivators surged toward the battlefield.","Seeing this, many coalition experts smiled.","With the Li Clan and Zhao Clan joining them, the Bai Clan would undoubtedly collapse.","The Li Clan and Zhao Clan forces rapidly approached the center of the battlefield.","Soon, both armies had entered the coalition’s formation.","Many coalition cultivators even moved aside, allowing their supposed allies to pass.","No one guarded against them.","After all, who would suspect their own reinforcements?","Then—","The eyes of the Li Clan and Zhao Clan cultivators suddenly turned cold.","\"Attack!\"","The roar exploded across the battlefield.","Shing!","Thousands of weapons were unsheathed simultaneously.","However, those blades did not slash toward the Bai Clan.","Instead, they turned toward the completely unsuspecting coalition army.","Blood instantly filled the sky.","One coalition cultivator after another was cut down before they could even react.","Several Immortal Realm cultivators were pierced straight through the chest.","Immortal Realm experts had their heads severed before they even understood what was happening.","The sudden betrayal instantly threw the coalition army into complete chaos.","\"What?!\"","\"They’re attacking us!\"","\"Li Clan! Zhao Clan! Have you all gone mad?!\"","Panicked cries echoed everywhere.","The commander of the Imperial Army stared blankly at the scene before him.","His eyes nearly popped out of their sockets.","\"What are you doing?!\"","His furious roar shook the battlefield.","\"Have the Li Clan and Zhao Clan betrayed the Desolate Heaven Empire?!\"","The leading elder of the Zhao Clan merely smiled coldly.","His eyes were filled with killing intent. His Qi erupted violently.","\"You can ask that in hell!\"","Boom!","His attack instantly blasted an unsuspecting Earth Immortal backward.","At almost the same moment, the Li Clan experts also launched their fiercest attacks.","Because the coalition had never expected betrayal, countless experts died before they could even raise their defenses.","The battlefield was instantly thrown into disorder.","Originally, the coalition army had barely managed to suppress the Bai Clan through sheer numbers.","Now, not only had those numbers suddenly shrunk, but another two Great Clans had joined the Bai Clan’s side.","The balance of the battlefield overturned almost instantly.","The coalition’s numerical advantage disappeared in the blink of an eye.","Instead, they found themselves surrounded from both the front and the rear.","The hunters had become the hunted!"]},{"number":678,"title":"Chapter 678: Yu Zidi’s Last Bargain","paragraphs":["Back to the Imperial Palace!","Yu Zidi’s entire body trembled with uncontrollable rage.","Never in his entire life had he experienced such betrayal at such a critical moment.","His bloodshot eyes slowly shifted toward Li Jianhong and Zhao Wutian.","He stared at the two of them as though he were seeing them for the first time.","His chest rose and fell violently.","He simply couldn’t comprehend it.","Just yesterday...","They had finalized every detail of their plan to destroy the Bai Clan.","They had discussed how to divide the Bai Clan’s resources.","Everything had already been settled.","Yet today...","Those same two people were openly standing beside the Bai Clan.","Not only had they abandoned him, but they had even dispatched the elites of their clans to protect the Bai Clan’s territory.","How could such a thing happen?","His mind desperately searched for an explanation.","(Could it be...)","(Had the conflict between the Three Great Clans been fake from the very beginning?)","The thought had only just appeared before he immediately rejected it.","The Bai Clan, Li Clan, and Zhao Clan had been mortal enemies for thousands of years.","How could all of that have been an act?","(Why?)","Why would the Li Clan and Zhao Clan betray him?","Hadn’t he already promised them enough?","Once the Bai Clan fell...","Half of the Bai Clan’s territory...","Half of its resources...","Everything had already been promised to them.","He had offered terms generous enough to satisfy even the greediest clans.","Yu Zidi simply couldn’t understand nor did he have the luxury of continuing to think.","Only now did he finally realize the situation he had fallen into.","On one side, Yu Feiyan’s forces had already surrounded the Imperial Palace.","On the other hand, the Bai Clan now possessed the support of both the Li Clan and the Zhao Clan.","Now wasn’t the time to think about why.","It was time to think about how to escape this situation.","The foreign delegations were no better.","The representatives from the Vermilion Pill Empire, Tianyu Empire, Azure Cloud Empire, and Jade River Empire all wore expressions of utter disbelief.","Their minds buzzed blankly.","They had heard every word transmitted through the communication jade.","\"Our forces... have almost been wiped out.\"","The sentence echoed repeatedly inside their minds.","Their faces gradually turned pale.","Although they hadn’t dispatched every cultivator from their empires, those sent to attack the Bai Clan were unquestionably among their elites.","Every one of them had been carefully selected.","Such a force...","Had actually been annihilated?","The representatives found it almost impossible to accept.","Originally, they had agreed to assist Yu Zidi because they saw an opportunity.","By helping him seize the throne, they could eliminate both the Bai Clan and then the Mu Clan in a single move.","Afterward, the Desolate Heaven Empire would become significantly weaker.","Their own empires could then seize countless benefits.","That had been the entire purpose behind today’s cooperation.","But now...","The Bai Clan still stood, which meant eliminating the Mu Clan had become virtually impossible.","Instead, it was their own forces that had suffered devastating losses.","The realization made every representative’s heart bleed.","Those weren’t expendable soldiers.","They were the very elites of their respective empires.","Many of the experts who had fallen had required centuries to nurture.","Some had consumed immeasurable resources before reaching their current cultivation.","Now, they had all been buried outside the Bai Clan.","Several representatives unconsciously clenched their fists.","Their expressions became incomparably ugly.","Originally, this had been nothing more than a profitable transaction.","Now, it has become a disaster.","Even if they managed to leave the Desolate Heaven Empire alive today, they had no idea how they would explain such catastrophic losses upon returning to their respective empires.","Worst of all, they were now trapped inside the Imperial Palace, facing Yu Feiyan’s forces.","Even if they helped Yu Zidi suppress Yu Feiyan’s forces, it would all be for nothing.","They couldn’t deal with the Bai Clan.","There was no benefit even if Yu Zidi somehow became the Emperor of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Qin Lingxiao shook her head.","A trace of disappointment flashed across her beautiful eyes.","She had already expected this outcome.","Still, a small part of her had hoped Yu Zidi’s words would prove true.","Unfortunately, the result was exactly as she had anticipated.","With Bai Chu’s Golden Immortal Realm cultivation guarding the Bai Clan and Bai Zihan’s meticulous planning, Qin Lingxiao had always believed it would be extraordinarily difficult for anyone to destroy them.","What truly surprised her, however, wasn’t the victory itself.","It was the Li Clan and the Zhao Clan.","Those two clans had been the Bai Clan’s mortal enemies for thousands of years.","Their hatred ran deep, and she learned about it very thoroughly.","Yet somehow, Bai Zihan had managed to make them not only abandon Yu Zidi, but even dispatch their elite cultivators to defend the Bai Clan.","That was far more unbelievable than defeating the coalition itself.","Even overwhelming strength alone shouldn’t have been enough to accomplish such a thing.","There had to be something else...","Perhaps something similar to her own technique.","Qin Lingxiao’s eyes unconsciously drifted toward Bai Zihan.","The curiosity within them deepened once again.","(Just what did you do...?)","However, now wasn’t the time to dwell on it.","Since the answer she wanted had already been revealed, there was no reason to delay any longer.","A faint killing intent gradually appeared within Qin Lingxiao’s eyes.","It was time to finish everything.","Meanwhile, Yu Zidi’s entire body tensed.","He could clearly feel the killing intent directed toward him.","His mind raced frantically.","His greatest reliance had always been the foreign delegations.","Even now, his own forces still held an advantage over Yu Feiyan’s army.","The only true variable remained Qin Lingxiao.","As long as the foreign delegations continued supporting him, he still believed there was a chance to seize the throne.","But that assumption depended on one crucial condition.","The foreign delegations had to be willing to continue fighting.","Yu Zidi slowly turned toward them.","Every representative wore an incomparably ugly expression.","Not one of them looked interested in continuing this battle.","Their minds were no longer focused on the fight.","Instead, they were all thinking about the exact same thing.","How to escape!","The coalition army they had dispatched to destroy the Bai Clan had almost been completely annihilated.","Their empires had suffered catastrophic losses.","And now, Bai Zihan knew their force has participated in the attack.","Would someone as ruthless as Bai Zihan simply let them leave?","The answer was obvious.","No!","The Bai Clan!","The Li Clan!","The Zhao Clan!","Combined with Yu Feiyan’s forces, none of the foreign delegations believed they possessed the strength to escape safely.","If they remained here any longer, their chances of survival would only decrease.","They had to leave immediately before Bai Zihan had time to deal with them.","Just then—","\"Wait!\"","Yu Zidi’s desperate roar echoed throughout the Imperial Palace.","Everyone turned toward him.","His eyes swept across every foreign representative. His voice was filled with urgency.","\"As long as you help me seize the throne today, I swear upon my imperial bloodline. After becoming Emperor, I will cede all the territories along the borders adjoining your respective empires!\"","Those words instantly caused countless people to gasp.","The expressions of the foreign representatives changed slightly.","Even Yu Feiyan frowned.","The border territories of the Desolate Heaven Empire were immensely valuable.","The empire had fought countless wars over those lands throughout history.","If those territories were handed over, the Desolate Heaven Empire would permanently lose a significant portion of its land.","Not to mention, voluntarily giving them away was no different from mocking every soldier who had shed blood to defend the empire.","This was clearly Yu Zidi selling the Desolate Heaven Empire for his own selfish ambitions.","Who would want such an Emperor?","Yu Zidi, however, no longer cared.","As long as he survived today...","As long as he became Emperor...","He was willing to pay any price.","Even if it meant selling away part of the empire itself.","The foreign delegations fell into silence.","Yu Zidi’s offer was undoubtedly tempting.","The border territories of the Desolate Heaven Empire had long been disputed lands.","For years, their empires had fought countless battles over those regions.","If they could obtain them without sacrificing any more soldiers, it would be a tremendous achievement.","Even returning with such territory would earn them immense merit within their respective empires.","Several representatives visibly hesitated.","However, that hesitation lasted only a brief moment.","Soon, reason prevailed.","One after another, they quietly shook their heads.","The reward was indeed extraordinary.","But they also had to be realistic.","Yu Zidi becoming Emperor?","What were the chances?","Even if they somehow defeated Yu Feiyan’s forces here...","Would the Bai Clan simply stand aside?","Impossible!","The communication jade had already confirmed everything.","Their coalition army, which included Yu Zidi’s forces, had attacked the Bai Clan.","They had attempted to wipe out the Bai Clan while Bai Zihan attended the coronation.","The Bai Clan would never overlook such a grudge.","As long as Bai Zihan chose to intervene, Yu Zidi’s chances of ascending the throne would instantly fall to zero.","No amount of promises could change that fact.","Thinking of this, the representatives became even more resolute.","Rather than gambling everything on an impossible outcome, it was far wiser to preserve their remaining strength.","Their highest priority was no longer helping Yu Zidi seize the throne.","It was finding a way to escape the Desolate Heaven Empire alive."]},{"number":679,"title":"Chapter 679: Abandoned by All","paragraphs":["Although Yu Zidi had offered such a grand promise, he quickly realized that the foreign delegations still had no intention of helping him.","Several representatives had already begun withdrawing from the battlefield.","Others remained locked in combat, but their eyes constantly searched for an opportunity to escape.","No one wished to continue risking their lives for him.","Yu Zidi’s heart sank to rock bottom.","Without the support of the foreign delegations, much less the Bai Clan...","Even Yu Feiyan’s current forces alone were enough to overwhelm him.","His mind raced frantically.","There had to be something.","There was no way he would accept being killed here, at the very event where he was supposed to obtain everything he deserved.","Suddenly, a thought flashed through his mind.","His eyes lit up as he immediately looked toward Yu Feiyan and shouted at the top of his lungs.","\"Ninth Sister! Let’s stop fighting!\"","His voice echoed throughout the Imperial Palace, causing everyone to turn toward him.","Yu Zidi took a deep breath before continuing.","\"Think about it carefully! Even if one of us defeats the other today...\"","\"So what? Can either of us truly sit securely upon the throne?\"","His gaze swept across everyone present before finally landing on Bai Zihan.","\"As long as the Bai Clan exists, the Imperial Family will never possess real authority!\"","Yu Zidi was finally using his brain.","Right now, the Bai Clan’s prestige had already surpassed that of the Imperial Family.","If the Bai Clan ordered everyone to head west while the Imperial Family ordered them to head east, the vast majority would follow the Bai Clan’s command.","Not only the Imperial Family, other great clans and major sects also no longer possessed the authority they once enjoyed.","In today’s Desolate Heaven Empire, the Bai Clan’s words carried more weight than imperial decrees.","\"Ninth Sister! I’m willing to step down. I’ll give up the throne! But before that...\"","\"We must first deal with the Bai Clan. Only after eliminating the Bai Clan can the Imperial Family truly reclaim its authority!\"","\"Otherwise, regardless of who becomes Emperor, the throne will exist in name only! I’m doing this...\"","He placed a hand over his chest.","\"...solely for the sake of our Imperial Family!\"","His righteous voice echoed throughout the palace.","Objectively speaking, his reasoning wasn’t entirely without merit.","As long as the Bai Clan remained this powerful, the Imperial Family’s authority would forever be overshadowed.","The throne would become little more than a symbol.","Even if someone sat upon it, they would never possess the absolute authority an Emperor should have.","Though Yu Zidi’s objective was very different from what he was saying.","He merely wishes to sow discord between the Bai Clan and Yu Feiyan, and when they engage in a clash, he can quietly slip off.","Yu Feiyan quietly looked at Yu Zidi.","She understood the logic behind his words.","If this matter had been left entirely to her, she might have actually considered it.","However, Yu Feiyan merely glanced sideways.","Her gaze settled upon Qin Lingxiao.","The decision was never hers to make.","She silently waited for Qin Lingxiao’s decision.","Qin Lingxiao remained silent.","Yu Zidi’s proposal was not entirely without merit.","Throughout her entire plan, the greatest variable had always been the Bai Clan.","Now that Bai Zihan had demonstrated his terrifying ability to manipulate even the Li Clan and Zhao Clan, the Bai Clan had become an even greater obstacle.","If she joined forces with Yu Zidi’s remaining army...","Combined with her own forces...","There might indeed be a chance to suppress the Bai Clan.","Perhaps they could even eliminate Bai Zihan altogether.","For a brief moment, Qin Lingxiao genuinely considered the possibility.","However, she slowly shook her head.","If there was one lesson Bai Zihan had repeatedly taught everyone, it was this—","Never assume you have seen all of his cards.","Every time people believed they had cornered him, he would calmly reveal yet another hidden trump card.","The coalition’s assault on the Bai Clan had been the perfect example.","No one had expected the Li Clan and Zhao Clan to suddenly betray Yu Zidi.","No one had expected Bai Zihan to have already taken control of two of the empire’s greatest clans.","If she chose to cooperate with Yu Zidi now...","Who could guarantee that Bai Zihan wasn’t waiting with yet another scheme?","There was no need to change her priorities and risk losing everything she had planned.","Besides, there was no need to take action against the Bai Clan right now.","As long as Yu Feiyan ascended the throne, the Imperial Family would fall under her control.","Once that happened, everything that had belonged to Yu Zidi would naturally become Yu Feiyan’s.","Only the foreign delegations would leave.","But judging from the current situation, they had already lost all desire to continue opposing the Bai Clan.","Even if they agreed to go with Yu Zidi’s suggestion, that would only include Yu Zidi’s original force which only has one Earth Immortal.","With such that, there was no way that they could win against the Bai Clan which is now supported by the Li and Zhao Clan.","Moreover, Qin Lingxiao had never truly cared whether the Bai Clan became the strongest force within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","She only needed the authority of the Imperial Family.","With the imperial throne under her control, she could mobilize the empire’s countless clans, sects, and officials to search for what she sought.","That alone was enough.","She didn’t believe the Bai Clan would stop something like that from happening.","At that moment, Yu Feiyan’s voice quietly sounded within her consciousness.","(Master, what is your decision?)","Qin Lingxiao answered without the slightest hesitation.","(There is no need to consider Yu Zidi’s proposal.)","A faint smile immediately appeared on Yu Feiyan’s face.","She slowly looked toward Yu Zidi.","Her beautiful eyes remained as calm as ever.","\"Prince Yu Zidi.\"","Her voice was as gentle and elegant as always.","\"I appreciate your concern.\"","She gave him a graceful nod.","\"But what comes after today, you needn’t trouble yourself with worrying about it.\"","A faint smile curved her lips.","\"I will take care of everything myself.\"","Her tone remained soft, polite, and refined, yet her words were anything but.","She wasn’t merely rejecting his proposal.","She was telling him that he would not live long enough to see what happened afterward.","Yu Zidi’s face instantly turned deathly pale.","With Yu Feiyan’s words, her forces erupted into motion once more.","The Imperial Palace instantly descended back into chaos.","Boom!","Countless techniques illuminated the sky as Yu Feiyan’s cultivators launched an all-out assault against Yu Zidi’s remaining forces.","Having lost the support of the foreign delegations, Yu Zidi’s side immediately fell into a huge disadvantage.","Meanwhile, the foreign representatives quietly withdrew from the battlefield.","Since they no longer had any intention of helping Yu Zidi, Yu Feiyan’s forces did not stop them and allowed them to leave.","After all, their objective was to kill Yu Zidi, not the foreign delegations.","Seeing that Yu Feiyan had no intention of pursuing them, the foreign representatives couldn’t help but breathe a sigh of relief.","\"We’re finally getting out...\"","Many of them revealed expressions of relief.","After everything that had happened today, they no longer wished to remain within the Desolate Heaven Empire for even another moment.","Their only thought was to return home alive.","Unfortunately, someone else had no intention of letting them leave.","Bai Zihan’s indifferent gaze slowly swept across the retreating foreign delegations.","A cold smile appeared on his face.","\"You think that after attacking my clan, you can simply leave?\"","Bai Zihan slowly turned toward Li Jianhong and Zhao Wutian.","His expression remained calm.","\"Kill them.\"","The two Clan Leaders didn’t hesitate in the slightest.","\"Yes, Clan Leader Bai!\"","The moment the order fell—","Boom!","The Li Clan and Zhao Clan experts immediately charged toward the retreating foreign delegations.","\"They’re attacking us!\"","The foreign representatives’ expressions changed drastically.","Unfortunately for them, most of them had already exhausted a tremendous amount of qi fighting Yu Feiyan’s forces.","Many had also suffered considerable injuries.","In their current condition...","How could they possibly withstand the combined assault of the Li Clan and Zhao Clan?","Slash! Slash!","Blood splattered across the palace square.","The number of surviving foreign cultivators rapidly dwindled.","Fear instantly spread throughout the foreign delegations.","At that moment, Elder Fu of the Tianyu Empire hurriedly stepped forward.","His face was completely pale.","\"Stop! You can’t kill us! We are representatives of the Tianyu Empire!\"","\"We entered the Desolate Heaven Empire under your official invitation!\"","His voice carried both panic and disbelief.","Never in his wildest dreams had he imagined today’s outcome.","Originally, they had believed this trip would bring immense rewards.","Instead, they now stood at death’s door.","Chen Muyang’s expression was no better.","The arrogance that had once filled his face had completely disappeared.","Just yesterday, these people had treated the Desolate Heaven Empire as their own backyard, bullying anyone they disliked.","Today, they themselves stood on the brink of death.","Escaping under the pursuit of the Li Clan and Zhao Clan had already become nearly impossible, so they tried to talk their way out.","Seeing Elder Fu speak, the white-haired elder from the Vermilion Pill Empire also hurriedly added,","\"Young Master Bai! This is all a misunderstanding!\"","\"We only cooperated with Prince Yu Zidi because we wished to build a good relationship with the future Emperor of the Desolate Heaven Empire!\"","\"We never intended to become enemies of the Bai Clan! We were only following Prince Yu Zidi’s arrangements!\"","He immediately dumped all the blame onto Yu Zidi.","Several other representatives hurriedly nodded.","\"That’s right!\"","\"We were deceived!\"","\"It was Yu Zidi who proposed attacking the Bai Clan!\"","\"We simply wished to maintain friendly relations between our empires!\"","Their voices were filled with desperation.","However, Bai Zihan merely looked at them as though they were clowns.","A mocking smile appeared on his lips.","\"Heh... Looks like you think very little of my intelligence.\"","His eyes gradually turned cold.","\"Save your excuses. I have no interest in listening to them.\"","He raised his hand indifferently.","\"Leave no one alive!\"","The Li Clan and Zhao Clan experts answered with another overwhelming assault.","The screams of the foreign cultivators once again echoed throughout the Imperial Palace."]},{"number":680,"title":"Chapter 680: Fall Of Yu Zidi!","paragraphs":["Yu Zidi’s forces had completely collapsed.","The forces who had once sworn absolute loyalty to him were now being slaughtered one after another.","The palace grounds had long since become a sea of blood.","Everywhere one looked, corpses littered the ground.","The few remaining experts around Yu Zidi desperately fought back, but their resistance was utterly meaningless.","Boom!","The Earth Immortal of the Crimson Thunder Palace slammed his palm downward.","Xuande, the Royal Ancestor, barely managed to block with his weapon.","Crack!","The artifact shattered instantly.","The overwhelming force continued unabated.","Xuande’s body exploded into a cloud of blood mist before everyone’s eyes.","Yu Zidi’s only Earth Immortal had fallen.","That single death completely crushed the last trace of hope within his remaining followers.","Many immediately threw down their weapons.","Others fled in every direction.","Some simply closed their eyes and accepted death.","The battle was already over.","Only Yu Zidi himself remained.","***","High above the battlefield, Qin Lingxiao quietly looked down at him.","Her expression remained indifferent.","She slowly stepped forward.","Every step she took caused an invisible pressure to descend upon the surrounding space.","Yu Zidi’s face turned deathly pale.","He hurriedly activated another defensive artifact.","Buzz!","A brilliant golden barrier surrounded his body.","This was one of the greatest life-saving treasures left behind by the late Emperor.","It was capable of withstanding attacks from an Earth Immortal for a considerable period of time.","Unfortunately, the opponent before him wasn’t an Earth Immortal.","Qin Lingxiao casually raised a finger.","A strand of Qi quietly condensed.","Then she flicked her finger.","Slash!","The seemingly insignificant strand of Qi instantly struck the barrier.","Crack!","A tiny fracture appeared.","Before Yu Zidi could even react—","Boom!","The entire defensive barrier exploded into countless fragments.","The priceless artifact was completely destroyed.","Yu Zidi’s pupils shrank violently.","\"N-No...\"","Yu Zidi stared blankly at his empty hands.","He had expended every life-saving treasure he possessed.","Now, none remained.","He slowly raised his head toward Qin Lingxiao.","Then he looked around the battlefield.","His army had almost been annihilated and the remaining ones had all surrendered or fled.","The foreign delegations he was allied with were being massacred by the Li Clan, and Zhao Clan.","There was nowhere left to run.","For the first time in his life, Yu Zidi truly understood what despair felt like.","Ironically, this was the very same despair he had once forced upon his own brothers and sisters.","When he had framed them.","When he had stripped them of everything they possessed.","When he had watched them desperately beg for mercy...","He had never imagined that one day, he would also face the same situation.","His pride.","His ambition",".","Everything shattered completely.","The next moment—","Thud!","Yu Zidi dropped to both knees before Qin Lingxiao.","The once arrogant prince who had believed himself destined to rule the Desolate Heaven Empire was now kneeling like a defeated dog.","Yu Zidi lowered his head.","His entire body trembled uncontrollably.","\"I surrender!\"","His voice cracked.","\"I surrender completely! I don’t want the throne anymore!\"","\"I’ll give it all to the Ninth Sister. I’ll never fight for it again!\"","He repeatedly kowtowed.","Bang! Bang! Bang!","His forehead struck the ground with enough force to draw blood.","\"Please...\"","His voice had become hoarse.","\"Just spare my life. I was wrong. I truly know I was wrong.\"","\"I’ll leave the Desolate Heaven Empire. I’ll never return.\"","He continued begging without caring about his dignity.","The countless spectators watched silently.","Many found the sight unbelievable.","This was the same Yu Zidi who had once carried himself with supreme confidence.","The same prince who had believed the imperial throne already belonged to him.","Now he was crying and begging, throwing away every last shred of dignity.","Yet Yu Zidi no longer cared.","Dignity?","Authority?","Pride?","Compared to his life, he realized that none of them were worth mentioning.","Qin Lingxiao quietly looked at the utterly defeated man kneeling before her.","Her expression remained as calm as ever.","There was neither pity nor satisfaction within her eyes, only indifference.","Throughout her countless years of cultivation, she had witnessed far too many scenes like this.","She had seen countless geniuses fall.","Countless prodigies beg for mercy.","Countless ambitious men kneel before death, desperately trying to cling to life.","Yu Zidi was merely one more among them.","His pleas failed to stir even the slightest ripple within her heart.","Besides, Yu Zidi had never been a righteous person to begin with.","Did he truly believe no one knew what he had done behind the scenes?","His schemes against his own brothers and sisters.","The countless assassinations.","The political purges.","The false accusations.","Even framing the Second Prince for crimes he himself had committed.","Every one of those actions had long since been known to her.","Such a person...","Even if she weren’t carrying out her current mission, she still wouldn’t feel the slightest mercy for him.","Her gaze remained emotionless.","A person who was willing to sacrifice everything for power...","Family.","Honor.","Conscience.","Even part of his empire.","Such a person deserved neither sympathy nor compassion.","However, she also didn’t despise him because the world has always been like this.","Even in the Qin Clan, she had witnessed countless people resort to every conceivable method in pursuit of greater authority and influence.","Those who stood at the peak were rarely innocent.","Yu Zidi was simply another person walking that path.","The only mistake he made was failing.","Every choice carried a price.","Every action carried consequences.","Now it was simply Yu Zidi’s turn to pay them, just as many who had lost to him before.","Qin Lingxiao slowly raised her hand.","A strand of terrifying Qi quietly condensed at her fingertips.","Yu Zidi’s face instantly lost all color.","His body trembled violently.","\"N-No... I can still be useful! I’ll become your slave. I’ll do anything!\"","He crawled forward on his knees, his forehead repeatedly striking the ground.","Bang!","Qin Lingxiao’s expression never changed.","The next instant—","Slash!","A brilliant ray of light flashed across everyone’s vision.","It was so fast that almost no one could follow it.","The entire Imperial Palace fell silent.","Yu Zidi’s desperate cries abruptly stopped.","His body froze in place.","A thin crimson line slowly appeared across his neck.","Thud!","Yu Zidi’s head slowly slipped from his shoulders before rolling across the bloodstained ground.","His lifeless body collapsed heavily beside it.","Bang!","The man who had once stood closest to the imperial throne...","The mastermind behind countless schemes...","Had died just like that without dignity.","The Imperial Palace became deathly silent.","Everyone stared blankly at the fallen corpse.","Yu Zidi was finally dead!","From beginning to end, Bai Zihan quietly watched everything unfold.","His expression remained completely unchanged.","There was neither joy nor satisfaction upon his face.","To him, Yu Zidi’s fate had already been decided the moment he chose to scheme against the Bai Clan.","From that day onward, death had merely become a matter of time.","If Yu Zidi had focused solely on ascending the throne...","If he had first become Emperor before provoking the Bai Clan...","Perhaps he would still have possessed some value.","At the very least, Bai Zihan might have allowed him to live for a while longer.","After all, a puppet Emperor was often more useful than a dead one.","Unfortunately, Yu Zidi wanted everything.","He wanted the throne.","He wanted absolute authority.","He wanted to eliminate the Bai Clan.","He wanted to dominate the entire Desolate Heaven Empire in a single stroke.","His ambition had far exceeded his ability.","Bai Zihan understood people like him very well.","Even if Yu Zidi had survived today wihout offending him, someone like him would never truly accept living beneath another person.","Then, sooner or later, he would have gone against the Bai Clan and met the same end.","Such people never accepted being second.","Their ambition would consume them until either they reached the summit or died because of their own greed.","In that regard, today’s outcome had merely arrived a little earlier than expected.","Whether today or sometime in the future, Yu Zidi’s ending would never have changed.","With Yu Zidi’s death, everything finally came to an end.","The remaining forces under his command immediately lost all will to resist.","Clang!","One weapon after another fell onto the ground.","\"We surrender!\"","\"We are willing to submit!\"","Countless Imperial Guards dropped to one knee.","Their expressions were filled with fear.","Unlike Yu Zidi’s personal retainers and those from his mother’s family, these soldiers had never truly belonged to him.","They belonged to the Imperial Family.","More accurately, they belonged to the throne itself.","Whoever sat upon the imperial throne was their master.","Previously, they had obeyed Yu Zidi because he had stood only one step away from becoming Emperor.","Now Yu Zidi is dead.","Yu Feiyan was the undisputed victor.","Their allegiance naturally shifted to the new ruler.","As for Yu Zidi’s personal guards and the cultivators who had willingly followed him, they were shown no such mercy.","Boom!","Yu Feiyan’s forces immediately launched their final assault.","Within moments...","Every one of Yu Zidi’s diehard followers had been eliminated.","Blood flowed freely across the palace square.","Soon, the only people left standing were the victors.","Qin Lingxiao slowly surveyed the battlefield before giving a slight nod.","Although the battle had ended, she had no intention of slaughtering the surrendered Imperial Army.","Doing so would only weaken the Desolate Heaven Empire unnecessarily.","After today, those soldiers would belong to Yu Feiyan.","She still needed as many capable subordinates as possible to carry out her future plans.","She gave the order to Yu Feiyan.","Yu Feiyan’s calm voice slowly echoed across the battlefield.","\"Those who have surrendered...\"","\"They shall be spared.\"","Hearing those words, countless Imperial Guards immediately lowered their heads in gratitude.","\"Thank you, Your Highness!\"","\"Thank you for your mercy!\"","Their voices echoed one after another.","The bloodshed gradually came to an end.","After countless schemes...","After the struggle between princes and princesses...","After the intervention of foreign empires...","After the attack upon the Bai Clan...","The battle for the throne had finally reached its conclusion."]},{"number":681,"title":"Chapter 681: Yu Feiyan’s Revenge","paragraphs":["Yu Zidi’s death marked the end of the struggle for the throne.","Those Imperial Court officials who had supported him throughout the succession battle were swiftly apprehended.","Some attempted to flee.","Others desperately pleaded for mercy.","A few even tried to distance themselves from Yu Zidi, claiming they had merely obeyed his orders.","None of it mattered.","Every official who had willingly participated in Yu Zidi’s conspiracies was dragged away under heavy guard.","Soon afterward, the palace guards escorted another group into the square.","The Empress.","The Imperial Consorts.","The various Queens.","The women who had once ruled the Inner Palace with unquestionable authority.","Now, every one of them wore pale faces.","Their luxurious robes were stained with dust.","Their elegant hairstyles had long since fallen into disarray.","Gone was the arrogance that had once made countless palace maids tremble, only fear remained.","Especially after seeing Yu Zidi’s headless corpse lying upon the bloodstained ground.","Several of the younger consorts immediately collapsed onto the floor.","Some covered their mouths to stop themselves from screaming.","Others burst into tears.","Even the once dignified Empress struggled to maintain her composure.","Her face had turned deathly white.","Only Yu Zidi’s mother reacted differently.","Rather than despair, hatred completely consumed her.","Her bloodshot eyes locked onto Yu Feiyan.","\"You little bitch!\"","She struggled violently against the guards restraining her.","\"If it weren’t for you, my son would have become Emperor!\"","\"You killed him! I’ll kill you! I’ll kill you!\"","Her shrill screams echoed throughout the Imperial Palace.","Yu Feiyan simply looked at her quietly.","There wasn’t the slightest ripple in her beautiful eyes, only coldness.","\"When you bullied my mother...\"","\"When you had your servants harass her day after day...\"","\"When you forced her into despair...\"","\"When you finally drove her to her death...\"","Her voice became colder.","\"Did you ever think this day would come?\"","The Imperial Consorts’ expressions immediately changed.","Many subconsciously lowered their heads, especially those who had bullied Yu Feiyan’s mother.","When they discovered that the Emperor had fathered an illegitimate daughter with a woman of no background, they repeatedly sent people to harass her mother and make her life miserable.","The Inner Palace would never accept her existence.","The Empress viewed her as a stain upon her authority.","The jealous consorts regarded her as a threat, unable to tolerate another woman receiving the Emperor’s affection.","They directed all of their malice toward the defenseless woman.","By the time the Emperor discovered what had happened, Yu Feiyan’s mother was already dead.","Yu Feiyan slowly closed her eyes.","When she opened them again, they had become even calmer.","Her gaze swept across every woman before her.","\"When Father Emperor finally brought me back to the palace and all of you bullied me... Did any of you think this day would come?\"","A bitter smile appeared on her face.","Although she had entered the palace, she had never truly belonged there.","Without the late Emperor’s protection, she would have died countless times.","The palace maids mocked her.","The eunuchs ignored her.","The imperial princes and princesses ridiculed her.","The consorts constantly found excuses to punish her.","At times, she wasn’t even treated as well as an ordinary servant.","Every day was spent enduring humiliation.","Every day was spent struggling to survive.","If not for the late Emperor’s favor, which deterred them from going too far, she would never have lived long enough to stand here today.","She had never forgotten any of it nor had they ever allowed her to forget.","At that moment, Qin Lingxiao slowly walked to Yu Feiyan’s side.","She glanced indifferently at the kneeling women before looking toward her disciple.","\"I have fulfilled my side of our agreement.\"","Her calm voice carried no emotion.","\"You may deal with them however you wish.\"","After saying those words, Qin Lingxiao quietly stepped back.","However, her eyes remained on Bai Zihan.","She had secured control over the Desolate Heaven Empire, but if the Bai Clan chose to intervene, holding onto the throne would become extremely difficult.","Fortunately, Bai Zihan didn’t seem to have any intention of interfering.","Initially, Bai Zihan had no desire to see a puppet Emperor controlled by a foreign force.","That was, until he learned Qin Lingxiao’s true objective.","He understood very well that Qin Lingxiao sought the throne only to search for the True God’s Legacy.","Perhaps she also intended to prevent other factions from the Central Glorious Continent from entering the Eastern Continent.","Either objective benefited Bai Zihan as well.","Therefore, he had no intention of preventing Yu Feiyan from ascending the throne.","Besides, the old Imperial Family and nearly all of their supporters were already gone.","The only remaining members of the former Emperor’s household were the women of the Inner Palace, and their lives now rested entirely in Yu Feiyan’s hands.","The reality of their situation gradually sank in.","The women who had once stood at the very pinnacle of the Inner Palace finally realized there was no one left to protect them.","Their authority and status were gone.","They were nothing more than remnants of the previous Emperor’s reign.","Now, the fate of their lives rested entirely in Yu Feiyan’s hands.","The arrogance that had accompanied them for decades completely disappeared.","One after another, they fell to their knees.","\"Your Highness!\"","A middle-aged consort suddenly crawled forward.","Tears streamed down her face.","\"I-I was forced!\"","She repeatedly kowtowed.","Bang! Bang! Bang!","\"It was all the Empress’ orders! I never wanted to harm you or your mother!\"","\"If I disobeyed her, she would have punished me. I had no choice!\"","She cried desperately.","\"I beg Your Highness to spare my life!\"","The moment someone took the lead, the others immediately followed.","\"That’s right!\"","\"It was the Empress!\"","\"Everything was her idea!\"","\"We merely obeyed her commands!\"","Several Imperial Consorts hurriedly pointed toward the kneeling Empress.","Their faces were filled with panic.","One elderly Queen wiped away her tears before speaking.","\"Your Highness, I never participated. I never once harmed either you or your mother.\"","She hurriedly continued,","\"I can swear a Heavenly Oath. If I have ever personally ordered anyone to harm you, may the heavens strike me down!\"","Hearing this, several other women immediately echoed her words.","\"We never bullied you!\"","\"We never sent anyone after your mother!\"","\"I even secretly sent food to your palace once.\"","One excuse after another filled the Imperial Palace.","Some blamed the Empress.","Some blamed Yu Zidi’s mother.","Some claimed they had merely obeyed orders.","Others insisted they had never participated at all.","Several women cried so hard that their voices became hoarse.","Their elegant makeup had long since been ruined by tears.","Their appearance no longer resembled the noble women who had once ruled over the Inner Palace.","The Empress looked around in disbelief.","\"You...\"","\"You dare betray me?!\"","Her voice trembled with anger.","\"You all followed my orders! You all enjoyed humiliating that lowly woman!\"","\"And now you’re putting all the blame on me?!\"","One of the younger consorts immediately shouted back.","\"You were the one who ordered us! You threatened anyone who refused!\"","Another Queen also hurriedly nodded.","\"That’s right!\"","\"If we didn’t obey, you would have targeted us instead! It wasn’t our fault!\"","The women had begun accusing one another.","Yu Feiyan quietly watched the chaotic scene before her.","The women who had once looked down upon everyone else...","The women who had ruled the Inner Palace with absolute authority...","Were now kneeling in the dirt, crying, screaming, and desperately pushing the blame onto one another.","Yu Feiyan’s beautiful eyes remained completely indifferent.","Not the slightest ripple of sympathy appeared within them.","She didn’t know whether they were telling the truth or simply fabricating excuses nor did she care.","In Yu Feiyan’s eyes, every single one of them belonged to the same detestable Imperial Family.","The very family that had destroyed her childhood.","The very people who had driven her mother to her death.","The very people who had forced her to survive each day like a servant instead of a princess.","The reason she had agreed to become Qin Lingxiao’s disciple and help her...","The reason she had followed every instruction without complaint...","Was never solely because Qin Lingxiao was powerful.","It was because Qin Lingxiao had promised her revenge.","Today, that promise had finally been fulfilled.","Yu Feiyan slowly raised her hand.","Spiritual Qi quietly gathered around her slender fingers.","A terrifying pressure instantly enveloped the kneeling women.","The expressions of the Empress and the Imperial Consorts changed drastically.","They finally realized what Yu Feiyan intended to do.","\"N-No!\"","\"Your Highness!\"","\"Please spare us!\"","\"We’re innocent!\"","\"We truly didn’t do anything!\"","The entire square erupted into desperate cries.","Yu Feiyan’s expression never changed as her cold voice echoed throughout the Imperial Palace.","\"You all disgust me!\"","Boom!","Spirit-Severing Realm Spiritual Qi erupted from her body like a tidal wave.","Brilliant rays of light swept across the palace square.","Slash! Slash! Slash!","Blood blossomed across the stone floor.","The Empress widened her eyes in disbelief before collapsing backward.","Yu Zidi’s mother froze with hatred still etched across her face before her body slowly fell lifelessly to the ground.","The remaining Imperial Consorts and Queens followed one after another.","Within only a few breaths, every woman of the former Emperor’s Inner Palace lay motionless.","Not a single one survived.","Yu Feiyan slowly lowered her hand.","She quietly looked at the bodies scattered before her.","The hatred that had weighed upon her heart for so many years had finally been avenged.","Yet instead of joy, she felt only an unfamiliar emptiness.","The people she had hated the most were gone.","Her mother, however, would never return.","\"Mother, your daughter has finally avenged you. Please, rest in peace!\""]},{"number":682,"title":"Chapter 682: The Empire Welcomes Its New Ruler","paragraphs":["Soon, the news spread throughout the entire Desolate Heaven Empire.","Like a hurricane, it swept across every city, every sect, every marketplace, and every village.","The entire empire was thrown into an uproar.","\"What?!\"","\"The one ascending the throne isn’t Prince Yu Zidi?\"","\"It’s the Ninth Princess?!\"","Countless people were stunned.","For months, public opinion had overwhelmingly favored Yu Zidi.","Whether because of his carefully cultivated reputation or deliberate propaganda, many commoners genuinely believed he was the ideal Emperor.","The sudden announcement that Yu Feiyan had become the victor left countless people unable to believe it.","Some immediately frowned.","\"Did the Ninth Princess rebel?\"","\"Did she seize the throne by force?\"","\"Could the Imperial Palace have suffered a coup?\"","For a brief moment, rumors spread everywhere.","Many who had supported Yu Zidi immediately denounced Yu Feiyan as a traitor.","However, before long, more news about what had happened began spreading.","\"What?! Prince Yu Zidi colluded with foreign empires to destroy the Bai Clan?\"","\"He even promised to cede our border territories as payment for their assistance?!\"","\"What kind of Emperor sells his own empire’s land to outsiders?\"","\"So that’s why several foreign empires suddenly appeared inside the Imperial Palace!\"","\"He’s a traitor!\"","\"He almost gave away our homeland!\"","\"It is also said that the First Prince framed the Second Prince, when it was actually he who killed his own brothers and sisters. What a vicious man!\"","Public opinion shifted almost overnight.","Many who had once praised Yu Zidi now cursed him more fiercely than anyone else.","The Imperial Family’s evidence was simply too complete.","There was no room for denial.","Of course, even if it hadn’t been true, Qin Lingxiao would have been able to fabricate a completely believable story to sway public opinion.","History has always been written by the victor.","If Yu Zidi had succeeded, then today’s story would likely have been completely different.","Yu Feiyan would have been branded the rebel.","Every scheme would have been blamed on her.","Yu Zidi would have portrayed himself as a benevolent ruler who had saved the Empire from a traitorous princess.","Unfortunately for him, he had lost.","And because he had lost, every one of his crimes was brought into the light.","The irony was that, unlike many political accusations throughout history, most of these crimes were genuine.","Had Yu Feiyan not exposed everything publicly, the people would have continued believing Yu Zidi to be the rightful Emperor.","She would forever have been remembered as the princess who rebelled against the throne.","By releasing undeniable evidence, she not only destroyed Yu Zidi’s reputation but also completely cleared her own name.","Of course, even if Yu Zidi hadn’t committed such unforgivable crimes, the victors could always have fabricated a few.","That was simply the nature of political struggles.","The dead could no longer defend themselves.","Soon afterward, another piece of news spread throughout the empire.","The foreign coalition that had attacked the Bai Clan had been completely annihilated.","The entire empire erupted into cheers.","\"Hahaha! They deserved it!\"","\"They dared invade our empire and attack the Bai Clan!\"","\"The Bai Clan is invincible! How dare those ants think they could destroy them within our own territory?\"","The common people were filled with excitement.","Although many feared the Bai Clan’s strength, they were still a force belonging to the Desolate Heaven Empire.","They had protected the Empire for thousands of years, and their recent contribution in defeating the Demonic Forces was known to everyone.","If not for the Bai Clan, they knew they would have suffered greatly.","When everyone learned that the invading armies had been almost completely wiped out, the Bai Clan’s prestige soared to an unprecedented height once again.","Then another shocking revelation spread.","\"The Li Clan and Zhao Clan fought alongside the Bai Clan!\"","\"What?!\"","\"Impossible!\"","\"The Three Great Clans reconciled?\"","Countless people stood frozen.","Everyone within the Desolate Heaven Empire knew of the thousand-year feud between the Bai Clan, Li Clan, and Zhao Clan.","They had fought one another for generations.","Their hatred had become common knowledge.","At first, many refused to believe it.","However, after confirmation arrived from all three clans, the disbelief gradually turned into excitement.","\"This is wonderful!\"","\"If the Three Great Clans have truly reconciled, then who else in the Eastern Region would dare invade our empire?\"","\"Exactly! Our Desolate Heaven Empire has never been stronger!\"","Hope gradually replaced uncertainty.","The empire had suffered numerous internal conflicts over the years.","Although they had always put aside their differences whenever danger threatened the Empire, most of the time they exhausted their resources keeping one another in check.","If they weren’t constantly fighting each other and instead focused on increasing their overall strength, the Empire would have become far stronger.","Moreover, when Yu Feiyan took the throne, the Bai Clan, Li Clan, Zhao Clan, and other top forces such as the Heaven Suppression Sect, Crimson Thunder Palace, and Frost Lily Pavilion were all present.","It showed that they did not oppose her ascension.","As the news continued spreading, resistance toward Yu Feiyan’s ascension gradually disappeared.","The common people no longer questioned the outcome.","Instead, cheers gradually spread throughout the empire.","\"Long live Her Majesty!\"","\"Long live the Empress!\"","\"The Desolate Heaven Empire has a new ruler!\"","Along with the announcement of Yu Feiyan’s ascension, another series of imperial decrees quickly spread throughout the Desolate Heaven Empire.","The first decree immediately surprised countless people.","Taxes would be reduced across the entire empire.","The burden that had weighed upon ordinary cultivators, merchants, and common families for years would finally become lighter.","Before the people could even recover from their surprise, another wave of good news followed.","One territory after another publicly announced its own decree.","\"To celebrate Her Majesty’s ascension to the throne, our territory shall waive all taxes for the next five years!\"","The announcement immediately caused an uproar.","\"What?!\"","\"Five years without taxes?!\"","\"Is this real?\"","People rushed toward the city notice boards to verify the news.","Soon, a second territory announced the exact same policy.","Then a third.","A fourth.","Within only a few days, numerous territories throughout the empire had declared five years of tax exemption.","The common people were overjoyed.","Many could hardly believe such generosity.","For ordinary families, taxes often determined whether they could save enough resources to survive another year.","Five years without taxation meant countless families would finally have an opportunity to improve their lives.","Laughter could be heard throughout the streets.","Restaurants became crowded.","Markets became livelier than ever.","\"Her Majesty truly cares for the people!\"","\"No Emperor has ever reduced taxes so quickly after ascending the throne.\"","\"The Ninth Princess... no, Her Majesty... is far better than Prince Yu Zidi!\"","Cheers gradually spread from city to city.","Naturally, none of this happened by coincidence.","Within the Imperial Palace, Qin Lingxiao calmly listened as reports continued arriving.","A faint smile appeared upon her lips.","She naturally understood that winning the throne was only the first step.","Winning the hearts of the people was equally important.","Yu Feiyan’s reputation had been built almost overnight.","Many still knew very little about her.","In contrast, Yu Zidi had spent years carefully cultivating the image of a wise and benevolent prince.","Although his reputation had already collapsed, Yu Feiyan still needed something to quickly earn the people’s approval.","There was no better method than allowing the people to directly enjoy tangible benefits.","The reduced imperial taxes had been Qin Lingxiao’s suggestion.","As for the five-year tax exemptions...","The territories announcing those decrees all shared one thing in common.","They were controlled by clans and sects that had already fallen under Qin Lingxiao’s influence.","They willingly accepted the temporary losses.","Compared to firmly establishing Yu Feiyan’s legitimacy, a few years’ worth of tax revenue meant very little.","As long as the people genuinely supported the new Empress, they believed everything was worth it, even though their actions were ultimately the result of Qin Lingxiao’s control.","Even forces such as Crimson Thunder Palace followed suit because they wished to curry favor with Yu Feiyan.","They had already stood against her once and didn’t want to risk worsening their relationship by refusing.","As for the Bai Clan, they had no intention of doing so.","People were naturally free to move to other territories if they wished.","However, most wouldn’t.","Why?","Because the Bai Clan possessed the strongest territory in the Empire.","That also meant it was the safest place to live.","What was a little tax compared to the safety of one’s life?","In any case, these benefits naturally delighted the citizens.","Every passing day brought more praise, more gratitude, and more support.","The voices opposing Yu Feiyan’s ascension gradually disappeared.","Instead, the people began celebrating.","\"Long live Her Majesty!\"","\"Long live the Empress!\"","\"Our Desolate Heaven Empire finally has a ruler who truly thinks of the people!\"","The cheers echoed throughout the empire.","However, while celebration filled the Desolate Heaven Empire, the atmosphere within the neighboring empires was the complete opposite.","Boom!","Inside the imperial hall of the Tianyu Empire, an aura of terrifying pressure erupted.","\"What did you say?!\"","The Emperor’s furious roar shook the entire palace.","\"The army we secretly dispatched has been annihilated?\"","The reporting official knelt upon the floor, his body trembling uncontrollably.","\"Y-Yes, Your Majesty.\"","\"Not only the coalition army, our entire foreign delegation that attended the coronation was also killed.\"","Silence!","Every official present felt a chill run down their backs.","The Emperor’s face became increasingly gloomy.","The army they had lost consisted of elite cultivators painstakingly nurtured over centuries.","Nearly twenty percent of the Empire’s military strength had vanished just like that.","Even worse, several important elders had also died within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","Such losses were enough to severely damage the Tianyu Empire’s overall strength.","Similar scenes unfolded within the Azure Cloud Empire...","The Jade River Empire...","And the Vermillion Pill Empire.","One imperial hall after another erupted into chaos.","Tables were smashed.","Tea cups shattered.","Furious roars echoed through the palaces.","No one had expected what was supposed to be a perfect opportunity to weaken the Desolate Heaven Empire...","To instead become one of the greatest defeats their empires had suffered in recent years.","Not only had they failed to destroy the Bai Clan, they had even lost their armies.","\"Quick! Send a message! We demand an explanation from the Desolate Heaven Empire!\""]},{"number":683,"title":"Chapter 683: The Four Empires’ Shameless Accusation","paragraphs":["Even though they had been the ones who dispatched their armies...","The very ones who had attempted to wipe out the Bai Clan.","Now that everything had failed so spectacularly, instead of apologizing, they shamelessly blamed the Bai Clan for annihilating their forces.","Well, It was bizarre.","It was shameless.","But they had no choice.","They had already sacrificed so much and yet achieved nothing.","How could they simply sit around and do nothing?","Their reputations had already suffered greatly for secretly carrying out such an underhanded operation, and now they had also suffered catastrophic losses.","Naturally, they needed someone else to shoulder the blame.","The excuse they came up with was actually quite clever this time.","They claimed that they had only dispatched their forces to assist the Desolate Heaven Empire in eliminating a hidden threat.","According to them, the Bai Clan was suspected of practicing Demonic Cultivation, citing the clan’s absurdly rapid rise in strength as evidence.","They also said that everything had been Yu Zidi’s plan and that they only decided to help because they can’t let such a threat go unattended.","Therefore, for the safety of both the Desolate Heaven Empire and the entire Eastern Region, they had supposedly agreed to help eliminate this hidden danger.","Unfortunately, they had been deceived by Yu Zidi.","The four empires unanimously expressed their \"deep disappointment\" toward the late prince.","According to their statements, Yu Zidi had fabricated evidence and manipulated everyone into believing that the Bai Clan had fallen onto the Demonic Path.","As a result, they had been misled into making the wrong decision.","The final portion of every statement maintained an unwaveringly righteous tone.","As for why they were saying that Yu Zidi deceived them and not saying that the Bai Clan were really Demonic Cultivators is because it is quite easy to prove.","The Bai Clan can simply have their bodies be checked thoroughly by others and prove those words false.","So instead of clinging to such weak arguments, they could say that they were deceived to make them think that it was the truth.","So they want to pin all the blame on the dead man, Yu Zidi.","Although the operation had failed because of Yu Zidi’s deception, the four empires insisted that everything they had done had been for the greater good of the Eastern Region.","They had merely wished to protect countless innocent lives.","Now that the misunderstanding had been exposed, they demanded that the Desolate Heaven Empire provide a proper explanation for the deaths of their delegations and armies.","Although they say that they were deceived, they still dared to demand an explanation and also asked to greatly punish the Bai Clan for going too far.","***","Inside the Imperial Palace, Yu Feiyan read the reports before her.","She almost burst into laughter.","\"They actually managed to come up with something like this? Do they think we’re five-year-old children who don’t know anything?\"","They had invaded another empire and attempted to destroy one of its greatest clans.","Yet after suffering defeat, they somehow transformed themselves into the victims.","Not only that, they even portrayed themselves as righteous heroes who had selflessly tried to save the Desolate Heaven Empire.","As for everything that had gone wrong, it had supposedly all been Yu Zidi’s fault.","Every crime had conveniently been pinned onto a dead man while they desperately tried to preserve their image as righteous cultivators.","Yu Feiyan shook her head in disbelief.","\"Their skin is truly thicker than city walls.\"","Beside her, Qin Lingxiao merely glanced at the reports before calmly placing them back onto the table.","Unlike Yu Feiyan, her expression did not change in the slightest.","It is nothing more than politics which she has seen countless times before.","Turning black into white and white into black.","Even something as heinous as invading another empire to destroy one of its greatest clans can be described as protecting everyone.","Yu Feiyan looked up from the report before turning toward Qin Lingxiao.","\"Master, what shall we do?\"","Although she now sat upon the imperial throne, she understood her position very well.","She was the Empress.","But Qin Lingxiao was the one making the important decisions.","Qin Lingxiao didn’t even pause to think.","\"Ignore them.\"","Her answer was simple.","\"There is no value in entertaining such ridiculous accusations. They are merely trying to preserve what little dignity they have left.\"","She slowly looked out of the palace window.","That, however, was only part of the reason.","The greater reason... was the Bai Clan.","Every accusation the four empires had fabricated ultimately targeted the Bai Clan.","If she chose to cooperate with their investigation, or even appeared to support their claims, the fragile balance they had established would immediately collapse.","The Bai Clan had not interfered with Yu Feiyan’s ascension to the throne.","That alone was already the best possible outcome.","There was absolutely no need to provoke them.","Qin Lingxiao understood this point very clearly.","Her current objective had never been to suppress the Bai Clan.","It was to locate the True God’s Legacy.","As long as Bai Zihan did not interfere with that objective, there was no benefit in becoming his enemy.","Moreover, those four empires had openly supported Yu Zidi during the struggle for the throne.","They had attempted to place Yu Feiyan in a hopeless situation.","Now that they had failed, they somehow expected the new Empress to stand on their side.","Qin Lingxiao found the idea rather amusing.","\"Who gave them the confidence to believe we would help them?\"","Indeed! Those people truly had no shame.","Qin Lingxiao casually set the reports aside.","\"Enough. There are more important matters.\"","Her expression became serious.","\"The search.\"","Yu Feiyan immediately understood.","She nodded.","\"The latest reports have already arrived.\"","She handed over another stack of jade slips.","Qin Lingxiao scanned through them one after another.","Every report contained the same conclusion.","Nothing unusual had been discovered.","No mysterious ruins.","No hidden realms.","No abnormal spiritual fluctuations.","Every region of the Desolate Heaven Empire was being searched thoroughly.","Yet there was still no clue regarding the True God’s Legacy.","Qin Lingxiao wasn’t discouraged.","If it had been so easy to discover, it would have already been found long ago.","\"We simply continue searching. Eventually...\"","\"We will find something.\"","Yu Feiyan nodded.","\"I understand.\"","She then opened another report.","\"As for the matter of investigating the Li and Zhao Clan.\"","Qin Lingxiao raised an eyebrow.","\"We’ve had people quietly investigate the matter. We’ve been trying to determine how the Li Clan and Zhao Clan suddenly sided with the Bai Clan.\"","She paused briefly before shaking her head.","\"Unfortunately, we still haven’t found anything. No one knows why the two clans suddenly changed sides.\"","Qin Lingxiao narrowed her eyes slightly.","That was something she cared about.","The Li Clan and Zhao Clan had hated the Bai Clan for over a thousand years.","Hatred accumulated over such a long period could not simply disappear overnight.","Yet somehow, Bai Zihan had accomplished exactly that.","Not only had he reconciled with them...","He had even convinced them to betray Yu Zidi at the most crucial moment.","That was no ordinary achievement.","After a long silence, Qin Lingxiao slowly spoke.","\"Continue investigating. I want to know exactly what Bai Zihan used to make two thousand years of hatred disappear.\"","\"I also want to know what made two thousand-year-old enemies willingly stand beside him.\"","Yu Feiyan hesitated for a moment.","\"Master. There is one more important report.\"","Qin Lingxiao’s gaze immediately shifted toward her.","\"Regarding the Bai Clan?\"","Yu Feiyan nodded.","\"Yes!\"","The moment those words left her mouth, Qin Lingxiao’s expression became noticeably more attentive.","Among all the forces within the Desolate Heaven Empire, only the Bai Clan truly warranted her caution.","Every move they made deserved careful attention.","\"What happened?\"","Yu Feiyan lowered her head to read the report once more.","\"According to our spies, it seems the Bai Clan is preparing to make a big move.\"","Qin Lingxiao’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"A move?\"","The first possibility that crossed her mind was obvious.","\"They’re finally planning to act against us?\"","Her voice remained calm, but countless thoughts flashed through her mind.","It made little sense.","If Bai Zihan truly intended to remove Yu Feiyan from the throne, why wait until now?","Only a few days had passed since Yu Feiyan ascended the throne.","During the battle itself, the Bai Clan had possessed countless opportunities.","With the Bai Clan’s overwhelming strength and with the Li Clan and Zhao Clan standing beside them...","Preventing Yu Feiyan’s ascension would have been effortless.","They could have simply declared their opposition or they could have eliminated Yu Feiyan altogether.","Yet Bai Zihan had done neither.","Instead, he had watched everything unfold without interfering.","Yu Feiyan gently shook her head.","\"No. Our spies don’t believe we’re their target.\"","Qin Lingxiao raised an eyebrow.","\"Then who?\"","Yu Feiyan looked up from the intelligence report.","A strange expression appeared on her face.","\"The Shen Clan!\""]},{"number":684,"title":"Chapter 684: Shen Liang’s Return","paragraphs":["Bai Xueqing sat quietly within her cultivation chamber.","The entire room had turned into ice due to her cultivation.","After an unknown amount of time, Bai Xueqing slowly opened her eyes.","She had already reached the Mid Void Refinement Stage, but she was still far from reaching the Top Void Refinement Realm.","Many elders had spent hundreds of years cultivating, yet their cultivation was no higher than hers.","Even her own master, Qinglan, was only one minor realm ahead of her.","Still, despite possessing such strength, Bai Xueqing had never once acted arrogantly within the Heaven Sword Sect.","She still respected Qinglan as her master.","She still addressed the elders politely.","She still fulfilled her responsibilities as a disciple.","Knock! Knock!","A gentle knock sounded from outside the chamber.","Bai Xueqing withdrew her aura before calmly speaking.","\"Come in!\"","The frozen door was forcefully pushed open.","Otherwise, opening it normally would have been impossible. The disciple had to shatter the thick layer of ice before finally entering.","The disciple respectfully bowed.","\"Senior Sister Bai, Peak Master Qinglan requests your presence.\"","Bai Xueqing nodded.","\"I understand.\"","Without asking any further questions, she rose to her feet and followed the disciple toward Qinglan’s residence.","Along the way, however, a trace of curiosity surfaced in her heart.","Master rarely summoned her during cultivation.","Could something important have happened?","The answer revealed itself soon enough.","Upon arriving at Qinglan’s courtyard, Bai Xueqing immediately noticed another person standing beside her master.","The moment she saw him, the warmth in her eyes instantly disappeared.","Her expression turned icy.","Shen Liang!","(Of all people... Why was he here?)","Suppressing the disgust in her heart, Bai Xueqing ignored him completely.","Instead, she respectfully bowed toward Qinglan.","\"Disciple greets Master.\"","Qinglan smiled gently.","\"You may rise!\"","As she looked at Bai Xueqing, a complicated emotion flashed across her eyes.","She might be Bai Xueqing’s master, but in terms of cultivation and perhaps even combat ability, she wasn’t much stronger than this disciple of hers.","She knew Bai Xueqing was talented and had taught her well, but she had never expected her to catch up in only a few short years.","Even in the Central Glorious Continent, Qinglan was certain there was no one as talented as Bai Xueqing.","She was equally certain that any top faction there would accept Bai Xueqing as their Saintess.","Anyway, the reason for calling Bai Xueqing was because the young master of the Shen Clan remained unbelievably persistent.","Even today, despite her refusal, he insisted on meeting Bai Xueqing.","Eventually, Qinglan had no choice but to summon her disciple.","She sighed softly.","\"Xueqing, I know you don’t wish to see him. I tried refusing him, but he insisted. He said he only wished to speak with you this once and won’t pester you again.\"","Bai Xueqing’s expression remained indifferent.","Only after Qinglan finished speaking did she slowly turn toward Shen Liang.","Her gaze was cold.","So cold that it carried not even the slightest warmth.","It was as though she were looking at a complete stranger.","No. Not even a stranger.","Someone beneath her notice.","\"What do you want?\"","Her voice was equally cold.","Without the slightest trace of politeness.","The only reason she was even willing to stand here and listen was because Qinglan had asked her to.","Otherwise, she wouldn’t have spared Shen Liang even a single glance.","In stark contrast to Bai Xueqing’s indifference, Shen Liang’s eyes lit up the moment he saw her.","There wasn’t the slightest trace of resentment on his face.","Instead, he looked genuinely delighted.","\"Xueqing!\"","His voice was filled with excitement.","\"It has been years... I’ve finally seen you again.\"","His gaze remained fixed upon her elegant figure.","Compared to the last time they had met, Bai Xueqing seemed even more breathtaking.","Her flawless face had become even more refined.","She truly resembled an immortal fairy untouched by the mortal world.","Shen Liang was completely captivated.","Bai Xueqing merely looked at him with unconcealed disgust.","Then, her gaze briefly landed on his right arm.","A hint of surprise flashed through her eyes.","(His arm... It had recovered.)","Years ago, Bai Zihan had personally crippled that arm.","She knew better than anyone how severe the injury had been.","For the Shen Clan to restore it, they must have paid an astonishing price.","The medicine alone was probably priceless.","Still, that thought lasted only an instant.","Whether his arm had recovered or not had nothing to do with her.","She calmly withdrew her gaze.","\"What do you want?\"","Her cold voice echoed through the courtyard.","\"If you have something to say, then say it. Don’t waste my time.\"","The smile on Shen Liang’s face immediately stiffened.","A trace of hurt appeared within his eyes.","\"Xueqing! I know you’re still angry. But everything that happened before was just a misunderstanding. I—\"","\"I don’t care.\"","Bai Xueqing interrupted him before he could continue.","Her expression remained as cold as ever.","\"What happened before no longer matters to me. So stop talking about it.\"","Bai Xueqing looked impatient.","\"If you have nothing else to say, then leave.\"","Shen Liang clenched his fists yet he refused to give up easily.","\"Everything I did... I did it for your sake. You have to trust me.\"","Bai Xueqing quietly looked at him.","Her face remained completely expressionless.","There wasn’t the slightest indication that his words had affected her.","Not even a little.","If anything...","She looked even more disgusted than before.","Anyone present could tell.","Forget believing him.","Bai Xueqing was one hundred and ten percent certain that not a single word coming from Shen Liang’s mouth was worth believing.","Seeing her unmoved expression, Shen Liang’s heart gradually filled with frustration.","His breathing became heavier.","Finally, he couldn’t suppress himself any longer.","\"I’ve loved you for so many years!\"","His voice rose involuntarily.","\"I’ve done everything for you! I’ve never stopped thinking about you!\"","He stared directly into Bai Xueqing’s eyes.","\"Can’t you forgive me just once? I’ve already paid the price for everything!\"","His voice echoed throughout the quiet courtyard.","Bai Xueqing’s expression remained unchanged.","Not a single ripple appeared within her icy eyes.","It was as though Shen Liang’s heartfelt confession had never reached her ears.","Without another word, she turned around.","She had already lost all interest in continuing this conversation.","Seeing her leave so decisively, Shen Liang panicked.","\"Xueqing!\"","He hurriedly stepped forward.","\"Wait!\"","Bai Xueqing did not stop.","Only then did Shen Liang grit his teeth and shout,","\"Our Shen Clan is willing to help the Bai Clan!\"","Those words finally caused Bai Xueqing to pause.","Shen Liang immediately thought he had finally gained her attention.","He quickly continued.","\"Our Shen Clan is willing to cooperate with the Bai Clan. We can become allies. We can help the Bai Clan in many ways.\"","\"The previous misunderstandings can all be forgotten.\"","As he spoke, confidence gradually returned to his face.","Although the Shen Clan had suffered repeated setbacks over the past few years, they were still one of the empire’s foremost clans.","At least, that was what he believed.","What he failed to realize was that the current Shen Clan no longer possessed the qualifications to negotiate with the Bai Clan.","Especially after the Li Clan and Zhao Clan had openly submitted to them.","Compared to those two clans, the Shen Clan simply wasn’t worth mentioning anymore.","Without the Li-Zhao Alliance, which had once gathered the forces that opposed the Bai Clan, that alliance had completely dissolved.","Countless forces that had once offended the Bai Clan were desperately trying to repair their relationship.","Some offered priceless artifacts.","Others willingly transferred mines, businesses, and territories.","Some even volunteered to become subordinate forces.","They all understood one thing.","Provoking the Bai Clan any further was courting death.","Among those forces, the Shen Clan naturally ranked near the top.","After all, aside from the Li Clan and Zhao Clan before their reconciliation, no one had opposed the Bai Clan more openly than they had.","Now, Shen Liang actually dared to stand here and say that the Shen Clan was willing to help the Bai Clan.","Bai Xueqing found it utterly baffling.","When someone is begging... Who does so with such an arrogant attitude?","Who speaks as though they are doing the other party a favor?","For a brief moment, she genuinely wondered whether Shen Liang had lost his mind.","In the end, she simply lost interest altogether.","There was no point wasting any more time on such a foolish person.","Bai Xueqing turned toward Qinglan.","She respectfully cupped her fists.","\"Master. If there is nothing else, this disciple will return to cultivation.\"","Qinglan nodded gently.","Bai Xueqing bowed once more.","Without sparing Shen Liang even a single glance, she calmly walked away.","Her white robes fluttered gently as her figure gradually disappeared beyond the courtyard.","Shen Liang stood there motionless.","His pupils trembled.","His breathing gradually became ragged.","She...","She had left just like that.","Crack!","His fingernails dug deeply into his palms.","Fresh blood slowly trickled down.","His face gradually twisted.","Confusion became unwillingness.","Unwillingness became resentment.","Finally, resentment transformed into madness.","\"I gave you everything...\"","His voice trembled.","\"I loved you for so many years. I was willing to do anything for you. And you...\"","His eyes slowly became bloodshot.","A crazed expression spread across his face.","\"So be it! If that’s your choice...\"","His voice became increasingly cold.","\"Then don’t blame me for taking action.\"","The terrifying hatred within his eyes caused even Qinglan’s brows to knit together slightly.","She suddenly felt...","That Shen Liang before her seemed like an entirely different person."]},{"number":685,"title":"Chapter 685: Shen Liang’s True Color","paragraphs":["Qinglan’s pupils contracted.","\"Hahaha... Hahahahaha!\"","Shen Liang suddenly threw his head back and burst into wild laughter.","The sound echoed throughout the quiet courtyard.","It was no longer the laugh of a sane person.","It was twisted with madness and obsession.","As his laughter continued, a terrifying aura suddenly erupted from his body.","Boom!","Violent qi surged in every direction.","The ground beneath his feet cracked apart.","Qinglan’s expression immediately changed.","His cultivation...","It was rising rapidly.","Peak Nascent Soul Realm!","Early Spirit Severing Realm!","Mid Spirit Severing Realm!","Then—","Boom!","A powerful wave of pressure swept across the courtyard.","Void Refinement Realm!","Qinglan’s eyes narrowed.","\"What?\"","Only moments ago, Shen Liang had merely been at the Core Formation Realm, yet within seconds, his cultivation had crossed multiple major realms.","Such a thing completely defied common sense.","However, the more Qinglan observed him, the more uneasy she became.","The aura surrounding Shen Liang was strange.","It was violent and chaotic, yet it wasn’t demonic qi or rather, it resembled demonic qi, but it was somehow different.","Even with Qinglan’s experience, she couldn’t identify exactly what it was.","\"Shen Liang!\"","Her voice became cold.","\"What have you done?\"","Shen Liang didn’t answer.","His bloodshot eyes had completely lost their clarity.","Only madness remained.","The aura around him continued to fluctuate violently.","Seeing the situation deteriorate, Qinglan immediately stepped forward.","Regardless of what Shen Liang had done to himself, she couldn’t allow him to continue.","Just as she was about to make her move—","Boom! Boom!","Two terrifying pressures suddenly descended.","The two guards who had accompanied Shen Liang stepped forward simultaneously.","Their cultivation erupted without reservation.","Great Ascension Realm!","Both of them.","Qinglan’s expression immediately darkened.","Previously, they had only appeared to be at the Spirit Severing Realm, and she was certain they hadn’t been suppressing their cultivation.","That was also why she hadn’t cared about Shen Liang bringing them. She could have suppressed them at any time.","Yet now, they had truly been hiding their strength.","She didn’t know how they had accomplished it.","Regardless, the Shen Clan had clearly come prepared.","The two men stood directly before her, blocking her path.","Two Great Ascension Realm cultivators were more than enough to stall Qinglan.","\"Peak Master Qinglan. This matter has nothing to do with the Heaven Sword Sect.\"","\"We advise you not to interfere.\"","Qinglan’s face turned icy.","\"Shen Liang is about to attack my disciple inside the Heaven Sword Sect, and you dare say this has nothing to do with the Heaven Sword Sect?\"","She glared at the two men with killing intent.","Even while facing two Great Ascension Realm cultivators, there wasn’t the slightest fear in her eyes.","\"It seems your Shen Clan doesn’t place either the Heaven Sword Sect or the Bai Clan in your eyes if you dare pull such a stunt.\"","She was saying that to threaten them but why would they dare to make a move in the first place if they were afraid.","At the same time, Shen Liang slowly lowered his head.","His blood-red eyes stared fixedly at Bai Xueqing’s figure.","His sinister laughter echoed once more.","\"Xueqing... I originally wanted to do things the peaceful way. I truly wanted the Shen Clan and the Bai Clan to reconcile.\"","\"I even came personally to ask for your forgiveness.\"","His voice gradually became colder.","\"But you! You wouldn’t even give me a chance. In that case, I can only force you.\"","His smile became increasingly twisted.","His thoughts had always been simple or perhaps too shallow.","The Shen Clan’s current situation had already reached its most desperate point.","The Li-Zhao Alliance had dissolved.","The Li Clan and Zhao Clan had submitted to the Bai Clan.","Meanwhile, the Shen Clan remained one of the Bai Clan’s greatest enemies.","There were only two possible paths left.","The first was to repair their relationship with the Bai Clan.","That was exactly what Shen Liang had attempted today.","If he could marry Bai Xueqing...","If he became Bai Zihan’s brother-in-law...","Would the Bai Clan still destroy the Shen Clan?","Unfortunately, Bai Xueqing hadn’t even given him the slightest opportunity.","She had rejected him without hesitation.","Since the first path had failed, only the second remained.","A sinister smile slowly spread across Shen Liang’s face.","\"If I can’t make you willingly become my wife then I’ll simply take you away.\"","His voice grew increasingly crazed.","\"Bai Xueqing! You’re the Bai Clan’s precious daughter. If I capture you, then the Bai Clan will have no choice.\"","His eyes burned with madness.","\"They’ll surrender! They’ll kneel before the Shen Clan.\"","The more he spoke, the more convinced he became.","It was as though this absurd plan had become the only path remaining for the Shen Clan.","Bai Xueqing naturally noticed everything that had happened behind her.","Although she appeared calm on the surface, her mind was already working rapidly.","She immediately took out a Transmission Jade from her storage ring.","Without hesitation, she injected her spiritual qi into it.","Buzz!","The jade briefly glowed.","Then... Nothing.","Her brows furrowed slightly.","She tried once more.","Again... Nothing.","The transmission simply failed to activate.","Bai Xueqing’s eyes narrowed.","(So that’s how it is.)","She understood.","No wonder Shen Liang had dared to make such a commotion inside the Heaven Sword Sect.","From the moment his aura erupted, enough pressure had been released to shake half the mountain.","Under normal circumstances, the nearby elders would have arrived almost instantly.","Even ordinary disciples would have rushed over to investigate.","Yet until now, not a single person had appeared.","\"There must be a barrier...\"","Bai Xueqing murmured softly.","She didn’t know what Shen Liang had used, but she realized it had to be some kind of artifact capable of isolating this entire space.","They had been completely cut off from the outside world.","Only now did Bai Xueqing realize how thoroughly the Shen Clan had prepared for this.","They hadn’t come here on impulse.","Everything had been planned long ago.","She slowly turned her head toward Qinglan.","At this moment, her master was already engaged in battle against the two Great Ascension Realm cultivators.","Qinglan was no Bai Zihan.","She couldn’t defeat two opponents of the higher realm by herself.","However, she wasn’t losing either.","She stubbornly held them back.","Likewise, the two Shen Clan experts weren’t fighting aggressively.","Their only objective was to stall Qinglan.","Every attack they launched focused solely on preventing her from breaking through.","As long as she remained occupied, Shen Liang could freely execute the second half of his plan.","Bai Xueqing’s gaze gradually became colder.","\"So you’ve isolated this place from the outside.\"","Shen Liang slowly smiled.","\"As expected of you. You figured it out so quickly.\"","He spread his arms slightly.","\"No one outside can hear what’s happening here. No one knows what is taking place and no one is coming to save you.\"","His bloodshot eyes were filled with obsession.","\"Xueqing. Just come with me.\"","\"I don’t want to hurt you. As long as you’re willing to cooperate, everything can still be resolved peacefully.\"","Bai Xueqing looked at him as though he were an idiot.","\"Peacefully?\"","A trace of ridicule finally appeared upon her cold face.","\"I...\"","Before he could explain, Bai Xueqing interrupted him.","\"You truly are beyond saving.\"","Her voice was completely devoid of emotion.","At the same time, her spiritual qi quietly began circulating.","If reinforcements could not arrive...","If communication had been completely cut off...","Then there was only one option left.","Fight!","Shen Liang stared at Bai Xueqing.","Instead of becoming angry at her words, he suddenly laughed again.","\"Hahaha...\"","The sound was chilling.","His bloodshot eyes were filled with madness and obsession.","\"Beyond saving? So be it.\"","He slowly raised his hand, pointing directly at Bai Xueqing.","\"Once I bring you back to the Shen Clan, I’ll have plenty of time to teach you.\"","His lips curled into a twisted smile.","\"I came here hoping you would make the right choice but you insisted on making things difficult.\"","His expression gradually turned sinister.","\"Don’t worry. After you become my woman, I’ll make sure you learn how to behave.\"","His gaze slowly swept across Bai Xueqing’s graceful figure.","\"There are countless methods to discipline an unruly wife. I’ll have all the time in the world to teach you every single one.\"","His smile became increasingly depraved.","Bai Xueqing’s eyes grew even colder.","Not because she was afraid.","But because Shen Liang’s words had become increasingly disgusting.","She had thought he was merely delusional.","Now she realized he was completely insane.","There was no reasoning with someone like him.","No amount of words would change his mind.","He stretched out one hand toward her.","\"Come. Don’t make me use force. It would pain me to hurt you.\"","Bai Xueqing quietly watched him.","Then, a trace of killing intent appeared within her icy eyes.","\"You’ve finished?\"","Her calm voice made Shen Liang pause.","Without waiting for an answer, Bai Xueqing slowly raised her own hand.","Cold air instantly gathered around her slender fingers.","The temperature throughout the courtyard plummeted once more.","Frost spread across the already frozen ground.","She looked directly into Shen Liang’s bloodshot eyes.","\"Listen carefully. I would rather die than spend a single day with someone as disgusting as you.\""]},{"number":686,"title":"Chapter 686: Shen Liang Vs Bai Xueqing","paragraphs":["Bai Xueqing attacked Shen Liang without holding back.","Clang! Clang! Clank!","Sword Qi and violent Qi collided repeatedly.","Shen Liang charged forward, his blood-red eyes completely consumed by madness.","\"You!\"","His furious roar echoed through the barrier.","\"When did you become so powerful?!\"","He had originally believed that after forcibly raising his cultivation to the Peak Void Refinement Realm, capturing Bai Xueqing would be effortless.","Instead, reality completely shattered his confidence.","From the beginning of the battle until now, he hadn’t gained the slightest advantage.","Every attack he launched was calmly neutralized.","Every technique he used was effortlessly avoided.","He couldn’t even touch the corner of Bai Xueqing’s sleeve.","On the other hand, Bai Xueqing remained astonishingly composed.","Her movements were elegant and graceful.","Every swing of her sword flowed naturally like drifting snow.","She wasn’t fighting desperately.","She was simply overwhelming him with pure skill.","The difference between them became increasingly obvious.","\"No!\"","Shen Liang roared.","\"I refuse to believe it!\"","His already unstable mind descended further into madness.","Violent energy exploded from his body.","\"I’ll subdue you! I’ll make you kneel!\"","\"I’ll make you acknowledge me!\"","His attacks became increasingly reckless.","Bai Xueqing silently watched him.","She neither mocked nor argued.","To her...","Shen Liang had already become someone unworthy of words.","Slash!","A brilliant streak of icy sword light flashed across the battlefield.","Before Shen Liang could react, his right arm flew into the air.","Blood sprayed everywhere.","His expression froze yet something unbelievable happened.","The severed arm suddenly trembled.","Countless crimson strands rapidly connected the broken limb to the wound.","Within a single breath, the arm reattached itself perfectly.","Not even a scar remained.","It was as though it had never been severed.","Bai Xueqing’s brows furrowed slightly.","(What kind of sorcery is this?)","Calling it regeneration would be an understatement.","She had seen regenerative physiques before.","Even those legendary physiques required time to recover.","Some needed several breaths.","Others required precious medicinal pills.","Yet Shen Liang’s body recovered almost instantly.","It wasn’t merely healing.","It was as though reality itself had been rewritten.","His arm had simply... returned.","Shen Liang looked at his restored hand before laughing wildly.","\"Hahaha! You can’t kill me!\"","His confidence instantly surged.","Without hesitation, he charged once more.","Bai Xueqing’s gaze remained calm.","If severing an arm wasn’t enough, then she would simply cut off something more vital.","Her figure disappeared.","The next instant—","Slash!","Her sword swept across Shen Liang’s neck.","His head flew high into the air.","Any ordinary cultivator would undoubtedly die after such a strike.","Yet the headless body remained standing.","Then, before the severed head even touched the ground, it transformed into countless crimson threads.","The body below did the same.","The countless threads intertwined in midair.","Within moments, Shen Liang stood there once again, completely unharmed.","He casually twisted his neck.","Crack! Crack!","\"Hahaha! I already told you. You can’t kill me!\"","Bai Xueqing narrowed her eyes.","Without hesitation—","Slash! Slash! Slash!","Her sword danced continuously.","One moment, Shen Liang was split in half.","The next moment, his chest exploded.","Then both legs were severed.","His torso was cut apart repeatedly.","Blood filled the courtyard.","Yet every single time, his shattered body reconstructed itself.","Again and again!","It was as though his body had become completely unkillable.","Even Bai Xueqing felt a trace of surprise.","She had never encountered such an abnormal ability before.","No matter how many times she cut him down, it accomplished nothing.","Meanwhile, Shen Liang’s emotions became even more chaotic.","Originally, he had believed this newfound power would allow him to completely overwhelm Bai Xueqing.","Instead, he realized something horrifying.","Even after reaching the Peak Void Refinement Realm, he still couldn’t touch her.","Every attack he launched missed.","Every technique was dismantled before it could reach her.","Bai Xueqing treated him like nothing more than a training dummy.","One sword after another landed upon his body.","He was continuously blown backward.","The battle had completely reversed his expectations.","He possessed an immortal body, yet he couldn’t even force Bai Xueqing to retreat a single step.","His confidence gradually turned into disbelief.","Then disbelief became humiliation.","Finally, it transformed into uncontrollable fury.","\"Impossible!\"","He roared hysterically.","\"Why?! Why can’t I even touch you?!\"","His maddened roar echoed throughout the isolated courtyard.","Bai Xueqing merely pointed her sword toward him.","Her icy eyes remained as calm as ever.","Although Bai Xueqing held the absolute upper hand in her battle against Shen Liang, she knew the overall situation was anything but favorable.","Her sword could suppress him.","It could slice him apart countless times, yet it couldn’t kill him.","However, her master’s situation was becoming increasingly dangerous.","Despite her profound strength, Qinglan was facing two Great Ascension Realm cultivators by herself.","She was barely managing to hold them back.","Every exchange pushed her slightly further onto the defensive.","The moment Qinglan fell...","Those two Great Ascension Realm cultivators would immediately join forces with Shen Liang.","At that point, even Bai Xueqing would have no chance of escaping.","Her eyes quickly swept across the battlefield.","Her mind rapidly searched for a solution.","\"If I can’t kill you, then I’ll simply immobilize you.\"","The Qi within her body erupted.","An incomparably cold aura spread throughout the courtyard.","\"Glacial Heaven Seal—Absolute Frost Domain!\"","Boom!","An endless tide of icy qi exploded outward with Bai Xueqing at its center.","The entire courtyard was instantly engulfed by a world of absolute frost.","Layers upon layers of ice spread across the ground.","The surrounding air froze solid.","Shen Liang’s expression changed drastically.","\"What?!\"","Before he could react—","Crack!","Ice rapidly climbed up his legs.","Then his waist.","Then his chest.","Within moments, Shen Liang had been completely sealed inside a gigantic block of crystalline ice.","His crazed expression remained frozen upon his face.","However, Bai Xueqing’s attack had never been aimed solely at Shen Liang.","The freezing domain continued expanding.","It quickly reached the two Great Ascension Realm cultivators battling Qinglan.","Crack!","Ice immediately began climbing up their feet as they were caught off guard.","Their movements slowed considerably.","Qinglan’s eyes brightened.","\"What powerful freezing Qi!\"","Unfortunately, the difference in cultivation was simply too great.","The moment the frost reached their knees—","Boom!","Violent Qi erupted from both Great Ascension Realm experts.","Their overwhelming cultivation instantly shattered the surrounding ice.","Crack! Crack!","Qinglan immediately retreated several hundred meters.","In a single flash, she arrived beside Bai Xueqing.","Both master and disciple now stood back to back.","Qinglan took a deep breath.","For the first time since the battle began, she had a brief chance to recover.","Her expression, however, remained extremely grave.","She lowered her voice.","\"Xueqing. We’re trapped.\"","Her eyes briefly glanced around the surrounding space.","\"The barrier is still active. I’ll hold them off. You break through the barrier and send a distress message.\"","Bai Xueqing immediately shook her head.","\"No!\"","Her answer was decisive.","\"I won’t abandon you, Master.\"","Qinglan frowned.","\"This isn’t the time to be emotional. Listen to me. If we both remain here, neither of us may survive.\"","Bai Xueqing calmly gripped her sword.","She understood Qinglan’s intentions.","However, she also understood the reality before them.","\"If I leave, you won’t be able to stop all three of them.\"","Her voice remained calm.","\"Against three opponents of this level, you won’t even have a chance to retreat. Much less for me to break the barrier.\"","Qinglan remained silent.","Because Bai Xueqing was right.","Even holding back one Great Ascension Realm cultivator had already pushed her to her limits.","How could she possibly hold back another?","If they chose to separate and pursue Bai Xueqing, she would be completely powerless to stop them.","Bai Xueqing continued.","\"Our best chance is to remain together. As long as we keep stalling them, there is still hope.\"","She looked toward the sky beyond the invisible barrier.","\"The Heaven Sword Sect will eventually realize something is wrong. This battle has already gone on for far too long.\"","\"Even if the barrier blocks sound and spiritual fluctuations, our disappearance cannot remain hidden forever.\"","Her eyes became even more resolute.","\"And even if the Heaven Sword Sect somehow fails to notice...\"","A faint warmth finally appeared within her otherwise icy gaze.","\"My family will.\"","Crack!","The gigantic block of ice imprisoning Shen Liang suddenly exploded.","Shen Liang stumbled out.","His face was extremely ugly.","The frost covering his body slowly melted away.","His blood-red eyes were fixed upon Bai Xueqing.","There was unwillingness.","There was humiliation.","And above all, there was rage.","One of the Great Ascension Realm cultivators glanced at him before speaking calmly.","\"Young Master. Do you still wish to fight Miss Bai alone?\"","His tone carried neither mockery nor contempt.","It merely stated the obvious.","From the very beginning, Shen Liang had specifically ordered them not to interfere.","He wanted to defeat Bai Xueqing personally.","He wanted to prove that he was no longer the weak man who had once been effortlessly suppressed by her.","He wanted Bai Xueqing to witness his newfound strength.","To admire him.","To acknowledge him.","That was why the two of them had remained occupied with Qinglan instead of helping Shen Liang.","Unfortunately, reality had proven far crueler than Shen Liang had imagined.","Not only had he failed to defeat Bai Xueqing, he hadn’t even managed to land a single meaningful attack.","Instead, he had been treated like nothing more than a target.","If not for his terrifying regenerative ability, he would have died countless times already.","Even the two Great Ascension Realm cultivators couldn’t help feeling astonished.","Bai Xueqing’s strength had already surpassed Qinglan’s.","Despite Qinglan possessing a higher cultivation realm, Bai Xueqing’s swordsmanship and control over Qi were clearly superior.","If Bai Xueqing were to step into the Great Ascension Realm, even the two of them together might not be her match.","Shen Liang clenched his fists.","Crack!","His fingernails dug into his palms once again.","His entire body trembled.","Humiliation.","Utter humiliation.","His expression twisted violently.","The last trace of reason disappeared from his eyes.","\"I don’t care anymore!\"","He roared hysterically.","\"Forget fighting one-on-one!\"","He suddenly pointed at Bai Xueqing.","\"Kidnap her!\"","His voice became crazed.","\"All of you attack together. We’re taking her back to the Shen Clan and completing our task!\""]},{"number":687,"title":"Chapter 687: On A Date","paragraphs":["Bai Zihan had never expected that one day he would be forced to go on a stroll, especially not one like this.","He walked leisurely through one of the main streets within the Bai Territory.","Beside him was Chu Ziyan.","The two of them had been engaged for a few years already.","Yet because of various events, they had rarely spent much time together.","Well, considering cultivators could go into seclusion for several years, it wasn’t too uncommon.","Previously, the Chu Clan also hadn’t been too enthusiastic about the marriage and didn’t think much about it.","Now, however, things were different.","Bai Zihan’s status had changed dramatically after becoming the Clan Leader of the strongest clan in the Eastern Region, and his talent remained unmatched in history.","Naturally, the Chu Clan was becoming increasingly eager to finalize the marriage.","Chu Ziyan herself had also been repeatedly encouraged by her clan to spend more time with Bai Zihan.","Even Bai Tianheng and Mu Yuelan had expressed their support.","As a result, Bai Zihan had been forced into this stroll.","\"Is this really necessary?\"","Bai Zihan asked helplessly.","Chu Ziyan glanced at him.","\"What? Are you that reluctant to walk with your fiancée?\"","\"Of course not.\" A faint, unhurried smile appeared on his face. \"To be graced with the company of such a beauty, how could I possibly complain?\"","He said it smoothly, without missing a beat. He had long since learned that arguing with women was a battle better avoided than won.","He had already mastered the \"Dao of Courting Women,\" which the System sold for 100 points.","From this, he knew that arguing with women wasn’t a good way to go.","Chu Ziyan smiled.","\"Good that you know.\"","A faint blush appeared on Chu Ziyan’s cheeks.","She quickly turned her head away, pretending to examine the bustling streets ahead.","The two continued walking side by side.","Their destination for today was simple.","They would spend the entire day strolling around the Bai Territory.","That was the agreement Bai Zihan had made with his mother.","Mu Yuelan had no problem with that, as she knew that Bai Zihan had many things to take care of.","The situation within the Desolate Heaven Empire was becoming increasingly complicated, even though things seemed calm on the surface.","However, Mu Yuelan had not forced him without reason.","For a good marriage, feelings needed to be cultivated as well.","After all, Bai Zihan and Chu Ziyan had already been engaged for a few years, and it was time to talk about marriage.","If they continued treating their marriage like a political arrangement without spending any time together, how could they possibly develop a proper relationship?","Therefore, Mu Yuelan had asked Bai Zihan to accompany Chu Ziyan for one day.","Just relax and spend some time with his fiancée.","Bai Zihan eventually agreed as well.","Well, looking around the Bai Territory was good as well.","The two continued walking through the bustling streets.","After several moments, Chu Ziyan looked around with some curiosity.","She had visited the Bai Territory before, but every time she came, she noticed something different.","The entire territory had undergone tremendous development over the past few years.","The streets were clean.","The buildings were orderly.","Merchants came and went constantly.","Cultivators could be seen everywhere.","Even ordinary mortals appeared energetic and prosperous.","Compared to many other territories within the Desolate Heaven Empire, the difference was obvious.","\"This place has changed quite a lot.\"","Chu Ziyan remarked.","Bai Zihan nodded.","\"Naturally. The Bai Clan has invested heavily in the development of its territory.\"","Chu Ziyan glanced at him.","\"Wasn’t the Bai Clan originally more focused on cultivation and strengthening its forces?\"","\"That was before.\"","Bai Zihan looked ahead.","\"Strength is important. But strength alone isn’t enough to build a prosperous territory. The people living under our protection also need to benefit.\"","As a modern person who had lived under capitalism, how could he not know that?","He was just a common man who had to suffer and endure a lot while those at the top took everything without even leaving a scrap behind.","Although high-level cultivators didn’t care about those below them or how they lived, Bai Zihan was different.","Although he couldn’t promise to treat everyone equally and give everyone an easy life, he could at least set aside some funds for the development of his territory which would make their life easier.","Things were much better in the Bai Clan’s territory.","Bai Zihan hated corruption and hated people abusing their authority.","After taking control of various aspects of the Bai Territory, he had made his position extremely clear.","No official was allowed to abuse their authority.","No powerful family was allowed to bully ordinary merchants.","No one was allowed to seize another person’s business through threats or underhanded methods.","If someone wanted to compete, they competed fairly.","If someone wanted to acquire a business, they negotiated fairly.","And if someone attempted to use their background to forcibly seize someone else’s property, the Bai Clan would intervene.","Bai Zihan had personally established extremely strict rules regarding such matters.","As a result, the Bai Territory gradually developed a reputation.","Business owners felt safe.","Merchants were willing to invest.","Talented individuals were willing to settle down.","Even ordinary people felt that their lives were protected.","Moreover, the crime rate within the Bai Territory was also among the lowest in the entire Desolate Heaven Empire.","After all, who would dare commit crimes within the Bai Territory?","The Bai Clan’s intelligence network was extremely efficient.","Once a crime occurred, the culprit could often be identified and captured within only a few hours.","Even if someone were to travel thousands of kilometers and try to hide, it would only be a matter of days before they were caught.","Even Great Ascension Realm cultivators couldn’t hide or escape.","Of course, living under the Bai Clan’s protection wasn’t free.","The taxes collected by the Bai Clan were relatively high.","Around twenty percent of a business’s profits had to be paid to the Bai Clan.","It was high compared to other territories managed by small and medium-sized clans, but compared to top clans, it wasn’t high.","Clans like the Li Clan and Zhao Clan charged forty to fifty percent for doing business within their territories.","Anyway, compared to them, the Bai Clan’s tax wasn’t high at all, and even if it were higher, there wouldn’t be much complaint.","The reason was simple.","They knew exactly what they were receiving in return.","Protection.","Security.","Fair competition.","Stable businesses.","Top infrastructure.","And countless other benefits.","For most merchants, paying twenty percent was far better than keeping one hundred percent of their profits only to have everything taken away by a powerful cultivator or influential clan.","Moreover, the Bai Clan wasn’t simply focused on increasing its own strength.","Under Bai Zihan’s direction, the clan had invested heavily in the development of the territory itself.","Roads were expanded.","Commercial districts were established.","Cultivation resources were properly managed.","Markets were organized.","Various industries were encouraged to develop.","Even ordinary people benefited from the changes.","So they didn’t feel like their tax money was being taken away for free without receiving any benefits.","Bai Zihan understood that a powerful clan could not rely solely on cultivation strength.","A truly powerful force required a stable foundation.","Resources.","Businesses.","Population.","Infrastructure.","Talents.","And above all, a territory capable of continuously generating wealth and cultivating new generations of experts.","Therefore, while Bai Zihan continued strengthening the Bai Clan’s cultivation forces, he also paid considerable attention to these other aspects.","Although he only did what was expected, the result was obvious.","The Bai Territory had gradually transformed into one of the most prosperous and stable regions within the Desolate Heaven Empire.","For the people living there, the Bai Clan’s existence was not merely a symbol of overwhelming strength.","It was also the reason they could live and conduct their businesses without constantly fearing that everything they possessed would disappear overnight.","Chu Ziyan continued walking beside Bai Zihan with a faint smile on her face.","The two of them didn’t talk much, yet somehow, she was quite satisfied.","She was able to spend an entire day walking beside Bai Zihan without worrying about clan affairs, cultivation, or the complicated matters of the Desolate Heaven Empire.","At the same time, she could experience the prosperity of the Bai Territory firsthand.","Everywhere she looked, there were people moving through the streets with smiles on their faces.","Merchants discussed their businesses.","Young cultivators talked excitedly about their cultivation goals.","Children ran through the streets.","Even ordinary mortals spoke about their plans for the future.","Some dreamed of opening their own businesses.","Others wanted their children to become cultivators.","Some were saving resources to purchase better cultivation techniques.","There was a sense of hope everywhere.","That was what impressed Chu Ziyan the most.","In many other territories, ordinary people lived completely different lives.","To powerful cultivators, mortals and low-level cultivators were often nothing more than laborers.","They worked.","They struggled.","They paid taxes.","And they continued living from one day to the next without ever knowing whether some powerful figure might suddenly take everything they possessed.","Their greatest aspiration was often nothing more than surviving.","But here, things were different.","The people living within the Bai Territory genuinely seemed to believe that their future could become better.","They weren’t merely struggling to survive.","They were thinking about tomorrow.","Chu Ziyan quietly observed everything around her.","Then her gaze gradually shifted toward the man walking beside her.","Bai Zihan!","The contrast was almost difficult to reconcile.","In front of his enemies, Bai Zihan could be absolutely ruthless.","Once he decided that someone was his enemy, he showed almost no mercy.","Even if hundreds of thousands of people stood before him, he could slaughter them without allowing his expression to change.","He was cold and decisive.","And sometimes, downright terrifying.","Yet toward his own people, he was completely different.","He meticulously considered the people under his protection.","He cared about the development of the Bai Territory.","He cared about the people who followed him.","He cared about his family.","And he was willing to spend considerable time and resources ensuring that the people under his protection could live better lives.","Chu Ziyan couldn’t help but smile.","Perhaps this was what made Bai Zihan different from many other powerful cultivators.","His ruthlessness was directed toward his enemies.","His kindness was reserved for the people he considered his own.","That distinction was extremely clear.","The two had also deliberately changed their clothing before leaving.","Neither wore the attire associated with their clans.","Therefore, unless someone knew them personally, it would be extremely difficult to recognize them.","And considering how crowded the streets were, it was perfectly normal for people to occasionally bump into one another.","Sure enough, an ordinary merchant hurried past while carrying several boxes and accidentally bumped into Bai Zihan’s shoulder.","The merchant immediately froze.","His face became pale.","\"I’m sorry! I’m sorry!\"","He hurriedly bowed several times.","However, Bai Zihan merely waved his hand.","\"It’s fine. Be careful next time!\"","The merchant immediately breathed a sigh of relief.","After apologizing once more, he quickly left.","Chu Ziyan quietly watched this scene.","If this had happened in the territory of some other powerful clan, the situation might have been completely different.","A young master being bumped into by an ordinary person could easily become a major incident.","The offender might even be beaten or imprisoned.","Yet Bai Zihan hadn’t even taken it seriously.","To him, it was nothing more than an accidental collision.","Chu Ziyan’s smile deepened.","No matter how powerful Bai Zihan became...","She didn’t think she would ever have to worry about being mistreated if she became his wife.","After all, she had even personally beaten him before.","And Bai Zihan had never held it against her.","Well, that incident had been his own fault anyway.","Remembering it, Chu Ziyan couldn’t help but smile.","The more she thought about it, the more she felt that Bai Zihan was actually quite the husband material.","Brutal toward enemies.","Gentle toward his own people.","Protective of his family.","For a woman who wanted a reliable husband, what more could she ask for?","Chu Ziyan’s cheeks became slightly warm.","She quickly looked away.","Bai Zihan, however, didn’t notice her expression.","He continued walking leisurely through the streets, thinking that the day was coming to an end.","Whoosh!","A figure suddenly hurried toward them from a distance.","The man wore the uniform of the Bai Clan.","His expression was extremely anxious.","As soon as he reached Bai Zihan, he immediately stopped and respectfully bowed.","\"Clan Leader!\"","He glanced briefly at Chu Ziyan before lowering his head again.","\"Miss Chu!\"","\"Sorry for disturbing you.\"","Bai Zihan immediately sensed that something was wrong.","\"Speak!\"","The messenger swallowed nervously.","Then he delivered the news that instantly changed the atmosphere.","\"Miss Bai Xueqing has been kidnapped!\""]},{"number":688,"title":"Chapter 688: The Kidnapping of Bai Xueqing","paragraphs":["At almost the same time, the atmosphere within the Bai Clan changed completely.","The moment news of Bai Xueqing’s kidnapping arrived, the entire clan immediately entered a state of preparation.","The Bai Clan’s forces stationed throughout the territory were quickly mobilized.","Everyone understood the seriousness of the situation.","Bai Xueqing wasn’t merely a disciple of the Heaven Sword Sect.","She was the daughter of the Bai Clan.","More importantly, she was Bai Zihan’s younger sister.","No one doubted what would happen if anything happened to her.","Within the main hall, Bai Tianheng’s expression was extremely solemn.","He looked toward Bai Ren.","\"Where is Zihan’er?\"","One of the servants immediately answered.","\"Young Master is currently with Miss Chu Ziyan.\"","Bai Ren continued.","\"Don’t worry. I’ve already sent someone to inform him.\"","Bai Tianheng’s expression suddenly changed.","\"You did what?\"","Bai Ren blinked.","\"I sent a messenger to inform him.\"","His expression became somewhat confused.","\"Did I do something wrong? Bai Zihan is the Clan Leader, and Bai Xueqing is his sister. Shouldn’t he be informed immediately so he can make the decision?\"","Bai Tianheng’s face darkened.","\"That’s exactly why you shouldn’t have merely sent someone to inform him!\"","Bai Ren scratched his head.","He still didn’t understand.","\"Why?\"","Bai Tianheng stared at him for several seconds.","Then he finally spoke through gritted teeth.","\"Have you forgotten what happened when Luo Qing was kidnapped?\"","The moment those words were spoken, Bai Ren froze.","His expression changed.","He finally remembered.","Back then...","When Luo Qing had been kidnapped, Bai Zihan had completely lost his composure and directly charged into the territory of the Demonic Cultivators, almost losing his life.","At the time, everyone in the Bai Clan had witnessed firsthand what Bai Zihan was capable of when someone he cared about was harmed.","Bai Ren’s expression gradually became serious.","\"...I remember.\"","Bai Tianheng sighed as he rubbed his forehead.","\"If Zihan’er hears that Xueqing’er has been kidnapped without anyone being there to control the situation, do you think he’ll calmly sit down and discuss the matter?\"","Bai Ren remained silent.","He had almost forgotten because Bai Zihan was usually calm and collected, always thinking matters through carefully. However, once he lost control of his emotions, things became very different.","But Bai Ren also wondered whether Bai Zihan would really lose control this time because he couldn’t tell exactly how close Bai Zihan’s relationship with Bai Xueqing was.","Although he knew that Bai Zihan cared about Bai Xueqing and would never harm her, it wasn’t as though the two of them were extremely close.","From a young age, they had almost treated each other as if they were an eyesore, unable to stand each other.","Would Bai Zihan really lose his control like last time or perhaps he didn’t care much about Bai Xueqing for him to do so?","Bai Tianheng’s expression became increasingly solemn.","\"We need to go to him just in case he loses control again.\"","He immediately turned toward the surrounding elders.","\"Prepare three Grand Elders.\"","***","The atmosphere seemed to freeze the moment the messenger finished speaking.","He sneakily peeked at Bai Zihan, trying to see any emotion on his face.","Bai Zihan didn’t react, but somehow, the temperature around him seemed to drop several degrees.","Chu Ziyan was the first to break the silence.","\"What?\"","Her expression changed drastically.","\"Xueqing has been kidnapped?\"","She couldn’t believe it.","\"How is that possible? Wasn’t she cultivating in the Heaven Sword Sect? Did someone attack the Heaven Sword Sect?\"","The messenger hurriedly shook his head.","\"Miss Chu, I don’t know the full details yet. All we know is that Miss Xueqing was kidnapped by Shen Liang inside the Heaven Sword Sect.\"","\"As for how he managed to do it...\"","He hesitated.","\"The matter is still being investigated.\"","\"How can that be?\"","Chu Ziyan’s expression became increasingly worried.","She didn’t understand how someone like Shen Liang could have kidnapped Bai Xueqing within the territory of the Heaven Sword Sect.","What had happened to the Heaven Sword Sect’s experts?","Why hadn’t anyone stopped him?","Chu Ziyan glanced toward Bai Zihan.","He had remained completely silent from beginning to end.","His expression was calm.","There was no visible anger, no panic, and no killing intent.","That somehow made Chu Ziyan even more uneasy.","She had expected Bai Zihan to explode the moment he heard that Bai Xueqing had been kidnapped.","Yet he hadn’t even frowned.","After several moments, Bai Zihan finally spoke.","\"Let’s return to the clan first.\"","His voice was calm and steady.","\"We’ll discuss everything there.\"","The messenger immediately nodded.","\"Yes, Clan Leader!\"","Without wasting any more time, the three of them began making their way back toward the Bai Clan.","The atmosphere along the way was unusually heavy.","Chu Ziyan remained beside Bai Zihan.","She occasionally glanced at him.","He still looked completely composed.","His steps remained steady.","His expression remained indifferent.","But Chu Ziyan had spent enough time with him to know that something was wrong.","The messenger, meanwhile, continued explaining everything he knew, including that Qinglan had also been kidnapped.","Chu Ziyan’s pupils contracted.","\"Master too?\"","The messenger hesitated before nodding.","\"Yes! Both Miss Xueqing and Peak Master Qinglan were captured.\"","\"Even Master...\"","Chu Ziyan’s voice became faint.","Her worry deepened considerably.","If even Master Qinglan had been captured alongside Bai Xueqing, then the situation was clearly far more serious than they had initially thought.","Chu Ziyan unconsciously tightened her hands.","She glanced at Bai Zihan again.","Still no reaction.","Halfway back to the Bai Clan, Bai Zihan’s group suddenly encountered several figures rushing toward them.","At the front was Bai Tianheng.","Behind him were three Grand Elders of the Bai Clan.","The moment Bai Tianheng saw Bai Zihan, the tension that had been weighing on his heart finally eased slightly.","\"Zihan’er! You’re here!\"","Bai Zihan stopped.","He looked toward Bai Tianheng and the three Grand Elders.","\"Father!\"","Bai Tianheng quickly approached him.","He had been genuinely worried.","He was afraid that Bai Zihan would lose control the moment he heard about Bai Xueqing’s kidnapping and immediately charge toward the Shen Clan without making proper preparations.","Bai Tianheng stared at him for a moment before finally letting out a breath.","At least he hadn’t lost his reason.","That was already a good thing.","However, his expression quickly became solemn again.","\"Zihan’er, we don’t know what the Shen Clan is planning. The fact that they dared to kidnap Xueqing’er inside the Heaven Sword Sect means they must have prepared something.\"","Bai Zihan’s eyes narrowed slightly.","He understood that point as well.","The Shen Clan wasn’t powerful enough to act recklessly.","They knew exactly what kind of consequences they would face if they openly kidnapped Bai Xueqing.","Yet they had still done it.","That meant they either possessed absolute confidence in their ability to escape...","Or they were relying on something the Bai Clan didn’t know about.","Bai Tianheng continued.","\"I don’t think the Shen Clan would do something like this without a reason. If they have any sense at all, they should know that kidnapping Xueqing’er is no different from declaring war against the Bai Clan.\"","The three Grand Elders nodded solemnly.","The Bai Clan had already become the strongest force in the Eastern Region.","The Shen Clan had no chance of confronting them directly.","So why would they suddenly make such a reckless move?","There had to be something behind it.","Bai Tianheng’s expression became heavier.","He knew that their clan was already the strongest in the region.","However, what if the threat came from outside the region?","Long Haotian was a good example.","Who was to say that the Shen Clan didn’t have help from someone like him?","Although the Bai Clan had grown rapidly, they still couldn’t afford to assume that no one from the Central Region would interfere.","Bai Tianheng continued.","\"If the Shen Clan has the courage to make a move against Xueqing’er despite knowing all of this...\"","\"Then they must either have some kind of hidden trump card or believe that the Bai Clan won’t be able to do anything to them.\"","His gaze became cold.","\"Either way, we cannot underestimate them.\"","He nodded.","\"Since you’re still thinking rationally, let’s return to the clan and investigate everything first. We need to know exactly what happened at the Heaven Sword Sect.\"","\"And more importantly...\"","His voice became heavier.","\"We need to determine where the Shen Clan took Xueqing’er.\"","Bai Zihan finally spoke.","\"Do we have any information about the Shen Clan’s movements?\"","\"Not yet.\"","Bai Tianheng shook his head.","\"The moment we received the news, I immediately sent people to investigate. However, the information coming from the Heaven Sword Sect is still incomplete.\"","Bai Zihan nodded slightly.","\"Then let’s return first. We’ll gather everything we know and determine our next move. Also call the Heaven Sword Sect Leader. I have a few questions for him.\"","Bai Tianheng nodded.","\"Good!\"","The group began moving toward the Bai Clan once again.","However, as Bai Zihan turned around, his eyes became slightly colder."]},{"number":689,"title":"Chapter 689: Messenger from the Shen Clan","paragraphs":["By the time Bai Zihan returned to the Bai Clan, the main hall was already filled with people.","The atmosphere was extremely tense.","Several elders of the Bai Clan stood along the sides of the hall, their expressions solemn.","At the side sat the leader of the Heaven Sword Sect.","Han Sha!","However, unlike his usual calm and dignified appearance, Han Sha looked noticeably nervous.","There was even a faint trace of fear hidden within his eyes.","After all, Bai Xueqing had been kidnapped right under the Heaven Sword Sect’s nose.","And she wasn’t merely an ordinary disciple.","She was Bai Zihan’s younger sister.","Han Sha naturally understood what that meant.","The moment Bai Zihan entered the hall, Han Sha immediately stood up.","\"Clan Leader Bai!\"","Bai Zihan didn’t answer immediately.","His eyes swept across the hall before finally landing on Han Sha.","That single glance made Han Sha’s heart tighten.","He immediately began explaining.","\"Clan Leader Bai, please listen to me. We truly didn’t expect Shen Liang to have such courage.\"","\"Who could have imagined that he would actually dare to make a move against Miss Bai inside the Heaven Sword Sect?\"","Han Sha’s voice was slightly hurried.","\"I had already warned everyone that someone like Shen Liang shouldn’t be allowed to approach Miss Xueqing casually. But because he was no threat, we allowed him to continue pestering Peak Master Qinglan and Miss Bai.\"","\"I had already made sure to appoint a few guards to keep an eye on them. Who knew he would somehow possess an artifact capable of blocking even the spiritual sense of Immortal Realm cultivators?\"","\"Otherwise, there is no way he could have escaped.\"","As he spoke, Han Sha’s expression became increasingly helpless.","It was obvious that he was trying to explain the situation.","But more importantly, he was trying to distance himself from responsibility.","Bai Zihan’s expression gradually became colder.","\"Enough!\"","Han Sha immediately stopped.","\"Keep those excuses to yourself. Tell me something useful or else...\"","Han Sha’s expression stiffened.","He lowered his head slightly.","\"Yes!\"","For a moment, he didn’t know what to say.","The truth was that the Heaven Sword Sect genuinely didn’t know what had happened inside the barrier.","By the time their experts discovered that something was wrong and investigated the area, the battle had already ended.","Only the traces of the battle remained, but Bai Xueqing and Qinglan were already gone.","There was no way to determine exactly how Shen Liang had managed to accomplish everything.","Han Sha took a deep breath.","\"We’re still investigating the matter, but there is one likely possibility of how Miss Bai might have been kidnapped.\"","\"Shen Liang may possess a high-level spatial artifact.\"","\"The Heaven Sword Sect is protected by powerful formations. Those formations don’t merely defend against external attacks; they also restrict spatial fluctuations within the sect.\"","\"Under normal circumstances, tearing open the void and traveling through space should be impossible.\"","Han Sha’s expression became solemn.","\"Even if someone forcibly tore open the void, the resulting spatial fluctuations would immediately attract the attention of our experts. Yet nothing like that happened.\"","\"That leaves us with only a few possibilities.\"","He paused.","\"Either Shen Liang possessed some method capable of completely concealing spatial fluctuations, or he possessed an extremely high-level spatial artifact.\"","Bai Zihan’s eyes flickered slightly.","Han Sha continued.","\"If it was the latter, then the artifact may have allowed him to bypass the Heaven Sword Sect’s spatial restrictions entirely.\"","\"That would also explain how he disappeared without leaving behind any obvious traces.\"","The hall fell silent.","Bai Zihan slowly sat down.","His fingers lightly tapped against the armrest, which only increased the fear in Han Sha’s heart.","He knew Bai Zihan didn’t care much about this all but rather wants to hear where Bai Xueqing was and how to rescue her.","Just then, the doors of the main hall suddenly opened.","A Bai Clan disciple hurried inside.","\"Clan Leader!\"","He quickly bowed before speaking.","\"A messenger from the Shen Clan has arrived.\"","The moment those words were spoken, the atmosphere in the hall instantly changed.","Several Bai Clan elders looked at one another.","A messenger from the Shen Clan?","After kidnapping their Young Miss?","How audacious could they possibly be?","One of the elders couldn’t help but snort.","\"They actually have the nerve to send someone here?\"","\"After kidnapping Xueqing’er, they still dare to come to our Bai Clan?\"","\"This Shen Clan has truly lost its mind.\"","Several others were equally furious.","The mere thought of a Shen Clan messenger standing inside their main hall after what had happened was enough to make their blood boil.","However, Bai Tianheng immediately raised his hand.","The elders gradually fell silent.","Bai Tianheng’s expression remained calm.","\"Right now, we don’t know what the Shen Clan is planning. More importantly, we need to know where Xueqing’er was taken.\"","His eyes swept across the elders.","\"And we need to know what they want. So control yourselves. Until we know exactly what is happening, don’t act recklessly.\"","The elders exchanged glances before reluctantly nodding.","They understood Bai Tianheng’s reasoning.","No matter how arrogant the Shen Clan was acting, Bai Xueqing’s safety was the most important thing.","If killing the messenger caused the Shen Clan to harm her, then it would be a terrible trade.","Bai Tianheng turned toward the disciple.","\"Let him in.\"","\"Yes!\"","The disciple immediately left.","A few moments later, another figure entered the hall.","It was a middle-aged man wearing the robes of the Shen Clan.","The moment he stepped inside, his eyes swept across the hall.","Surprisingly, there wasn’t even a trace of fear on his face.","Instead, there was a faint smugness in his expression.","It was as though he were completely certain that everything was under his control.","Several Bai Clan elders immediately clenched their fists.","Their expressions became ugly.","Who in the entire Eastern Region would dare behave like this inside the Bai Clan’s main hall?","Especially after kidnapping the Bai Clan’s Young Miss?","If it weren’t for Bai Xueqing’s safety, several of them would have already attacked.","The messenger, however, seemed completely unaware of the danger surrounding him.","He calmly walked forward.","Bai Zihan looked at him.","His expression remained completely indifferent.","\"What message does the great Shen Clan have for our Bai Clan?\"","His voice carried a tone full of sarcasm.","Unfortunately, the messenger didn’t seem to notice it at all.","His chin lifted slightly.","\"Clan Leader Bai!\"","His tone was arrogant.","\"Miss Bai Xueqing is currently in the hands of our Shen Clan.\"","The hall instantly became silent.","Even though everyone already knew this, hearing the words directly from the Shen Clan’s messenger still caused their expressions to darken.","The messenger continued.","\"If the Bai Clan knows what’s good for you, then you should behave yourselves. Don’t do anything reckless.\"","\"Otherwise...\"","He deliberately paused.","\"The consequences will be something you will regret for the rest of your life.\"","Several elders nearly lost control.","Where in the world have they ever tolerated such arrogance in their own territory?","Not to mention now, even when they weren’t the absolute strongest, no one would dare have such arrogance.","How can they do nothing when they are being threatened?","One elder’s killing intent surged.","\"This bastard—\"","Bai Tianheng immediately glanced at him.","The elder clenched his teeth and forced himself to calm down.","For Bai Xueqing’s sake...","They had to endure.","Han Sha, meanwhile, stared at the messenger as though he were looking at an idiot.","He almost couldn’t believe what he was hearing.","Was this man really threatening the Bai Clan?","After kidnapping Bai Xueqing, the Shen Clan had actually sent someone here to flaunt their success and threaten the Bai Clan?","It was almost like stealing something from another person and then proudly returning the next day just to show the owner what had been stolen.","Didn’t this messenger understand where he was?","More importantly—","Wasn’t he afraid that the Bai Clan would lose their patience and kill him on the spot?","Yet Bai Zihan remained completely calm.","He didn’t even seem bothered by the man’s arrogance.","He simply looked at him.","\"What does the Shen Clan want?\"","His tone remained indifferent.","\"And where is my sister?\"","The messenger’s confidence grew even further upon seeing Bai Zihan’s reaction.","He mistakenly believed that Bai Zihan had understood the situation he was in.","He thought the Bai Clan had been forced into submission.","Naturally, his arrogance increased.","\"Very good. You are indeed worthy of being the Bai Clan’s Clan Leader.\"","He smiled smugly.","\"You understand the situation quickly.\"","Bai Zihan didn’t respond.","The messenger continued.","\"If you want to see Miss Bai alive...\"","His eyes narrowed.","\"Then the Bai Clan must hand over someone as well.\"","The hall became completely silent.","Bai Zihan’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Who?\"","The messenger smiled.","\"Jin Yuelin! Hand over Jin Yuelin. Then the Shen Clan will release Miss Bai. If you refuse...\"","His smile disappeared.","\"Then you can forget about seeing her alive again!\""]},{"number":690,"title":"Chapter 690: System Mission!","paragraphs":["The arrogant messenger thought that he could safely threaten the Bai Clan.","After all, their precious daughter was in his hands.","Several Bai Clan members exchanged glances.","Although the Shen Clan’s demand was outrageous, there was one thing they couldn’t deny.","If handing over Jin Yuelin could guarantee Bai Xueqing’s safety, then many of them felt that it was worth considering.","After all, Bai Zihan had once saved Jin Yuelin’s life.","The clan had also provided her with considerable resources for her cultivation, including resources for her brother, Jin Yuanzhan.","Wasn’t it only natural for her to repay that debt now?","In their minds, the value of Bai Xueqing was obviously far greater than Jin Yuelin’s.","Bai Xueqing was the Young Miss of the Bai Clan.","She was also an extremely talented cultivator and one of the most promising members of the younger generation.","Compared to her, Jin Yuelin was an outsider.","Although she was also extremely talented, compared to someone who shared the same bloodline, it didn’t matter much.","If one life had to be exchanged for another, most of the Bai Clan members would naturally choose Bai Xueqing.","However, there was still one thing that they couldn’t understand.","Why would the Shen Clan go so far?","Why would they risk kidnapping Bai Xueqing just for Jin Yuelin?","There had to be something more behind this.","Perhaps their true objective was something else, and they were using such a ransom merely to distract the Bai Clan.","The messenger, however, didn’t seem concerned with what the Bai Clan was thinking.","He continued speaking.","\"Of course, that’s not all.\"","Bai Zihan glanced at him.","The messenger smiled.","\"The Shen Clan also requires three Heaven-Grade Artifacts.\"","Several elders immediately frowned.","Three Heaven-Grade Artifacts?","That was already an enormous demand, though it wasn’t impossible for the current Bai Clan to provide them.","Even if it were ten, for Bai Xueqing, it would be nothing.","But the messenger wasn’t finished.","\"Furthermore, I will need to be treated properly while staying here.\"","His expression became even more arrogant.","\"I want the finest wine. The finest food. And the best dancers to entertain me.\"","His eyes swept across the hall.","\"Everything must be prepared according to the standards of the Shen Clan. If I’m not satisfied with how I’m treated, then don’t even think about me returning to report the Bai Clan’s response.\"","The hall became deathly silent.","Even Han Sha looked at the messenger in disbelief.","This man...","Was he truly trying to provoke the Bai Clan?","He had already demanded that someone from the Bai Clan be handed over.","Then three Heaven-Grade Artifacts.","And now he wanted the Bai Clan to entertain him with wine, food, and dancers.","It was almost absurd.","Most messengers, even if they came from an enemy faction, would be subservient when entering the Bai Clan.","But this messenger didn’t seem to understand the reality of his situation.","Bai Zihan, however, remained surprisingly calm.","He simply looked at the messenger.","\"Anything else?\"","The messenger thought for a moment.","Then he shook his head.","\"That’s all for now. If anything else comes to mind later, I’ll naturally inform you.\"","Bai Zihan nodded.","\"Good!\"","The messenger’s smile widened.","He thought Bai Zihan had finally submitted.","He had completely misunderstood the meaning behind that single word.","\"Since you’ve understood, then—\"","SLASH!","Before he could finish speaking, a terrifying sword Qi suddenly flashed through the hall.","The messenger’s four limbs were severed almost simultaneously.","His arms and legs flew through the air.","Blood sprayed across the floor.","\"ARGHHHH!\"","A miserable scream erupted from his mouth.","The messenger collapsed onto the ground, his entire body convulsing violently.","Only then did the pain fully register.","He stared at his severed limbs in disbelief.","He couldn’t understand what had happened.","A moment ago, everything had still been under his control.","Yet now...","He had been crippled before he could even react.","\"Ahhh!\"","His screams echoed throughout the hall.","The Bai Clan elders remained silent while Han Sha could only look at him with pity.","Han Sha knew that a demon like Bai Zihan wouldn’t have developed a good temper.","Bai Zihan had never been negotiating with this messenger.","He had simply been listening and watching the ridiculous performance of this clown.","The messenger slowly raised his head.","His trembling gaze finally landed on Bai Zihan.","The moment he saw Bai Zihan’s expression, his heart sank.","There was no anger.","No rage.","No emotional outburst.","Only coldness.","Bai Zihan looked down at him as though he were already a dead man.","Perhaps the Shen Clan had already regarded this messenger as disposable.","After all, they had deliberately chosen someone with such an arrogant personality for a task like this.","Perhaps they had even hoped that he would die.","Otherwise, knowing his temperament, why would they have sent him to the Bai Clan?","Of course, Bai Zihan didn’t really care about the Shen Clan’s intentions.","Whether the messenger had been abandoned by them or not made no difference.","He had already crossed the line.","Bai Zihan had no intention of showing mercy.","\"Don’t let him die easily.\"","His voice was cold.","\"Torture him in the prison.\"","\"Yes, Clan Leader!\"","Several Bai Clan cultivators immediately stepped forward.","The messenger’s expression changed drastically.","\"N-No! Clan Leader Bai, please! I was only delivering a message. P-Please spare me! I-I was wrong!\"","The arrogance from earlier had completely disappeared.","He desperately begged for mercy as two Bai Clan cultivators grabbed him.","\"I will put in a good word for you. The Shen Clan will definitely—\"","His words were cut off as he was dragged away.","His desperate screams gradually faded into the distance.","Everyone in the hall understood what awaited him.","The arrogant messenger who had entered the Bai Clan’s main hall with such confidence would spend the rest of his life experiencing nothing but pain.","Several Bai Clan members felt extremely satisfied.","That was what happened when someone dared to act arrogantly in front of the Bai Clan.","However, Bai Tianheng’s expression remained solemn.","He wasn’t concerned about the messenger.","He was concerned about Bai Xueqing.","\"Zihan’er.\"","His gaze became serious.","\"What about Xueqing’er? The Shen Clan will come to know what happened to their messenger. If they discover that we’ve tortured him...\"","His expression darkened.","\"Who knows what they might do to Xueqing’er?\"","The other elders also became concerned.","That was the most important issue.","No matter how satisfying it was to punish the messenger, Bai Xueqing’s safety came first.","Yet Bai Zihan remained completely calm.","\"Don’t worry, Father. I already know where she is.\"","The entire hall fell silent.","\"What?\"","Bai Tianheng stared at him in surprise.","Even the surrounding elders were stunned.","They had spent all this time trying to figure out where Shen Liang had taken Bai Xueqing.","How had Bai Zihan suddenly discovered her location?","Bai Zihan didn’t have time to explain everything.","Because at that moment, a familiar notification had already appeared within his mind.","[ Emergency Mission: Save Bai Xueqing. ]","[ Mission Location: ...]","The System had suddenly issued an emergency mission.","More importantly, it had directly provided the location of Bai Xueqing.","That was the reason Bai Zihan had been completely fearless when dealing with the messenger.","There was no longer any reason for him to give the Shen Clan face.","He knew exactly where his sister was.","And as long as he knew where she was, the Shen Clan’s threats were meaningless.","Bai Tianheng quickly asked,","\"Where is she?\"","Bai Zihan looked toward him.","\"The Shen Clan is more cautious than we thought. They didn’t keep Xueqing’er inside the Shen Clan’s territory.\"","His eyes became slightly colder.","\"She’s thousands of kilometers away.\"","The elders exchanged glances.","Bai Tianheng immediately understood.","\"Thousands of kilometers away? That’s probably deliberate.\"","Bai Zihan nodded.","\"Exactly. If the Bai Clan attacked the Shen Clan directly, we would naturally search their territory first.\"","\"But if Xueqing’er isn’t there...\"","His gaze sharpened.","\"We could destroy the entire Shen Clan and still find nothing.\"","The Shen Clan had clearly considered that possibility.","They had deliberately separated Bai Xueqing from their main territory.","That way, even if the Bai Clan launched an attack, they could pretend they had no idea where she was.","It was a cautious strategy.","Unfortunately for them, it was useless now.","The timely System mission had appeared, and it was also the first time the System had explicitly sent him a mission.","Until now, he only got for his achievement and the System has never issued a mission.","There were many questions Bai Zihan had, but for now, his priority was saving Bai Xueqing.","\"We’ll deal with this carefully.\"","Bai Tianheng nodded.","\"What’s your plan?\"","Bai Zihan immediately answered.","\"Father, you and the others will go to the Shen Clan. Also take Jin Yuelin and pretend that you’re going along with what they asked for.\"","\"Also demand an explanation for what happened and try to buy as much time as possible. Let them think that we believe Bai Xueqing is in their territory.\"","The elders immediately understood.","It was a distraction.","Bai Zihan continued.","\"Meanwhile, I’ll form a small team. I’ll personally go to the location where Xueqing’er is being held.\"","\"We’ll rescue her before the Shen Clan realizes what we’re doing.\""]},{"number":691,"title":"Chapter 691: The Bai Clan Descends Upon the Shen Clan","paragraphs":["Within the Shen Clan, the atmosphere was completely different from that of the Bai Clan.","Several important members had gathered in the main hall.","Their expressions were excited.","\"Once the Bai Clan hands over Jin Yuelin, everything will be settled.\"","\"With her as a hostage, the Bai Clan won’t dare act recklessly.\"","Several elders nodded in agreement.","The situation seemed extremely favorable for the Shen Clan.","However, one elder suddenly frowned.","\"Are we certain that everything will go smoothly?\"","The hall became slightly quieter.","If something went wrong...","The consequences would be unimaginable.","An elder immediately waved his hand.","\"Don’t worry. Everything has already been arranged. We have the support of the Lord!\"","The atmosphere relaxed again.","However, one of the older elders suddenly spoke in a solemn tone.","\"Don’t become careless.\"","Everyone looked toward him.","His expression was serious.","\"If we fail to accomplish what the Lord ordered...\"","He paused.","\"You should all know what awaits us.\"","The expressions of several people immediately changed.","The excitement from earlier disappeared.","A trace of fear appeared in their eyes.","The Lord’s punishment.","Just thinking about it was enough to make them shudder.","No one in the Shen Clan dared to question the Lord’s authority.","If they failed...","The consequences would be far worse than death.","For several moments, nobody spoke.","Then another elder suddenly laughed.","\"Hahaha! Why are you all so worried?\"","His confidence quickly infected the others.","\"Everything has gone according to plan. The Bai Clan will be forced to follow our demands. There is absolutely no way we can fail.\"","The other members gradually relaxed.","That’s right. What could possibly go wrong?","The Bai Clan might be powerful within the Eastern Region.","But this matter had been carefully planned from the beginning.","\"Hehe, I want to see their faces when they find out that all this bargaining is a lie. Bai Tianheng might die of anger! Haha...\"","From the beginning, they had never planned to give Bai Xueqing back.","\"B-But the Bai Clan won’t let us off easily if we do this.\"","\"Hmph! With the Lord’s support, are you afraid that we can’t handle the Bai Clan?\"","Just then—","Boom!","The entire Shen Clan suddenly trembled.","The expressions of everyone inside the hall changed.","\"What happened?\"","Boom!","Another terrifying rumble shook the surrounding space.","A monstrous pressure descended upon the entire Shen Clan.","The smiles disappeared from everyone’s faces.","Several elders immediately rushed outside.","The moment they looked toward the sky, their pupils contracted violently.","A vast group of cultivators, along with a huge flying ship, was approaching the Shen Clan.","Their momentum was overwhelming.","The sky seemed to darken beneath their presence.","Terrifying spiritual pressure spread in every direction.","The Bai Clan had arrived!","And they had arrived with a force that seemed capable of destroying heaven and earth.","The previously confident Shen Clan members were instantly stunned.","\"What...\"","\"How many people did they bring?\"","Someone’s voice trembled.","No one answered.","They were too shocked to speak.","The Bai Clan’s forces surged forward like an enormous storm.","Their killing intent was not concealed in the slightest.","It was as though they had come prepared to tear the entire Shen Clan apart.","The same elders who had been confidently discussing how the Bai Clan would eventually submit were now completely silent.","One of them swallowed hard.","\"Gulp!\"","His throat moved visibly.","Another elder’s face had already turned pale.","\"This...\"","His voice trembled.","\"Are they really here to negotiate?\"","No one responded.","Everyone could see the answer.","This didn’t look like a force that had come to negotiate.","It looked like an army preparing to destroy the enemy.","Even the most arrogant Shen Clan members couldn’t maintain their confidence anymore.","They had believed the Bai Clan would be forced to compromise because Bai Xueqing was in their hands.","Yet now, facing the terrifying momentum approaching them, they suddenly felt an inexplicable chill.","The entire Shen Clan fell silent.","No one dared to speak recklessly anymore.","Soon, a group of figures descended before the entrance of the Shen Clan.","At the front stood Bai Tianheng.","Behind him were several powerful Bai Clan experts.","Jin Yuelin and Jin Yuanzhan also stood among them.","Jin Yuanzhan’s expression was extremely ugly.","His fists were tightly clenched.","His eyes were fixed on the Shen Clan with barely concealed fury.","His little sister had been targeted by the Shen Clan.","How could he possibly remain calm?","The Shen Clan’s gates slowly opened.","A middle-aged man walked out.","He wore a dark-colored robe embroidered with the insignia of the Shen Clan.","His expression was calm and dignified.","This man was the current leader of the Shen Clan—","Shen Wuheng!","As the leader of the Shen Clan, Shen Wuheng naturally possessed considerable authority.","However, at this moment, even he couldn’t completely hide the nervousness in his heart.","The lineup standing before him was simply too terrifying.","The Bai Clan had clearly mobilized a significant portion of its strength.","Even though Shen Wuheng had been prepared for this, actually facing them was an entirely different matter.","Nevertheless, he forced himself to remain calm.","He stepped forward.","\"Clan Leader Bai!\"","His voice was steady.","\"Have you brought the person we requested?\"","His gaze shifted toward Jin Yuelin.","\"If you have, then everything can proceed smoothly.\"","He paused briefly.","\"But if you haven’t...\"","His expression became slightly colder.","\"You should understand what will happen to Miss Bai Xueqing.\"","The words sounded confident.","Yet only Shen Wuheng himself knew how nervous he truly was.","The Bai Clan’s pressure was simply too frightening.","Even though he knew that the Lord was supporting them, he couldn’t help but wonder—","Would that support really be enough?","Could the mysterious Lord truly protect the Shen Clan from the Bai Clan?","For a brief moment, doubt appeared in Shen Wuheng’s heart.","But he quickly suppressed it.","No!","There was no need to doubt.","The Lord had already arranged everything.","Moreover, their Shen Clan couldn’t possibly remain in the same empire as the Bai Clan.","If they didn’t do this, they could only watch helplessly as the Bai Clan swallowed them up.","This was something they had to do for the survival and prosperity of the Shen Clan.","His confidence returned.","Sure enough, when he noticed Jin Yuelin standing among the Bai Clan’s group, Shen Wuheng’s heart finally relaxed slightly.","They had brought her.","That meant the negotiation had begun exactly as they had expected.","He stepped forward.","\"Good!\"","His gaze became sharper.","\"Bai Tianheng, listen carefully. Hand Jin Yuelin over to us, and we will immediately hand your daughter back to you.\"","However, Bai Tianheng didn’t move.","Neither did Jin Yuelin.","Shen Wuheng frowned slightly.","Why weren’t they handing her over?","Before he could say anything else, Bai Tianheng finally spoke.","\"Shen Wuheng!\"","The Shen Clan Leader’s expression stiffened slightly.","Bai Tianheng’s gaze became cold.","\"Before we discuss the exchange, answer one question. Why did you kidnap my daughter?\"","Shen Wuheng’s expression changed slightly.","Bai Tianheng continued.","\"You should know very well what happens to those who dare scheme against the Bai Clan.\"","His voice wasn’t loud.","Yet every word carried a heavy pressure.","\"Kidnapping Bai Xueqing is not something that can be dismissed as a simple misunderstanding.\"","\"You deliberately targeted my daughter. You knew exactly who she was. And your son still chose to do it.\"","Bai Tianheng’s eyes narrowed.","\"So tell me, Shen Wuheng. What exactly are you trying to accomplish? Do you really want to go to war with us?\"","Shen Wuheng’s expression changed slightly under Bai Tianheng’s cold gaze.","However, he quickly forced a smile.","\"Clan Leader Bai, you’ve misunderstood.\"","His tone became somewhat conciliatory.","Bai Tianheng’s eyes narrowed.","\"Misunderstood?\"","\"Yes!\"","Shen Wuheng nodded.","\"We never intended to provoke the Bai Clan. Our objective from the beginning was only Jin Yuelin.\"","His gaze shifted toward the woman standing behind Bai Tianheng.","\"However, she has been heavily protected by the Bai Clan. We had no opportunity to approach her. So...\"","Shen Wuheng spread his hands helplessly.","\"We had no choice but to take more extreme measures.\"","Shen Wuheng continued.","\"Of course, we understand that this matter has caused some unpleasantness. Therefore, the Shen Clan is willing to make a concession.\"","His expression became serious.","\"As long as the Bai Clan hands over Jin Yuelin, we will immediately return Miss Bai Xueqing.\"","He paused.","\"Once the exchange is complete, everything will be over.\"","Bai Tianheng stared at him.","Then—","\"Hahaha!\"","A burst of laughter suddenly erupted from his mouth.","It contained no amusement whatsoever. Only anger.","The laughter echoed across the area before gradually fading.","Bai Tianheng’s expression became cold.","\"So that’s your explanation?\"","Shen Wuheng remained silent.","Bai Tianheng shook his head.","\"You wanted Jin Yuelin. Because you couldn’t get to her, you kidnapped my daughter.\"","\"And now you’re standing in front of us telling me that you had no choice?\"","His voice gradually became colder.","\"What kind of joke is this?\"","Shen Wuheng’s expression stiffened.","He quickly replied.","\"Clan Leader Bai, regardless of how you feel about it, this is the reality. We are only asking for Jin Yuelin.\"","\"If you hand her over, Miss Bai Xueqing will be returned safely.\"","Bai Tianheng stared at him for several moments.","\"It isn’t impossible but along with my daughter, you must also end your son and the ones who attacked her.\"","\"Unless I punish them myself, I won’t feel satisfied!\"","Shen Wuheng’s expression immediately darkened.","\"That is impossible!\"","Bai Tianheng’s eyes narrowed.","\"Impossible?\"","\"Yes. My son and the others were only following the Shen Clan’s orders. I cannot hand them over to you.\"","Bai Tianheng laughed coldly.","\"They harmed my daughter. And now you want me to simply let them go?\"","Shen Wuheng frowned.","\"Clan Leader Bai, Miss Xueqing is still alive and unharmed. As long as you hand over Jin Yuelin, we will return her safely.\"","Bai Tianheng’s expression became cold.","\"If the people who harmed my daughter are left unpunished, where do you expect me to put my face?\"","His voice carried a hint of anger.","\"She is my daughter and a member of the Bai Clan. If those who dared to harm her can walk away without consequences, then what will the rest of the world think of the Bai Clan?\"","\"Will anyone still fear us?\"","Shen Wuheng’s expression became increasingly ugly.","Bai Tianheng continued coldly.","\"You want Jin Yuelin.\"","\"Fine. We can discuss that.\"","\"But the people who harmed my daughter must be punished. Otherwise, this matter is not over!\""]},{"number":692,"title":"Chapter 692: Bai Xueqing in Captivity","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, while Bai Tianheng continued wasting the Shen Clan’s time, Bai Zihan and his team were already heading toward the location where Bai Xueqing was being held captive.","This operation was deliberately kept small.","Only the strongest experts had been brought.","Three Earth Immortals!","And Bai Ren, who possessed Golden Immortal strength.","There was no need to bring too many people.","Doing so would only increase the chances of alerting the Shen Clan.","Bai Zihan stood at the front of the group, his expression calm as he silently calculated their chances.","The Shen Clan clearly believed that the Bai Clan had no idea where Bai Xueqing was being held.","That confidence was precisely what gave them an advantage.","As long as they believed that the Bai Clan didn’t know where Bai Xueqing was being kept, they wouldn’t deploy too many people to guard her.","Especially since they knew that the Bai Clan’s forces were currently at the Shen Clan.","If they sent too many people to guard Bai Xueqing, there was also a high chance that their movements would attract attention.","With three Earth Immortals and Bai Ren accompanying him, Bai Zihan was confident that rescuing Bai Xueqing would not be too difficult.","Just then, a communication talisman suddenly lit up.","Bai Zihan glanced at it.","A message from Bai Tianheng.","They had arrived at the Shen Clan.","And, more importantly, Bai Tianheng was already making a huge commotion.","He was deliberately drawing the Shen Clan’s attention toward himself.","A faint smile appeared on Bai Zihan’s face.","\"Father has arrived.\"","The surrounding experts immediately became serious.","Bai Zihan looked ahead.","\"Then there’s no reason for us to wait any longer.\"","His eyes became sharp.","\"Move!\"","The moment his voice fell, the entire group accelerated.","The moment Bai Zihan gave the order, the entire group immediately concealed their auras.","No one dared to release the slightest trace of Qi.","They also didn’t dare tear open the void.","Under normal circumstances, traveling through the void would be much faster.","However, the spatial fluctuations created by tearing open the void could easily attract the attention of nearby experts.","The same applied to flying at high speed.","Therefore, they had only one choice: using their physical speed.","Fortunately, everyone in the group was extremely powerful.","Their physical speed alone was astonishing.","Whoosh!","Several figures flashed across the land like ghosts.","Their feet barely touched the ground before they disappeared into the distance again.","They moved silently, relying purely on their physical strength to travel toward their destination.","***","Meanwhile, thousands of kilometers away.","Inside a secluded underground chamber.","Bai Xueqing slowly opened her eyes.","Her vision was initially blurry.","She tried to move but the moment she did, she felt the restraints around her body.","Her expression changed.","She immediately looked around.","The first thing she saw was a familiar figure.","\"Master...\"","Bai Xueqing’s eyes widened.","Qinglan was tied up nearby. Her condition was no better than Bai Xueqing’s.","Her hands were bound, and her cultivation had clearly been sealed.","Bai Xueqing’s expression immediately became solemn.","She tried to recall what had happened.","The memories slowly returned.","At that time, she and Qinglan had been fighting against two Great Ascension Realm cultivators and Shen Liang.","Although the situation was dangerous, Bai Xueqing had not been losing.","She had been able to hold on.","Even if she couldn’t defeat them immediately, she had been confident that she could continue fighting.","But then, something unexpected happened.","Shen Liang had suddenly activated a strange artifact.","A powerful spatial fluctuation had erupted.","A teleportation artifact!","Bai Xueqing’s expression changed slightly.","Shen Liang had used that artifact to summon additional cultivators.","More importantly, their cultivation was so powerful that Bai Xueqing couldn’t even clearly sense their realms.","After that... Her memories became blurry.","She couldn’t remember exactly what had happened afterward.","She could only vaguely recall being surrounded.","Then—nothing.","When she woke up again, she was already here.","Bai Xueqing’s heart sank.","She immediately understood what had most likely happened.","She had been defeated and Shen Liang had kidnapped her.","At that moment—","\"Hehe...\"","A familiar voice suddenly echoed through the chamber.","\"You’re finally awake.\"","Bai Xueqing’s expression instantly became cold.","She looked toward the entrance.","A figure slowly walked into the chamber.","Shen Liang!","He wore a smug smile as he looked at the two women.","Seeing Bai Xueqing awake, the smile on his face widened.","\"Hehe, it seems your injuries weren’t as serious as I thought.\"","Bai Xueqing stared at him coldly.","\"Shen Liang!\"","Her voice carried obvious killing intent.","\"You’d better pray that the Bai Clan never finds you.\"","Shen Liang’s smile froze slightly.","Then he laughed.","\"Hahaha! Your Clan?\"","He shook his head.","Shen Liang’s smile became even wider.","\"Do you really think the Bai Clan can save you?\"","He slowly walked closer.","\"The Bai Clan is already under the hands of our Shen Clan.\"","Bai Xueqing’s eyes narrowed.","Shen Liang continued smugly.","\"You think the Bai Clan is strong? Hehe... You have no idea who is backing our Shen Clan.\"","His expression became increasingly excited.","\"For them, a clan like the Bai Clan is nothing more than a slightly larger ant. The Bai Clan’s strength may be impressive in the Eastern Region, but before that existence, it means nothing.\"","Shen Liang’s eyes gleamed with excitement.","\"The Bai Clan’s doom has already arrived!\"","Bai Xueqing looked at him coldly.","She clearly didn’t believe his words.","However, she couldn’t completely dismiss them either.","After all, too many strange things had happened recently.","Shen Liang’s severed arm had somehow recovered.","His cultivation had even advanced all the way to the Void Refinement Realm.","And there were also those cultivators whose cultivation and identities she didn’t know.","There was clearly something unusual happening behind the Shen Clan.","Even so, Bai Xueqing still refused to believe that the Bai Clan would lose, especially with Bai Zihan.","Bai Zihan also possessed countless strange methods and trump cards.","Even she didn’t know how many secrets he was hiding.","There was no way someone like Shen Liang could understand what Bai Zihan was capable of.","As long as Bai Zihan was still there, Bai Xueqing couldn’t believe that the Shen Clan could truly destroy the Bai Clan.","Shen Liang, however, misunderstood her silence.","He stepped closer, his eyes filled with greed.","\"Of course, there is still a way for you to survive.\"","Bai Xueqing frowned.","Shen Liang grinned.","\"Submit to me. Become my woman. If you agree to serve me obediently, I might consider pleading with the Lord on your behalf.\"","His expression became increasingly arrogant.","\"Perhaps I can even convince them to spare your life.\"","Bai Xueqing stared at him for several seconds.","Then she coldly replied,","\"You should look in the mirror first.\"","Shen Liang’s smile froze.","Bai Xueqing’s eyes were filled with undisguised contempt.","Shen Liang stared at Bai Xueqing for several moments.","Instead of becoming angry, his smile gradually widened.","\"Good! Good!\"","His eyes were filled with excitement.","\"I wonder how many days your arrogance will last.\"","His gaze swept over Bai Xueqing’s face.","\"Let’s see how long you can maintain that expression.\"","Slap!","A sharp sound echoed through the chamber.","Shen Liang suddenly slapped Bai Xueqing across the face.","Her head was forced slightly to the side, yet Bai Xueqing didn’t cry out.","She didn’t even make a sound.","Slowly, she turned her head back.","Her eyes locked onto Shen Liang.","They were filled with icy killing intent.","Shen Liang wasn’t frightened.","Instead, his smile became even wider.","\"Still glaring at me?\"","He laughed softly.","\"Good. Very good.\"","He reached out and grabbed Bai Xueqing’s chin, forcing her to look directly at him.","\"You’re enduring quite well. I wonder how long you can continue.\"","Bai Xueqing remained silent.","Her eyes were cold enough to freeze the surrounding air.","Shen Liang seemed to enjoy her reaction.","\"Watching someone as proud as you slowly lose that arrogance will be far more interesting.\"","Just then—","A cold voice suddenly came from behind him.","\"What are you doing?\"","Shen Liang’s expression instantly changed.","The arrogance on his face disappeared.","His body stiffened.","He immediately turned around.","The moment he saw the figure standing behind him, his pupils contracted.","Without hesitation, Shen Liang stepped back and bowed deeply.","\"Greetings, Sir!\"","His voice was filled with respect.","And beneath that respect was unmistakable fear.","\"What brings you here, Sir?\"","The man glanced past Shen Liang and looked at Bai Xueqing.","His expression remained indifferent.","\"I came to check on her.\"","Shen Liang immediately nodded.","\"Of course, Sir!\"","He glanced at Bai Xueqing and smiled.","\"Don’t worry, Sir. I’ll teach her a proper lesson. I’ll make sure she becomes obedient to me.\"","Slap!","A terrifying force suddenly struck Shen Liang across the face.","His body was sent stumbling several steps to the side.","He froze in disbelief, clutching his burning cheek.","The man looked at him coldly.","\"Do you really think someone like you is worthy of coveting her?\""]},{"number":693,"title":"Chapter 693: A Failed Experiment","paragraphs":["The man stared at Shen Liang with undisguised disgust.","He had already reached this stage, yet Shen Liang still didn’t understand anything.","The man slowly took out a handkerchief.","He wiped his palm carefully, as though touching Shen Liang had made his hand dirty.","Then he turned his attention toward Bai Xueqing.","Shen Liang’s expression twisted with rage.","The fear he had shown moments ago seemed to vanish completely.","\"What do you mean by that?!\"","He roared.","The man glanced at him indifferently.","\"She is someone who will become the Lord’s woman.\"","The moment those words fell, Shen Liang froze.","His eyes widened.","For several seconds, he couldn’t believe what he had just heard.","Then—","\"You’re saying...\"","\"Yes! So know your place.\"","Shen Liang’s expression gradually twisted with fury.","His fists clenched tightly.","He had done all of this for Bai Xueqing.","He had risked everything.","He had kidnapped her.","He had brought her here.","He had even offended the Bai Clan and now someone was telling him to simply step aside?","How could he accept that?","\"I will kill you!\"","Boom!","Shen Liang’s aura erupted violently.","Peak Void Refinement Realm!","His figure shot forward like a cannonball, charging directly toward the man.","\"Idiot!\"","The man didn’t even bother to move his feet.","He simply raised his hand.","Slap!","A terrifying force struck Shen Liang across the face.","His entire body was sent flying.","Bang!","He crashed heavily into the wall, causing the entire chamber to tremble.","Bai Xueqing’s eyes narrowed slightly.","However, Shen Liang wasn’t finished.","He slowly climbed out of the rubble. His eyes were bloodshot.","His expression was completely distorted.","\"AHHHHH!\"","He roared.","The aura around his body suddenly surged again.","Crack! Crack!","Strange sounds came from within his body.","His muscles twisted.","His bones began to change.","His skin became increasingly distorted.","The aura surrounding him grew stronger and stronger.","Great Ascension Realm!","Bai Xueqing’s expression changed slightly.","This was no longer a normal breakthrough.","Something was happening to Shen Liang’s body.","His appearance rapidly became more grotesque.","His skin darkened.","Veins bulged across his body.","His face twisted into something barely resembling a human.","His fingers lengthened into sharp claws.","A disgusting aura spread throughout the chamber.","Bai Xueqing stared at the transformation in silence.","(What exactly had happened to Shen Liang?)","The man merely watched with indifference.","Shen Liang’s sanity seemed to have almost completely disappeared.","\"Die!\"","With a roar, he charged forward again.","This time, the man finally moved.","His figure flashed.","Before Shen Liang could even react—","Boom!","A terrifying force pierced directly through his body.","Shen Liang’s eyes widened.","His monstrous body suddenly froze.","Blood flowed from the corner of his mouth.","The man withdrew his hand.","Thud!","Shen Liang’s body collapsed heavily onto the ground.","He was dead!","The man looked down at Shen Liang’s corpse.","He slowly shook his head.","\"A failed experiment.\"","His eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Not completely though.\"","A faint trace of interest appeared in his eyes.","\"He did produce some very interesting results.\"","Bai Xueqing had watched everything unfold in complete silence.","Shock filled her eyes.","There were two things that left her deeply unsettled.","The first was Shen Liang’s transformation.","That disgusting appearance had been completely beyond her expectations.","The second was the strength displayed by the man standing before her.","It was terrifying.","Bai Xueqing was certain that he was not merely at the Immortal Ascension Realm.","In fact, he might not be an Earth Immortal.","His strength was clearly beyond anything she had encountered before.","Yet strangely, that wasn’t what concerned her the most.","What Bai Xueqing found even more curious was what the man had said before.","A failed experiment.","What exactly had he done to Shen Liang?","Bai Xueqing looked at him.","\"What did you do to him?\"","The man glanced at Shen Liang’s corpse before turning back toward her.","His attitude remained polite.","\"That is something Miss doesn’t need to worry about.\"","Bai Xueqing narrowed her eyes.","She carefully studied his expression.","There was no intention of explaining.","No matter how she questioned him, he clearly wouldn’t answer.","And she had to remember her current situation.","She was merely a prisoner.","There was no reason for him to tell her anything.","Bai Xueqing didn’t continue pressing the matter.","Instead, she asked another question.","\"Who is this Lord? What does he want from me?\"","The man’s expression became slightly more respectful.","Even his tone carried a trace of reverence.","\"The Lord is the most respected and talented man in this world. His existence stands above countless others.\"","\"He possesses unparalleled talent and strength.\"","The man’s eyes revealed genuine admiration.","\"Miss should consider yourself fortunate to be able to become the Lord’s woman. Once you meet him, you will understand what kind of fortune has fallen upon you.\"","\"He is the best man in the world! A god among men!\"","Bai Xueqing listened quietly.","The more she heard, the more disgusted she became.","Bai Xueqing slowly looked around the chamber.","Her eyes swept across every corner.","Unfortunately, she couldn’t find any obvious way to escape.","Her cultivation had been sealed, and even if she somehow managed to break free from her restraints, she had no idea how many enemies were waiting outside.","Under the current circumstances, escaping would be extremely difficult.","She sighed inwardly.","Then, as if she had suddenly thought of something, a faint smile appeared on her face.","\"Oh? Does a man more brilliant than me exist? \"Mind telling me more about this ’Lord’?\"","The man’s expression changed slightly.","\"Who?\"","He abruptly turned around.","A figure was standing behind him.","Bai Zihan!","Bai Zihan’s expression was calm as he looked directly at the man.","Then his gaze shifted toward the corpse lying on the ground.","Although Shen Liang’s appearance had become almost unrecognizable, Bai Zihan still recognized him.","\"He is already dead?\"","A trace of disappointment appeared in his eyes.","\"Pity!\"","He had originally been looking forward to personally torturing Shen Liang.","Now, that opportunity was gone.","The man’s expression became solemn.","He stared at Bai Zihan for several moments before finally speaking.","\"How did you find this place?\"","For the first time since his appearance, genuine surprise could be heard in his voice.","The arrogance and indifference he had displayed earlier had disappeared.","Bai Zihan didn’t answer. Instead, he looked at him calmly.","\"Answer me! That way you can make things easier for yourself...\"","The man’s expression froze. Then—","\"Hahaha!\"","He suddenly burst into laughter.","His previous surprise quickly disappeared.","\"So what if you found this place?\"","He looked at Bai Zihan with a hint of ridicule. His aura slowly began to rise.","\"You are already dead!\"","\"Do you think this old man is dead?\"","Bai Ren also showed himself. His gaze was cold as he looked at the man.","He cracked his knuckles.","\"Why don’t you defeat me first?\"","The moment his voice fell, three more figures appeared beside Bai Zihan.","Three Earth Immortals!","All four of them released powerful auras.","Bai Xueqing’s eyes widened.","The moment she saw Bai Zihan and the others, the heavy feeling in her heart finally eased.","Bai Zihan had come. And with him were Bai Ren and three Earth Immortals.","The man’s expression darkened.","\"More intruders?\"","He frowned.","Looking at the situation before him, it was obvious that Bai Zihan hadn’t simply stumbled upon this place by chance.","Furthermore, the four experts who had appeared behind him were clearly powerful.","The man carefully examined them.","\"Who are you? And why are you interfering?\"","Bai Zihan glanced at him.","\"This idiot. You kidnapped my sister and don’t even know who I am?\"","He shook his head.","\"Looks like your arrogance is even greater than mine.\"","The man’s pupils suddenly contracted.","A moment later, realization finally dawned upon him.","\"You... Bai Zihan?\"","His expression changed.","\"Weren’t you supposed to be at the Shen Clan?\"","Bai Zihan raised an eyebrow.","\"Why should we go there?\"","His gaze shifted toward Bai Xueqing.","\"Isn’t my dear sister here? You thought you could deceive us with your little trick?\"","\"YOU...\"","The man’s expression became furious.","For a moment, killing intent surged from his body.","However, he quickly suppressed it.","A smile gradually returned to his face.","\"Hahaha! I see.\"","He looked at Bai Zihan with a completely different expression.","\"I underestimated you. You aren’t as foolish as you seemed.\"","Bai Zihan smiled faintly.","\"And you are just as foolish as you look.\"","His gaze became slightly colder.","\"Perhaps your so-called Lord is even more foolish.\"","The moment those words fell, the man’s expression completely changed.","His previous calmness vanished.","\"Shut up!\"","A terrifying fury erupted from his eyes.","\"You dare insult the Lord?\"","His voice shook the entire chamber.","\"Who do you think you are? An ant like you has no right to speak about the Lord!\"","Boom!","A terrifying aura suddenly erupted from his body.","Golden Immortal!","The pressure swept through the entire chamber like a storm.","However, Bai Zihan and the others didn’t panic.","Not even the slightest trace of surprise appeared on their faces.","Instead, Bai Ren merely narrowed his eyes.","\"So that’s it.\"","Bai Zihan’s expression remained calm.","He had already expected this.","If the Shen Clan didn’t possess the backing of at least a Golden Immortal, how could they have the courage to provoke the Bai Clan?","The man looked at their calm expressions and frowned.","He had expected fear, shock and perhaps even desperation.","Yet none of those emotions appeared.","Bai Zihan simply stood there, looking at him as though his Golden Immortal cultivation wasn’t particularly impressive.","A faint smile appeared on Bai Zihan’s face.","\"So you’re only a Golden Immortal? How dare you be more arrogant than this young master!\""]},{"number":694,"title":"Chapter 694: Gu Master","paragraphs":["The man found Bai Zihan’s attitude utterly ridiculous.","A mere Great Ascension Realm cultivator was actually looking down on a Golden Immortal?","This level of arrogance was far beyond anything he had ever seen.","\"Hmph! I’ll show you your place!\"","The man’s aura erupted as he charged toward Bai Zihan.","However, before he could reach him, another figure stepped forward.","Clang!","Bai Ren’s fist collided directly with the man’s palm.","The terrifying impact shook the entire chamber.","\"I already told you.\"","Bai Ren’s eyes were cold.","\"If you want to reach our Clan Leader, you have to get through me first!\"","The man’s expression changed slightly.","He hadn’t expected Bai Ren to be this formidable, almost reaching his own strength.","However, this wasn’t completely unexpected.","It was already widely known that the Bai Clan possessed two Golden Immortals.","Although many people still regarded that information as nothing more than a rumor, the man had naturally prepared for the possibility.","\"Hmph! Do you think I came here without making any preparations?\"","He suddenly raised his hand.","A sharp whistle echoed through the chamber.","Whoosh!","Two figures suddenly appeared behind him.","The moment Bai Zihan and the others saw them, their expressions changed slightly.","The two figures looked vaguely human.","But their bodies were pale and withered, resembling corpses that had been given life.","Their eyes were dull.","Their skin was dry and lifeless yet terrifying energy surged from within their bodies.","They immediately charged toward the Bai Clan’s forces.","\"What is this?\"","Bai Ren’s expression became solemn.","The strange existence before him looked human, but its aura was completely different from that of an ordinary cultivator.","It didn’t possess the vitality of a living person yet its strength was extraordinary.","At the same time, the other corpse-like figure was intercepted by the three Earth Immortals.","Boom!","A terrifying battle instantly erupted.","The man looked toward Bai Zihan and laughed.","\"Hehe... Bai Zihan, now who can save you?\"","A shaken voice suddenly echoed within Bai Zihan’s mind.","(H-How can they still exist?)","It was Immortal Emperor Feilian.","Bai Zihan could clearly hear the immense shock in her voice.","He immediately asked,","\"You know what this is?\"","Empress Feilian remained silent for several moments.","Then she slowly spoke.","\"He’s probably a Gu Master.\"","Bai Zihan’s expression changed slightly.","\"A Gu Master?\"","\"Yes!\"","Empress Feilian’s tone was solemn.","\"Those two things should be corpses controlled by him. To control Golden Immortal corpses to this extent, he must be an extremely powerful Gu Master.\"","Bai Zihan fell silent.","Considering all the novels he had read in his previous life, he immediately understood what Feilian meant.","However, one thing still confused him.","Why was Feilian so shaken by their existence?","\"Are they really that strong?\"","Empress Feilian paused.","\"They themselves aren’t necessarily that powerful but that’s not the frightening part.\"","\"As long as they are given enough time and can obtain enough powerful corpses, their strength can continue to increase.\"","\"There’s practically no limit.\"","Empress Feilian’s voice grew colder.","\"And that’s still not the worst part. The worst part is that they will do anything to obtain suitable corpses.\"","\"They don’t hesitate to slaughter millions of living beings. The more chaos and death they create, the more they thrive.\"","\"They love sowing chaos. They love starting wars. Because every war means countless deaths.\"","\"And every death provides them with more corpses to use.\"","Bai Zihan’s eyes narrowed.","\"They’re even more hateful than Demonic Cultivators!\"","Empress Feilian’s voice carried unmistakable hatred.","For Feilian to say that,one should understand just how much she hates them.","Bai Zihan had never heard Feilian speak with such hatred before.","It seemed that her hatred toward Gu Masters ran far deeper than he had imagined.","Empress Feilian’s voice became solemn.","\"No matter what, you must kill him.\"","Bai Zihan’s expression turned cold.","\"Of course!\"","He didn’t need Feilian to remind him.","The man was already his enemy.","There was no way he would simply let him leave.","However, before killing him, Bai Zihan still wanted to obtain information about the so-called Lord.","That mysterious existence is the one who is clearly after Bai Xueqing.","Meanwhile, the man stared at Bai Zihan.","His expression gradually became ugly.","From the beginning until now, Bai Zihan had remained completely calm despite having thought to corner him.","There was no fear. Not even the slightest trace of concern.","Rather from the start when he thought he had cornered him, Bai Zihan didn’t seem to pay attention to him at all.","The man couldn’t tolerate it any longer.","\"Bai Zihan!\"","His voice exploded with fury.","\"You think ignoring me can change your situation? Then think again!\"","The man suddenly moved.","Whoosh!","His figure transformed into a blur as he rushed directly toward Bai Zihan.","There was no one left to protect him.","The three Earth Immortals were already completely occupied by one Golden Immortal Corpse.","As for Bai Ren, he was desperately trying to break away from his opponent.","However, the Golden Immortal fighting him was extremely strange.","Bai Ren had tried several times to deceive it and shake it off, but instead of retreating when struck, the corpse would simply endure the attack and continue pursuing him.","It seemed completely indifferent to its own injuries.","Its only objective was to keep Bai Ren occupied.","Bai Ren’s expression became increasingly anxious.","He knew exactly what the man was planning.","\"Bai Zihan!\"","He wanted to rush over and protect Bai Zihan.","But there was nothing he could do.","The enemy in front of him was simply too persistent.","Even when Bai Ren deliberately exposed an opening, trying to lure it away, the enemy didn’t fall for the trick.","It simply endured his attack and continued fighting. It was as though it were hell-bent on keeping him here regardless of the cost.","\"Damn it!\"","Bai Ren cursed inwardly.","They had never expected there to be three Golden Immortals here.","One was the mysterious man himself.","And the other two were these terrifying corpse beings.","\"We should have brought more people!\"","Bai Ren gritted his teeth.","If they had brought even one more Golden Immortal, the situation would have been completely different.","He couldn’t help regretting his earlier decision.","He had even given the Saint-Grade Sword to Bai Chu because he had believed that the opponents waiting at the Shen Clan would be far more powerful.","Who could have imagined that the real danger would be hidden here?","Meanwhile—","The mysterious man had already reached Bai Zihan.","His eyes were filled with killing intent.","\"Hehe... Let’s see how arrogant you can remain now.\"","A voice suddenly echoed within Bai Zihan’s mind.","\"Do you need my help?\"","It was Empress Feilian.","Bai Zihan shook his head.","\"No!\"","His gaze remained fixed on the man before him.","\"I want to try fighting him myself.\"","That answer was only half the truth.","Bai Zihan genuinely wanted to see just how powerful the man who is Gu Master was.","But more importantly, he didn’t want Feilian to exhaust herself and fall unconscious again because of him.","He couldn’t afford to let that happen a second time.","Bai Zihan took a slow breath.","\"Heaven’s Mandate Reversal!\"","Boom!","A terrifying aura suddenly erupted from his body.","His cultivation, which had originally been at the Late Great Ascension Realm, surged violently.","Late Great Ascension.","Peak Great Ascension.","Immortal Ascension!","In an instant, Bai Zihan’s cultivation had risen all the way to the Peak Immortal Ascension Realm.","The man’s expression froze.","For a moment, shock appeared in his eyes. But it quickly disappeared.","\"A little trick!\"","He sneered.","\"Do you really think that raising your cultivation to the Immortal Ascension Realm will allow you to fight me?\"","Boom!","The man’s figure flashed.","His palm struck toward Bai Zihan with terrifying force.","Yet—","Bang!","Bai Zihan raised his hand and blocked the attack with astonishing ease.","The man’s expression changed.","\"What?!\"","He immediately increased his strength yet Bai Zihan remained completely unmoved.","\"NO WAY!\"","The man’s eyes widened.","It was a genuine surprise.","Whether Great Ascension Realm or Immortal Ascension Realm, to him, it made a very little difference yet Bai Zihan whose cultivation was only at Immortal Ascension managed to stop his attack.","Bai Zihan looked at him calmly.","\"Hmph! Only this much?\"","A faint trace of disappointment appeared in his eyes.","\"Looks like Gu Masters aren’t much stronger than ordinary cultivators after all.\"","Bai Zihan’s thoughts quickly turned.","After exchanging blows with him, Bai Zihan had already reached a rough conclusion.","Without those corpse beings, this Gu Master was actually weaker than an ordinary Golden Immortal.","At least compared to Bai Ren, the difference was obvious.","Of course, once he controlled those Golden Immortal corpses, his combat strength increased dramatically.","But without them—","He was merely an average Golden Immortal, or perhaps even slightly weaker.","And that was enough for Bai Zihan to understand something important.","Gu Masters themselves weren’t necessarily terrifying.","Their true strength came from the corpses and other methods they controlled.","They, themselves, were weaker than other cultivators!"]},{"number":695,"title":"Chapter 695: The Gu Master’s Deadly Poison","paragraphs":["The Gu Master stared at Bai Zihan in disbelief.","\"How did you know?\"","His voice was filled with genuine shock.","Even the ancient monsters of the Central Glorious Continent would have difficulty recognizing their techniques.","After all, Gu Masters had always been extremely secretive, and it had been many years since they had made a big move.","They rarely revealed their identities and concealed their techniques even more carefully.","Yet in a place like the Eastern Continent, someone had actually recognized his methods at a glance.","The Gu Master’s eyes gradually became filled with caution.","He had to capture Bai Zihan.","As long as he captured him alive, he could force him to reveal how he had recognized the technique.","Otherwise, he would never be able to understand how someone like Bai Zihan had seen through him.","However, before he could make another move, Bai Zihan suddenly began speaking.","\"Gu Masters really are as pathetic as I imagined. You hide behind corpses because you don’t have the courage to fight anyone yourself.\"","\"You don’t cultivate your own strength. You hide behind dead bodies and let them fight for you.\"","He glanced at the two Golden Immortal corpses battling Bai Ren and the three Earth Immortals.","\"Bullying the weak. Attacking in groups. Using corpses to compensate for your own pathetic self.\"","Bai Zihan chuckled.","\"Is that all you people know how to do?\"","The Gu Master’s face twitched violently.","Bai Zihan didn’t stop.","\"If you like corpses so much, why don’t you become one yourself? At least then, you’ll finally be useful.\"","\"Perhaps someone might even be willing to refine your corpse.\"","The Gu Master’s expression became hideous.","Bai Zihan looked him up and down.","\"Although your corpse probably wouldn’t be worth much. Your cultivation isn’t impressive, your strength isn’t impressive, and your techniques are nothing special.\"","\"Even after becoming a corpse, you’d probably still be useless. How pathetic!\"","Every word was an insult.","Every sentence struck directly at his pride.","The Gu Master’s face twitched violently.","His fists clenched so tightly that his knuckles cracked.","\"Y-YOU!\"","His entire body trembled with rage.","He had never imagined that someone could insult him so thoroughly.","If anger could kill, Bai Zihan would have already died countless times.","Those insults had all come from Empress Feilian.","Bai Zihan had merely repeated them.","Bai Zihan couldn’t help feeling impressed.","He had never imagined that the elegant and dignified Immortal Emperor who had once ruled over countless cultivators could actually hurl insults like this.","He silently gave her a thumbs-up.","With age truly came wisdom.","Her way of insulting people was simply too good.","Compared to her, he still had a long way to go.","Meanwhile, the Gu Master’s face had already turned completely red.","He had originally intended to capture Bai Zihan alive.","Now, that thought has completely disappeared.","There was only one thought left in his mind.","Kill him!","\"I’ll kill you!\"","Boom!","His Golden Immortal aura erupted once again.","His killing intent surged like a storm.","The Gu Master charged toward Bai Zihan with terrifying momentum.","This time, he no longer cared about capturing Bai Zihan alive.","He was determined to tear this arrogant brat apart!","The Gu Master charged forward.","Bai Zihan’s eyes narrowed. He took out his sword.","Clang!","A dazzling sword light flashed through the chamber.","Slash!","The Gu Master narrowly dodged the first strike, but another sword slash immediately followed.","And then another.","The sword lights tore through the air one after another, forcing the Gu Master to retreat.","His expression gradually became more serious.","At first, he had believed that killing Bai Zihan would be easy.","After all, Bai Zihan’s cultivation was only at the Peak Immortal Ascension Realm.","But after exchanging several blows, he realized that he had been completely wrong.","Bai Zihan was far more difficult to deal with than he had expected.","In fact, Bai Zihan’s current combat strength was even greater than that of an ordinary Earth Immortal.","For a Golden Immortal like him, killing an Earth Immortal should not have been difficult.","Yet Bai Zihan was clearly not an ordinary Earth Immortal-level opponent despite his Immortal Ascension cultivation.","And that sword...","The Gu Master’s expression became increasingly ugly.","Every time Bai Zihan’s sword struck him, it left behind a terrifying wound.","The sword itself seemed extraordinarily sharp.","Even his Golden Immortal body was unable to completely withstand its edge.","The more they fought, the more shocked the Gu Master became.","Bai Zihan’s strength was completely beyond his expectations.","\"Before I kill you...\"","Bai Zihan suddenly spoke while swinging his sword.","\"How about you tell me something about your so-called Lord?\"","The Gu Master’s expression darkened.","\"Arrogant!\"","Boom!","His Golden Immortal aura erupted once again as he attacked Bai Zihan.","Bai Zihan’s expression remained calm.","\"Since you don’t want to talk...\"","His sword suddenly changed direction.","\"Then I’ll beat the answer out of you.\"","\"Nine Shadows Flowing Light Sword!\"","Whoosh!","The sword light suddenly divided.","Nine figures appeared around the Gu Master.","Each figure held a sword.","The nine figures simultaneously attacked.","Slash! Slash! Slash!","Sword lights erupted from every direction.","The Gu Master desperately defended himself, but the attacks came too quickly.","Slash!","A sword struck his shoulder.","Bang!","Another slammed into his chest.","Bang!","A third struck his back.","The nine shadows surrounded him completely, unleashing a relentless barrage of attacks.","The Gu Master was beaten from one side to another.","His previously arrogant appearance disappeared completely.","Blood sprayed from his mouth.","His body was covered in wounds.","Finally—","Boom!","A powerful sword strike sent him crashing into the ground.","Bai Zihan stood calmly before him.","His sword remained pointed toward the Gu Master.","\"Feels like talking now?\"","The Gu Master slowly rose from the ground.","Blood stained the corner of his mouth.","His expression was no longer arrogant. Instead, there was a trace of solemnity.","\"Bai Zihan...\"","He wiped away the blood.","\"You’ve earned this.\"","His eyes became cold.","\"The Lord ordered me never to use this unless absolutely necessary. But since you’ve already recognized our techniques...\"","A sinister smile appeared on his face.","\"I won’t be holding back anymore!\"","The moment his voice fell—","Boom!","A strange aura suddenly erupted from his body.","Dark-green mist began spreading outward.","The moment the poisonous mist touched the ground—","Hiss!","The ground immediately began corroding.","Even the surrounding rocks couldn’t withstand it.","They rapidly melted away, releasing a pungent and terrifying smell.","Bai Zihan’s expression became solemn.","The poison was extremely dangerous.","Even the slightest contact could cause the body to rapidly corrode.","Bai Zihan immediately turned his head.","\"Bai Ren! Take Xueqing and Senior Qinglan and get out of here!\"","Bai Ren’s expression changed.","\"But what about you?\"","Bai Zihan’s gaze remained fixed on the Gu Master.","\"Hmph! I can’t let him escape.\"","Bai Ren hesitated for a moment.","Then he gritted his teeth.","\"Let’s go!\"","The three Earth Immortals immediately moved toward Bai Xueqing and Qinglan.","At the same time, the two Golden Immortal corpses continued fighting.","The Gu Master didn’t order them to stop.","He couldn’t afford to.","Bai Xueqing was still the person the Lord wanted.","If she died here, he would have to face severe punishment worse than death.","Moreover, he still intended to capture Bai Zihan alive.","To accomplish that, he needed the two refined corpses to keep Bai Ren and the others occupied.","\"Keke...\"","The Gu Master looked at Bai Zihan through the poisonous mist.","\"You really are confident. But...\"","His smile became increasingly sinister.","\"Do you really think my poison is something you can withstand?\"","The Gu Master had no intention of killing Bai Zihan.","At least, not yet.","He wanted Bai Zihan alive. But before that, he wanted him to suffer.","He wanted to see this arrogant expression disappear.","He wanted to hear Bai Zihan scream in pain and beg for mercy. Only then would he feel satisfied.","As for Bai Xueqing...","He would capture her eventually.","But right now, Bai Zihan was his priority.","Meanwhile, Bai Ren and the three Earth Immortals had already reached Bai Xueqing and Qinglan.","The moment they broke their restraints, Bai Xueqing’s eyes brightened.","\"Grand Elder!\"","\"Xueqing’er!\"","Bai Ren immediately helped Qinglan up.","\"Let’s leave!\"","They didn’t waste any time.","With the situation changing rapidly, remaining here was too dangerous for someone like Qinglan and Bai Xueqing.","Even Bai Ren felt a bit of threat from the poison.","He didn’t know what Bai Zihan had up his sleeve to be confident to stay behind. Anyways, he decided to trust him once again.","Bai Xueqing also looked at Bai Zihan with complex emotion but knew that there was nothing she could do to help.","If anything happens to him, then she would feel guilty for the rest of her life. Though seeing his arrogant self, she felt that she shouldn’t worry too much.","The three Earth Immortals immediately surrounded Bai Xueqing and Qinglan, protecting them as they retreated.","Soon, Bai Ren and the others disappeared from the chamber.","The Gu Master didn’t care.","His attention was entirely focused on Bai Zihan.","\"Keke...\"","He smiled sinisterly.","\"Now it’s just you and me.\""]},{"number":696,"title":"Chapter 696: Two Golden Immortal Corpses","paragraphs":["The poisonous mist continued spreading.","It completely surrounded Bai Zihan.","The Gu Master stared at him expectantly.","He imagined Bai Zihan collapsing to the ground.","He imagined him clutching his body and screaming in agony.","He imagined that arrogant face finally becoming terrified.","But—","Nothing happened.","Several breaths passed.","Then several more.","Bai Zihan remained standing.","His expression hadn’t changed in the slightest.","He simply looked at the Gu Master.","Like he was looking at a clown performing some ridiculous trick.","The Gu Master’s smile slowly disappeared.","\"...\"","His eyes widened.","\"H-How?\"","The poison had already reached Bai Zihan’s body.","Yet there wasn’t even the slightest reaction.","No screaming.","No struggle.","Not even a change in expression.","Bai Zihan glanced down at the poisonous mist surrounding his body.","Then he looked back at the Gu Master.","\"Is that all?\"","The Gu Master’s face became pale.","\"Impossible!\"","He couldn’t believe what he was seeing.","This was his strongest poison.","Even a powerful Golden Immortal Realm cultivator should not have been able to withstand it so easily.","Yet Bai Zihan was completely unaffected.","How could this be?","What the Gu Master didn’t know was that Bai Zihan’s body had already undergone countless refinements.","Bai Zihan now possessed the Primordial Chaos Body.","His physical body had been tempered repeatedly under extreme conditions.","This poison was certainly powerful.","But it was nowhere near powerful enough to destroy his body.","The poisonous Qi entered his body.","Instead of corroding him, Bai Zihan’s Primordial Chaos Body began refining it.","Bai Zihan could feel the Qi circulating through his body but rather than destroying his body, they were being absorbed like any other Qi.","\"This poison isn’t bad. But it’s still not enough.\"","The Gu Master’s expression became increasingly distorted.","\"Impossible! How can you still stand?!\"","His voice was filled with disbelief.","\"This is my strongest poison! Even a Golden Immortal Realm cultivator shouldn’t be able to withstand it!\"","Bai Zihan looked at the Gu Master calmly.","\"Just because others can’t withstand it doesn’t mean I can’t.\"","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"Looks like this is all you’ve got.\"","The Gu Master’s expression became even more distorted.","Anger and disbelief flashed through his eyes.","\"Kid!\"","His voice trembled with fury.","\"Just because my poison can’t affect you, don’t think that means you can handle me!\"","His gaze suddenly shifted toward the two Golden Immortal corpses.","\"My two refined corpses are more than enough to kill you!\"","The moment his voice fell—","Boom!","The two dormant corpses suddenly erupted with terrifying Qi.","Their lifeless bodies trembled.","A terrifying pressure instantly filled the chamber.","The Gu Master pointed toward Bai Zihan.","\"Kill him!\"","Whoosh!","The two Golden Immortal corpses moved simultaneously.","Their figures transformed into two streaks of light as they charged toward Bai Zihan at full speed.","Bai Zihan’s expression became solemn.","He immediately raised his sword.","Clang!","A massive fist collided with his sword.","The terrifying impact forced Bai Zihan backward several steps.","Before he could stabilize himself, the second corpse had already appeared behind him.","Boom!","A palm struck toward his back.","Bai Zihan quickly turned around and blocked the attack with his sword.","The impact shook his entire body.","Fighting one Golden Immortal was already difficult.","Fighting two simultaneously was an entirely different matter.","Moreover, both their physical strength was much higher than the Gu Master.","And these corpses had no fear of death.","They didn’t care about injuries.","They didn’t care about defense.","They simply attacked relentlessly.","Whenever Bai Zihan wounded one of them, the other immediately took advantage of the opening.","Whenever he attempted to distance himself, they pursued him without hesitation.","Boom! Boom! Bang!","The chamber shook violently as the three figures clashed.","Bai Zihan’s sword repeatedly struck the corpses.","However, the two Golden Immortal corpses continued fighting as though they couldn’t feel pain.","One punched toward his chest.","Bai Zihan twisted his body and narrowly avoided it.","The second corpse immediately attacked from the side.","Bai Zihan raised his sword.","Clang!","The terrifying impact sent him sliding backward.","His expression became increasingly solemn.","These corpses were truly troublesome.","They were not necessarily stronger than Bai Ren individually.","But their complete disregard for their own lives made them extremely difficult to deal with.","Moreover, there were two of them.","The Gu Master watched the battle from a distance.","His eyes gradually filled with excitement.","\"Hahaha! Bai Zihan!\"","His laughter echoed through the chamber.","\"Let’s see how long you can keep that arrogant expression!\"","The two corpses continued attacking relentlessly.","Bai Zihan was gradually forced onto the defensive.","The Gu Master’s smile became wider.","He could already see the outcome.","Soon!","Very soon!","Those two refined corpses would tear Bai Zihan apart.","\"Die!\"","One of the corpses roared as it launched another devastating attack.","Bai Zihan’s sword collided with its fist.","Boom!","The force sent him backward.","The second corpse immediately followed.","Bai Zihan’s expression changed.","\"Nine Shadows Flowing Light Sword!\"","Whoosh!","His sword light suddenly split apart.","The nine figures moved simultaneously, attacking the two refined corpses from different directions.","\"Kill!\"","One of the shadows slashed toward a Golden Immortal corpse.","Clang!","The corpse raised its arm and blocked the sword.","At the same time, another shadow attacked from behind.","However—","Whoosh!","The corpse’s figure suddenly disappeared.","Its speed was astonishing.","Bang!","A single punch shattered the shadow.","The sword light dispersed into nothingness.","Bai Zihan’s eyes narrowed.","\"So fast...\"","Before he could react, another refined corpse had already moved.","Bang!","Another shadow was destroyed.","Then another.","One after another, the nine shadows were torn apart.","The two refined corpses moved with terrifying speed, destroying each shadow almost immediately after it appeared.","The Gu Master also joined the attack.","Although he couldn’t easily contend with Bai Zihan’s true body, destroying the shadows was another matter entirely.","The shadows only possessed a portion of Bai Zihan’s true strength.","For a Golden Immortal-level Gu Master, destroying them wasn’t difficult.","Boom!","Another shadow was shattered by his palm.","\"Hahaha!\"","The Gu Master laughed excitedly.","\"Your tricks are useless. Let’s see how long you can continue!\"","Bai Zihan’s expression remained calm.","The Nine Shadows Flowing Light Sword had indeed failed to achieve the effect he wanted.","The two refined corpses were simply too fast.","And the Gu Master was more than capable of dealing with his weaker shadows.","Soon, the remaining shadows were destroyed one after another.","The final shadow exploded into sword light.","The battlefield returned to normal.","Bai Zihan’s true body was once again surrounded by the two refined corpses.","Boom!","One of them struck him directly in the chest.","Bai Zihan was sent flying.","Before he could stabilize himself, the second corpse appeared beside him.","Boom!","Another attack landed.","Bai Zihan’s body crashed heavily into the ground.","The Gu Master’s eyes lit up.","\"That’s it! Kill him!\"","The two refined corpses immediately pursued him.","Their attacks fell like a violent storm.","Boom! Boom!","Bai Zihan was repeatedly struck.","His body was forced backward again and again.","At first glance, the situation looked extremely dangerous.","He had been completely backed into a corner.","The two Golden Immortal corpses continuously bombarded him from both sides, leaving him almost no opportunity to counterattack.","Yet strangely, Bai Zihan didn’t seem to be seriously injured.","Even when a terrifying fist landed directly on his body, the damage was surprisingly light.","His clothes were torn.","A faint trace of blood appeared at the corner of his mouth.","But that was all.","His bones didn’t break.","His organs weren’t damaged.","His body didn’t collapse.","It was as though his physical body was indestructible.","The Gu Master’s smile slowly disappeared.","\"What...?\"","Another fist slammed into Bai Zihan’s chest.","Boom!","Bai Zihan was sent flying again.","He rolled across the ground before slowly getting back onto his feet.","He wiped the blood from the corner of his mouth.","His expression remained calm.","The Gu Master’s eyes widened.","Those two were Golden Immortal corpses. Their physical strength was terrifying.","Even ordinary Golden Immortals couldn’t simply endure their attacks with their bodies.","Yet Bai Zihan, a cultivator whose cultivation was only at the Peak Immortal Ascension Realm, was actually enduring their attacks with his physical body.","And although he was being pushed back continuously, his injuries remained extremely light.","The Gu Master’s expression gradually became solemn.","\"What kind of body does this guy have?\"","Although the situation looked unfavorable, Bai Zihan wasn’t panicking.","He raised his sword to block yet another attack.","Boom!","The impact caused his arms to tremble.","The Gu Master became increasingly excited.","No matter how much time it took, he would savor it slowly.","He would watch as Bai Zihan writhed on the ground and struggled to stay alive.","His eyes never left Bai Zihan.","He wanted to personally witness the moment Bai Zihan was killed.","But the next moment, a terrifying force suddenly struck him from behind.","The Gu Master’s expression changed drastically.","\"What?!\"","Before he could react, a powerful hand grabbed him.","Bai Ren’s figure appeared behind him.","\"You became too distracted.\"","The Gu Master’s pupils contracted.","He then realized what had happened.","The poison had already dispersed.","While he was completely focused on Bai Zihan, Bai Ren had silently returned.","His aura was completely concealed.","The Gu Master didn’t notice him.","He was too invested in the battle before him.","And Bai Ren had been waiting for this exact moment.","\"Damn—!\"","Before he could finish speaking, Bai Ren slammed him into the ground.","Bang!","The entire chamber trembled.","Bai Ren pinned him down with overwhelming strength.","The Gu Master’s face twisted with disbelief.","How could he have let down his guard at such a critical moment?"]},{"number":697,"title":"Chapter 697: The Gu Master’s Final Choice","paragraphs":["Bai Ren’s eyes were filled with fury as he pressed the Gu Master firmly against the ground.","The Gu Master struggled violently. However, Bai Ren’s strength was not something he could easily escape from.","\"Stop them!\"","Bai Ren’s voice thundered through the chamber.","The Gu Master’s expression changed.","Bai Ren tightened his grip.","\"I said stop your refined corpses!\"","His eyes were filled with cold killing intent.","\"Or do you want to find out what happens next?\"","The Gu Master’s face twisted.","He immediately understood what Bai Ren meant.","The two Golden Immortal corpses were still attacking Bai Zihan.","As long as the battle continued, Bai Ren couldn’t fully focus on restraining him.","If the corpses were ordered to stop, however, Bai Zihan would be free.","Then Bai Ren and Bai Zihan could deal with him together.","The Gu Master was naturally unwilling.","Those two refined corpses were his greatest weapons.","Without them, his strength would be greatly reduced.","However, his life was currently in Bai Ren’s hands.","He had little room to disobey.","The Gu Master’s expression became increasingly ugly.","\"Fine!\"","He gritted his teeth.","Then, with great reluctance, he gave the command.","\"Stop!\"","The moment his voice fell—","The two Golden Immortal corpses froze.","Their attacks stopped instantly.","Bai Zihan, who had been continuously fighting against them, also stepped back.","The chamber gradually became quiet.","The two refined corpses stood motionlessly nearby.","Bai Zihan slowly lowered his sword and looked toward the Gu Master.","From the beginning, Bai Zihan had indeed struggled.","The two Golden Immortal corpses had been extremely powerful.","Fighting them simultaneously was genuinely difficult, even for him.","However, Bai Zihan had never truly been pushed to the point of desperation.","He didn’t use Fate Severing or any of his other techniques, purposely making it seem as though he was being pushed back.","His purpose had been simple.","To keep the Gu Master’s attention completely focused on him.","Bai Zihan wanted the Gu Master to believe that victory was already within his grasp.","And judging by what had just happened, his plan had succeeded perfectly.","Of course, the struggle itself had not been entirely an act.","Facing two Golden Immortal corpses at the same time was genuinely difficult.","Even with his extraordinary strength and Primordial Chaos Body, Bai Zihan couldn’t defeat them easily.","The Gu Master had become too focused on watching Bai Zihan’s supposed defeat.","Too convinced that Bai Zihan was already trapped.","And because of that, he had completely failed to notice Bai Ren.","The Gu Master suddenly began struggling violently.","\"Let me go! Otherwise—\"","\"Otherwise what?\"","Bai Zihan interrupted him with a faint smile.","Bai Zihan slowly walked closer.","\"Are you going to beg your so-called Lord to come and save you? Heh!\"","A mocking expression appeared on his face.","The Gu Master’s eyes immediately filled with fury.","\"You—!\"","Bai Zihan ignored him.","His expression gradually became cold.","\"Just answer what I asked.\"","He looked directly into the Gu Master’s eyes.","\"Tell me about your Lord. Who is he? And where is he?\"","For a moment, the Gu Master remained silent.","Then—","\"Hahaha...\"","He suddenly burst into hysterical laughter.","The sound echoed through the chamber.","\"You want me to betray the Lord?\"","His eyes were filled with madness.","\"You must be dreaming!\"","Bai Zihan frowned slightly.","\"So, you refuse to talk?\"","The Gu Master sneered.","\"Even if you kill me, I won’t tell you anything!\"","Bai Zihan glanced toward Bai Ren.","Bai Ren immediately understood.","Without hesitation, he raised his hand and pressed it against the Gu Master’s body.","The Gu Master’s expression changed.","\"What are you—\"","Boom!","Bai Ren’s spiritual Qi surged into his body.","It directly struck several of his meridians.","\"AHHHHH!\"","The Gu Master’s body trembled violently.","His face immediately turned pale.","Cold sweat covered his forehead. Bai Ren’s expression remained indifferent.","\"Talk!\"","The Gu Master gritted his teeth.","His entire body trembled from the pain.","Yet even then, he refused to speak.","Bai Ren increased the pressure.","Crack!","The sound of damaged meridians echoed from within the Gu Master’s body.","The pain was enough to make an ordinary cultivator beg for death.","However, the Gu Master’s eyes only became increasingly bloodshot.","\"Hahaha...\"","He laughed weakly.","Bai Zihan’s expression gradually became cold.","\"You’re still refusing?\"","The Gu Master lifted his head.","His gaze was filled with hatred.","\"You think this is over?\"","His voice became increasingly sinister.","\"Our time will come.\"","He stared directly at Bai Zihan.","\"And when that time comes... the Lord will avenge me.\"","A strange smile appeared on his face.","\"You will all die!\"","Bai Ren frowned.","However, the Gu Master continued laughing.","\"Perhaps by now...\"","His smile became increasingly twisted.","\"The Bai Clan at the Shen Clan has already been destroyed.\"","Bai Zihan’s expression changed slightly.","\"Hahaha!\"","The Gu Master’s laughter became increasingly wild.","\"You people were so focused on rescuing Bai Xueqing that you forgot about the Shen Clan. My senior brothers are there. Your measly Bai Clan can’t defeat them!\"","\"HAHAHAHA!\"","His laughter suddenly stopped.","The Gu Master’s body stiffened.","His eyes widened.","Then—","Blood flowed from the corner of his mouth.","Bai Ren’s expression immediately changed.","\"What’s happening?\"","The Gu Master’s body trembled violently.","His breathing became weaker and weaker.","Within moments, the life in his eyes began to fade.","Bai Ren immediately checked his condition.","His expression darkened.","\"Poison!\"","Bai Zihan’s eyes narrowed.","The poison had already spread throughout the Gu Master’s body.","It was too late.","Bai Ren quickly examined his mouth.","Then he discovered something unusual.","Hidden beneath one of the Gu Master’s teeth was a tiny, concealed capsule.","The Gu Master had hidden poison inside it from the beginning.","When he realized there was no escape, he had bitten down without hesitation.","He had chosen death rather than reveal anything about his Lord.","Bai Ren slowly withdrew his hand.","His expression was solemn.","\"So ruthless...\"","Bai Zihan looked silently at the Gu Master’s corpse.","The man had endured severe pain.","He had faced death without hesitation.","And in the end, he had chosen to kill himself rather than betray his master.","That alone revealed something important.","The so-called Lord possessed an extraordinary degree of control over his followers.","Or perhaps the Gu Master was simply fanatically loyal to him.","Bai Zihan looked toward the lifeless Gu Master.","Bai Zihan raised his hand.","A spiritual flame condensed above his palm.","Bai Ren’s expression changed slightly.","\"What are you doing?\"","Bai Zihan looked calmly at the Gu Master’s body.","\"Making sure he’s actually dead.\"","The next moment—","Whoosh!","The spiritual flame shot forward.","It headed directly toward the Gu Master’s body.","However, the instant the flame touched the body, the corpse suddenly moved.","Boom!","The Gu Master’s eyes snapped open.","His body shot backward.","His previous deathly appearance disappeared completely.","Blood was still visible at the corner of his mouth, but the Gu Master was undeniably alive.","Bai Ren froze.","\"...\"","He stared at the Gu Master.","Then at Bai Zihan.","Then back at the Gu Master.","\"You were pretending?\"","The Gu Master’s expression was extremely ugly.","His eyes were fixed firmly on Bai Zihan.","Bai Zihan merely smirked.","\"Heh.\"","Bai Ren looked toward him in disbelief.","\"Bai Zihan... how did you know?\"","Bai Ren had personally checked the Gu Master’s condition.","His breathing had disappeared.","His heart had stopped beating.","Even his life force had seemingly vanished.","Bai Ren had been unable to find the slightest flaw.","If Bai Zihan hadn’t suddenly tried to burn the body, he would have genuinely believed that the Gu Master was dead.","Bai Zihan shrugged.","\"I didn’t know for sure.\"","Bai Ren blinked.","\"You... didn’t know?\"","Bai Zihan looked toward the Gu Master.","\"I was simply being careful.\"","His eyes narrowed slightly.","\"A coward like him values his life more than anything.\"","The Gu Master’s face twitched.","Bai Zihan continued without hesitation.","\"Yet suddenly, he was willing to sacrifice himself for someone else?\"","He shook his head.","\"That’s already suspicious enough.\"","Bai Ren remained silent.","Bai Zihan pointed toward the Gu Master.","\"And even if he really had died, unless I saw his body burned to ashes, how could I guarantee that he wouldn’t suddenly come back to life?\"","Silence!","Bai Ren stared at him.","Then he slowly raised his thumb.","\"...That actually makes sense.\"","If they had simply believed the Gu Master was dead and left his body behind, they might have been completely fooled.","The Gu Master could have waited until they were gone before escaping.","Or perhaps he could have launched a surprise attack when they least expected it.","Bai Ren’s gaze toward Bai Zihan became increasingly strange.","The Gu Master himself was equally stunned.","He had carefully prepared this method.","The poison he had taken wasn’t meant to kill him but to place him in a state where he appeared to be dead.","Even Bai Ren, a Golden Immortal, had failed to discover anything unusual.","Yet Bai Zihan’s reasoning for exposing him was simply—","Unless I see you turned into ashes, how do I know you’re really dead?","The Gu Master’s face twitched violently.","What kind of logic was that?","Who even did that?","\"You...\"","Before he could say anything else, Bai Zihan calmly turned toward Bai Ren.","\"Elder, torture him until he’s willing to talk.\"","Bai Ren immediately understood.","A cold smile appeared on his face. The Gu Master’s expression changed instantly.","\"Wait!\"","He immediately raised his hands.","\"I’ll talk! I’ll talk!\"","However, Bai Ren’s fist was already flying toward him.","Bang!","The Gu Master was sent crashing into the wall.","\"ARGH!\"","Before he could recover—","Bang!","Bai Ren appeared in front of him and kicked him directly in the stomach.","The Gu Master’s body folded.","He crashed to the ground.","\"I said I’ll talk!\"","Bang!","Another punch landed on his face.","The Gu Master’s eyes widened.","\"Wait! Wait! I—\"","Bang!","Another strike landed.","This time, Bai Ren grabbed him by the collar and lifted him into the air.","The Gu Master’s face turned pale.","Bai Ren smiled coldly.","\"You dared to fake your death and fool this old man?\"","His grip tightened.","\"Do you really think I’ll let you off that easily?\"","\"ARGHHH!\"","The Gu Master’s miserable screams echoed throughout the chamber.","Bai Zihan stood nearby with his arms crossed.","He watched calmly.","The man had been given a chance to speak.","He had refused.","He had then chosen to deceive them.","Now that his trick had been exposed, there was no reason to make things easy for him.","Who knew whether he would tell them the truth or not?","Therefore, before anything else, he needed to understand one thing.","The consequence of deceiving them!"]},{"number":698,"title":"Chapter 698: Bai Clan Vs Shen Clan!","paragraphs":["Back at the Shen Clan!","Bai Tianheng had been speaking nonsense for several minutes—or at least, that was how Shen Wuheng saw it.","One moment, Bai Tianheng demanded a larger amount of compensation.","Next, he questioned the Shen Clan’s sincerity.","Then, just as Shen Wuheng thought they were finally getting somewhere, Bai Tianheng would suddenly raise another unreasonable demand.","Nothing seemed to satisfy him.","Rather than the Shen Clan holding a hostage, it was as if they were the ones negotiating for something.","Shen Wuheng’s expression became increasingly ugly.","His patience had already reached its limit.","Finally—","\"Enough!\"","His voice echoed through the hall.","Bai Tianheng looked at him calmly.","Shen Wuheng’s face darkened.","\"Bai Tianheng, I don’t think you care about your daughter at all.\"","His eyes narrowed.","\"You’re simply using this opportunity to deliberately make things difficult for my Shen Clan!\"","Bai Tianheng smiled.","\"You got half of that right.\"","Shen Wuheng frowned.","Bai Tianheng leisurely leaned back.","\"I do want to make things difficult for you.\"","Shen Wuheng’s expression froze.","What did he mean by that?","Before he could understand, Bai Tianheng’s smile gradually disappeared.","The Bai Clan had already received the message.","Bai Xueqing had been rescued.","There was no longer any reason to continue wasting time.","No longer any reason to play along with the Shen Clan.","Bai Tianheng slowly stood up.","The expression on his face became cold.","\"Enough talking.\"","Shen Wuheng’s pupils contracted.","Bai Tianheng looked around the hall.","Then—","\"Kill them!\"","The moment those two words fell—","Boom!","Terrifying auras erupted throughout the Shen Clan.","The Bai Clan experts, who had remained calm until now, instantly moved.","Their killing intent swept through the entire area.","Shen Wuheng’s expression changed drastically.","\"What?!\"","He had never expected the Bai Clan to suddenly attack.","They hadn’t even secured Bai Xueqing’s safety yet!","Was Bai Tianheng insane?","\"W-Wait!\"","Shen Wuheng immediately shouted.","\"What are you doing?!\"","Bai Tianheng looked at him coldly.","\"Are you blind?\"","Shen Wuheng’s face turned ugly.","\"Bai Tianheng! Aren’t you afraid of what might happen to your daughter?\"","Bai Tianheng scoffed.","\"My daughter?\"","A mocking smile appeared on his face.","\"You still think Xueqing is in your hands?\"","Shen Wuheng’s expression froze.","Bai Tianheng’s eyes were filled with disdain.","\"Do you really think we didn’t know that my daughter wasn’t here?\"","Shen Wuheng’s pupils contracted.","Bai Tianheng continued.","\"We already sent people to rescue her. And now...\"","A cold killing intent flashed through his eyes.","\"You’ll pay!\"","Shen Wuheng’s expression changed repeatedly.","\"Impossible!\"","Although he didn’t know how the Bai Clan had discovered that Bai Xueqing wasn’t in the Shen Clan, Shen Wuheng still found the situation difficult to believe.","Rescuing Bai Xueqing was impossible.","The place where she was being held was extremely well hidden.","More importantly, the person guarding her was far more powerful than anyone here could imagine.","Even if the Bai Clan had somehow discovered the location, how could they possibly rescue her?","There was simply no way!","Shen Wuheng clenched his fists.","\"You think I would believe such nonsense?\"","Bai Tianheng merely smiled.","\"Whether you believe it or not is no longer important.\"","His expression turned cold.","\"Because you’re going to die anyway.\"","Boom!","The Bai Clan experts immediately launched their attacks.","Shen Wuheng’s face turned pale.","He finally understood.","Bai Tianheng had never intended to negotiate with him.","From the very beginning, all those unreasonable demands and endless arguments had merely been a way to stall for time.","He had been playing with him.","And Shen Wuheng had fallen for it completely.","However, there was someone else who found the news even more unbelievable than Shen Wuheng.","The senior brother of the Gu Master whom Bai Zihan had captured.","\"Impossible...\"","Not only was his junior brother a Golden Immortal, but he also had two refined corpses at the Golden Immortal Realm.","With that kind of strength, how could a backwater clan like the Bai Clan possibly defeat him?","Not to mention, most of the Bai Clan’s forces were here.","Unless...","A terrifying possibility suddenly appeared in his mind.","\"No...\"","The Gu Master’s expression gradually changed.","Could the Bai Clan really possess strength beyond what they had estimated?","It no longer mattered what the Gu Master’s senior brother thought, nor did it matter whether Shen Wuheng believed Bai Tianheng’s words.","The Bai Clan had already made their move.","And once they moved, there was no turning back.","Boom!","A deafening roar suddenly echoed through the sky.","The massive flying ship hovering above the Shen Clan began to move.","Countless cultivators within the Shen Clan raised their heads.","Their expressions changed drastically.","The spiritual cannons on the flying ship began gathering terrifying amounts of energy.","One after another, blinding lights appeared.","Shen Wuheng’s pupils contracted.","\"Not good!\"","Before he could give another command—","Boom!","The first attack descended.","A massive beam of Qi crashed directly into the Shen Clan’s protective formation.","The entire formation trembled violently.","Cracks immediately spread across the barrier.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","The attacks didn’t stop.","One blast after another descended from the Bai Clan’s flying ship.","Each strike carried terrifying destructive power.","The Shen Clan’s protective formation flickered violently.","The cultivators maintaining the formation immediately turned pale.","\"Hold it!\"","\"Don’t let the formation collapse!\"","Several Shen Clan elders shouted desperately.","However, everyone could see the truth.","The formation wouldn’t last long.","At most, a few minutes.","Shen Wuheng stood within the main hall, his expression becoming increasingly ugly.","His fists slowly clenched.","There was no longer any need to negotiate.","The Bai Clan had made their intentions perfectly clear.","They weren’t here to bargain from the beginning.","Their only objective was to destroy the Shen Clan.","\"Damn it...\"","Shen Wuheng gritted his teeth.","Shen Wuheng suddenly remembered something.","His expression changed slightly as he quickly turned toward the man standing nearby.","\"Sir!\"","The Gu Master’s senior brother slowly opened his eyes.","Shen Wuheng immediately bowed.","\"What should we do?\"","Now that the Bai Clan had bared its fangs, the Shen Clan could only rely on their powerful backers.","After all, the Shen Clan had dared to provoke the Bai Clan in the first place because of them.","Without their support, Shen Wuheng would never have been foolish enough to openly make an enemy of such a powerful force.","The Gu Master merely snorted.","\"Hmph!\"","His expression remained calm.","\"Why are you panicking?\"","Shen Wuheng was slightly stunned.","Outside, the attacks continued.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","The entire Shen Clan shook violently.","The protective formation was already covered in cracks.","At any moment, it could collapse completely.","Of course, Shen Wuheng was worried.","The Gu Master slowly stood up.","A cold smile appeared on his face.","\"No need to worry.\"","His gaze shifted toward the Bai Clan’s flying ship hovering above them.","\"Let them enter.\"","Shen Wuheng frowned.","The man continued.","\"Once they enter the Shen Clan...\"","A cold killing intent flashed through his eyes.","\"We’ll kill them all.\"","Shen Wuheng’s eyes widened slightly.","A look of relief gradually appeared on his face.","The Shen Clan had been completely prepared for a war with the Bai Clan.","From the very beginning, they had expected that things might eventually reach this point.","After all, once they got their hands on Jin Yuelin, they had never intended to return Bai Xueqing.","The only difference was that they had originally hoped to use Bai Xueqing to keep the Bai Clan under control and restrict their movements somewhat.","Unfortunately, their plan has failed and the Bai Clan is coming at them with their full force.","However, that didn’t mean everything was over.","Shen Wuheng’s eyes gradually became cold.","\"So what if they rescued her?\"","They had only sent a portion of their forces to rescue Bai Xueqing.","Once the Bai Clan’s main force here was destroyed, those few people would be left alone.","By then, capturing Bai Xueqing again would be easy.","The Gu Master’s expression was filled with confidence.","As for what had happened to his junior brother, he wasn’t entirely sure.","Perhaps his junior brother had failed in his mission.","Or perhaps, a darker possibility crossed his mind.","Perhaps the Bai Clan had actually managed to kill him.","However, the Gu Master quickly dismissed the thought.","Either way, it didn’t matter much.","If his junior brother had truly failed, then he would simply clean up the mess himself.","That was all!","His gaze slowly moved across the battlefield.","Then it stopped on Bai Chu.","The Gu Master’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Among the Bai Clan’s forces, Bai Chu was the only one who truly caught his attention.","A Golden Immortal!","A faint smile appeared on the Gu Master’s face.","\"If I can refine him...\"","His eyes gradually became filled with greed.","Then his strength would increase once again.","The number of Golden Immortal corpses under his control would also increase.","That alone was enough to make this battle worthwhile.","As for the others, the Gu Master swept his gaze across the remaining Bai Clan experts.","The Earth Immortals.","The Immortal Ascension Realm cultivators.","They were useful as well, but none of them were particularly valuable in his eyes.","Other than Immortal Realm, he wasn’t much interested in other realms.","Of course, that didn’t mean their corpses would be useless.","Their corpses could be given to his disciples.","They would make excellent refined corpses for those with weaker cultivation.","A sinister smile appeared on the Gu Master’s face.","\"Let there be chaos!\""]},{"number":699,"title":"Chapter 699: The Moment of Chaos","paragraphs":["Boom! Boom! Boom!","The bombardment continued without pause.","Each attack from the Bai Clan’s flying ship caused the Shen Clan’s protective formation to tremble violently.","The cracks covering the barrier continued to spread.","The Shen Clan cultivators responsible for maintaining the formation were already struggling.","\"Hold it!\"","\"Pour more Qi into the formation!\"","\"Don’t let it break!\"","Their desperate voices echoed throughout the Shen Clan.","However, the situation had already reached its limit.","The Bai Clan’s flying ship was simply too powerful, and its attacks were relentless.","Boom!","Another terrifying blast descended.","This time—","Crack!","A sharp sound echoed through the sky.","Everyone looked up.","A massive crack had appeared across the Shen Clan’s protective barrier.","The expressions of countless Shen Clan members immediately turned pale.","Before anyone could react—","Boom!","Another attack struck.","Crack! Crack! Crack!","The massive crack instantly spread throughout the entire formation.","Like a shattered mirror, countless fractures covered the barrier.","BOOM!!!","The Shen Clan’s protective formation finally collapsed.","A terrifying explosion swept through the area.","The enormous barrier shattered into countless fragments of spiritual light.","The cultivators maintaining the formation were thrown backward.","Several of them coughed up blood.","Others were directly knocked unconscious.","The entire Shen Clan was exposed.","Above them, the Bai Clan’s flying ship continued hovering in the sky.","Its massive shadow covered the battlefield.","Inside the ship, Bai Tianheng looked down at the Shen Clan.","His expression was completely cold.","\"Attack!\"","The moment his voice fell, the Bai Clan moved.","Whoosh! Slash! Slash!","The moment the Bai Clan entered the Shen Clan, the slaughter began.","A Bai Clan expert crashed through a group of Shen Clan cultivators.","Several figures were sent flying.","Blood filled the air.","The Shen Clan immediately tried to resist.","However, the moment the two sides truly clashed, the difference between them became painfully obvious.","The Shen Clan stood no chance at all.","The Bai Clan’s cultivators possessed superior cultivation techniques.","Their martial arts were stronger.","Their artifacts were better.","Even their overall cultivation was higher.","Against such an overwhelming advantage, how could the Shen Clan possibly compete?","Boom!","A Shen Clan elder unleashed his full strength.","A powerful technique shot toward his opponent.","However, the Bai Clan elder merely raised his weapon.","Clang!","The attack was easily blocked.","Before the Shen Clan elder could react—","Slash!","A sharp light flashed. His body was sent flying backward.","\"AHHH!\"","His miserable scream echoed through the battlefield.","Elsewhere, the situation was no different.","The Bai Clan cultivators charged through the Shen Clan’s defenses like wolves entering a flock of sheep.","One after another, Shen Clan cultivators fell.","\"Stop them!\"","\"Don’t let them advance!\"","\"Reinforcements!\"","The Shen Clan elders shouted desperately.","However, their voices were quickly drowned out by the sounds of battle.","Boom!","Another Shen Clan expert was blasted into the ground.","Crack!","The ground beneath him shattered.","Before he could even stand, a Bai Clan cultivator descended from above.","Boom!","The attack landed. The Shen Clan expert’s body went completely still.","Fear gradually spread throughout the Shen Clan.","They had expected a difficult battle.","They had prepared themselves to face the Bai Clan.","But they had never expected the difference in strength to be this great.","The Shen Clan was being completely massacred.","Shen Wuheng stood in the distance, his face becoming increasingly pale.","\"How...\"","He clenched his fists tightly.","\"How can this be happening?\"","The Bai Clan was simply too strong.","Their cultivators were crushing the Shen Clan in nearly every confrontation.","And the most terrifying part was that the Bai Clan had barely suffered any casualties.","Meanwhile, the Shen Clan was losing people every moment.","If this continued, the Shen Clan would truly be destroyed.","Shen Wuheng’s heart trembled.","His gaze immediately turned toward the Gu Master.","Until now, the Gu Master had not made a single move.","He merely stood there, watching.","Observing the battlefield with a strange expression.","As though the deaths of the Shen Clan cultivators had nothing to do with him.","\"Sir!\"","Shen Wuheng hurriedly approached him.","His voice was filled with urgency.","\"Please help us!\"","The Gu Master slowly turned toward him.","Shen Wuheng clenched his fists.","\"If this continues, my Shen Clan will be destroyed!\"","The Gu Master remained silent.","His gaze shifted back toward the battlefield.","Another Shen Clan cultivator fell.","Then another.","Then another.","Blood gradually covered the ground.","A faint smile slowly appeared on the Gu Master’s face.","More deaths.","More corpses.","To him, that was not a bad thing.","It was precisely what he wanted.","Every dead cultivator was a potential refined corpse.","Although the Shen Clan cultivators were not particularly powerful, their bodies were still useful.","Some could be refined into puppets.","Others could be used as materials.","The more people who died, the more he gained.","As for the Shen Clan itself?","The Gu Master’s eyes became cold.","Their usefulness had already come to an end.","They had served their purpose.","They were no longer needed.","In fact, their corpses might be more useful to him than their continued existence.","Shen Wuheng stared at him.","His expression gradually changed.","The Gu Master’s silence made him feel increasingly uneasy.","\"Sir?\"","The Gu Master finally looked at him.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"Why are you so worried?\"","Shen Wuheng’s face twitched.","Why was he worried?","His clan was being slaughtered!","At this rate, there might not even be a Shen Clan left by the end of the battle.","However, Shen Wuheng suppressed his anger.","\"Sir, please!\"","His voice became increasingly urgent.","\"If you don’t act soon, the Shen Clan won’t be able to hold on!\"","Even after Shen Wuheng’s desperate plea, the Gu Master showed no intention of intervening.","Bang!","Another figure was sent crashing into the ground.","Blood splattered across the battlefield.","Shen Wuheng’s face became increasingly pale.","He clenched his fists tightly.","Finally, he gritted his teeth.","\"Sir...\"","The Gu Master did not respond.","Shen Wuheng’s expression changed.","Then he took a deep breath.","\"The Lord asked you to help us.\"","The moment those words fell, the Gu Master’s expression changed.","His head slowly turned.","A pair of cold eyes landed directly on Shen Wuheng.","The terrifying pressure in his gaze caused Shen Wuheng’s heart to tremble.","\"If you don’t...\"","Shen Wuheng swallowed the rest of his words.","However, the Gu Master had already understood what he was trying to say.","\"You dare threaten me?\"","His voice was cold.","Shen Wuheng’s face immediately changed.","\"I-I wouldn’t dare!\"","The Gu Master’s eyes narrowed.","\"Then what did you mean?\"","Shen Wuheng clenched his teeth.","His heart was filled with fear.","However, he had no other choice.","If he did not bring up the Lord, he feared that this man would simply continue standing here and watching as the Shen Clan was destroyed.","\"Sir, you’ve misunderstood.\"","Shen Wuheng quickly lowered his head.","\"I wasn’t threatening you. I was merely reminding you of the greater cause. The Lord personally arranged for you and your people to assist us.\"","\"If the Shen Clan is destroyed, wouldn’t that affect the Lord’s plans as well?\"","Silence!","The Gu Master’s gaze remained fixed on him.","Shen Wuheng’s back was already covered in cold sweat.","He had never expected that the person sent to assist them would be this indifferent toward the fate of the Shen Clan.","To the other party, it seemed that whether the Shen Clan survived or perished did not matter at all.","Suddenly—","Bang!","The Gu Master raised his hand. Shen Wuheng didn’t even have time to react.","A powerful force struck his chest.","\"UGH!\"","His body flew backward.","Boom!","Shen Wuheng crashed heavily into the wall.","The wall cracked from the impact.","He coughed violently and struggled to stand.","The Gu Master looked at him coldly.","\"Watch your words!\"","Shen Wuheng’s face turned pale.","However, despite his anger, he did not dare show the slightest hint of dissatisfaction.","He knew very well that provoking this man further would only lead to his death.","The Gu Master snorted.","Although Shen Wuheng had irritated him, the man had not been entirely wrong.","He was indeed here because of the Lord’s orders.","And he had a mission to complete.","The Shen Clan had already served its purpose, but the Bai Clan was another matter.","He had originally planned to let the battle continue a little longer.","The more people who died, the more corpses he could collect.","However, if the Shen Clan was completely destroyed before he fulfilled the Lord’s mission, there would be some inconvenience.","The Gu Master slowly stepped forward.","Boom!","A terrifying aura erupted from his body.","The surrounding air instantly became heavy.","Shen Wuheng’s eyes filled with hope.","(Finally!)","The Gu Master rose into the air.","His cold gaze swept across the Bai Clan cultivators below.","\"Today...\"","His voice echoed throughout the battlefield.","\"I will show you that even the most powerful clan in the Desolate Heaven Empire...\"","His aura continued to rise.","\"...is nothing more than a slightly bigger ant before us!\""]},{"number":700,"title":"Chapter 700: Power Of Gu Master!","paragraphs":["While the Bai Clan was destroying the Shen Clan, they had not become overconfident.","From the beginning, they had known that the Shen Clan possessed a hidden trump card, possibly a powerful backer.","And Bai Zihan had already sent the information back.","Among the Shen Clan’s forces was a cultivator at the Golden Immortal Realm.","More importantly, that person was a Gu Master capable of controlling refined corpses.","And according to Bai Zihan’s information, the man was highly likely to possess Golden Immortal-level refined corpses.","Because of that, the Bai Clan had prepared accordingly.","Bai Chu had remained on standby from the very beginning.","Although the Bai Clan cultivators were slaughtering the Shen Clan, Bai Chu had never truly joined the battle.","His attention had remained fixed on the surroundings.","Waiting for the hidden enemy to finally reveal himself.","The same was true for most of the Bai Clan’s Earth Immortals.","The Shen Clan itself only possessed two Earth Immortals.","There was no need to send the Bai Clan’s full force against such opponents.","Three Earth Immortals were already more than enough.","The remaining experts stayed behind.","They were waiting for the real threat.","And finally, that threat made his move.","Boom!","A terrifying aura suddenly erupted across the battlefield.","The Bai Clan cultivators immediately stopped.","Countless eyes turned toward the sky.","The Gu Master stood above the battlefield. His robes fluttered in the wind.","A cold and sinister smile appeared on his face.","\"Today...\"","His voice echoed throughout the battlefield.","\"I will show you that even the most powerful clan in the Desolate Heaven Empire...\"","His aura continued to rise.","\"...is nothing more than a slightly bigger ant before us!\"","The Bai Clan cultivators remained calm.","Bai Chu merely narrowed his eyes.","The enemy had revealed himself.","The Gu Master looked down at the battlefield.","His gaze swept across the countless Bai Clan cultivators. Then he raised his hand.","\"Come out!\"","The moment those words fell, three terrifying auras suddenly erupted behind him.","Three figures slowly appeared.","The moment the Bai Clan experts sensed their auras, their expressions changed slightly.","Golden Immortals!","Three Golden Immortal refined corpses!","Unlike the Gu Master whom Bai Zihan had fought earlier, this Gu Master had come fully prepared.","And those three Golden Immortal corpses were only the beginning.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","One powerful aura after another erupted.","Fifteen figures appeared behind the Golden Immortal corpses.","Each of them possessed the cultivation of an Earth Immortal.","Their expressions were lifeless. Their eyes were dull. However, the pressure they emitted was unmistakable.","Fifteen Earth Immortal refined corpses!","And behind them, more figures appeared.","One after another.","Immortal Ascension Realm corpses.","There were several of them.","Their bodies floated silently in the air.","A massive army of refined corpses had appeared.","Shen Wuheng stared at the scene in shock.","Even he had not expected the Gu Master to possess such a terrifying force.","Three Golden Immortals!","Fifteen Earth Immortals!","And several Immortal Ascension Realm refined corpses.","This was the true strength of a real Gu Master.","The Gu Master Bai Zihan had encountered earlier had only brought two Golden Immortal refined corpses.","But this man was different.","He had brought an entire army.","His strength was enough to level many empires in the Eastern Region.","The Gu Master’s sinister smile widened.","\"Go!\"","The moment he gave the command, the refined corpses moved.","The three Golden Immortal corpses took the lead.","Their terrifying auras swept across the battlefield as they charged directly toward the Bai Clan.","Behind them, the fifteen Earth Immortal corpses followed.","The Immortal Ascension Realm corpses also descended.","The entire army moved at once.","\"Golden Immortals...\"","Bai Chu’s eyes narrowed.","Finally, a trace of fighting spirit appeared in his eyes.","The three Golden Immortal corpses were not ordinary opponents.","Although they were only refined corpses, their bodies still possessed the strength of Golden Immortals.","And with three of them attacking at the same time, even Bai Chu could not afford to be careless.","However, the Bai Clan had already expected this.","\"Everyone!\"","Bai Chu’s voice echoed throughout the battlefield.","The Bai Clan experts immediately looked toward him.","Bai Chu raised his hand.","A powerful aura erupted from his body.","\"Follow me!\"","The Gu Master’s expression suddenly changed.","His eyes locked onto Bai Chu.","More precisely—","Onto the sword in Bai Chu’s hand.","The moment Bai Chu drew it, an ancient and overwhelming aura spread across the battlefield.","Buzz!","The sword trembled slightly. Yet that faint movement caused the surrounding Qi to become restless.","The Gu Master’s pupils contracted. Then his eyes widened.","\"That aura...\"","His breathing became heavier.","For several moments, he simply stared at the weapon.","Then his expression slowly changed from surprise to disbelief.","And finally, Ecstasy!","\"A Saint Grade Artifact!\"","Such treasures were incredibly rare.","Even many powerful Supreme Immortals would never have the opportunity to possess one.","Only the most powerful experts could truly obtain such treasures.","The Gu Master himself had only seen Saint Grade Artifacts a few times throughout his life.","Each time, they had been in the hands of terrifying experts.","People far beyond his current level.","And yet now, a Saint Grade Sword had appeared before him.","\"Hahaha!\"","The Gu Master suddenly burst into laughter.","His laughter became increasingly wild.","What an unexpected harvest!","Originally, he had only intended to deal with the Bai Clan and collect their corpses.","However, Bai Chu had now given him something far more valuable.","A Golden Immortal corpse.","And a Saint Grade Artifact.","The Gu Master’s eyes burned with greed.","\"When I have both...\"","His smile widened.","His strength would increase tremendously.","With another Golden Immortal corpse under his control, the number of powerful corpses he possessed would increase once again.","And when he obtained the Saint Grade Sword...","His combat strength would rise to an entirely new level.","Perhaps he might even be able to rival some of the top executives within their organization.","At that point, he would no longer be an insignificant figure.","He would truly make a name for himself.","\"Hahaha!\"","The Gu Master could no longer suppress his excitement.","His gaze remained firmly fixed on Bai Chu.","In his eyes, Bai Chu was already dead.","No!","He was already his refined corpse.","The Gu Master slowly raised his hand.","\"You two!\"","The two Golden Immortal refined corpses immediately stopped.","Their lifeless eyes turned toward him.","The Gu Master’s expression became cold.","\"Kill him!\"","Whoosh!","The two Golden Immortal corpses immediately changed direction.","Terrifying pressure erupted from their bodies.","The air around them twisted violently.","They shot directly toward Bai Chu.","At the same time, the Gu Master’s gaze shifted toward the remaining Golden Immortal corpse.","\"Go!\"","His eyes then moved toward the Bai Clan’s Earth Immortal experts.","\"Kill as many as you can.\"","Whoosh!","The third Golden Immortal corpse moved as well.","It descended directly toward the Bai Clan’s formation.","Behind it, the fifteen Earth Immortal refined corpses charged forward.","The Gu Master’s expression remained calm.","He had to admit, he had underestimated the Bai Clan.","The number of Earth Immortal experts they possessed was far greater than he had expected.","Not only were they more numerous than his refined corpses, but their cultivation techniques, martial arts, and artifacts were clearly superior as well.","If the Earth Immortal corpses fought the Bai Clan’s Earth Immortals alone, they would be at a severe disadvantage.","However, the Gu Master did not care.","Because he still possessed Golden Immortal refined corpses.","A Golden Immortal was an existence far above an Earth Immortal.","Even if the Bai Clan possessed more Earth Immortal experts, how could they possibly resist a Golden Immortal?","The Gu Master sneered.","\"Let’s see how long you can survive.\"","In his eyes, Bai Chu had already lost.","Even if Bai Chu possessed a Saint Grade Sword, the difference in numbers could not be ignored.","Two Golden Immortal refined corpses were attacking him at the same time.","Could Bai Chu really defeat them both?","The Gu Master didn’t believe it.","A Saint Grade Artifact was powerful.","However, its strength still depended on its user.","Bai Chu was only one person.","And he was facing two Golden Immortal corpses.","At the same time, the remaining Golden Immortal corpse had descended toward the Bai Clan’s Earth Immortal experts.","The pressure it emitted immediately caused the surrounding Bai Clan cultivators to become alert.","\"Be careful!\"","One of the Bai Clan elders shouted.","Boom!","The Golden Immortal corpse raised its hand. A massive palm descended from the sky.","The Earth Immortal experts immediately scattered.","BOOM!!!","The attack crashed into the ground.","The entire battlefield shook violently.","At the same time, the fifteen Earth Immortal refined corpses charged forward.","The Bai Clan experts immediately responded.","\"Kill them!\"","Boom!","Terrifying auras erupted.","The Earth Immortal experts who had been standing by finally moved.","Several powerful techniques shot into the sky.","The refined corpses did not hesitate.","They charged directly into the attacks.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Explosions echoed throughout the Shen Clan.","The battlefield instantly descended into more chaos."]}]);
